window.REVIEW_STATS={"total": 3024, "byCompany": {"Expatrio": 1589, "Fintiba": 1435}, "byPlatform": {"google_maps": 328, "google_play": 445, "apple_app_store": 232, "trustpilot": 1975, "trustindex": 44}, "byCompanyPlatform": {"Expatrio|google_maps": 252, "Fintiba|google_maps": 76, "Expatrio|google_play": 255, "Fintiba|google_play": 190, "Expatrio|apple_app_store": 119, "Fintiba|apple_app_store": 113, "Expatrio|trustpilot": 963, "Fintiba|trustpilot": 1012, "Fintiba|trustindex": 44}, "themes": {"Support / no reply": 1456, "Activation / PostIdent": 536, "App bug / crash": 1239, "Payout delay": 735, "Fees": 409, "Refund / money back": 192}};
window.REVIEWS=[{"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I’ve been trying to resolve an issue with my Expatrio blocked account and have been very frustrated by the customer support experience.\n\nI need to make some changes to an existing blocked account, and I completed the requested verification steps and provided the information needed to update my blocked account, including the monthly payout amount for the remaining five months. Despite this, I still have not been able to get the issue properly resolved or receive a clear explanation of the appropriate next steps.\n\nWhat makes this especially frustrating is that blocked accounts are closely tied to visa and residence requirements in Germany, where timing can matter a great deal. When customers are dealing with time-sensitive immigration matters, there needs to be a reliable way to get account issues reviewed and resolved promptly.\n\nI’m posting this review in the hope that someone at Expatrio can look into my case and actually resolve it. I’m happy to update the review once the issue is fixed.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Hello - we are very sorry to read this. We'd like to understand more about ths review, please contact us with more information at marketing@expatrio.com. Your feedback is very important to us.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Very poor experience. They reply once a week. I am stuck here and losing time.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Poor customer service with some bots", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "They are not responsive.  I've been trying to reach for almost 3 weeks.No response. I can't even use to open my bank account", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Never use expatrio. Terrible experience. My visa got rejected about 2 months ago. Still they are not giving me money back. I made soo many complains. I am done with this company. Never in my life using exaptrio. Very terrible company. Please use coracle. I will also attach the screenshot what I see for 2 weeks now. Never use expatrio. Very very bad company. Not returning my money", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Hi Vladyslav - customer feedback is very important to us, we'd appreciate hearing more details about this review. Please contact us at marketing@expatrio.com with more information :)", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I applied for a blocked account (Sperrkonto) to get my visa, and it didn't take long to open. However, I received a 9-month visa for Germany, but the account was set for 12 months. I wrote an email to change it, and although they initially said I could do it directly through the app, they later told me that a blocked account requires a permit from the German government. I obtained that document and sent it via email, but once I actually sent the crucial documents, they didn't even look at them and just kept demanding that I send them again... I don't know if they are even reading my emails properly, and they aren't answering my calls. I am in urgent need of money, but my account is stuck and I can't do anything. The service is truly the worst, and it is impossible to contact a representative directly. They have an unreliable system. Please, do not use Expatrio!!!", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am extremely disappointed with my experience.\n\nI opened a blocked account with Expatrio and transferred my money as required. However, I have been unable to access my own funds because of a verification issue caused by the way Expatrio handles my name.\n\nTo my first name they added my patronymic (father's name). During the POSTIDENT identification process, Deutsche Post correctly identifies me, because their system automatically reads only the first name and surname from my passport. Expatrio, however, insists that my patronymic must be included in my first name, making the verification impossible.\n\nI have exchanged numerous emails with customer support over several weeks, but the issue remains unresolved. Because of this, I cannot access my own money, which has caused serious financial difficulties.\n\nI hope someone from Expatrio's management or complaints department sees this review and contacts me with a practical solution. I would much prefer to resolve this matter directly than escalate it further.\n\nUser ID:1430327\n\nUPD. I had to go to Berlin office to Go through so named Identification process, but error in my name was not fixed. Also they didn't reimburse my travel and living expenses.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "WARNING! GERMAN WARNS ALL PEOPLE FFROM LATIN AMERICA! EXTRA COST 1.000 EURO (Travelling 2 Berlin)\n\nAbsolutely terrible experience. I went through this process with my girlfriend, and it was a complete mess from start to finish. For many people from Latin America, the only way to complete the verification seems to be traveling all the way to Berlin, which is outrageous, impractical, and unnecessarily expensive.\n\nThe support is awful — no real phone number, and the chat replies feel either automated or completely uninterested in helping. It gives the strong impression that the company is more focused on holding on to customers’ money than actually solving problems.\n\nWe ended up with over 1,000 (!) euros in extra costs just to make this verification possible. That is an absurd burden to place on customers for a basic process that should be simple and accessible. This company should seriously rethink its entire approach to customer service and international users.\n\nAvoid this provider if you value your time, money, and sanity.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It worked out after all! I was skeptical at first, but I managed it in a short time thanks to the support. Thank you very much! I have one request: if you could make expartio available in German, that would be great!", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am trying to reach them... so far since 3 days can not reach them.!! no phone, no bot, no email..totally no responding", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "This could truly be the worst experience I had with a company. 5 weeks in Germany, Expatrio still has NOT activated my health insurance.\n\nThis is an illegal situation to be in. Please choose another service carefully for your expat needs!\n\nCustomer support is non existent. Multiple tickets raised. Around one week between replies and each time a copy paste or chat bot answer\n\nStay away", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "[WARNUNG / WARNING] Extremely unprofessional and unreliable service.\n\nToday is July 24th, 2026—my scheduled payout date—but Expatrio has failed to release my monthly blocked account funds for August without any prior notice or explanation\n\nTheir customer support is a total disaster. The automated chatbot is deliberately programmed in a loop to block connection to human agents, and they are completely ignoring urgent emails. Because of their severe operational failure and negligence, I am currently trapped in Germany with ZERO cash for the weekend. This is an unacceptable breach of trust that directly threatens a student's basic livelihood.\n\nIf you are a student planning to come to Germany, avoid Expatrio at all costs and use alternative services like Coracle or Fintiba. I have already filed an official financial complaint to BaFin regarding this matter.\n\nUnverschämter Service. Geben Sie mein Geld sofort frei!", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The service was quick when I wanted to open a blocked account. I got everything done within 12 hours. Even the support team was responding to my enquiries within half an hour.\n\nBut when I applied for the release of the blocked amount, it's been 3 days. I haven't got any response from the team, neither the money.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have very bad experience. I  used expatrio for my chancenkarte visa application and when I arrived in Germany, I activated blocked account but I couldn´t see connect to bank account. I am still having issues. And it s so very hard to get customer service real human. I still couldn´t.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Extremely poor customer support and needlessly complicated account activation process that led me on my last nerve and I stress totally out since a week. Since I could not finalize the blocked account activation due to Expatrio’s system errors and unsupportive and ignorant customer service team (I received only message from their AI Assistant said that they are trying to response all the requests but I dont find any effort from them). I’m facing now an urgent financial problem as I’m dependent on the monthly disbursement to cover my living expenses, at the moment I’m desperately thinking about where can I have money to pay for my rents, foods, hygiene products and semester fee when all my money is stuck in their lengthy unsupportive bureaucracy system. I dont wanna ask my parents sending more money as in order to deposit nearly 13,000 euros into this stressful Blocked account they worked hardly enough!!!!!\n\nThe way Expatrio “support” their customers who are mostly students depending on the monthly payout is really annoying. I write my exams in 2 weeks, but now I’m bearing the unnecessary stress resulted by Expatrio and have to spend so much time to find a way to get money back instead having that time for learning", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "There customer service is very very bad!", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Horrible app. They charge you several euros and offer terrible service.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Due to a technical issue with my bank account, I was unable to make transfers and pay my rent for six days. However, the real disappointment wasn't the technical issue, but the inadequate customer service. My requests for help only received unhelpful AI-powered responses; no actual customer representative contacted me.\n\nIt was unacceptable to have no one to reach while experiencing the stress of being late on rent in a country I was unfamiliar with. The problem was finally resolved after I tried repeatedly every day. I do not recommend a service that cannot provide real customer support in emergencies.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am a Brazilian who have Euros in my wise account and can't make the transfer to create a blocked account. Total nonsense, don't recommend this circus for anyone", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Bad experience:( i don't know why google doesn't want to me give 1 star to expatrio. And 1 star for Google as well. I think they do collaboration. Why do you delete my review???", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "This is the worst company ever; they don't have a phone number and have been harassing me for two weeks.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I rarely leave negative reviews, but unfortunately my recent experience with Expatrio has been extremely disappointing.\n\nOpening and funding the blocked account was straightforward, but the process of accessing my own funds afterwards has been unnecessarily stressful and bureaucratic.\n\nI have already fulfilled the purpose for which the blocked account was opened, obtained the official release confirmation (Sperrfreigabe) from the German immigration authorities, and submitted every document requested. Despite this, the process remains stuck in a lengthy review stage with little communication beyond automated responses.\n\nWhat has been particularly frustrating is that these are my personal savings, which I urgently need for my relocation and accommodation costs. Being told that a simple blocked account closure may take up to four weeks after all required documents have been provided places customers in an extremely difficult position.\n\nI understand that compliance procedures are necessary, but there should be a more efficient process for cases where all legal requirements have already been satisfied.\n\nI sincerely hope Expatrio reviews its blocked account closure procedures, as the current process creates unnecessary financial hardship for customers during what is already a stressful relocation period.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Do not use expatrio, they wrongfully closed my block account and have no human staff to resolve the issue. They cannot be contacted over phone, email, chat, or mail.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The first year everything went well, however now they only accept flywire for their transfers, seeing the price of this, I added around 800 EUROS EXTRA to transfer the amount needed.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Insane. Out of 12 transfers, one didn't go through, so I still have money to receive, but it shows up as non-existent in the app. Even when I inquired, I received an AI response saying it doesn't matter as long as the KONTOAUSZUG details …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Please please do not use Expatrio services if you wantto save yourself the trouble of your funds being stuck with them for months with no response from anyone from customer care. …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am extremely disappointed with my experience regarding the physical debit card service. …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have recently arrived in Germany as a student, and I urgently need access to my blocked account funds for my monthly expenses. However, even after completing the verification process three times, my account is still showing “awaiting …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Systematic PostIdent error and complete refusal of customer service.\n\nBeware of this provider! …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "To be honest please DO NOT CHOOSE. Iam having issues with blocked amount activation and I have tried contacting them throught mail and I have not got any responce. Their apps are buggy and are causing a lot of issues.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "A huge bureaucracy for a simple issue. I have already sent several emails, in the last two emails, they simply did NOT answer the question asked. Very stressful experience.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Hi Sylvie - we would love to know more about this review so we can make improvements or help you out! Please contact us at marketing@expatrio.com so we can help you 😊 …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am having problems with my account, I haven't received any answers from the email system.\nI activated my account, verify my information and had a called to verify it's …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Very frustrating service, can not say they provide services at all. Even have yo send multiple mails over and over to get reply mails. Even though it doesn't have any solution for the problem. The 4.2 rating they got on Google is definitely because of some paid service it is definitely not the real customers", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I'm really angry and you're causing me trouble. Even though I've uploaded my visa, passport, and registration papers, you're still telling me I need a residence permit and I can't withdraw my money. My cash is running out. You're a joke. …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "worst company ever seen.\n\nsimple request they take huge amount of time, not recommended", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Repeated request and begging for return of my own funds that they have kept. Will escalate with German legal authority else I see no other option.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "This service doesn't even deserve a star. It is so bad that I ended up  taking them to court. For all those opening a blocked amount, they will cheat you with the service, there's practically no way you can reach out to them, their chatbot …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Poor slow service. Takes 1 week to open account and then receive funds. While embassy only gives 7 days for entire process. Expatrio is not aligned with german missions abroad and i am not even sure if they can keep your money safe or not", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Dear Expatrio Team,\n\nI transferred the money to my Expatrio blocked account on Friday, December 12th. …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Not recommended. We no longer needed the blocked account and closed it, requesting a payout. We submitted the cancellation request multiple times via the online form. Nothing happened. No response or feedback. Emails are also ignored. No …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have applied for the address verification on 9th December\nStill it shows activation in process\nIn the app they say that it takes upto 1 business days but it’s been 3 business …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Absolutely disastrous customer experience. Avoid this company at all costs.\n\nI have never dealt with a service that provides such contradictory and …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "BEWARE FUTURE STUDENTS & SPONSORS: Expatrio Will Take Your €12k+ Instantly, But Won't Let You Have It Back …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "⭐ 1-Star Review – My Experience With Expatrio Has Been a Nightmare\n\nIn my personal experience, Expatrio’s entire verification and activation process …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "That's a terrible service! My money are in their correspondent bank CREDIT MUTUEL ARKEA ( SWIFT Code CMBRFR2BXXX) since 6th of November, more than 3 weeks and has not reached my blocked account. Support doesn't help, doesn't answer and only …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Not professional and not customer friendly.\n\nExpatio makes it easy to take your money but very difficult to refund your …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "You can use it to avoid being penniless abroad.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am shocked by the unprofessionalism of Expatrio’s service.\n\nAccording to the information on their official website, once health insurance is …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Worst customer service I’ve ever dealt with\n\nMy transfer took three weeks because the first one bounced — and nobody told me. …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The customer service is not helpful and it is not possible to speak with an actual person.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The service is unacceptable...\nThe blocked account service they offer is woefully inadequate. …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I’ve been trying to activate my Expatrio account for three weeks now, but I haven’t been able to because they don’t have the data needed to verify my new Chilean passport. I’ve sent multiple emails to Expatrio over the past three weeks and …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It was so bad everything. It has problems with Apple products for the verification. I would NOT recommend to use Expatrió. Wish I had never chosen it as an international student. The chat-bot is useless.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The account has been practical and has worked well for me. However, I want to warn you about a very frustrating issue: I strongly recommend NOT ordering the physical card. In my case, I ordered it about 10 months ago, and despite paying the …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Bad customer service", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Disgraceful service; they don't answer emails, and their system crashes constantly. I couldn't quickly unlock my blocked account.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I tried multiple times to verify my identity using the video call method and was unable to. The app would crash every time before the chat could start. When it finally worked (the next day), it was done quickly.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I've been trying to reactivate my blocked account for 4 days. I'm ready to start a conversation, but it keeps sending me back to the login screen. This has happened repeatedly. After finally managing to get into the conversation, I get a …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "So can i send money to a blocked account which belongs to my cousin but the funds coming from my own account and we have different surnames. I couldn't get any phone number on your website to enquire.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "They are not straightforward\nMy sister used them for her visa, unfortunately the German embassy asked her to withdraw her application as she did not complete the tuition fee for school …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Hi Luke - sorry to see this! We would love to hear more so we can work on any improvements or assist you with any issues you are facing! Please contact us at service@expatrio.com with more information 😊 …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Really poor service by customer support. I tried to get money back because of visa rejection but every time asking for a document to get from embassy. And embassy replied there is no need of any document when you have visa rejection letter. …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "If only they were so quick to return the money as they were to take it from you.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Worst customer service ever. I had an issue applying and is impossible to get a solution after months of no sense mails. As if they don’t care at all for the customer.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "They said they would handle my insurance in Germany. Then, without asking me, they canceled it. We're ready to pay the premiums, we have the money. I'm a lawyer. They made me travel around Germany without health insurance, jeopardizing my …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Expatrio. I've been paying €1620 for my training program there for 9-10 months. I'm not in Germany, my training program is pending, and I can't get a Visa card because I'm still in Baku. But yesterday I checked and saw that only €1517 …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am beyond frustrated with Expatrio. My first blocked account with them 3 years ago was simple, but now it’s a nightmare. They falsely list video verification as an option for account activation but then force you to go to the post office …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "SCAMMERS. Expatrio AGAIN and AGAIN has made it difficult to refund my money because they reply back with autobots with no customer service to call me or excalate my issue. I have numerous upload my documents and I get an autobot. REFUND my MONEY. Stop charging fees for unprofessional and possibly a SCAM service.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I changed my phone recently, and since then I haven’t been able to access my Expatrio bank account. I can log into the app, but the banking feature is completely locked. I emailed them three times, no response at all. I tried to find a …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Hi Amrednar - we would love to help you out and figure out more about your rating! Please contact us at marketing@expatrio.com and let us know more information. Our team is here to support you with any issues you may have 😊 …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "As I've seen in other reviews, I also use Expatrio for similar reasons, but for 6-7 months they haven't been able to approve my insurance documents. When I spoke to them on the phone, they said the documents were complete and that it was an …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "This company has been driving me crazy for the past few days.\nTo reactivate my blocked account, they're asking me for a rental contract from Germany, an electricity/water bill in my name, or a letter from my health …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "This has been the worst customer service experience I’ve ever had. I requested a simple correction to my insurance certificate on June 24th and, despite sending numerous urgent emails and following up through every possible channel, …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "WORST!😡 WORST!!😡😡 WORST!!! 😡😡😡\n\nI am extremely disappointed with the customer service experience from Expatrio. …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Honestly, a very bad experience with Xpatrio. Customer service doesn't respond. Be careful if your visa from your home country is only for 6 months. In Germany, they require an extension of the blocked account, but Xpatrio will NOT release …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Terrible customer service! Closing a blocked account is so complicated as the request documentation that is very hard to get in the first place!", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "That’s the worst company in the world. I’m so sorry I have to use it to study in Germany :)\nProbably it’s better to use Fintiba but it’s also horrible :)", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I’ve been trying to activate my blocked account through Expatrio after arriving in Germany, but the process is extremely frustrating and unclear. I was told a free German bank account would be opened automatically, yet I never received any …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am still waiting to receive the funds that were reverted nearly three weeks ago. I have not been provided with a clear explanation for the delay, and communication has been extremely frustrating. My legal representative has also been …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The website is automatic but be warned that there is no real support happening. Having individual request will just end in typical problems such as: „we will check internally“ which leads in no response. This made us miss the time schedule to request the visa in time. No response from „internal“ for 2 weeks…", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It's impossible to talk to a person, only a robot. There's no phone. You send a message and receive an automated response.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Do not trust Expatrio. This service needs Auditing. They have withhold my money and refuse it.\nI have escalated my matter a few times and I am speaking to autobots and no one has bothered to call me.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "i did my block account identity verification in post office but still it is showing identity verification waiting in my expatrio app i don't know why this type of things happens with me please fix this problem", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I'm doing Erasmus in Germany and I want to activate my blocked account to open a bank account, but they say they can't do the online process because I have a green passport. Even though the only way to contact them is by email, I'm not …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "In December 2024 I arrived in Germany. I waited a long time for the Christmas weekend, then the weekend in January, then I waited a long time for the term to register here, then I waited a long time to open my bank account in Germany, and …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Hello! Good afternoon! I'm having problems activate my blocked account, I need urgent help Apparently my passport does not help you I need an answer urgently", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I'm incredibly disappointed. I've been in Germany for 15 days and I can't activate my Expatrio account because of the address verification. I've sent numerous emails to support, but haven't received a response. How am I supposed to have an apartment and an official address if I have no money?", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Honestly, they were always helpful when I opened my account, when I upgraded my account and I didn't have much of a problem. It all started when I arrived in Germany and wanted to activate my account. When I arrived in Germany, I wanted to …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Hi Jeread - we are very sorry to see this rating. Please contact us at marketing@expatrio.com with more information!", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "By the way I am impressed with blocked account service but,\nToday I've received a letter from TK health insurance in which they have cancelled my insurance.Because they say that pathway programme students cannot be …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am extremely disappointed with Expatrio’s verification process and overall support. I’ve attempted the video verification four times — each time the agent confirmed that everything was completed successfully. Yet, the app keeps prompting …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am truly angry and disappointed with Expatrio. I referred several friends using my referral code – I met all the requirements for the rewards. Despite this, I haven't received a single cent to this day. After contacting customer service …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Don't even think about depositing your money. I've been trying to get my money for 5 months, I can't get it back. They didn't cause any problems when I deposited the money. However, they always cause problems when you want to get it back. I …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Unjust Treatment and Inefficiencies in My Blocked Account Experience\n\nHello, …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Horrible. They have no customer service. They use an AI to answer your questions. They did not disburse my money and there was no way to contact them asking why. Regret using Expatrio. Avoid at all costs.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am not able to activate my Block account as I am not receiving any coupen through my email", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I opened an Expatrio blocked account for my Erasmus program in Germany. Despite completing the identity verification process at the post office, their app and system keep sending me back to the 'activate' stage, indicating I haven't even …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Hi Walid - thank you for taking the time to rate us. Is there anything we can support you with further? Please do not hesitate to contact us at service@expatrio.com so we can help you out 😊 …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I uploaded all the required documents and completed the verification process 10 days ago, yet I am still encountering an error in the app. The “Pair Now” option is not active. The customer representative in Turkey is extremely rude and …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Hello - we would love to learn more about your rating and help you out! We are dedicated to providing the best experience we can to our customers but in order to do this we need some more information from you. Please contact us at service@expatrio.com with more details 😊 …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "UserId : 875911\nI'm Ganesh Sreepadam -  using Expatrio for my Germany blocked account and health insurance. As I write this review, I've transferred my funds to the Indian bank …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The bank is holding my money, and I still haven’t received my funds! My balance shows that I have money available, but they haven’t transferred it to me. My rent is due, and I don’t even have enough for basic groceries. This is completely unacceptable! I need my money immediately", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I opted fro value package and chose ottonova health insurance but then I am seeing that a lot of jobs specifically require you to have a public health insurance so I tried call expatrio to change my health insurance to Tk public health …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Literally Zero response do not choose expatrio.\nThey take maintenance charges before activation of block account\nAnd deduct 10 Euros and  more  often without intimation and will not reply ur …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Unacceptable Lack of Response When i Demand for Cash Back Bonus\n\nI WILL NEVER EVER RECOMMEND THIS TO ANYONE DONT TAKE THIS", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I want to transfer my money and scared after all these negative messages", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I need help with two issues on Expatrio and I can't get help with either.\n\nThe response is standardized and I can't get in touch with anyone from support. …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "We have called several times, to know some information. We have amount which is blocked and we want that funds to be transfer to another bank like commerzbank. But students telling Expatrio is not allowing to open other account but they are …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Everything was great with the blocked account, till I decide to close the bank account because of my visa changes and I provide a new IBAN in February, is supposed that the money comes from 23th with 2 or 3 days of delay, now is 8 days and …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Hello, I need to add my tution fees to blocked account as a additional Basic Sum as per visa requirements. I have mailed to the Expatrio support team. Please check the mail ASAP. Before 24th of Feb I need to get the confirmation document. It's very urgent. I hope you understand.\nThanks.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Terrible service. Opened a blocked account 6 weeks ago and still cannot access funds. No one responds to emails and phone system is recorded only. Do not use - go and use a bank instead.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "No one can help me they sent me my money to wrong account number. I need to call but . It is not working. I already sent mail but no one reply me.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Hello! We are sorry to see this low rating, could you please give us more information about this? You can contact us at marketing@expatrio.com with more feedback.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I had created Expatrio blocked account application on 20/01/2025 and while creating the account it was promised that the account verification will be done in 24hours. It's been almost 4 days and my application is still under review. …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Account activation delay and ignorance\n*No customer support at all !\nI am an international student at IU on the Berlin campus. I have already opened …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am writing this review for Expatrio as I was trying to contact the number listed on their website to sort out the refund of canceled blocked account for a relative of mine. The case here is that the funds ( €11400 to be exact) were …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Worse experience about customer service. I am mailing since three days and no one replies me", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "very very bad, no response to the calls, very high service charge and no responsibility/ good help provided. Strictly not recommended. Before this company all stundents used to directly contact Deutsche bank and TK to create blocked account …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I applied to close my Expatrio account and requested the transfer of the remaining balance. It has been 4 days so far. If I can get my money back without any issues, I will give a 5-star rating. So far my experience with expatrio is good …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Not recommended! If your visa is denied and you want to close your blocked account, they will resist tooth and nail. You'll be forced to fill out complicated forms, some with completely irrelevant information. Once all that's done, they …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Since i didn’t got my Residence Permit yet, they say they will jeopardise my account as a warning.I only have visa right now, and there is no option for uploading Anmeldung.I have written mail but they didnt responded.I called them ,they didnt took the call. Not satisfied", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Unreliable system and poor customer service", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Bad customer service, do not respond, they haven’t give me my money for four months now", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The worst experience, they haven’t give me my money for four months now and they don’t answer, the customer service is so bad, I do not recommend", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Really bad service when refunding the money after visa refusal. First my funds were sent in the wrong IBAN number missing the last four digits i provided which were mentioned twice in the details i sent. After that i have been told to wait …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It’s showing it’s open but when I came here it’s close I am trying to reach you out from 5 daysss and there is no respond", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Hello, my name is Deepanjay Paul. I opened my blocked account with Expatrio instead of other platforms, thinking that they offer good service and are reputable in what they do. However, I now realize I was wrong about that. I am trying to …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Do not go near Expatrio.My daughter had a terrible experience with them. A faceless internet bank with zero customer service. No phone service. You can go insane trying to interact with their AI Livechat Bot or you can wait 24-48 hours for …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The customer service representative who verified my identity through video call with Expatrio was rude. She just hung up on me. I felt really bad. I ended up going to the post office to verify my identity. The post office employee was incredibly friendly. I was discriminated against.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I’m sharing my experience with Expatrio in the hope that someone can guide me or help resolve this issue. …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The customer service really needs to be updated. AI generated replies to queries are not appreciated because mostly it's impossible for that system to understand the problem. When i tried contacting a human customer support team. I still …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have been trying to call the expatrio customer service from India and the wait time is so long. Even after hours of trying, the call doesn't get connected. I am nearing my deadline for document submission to the visa office and this is really bad and frustrating. I wouldn't recommend anyone to use expatrio if their needs are urgent.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "EDIT (13/11/24): I had to take drastic action and guess the email addresses of Expatrio's managers to finally get help from their team. Only after sending an email explaining how urgent my situation was and exposing how much I was being …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I do not recommend Expatrio to anyone. I arrived in Germany a few weeks ago and still I couldnt activate my blocked account because my visa photo is still pending.So i couldnt activate my blocked account, It has been a long time since then, …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I've been waiting for my physical card for over a month now, and customer support has been completely unhelpful. Every time I reach out, it's just a bot responding with the same repetitive messages, without offering any solution. Very disappointed with this service.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "This place seems to be going under. It used to be the best place I've ever been, but things are not looking good. …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It's very difficult to get the blocked money back. No customer service hotline is available. …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have submitted enough funds yet it is showing insufficient funds and customer care is not picking up call\nNo way to meet up in office or personal …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "My experience with expatrio was not good at all. Landed here on 3rd oct and still struggling to get my block account money. They didn’t respond to mails. Whole month i spend money by borrowing from others. Now i have to pay my nov rent in 3 …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "My experience with Expatrio has been a nightmare. I applied for the Value package but my college does not accept my private health insurance because I'm under 30. I have been trying to contact Expatrio for weeks but they don't answer me and …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Very bad customer support. I'm not able to activate my blocked account after reaching Germany. I have mailed them and tried to call them but not getting any response. I've been struggling here for a month to activate my account and they are …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I don't even want to give 1star to it. But my money is with them so I have to give atleast one star. …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I've been in Germany for 3 weeks and I haven't had any money for 3 weeks! I've already told them that I need the money to live here. And nothing. They don't answer the phone and the email is very slow. An email was sent 2 days ago saying …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Expatrio has put me in every tough situation. I landed in berlin on 1st Oct and I don’t have my account activated yet, thats 3 weeks now even after submitting all the required documents. …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Customer service has resolved the issue. It's recommended to call or contact customer service via voicemail, as email is too slow… …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "You guys are making my stress level so high. Why isn't my request processed yet? Please... Guys... please respond. No one is even responding to the mail or on the phone. …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "really bad experience in activating my block account as expatrio requires a physical verification for opening it account and it requires a postident coupon for it but its been more than 3 weeks since it is stuck on it and even after raising …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "even though the process was easy to understand and follow along, at the moment (october 2024) they do not hold the new version of the brazilian passport in their system for verfication. This means that the online verification process when activating your accunt is not possible, only by post.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I’ve been trying to contact the service center for the past two weeks, both by email and phone (but no one answered). Yesterday, they finally responded to my email. …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "After checked I opened my blocked account on Expatrio. Everything was good until I came to Germany . I came and tried to activate my bank account but they had a lot of trouble. I called many times they even do not respond. For request mails …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "My mobile device pairing issue is still not resolved. I have already shared my poor Expatrio experience on Trustpilot but no one seems to even care.\nIt has been almost 4 weeks and my blocked account is not yet activated. I am …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The service is abysmal! No response to emails, and the phone service is even worse. I waited 25 minutes and then they just hung up. They have no respect for their customers' time – I get the feeling they're completely overwhelmed. And the …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "After activating my self-protection account, I received neither a confirmation email nor any remittance. The main problem is the lack of customer service. Email replies are intermittent, and the responses simply tell me to refer to …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have been trying to activate my blocked account through the expatrio app. Even though I have a bank account with different bank i have been asked to open bank account with Expatrio. I have shared all the required documents as requested by …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have been trying to activate my blocked account since two days. I have already shared my IBAN and BIC number with expatrio but I have not received any reply from expatrio yet nor expatrio customer care is receiving my calls. Please resolve my issue as soon as possible.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am very disappointed, yesterday I called them and waited literally for TWO WHOLE HOURS. No replies at all, left a voicemail no answers. I was willing to ask them about Blocked Account, such a shame for them. Not recommended.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Greetings, I am facing a very irritating problem while trying to activate my blocked account. When I try to contact Expatrio through the phone, it always tells me that the number is unavailable (I called at 11am to 4pm.). And when I try to …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Do not choose this company if you are going to study in Germany. Their customer service is extremely slow to respond and unprofessional, sometimes even ignoring me completely. I sent numerous emails before they finally replied, and even …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Please, do not use this service if you value your time and money. Their payment partner for this region (flywire/cohortgo) is not supportive. I made my payment only to find out that it was rejected. I emailed expatrio and they sent me a …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I was satisfied about the service before I arrived Germany but not after arrival. I had been told that I need to identify myself by going to the Postbank and I did it. But after that, my status on the expatrio portal said my identification …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The process is very slow. When I have transferred the funds in my blocked account, it was credited next day. But when I have requested to close the account and ask for refund(due to visa rejection)then it is taking long. I have submitted …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am currently facing a very frustrating experience with Expatrio. Initially, everything seemed to run smoothly, so I transferred the necessary funds to my blocked account, expecting to receive my confirmation certificate soon after. The …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Has anyone ever faced the same predicament I am currently facing? I applied for a Germany visa and was denied. I had put money in my blocked account in Xpatrio bank which is EUR11285. End of June I then applied to have my funds credited …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Regarding the advantages, one can mention the reliability in document processing and the timely deposit of money into the blocked account. …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "NOT VISA COMPLIANT. Since I'm over 30, they gave me private health insurance. When I went to my visa appointment, the visa officer told me the health insurance they provided did not fulfill the visa application requirements. The only reason …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Poor Customer care and no response from their end. I have sent amount via bank account to expatrio block account but they have not updated the amount in block account. Don't use Expatrio.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The office is not open, all their services are online.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have had a super bad experience with Expatrio. My money has been blocked in Expatrio for close to a year without any response and dispersment of my money. I called them and gave them my details and they still haven't released my money. ABSOLUTELY HORRENDOUS SERVICE FOR SOME COMPANY CLAIMING TO BE THE BEST!!!!", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "They're making it very hard to return my money. I'm trying for months. The video activation was refused even though I had my documents in hand. The post office activation is not working", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Stay away from Expatrio! They're major scammers in cahoots with Mangopay! We've been trying to get our money back for a year. They send us generic emails saying they're having technical problems with international transfers and that they're …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Hi Karl, we are very sorry to see your one-star review. In order for us to take steps to improve Expatrio for you and other users, we would really appreciate if you could send us more feedback. You can send us a mail at … More", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Today I had my Video call from Expatrio for activation of my account. The woman who connected first was really rude and aggressive. She didn't finish my activation or didn't want to do it. Unfortunately,  I don't remember her name. I think …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I tried calling the hotline countless times. Each time, I was told the average wait time was 2 minutes, and each time I waited in vain for more than 20 minutes. I don't think this provider is an option for me. UPDATE: I finally got through …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Hi Heet- unfortunately I do not see your name in our customer base so I cannot locate your issue. We are very sorry to see your 1-star review. Please reach out to us at service@expatrio.com with more information so we can understand your review better, and make changes to rectify the issue!", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Hi Dhruv- unfortunately I do not see your name in our customer base so I cannot locate your issue. We are very sorry to see your 1-star review. Please reach out to us at service@expatrio.com with more information so we can understand your review better, and make changes to rectify the issue!", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Hi Dharmik- unfortunately I do not see your name in our customer base so I cannot locate your issue. We are very sorry to see your 1-star review. Please reach out to us at service@expatrio.com with more information so we can understand your review better, and make changes to rectify the issue!", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Very bad service.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Expatrio offers a great product, which I haven't fully got to know in detail, but I must say that in terms of problem resolution it is absolutely terrible. I've been in Germany for almost two weeks now and still I've had many problems to …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "This company and app are terrible. They charge a transaction fee of around 50 euros, but the service is zero. They even help you open a Revolut account; they're attentive until the blocked account is reactivated, but when you ask how to …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Very Disappointed with expatrio’s service! My brother is a student, residing in Berlin. He hasn’t been receiving his money since 3 months from the blocked account despite endless interactions on emails and calls! All of his university …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Worst blocked account company for international students in Germany. The money that was sent to expatrio is for financial security of a student. My friend's money has not been disbursed for 3 months now and because of that all his services …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Issue with returning the money. They rejected my application", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Hi Aneha, thank you for the review. We would like the opportunity to investigate your feedback further. We ask that you please contact us at service@expatrio.com, and please provide your contact details in the email. We’ll work with you to resolve any issues as quickly as possible.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I really like that they have resources geared towards Spanish speakers, and that the information and instructions are clear and the transfers are confirmed very quickly, which is very reassuring. …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "A very unsatisfactory experience with the service. Despite having €1060 available, I haven't received my money for a month. The staff are extremely rude and refuse to verify my identity with the absurd excuse that their program can't read …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Worst company I had to deal with in a long time. Refuses to free a blocked bank account and transfer all funds back, after having provided all necessary documents time and time again. Does not accept official documents by a German embassy in my case. Do not recommend at all.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "This is a terrible service. My experience starten in November 2022, I had deposited money in my blocked account through a transfer from my uncle. It all went smoothly. Then 2 months later my Visa application was rejected. Between February …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Unfortunately expatrio seem to discriminate against Iranian citizen. After being able to set up an account in 2020 (as an Iranian) I had to do a renewal to prolong my visa. However, without further reasoning (and despite the legal preconditions not having changed) they were refusing service now.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Expatrio has blocked my previous bad review from showing... therefore let me try again. When I moved to Germany, I had to wait one month for my bank account to be activated and did not receive my TK health insurance card for over 2 months. …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Dear Ozgur Korkmaz Celiker, thanks for your review. We would like to hear more about your experience, so that we can use your valuable feedback to deliver an even better experience next time. Please reach out to us at service@expatrio.com … More", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "A month since arriving in Germany in 1st March and having did the verification twice and still hasn't got my first batch of money which they claim is \"1 business day\" to process. Gave no reason for that and endless waiting. Wrote by email …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "As I see from the reviews here, this is not first time they cannot handle and solve any problems despite several emails and phone calls. They ask you to send an email to their customer support, but respond you with a template answer as if I …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It is sad that I have to write this review because as much as I know that there are some people at Expatrio working hard to solve the issues that have arose from the banking partner migration process, I still do believe that the whole …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "PLEASE AVOID THIS SCAM SERVICE!!\nExpatrio is the worst ever, they do the financial aspect of their service through a partner and they blame it on the partner later. They never provide any help. …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Do you have phone in your bank,if you have it learn how to receive it", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The service at this bank is absolutely disappointing. I activated my blocked account online in mid-August, but nothing has happened to this day. I've tried calling countless times, but only got through twice. The first time, an employee …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Disappointed they don't do online verification of documents any more. Now, I gotta go with my ID to the post office. Why change to something inconvenient? Everything else is good.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am not satisfied with the service and I would take action about it. I blocked my acount two months ago and they don't activate it for me. I called them for identification process and it finished, but they didn't active my account and …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "On the evening of 20 August, I had a video identification call to activate my account. …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "No money, no contacts\nI have been using a blocked account since November 2022, everything was fine, but last month there were problems. For almost three weeks I still can not receive …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I would not recommend using Expatrio to anyone. I requested a return of my funds 6 months ago and provided all of the necessary documentation. When they processed my return, they sent my money to the wrong place and are now saying that they …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I was a customer, and the customer service is extremely lacking. My emails are not answered, and I've even tried calling the hotline. It was said the waiting time is 3 minutes but I couldn't even reach them out and had to wait up to 45 …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "My first blocked account ended after the last remittance in July, but I opened a new account in June, hoping it would be renewed for another year. Now it's August, and I haven't received my money. The phone calls haven't been resolved. No …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Everything ran smoothly for the first account, then I needed to extend the account. …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "There is no problem until you open an account with a new Turkiye passport and load your money. but when i want to introduce the account to the German bank, they do not accept it.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Ever since they switched to a new bank, the service and the activation process has been an absolute nightmare. Expatrio tells you that your blocked account will be automatically activated a month after they have received the money but it's …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Horrible Service, couldn't activate the extension of my blocked account, had so much problems with it. Also the time it takes to process the money, they should do it earlier if the days are on weekends. Honestly for the first few months is okay, but I wouldn’t recommend it for extensions", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am a long time user and their customer service is not reachable on the phone. Waited for 20 mins (twice). Still no answer.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Update: On March 2023, Expatrio tried to remove this review through a Google claim. They said I never interacted with them. As you can see they couldn't delete it as I have all the evidence of the interaction. …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Hi Samarth, thanks for your feedback. While we apologise for your experience, we hope that we can use this to improve in the future. Please send us an email with more details to service@expatrio.com.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I've trying to contact Expatrio from 3 days. I have mailed them and haven't gotten any reply whatsoever. And their contact number is of no use, one can't get through their waiting time. And they are off on Saturday and Sunday. There's no way to get things done.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am not happy with Expatrio, my daughter is an international student in Germany from Zimbabwe.\nWe funded her blocked account through Expatrio. …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Dear Yulitza Fuenmayor, unfortunately I can not find an Exaptrio account under your name. If there is something we can do to improve your experience with Expatrio please do not hesitate to contact us at service@expatrio.com.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The customer service is terrible. I have wired my blocked account money for a while now and I need the 06 Blocked Amount Confirmation for my Visa Appointment and I have tried to contact their customer support with proof of payment and they …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Today I have to update my review and report that I'm having problems again. This company reported my insurance policy as starting a year before my arrival (March 2022 when it was actually 2023). Now the health insurance company is charging …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am trying to contact the expatrio since last Thursday onwards my visa interview is on Friday currently my monthly payout of the blocked account is 869 euros but it should be 934 euros please help me in upgrading it.I have already sent requests and waiting for the reply mail.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I don’t like to write bad review and always giving a chance before doing so but here I am. When started process and sent my money to Expatrio, everything went smoothly and customer support was quick on reply. However, when it comes to …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Please, anyone planning to study in Germany, don't choose this company! My remittance took half a month to arrive, which is seriously affecting my visa application. And their customer service is incredibly slow to respond. It's driving me crazy every day.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It’s the worse ever! They say we will contact you within 24 hours but they don’t do! And i initiated a payment to increase the amount based in the authorities request after i couldn’t download the confirmation Gabrielle one of the customer …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Don't use their service. They're understaffed and it's impossible to reach them by phone or email and your money is just floating in the air. I've been waiting 2 months for them to release my block account. Very irresponsible.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Very bad experience.\nIt was never informed clearly while opening the account about how to activate the account, apparently one needs to go to a german post office for identity …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "On 21st April 2023 i opened my Blocked, they told me Re-upload my passport since quality was not sufficient.\nToday is 1st May 2023 still I haven’t received any feedback from them. I also tried to contact them using their customer care form haven’t received any update yet so far.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Absolutely terrible. It has been over 2 weeks since I wired them money for my blocked bank account and I still have not heard back from them. STAY AWAY!", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Very bad experience after arriving in Germany. They are not paying my monthly payout. They introduced a new scheme of identity verification at the nearest post office. I have done that verification and even after 2 weeks I didn't get my …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Impossible to have communication with the bank, the emails don't work, the phones don't work, the page doesn't work. I've been solving a change in the amount of the blocked account for a whole week. Nobody gives a solution is the only thing missing for the embassy.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "No one actually responded to my email until I asked for help from a larger organization to connect me! and I already waiting 24hr and one business day.  The contact number taking so long to answer. And now is my third time to go the post …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Horrible experience with expatrio.\nIt has been 2 months till now I didn't receive my monthly amount even my blocked activation didn't take place. They keep on pointing out mistakes on my passport …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Slowest service and mobile application.\nNo proper information or replies on time.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Like hundreds (possibly thousands others), we're all having issues with our block account from expatrio. They advised to us bring enough money to cover while we wait for activation but it has been two months! We are international students …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have reached Hof, Germany and have linked my blocked account with the local bank Sparkasse. As you know to complete the blocked account you have asked me to go to post office for passport verification but there is problem with my passport …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Pathetic customer service, takes ages to activate account.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have created blocked account in expatrio and i have transferred my money a week ago . i haven't received my payment confirmation. It has been more than the time limit that they say which would usually take and now I am vexed with the …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "WORST SERVICE EVER. IM TRYING TO GET MY MONEY SINCE ALMOST 3 WEEK BY NOW, THEY DONT ANSWER ON THE CELLPHONE AND THEY ANSWER THE EMAILS VERY SLOWLY, and the answer is the same that they wrote me 1 week ago. This is ridiculous, I’m living in …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have been trying to reach them for several hours for days on the phone with no response or other option. They don't answer the messages either. I even went to the office in Berlin, but no one was there. I have not been able to activate …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Wrote on trust pilot, doing my duty here as a consumer here. Please be informed that if you might be in the same situation as I am. Blocked account cannot be activated. No follow up from Expatrio. All my emails and calls unanswered. Put …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "worst service and customer support", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Im having the worst experience with expatrio.\nI opened an account and they approved my details and passport, after that I transferee all the required money for my visa application. Then they said our bank …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am trying to contact customer service but I waited 20 minutes on the phone. I hope they will help us soon. …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The worst experience that I've ever met. I am waiting for my money to be transferred to my current bank account already for a month! I do not have any cash left. And the support is doing nothing and all they keep saying is that I just have …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "One of the worst customer service ever for such an important process. I am trying to reach them with email and phone since days and ask about my process. It has not been processed since 3 days even though they say within 24 hours they …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I tried to open a blocked account but they never answer after 20 call and dont answer to my emails. I even dont trust them enough now to block my money in their accounts. If you have the choice, I recommand you to try another service.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I’m having a really difficult time with Expatrio. They advertise that the service for a blocked account has a 24 hour turnaround but I uploaded my passport for review two weeks ago and it still hasn’t been processed. I’ve sent a contact …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Have been trying to upload a picture of my passport to open a blocked account for the last 2 hours. It doesn't matter how i take the picture (I took more than 200) the algorithm doesn't want to accept it. Customer support didn't offer me any useful information (the same tips that are on the website). I'm going to use fintiba", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Hi Allen, thank you for the review. We would like the opportunity to investigate your feedback further. We ask that you please contact us at service@expatrio.com, and please provide your contact details in the email. We’ll work with you to resolve any issues as quickly as possible.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The worst experience with this company.\nAll their staffs don't care about our procedures after receiving our money, and never should  we expect their service. …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The payment of each month was very punctual, the website and the forum are very helpful. It was not complicated to use the platform. But I have to take two stars off because I never received the refund that they promise with the \"value …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Dear BM, thanks for the rating, please let us know if you have any constructive suggestions, simply contact us at service@expatrio.com or call us at  +49 (0) 30 25557415.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I used Expatrio the first time that I needed a blocked account for Germany and was excited by how easy and seamless everything went. Therefore, this year, I decided to open another blocked account with them for my resident's permit renewal. …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "For the Blocked Account it was a good service, 100% recommended, but for the Insurance, I have 3 months here already and I haven't received yet my Insurance Card, and I did all the inscription through X-Patrio.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Appalling service and a lack of professionalism.\n\nMy experience with Fintiba has been extremely disappointing. I have been trying to get my funds back for over three years now. During this time, I have had to provide numerous documents and follow various procedures, with explanations that constantly change.\n\nI was successively asked for additional documents, then told that the transfer had been made before being returned, even though my bank had no information about it. Next, I was asked to have a notarized document drawn up. I followed all their instructions and provided the requested documents.\n\nFinally, after completing all the steps, I was told that everything was now in order and that the payment would be made within 4 to 5 days. Even this timeframe was not met.\n\nThree years of dealing with the process to get my own money back is completely unacceptable. The lack of clarity, the contradictory information, and the slow processing give an impression of serious disorganization and a lack of professionalism.\n\nI strongly advise against using this service for anyone considering entrusting them with their money. I do, however, hope that Fintiba will eventually resolve my issue and return the funds owed to me.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I deposited the required funds to my Fintiba blocked account on 11 August 2026 for my German student visa. Today is 25 August. Fourteen days later, my account is still not verified, and Fintiba is now the sole obstacle to my visa application for my Bachelor's studies at starting in Ocotber 1st.\n\nThe facts, in order:\n\n• 11 Aug: Funds transferred.\n• 12-14 Aug: All requested documents uploaded, and proof of source of funds demanded despite the funds coming from a European country.\n• 14, 17, 19, 22 Aug: Four separate follow-up emails to support. Zero substantive replies.\n• 15-24 Aug: My university admission letter was rejected FOUR TIMES for \"verification\" — despite being an unconditional admission accepted by the university, and despite my subsequent proof of full enrolment, which I also uploaded. As I had to contact health insurance without their support, I couldn't depend on them.\n• 25 Aug (today): Fifth call to support. After I gave the agent my ticket number and it looked as if she was going to help, I was put on hold for 8 minutes and then the line was disconnected.\n\nI still have no blocked account confirmation nor travel insurance and no updates. Both documents are legally required for my visa file. Both are entirely blocked on Fintiba's side.\n\nFintiba markets itself as fast, reliable, and student-friendly. The reality is that the funds are sitting untouched at your partner bank for two weeks, silence from support, opaque document rejections, and 5+ phone calls with no help whatsoever. And I can tell I am not the only person facing this.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I don’t recommend it at all. There have a lot of delays. If you don’t want to be broke in abroad just try some alternative other than Fintiba", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Worst financial service… they are not releasing my friends well earned own money from her blocked account. Why? We don’t have any info, they are not accountable for their actions… this needs further investigation. Shame on you!", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I don’t write reviews often but I physically cannot let this slide. I’ve been a Finitvia customer for over a year and the last four months have been an absolute nightmare. I made a deposit that never showed up in my account. Not “delayed” — just gone, like it evaporated into thin air.\n\nI contacted support more times than I can count. Every single time it’s the same script: “we’re looking into it,” “please allow 3-5 business days,” “our technical team is aware of the issue.” Four months later, still nothing. No money, no real explanation, no compensation for the stress this has caused.\n\nAnd it’s not even just me — every time I open the app there’s some new glitch. Balances that don’t update, transfers that fail silently, error messages that make zero sense. For a bank that markets itself to students who genuinely NEED to trust their money is safe and accessible, this is unacceptable. This isn’t a “minor bug,” this is my actual money we’re talking about.\n\nI’ve asked for a supervisor, I’ve asked for a formal complaint reference number, I’ve asked for literally anything in writing confirming they know where my deposit is. Nothing. Just silence and copy-paste responses from support.\n\nIf you’re a student thinking about opening an account here — please, save yourself the headache and go somewhere else. I wish I had", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "No costumer services, no help , wrong advise, terrible experience", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Their customer service is terrible, it seems they don’t know how to reply to emails. Be careful if you have a complaint, the customer service won’t care and all you will get is a queue ticket that’ll last a lifetime!\n\n*Support ticket ID 1295825, on the email it says \"we already transferred manually\" but when i call the customer service numbers on the third day they even don't know whether the money is already transferred or not🤡", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "For a month now, despite multiple text messages, calls, and ticket submissions, I have received no concrete feedback regarding my issue.\n\nI was only informed that an internal escalation had taken place.\n\nTicket number: 1329957\n\nWhat is the current status of this matter? What specific action was taken as part of the internal escalation?\n\nWho is responsible for further processing my request?\n\nWhen can I expect a firm resolution or a final answer?\n\nAfter a month and several attempts to contact you, the communication to date is no longer acceptable.\n\nPlease forward my request to a responsible manager and provide me with concrete feedback as soon as possible.\n\nThank you.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I strongly do not recommend Fintiba.\n\nMy blocked-account extension has been unresolved for weeks despite repeated emails, calls and escalation. They already received my money and deducted their fee, but I still have not received the required documents or payout.\n\nBecause of the delay, I have also incurred additional financial costs from failed payments.\n\nSupport repeatedly tells me to wait, but provides no concrete resolution. For a service that students depend on for visas, residence permits and living expenses, this level of support is unacceptable.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Don't deal with this organization, don't send them money! Fintiba is broken. They don't provide Blocking Confirmation after the money is deposited into their account, but instead launch an endless verification process to determine the origin of the funds. There's no clear list of documents, and additional requests arrive every three weeks via email. People are wasting time and money, and their plans are ruined. It's been more than two months since the money was sent, three sets of documents have been submitted, and nothing has been received. A letter has been written requesting a refund and account closure. Nothing has been received. The support chat says the refund will take 6-8 weeks.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "We were forced to open a blocked account with Fintiba for my son’s student visa, and it has been my worst experience with a financial institution to date. Because my son is a Russian citizen, Fintiba requested proof of the source of funds. We uploaded all the required documents immediately. It has now been more than four weeks since we submitted documents, and we have received no feedback other than 'please wait.' Fintiba initially stated that the processing time would be 3–4 weeks, but that deadline has long passed. We are in a completely hopeless situation: the bank has our money, we have no documents for the visa, and there is no indication of when we will get them. If you have the option to use other providers, I strongly advise you to avoid Fintiba.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Avoid this company at all costs! I transferred money to my blocked account on June 22nd. It took them six (!) whole weeks and multiple support tickets just to send me the list of documents required for the source of funds verification.\n\nTo make matters worse, they finally sent this list the exact day AFTER we had already submitted our visa applications. Because of Fintiba's unacceptable delays, we were forced to open a second blocked account with another company (EduBao) just to meet our visa deadline.\n\nSince the Fintiba account is no longer relevant, we are now trying to get our money back. However, their customer support completely ignores us. Heaven only knows how much more time and effort it will take to get a refund.\n\nNever use this company under any circumstances! They will ruin your schedule and ghost you when you ask for your money back.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "DO NOT TRUST THIS APP AND COMPANY. Fintiba completely frozen my verification process for nearly 2 months (from June 11 to August 4), completely violating their advertised processing times. Because of their severe operational delays, I did not receive my blocking confirmation (Sperrbestätigung) in time, missed my mandatory university deadline in Berlin, and my educational plans were completely ruined.To make it worse, when I sent a formal cancellation request on August 4 while my profile was still unverified, they ignored it. Instead, they retroactively activated my account 3 days later just to force me to close it manually and steal a €159 Fintiba Plus setup fee and monthly administration fees for services they failed to provide.I demand a 100% full refund of my €12,073 without any unjust deductions. If this is not resolved immediately by their management team, I am submitting official complaints to BaFin, the European Online Dispute Resolution platform, and the Verbraucherzentrale for unfair business practices. Total scam.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am currently dealing with FINTIBA and want to warn any incoming international students: whatever you do, DO NOT block your funds with FINTIBA.\n\nLike most non-EU students, I had to open a blocked account for my visa. I made the mistake of trusting Fintiba. Now, they are completely refusing to release my money. I have hit a wall communicating with them, and they are holding onto the funds with no valid justification.\n\nI have already called and emailed BaFin and the Versicherungsombudsmann for help, but shockingly, both organizations told me that this blocked account and this company are unknown to them.\n\nBecause of this, I've realized it is better to contact the Ausländerbehörde directly. I am going to explain the situation to them—that companies like Fintiba are running a scam on people like us—and ask the authorities to give us another solution to show we have enough funds to support our lives in Germany, at least to protect future students.\n\nDealing with this level of financial uncertainty while trying to focus on my studies is incredibly stressful. If you are in the process of planning your move, please save yourself the anxiety, the risk, and the potential legal fees. Choose a different provider for your blocked account, or just explain the situation to the Ausländerbehörde and ask them to give you another alternative. DO NOT BLOCK YOUR FUNDS WITH THEM.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Really really had a worst and  annoying experience with fintiba. I would never suggest anyone opening a block account with fintiba. Their Helpline number is useless no one answers the call and if luckily someone answered they just talk to u for a kind of formality and they do not give u a right solution in fact their help line number can be more called as stress creating number. Their prosess are even slower then a turtle.\nThank you", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "My experience with Fintiba was unfortunately very disappointing.\n\nAfter my visa application for Germany was rejected in 2024, I sent Fintiba the rejection notice and requested the closure of my blocked account and the withdrawal of my balance. Despite contacting them multiple times, I received no clear information for an extended period regarding the status of my request or what specific requirements were still lacking for the account closure.\n\nOnly after contacting the German Embassy and requesting assistance did I receive notification from Fintiba that my blocked account was now to be closed. I am pleased that this step has now been taken.\n\nHowever, one important point remains unresolved: Since 2021, €4.90 has been debited from my blocked account monthly. Despite several inquiries, I have yet to receive either a comprehensible explanation for these charges or a detailed breakdown of the debits.\n\nI expect greater transparency from Fintiba, timely communication, and a full explanation of the charges that have been applied for years. I hope that the company will address these outstanding issues promptly.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I extended my account in August for 12 months. I already had the money needed for 2 months, and they asked me to pay the needed amount for the remaining 10 months.\n\nSince last October, I have received no money at all, and I have been contacting them to resolve the issue since February with no clear answer and no one helping me to this day. I tried asking for a supervisor or someone who could solve my problem, but they always say they can't do it or find some excuse.\n\nThe customer support is one of the worst I have ever experienced. It takes them at least 20 minutes to answer, and sometimes they just hang up. The employees are impolite and sometimes shout at customers, even trying to shift the blame onto me.\n\nTo resolve the issue quickly, I asked them in May to extend my account for a 9-month period, thinking I might be able to get my money back this way. Instead, they sent me an extension for 12 months, asking me to pay for the whole duration even though I already have enough money for 10 months in my account.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Haven't recieved a blocking confirmation since 40 days now. I've got till 3rd of August to reply to The Ausländerbehörde regarding this. The customer care helpline speaks very reassuringly but, NOTHING seems to happen or change in the backend. My funds have been delayed for August and looking at other's reviews, it seems like I'm doomed.\n\nFintiba was great until April 2026, before they tried migrating their accounts to another bank. Anybody who's looking to open a new blocked account with them, word of advice, PLEASE DON'T.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "♦️❌️❌️❌️❌️‼️‼️‼️‼️‼️‼️\n*Not recommended for African/Kenyan students*  ♦️❌️❌️❌️❌️‼️‼️‼️‼️\nI opened a blocked account with Fintiba for my German student visa. Before payment, communication was quick. After depositing, support became extremely slow and emails go unanswered for weeks. As an African applicant, I feel like we are treated as \"low priority\" customers compared to others. Response times are poor and there is no proper guidance during the process. It has been very stressful and uncertain. For Kenyan and other African students who need timely support for their blocked account, I strongly suggest looking at Expatrio or Coracle instead of Fintiba.\n\nticket 1311347", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Extremely poor service and absolute unreliability!\n\nContractual promises regarding timely payouts are repeatedly broken. This is the …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Unfortunately, I am very dissatisfied with the service. Despite multiple inquiries, the reopening of my blocked account is taking an unreasonably long time. Communication is slow, and I am not receiving clear information about the processing status. I would have expected a faster response.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Very disappointing experience with Fintiba\nI am unable to complete my payout setup because I never receive the required verification code by email or phone, which prevents me from accessing my own funds. …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I accidentally uploaded the wrong selfie for my verification, which was my mistake. However, Fintiba kept me waiting for a WHOLE MONTH without sending a single rejection or error message! A professional institution dealing with visas should …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Unfortunately, I had a very disappointing experience with Fintiba's customer service. …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ticket #1269301\n\nMy experience with Fintiba support has been extremely disappointing. …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am extremely disappointed with my experience. My blocked account payouts have been delayed for more than three months, and I am still waiting for my remaining funds of approximately €3,100. Although the support team has replied to my …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Very disappointing experience with Fintiba. I only used their platform once to compare blocked account and insurance options, but I never accepted, signed, or activated any insurance with Fintiba or Barmer. I never used their services …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ist really so shit I never see …you can wait 10-20 minutes that juts out off your phone like nothing …and that don’t can help you nothing abut it ..I ahve wait to close my account already more Dan 3 week …thay can’t du nothing you can only wait and dint know how long wait and how long more to wait das ist shit service I never see..!!", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Absolute disaster. Fintiba has been withholding my contractually mandated payouts for over 2 months now due to a technical glitch in their system. The application fails to send the required mTAN SMS, and the verification input field for the …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "the worst provider one can imagine! unresponsive and unprofessional! you send an email today, they reply 40 days later! customer support hotline is another tragedy! nothing is satisfactory", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Editing my review after phone call with one of your representative, hopefully thing will be settled down.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "For me i didn’t have a good experience with their services after i been with them for 2 years", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Review in June:\nFintiba has a horrible customer support. They facilitate everything for you when you want to open the blocked account and transfer the money. But when it comes …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Very bad service....", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I've been waiting for over three weeks for my blocked account to be opened, and still nothing has happened. …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "⚠️ FRAUD ALERT! DO NOT DEAL WITH FINTIBA! ⚠️Fintiba is illegally withholding my money and my wife's money! After we failed to submit our visa documents, we closed our blocked accounts with an official release from the Consulate. It has been …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "i advice anyone not to deal with them any more they will create the block account and once you need your payout they will not give you anything", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have never had such a bad experience with a service provider as I did with this one. …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I opened my account before of my university admission letter by my passport number and I was proceeding the further steps very smoothly , I just had a week of pause in the process for the verification and I'm 100% sure they have all my …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have a Fintiba account but I can't access my money. I sent emails but received no solution. I've been trying to reach an authorized person for 1.5 months. I want someone in charge at Fintiba to contact me and resolve my problem.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Don't try to open a blocked account there. It will cost you your mental health and German visa, not speaking about your money.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Fintiba is an absolute joke. My money has not yet been deposited to me, I have waited for 3 weeks, could not pay rent, or even go to the supermarket to buy groceries. I have called customer support several times, sent emails, placed a …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Their support service is very slow. It has been 2 weeks that we cannot get Blocked Account Confirmation Letter because we sent the money to existing account. Support Agents dont solve the problem and they are always telling that they are …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Shameless people with no sense of responsibility. When I call you, you cut the call. What is the use of calling customer support when you cut calls. It is my last payout and I have sent multiple emails since two months, I have not received my money since last two months, Ticket is 1175629", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "DO NOT USE THIS COMPANY! Absolutely ZERO customer support.\nMy visa was rejected and I have been emailing them for 3 weeks to release my money. I am currently in a third country, I urgently need my funds, and I have to …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I opened a blocked account with Fintiba for my language visa in Germany. After arriving in Germany and uploading my visa to the system, I was shocked: instead of the dates shown on my official visa documents, the payment start date was …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Firstly, it was never obviously stated anywhere that after extending my blocked account, I would have to have at least around 6000€ on my account to receive my payout. …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "HORRIBLE customer support, payments come extremely late without reasoning (today is the 11th of May!!!!!), do not, EVER, use Fintiba for a blocked account!!! I almost got kicked out of my apartment because my fiancé couldn’t pay rent, given …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Completed WebID video legitimation on April 25, 2026 (Order 1914626). Was promised IBAN within 2-3 working days. Today is the 9th working day — status still Pending, no IBAN issued. …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "My Visa May Expire Because Fintiba Keeps Delaying My Blocked Account Confirmation\nI had already opened a blocked account with Fintiba and decided to extend it for …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Terrible service. Never replies to emails...when we manage to connect phone calls, they tell you wait for the email replies. They try and hold the money as long as they can without releasing it to the customer(probably for the measly interest they can get out of it)!!", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "*AVOID FINTIBA UNLESS YOU WANT TO BE LEFT BROKE ABROAD*\n\nIf you are a student or worker planning to open a blocked account in Germany, do …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Very poor and unprofessional service.\n\nI've been in Germany for a month. …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I arrived in Berlin on April 5, 2026. On April 7, 2026, I tried to complete my transactions through the app, but it kept giving me a \"missing documents\" error, and it still does. There was a change of bank. The transaction couldn't be …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am extremely disappointed with Fintiba. The blocking confirmation document they provided me is missing the monthly payout amount – a mandatory detail required by the BfAA office for my visa application. Without this, my visa cannot be …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Very disappointing experience. I did not receive my payout from the 14th of this month, and I have had ongoing issues since the 1st of the month linking my Fintiba blocked account to my bank account. It took more than 9 days to address the …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "My payment is almost three weeks late which is putting me in a really difficult situation. I have called Fintiba three times and each time they told me the money will be transferred in a couple of days, which did not happen. They also told …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "If it were possible, I would give zero stars. The service is absolutely terrible. I honestly don’t understand how they have a 4.8 rating it makes me question whether these reviews are genuine. Future customers should be very careful when dealing with this bank. Overall, a complete waste of time.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Very disappointing experience with Fintiba.\n\nMy blocked account has been pending for over one month, even though I have …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "If you aren’t from a country that’s on friendly terms with Germany, DO NOT use this service. …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Poor performance 🤮🤢 …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Terrible! I've been waiting for my money for 10 days now. Support can't do anything. I'm not getting any replies to my emails. They want me to call every day, but that doesn't help either.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "They open an account very quickly, but closing it is very difficult. For 5 months now, I have not been able to close the account and get my money back.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Id there is minus 5 I would give it.\nPoor, very stressful, and ambiguous customer service.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "very bad in everything specially the call center, there is a guy called Alex ,i called him for a problem of my son today at 10:30 a.m , today 11\\2\\2026, he closed the phone during conversation, 6000 Euro, my son paid and the system has …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Extremely poor and unprofessional service.\n\nOur attempt to open a blocked account for the Chance Card failed completely. A …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Disaster for people who want to get their money refunded!!!!! Technical issues and steps that never end. Just waiting for weeks, months, nobody cares, they only give general information on the phone. Our own money, in our own blocked account will not be refunded quickly, I don't know what to say, it's 2026!!!!!!", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Fintiba is by far one of the worst service providers I have ever dealt with. Their customer support is practically nonexistent. Emails go unanswered for weeks, urgent cases are ignored, and there is no reliable way to speak to a real …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Stay away! Your money will be withheld!\n\nI am writing this complaint on behalf of my mother, for whom we opened a blocked …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I've been waiting for over five weeks for my blocked account to be opened, and still nothing has happened. According to Fintiba, the problem supposedly lies with their partner bank, which is unable to provide account details for \"technical …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Unfortunately I have been met with constant resistance from Fintiba regarding the “legitimation” of my documents. Beware that there are a lot of hidden procedures that come after you successfully open your closed account, to actually get …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Two years ago, I opened a blocked account for my visa, and the whole process went very smoothly. However, it seems that the company has undergone major changes, because now I’m opening a blocked account again and almost nothing works! …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I made a review of 3 stars a while ago saying I couldn't get to any costumer service at all: nobody answered me any email I sent, the bot on the app/page didn't work, the human chat was never answering and nobody was picking up the phone. …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "From my experience of using blocked account in Fintiba, I can say the following:\n1. If you are a student, you are opening a blocked account for the first time, …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Worst customer service I have encountered in my life. They simply don’t care and won’t help no matter what the issue is and how bad it is impacting your life. Pretty sure it’s just a robot even for emails because the answer make no sense …", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "It was good with the phone later....May be some technical issue was there.", "p": "google_maps"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "sooo primitive software for a banking app. Improve your features such as being able to see how much you spend, how much you earned between specific dates. Authentication doesnt work well also, put a page to see waiting approvals. bla bla bla. Improve your software.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am very disappointed with the Expatrio app. The customer service does not respond quickly, and getting help can take a long time. The identity verification process is also very complicated. There are so many steps and so much verification required. It is difficult to access and withdraw your own money.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "when search study options dead overlay appears asking emal", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Excellent experience with Expatrio. The entire process was well organized, transparent, and easy to follow. Their support team was professional, responsive, and genuinely helpful whenever I needed assistance. Expatrio made an important part of my preparation for studying in Germany much smoother and less stressful. Highly recommended for international students..", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "stupid dumb app keeps locking me out", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Always having issues", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "worst service I have ever had. Every time I send an email they take 3 days to reply. it is also valid for any email reply too. there is no phone number to direct communication. I have been communicating for the last 17 days to resolve my problem. what a worst service.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "very good", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "reliable quick services", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "very very bad pls don't use this app 🙏", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "After you activate your account, everything is great. They keep you updated when there is maintenance happening, which takes about 2 hours, and it happens in time when you're asleep, which is good. When you have a question, you reach out to them by email, and they go above and beyond for you.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "great", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "not got application i can't update product mail make ticket complaint then only hopefully you get some answer from other side else nothing just watch and wait of mercy of there work", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I cannot update my data. i cannot find any email address. i cannot find live chat on app.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "good 👍", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "This app is leagues behind others. A perfect example is that every time I approve a transaction it says it is denied but still goes through. Expatrio itself does what you want but this app is terrible and needs a severe rework", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "no service, paid 10 euros for physical card, no tracking or anything. no proper response from team even if we mail.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have made research and came to understand that Expatrio is good since I am planning to go to Germany within very few years I hope I will enjoy their experience when I reach in Germany come back and check on this review", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "give a try", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The process is smooth and the customer service is sufficient", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "They withheld the money from my final installment until I updated my visa status, which I consider to be completely unacceptable; it is my money, and I was counting on it—they cannot deny me access to my own funds.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The way to get back your money if the visa is registered is so back and forth, it's like finding a treasure", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Cannot even activate a blocked account.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "expatrio is constantly making me regret my decision to stay with them after the one year. apps not working well a lot of the times and can't even log in with passcode in urgent cases and sometimes it makes you do new passcode like i didn't had one before.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Their service is too bad, postident is not working and they are asking to travel 800 kms to unblock the money.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "scam scam scam 100 emails to the support and service without any one response u will lose your money with this scam company", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am highly satisfied with Expatrio, came from Pakistan. Best services", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "My experience so far... (Currently I'm unable to use my account - I don't know why. Got the following messages: May 25 2026: Residence permit successfully uploaded... you will have continued access to your Expatrio Bank Account as usual. May 26 2026 Your Expatrio Bank Account has been suspended... If you now have a valid proof of residency (Residence Permit or Fiktionsbescheinigung), However, from the uploads section my Fiktionsbescheinigung is flagged as approved.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The process to get back money when the visa is no longer a thing am going for is so crazy", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Not working at all", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "very bad app . open initially for uploading money but after reaching in Germany in the name of process of verification of identity like passport in post office is not occurred and no help from customer service. and particularly stuck in this process and no money to the student how he/she can survive", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Worst service doesn't even have a customer service. At least be responsible for others money. We provide money for a good service not to chat with stupid chatbot. I hope these people don't reply with a chat bot for this comment too. I have tried all means to contact these guys and this is the last resort. There are other apps which are much better.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Need Anmeldung to activate account, way better to use N26.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I had a very stressful experience with Expatrio blocked account activation. The blocked amount transfer was completed successfully without any issue, and I also completed POSTIDENT verification at a Deutsche Post branch. However, the account activation status did not update properly afterward. Despite already completing in-person verification, I was later asked to travel from Trier to Berlin for another verification appointment. For an international student, this means significant travel costs", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "they are very unhelpful when it comes to rescheduling the dates of blocked account . even , support team don't respond you for weeks", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "nice app", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Highly frustrated with the current support model. Poppy (the AI bot) is a massive step backward and makes it impossible to get help. Replacing your support staff with a bot was a mistake, please bring back real people so we can actually use the app effectively.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "good experience, initially afraid of opening an online blocked account,but I'm comfortable", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Took me only a day to setup and transfer all the funds. Would highly recommend.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "fantastic", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "i have faciing a problem regarding pair device . I recommend you all u have faces the problem when you come in Germany I have facing problems , I upload All the documents when I pair the device I can't pair still struggling", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The app is riddled with bugs and having to navigate it is simply frustrating", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "good 😊👍", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "its too much good", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It's a good service", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "why it doesn't shows the the direct debit deduction notification in your mobile also it's their app does not have more security feature like fingerprint password and also an option to hide your account balance and after you make payments the receipt should be generated instantly and an option to share them. and one feature I would like to to have is when a payment is made they should also mention how much balance is remaining. plus it's always open even when you leave it open in all the tabs.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "she was kind and quick", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Used for Visa blocked account. zero stars, they did not let me pair my device, so my money is stuck. When you have an issue there is no way to contact a person, only FAQ documents.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "This was a super smoth process!!", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "great", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "there is NOT possible that in 2026 still bank accounts that ask money for management of the account. is an insult that the embassy forceses you to be robbed by a bank to apply for a visa. personal i have a DE IBAN with another bank by free and i have to pay to an other bank to have part of my money blocked.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "For me the app worked terribly, it took significant time and effort getting my account activated dispute having all my documents. Expatrio seems to be a good service, but they really need to fix the app.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have completed the post verification six times, but I keep receiving the same response every time. This is very frustrating , need to work on your verification process! and definitely i personally never recommend anyone this service.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "worst UX ever", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "still on it but the little I have seen was awesome.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Always having system problems making it too difficult stressful for applicant to transact", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "very prompt and effective", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "too slow and tedious process", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "push notifications for transactions needs to get fixed. its gone when i launch the app", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "good", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I had not yet received money into my acount, even after doing the POSTIDENT verification last month and I sent quite few request to support team and they give the same standard answers \"Do POSTIDENT coupon verification\", when I told them I did already a month ago at Deutsche postoffice!! Tired of writing them! I can't even call them! Please resolve the issue, it's been frustrating, I left Germany and can't do verification at your office!", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "This is the worst app I've ever used. I can't upload any of my documents, and when I try to get support, I can't reach anyone, even though my documents are ready. You'll always be the one in a difficult situation", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "can't verify transaction from my bank account", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "the help section isn't even clickable.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The app works well, their Customer Service responds quickly, but EVERY time I need to update or confirm documents, etc., there are problems.. I don't know if their company is poorly managed or if there are problems in their programming, but I am constantly contacting Customer Service to correct their errors. Would not describe the experience as even \"satisfactory\"..", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "This is definitely not user friendly at all. I read instructions at help center, even so cannot solve simple problems. I have never used such a terrible bank app. I wish I could change my bank. Unfortunately since my blocked account is on this bank I am stuck for a year. But after that never again, never", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "all my documents are verified and now i don't see any step further of how I have to start with the verification process. the chatbot keep telling me to verify but where do I get this option No idea! The chatbot keeps getting me back to the same question if I am in germany and if I started the activation process. it's been over a week since I am in Germany and despite of all correct documents I still have no access to my blocked funds because of this inefficient and confusing mobile application!", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "One of the worst apps of all time. Can't use the banking section without the app crashing like 7 time before one button works.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "mera inter k bad 9 years ka gap hy kiya ab m kisi b german uni m admission ly sakta please guide", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "doesn't load pages, keeps loadimg and loading. whats the point of having an app which doesnt work.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Very helpful app", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "No call/chat support. Email support takes eternity. Fed up with the follow ups.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Honestly, how long is it supposed to take to activate a blocked account. I need the money to pay for so many things, but I am locked behind a waiting time that's ridiculous. You have the money and all my information! what more do you want to activate a bank account? Why can't it be as easy as the setup? it would have been so much easier and faster to transfer all the money from expatrio to Fintiba. I am so sick of this.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The app user interface is really bad, please do something about this. It keeps forgetting that we have already setup the login passcode", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "i cant change the insurance part.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "bugs bugs bugs", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Expatrio mishandled my blocked account. My visa was for 12 months, but they only scheduled 10 months of payouts because I arrived late. Now 2 months of my own money are stuck, and their support gave no real solution. Very rigid and unhelpful service- Not recommended.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Good", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Horrible service. Uploaded my documents 5 times, every time they claim “verified,” but the app still says proof of address pending. Stuck in a useless loop. My residence permit is expiring and support shows zero sympathy—just robotic copy-paste replies. Broken system, no real help. If you value your time and future, avoid Expatrio at all costs.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "it's just so slow", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have changed my Germany address in the App after that my user ID becomes Null, and there is nothing shown of mine in the App.. I have called even email them. they didn't respond..", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Absolute trash app. Constantly and randomly crashes. Also the support is useless and relies on a terrible ai bot that provides no real help. Using expatrio has been a terrible experience.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "account verification keeps crashing", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Great user experience. Great Services. Great Customer support. Worth every penny spent on it for making everything easy.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Can't provide video verification when the app has bugs and keeps crashing. \"AcTivAtE yOuR account In ThReE eAsY StEpS\". Right. What the app lacks in ease, it makes up for in headaches to activate your account. I understand a lenghty verification of identity is needed due to security. But wow, they give you one tool (Through the app ONLY) for secure self help and it still manages to let you down. prepare for a headache if they havent fixed any of the bugs by the time you use the app.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The app seems to be broken at times. Currently I don't have an option to open my bank account via visa, only the residence permit And the contact us button isn't working", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "terrible customer service. onlt chat option is an ai that is not helpfu at all and they never pick up phones.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Excellent 👍", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Recently moved and activated account and my rent needs to pay. At the time of month end and new month start where I have to move with new contract it's blocked the access(Telling that technical maintenance ongoing for banking). Now where I go and live without access to my money? What is the meaning of the securing hefty amount with you?", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "There will be some updates to the app every time I open the application. Fixing issues with the app is always appreciated. But having to update every single time is really annoying. Can you please combine the releases to the app so that there are fewer updates?", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "this app not work properly and iam getting stressed...", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am beyond frustrated with Expatrio. My first blocked account with them 3 years ago was simple, but now it’s a nightmare. They falsely list video verification as an option for account activation but force you to go to the post office. After complaining, they moved me to Mangopay, promising an easier process and no extra fees—yet I was charged setup and service fees twice! After 12+ emails, they only refunded part of it and kept giving copy-paste responses. Zero accountability, zero help.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "excellent", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Everything is fine but why do you release some new update every singleeee day, it's irritating to update every day hire better developers", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Please do not make your block account in this bank. I have paid €10 to get a physical card a month ago and I haven't received it yet. The bank is unable to provide you tracking information. There is no physical branch for this bank anywhere in the country. Also, they do take maintenance break once in a week where you can not make your online transaction. you can not even deposit cash into Atm machine. I highly recommend everyone to open your block account in different bank.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "they don't payout block amount on time and when we try to reach out customer care contact number the IVR says that the hold time is 4 minutes but there are no agents answering the call even after 20 minutes. The most pathetic service didn't expect this.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have been locked out of the application for 5days now, something needs to be done about the constant bugs", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Excellent cooperation and service", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Play store doesn't have 0 star. Such a worst app. It's services didn't works. Feels like filling a court case against them. They have blocked the account and saying that we are fixing it, but are unable to fix. And when you Email them, they will say that we will fix it tomorrow. It feels like mental Harassment. You could not even see your Bank details. Such a worst app. I wouldn't recommend. I regret deeply!!!!", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "HOW MANY TIMES DO I HAVE TO SEE THIS?! 🤬🤬🤬 Uh-Oh! It seems something went wrong. You are now locked out of your account Please come back 12 hours after the initial block time, If the problem persists please reach out to our Customer Support Agents Edit: The issue was fixed, but still, the problem was unacceptable and took a long time to fix.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Takes way too long to load the page", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "worst app, has locked my bank account and I am unable to access it from past few days. they Keep saying they will fix it. and I am not even receiving an OTP for pairing the device.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Even after doing the updates regularly, it shows: You are now locked out of your bank account. Try afte 12 hours. It's been 3days, and it is still the same. Feed up with the interface. Worst experience.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "My Bank Account Has Not Been Opening For 3 Days Now. Expatrio takes The Monthly Fee And Still Cannot Properly Maintain Their Apps. Worst Bank App.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "worst customer service and horrible banking service...", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "tooo many problems", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "They have blocked my access to my bank account for the last 2 days due to some technical error on their part and I need to access the bank section in order to freeze my card because it might end up at the wrong address.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "when is the bug fix coming. I am literally waiting on money to give to my landlord. they keep saying it Will be fixed for 2 days now. I can't do anything in that case. all my money is stuck and the Bank account says i am locked out for 24 hours.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "banking app hasn't been working since 3 complete days.Couldn't check my card details because of this.Needs a lot of work.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I've been locked out off my banking account for the past 24 hours now. I tried calling them, emailing and I get the same response that its a bug issue and its been happening with everyone we'll fi it soon and all. How am I supposed to access my blocked amount If there's gonna be repeated bug issues and all. Cleared cache reinstalled tried logging in from laptop but nothing worked. I Please try and get it fixed ASAP.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have had horrible experience with their bank. I do no recommend at at all.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "One of the world's worst bank application. I have blocked account funds in bank account and I couldn't able to access the bank account itself. I've tried dropping a email and suggested to clear the cache and after that it gone even more worst. I've replied the same to service team but there is no response and again after 24hrs dropped an another no response. If I'm unable to access the bank account and use the funds then what is the purpose of this blocked account and bank account. Worst bankapp", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Very bad customer service and the worst apps I have ever used. Very complicated procedure.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "worst customer support", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Easy and safe to use.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Great Experience", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Excellent service and very helpful for us. thanks 👍", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "poor experience", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "the lowest quality app I've ever seen", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "best communication and other service", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I would Never ever ever recommend you to use Expatrio for block account. I recently did the biometric authentication at deutch post as required to use block account and then asked 3 security questions. Although I answered them correctly it says Invalid answer. After few attempts they blocked me. Now they have my money, and I am not able to access it. Edit: Issue Solved 😄. Thanks 👍", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "wonderful app and too much excellent service with fast response.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Pathetic customer service, very slow service. Wouldn't recommend this service to anyone", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Thanks for keeping my money stuck in this terrible app. Now I can't even do anything. The one liner generic reply from the customer service isn't helping either. Worst app. Terrible service", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "no at all getting payment notifications", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "horrible, horrible, horrible. Do not use their services go for the other blocked account services. Absolutely pathetic customer service, you can't reach them by call or live chat, you can't go to their physical location. Never ever choose their free bank account service I repeat never.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I'm very frustrated with their new blocked account activation process for transferring money. They now require verification through the post office in Germany, and even after that, they still ask for additional personal details through security questions. Even when I enter the information correctly, it says it's wrong when I try to link it with their bank account. Please remove these kinds of activation methods — they are extremely frustrating.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Great!", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "well while making the blocked account their constomer service is good but after your in Germany and you contact them they are slow some time they don't even reply. last week I put one query to their website and it stated don't spam us so I waited one week I got no reply then again put the query this time I got a reply in 2 day 🙄. I have given them the asked doc again it's been 3 days and I am waiting.but overall there app there own bank which you get is good .", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Good", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "When are you going to fix the balance issue? Literally, a banking app that displays the wrong balance, says enough. Very buggy service! Such bugs should not exist in a banking app.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "payment interface is not good. tried to book a train ticket and when it sent push notification for payment confirmation, the app didn't show anything. lots to improve", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "great app and great help to an international student like me", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "dont support my nationality , so very, very, very bad apps , it wast my time", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "why i cant upload document in app, i am trying to send mail past 2 days is that possible to do upload my visa n rental agreemnet documents in expartio website but i did not get response kindly replly", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Good centralized application.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "This is the one of the buggiest app in the playstore. Nothing works as intended. Transfers takes days to process. Don't use it as a banking app. Payment authorisation doesn't work every time.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Android App does not support Apple login", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "IDnow does not work!", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I find it so hard to download and do something after....about Expatrio Banking App", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Third class app with third class customer service.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Terrible experience. They keep rejecting my passport scan copy no matter how many times I uploaded it meeting full requirements. Please people be aware . They are treating us as if they are doing it only for us. I had a horrible experience with them. I can't recommend anyone.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I've done my identity verification, but it's just frozen like that for a day now and I had to upload my documents like 5 times. Each.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Expatrio app is crashing while setting up passcode login. Please resolve this bug asap.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Poor Customer Service & App. Come to Germany on 09.01.2025 and tried to activate both my account and my insurance. First steps were okay, however; when it comes to last step, you can say, \"OH MAN!!!\".Trying to get in my banking section but nope, good try(ies) though. Trying to reach a person? Send a mail and wait till next day ( If you send it in Friday, wait till Monday). Worst of it I'm literally sick, I need to see doctor but will I able to activate my insurance? Now, thats a mystery...", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Please consider to fire who design this app for Android, id verification is super laggy, after that i got stuck in pair the device step, I can't continue after I enter postal code! I used to trust expatrio when they were working with mango pay, there is no problem. But with aion right now, I just can't.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Very frustrating app, in my case when trying to open my bank account. Been trying to verify my account for more than 24 hours now", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "can't set up the login password. every time email otp login is needed with password.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It's been 3 weeks I have been in germany , I did all the possible things that was asked of me by the expatrio support team to activate yet my issue is not solved , the banking section is not opening and the app is full of glitches . Now they are not replying any of the emails . Please solve this issue asap", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I cannot recommend anybody to expatrio. Worst customer service. Why keep on sending autogenerated AI replies to important issues that requires comprehensive, urgent and adequate answers. The worst part is that the mails are responded to after centuries.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "the worst customer experience possible. customer service replies you incredibly late, you cant report transactions that does not belong to you, app Interface is frustratingly bad. I am very disaplointed and regretful to trust these people with mit money.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Fast, legitimate, and user friendly service. It is highly acceptable by German embassy and consulates. I highly recommend it. If it was not for Expatrio, my visa wouldn't have been approved. Thank you expatrio. Keep up the amazing work.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "My banking account tab just disappeared from the app, and my money stuck there because I can't access it", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Everytime I to initiate a payment towards by blocked account, it just gets stuck and time out. It's working fine on the website, so the app is useless.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "How many times ever I try to enter the passcode, it says wrong even if entered correctly, and it is not allowing me to forget passcode, fed up 😢", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Simple and elegant. No fuss over big details and it is clear about the requirements. Thank you Expatrio for a good user experience in aiding me towards my journey in Germany.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Don't use expatrio. you will regret", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "After all the blocked account amount was transferred, these guys stopped helping me. For all queries I am receiving a generic AI response even after asking for human support multiple times. They responded to all my queries perfectly before the transfer. I advice everyone to choose other options.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I've not recieved my disbursement yet! I've done everything, my documents are approved, I've been waiting for weeks and Expatrio has done nothing! Please speed up the process.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "No proper customer support despite sending lot of emails stating I haven't received my funds. The same automated response with no proper response to the issue addressed is repeated every single time you send an email. Expartio team please respond to the issues related emails", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Worst service! For blocked account activation i have done 3 TIMES postident verification still it is stuck. I havent getting any proper help from expatrio team too. Steps i followed: On app,went to banking tab (status:awaiting activation) clicked on activate button (status : identity verification waiting) Went to postident office, verified myself. Just after doing verification, status changed again to \"awaiting activation\" with activate button (which makes no sense). 8 DAYS,No progress", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "App crashes when looking for banking details fix it", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Please stop sending out automated email responses for important issues. I have uploaded all the documents for my health insurance but it still shows that my account is in review. Its been more than 2 weeks. And whenever I mail expatrio regarding this I get an automated response from your terrible AI assistant asking me to do steps I have already done. Please update as soon as possible.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It's been one month and Expratio have not disbursed my first disbursement . Every time I mail them it takes 10 days to get a response from them . I even tried to call them , however the response is same . I am stuck in the app and it's keeps on showing me error.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Very bad service i tried to activate my bank account and they were asking for my IBAN and BIC, but then my friends blocked account got activated without that. When I tried to contact the customer service via email they are just giving me an automated response which is useless. Please fix it and please reply to your emails.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I've been trying to contact support and activate my Blocked account / Bank account since a month. The support sends the same auto generated emails stating my account is activated. But it is not. I've tried sending almost 10 email by now showing proofs. Edit: everything is working now, it took roughly 3.5 weeks to sort everything out and continuous emails.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Very bad experience with the app. Facing issues to activate my blocked account and now after a month it's fixed. But now I'm not able to link or open my bank account in the app.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Perfect", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Terrible experience with the blocked account activation. It failed three times and I was unable to open my German bank account for weeks after arriving in Germany. The Expatrio staff were late in responding to my emails and unhelpful in explaining why the identification failed and did not give proper solutions.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have taken expatrio value package and till date my university didn't received my M10 insurance certificate and my university is not allowing me to enroll into university without M10 further I have contacted Expatrio incall and email but I didn't get a proper response and my M10 certificate very disappointed with the Expatrio team", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have to recommend against using this service. It shouldn't take 3 times to complete the identity verification due to your app glitches/failures. First time: completed the entire process to activate my account including the call. The Ident specialist I talked to didn't really know what they were doing. App froze after, crashed, Expatrio claimed I never did it. Second time: Started over, Ident specialist answered & just hung up. App crashed. Third time: finally worked after another crash.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Very good application it's providing their own bank and it's very use full no need to open another Bank account", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "\"I have been in Germany for two weeks and still haven't received my blocked account funds. I've uploaded all the necessary documents, but despite contacting Expatrio multiple times via email, I haven't received any response. This lack of communication and delay is causing me significant stress. I expected better service for such an important financial matter. Very disappointing!\"", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Crashes every time I try to access my blocked account. Tried the other method of Postident, but I can't even get to my blocked account screen to do that before it errors. I have money I NEED to activate transfers for my visa. From looking at the reviews, this is a known issue for a week. This is unacceptable.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Worst service....", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Insatisfait", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "There is a serious problem with the app. Probably after the October update. I can't go into my insurance or blocked account via the mobile app without the page having trouble loading and ends up logging me out due to error. The recent update keeps causing me and others who are posting on this review to crash on android.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "My overall experience was great before coming to Germany, but now the app is so buggy that I cannot even make it past the main screen to just see the blocked account.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The app was designed by a child. It is full of bugs. And for some damn reason, they force you to use it for everything. I am unable to activate my blocked account, I have been trying for 3 days but it isn't working because of the stupid app. The customer support isn't even replying to my emails. It's truly infuriating.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Worst service i experienced, I am facing an issue from 2 to 3 days I sent 2 mails and I try 2 time to call expatrio but not a single reply expatrio please reply and solve my query. I need to link my expatrio application with bank account I am facing issue not able to connect it.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I cannot review my digital card details for 5 days through app. There is some software issues. I am not able to purchase anything. It is huge problem.....", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "When trying to authenticate to activate my GF's blocked account the app crashes every time. On her phone and mine both. It is an android problem. We had to ask for a friend's with iPhone to get it activated", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Yes it is good", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "No proper customer service. Also delayed my submission of the insurance to the university. Never use expatrio. Had the worst experience.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Very poor service After everything done, they signed me up with a very bad health insurance and now I can't take public health insurance even though I am eligible for it. My university is not accepting my private health insurance and I am not getting my ID card because of that. I am trying to resolve this for a month but they are not responding to my mails at all. Very very bad service", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Literally one of the worst app you can found for your blocked account. I've been trying to contact them for hours and I am always on hold. plus the customer care officer was sounding so low that I cannot even hear her and then she hung up.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Would not recommend this to anyone who is in on a timeline. It is taking 2 whole days just for my blocked account verification. I heard that expatrio is quick which is why I opted for it because I was on a tight timeline. But this is proving to be a nightmare and now I am on a risk of missing my visa appointment because of it. This is the worst experience ever.Definitely donot recommend", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Worst customer service. They reply neither on mail nor pickup the call.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Horrible experience", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Worst service they are providing I am trying to contact with them from last 4 days as i am having a visa appointment today and still there is no reply. I have transferred the money to their bank account yesterday but still there is no confirmation from there side.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It's easy to upload money. Thank you for making my study in Germany a reality", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Please stop forcing people to use app for every single thing. To use my bank account I can still do it in my laptop in browser. I don't need to suffer the tsunami of bugs in this app. App logs you out completely and when you login you have to give another email OTP. I haven't been able to check my band details since weeks because it keeps shutting down. Please stop forcing us to use an app when you can't get the app to work properly.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Worst app interface,We know that we cant transfer money from this app then why is the necessity to make double authentication ? As if someone will steal away the phone and start using my Expatrio! Email OTP is the worst decision by the company.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Fast service. Secure. Excellent customer care. Website has great and simple UI Design", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Please add an option to login via fingerprint authentication. Entering password and then a verification code each time is time consuming.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "sorry but Minus 10 star for the idiot person who developed this application !.. Useless email OTP security feature to login.Worst app login interface,Very slow(stuck) and time consuming.Why cant u just give fingerprint or passcode login.Why do u like wasting user's time??", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "fabulous", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I got my blocked account confirmation just 8 hours after I sent the money. And this is with the regular international money transfer not with \"expatrio payment\" (because I did not have that option in the app). Hope this good experience goes on in the withdrawal phase in Germany.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Excellent", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It's been working well so far. They come back to you quick. It's been so easy to use", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Prompt payment processing with no delays. I appreciate the exceptional service provided for the release of my blocked funds. Thank you!", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "excellent service", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Super helpful app for blocked account creation, and health insurance application.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Logs me out of the app every 1 minute, and then have to login again. \"Oh no you lost your internet connection\" when im right next to my router. Useless app.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Great app, I really enjoyed it, but there is no portal to directly contact the Expatrio assistance team for personal information and assistance. I suggest there is a means for direct communication for assistance of some issues not mentioned in FAQ. The app is outdated and does not respond well 😐 need to fix these issues.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Doing payment was a bit confusing but it is due to the online portal and formalities of my local bank. Expatrio portal was smooth and support team was also very quick.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Not friendly", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Not logging in with google with Android 14 s24 ultra. Fix please", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The app does not work properly", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Worst app ever. Never go with this one.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Great opportunity 😃", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "App isn't loading for activation of Bank account", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I downloaded the Expitro app and it was a complete waste of time. I have uploaded all my documents but still after a two weeks gone and my documents not verified by your team. The interface was clunky and confusing, and it kept crashing whenever I tried to input my information. I couldn't even get past the first screen without encountering an error. Save yourself the trouble and steer clear of this app.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Good work;", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The processing of the documents is very slow.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It keeps on getting logout after a few minutes...very frustrating", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Best blocked account provider, all process happened quickly, thanks to Expatrio team.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I don't recommend this company I have activated my blocked account, but i didn't receive my money, After many complaints, all they did was pin the problem on their partner Mangopay, who sometimes did maintenance and sometimes said we were investigating the story. Two weeks ago until today, 3 payouts from my account have been missing", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Won't let me login in any kind of way, despite it's perfectly fine on the browser.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Application is very slow.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Same for me like everyone, when you try to activate your account it doesn't work, fix your bug! i need my money", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I can login to the website but can't login to this app even though I'm using the same credentials. How am I supposed to unblock my account now? Expatrio support is pathetic.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Thank you for super fast process. (5 🌟) But this app is slow... Work on it... Still I give 5 🌟 bcz of super fast process like account of opening and money transfer and easily download documents.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am very disappointed with the expatrio service. I block the money and have been trying to unblock it for the last one month. I contacted customer service also. I am continuously getting a problem for unblocking. I am in germany, and have to borrow money from friends for expenditure, even though i have money.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Many thanks to Expatrio", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "App is broken. Fraudulent company. They are not releasing monthly payouts!! Activation is what they call fraud. Dont put ur money here", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Dont recommend at all. After 9 months of monthly payouts they decide to change some terms and conditions so now people have to go through the hustle of updating everything again or else they won't process your own payment which is from your own money. If a company changes it's terms and conditions and they cannot even transfer your data on their own safely to the another firm just because they have affiliated with that firm then I don't know what they are doing as a firm.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "DON'T USE EXPATRIO Worst and slowest customer service If any mistake happened they will try to steel your money!!!", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Poor app , also poor service , if you go their Berlin office for help regarding your blocked account they will not help you. Looks , your money is with them and they don't know about anything. One more thing, when application is poor as we know but , website is also useless because you can't activate your booked account. Berlin office people don't about theirs own services and they will help you in anyway. I'm very disappointed from Expatrio.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "App doesn't allow me to even upload the documents to verify and receive my monthly payouts", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Terrible when the company forces you to use this unfinished app to activate the blocked account and It ISN'T WORKING then you CANNOT GET YOUR MONEY", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Very bad app not able to upload documents. Activation of the account is not possible. Expatrio do not provide other options to upload documents. The blocked account will remain blocked and the students are losers. Very bad experience. The support is bad. The customer care will blame the user for the drawback of the app. No reply for emails. Strange company.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Not able to upload files. Very very bad app", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Worst customer service", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Application has lots of bags and fails during operations.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Everything is a mess if you apply insurance with Expatrio and I couldn't reach them on call. Even though I gave my address in insurance application they changed my address to their address while submitting to the Insurance company.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "After the recent update the app shows a \"no Internet connection\" on a wifi network, it only works on mobile data now.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It really is a clunky app. The service itself is okay but the app is slow, not responsive and feels outdated", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Very slow response", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Terrible experience !!! Very poor customer service. I've emailed them and I've been waiting for my blocked account activation for over a month and these guys cannot even give an update on it. If you're reading this, don't go with this provider. Choose coracle it's way better.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "when the time came to activate my Blocked account there were so many issues. There was some update preventing me from activating my blocked account. They said 24 Hours was the waiting time but its been 3 days.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Good for students for blocked account, Works smooth", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Its very annoying that the service is very bad and you will regret taking them.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "No trouble with the app, just with the company itself, specifically the bank that they are using for the blocked accounts, monthly payment is delayed for more than 2 business weeks so far, support is kind but will only tell you to wait. I personally recommend any other alternatives for the blocked account, instead of getting financially screwed out of nowhere.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Unable to login to the mobile version!!", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I can login through the web but not able to login through app with same username and password.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Couldn't login and no message explaining what the problem is", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I can login through the web but not able to login through app with same username and password. Finding difficult to activate my blocked account.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The blocked account opening and find transfer was hassle free. Best service provider for blocked account.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Referral reward is scam", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I can login my account from the app but i can't login from my web browser... What seems to be the problem?! Any help", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "its imposible upload my passport photo, I tried with diferents device and had the same error. 😖", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "This is responsive version of web portal. App level smoothness awaits. But, MVP is great. Waiting for newer versions.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Nice app and easy to use", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Easy to use and nice design.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "1 month already & my money transfer hasnot been approved yet😢", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Bad customer service, very late replies", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "By far one of the worst services I have ever used. The customer care is functionally useless. I have an outstanding request that has not taken four months to be addressed, and no resolution yet. They are genuinely lucky as a foreigner, you don't have much choice once you are locked into a blocked account, I suspect this is how they have managed to retain several of their customers. Look somewhere else for better services, a mattress bank might even perform better than what they have to offer.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Very disappointing experience with Fintiba. They charged fees without clear explanation, even after I asked for clarification. More importantly, the monthly payments were delayed, which goes against the core purpose of the contract. Very poor transparency and reliability. I cannot recommend Fintiba.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The worst company ever...", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Finitba Support service does not exist. About 10 emails have been sent, multiple messages to irresponsible AI chats, 4 or 5 attempts to call - all these have never ever been responded by Fintiba. So disrespectful behavior for the service that is aiming to manage blocked account money transfer for international students in effective manner that is so important to obtain visa D in the short period.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "even though i have transferred the money from over one month and a half from a german bank account i still haven't received the blocking confirmation i need for my visa. i have already had an appointment at the german embassy and they gave me around two months deadline to send the blocking confirmation but because of the delay from them i will get my visa rejected because i didn't send the document in time . i tried emailing them but they didn't help at all .", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Very bad exp infact worst the support never replies the employees never reply they don't send required doc's all they know is just to ruin your visa appointment.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Complete service breakdown. Avoid. Last year this service was good, but this year it is a total disappointment. The app is completely malfunctioning. Customer support is nonexistent. it took them an entire month to reply to my June inquiry, and their hotline leaves you on hold for over 40 minutes with no answer. I submitted an urgent payout request with my Berlin immigration documents on July 18th and am now facing a financial emergency because my funds are locked without any response. Terrible.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "worst customer support. the tickets never get answered and they hang up after they hear you speaking english", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "i have been trying to close my acc and recieve my money back for more then 6 months support team never respond for like 2 3 months they told me the account will be closed in 1 month max and then they never reply again phone support couldnt even locate my account ask me to wait another week and then call again and send another mail", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "very bad experience, no support and no response. it is a scam, don't use it. use only Expatrio.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I had problems with my last payout, Fintiba didn't send it, and since 10 days I sent them emails which they didn't reply to, and called them but the costumer service were not helpful at all and didn't understand the problem and kept telling me to wait day by day, and now I try to call them, they don't answer. They even cut the monthly 5 euro from my payout, in which they didn't send, ans was supposed to be the last. You don't feel safe at all with a service you can't reach to.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Very weak technical support I have been reporting the same issue for more than three weeks now, and nothing has been fixed. Every time I contact support, they just tell me “next week” and nothing actually happens. For a financial service that students fully rely on, this level of technical support is unacceptable. I hope the team takes user issues more seriously and improves their response time.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I felt like a scam. Weeks to wait for a reply, no phone calls are working, difficult to Identify ID. Hidden fees also. My friend stuck with his account for 3 years and deducted monthly. I don't recommend it for Block Account when you are planning to come to Germany. Actually this is a Zero Star review.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "they have the most bad and ignoring support around the world", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "worst service ever it's been 2 months since I arrived in Germany still didn't get money I wish I had option to upload proof these people they don't care about you if you call them they will give wrong information most of time and I have proof for it. And there is been a ticket which is I'm high priority from 3 weeks still no reply if I call the person will be like I can't do anything sorry you have to wait. My friends from other providers have got the money that day itself. I can'teven pay rent.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Worst customer service when in Germany. Already been a month since my visa and still can't access my money from the account. I think they withhold money as long as they can, in order to make whatever measly interest they can!!!!", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "from 30/4/2026 i procced for my blocked account closure , today is 21/5/2026 still waiting for my vertification , without saying anything if my paper all in good condition or something is missing , and i most leave germany before the end of the month , the support team just tell me on telephone everything is fine just wait.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "SO bad experience with finteba please don't download or don't block amount with finteba it's world worst app I have block an amount with finteba and than I want to withdrawal my amount so now they are not releasing my amount and when I complaint to hem they sa just l little bit wait we will release amount from after two months they are not giving a clear answer", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Worst customer service ever. I have already completed all the required steps for unblocking. It has been 2 months now, no feedback, emails go unanswered, migration from Sutor bank cancelled, so much risks and lack of transparency. Despite these steps being finished I am still unable to receive my payouts yet I need to pay rent.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Terrible service. Never replies to emails...when we manage to connect phone calls, they tell you wait for the email replies. They try and hold the money as long as they can without releasing it to the customer(probably for the measly interest they can get out of it)!!", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "don't open your account in fintiba", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The worst. Support system sucks", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "worst support system, have sent them an email but its been days and they haven't responded anything. I'm out of money now and waiting for their response.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Monthly payout is late and customer service cant do shite and ask to \"wait\" but its already a week", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "kharaaaaaaa application zany w rabyy tal3 den omy", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Worst flicking experience on OTPs so far. It does not send OTP codes", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "the worst app and service I have come across my entire life. the app doesn't respond and capture anything properly and need to wait atleast 10 minutes to Connect to an agent and whom doesn't have time to even get to know whats the real problem is. their email support doesn't even respond maybe you will get email saying thank you for your mail we get back to you. I am really disappointed, I wish I could have any other app instead of this one", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Dear team, Initial set of concerns have been highlighted via email. Appreciate if response / resolution can be provided in 2 days.Kindly revert if more than 2 days is required for the same", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "service client 0 3 months after requesting partial refund No response", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "app became completely unusable", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "worst service ever", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The app is not secure anymore after recent updates. I activate biometric however it does not work. The app does not require any pin or fingerprint before signing in. So I just can't keep it in my phone.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I absolutely hated my experience with this app. If you have another option to use please pick the option. Their customer care services are horrible. They take literally months to review documents even after they tell you it will take 11 days. They take too long to show reflection of the money in your blocked account. Stay away from this app! It's just filled with problems and it's so difficult to use. Never using it again", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Customer support is really awful I emailed 3 Times for account closure they have not even replied once and there is no option to close account in Application or on website", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Using Fintiba was the worst mistake I could have done. I needed to open my blocked account asap and decided to use fintiba instead of expatrio, the money took 2 months to get into the account, since I needed the blocked account urgently, after three weeks with the very poor costumer service assuring me that the money takes 2 weeks top, I decided to use expatrio, the money got into my account in 3 days there, using the same method. it's been 6 months and I still haven't received my money back.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "hi, when I requested to recover my password, you sent me an email containing a field in which I'm required to enter a verification code, the point is I got no code whatsoever nor am I able to interract with said field, in fact the field resembles a static image more than an interractive widget, could you please fix the problem? and thank you", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Extremely disappointing experience. I closed my account and was informed that my refund would be processed, but the money was delayed for weeks without clear communication. I had to send multiple emails just to get basic updates, and even then responses were inconsistent and slow. I would strongly advise students to think carefully and be prepared for long delays and poor support if issues arise.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "employees when you need to make a video call are uncooperative and unfriendly. They often just hang up if you ask them to repeat the question. If i had the choice to use another bank i wouldn't hesitate. very bad and I'm very upset with them. zero stars 0", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "if you're coming to Germany from a developing country and you know what's good for you, avoid fintiba like a deadly plague. you'll thank your stars you found this review", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The app kept removing €4.90 every month until about €300 or even more was removed from my account over a period of 5 years. This is broad day th*ft. While trying to process my visa I didn't know I had falling short of the intended amount needed and I wasn't given any notification from the app. I regret ever using the app and If it's possible to give less than 1 star would gladly do... If your country delays in processing your papers please run from this app. They will milk you off completely", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "This new update is not it; there was no proper testing done before release. 1. I tried Changing monthly payout- my balance was reduced and I was asked to transfer more money, like it was my initial transfer. 2. Reducing the monthly payout back to the original amount - I got a new blocking confirmation and surprisingly another deduction. 3. Trying to contact customer support- after chatting with the bot and clicked on \"my problem was not solved\" it took me to a nonexitable black screen.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "An annoying app—it asks for tons of documents and paperwork just to use it, and the whole process wastes a lot of time. It's ridiculously bureaucratic.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have been directed to update the app but after updating I am still being requested to update again when I open the app", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "your App is not working and stuck on login page", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Don’t fall for their “free travel insurance, phone number, technical support” — it’s a scam. I’ve been in Germany since October 2 and still can’t access my money because their system can’t send a simple code. A week has passed, and support keeps contradicting itself. In the end, you’re left without help or money. This is by far the worst possible option for a blocked account. If you don’t want to ruin your first weeks in Germany, stay as far away from this useless organization as possible.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "It’s been over a week and the verification code issue still hasn’t been solved. I can’t access or use my money because of this problem, and it’s really frustrating. As a new user, I expected faster support since people often need their funds urgently to cover important commitments. Customer service keeps saying “we’re trying to fix it,” but nothing changes — every day there seems to be a new issue. Very disappointing experience so far.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "If you are coming from a Developing Nation (High risk county), better not use this app. There are far better apps than Fintiba. They will ask you for 1000+ documents and not accept your documents until they are European standards. The embassy asks for less documents than Fintiba does. And they do not understand that every country has a different set of rules and regulations. Until and unless all the documents are up to their requirements, your own money gets stuck with them.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Support is super slow. Hard to make any changes with your blocked account.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Hi Fintiba Good Bank", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "worst experience ever,,, they are verifying my passport from 1 week... if you are about to open block account plz go with coracle", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Worst bank. I don't advise anyone to use it. They cancel your 'free' travel insurance coz I didn't activte my pyouts and claiming that they set me three warnings , Lies. Plz stay away and use other banks.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Terrible customer support team! Been communicating with them for over three weeks, and not even one single question or inquiry was solved/answered. Terrible!", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Es war eine sehr enttäuschende Erfahrung, ein Konto bei Fintiba zu eröffnen, und ich bin überhaupt nicht zufrieden! Ich habe vor einem Monat ein Konto bei Fintiba erstellt und seitdem wurde meine Bestätigung nicht ausgestellt. Ich habe mehr als acht offizielle Kauf- und Verkaufsdokumente übersetzen lassen, aber sie verlangen weiterhin den Nachweis der Herkunft des Geldes. Wie kann ich Ihnen den Goldkauf beweisen, den ich vor mehreren Jahren in bar getätigt habe?", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Couldn't open the app most of the time, it always shows errors while logging in on both application and website. Terrible experience.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "November 2023, fintiba took €120 from my blocked account money, refused to render the service, then returned the remainder after 1 month of refusing to answer my emails", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "November 2023, 16 months since fintiba illegally took €120 from the money I sent for my blocked account and then returned the remainder a month afterwards. Coracle later helped me open a new blocked account afterwards. Unfortunately, I know no German authority to report this incident to because I am a Nigerian living in Germany", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Support is not upto the mark. You wont get bank transfer related queries properly answered. Some of the support team member's responses are pathetic.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Does not allow me to upload document. It says \"Media library permission denied! Please enable it at settings\". In settings I gave it all permissions, it says \"no permissions denied\"", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Looks helpful, but execution is not as good as advertised. Looks monopolizing and commercialize overseas students management (with opaque fees etc), but no real good service. And if you need help, respond will come in 3 working days. Students are in need of support, they paid, and some processes cannot wait, and blocked by this service. This service should not be recommended as official German (education) service. I've seen similar negative comments. With questionable positive reviewers.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I wish i could give you guys negative star. Your service is slow and the hidden things are a surprise.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have a very bad experience with this bank i had a blocked acc with them to study in germany and my pay out is delayed for more than 20 days for no reason", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Is not fast or easy to use", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Very bad experience..we did insurance for 2024 but they did for 2025 ..for this fintiba mistake we suffered too much..expatrio is best..", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "App is not always responding", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "For me it was a waste of time. There was no money transfer tool in the app. I've clicked the help button. It was just an algoritmic help tool. It told me that fintiba transfer button could not be seen before the account had been created successfully. But I had already received both a mail and the app notification that says that my account had been created succesfully and ready to transfer.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Terrible app won't even let me login for the first time it says update available even tho there is no update", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Verification takes too much time", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Very bad experience with the customer service ,and the service they give is so limited .iam really dissapointed ,i lost my appointment in the immigration authority because of their mistake", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I can't login", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "app keep crashing again and again sometimes remains login for few hours there is no logout button too.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The app always gives some error. It does not work smoothly", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Poor and rude customer service and help center. No action taken on urgent actions such as confirmation.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Dear Team, The application isn't allowing me to login to my account. I have tried reinstalling and yet it's the same.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Can't even login! The apps throws a time out error saying I need to update it even though I have installed the latest version. These Germans are way behind in terms of tech in apps , even though they claim to be an advanced country.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "M unable to opn fintiba app ......nd unable to access my account", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The app says to update and when I'm clicking on the button, it is redirecting me to Google Playstore, but there is no option to update the app. I am unable to access the app. Please help urgently.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Worst service ever!! Find another service if possible. I asked for a refund and no one gets back to you and their service is so slow. Stay away from Fintiba!!", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "They have the wrost ever customer support. I emailed them an weeks ago of my interview to update my documents. They auto reply my email and give you fake hope. Their email support wrost ever. Never recommended to anyone again to use their service.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Fintiba app is not opening It just says update available while there is no update available. I uninstalled the app and installed it again a couple of times, but nothing happened..", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I don't know what happened to my fintiba. It asks me to update the app while opening it. But there is no updation in the playstore. Now I cannot open fintiba and access my account. I'm totally helpless.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I don't know what happened to fintiba. I have transfer my money to fintiba but it's not showing on my account. I called them but the call center people are rude. Now i have no money and no residence permit. Feeling helpless.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "They didnot have patience when they didnot know how to speak.After that, they hung up the phone and did not the number. They don”t give me what I a tan number need.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Customers service is extremely bad and they ain't helpful..", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "horrible costumer service ! over charges clients ! and don't get me started on Mawista insurance", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Unable to open the app. Says 'Update Available' and redirects to playstore even though I'm using the latest version.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Terrible app, terrible company, horrible staff and I hope they don't survive the recession.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The customer service is very poor. instead of solving problem they just send emails that don't help at all.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I couldn't open my account because it's asking me to update the app yet I couldn't update the app because it's only giving me option to uninstall.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The process of giving them money is as fast as a finger snap, now if you want to talk to someone, NOBODY IS THERE TO ANSWER YOU, you want to talk to support? NOPE, there's just a broken piece of chat but with only written answer boxes and if you write anything else the chat bot breaks for 2 days and you receive no help when there are errors in the program. My experience with this app was of sewage.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "This company will leave you in a bad state", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Very very bad ,i do not recommend dealing with them I am waiting for the approval to open the closed account from you for a month and until this moment I did not get an answer", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Don't use it. Worst service ever, there are other options (blocking account)", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am in germany since 3 months. Fintiba team has enter my date of arrival in 2023 So I am not receiving my payouts automatically at the end of month as my payouts dates are showing as 11.09.2023. It's toomuch Because of wrong arrival date enter by some of employees of Fintiba and I am not getting my ownmoney. Every time I called Fintiba team they told me They have send my request to back office and it will be solved. It has been 3 months I don't know when \"BACKOFFICE\" will change my arrivaldate", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Never ever use this company. I have been trying to get access to my money for like a month already. Illiterate workers barely speak English and absolutely do not do their job. They always say that they would do something but eventually nothing happens. Today I called them 3 times. First time the kept me on hold for 5 minutes and never came back, the next person just hung up the phone when I was explaining my issue, the third person kept kept me on hold for 5 minutes and then hung up the call", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Poor Closure Service Unfortunately after the closure of the account despite the written promise to transfer back the amount in maximum of 2 weeks the company has not done it so far and they are still keeping my money against my will and against their promise. I do not recommend the service at all.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I waited 2 weeks until they informed me that the documents I sent was not verified and I needed to upload them again. In this meantime I asked them about my verification and did not even get a response only until a day before my visa application. Thanks for the great service and support. Thank god there was the other app lmao.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "After the update the app doesn't want to open!", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "app keeps crashing can't even manage to open it or login, updating it didn't help either.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The app does not open", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Unable to login after the update.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Used to be a great service. Now the app doesn't work propeely, the call-center representatives are of no help and the complain doesn't get resolved in the given time (3-5 business days) unless you make a lot of calls and beg them for some help", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Since the last update I'm unable to open the app, it crushes during launching every time. This is unheard of for a banking app, we need to be able to access our account at all times.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "There is a red rectangle in the middle of the screen and it does not dissapper. Holy .... you are funny xd", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The app keeps crashing as soon as I press the login button.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "App crashes frequently after the last update", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Before your last update everything was smooth. Now the application does not launch and immediately crashes. I cannot access my bank account and this is horrific", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "It's really frustrating to use this appp, I couldn't upload my passport copy and selfie photos, all my working end with timeout error, please help me to overcome this problem , I need urgently to upload my documents for passport verification.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The app can't start, it crach", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "App not working since last update", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "There's a crash in last version please fix it", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The app doesn't work after the latest update, always crashes", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "If you have an option don't take their service, their customer service is just horrrble. They won't reply to your email, keep your international call on hold, and force you to talk to a bot. I mean I had a small problem for which I wanted their attention for 2 minutes but couldn't get one.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Fraud app. I lost my money due to this app. Queries are answered as if they are system-generated. No proper support. I suggest everyone not to use this app.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "It Does not work in my Phone..", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I had the worst experience so far. Manually created health insurance and current account. Again and again I need to send a mail to support team for proper visa document. Once received only blocked account details and again after ping they sent attached health insurance documents with blocked account now my current account documents are not yet received.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The app is not opening in my phone. Kindly help to resolve the issue", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Whenever I open it and fill my email and password it crash. Was working well two weeks ago.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "One of the worst service I have ever got. I want to close my health insurance contract because I will arrive in Germany on June 2022. I already mailed lot of time to fintiba team but I they didn't help me yet. Very very bad service. Don't use fintiba as your block account or any service.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I want to close my block account due to refusal but when I want to attach my letter in close account section it is not working please help me", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I would suggest, not to go with fintiba. Customer support is poor, they don't reply for weeks. In application they would show you some random false data of yours and won't even correct it after complaining about it multiple times. Worst experience ever.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Filled my first name and surname just like in my passport but after completing every steps my whole name (first name and surname) is shown after surname. Blank for first name is empty. Does anyone know how to correct it.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Disgusting. Everything works very slowly but fine until you get to Germany and then they show you their true colours. It will take you ages to be able to access your our funds. If you want to be with them, be my guest but make sure you have additional funds to last you some few months. My rating will be negatively if that was allowed.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "One of the worst services you can use as a German international student. They have a bot as customer support and they rarely answer your queries if you forward to a human. Its been over a fortnight since I submitted my complaint and I'm being continued being charged despite not having entered Germany so far. If you're a potential international student, I would recommend you to look elsewhere. You'll thank me for it!", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "My app isn't working for several days. Whenever i open the app, it just stops Automatically, and nothing happens after. !!! Disappointing!", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am completely frustrated with the refund process with Finitba. I wired around USD $12900 for my brothers living expense into the blocked account with Finitba. However, my brother was not able to get the German Visa so we asked Finitba to refund the money back to the original account the wire came from. Now, they are asking to fill a reversal form and the reversal form states that they cannot send it back to the account in US. It asks for a correspondent bank in Europe (except UK). My bank stat", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am waiting from month but they can not transfer my payment back in my bank account .", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Tried 6 -7 times all the times it is crashing at the last page whilefilling the e mail id pathetic app horrible", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "App crashing on the last sign up page. Do not even waste your time. I've tried multiple times on multiple phones . Crashing everytime", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I can't sign up through the app! The app suddenly shuts down and closes when i type in my email ...", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Can't login using the app", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "How can i cancell the account and return all the money in the different accounts they were?", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Worst experience ever!! Everyone reading this please don't do my mistake", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Fintibot doesn't work as expected and causes more issues rather than resolving them.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "This is a terrible service.Takes a lot of unnecessary time (2 weeks while money is blocked) to set the account for blocked accounts for students and in the end does not pay you what it promises (your own money).and After the account is set up, instead of the 853 € monthly pay out, you'll get 848 €, the rest of it lost as some more \"fee\" or as i would call it robbery. I am extremely disappointed and dissatisfied with their system and honestly the only real bad thing i experienced in Germany.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "They charge 89€ for first time and then, every month 4.9€/month,, it's mean almost 150€ you have to pay them from your blocked money. So get ready for that .they should clear all this thing before opening account.if unfortunately your visa get rejected and you plan to keep your money with them it's stupidity because they will keep charging 4.9€ for nothing. Better to take it out keep in bank in your home country, till your visa arrive ,and earn interest from that money .best option is open in DB", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have created a new account but when I do I get my inncrct pswrd or incrct eml Why?", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Terrible using this app 😡 Why there is a pop up coming every time(There is a update) and in real there is no update. I have fully closed and reinstalled the app. I did it twice please solve this bug. This message should be on top priority. Help please and let me know 🙏", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have been trying to make a login account , but the app force closes whenever i type my email address on 4/4 page . It has happened 5 times. Please fix it ASAP.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Cant login even i didnt do anything. I have tried to login with my own password but i won't log in. I have reset the password twice and tried to login with reset password but still won't log me in. What should i do bro", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am trying to download fintiba app but it doesn't work. I tried alot but unfortunately I wasn't able to get it on my screen.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Always give me white picture with no access to the app dont know the reason", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have installed fintiba whenever I open the app goes to update when I press update the app is not showing any update please resolve the issue 04-11-19 Again facing login problem the is not login, you are requested please resolve the issues on top priority basis", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "It always give update app optine , while I have updated app", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Not recommended.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have already updated to the latest version, but the app kept asking me to do that and refused to be opened.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The app keeps telling me to upgrade when I already have the latest version!", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "This app always ask for updates and after taping on update it goes to google apps but there are no updates. Fintba app is making the users fool.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Eventhough I have an updated app, it is showing like update to latest version.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I had a bad experience with fintiba, when I arrived in Germany, the legitimazation documents given to me by fintiba was rejected by the postal bank and was given another form to present to a local bank. the process because quite complicated and took long, I runned out of money and could pay My rent or buy gloceries... I wont recommend fintiba", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I'm facing big problems with it😡, why this app is not openning. I need to log in to my account immediately 😡😡😡", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Damn it 😡😡😡😡😡😡😡😠😠😠", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "they have the most awful customer care ever. If you don't have to, never ever dont work with Fintiba. They just answer when they want to get the money, in other situations they answer you after so long time, and they dont care about customers at all.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "the app keeps crashing, I cant even login", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "its not even getting install. please help.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "always session expire. fake app", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "After I started using this app, I have understood that Germany desperately need software tech guys from India, such a poor app.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I'm unable to create my account and order the fintiba plus package, they always say email incorrect or reset password. What can I do I need to set up my blocked account", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have updated and is still not opening", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "this is the best app", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Fintiba services are all talk and no action! Ordered the sim card to my home country.... Never received it. They provide advice like doing rental deposit guarantee but don't inform you that you need to arrive and yourself up here first to get it. Sent my name incorrectly to the legitimatization company so my first payout was severely delayed. App sends same documents over and over, doesn't refresh properly.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "This app is confusing. I literally want to call it a scam. Why when i already set up everything for my first pay out, the app start crushing saying \"update available\" while actually there's NO update to do. Even on the website I am unable to log in. But that's not the worst... Those \"sudden\" fees they start to abduct from our money is NOT SERIOUS AT ALL !!!! They don't even advice us about that, like what??? I put a lot of money in there, this is so disappointing...", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Responses and services are good. But beware of their fees structure and hidden charges. There was an reduction of approx. 90 euros from my last month payout, when i contacted them they replied like it may be the fee deduction or difference from the first monthly payout(in my case both first and last payout amounts were same). They are already deducting fees from our payouts and calculations are not correct.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Whenever I try to open it...it often shows update, however when i try to update it automatically close...", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I can't open the app and there's no update too. What should I do?", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "After ur recent updates, I am unable to open my account on app or any browser. Even after update ur application is still showing \"UPDATE AVAILABLE\". I needed fintiba urgently and here I am waiting for it to start/login from last 4 hours. And what is with the crashing thing , app crashes in middle. I know you will say that please raise a ticket and share your concern- but you guys reply after a period of 5 days. This is something becoming unbearable. Please 🙏 do something about this.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "At the beginning, the app was working perfectly but now I can't login because the page doesn't appear. Tried to login using a browser but no results for the \"my fintiba login\"...what is going on?", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "account not opening for many hours. When logged in from pc, it says page not found and from mobile app the fintiba logo keeps on revolving", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "update problem.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Most of the times when I open the app they say update required although the update does not exist", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "the app always closed by itself when i try to do something in it", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have successfully registered on Fintiba and intend to create a blocked account with the monthly deposit amount of 1,030 EUR for three months (a total of approximately 3,090 EUR). However, I am unable to complete the process because the \"Transfer Document\" cannot be generated or downloaded from my dashboard.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "l have experience flexibility in the use of this app.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Okay", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "unable to get through to the help desk,I have some questions", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Their charges are too much", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I thought to give 4 stars but when I update this app, it takes more times to be updated , it stock at 87% while updating.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "App is working fine. But my doubt is why does it takes finitba agents 4-5 working days to get to us with the solution. Like my condition is urgent and need immediate remedy (like visa on hold immediate). Finitba team please reply fast. Query is raised from the same email id. Thanks", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "recent update is keep carshing..", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The app keep crashing every time i try to open it", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have one issue , yesterday the blocked amount was transferred to my account and an email sent to me by fintiba regarding payment transferred also i had seen that the amount was shown in my account yesterday but today when i logged into my account my current balance is showing zero 🥺 what is this? When my money is arrived in my account why the app is showing zero balance? They are asking for the next process which is to provide the sources of fund that's okay but why my money is not showing?", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "App continually crashing at the last page of the sign up page, halfway through entering email address. Tried with 3 android phones , same result. Edit , as the developer promptly mentioned , you can use the website for sign up. The app still is unresponsive but at least you can do the job. Of course I'll make it 5 stars when the new app update comes.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Vielen Dank fürs Update!", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Good", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Since i updated, the app automatically shuts down when i open up.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The app was good before now, presently asking you to update without no updates. Can't open it on my phone. I reinstalled and the present persists.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "the app is refusing to upload 3 photos of my passport !!! the next day i recieve a verification failure with a note (please upload all 3 photos of the passport). please fix this issue", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Good", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The app keeps crashing on me when I am at the visa application tool, and I cannot continue. And also I do not have a TIN and I select the option that I do not have it, and yet it still says I must put in my TIN.", "p": "google_play"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I’ve tried the call in different languages to validate/activate my blocked account and just the attendant was listening me. I deleted the app and tried again but it doesn’t work at all.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "They’re not returning my money and rejected my id verification", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "They forced me to hace a german phone number to receive my money. They didnt tell me this in advance, only by the time i want to activate my account.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Easy but comes with a price, bad costumer", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "In iPhone can’t forget my last Login and cannot Login new Account", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "各种技术问题都弄不好，app都无法视频认证，你做毛的保证金担保账户啊，德国都是按月扣钱的，账户没钱要交很贵的手续费的，就你们这水平赶紧黄了算了", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am trying to activate my blocked account, but cannot click on \"activate\" button. Can't close a window, just getting a black page.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The identification process can never start after you clicking the button when you have a good network and give all the permission to them.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "You should do this verification process before talking the customers money, not after getting the money and when they want release the money. Due to your technical fault I had gone through huge difficulties and had to wait 2montjs to unblock the money.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Solo entro 1 vez al mes y todos los meses hay un problema diferente con esta cuenta, piden los mismos documentos una y otra vez, no hay servicio al cliente. Y lo más frustrante es que no hay más opciones!", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "★☆☆☆☆\n\nMy experience with Expatrio’s customer support has been extremely disappointing.\n\nMy residence permit documents have already been approved, and I received an email stating that I could proceed with the video identification process. However, the app still shows that my documents are under review and continues to request additional uploads. Because of these contradictory statuses, I have been unable to complete the activation of my blocked account.\n\nI contacted customer support and explained that the matter is urgent, as I depend on the monthly disbursement to cover my living expenses and pay my university fees. Despite waiting several business days, I have not received any response and support.\n\nAs an international student, access to these funds is essential. Delays and unclear communication in such an important process create unnecessary stress and financial difficulties.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "wth do i have to do with this bs? i’m a student in Germany for 2 years already. this is ridiculous", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Terrible bank. Zero communication. They only communicate via email, and their responses are either extremely slow or they don’t reply at all. They never solve problems. Terrible staff. I absolutely do not recommend them. They will literally drive you insane.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I’m absolutely dissaponted for their service, for 3 months they can’t approve my verification, which is absolutely on their side they can’t fix. They already change their contact person and I every time have to explain everything from the beginning, and they keep giving me generic response. After 3 months I still have no access to my money, I live in Germany for many years, before that I was using Fintiba, and this time I decided to change to Expatrio because of their lower fees and I think I made a big mistake.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Not good at all.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The app is heavy as a truck", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "This app is forcing you to get value package eventhough you need only the blocked account # in the desktop you will find blocked account only feature but in phone app you don’t find it and it just like promoting their value package  #cannot change an application when you start it  #horrible customer service # no reply at all only chatbots", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "He escrito numerosos mails sin recibir ayuda alguna como estudiante. Sigo esperando por alguna respuesta, mi situación es urgente porque no tengo acceso a mi cuenta bancaria!!!!!!!!!!!!!!", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "When these people need you to sign up for their services, they will haunt you with emails and reassuring messages but when you sign up and you need them to simply respond to a make something clear, they’ll ignore you like a boyfriend or girlfriend who has ghosted you. DO NOT TRUST THEM! I REPEAT, DO NOT FALL FOR THEIR TRICKS!", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "after doing a transaction i cannot even download the document i needed. It has some critical bugs. Very few features yet none of them are fully functional. If I did not need this bank account immediately I would never use expatrio banking. I can not even make sure the money has transacted or not. Also I made insurance with TK using expatrio and Expatrio kept saying there was a mistake on TK side and my insurance has been cancelled. I was really stressed. Then I went to TK's office to ask about this situation and they told everything was OK and nothing was canceled. The problem was related to Expatrio's system and it took too much effort to fix this since I was not in Germany back then. \n\nVery problematic system and app.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Hesap açılışta zaten müşteri hizmetlerine ulaşamadım. \nBu yüzden çok pahalıya parayı transfer etmek zorunda kaldım.\n2) hebin aktifleşmesi yine problem sistem hataları oluyor müşteri temsilcisine ulaşana canınız çıkıyor günler alıyor ve sizin sorununuzun çözümu del genelde yazdıkları. \nParanız gelir ama gecikmeli. \nPara havale edersiniz paranın hesabiniza yansimasi zaman alir. \nSistem surekli her ay hata veriyor hatayi çözmeye çalışırken yine günler geçiyor paranizi alamiyorsunuz. Kira ödemeniz için buna ihtiyaciniz var ise ev sahibiyle sorun yaşamanız kaçınılmaz. Kartlarını kullanim dedim 10€ hizli teslimat ödedim, 3 gün içinde teslim etmeleri gerekirdi; 10 gündür kart yok. İptal edin iptal edemeyiz. Hiçbir taahhütlerini yerine getiremeyen, sürekli sorun yaşatıp, muhattap bulamadığınız bir yönetim.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "What a stupid app. If someone comes to Germany for the first time, how do they expect them to already have a residence permit?\n\nI tried to open a bank account with them, and they asked me to do verification via the post office. We went there and completed it. After that, there was an option to pair my blocked account with the bank account. But whenever I click pair, it just redirects me back to the home screen.\n\nBecause of this, I also don’t have the option to add another bank account. I already opened another bank account with a different bank, and now I’m completely stuck.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "This buggy app and system keeps resetting my activation process. The support team is useless as they are unable to activate my account even after I provided solid proof of my case ID and Postident verification. On top of that, they take forever to respond to a support ticket. 3 days no response while they claim to reply within 1 business day. \n\nHow is a simple activation taking so long? I was forced to physically visit the post office multiple times while the activation kept failing again and again. Imagine the frustration, being new to a place and trusting a provider with so much of your money, all to receive no support at all. \n\nPlease save yourself the headache and do not use Expatrio to hold your money, especially if you are new to a country as a student and all your money is stuck because of a buggy app, system and slow support team.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Thanks to this, I couldn't register for school and I failed to apply for a visa. The opening of an account that takes 1 day or 3 days at the latest has been less than 9 days, and even if the insurance is approved, it has not been transferred to the school, so it is not possible to register. The inquiry comes a day later and it's uncomfortable because the automatic response comes first. I don't recommend it unless you have a lot of time. You may not even be able to start studying abroad just because of this application.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "难用，态度差", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Expatrio’s sign-up flow for a blocked account makes it very hard to opt out of their free bank account. It then becomes very difficult to complete the blocked account set-up process. \n\nAlthough they have a team staffing chat support, the world’s dumbest chatbot will make it extremely difficult to reach them unless you start “shouting” in all caps and cursing. This is sadly more and more the case with e-services. It does not inspire confidence.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "In my personal experience, Expatrio’s entire verification and activation process has been needlessly complicated, buggy, and incredibly frustrating. What should be a simple setup ends up taking days or even weeks because of how poorly their systems are built.\n\nThe video verification was a disaster. The agent could not hear me, forcing me to restart the process several times. When I finally managed to complete it, my account still didn’t update. I had to redo the whole thing more than once just to get it to show as completed.\n\nThen came the document upload. You would think it would take a few minutes to verify your documents, but instead it takes days without any clear communication while you’re stuck waiting.\n\nThe device pairing is where things completely fall apart. No matter how accurately you enter your information, the pairing simply does not work. At one point it even said my device was successfully paired, only for it to revert back to not paired the next time I logged in. It honestly feels like the entire platform is held together with DUCT TAPE AND LUCK.\n\nCustomer service is slow and unhelpful. When they finally respond, they just repeat basic information you can already find on their website while ignoring the actual issue you’re dealing with. It feels like they are not properly reading your messages.\n\nOverall, the whole process has been incredibly disappointing and stressful. Expatrio’s systems are unreliable, their app is broken, and their support is ineffective. Based on what I have gone through, I would not recommend using this service.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It is very bad for varification!!!", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It tricks people to open its bank account and the review of the activation lasts forever and get no progress and you get no replies on email. And you also cannot contact them through  phone-call because they don’t provide this service!", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Infact the staff who did the video verification with me was very disrespectful and such a person shouldn’t be kept in an institution like Expatrio. She was acting like she was tired of her job and didn’t want do it .", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "apps in ios 26 cannont connect with microphone even technically good check", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have been trying to verify my documents for the past 5 days now to be able to get my payouts . For the past 5 days I haven’t been able to verify, if I try video verification, I can’t hear them speak , I uploaded my documents twice (Anmeldung, Mietvertrag) Both were rejected while they were both listed as possible documents. I haven’t been essentially stranded and can’t get my payouts. I don’t know what kind issue is going but I desperately need help.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "WHY DOES THE APP REQUIRE 10 UPDATES PER WEEK? Seriously tho? Maybe hire better developers.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "My banking is blocked and I can’t access to my funds for 4 days I wrote 3 emails and there is no answer. What kind of a financial company doesn’t have customer support line, I cant find the number in their website. So if there is a REAL security problem why there is no email or sms to inform me about why my account is locked.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "A hundred people reply on rhe same email different things and the problem never gets solved", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Buggy, slow, can’t find transaction based on month. UI/UX design is bad", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Unclear information, money was deducted for the same content but many times, the staff intentionally did not explain clearly, intentionally beat around the bush. Really disappointed", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "En la mayoría de los casos funciona bien, me gustaría que dejaran de actualizar la app cada dos días pq es un incordio. Deberían tener más opciones de seguro de salud.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "This app required at least 9 updates per month. \nPlease fix this.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I definitely don’t recommend using Expatrio. Coming to Germany you have enough stress, but with Expatrio you need to deal with additional stress from the freezing app and not being able to get your money. If I could I would put zero stars", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Rezalet bir uygulama her gün güncelleme geliyor", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "As I found out that developer updated this app every few days, it became very annoying whenever I want to check my account but need to download the update. Also please fix background value caching, especially when we need to type bank account transfer address and switch the app, and suddenly what we typed before is gone", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am already in Germany and can’t pair my account. Expatrio do not help me to activate my account. I need money and I can’t get my payout.!!!!", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "excited to use Expatrio for my blocked account, but the experience has been nothing short of frustrating. The verification process feels outdated and unnecessarily complex. I have uploaded my passport photo more than three times, yet it keeps getting rejected. It almost feels like they are doing me a favor instead of providing a service that I am paying for.\n\nThe entire process is slow and inefficient, making me question whether they are truly operating in the 21st century. Instead of simplifying things for international students, they seem to create more hurdles. I sincerely hope they improve their system, but for now, I can only wish myself luck in getting my money into a blocked account.\n\nIf you are considering Expatrio, be prepared for delays, repeated document submissions, and a lot of unnecessary drama.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It is always deleted all of the information i wrote for transfer when i press home button. Please fix it", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Terrible costumer service i definetly not recommend Expatrio go for other solutions it took almost a week took to get answer by costumer services. Also they are not solving anything just empthy answers.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "So I've been trying to get verified. The first \"verification expert\" didn't understand how light works and couldn't see the watermark on my passport, even though I told her she needed to turn off the camera's light so I could hold it against the light and make it visible. Next she wasn't able to send the code so she tells me to exit the app and do it again. It is been more than 2 hours and I can't get another person to answer.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Please add basic banking features for tracking spending according to categories like groceries, rent, etc.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "If you can't create an app, please just bring back the options on your website. Nothing works on this app, couldn't ipen a blocked account already for teo months and customer support don't answer me or when they do they're just useless. I have all the neccesary documenta ready but can't upload them. Just don't trust this company at all.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am trying to reach support team, but they haven’t respond me about one week.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have been trying to reach out to the expatrio customer support team for the last one week. \nI have facing issue accessing the funds and Expatrio team has not been responding to me.\nTerrible service!", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Die Leute im Online-Support sind sehr respektlos.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I’ve been trying for two weeks now to unblock my bank account and my app won’t let me because of an error, I keep trying to contact expatrio support but they haven’t answer my yet, this is almost my third week trying to use my bank account ://", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Worst experience ever been trying to activate my blocked account for days and no phone code is received although the phone number is correct! Please fix this", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have been trying to activate my account for a week now. Please, How do I provide proof of residence with KVR when I don't have money to pay for an accommodation? \nI cannot even increase the amount I get as my first payout. I sent a request that I could be I still cannot. \nPlease help. I am getting stranded here with no money but I have so much in my Expatrio.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Its 2024 and i have to get a code sent to my email everytime I try to log in.\n\nFace Id  is not available!", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I was using expatrio 3 years ago and I did all of my jobs easily. Right now, I needed to use it again. It is terrible. It requires to send visa dokument but there is even no button on the page??? I sent an email, they did not even care about it, they said please upload it in mobile application. There is no BUTTON. And making id identification was another big problem. I had enough internet connection but people who I am trying to connect refused and closed connection immediately bu saying check you internet connection, they did not even try 4 seconds. \n\nI do not advice anybody.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "So slow service. No any customer care. They are not even ready to help their customers. Extra Charges are there. So I will suggest you go for other service providers but not with this.\nThey have very worst service I have ever experienced.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Sehr schlechte Service, wenn es für Deutschlernende entwickelt, sollte es Arbeiter geben, die mit Leute Deutsch sprechen können! Man findet sehr schwer und langsam Arbeiter, die hilfsbereit sind! Sehr unzufrieden!", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I can’t restart my identity check with IDnow but the app won’t let me change my identity verification check to PostIdent. And customer support cant give me an estimate time period when can this be fix!", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "So many five star reviews but not a single person said anything about why they give five stars??? Maybe spend money into making sure everyone CAN LOG IN instead of getting all these fake reviews.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Hi i cant even log in in your app as a gmail account", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Expatrio Explained: Official time listed on Expatrio website for a transaction is 3-5 days. It’s been 9 days excluding the weekends and there is no sign of where my money is gone. Now calling Expatrio and they never pick my call anymore or send me to a recorded line. It seems they have no idea what to do so they noted my number and now not answering. I am lost and not sure what to do. Have send them email too but no response. I feel like I am being scammed and lost all my money. I need help please. Thank you!", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I opened an account here to sort out a blocked account for my German visa. \n\nThey provided me with the wrong IBAN code so I can’t transfer the money over. No in person customer service and the online help assistant took me round and round in circles without being able to provide information or the correct details so I can actually transfer the money. \n\nTime is of the essence and the best I was offered was an email address where they would reply in 3-5 working days. \n\nThe reply I got via email from their “customer support team” was from their chat bot providing the same general info saying have you read the FAQ.\n\nSo frustrating when time is important and you need things sorting quickly. It shouldn’t be this complicated to send money from one account to another. \n\nI am going to try elsewhere", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "執笠啦", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Complaint 1: The Blocked Amount provided by Expatrio does not comply with the official requirements for the German intensive language course residence permit. The actual legal requirement for 12 months is €13,094 (€1,091.17/month), as confirmed by the Munich Foreigners Office. \n\nExpatrio only allowed me to deposit €12,133. After transfer fees, the confirmation they issued showed just €11,904 (€992/month), which is below the legal threshold. You can verify this on their own calculator Expatrio's website. \n\nAs a result, the Foreigners Office contacted me, stating the amount was insufficient and requested an additional deposit along with a new confirmation.\n\nWhen I contacted Expatrio about the issue, they told me I had to extend the blocked amount and pay a mandatory €69 fee — a charge that would have been unnecessary if they had requested the correct amount in the first place. This feels like a fraudulent and unfair practice.\n\nComplaint 2: They also refused to refund the €69 “Initial Set-up Fee”, even though I activated all required products (bank account and Dr. Walter insurance).\n\nComplaint 3: Expatrio charges €10 for the debit card. You are required to use it once and activate it with a PIN before you can add it to your digital Wallet. However, even after following all the steps, it still can't be added to the Wallet.\n\nFinal advice: Think twice before opening your account with Expatrio. Poor compliance, hidden fees, and non-functional services are not what you expect when moving to a new country.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I’ve tried to activate my blocked account, but it’s been weeks but still problems, and there is no response from staff and Support Team. Email only replied by AI. Won’t recommend this app to my relatives", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Their customer care doesn’t reply", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "This app is not working properly. After I arrived in Germany, I tried many times to complete the ID verification process, but the app keeps showing popups and sending me back to the previous steps again and again. Because of this issue, my account activation is still pending. Very frustrating experience.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am very disappointed with Expatrio’s handling of my wife’s blocked account. Her visa started in June, but due to personal circumstances we could only travel to Germany in September. Despite this, Expatrio refused to release the monthly amounts for June, July, and August. They only released funds from September onwards, without giving any concrete reason or justification.\n\nThis is extremely unfair, as the money in the blocked account is our own and meant to support us during our stay in Germany. The lack of flexibility and transparency creates unnecessary stress for new expats who are already dealing with the challenges of relocation.\n\nTheir support team provided no clear answers and simply denied access to the funds which we rightfully deserve. I would caution anyone considering Expatrio to be very careful and to clarify all terms in detail before trusting them with your money.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Why would you want the user to force update every time they open the app ?", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Service is too worst! After getting my visa rejected I had applied for a refund and already completed all the process for refund and send a demand draft through a courier as per there mail after receiving demand draft they will share a stamp and sign letter which can be use for refund process they didn’t share any stamp and sign paper 1 week completed and also there is no one replying on phone calls and email.\nRequested you to do needful!", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I’m exaggerating but how many times are you updating the app in a week? May be thrice? \n\nIf I need to check something urgent then update pops up, it’s irritating", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Every time i open the app there is an update and i have to do it no matter what its so irritating", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "So I am currently in Germany. I am trying to activate the blocked account from last week onwards i submitted the documents at first. The app is so buggy the documents got submitted on their own I myself have no idea of how the documents got submitted. And the page at which the documents got submitted got lagged after which I tried to connect them with customer support which did not work wrote them a email on which I got a auto generated email which was of no use later on got a mail stating the documents were insufficient I then submitted all the required documents. After which I got the appointment to go to the nearest postident (post office) for the manual verification. I immediately went there and did the required procedure and it was done properly and submitted from their end after that I got a email from Expatrio on 14/03/2025 stating (You have unlocked your Bank Account. Start using your Bank Account to pay rent, do online shopping, transfer money, etc.) looking at the mentioned statement I thought it will be done maximum by Monday to Tuesday as 14/03/2025 was a Friday. Saturday, Sunday’s are non working days but today it’s Wednesday (((BUT WHERE’S THE MONEY AT) what should I transfer?????? I have not even got a single update on the mail that I have sent them poor customer service would not at all recommend anyone to go ahead with expatrio. As a customer I wanted to connect to the customer service agent had to go through the IVR(interactive voice response) which will give you options to dial 1,2,3 me assuming that I will get connect to the customer service representative did the process instead of me getting connected to the customer agent the IVR itself is answering me which is of at most no use at all the AI that assist you on the app as well show’s option frequently asked questions. When you put your own question I mean come on level up with the customer service and the AI. I have already paired my device. I also have a notification from expatrio stating (Device Paired Congratulations! You have successfully paired your phone.) still every time I open the app it tell’s me to pair the device when I click on it the screen goes no where. What should I do give me a resolution as soon as possible I am a student and I am in need of funds.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The Expatrio team does not care about you. They take their own time to reply. Blocked account money is taken fast but they fail to respond on the emails on time. Don't use their services. They don't have an office, no walk-ins, cannot call them. It's just a scam for all international students. Basically we should cry our blood before they do anything.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Support is worst nobody will respond, refund process will take hell lot of time its been more than a month still my refund status is not changed. They will reply to the mails for every 1week or 2week and sometimes more than 3weeks once. No one will support they have worst support system. I’m feeling like whether they will refund my amount (11lakh +)or not", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Don’t take this if you want open account you can easy open and you will credit in two day when you want close blocked account and you need funds back they will take more than 3 months and they won’t response properly to mails", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Always when I try to use this app, an unexpected error come up. Just for documentation I used this app. But if not, I’d rather prefer not to use it. And the help desk is not very useful", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "When I click on logout and unpair it keeps loading.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "There is a message saying that I need to update the app before opening it.\nHowever, even after updating, the same message keeps appearing and I am unable to open the app.\nI am having trouble because I need to make a payment.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Blocked Account 송금 모두 한 후 컨펌 서류 다운 받으려하는데 전혀 안되네요.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I feel like the service team is answer very lately nowadays, I had problem about subscribing insurance as my account error but the response was like after solve the problem.\nAlso now my block account not working so I couldn’t get monthly payout yet. Of course the service team not answer this time too. \nI can’t received my fxxking money", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I used the block account service, but the procedure for activating kept changing. Unstable technology didn't solve the problem, and it made me feel like they were keeping my money tied up on purpose. Support team only  gave me the stereotypical answers without solutions. I wasn't the only one, my friends had the same problems too.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The app doesnt work after logging in it just stays in a blank page, please fix it ASAP\nThank you!", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Abrir la cuenta bloqueada es un desafío y un desastre, necesitaras mucha paciencia y llevar mucho dinero extra por que esto puede tardar mucho", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Calendar picker is stuck.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Soo primitive for a banking app, feels like it’s from 2010’s. Wouldn’t recommend for daily use.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Why is this app so slow? I can not get in the blocked account page it does not open, it’s always loading. I think this have to be a helpful app but why it is making things harder than it is. I really did not like it. I apploded this app because I had to but even at the very beginning it caused problems. It should be fixed so that people can get the help they need.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Don’t create an Expatrio account. It is really big regret. And until your 12 months finish they at least take 1000 Euro from you. Account charge, creating account charge, tax, monthly charge, buffer charge, charge charge charge. Once you out money in their hand they just find unreasonable ways to cut of your money. And also they are really bad at costumer service. When you have problems you are stressing on your side but they answer you only via mails which takes weeks and, the answer going to be completely irrelevant to your question and problem. The only thing I can recommend you about Expatrio is stay away from it to be happy. Otherwise you will stress a lot suffer a lot and lose a lot money. They charge 69 twice for nothing. When l asked them about reason they answer me weeks later and says sorry it can happen sometimes. And sent my money back. I mean you need to awake and count all the penny you have otherwise they are stealing from you. I have conversations mails as a proof if in case they will deny what l am saying here", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I can’t update it and the app is full of bugs", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "You always have updates, and we need to make it manually, please change it to be automatically.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "You can’t see your old transactions in the app just a few about 10 , for me that’s not good , i tried to contact them to send me at least a bank statement to see when i spent my money but they didn’t reply to my email.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The worst customer support. Currently they are not checking the issue and not providing solution. The first thing to do is leaving the app. \nI cannot review my banking account from the brand new device. Not recommended.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I can not change my account in app, first i log in with my friends account after that i log out i couldn’t change account name. I deleted app a couple of times but every time that was my friends account, i couldnt change because app didnt let me. This is really bad app", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The App is problematic. When you come to download the 05 file, it is empty. There is nothing. If there is nothing, why does the download sign appear? When I click on help, I get an e-mail address. App is problematic. The message that appears on the first page: \"Aaaah! Something went wrong Brace yourself till we get the error fixed. You may also refresh the page or try again late.\" No one is interested. No Support. No one checks/follows up the problems in the app. I cannot find support in the app, When I search for Support on the web, YouTube comes up. They have put a lot of videos on YouTube. There is a person with a nonsense explanation. It's as if he is launching a shuttle into space to explain something that only takes three steps. A messy explanation. From topic to topic. \"No, I'll explain that later, no, I'll explain that here... .What are you talking about? Don't get into what you're going to tell next. I don't recommend it, stay away. It doesn't even deserve 2 stars.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Personally I’am not happy that I chose expatrio for my studies in Germany but I have to use it. And every time when i open the app i have to fill up all my information again. It doesnt remember even my email. I set up a code but it didnt work. It’s so annoying. There should be an easy log in option.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am trying to login, but it is not opening.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The payment partner they use for the blocked account payments (flywire/cohortgo) is awful. My payment was rejected and returned to my bank. When I asked why, they told me it was my bank’s error. Later, they said actually their bank rejected the payment but they are “not able” to specify the reason. I waited over 10 days for that nonsense response because it appears their support team is awful. Do yourself a favor and find a different blocked account provider.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It’s been a month since I registered in Germany and I cannot even access my money! I am just given an error message when I try to open my bank account! I completed all the verifications and just need to activate my bank account but it won’t let me!!", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "the app is ok, the problem is customer service and actually being able to use your blocked money! I have been trying to use mu blocked\nmoney for 10 months but the customer service keep emailing me un useful articles and do not solve my issue to be able to get money out! and it is still an ongoing problem. if you can use another platform do NoT use this", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Someone is pushing out updates with no checks. Cant get through account verification without a million bugs.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "This \"service\" is terrible. Submit bank statements instead. The bank account is a joke, won't let you see more than a few transactions. Statements only show your monthly blocked account transfer. Fee is ridiculous. No human help. When I arrived in Germany, took a week to activate. I had to open a different bank account to get money. Do yourself a favor and avoid!", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Can’t get help from actual humans. UI is awful. Can’t do anything from your computer.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am writing this review as a warning to any family member, parent, or sponsor planning to fund a student's blocked account through Expatrio. My experience with this company has been deeply unprofessional, financially draining, and psychologically exhausting.\n\nI transferred over €12,000 to support my sibling’s education in Germany. The funding process was dangerously easy—they accepted my money instantly without a single question. However, getting that money refunded has become a month-long nightmare of incompetence.\n\nThe \"Bait and Switch\" Experience:\nExpatrio is happy to take third-party funds (via Wise/Wells Fargo) to open an account, but when it comes time to refund that exact same money to the original source, they suddenly feign blindness.\n\nWhy This Has Been Torture:\nFor over 30 days, my sibling and I have been battling their support team to simply return my own money to me.\n* Forensic Proof Ignored: I have provided a complete, verifiable audit trail. I submitted my Wells Fargo bank statements side-by-side with the Wise transfer receipts. The dates match exactly. The amounts ($3,000 per transaction) match exactly. My name and address are on both documents.\n* Incompetent Review Process: Despite providing a \"1:1 correlation\" where I even highlighted the specific line items in yellow, their team repeatedly replies with generic copy-paste rejections claiming \"insufficient documents\" or that \"references don't match.\" It feels like no one is actually reading the files we upload.\n* Gaslighting: They keep telling us to \"refund to the student's personal account for simplicity,\" completely ignoring our repeated explanations that this is not an option for us.\n\nThe Bottom Line:\nThis company operates with a double standard: Zero scrutiny when taking your money, maximum obstruction when returning it.\n\nWe are not asking for a favor; we are asking for them to read standard financial documents (Bank Statement + Transfer Receipt) that prove the money came from me.\n\nIf you are a parent or sibling funding a student, do not use Expatrio. They will hold your significant capital hostage behind a wall of robotic support emails. We are now facing severe financial strain because they refuse to acknowledge plain evidence.\n\nTo Expatrio Management: Review case. Stop hiding behind \"insufficient docs\" and look at the evidence provided. Release my funds.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "When I was getting ready to move to Germany, this seemed like the perfect choice. I have had nothing but issues with them since I activated my account. For starters: THERE ARE NO HUMANS TO TALK TO. You have to send an email and then wait forever. There’s no emergency number when something unexpected, hard to explain, or confusing to put into a question comes up. It took them a month to actually grant me access to my funds. Now I’m at the end of my stay in Germany, and they automatically closed my account because they paid out all of the scheduled payments. I wasn’t worried about it because the notification said I could keep using my card like normal as long as there were funds available. They said they would charge 5 euros a month as a maintenance fee, or that I could extend my account, and that seemed fair, so I left it alone. I didn’t need to extend it. I had a little over 2k left in my account to cover my expenses until I moved. They closed my account in September. By October, I had 10 euros in my account as a buffer and absolutely no sign as to where the rest of my money went. I went to the chat bot for help (because you can’t call and emailing takes days and sometimes weeks), and it also was completely NOT helpful. Finally, I had to send an email to customer service and now I have to wait for someone to get back to me. In the meantime, I have no way of accessing MY MONEY and will have to figure out a way to feed myself for the next month and a half until I move. DO NOT GO WITH THIS BANK. ANYTHING ELSE HAS TO BE BETTER THAN THIS. IT’S THE WORST!", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Agree 100% with 1 star review. I‘ve tried to activate my account for the last 4 days. Nothing. Technical problems, no human response. Undecided to go ahead and proceed with the activation to the vesting my abilities bc I gave up on anyone answering my W9 tax question. I can only activate it on my phone, not sure why I can’t use my laptop. Once someone video called me, their connection was horrible, I could hear all them arguing, talking , but they couldn’t see me, and just like that hang up on me. So I tried to change activation method to post office, the app when blank and I did not get an email. At this point, not sure how I will get my money. Hope I don’t get a health emergency, sadly, I’ll need family support. Unbelievable, not one person has reached out. Email answered by a bot, phone number never answered, not a choice to leave a voice message. Service email is ALWAYS answer by a bot.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "DO NOT ORDER PHYSICAL CARD THEY CHARGE YOU TEN EUROS WITHOUT MAKING IT CLEAR AND EVEN WHEN YOU TRY TO CANCEL IMMEDIATELY THEY SCREW YOU OVER. DO NOT CHOOSE THIS COMPANY WHATEVER YOU DO", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I keep getting error messages and am unable to change some of my personal information and the correct arrival date in Germany. Plus, customer service is an AI-bot and it stinks! There is no HUMAN to contact. I would NEVER recommend Expatrio at all! I can’t wait to close this account!", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "While this service seemed all inclusive and super easy to use it has turned out to be the opposite. To activate your account you need a German +49 phone number. However, to get the phone number you need the IBAN from the bank account. This leads you in a never ending circle. After scouring their website for help I found their article on cell providers, and sure enough…they ALL require an IBAN to make the purchase. Until the either contract with a company to provide a German phone number upon entry to Germany, or change the requirement for the required phone number to activate the account with YOUR money in it I will be leaving a 1 star review and telling everyone to avoid this service if at all possible. After contacting customer support I got a silly automated message giving me the exact same information I already found in their website, and I doubt the human response is going to be much different. Extremely disappointed by a product that seems so amazing until I actually need it to do things and survive. I’m glad I’m not in a medical emergency, because you can’t use that either! Pathetic how they gloss over all of these details during the entire process until the very end when you need them the most.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The layout seems simple to use. I need to add money to my blocked account, and I read the tutorial online. I can’t find the option in my “user portal” to add funds to my account! I reached out via online/email, replying once as instructed and waiting patiently for email replies. I’ve been playing the email game for almost two weeks—but I want to get the ball rolling to get my temporary residence permit! I can’t do that without an updated amount to my blocked account. Now I have to extend the account longer to show I have the proper amount for 12 months!", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "This is a good product, but the update cycle is WAY too frequent. Every time I open the app it requires a new update. It’s massively hurting the usability of the app overall.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "too much errol", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "muốn chứng minh tài chính 12 tháng mà chuyển khoản xong lại bị hoàn về vì chỉ dc 9 tháng. làm hồ sơ gấp rút mà huỷ lên huỷ xuống mất hết cả thời gian", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "too much trouble, too much to ask for when i have sent important things. i find it wrong to use", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Opening a blocked account is quick, but closing one takes too long. I submitted the form over a month ago, but my account status hasn't changed. And I was charged account fee for that month. When I ask for an update, they respond slowly.\nI'm disappointed.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Just randomly deduct my money without leaving any trace. 2 weeks of writing emails for complaining but no active support from them.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Cập nhật app xong không mở được tài khoản phong tỏa ( lúc nào cũng lỗi app) . Được nhắn rằng sẽ xử lý trong 24h nhưng không hề thấy gì ( đã 3 ngày trôi qua rồi)", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "tôi đã mở tài khoản của mình gần 1 năm và khi cần hỗ trợ tôi không nhận được sự giúp đỡ cần có. lẽ ra mọi thứ cần được giải quyết trong 24h nhưng tôi phải đợi đến 3 ngày và vấn đề không hề được giải quyết", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I needed to do the blocked account for my master in Germany, so far I had a thousand problems, their support is ridiculous, it takes days or weeks to solve simple problems, I can’t start transferring my OWN money from the blocked account until I get my residence permit even if it takes MONTHS to finish the process! Leaving me to have to struggle through months with no access to my money! I really hope I never need to use their services again!", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "It doesn't work. It closes alone immediately after I try to open it.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "App crash in new update when choosing make payment.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Unfortunately the choices for blocked accounts in Germany are very few at the moment. Most banks don’t offer them, so forced to use fintiba.\n\nI have an issue with Fintiba *requiring* an app download to get the essential documents from them. This is dumb. Why is it not possible to receive the documents over the web? In fact… why have a web portal at all then?\n\nAs for the service itself, they are a legitimate provider.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "It's not recognizing my password", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I got locked out of my account and my email address was changed by a 3rd party and when I complained to customer support they didn’t do anything", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "E-Mails werden tagelang nicht beantwortet, durch Telefonat halt hart zu erreichen, plus Ansprechpartnerinnen stellen kein Interesse dar, meine Anfrage zu beantworten", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Very disappointing experience with Fintiba. The Source of Funds verification took weeks with no clear timeline or meaningful updates. This caused serious delays with my German student visa process. Customer support was unable to provide any information.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I don‘t recommend using it for a blocked account, Problem with Sending Money arose as early as the first month. When Contacting Customer Service , responses arw extremly delayed and issue remains unrevolved (the replay is simply thst they don‘t know when the problem will be fixed) there are many alternatives solutions avalible such as Expatrio.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ich bin völlig verzweifelt. Seit einer Woche bin ich ganz allein in Deutschland und habe keinen einzigen cent, weil Fintiba wegen eines APP- Fehlers!! Mein Geld nicht freigibt. ICH KANN MIR WEDER ESS NOCH EIN TICKET FÜR DIE BAHN KAUFEN!!!!\nObwohl ich alle schritte und die Videolegitimation längst erfolgreich abgeschlossen habe, zeigt die APP weiterhin einen Fehler an. Das ist eine Kleinigkeit, die der IT SUPPORT!! In 5 minuten beheben könnte aber NIEMAND ANTWORTET MIR ODER HILFT MIR!!! \n Sie lassen menschen in eimem fremden land buchstäblich hungern und ohne geld zurück !! \nKeiner reagiert auf Nachrichten und jetzt ist das Wochenende da. \nMachen Sie nicht derselbe Fehler wie ich - vertrauen Sie Fintiba NIMALS Ihr GELD an !", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I cannot recommend Fintiba. While opening the blocked account was easy, getting my money back was a very stressful and frustrating experience. After requesting the refund, it took several months to receive my money, and fees continued to be deducted during this time.\n\nIf you are considering Fintiba, keep in mind that opening a blocked account is only part of the story. Closing the account and getting your money refunded can become a long and stressful process.\n\nI eventually received my money, but only after months of persistent follow-ups. Based on my experience, I cannot recommend Fintiba.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "For reference, my Fintiba customer ID is 615-974-461.\n\nMy experience with Fintiba was fine until I had to extend my blocked account. That’s where everything started to fall apart.\n\nThe extension itself was confirmed by email, but my app still showed that no next payout was registered. I contacted support because I wanted to make sure my monthly payout would actually arrive. Instead of looking into my account, I kept receiving the same basic instructions. I was told to register my payout myself, even though I had already sent screenshots showing that this was impossible because the entire payout page was greyed out and there was nothing I could click or edit.\n\nI tried everything. I used the AI chatbot, which was only able to repeat general instructions. I emailed support several times, and my replies either went unanswered or ignored what I had actually written. I even had to email the CEO’s address just to receive a response. When I called customer support, I waited around 40 minutes, only to be told that my money should arrive automatically. That wasn’t my question. I wasn’t asking what should happen. I was asking someone to actually look into why it wasn’t happening.\n\nThe biggest problem is not that technical issues exist. Technical issues happen. The problem is that nobody seemed willing to spend even a few minutes checking my account. I spent about a month trying to resolve this. Every time I explained the situation, I was sent back to the same generic instructions, the chatbot, or told to wait.\n\nWhat I find most disappointing is that I have reached the point where I feel the need to write public reviews simply to get someone’s attention. Nobody should have to hope that a public review will succeed where normal customer support has failed, especially when the issue is access to their own money.\n\nBecause of this delay, I have been left without access to my own funds. I have had to postpone my appointment with the immigration office, I have not been able to switch to public health insurance, I cannot pay my rent, and I cannot cover basic living expenses. This is a company that manages blocked accounts for international students. When something goes wrong, there needs to be a reliable way to reach someone who will actually investigate and resolve the problem.\n\nI was patient for a month. At this point, I simply can’t afford to keep waiting.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ich möchte meine Mawista-Versicherung kündigen, nachdem ich eine gesetzliche Krankenversicherung erhalten habe.\n\nIch habe Fintiba eine E-Mail geschickt, um die Mawista-Versicherung zu kündigen. Allerdings möchte Fintiba, dass ich 170 € für die Kündigung bezahle.\nEigentlich ist das sehr schlimm !!!", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Can’t extend my blocked account, although my visa is expiring in 2 months. I’ve been contacting support for few weeks now. No response whatsoever. Moving to expatrio, bye bye 👋👋👋", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Wrost app ever i uploaded my visa one month before and till know I didn’t get any payment from my blocked account to my bank account and if i call them they just say wait since a month i am waiting", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Extremely disappointing experience with Fintiba.\n\nDespite submitting every requested document, completing the full verification process, and complying with all additional requirements, my blocked account remains inaccessible with no meaningful resolution provided.\n\nWhat is particularly concerning is the quality of customer support. Responses are delayed, generic, and largely ineffective. Instead of resolving the issue, support repeatedly asks for patience while providing no clear timeline, accountability, or practical assistance.\n\nFor a company handling essential funds for international students and visa holders, this level of inefficiency is unacceptable. Access to blocked account funds is not a minor inconvenience: it directly affects people’s housing, living expenses, and legal stability in Germany.\n\nBased on my experience, I cannot recommend Fintiba to others. If I could go back in time, I would seriously consider alternative providers with more transparent processes, competent support, and faster issue resolution. The service presented during registration does not reflect the reality of the experience once problems arise.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "When the last payout done, I ask for the remain of my money in the account, they wait another 3 week just to take another 4 euro and send me an email that we will do it soon, big compagnies don't do this for few euro.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Worst sperrkonto(blocked account) app ever.This company delayed my payments for 10 days.Because they don’t have the knowledge of transfering money to another account in public holidays won’t work.As a banking app this is unacceptable.Because of their own mistakes my payment for 2 months got delayed for 10 days each.I was about to kicked from my place because i couldn’t pay rent due to their incompetence.Don’t use this app use expatrio or another app.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "If i could i would put 0 star\nJust if you want your money safe and seamless payouts go try another cause this company not reliable and have too many technical problems that would make you frustrated a lot\nI faced an issue (it was caused by a system bug) and that happens before my flight by a week thank god not before applying to visa and i raised a ticket a week after nothing happened just an automated mail sent daily and i called them they said your problem will be solved then i waited a couple of days nothing happened i called for the second time the agent raised another and told me that the first agent done nothing and in 24 hrs my problem will be solved i waited nothing happened i called agent has weird attitude and keep saying the same words and said it takes 48hrs not 24 then we talked he didn’t say anything good and hung up with me while i am talking. I called right after and the same agent from yesterday answered and said that (i must be patient they will contact me through out the day by mail) i asked about the context she said she doesn’t have the authority but she believes that they will contact me. Then what i should wait till when so they could send the payout i am not the only one there is an unlisted video attached in the automated mail that many people have the issue ( which makes them unreliable as they claim)", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I’m extremely disappointed with the Fintiba app and service. It has been more than a week since I requested my blocked amount, and I still haven’t received it. I rely on this money to pay my rent and other essential bills, and right now I literally have zero money because of this delay. This situation is incredibly stressful and unacceptable.\n\nCustomer support has not provided any clear timeline or proper solution, and the lack of urgency is very frustrating when people depend on this money for basic living expenses.\n\nI would never recommend this app to anyone dealing with a blocked account. If you are considering your options, I strongly suggest going with Expatrio or Coracle instead. My experience with Fintiba has been nothing but delays and stress.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Die von mir überwiesenen Gelder wurden vollständig gutgeschrieben, doch obwohl ich bereits zwei Tag gewartet habe, habe ich noch immer keine Bestätigung erhalten. Der Nachweis ist in der App nirgends zu finden, und der Vorgang bleibt bei dem Schritt hängen, bei dem ich Geld überweisen soll – obwohl der angezeigte erforderliche Betrag es unmöglich macht, weiterzumachen. Der Kundenservice bietet lediglich repetitive Plattitüden und leistet keinerlei sinnvolle Hilfe.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Stressing and to many updates", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "My experience with Fintiba has been extremely frustrating and disappointing. I transferred the full required amount for my blocked account two months ago, yet I still haven’t received access to my money. Despite having sufficient funds in my account, the staff handling my case kept asking me to top up, giving unclear explanations, and provided no real assistance.\nMeanwhile, Fintiba deducted service fees for August, September, and October, even though my money was already in the account and I could not access it. I have been waiting for two months, and during this time, my funds have been held without any progress, causing me serious stress and inconvenience, especially since I need the money for my living expenses.\nThe communication has been poor, and it feels like the staff are more focused on asking for additional payments than actually resolving the issue. This experience has been unprofessional, frustrating, and stressful.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I opened my blocked account on 26.08.2025 and transferred the required amount. Due to a technical error, the balance was displayed twice. Unsurprisingly, this issue – their own financial problem – was solved immediately. Suddenly, everything worked smoothly: no delays, no repetitive responses, just instant resolution.\n\nBut when it comes to my official blocked account statement, the story changes completely. I have been waiting for days, even though I urgently need this document for my residence permit. Each time I contact customer service, I receive the same copy-paste reply: “please wait 24 hours.” These 24 hours keep repeating endlessly.\n\nThe impression is crystal clear: when it’s about their money, things move fast and without obstacles. When it’s about the customer’s needs, especially critical documents, you’re left in a loop of empty promises. For a company that depends on international students, the priorities are clearly in the wrong place.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I’ve had my blocked account for over 2 years now and I had mostly a good experience with it. However, whenever there’s a tech problem the client support is terrible. I changed my IBAN because of my bank but for some reason the monthly transfer keeps on being done to my old account even though I’ve changed the IBAN multiple times. So every month, the transfer bounces and I have to change it AGAIN. I’ve contacted the customer support twice already and their answer are only “you can update the IBAN here” and that’s it. But apparently they’re not reading my message because that’s not the problem at all? I’ve explained throughly the situation but they completely ignore it. I will definitely be closing my account when the current period expires and will not recommend it again.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Funktioniert gar nicht seit heute Morgen!!! Steht irgendwie so bugs gefunden und muss noch aktualisiert werden", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "so in the app i have done the video legitimation and received the tan code and everything but they still say that i need to do the video legitimation and when i click on it it says session has expired and today i was supposed to get my money transferred and i still haven't gotten any single penny👎👎👎", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I want to use this opportunity to share my impression not only about the app, but about the service in general as well. \n\nThe app is really very old. No face ID, and even the first screen where you log in looks like it was made in 90-ies. I once had to change my phone number, and because I no longer had access to my old number, they asked me to send them a photo of myself with my passport and an A4 paper with the new phone number written on it - I had to do that twice, because they could not read my ID first. This means that their processes are fully manual. \n\nOn the page where they list the banks where one can open a regular bank account, there are four banks, but only one of them (Sparkassa) opens accounts for foreigners who have not yet received their residence permits; other banks refuse to open accounts if you only have a visa - and it takes months to get the residence permit. But the guys at Fintiba don’t care and keep showing all four banks, so that their clients lose their time trying to open an account with them, which is doomed for failure. \n\nWhen my blocked account was depleted (all monthly payments were done), instead of closing this blocked account they sent me an email ‘thanks for choosing Mawista as your private health insurance’ and charged my account 349 euro! \n\nVery old app, very poor service", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Man kann einfach so keine Auszahlungen in einigen Monaten bekommen. 4 Monate war bei mir alles gut, dann habe ich im fünften und im siebten Monat keine Auszahlungen erhalten, obwohl ich dem Support dreimal E-Mail geschickt und sie angerufen habe. Ich würde Fintiba gar nicht empfehlen, weil man nicht sicher sein kann, dass er nächsten Monat sein Geld bekommt", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "This app has repeatedly disappointed me. It’s been 1 week and I still haven’t gotten my money. They support has been absolutely horrible and they don’t reply and if they did it’s days apart. I’ve never met a more frustrating app ever.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "However this is already the latest version", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The latest update has made the app unusable. Whenever I enter my login informations and press enter, the app just crashes making it almost unusable. Have to rely on the computer web interface to use it", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Mehrmals angerufen nur zwei mal aufgenommen. Die Probleme sind immer noch nicht geklärt bzw. gelöst. Sehr schlechtes System, man kann auch nicht Registrierungsschritte zurücksetzen.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ich möchte mein Visum verlängern, aber sie haben mir nie geantwortet, nur wochenlang mit automatischer E-Mail.  beschlossen, den Anbieter zu wechseln", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I’m unable to open the app. Ive installed and uninstalled it countless time and still cant open it. Please fix this", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Mit IPhone kann ich nicht diese App öffnen,was soll ich tun!", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Seit ein Woche kann ich nicht mein geld haben.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Schlecht App", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Iphone 7Plus IOS 11.4.1, Die App an sich war sehr gut, das Sperrkonto ließ sich innerhalb von 48 locker eröffnen, allerdings kann ich jetzt nicht mehr die App öffnen, um die zweite Verifizierung vorzunehmen und das gesperrte Geld monatlich zurückzubekommen. Wahrscheinlich ein Softwareproblem, aber eine gute Bank sollte dieses schnellstmöglich beheben, zumal ich bei der Bank circa 10.000€ gesperrt habe 😅", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The app as well as the website is full of bugs to the point I am questioning if that’s actually the official app and website for Fantiba or it’s some scam app and website !!!  It’s either getting me stuck like it acts like I didn’t check all the boxes and now the app returned me back to submitting my info after I have already finished all the steps .. I don’t feel safe sending the money", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "It says i need to update the app but it is already up to date", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Absolutely disgraceful and unprofessional customer service. My funds have been frozen for over 18 months with no valid explanation provided. Every time I’ve attempted to contact the bank, I’ve been met with rude, dismissive responses—essentially told to 'wait' or brushed off entirely. Email communication is painfully slow; it takes up to two weeks to receive a reply, and even then, the response offers no resolution. After that single, useless reply, they go silent, forcing me to start the process all over again. Phone calls are equally futile,no one provides meaningful assistance. Requests to talk with someone senior are simply met with rude responses that the managers are listening to all this and a call transfer to a supervisor is not possible at all.The only consistent communication I receive from them? A heart emoji, as if that makes up for their complete negligence. My advice to anyone reading this: if you sense even the slightest issue with this bank, do not wait patiently like I did. Go straight to legal counsel. Do not rely on their 'support'—they will not help you. After 18 months, my money remains trapped, and this bank has shown zero accountability.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "App doesn’t open.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I can’t make an edit or correction  an issue  without telling a Bot and this makes the system unreliable. The Bot does not even help with my issue", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The app isn’t working", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "App not even starting on my iPhone 7", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "can’t open this app", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Fail to login to the APP", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": ".", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I still CANT open the app!!!!!!!", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "please fix the app because it keeps on crashing and i have some improtant documents that i need to download , this is so uncomfortoble why can we just download the files from the website", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Please fix the app, it keeps crashing when i tried to launch it, please help, i need to download some documents from it!", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I cannot open the app at all after the most recent update! Developers please fix this!", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "why can't this app work on my phone?\nmy ios is compatible with the app, but every time i tried to open the app, it's always forced to close.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "DO NOT open a bank account with this bank, they have the worse customer service, they don’t reply to your emails or answer your phone calls. My money is stuck with them and I can’t have it back because they don’t answer the phone or reply to my emails. Also the in-app support doesn’t work.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "This app doesn’t even open on my IOS phone!!", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "it’s been 3days I keep calling, each time I am on the line waiting for 40mins and no one picks up!!!", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "absolutely terrible and stressful experience, never recommend fintiba for opening blocking accounts \n\nafter transferring my founds 23.08 - weeks without response, no support, months for “confirming sources of founds” with no time limits and clear requirements what else documents you need to send\n\nas a prospective student you put so much effort to get into the university and you get this attitude.. \n\nif you don’t want to risk your student visa, stay away from fintiba", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "4 digits confirmation is not arriving at any email im providing!", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The app don’t want to open for me", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The app does not open on my iPhone, I don’t know what the problem might be.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "It’s been a couple of weeks since I can’t enter into my account and I need my last month information :/", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The app doesn’t let me log into my account, it’s been a problem for several days now.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "App won‘t open", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The app doesn’t even display my account. Been on it for days. It accepts my password but i cant view my account. Impossible to download the necessary documents as directed from the website", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The app automatically closes once I open it on my Iphone 7+ since the update in August and I waited for new updates to see if that would change once I update, yet no changes. Disappointed, fix up.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "This is the third time I’m deleting and downloading this app because it stops working after upgrade", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Help!!!!!The app is not working", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I Upgraded the Fintiba App on my IPhone 6s and it stopped working......whenever I try opening the app......it shuts down automatically......Help Please", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I downloaded the app but it can’t launch, seems like the coding is bad, maybe fix it ?!!!", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Пытались открыть сыну блокированный счет, больше месяца делали вид, что проверяют наши документы, на письма в поддержку не отвечают, дозвониться не возможно, сейчас пытаемся вернуть наши деньги, в итоге ни денег, ни счета🤬", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "DO NOT TRUST THIS APP. Fintiba completely frozen my verification process for nearly 2 months (from June 11 to August 4), completely violating their advertised processing times. Because of their severe operational delays, I did not receive my blocking confirmation (Sperrbestätigung) in time, missed my mandatory university deadline in Berlin, and my educational plans were completely ruined.To make it worse, when I sent a formal cancellation request on August 4 while my profile was still unverified, they ignored it. Instead, they retroactively activated my account 3 days later just to force me to close it manually and steal a €159 Fintiba Plus setup fee and monthly administration fees for services they failed to provide.I demand a 100% full refund of my €12,073 without any unjust deductions. If this is not resolved immediately by their management team, I am submitting official complaints to BaFin, the European Online Dispute Resolution platform, and the Verbraucherzentrale for unfair business practices. Total scam.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Access to my account was received again. But it doesn’t work stable.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The help center is not actually trying to help you. They answer on email after one week , and  calls they put you on wait until you lose patience. Been trying to receive my blocking confirmation for 2 weeks now . AND NOTHING .", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Why is it required to install the app in order to download documents? \nIt makes no sense.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am so disappointed with the customer support that Fintiba provides. Even for simple requests, they take several days and sometimes week to process them. Also the user experience is so bad in the app and on the website… It is very unclear how to fill in different forms, what do different menu items mean and so on. Instead of simplifying my life in Germany, Fintiba makes it more complicated. Please hire more people to reply to the customer support requests, and also hire a good UX designer so that the interface gets more comprehensive!", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "It’s extremely bad that I have to log in every time I launch the app.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I downloaded the app today. it worked well for about two hours, and now it doesn’t even open", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Downloaded the app yesterday and it worked fine, when I tried to access it today it keeps saying “update required”", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Плохо работает", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Please take care abt it. I’ve recently downloaded it, after 10-15 using it stoped working! Should I redownload it or wait for upgrade?", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "40 gündür hesabımı tamir edemediler, param tutsak resmen, önermiyorum", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "They haven’t sent my payout for a week and after contacting them 4-5 times, they sent me less than the amount! Apparently they cut the amount as they please!", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have made the account last year to apply for a visa in Germany but my visa has been rejected , so normally I request to close my account but unfortunately they have the worst customer support, they don’t respond to any emails or have a system that you can use without any help ,  I still have not got my money out of the bank and it’s been a month since I requested to close the account", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Merhaba gelen OTP kodunu giriyorum 3 gündür sunucu hatası alıp duruyorum.Acil yardımınızı bekliyorum.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have called them 5 times each lasting over 12 minutes, no body picks up the phone!", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I can’t take my money back after 6 months! They say we sent it back but don’t provide any proof. I lost 7k euros", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "It just does not have a screen for the login. It only allows me to create an account which I already did by using web browser. I just want to login without signing up again.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "It is the fourth month I want to try take my money (10000 euros) back , but the Fintiba bank team making excuse and don’t want to give back money. I don’t recommend this bank specially those who are from third world countries. German Consulates and embassies don’t consider you as human. Even they don’t realize you as a human. They will not help you too. Don’t wast your money and time with these people.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I tried to log in my account but the suddenly ı lived the password error problem ı am sure e-mail and password are true please solve my problem", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I tried to log in to my account today, but the password or email is incorrect. I am 100% sure that my password and email address are correct. After I clicked the \"Forgot Password\" button, I entered my email address, but the link you sent me to renew my password redirects me to the login page! I can't renew my password! I am an Erasmus student in Germany and I have such a problem when I need the money the most.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The application is keep closing whenever I open the app.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I had to close my blocked account.  850 euro of my money was sent incomplete.  I emailed them many times and asked them to fix it, but it is a careless and sloppy bank.  My problem is still not solved.  my emails are being answered without being read properly.  frustration..", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ich benutze iPhone 11 und kann mich seit gestern nicht anmelden. Ich habe nur einen weißen Bildschirm. Ich bitte Sie es zu überprüfen", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Crashed on 8plus, 12.1.4", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ich benutze iPhone 8 plus und diese App funktioniert nicht auf meinem Handy.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ich benutze ı phone 5 S . ıch kann nicht open app.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I use iphone 6 and whenever i try to open your app it kicks me out please help!!", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The application hasn’t worked for 2 days.That says it needs upload.When you click to the button,it doesn’t work.Can you fix that please ?", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "It is kicking me out whenever i click on app..", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Update: STILL NOT WORKING!!!!\n\nAs soon as I click on the application it just kicks me out. I cannot login check anything out nothing zero. Please fix this as soon as possible.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "APP SHUTS DOWN WITHOUT OPENING!!!!!!", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "When I tab the app, it seems like opening but it doesn’t. I need to check my account. Also when I try to sign on website , everytime it required to change my password. Can you just help me please ?", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Diese App funktioniert nicht.  Bitte beheben Sie das Problem und lassen Sie die App funktionieren.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Yapacağınız güncellemeyi....", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "When the app is opened, I can log into my account but the rest does not work. All you can see on the screen is a white blank page.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Funktioniert nicht.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "When you touch on the app logo you don’t see your account details but a white page.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "This experience took the longest time for me .i think maybe because it was my first time doing it with no agency but also because of some misunderstanding all in all it was a humbling experience and you should be patient . Although i would still  recomend the app no hate", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "На IOS вообще не запускается.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Installed it but it doesn’t open a single window when try opening it. Disappointed", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Before submitting your release version, test it on different screen resolutions. I use the iPhone 13 mini and I can’t see the Login button in your app. Because your UI is not adaptive.", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am failing to upload my passport page +selfie. After taking both it writes timeout error and its been doing this for the last 5 days. Please help my documents are neeeded ASAP", "p": "apple_app_store"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Unfortunately, I have been waiting for Expatrio to verify the account/passport details, and the delay is becoming extremely concerning (with no timeline in sight). My German student visa appointment is just days away, and we still need to transfer the funds and obtain the required blocked account confirmation.\nThis is not a situation where customers can simply wait indefinitely. A delayed verification could potentially prevent someone from having the required financial documentation ready for their visa appointment and put their studies at risk.\n\nCase number: 00064892\n\nPlease urgently resolve this verification issue. The funds are ready to be transferred, but I cannot proceed until the verification is completed.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Very slow service. I submitted my documents for the refund process following a visa refusal on August 13, 2026, and Expatrio asked me to wait for a week. Today is August 25, 2026, and I still haven't received any email regarding the progress of this process, despite several follow-ups. I am disappointed with your service. ID 1220011.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Very poor service and failing systems. On August 2, 2026, I received official written confirmation from Expatrio that my documents were accepted and my blocked account was fully activated. However, between 21/08 and 22/08, I received misleading guidance, and my tickets were closed without resolution. On 24/08/2026, instead of receiving my confirmed payout, the system automatically delayed it until 24/09/2026. Holding a student's living funds after officially confirming activation is unacceptable.\nUser ID: 372605", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Update: After two weeks, I finally received the correct documents. It seems the customer service team and the system weren’t working in sync. After customer service instructed me to refund the full amount, the system automatically closed my account and attempted to refund all my transfers. My ticket was transferred to several different customer service representatives before the issue was finally resolved.\n\nTitle: Urgent: System Error on Active Account Jeopardizing Student Visa\nI am submitting this review due to extreme urgency.\nMy activated Blocked Account's start date was mistakenly set retroactively to September 2025 instead of 2026, triggering an improper payout and leaving my account with incorrect details. After waiting 4 days for support, I received a templated response that completely missed the issue.\nWithout the corrected 06 Blocked Account Confirmation, I cannot apply for my emergency German student visa for the upcoming October 1st semester. I have followed all protocols, yet my urgent issue remains unresolved during this critical period.\n I request a supervisor to review my ticket and manually correct my activation start date immediately.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Absolutely terrible service. I was originally using Dr. Walter insurance through Expatrio. They told me that I had to cancel it myself to switch to Ottonova for my Master’s degree. So I went through the hassle and secured the cancellation confirmation on August 12th. However, ever since I submitted it to Expatrio, it has been a week of total radio silence. Their chatbot just says it's not their responsibility and cuts me off, and nobody picks up the phone. My university enrollment is at serious risk because of Expatrio's incompetence. Process my change request immediately.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "My account is officially closed, but the app banking dashboard is completely frozen on the static \"closure details provided\" screen. I cannot input any text fields. I responded to your email query with my official Expatrio account PDFs and my dad's external bank IBAN/beneficiary details for the manual refund. My family is facing extreme financial stress due to this delay. Please have a human administrator manually review my email ticket and release the transfer to my dad's account today. My User ID is 989541", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I just don’t get it: Why my private insurance, which ended on the end of march still shows its status as “active” on the Expatrio App. This lead to a consequence that I cannot purchase any other insurance for my student visa.\nAnd during a couple weeks of argument. I still don’t get any response of a real person. Every letter I’ve got sounds like a canned response. What is going on with the support team?", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Very disappointed, they have been holding my funds for more than 2 months now . No reasonable action has been done to resolve my issue.\nJust a bunch if emails again and again passing to same team.\nName : Ketan Chandra \n\nDidnt expected this from Expartio.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have been trying to get my health insurance confirmation sent to my university for over two weeks, but the issue is still unresolved.\n\nI have contacted Expatrio multiple times and asked for help, as this document is essential for completing my university enrollment. All my other documents and payments have already been approved by my university, and I am currently unable to complete my enrollment simply because the insurance confirmation has not been transmitted.\n\nIt is extremely frustrating to wait for more than two weeks for such an important and time-sensitive issue, especially when it directly affects my university enrollment. I really expected faster and more effective support.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "No reply from the customer support for urgent matter.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "My problem wasn't solved", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Good Service Overall, But Disappointed with Ambassador***\nExpatrio offers reliable services for blocked accounts and relocation, but my experience with one of your local Turkish representatives, Mert Eroğlu, was highly disappointing.\nInstead of helping, he displayed aggressive, unprofessional behavior, pushed personal affiliate links, and actively spoke negatively about Expatrio's reliability, causing unnecessary confusion.\nWhile the service itself is solid, Expatrio needs to implement much stricter vetting for its brand representatives. Unprofessional ambassadors undermine customer trust and damage an otherwise good platform. I hope management takes necessary action to improve ambassador quality.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Die Freundin unseres Sohnes musste vorzeitig abreisen und wartet seit März 2026 auf die Auszahlung ihres Guthabens, obwohl sie alle Unterlagen mehrmals eingereicht hat. Katastrophale Erfahrung! Der Kundendienst ist absolut ineffizient, die E-Mails an die Beschwerde-Stelle (\"Formalcomplaints\") werden nicht beantwortet. Es ist unmöglich jemanden telefonisch zu erreichen. Wir werden jetzt einen Rechtsanwalt einschalten und auf Social Media ausgiebig über diese Erfahrung berichten. Wenn Sie ein Sperrkonto benötigen, suchen Sie einen anderen Anbieter!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Good email updates and quick service. However it is difficult to find information on the website. I still cannot find the medical insurance policy; like what it covers and what it doesn’t. \nThe information about the blocked account however is somewhat decently provided.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I was required to make my payment through Flywire solely because I am a Chinese customer. I find it unacceptable that customers are required to use a specific payment provider based on their nationality, particularly when this results in a significant financial disadvantage.\n\nDue to the exchange rate applied by Flywire, I was charged more than RMB 1,000 above the real-time exchange rate — almost €200 in additional costs. This is a substantial and unreasonable amount of money, and I should not be expected to bear this loss simply because I was required to use a particular payment platform.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "These guys are complete scammers in the sense that they are not providing any sort of communications with the customer. The app shows I have less money in my account than I actually should have. I had more problems regarding my blocked account. I tried to reach them but they don’t have any contact number. All you can do for support is use their contact form and then you'll be only replied to by a AI generated reply by a bot!! How crazy is that??! If you have any serious issue with you blocked account, all you can do is hope that they find the problem and fix it themselves, as you can't reach them yourself. Even the document uploading for opening a bank account was a nightmare. I uploaded everything correctly multiple time and they automatically reject it every time. I couldn't reach them after trying multiple times. Overall, I would say, it's such a disingenuous company, with no support for customers with no clear communication channel. \n!!!!!! AVOID THIS SERVICE!!!!!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "No pude recibir una notificación de que ottonova se había comunicado con la universidad y me lo pedían para el enrolment, de resto todo perfecto", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "There is no possiblty to connecting real staff with out talkink with a bot and also I'm still waiting for a real crucial Process to be solved, which took more than 7 business Day and im still talking with agents.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have been trying to activate my blocked account payouts for almost two weeks, despite completing every verification and documentation requirement requested by Expatrio.\n\nMy money was transferred into the blocked account within hours. However, getting access to my own money has turned into a two-week process involving repeated verification requests, proof of address, proof of residency, identity verification, and finally another identity verification just to change my phone number.\n\nMy phone number was eventually changed, and I was told that UniCredit would update it within two business days. That timeframe has passed, and I still cannot receive the SMS required to activate my payouts.\n\nWhat makes this even more frustrating is the customer support. Instead of actually investigating the situation, I repeatedly received generic, automated responses that did not address the problem I was explaining. I had to keep contacting support and explaining the same situation over and over.\nI understand that Expatrio works with a banking partner and that some processes may take time. What I find unacceptable is the complete lack of effective communication and the fact that I have been left without access to money I depend on for my living expenses, despite having fulfilled every requirement asked of me.\n\nThis has been an extremely stressful and disappointing experience. A service dealing with people's essential living funds should have much faster and more effective support when something goes wrong.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "客服不太好找，刚开始碰到问题不知道去哪里问。后来发现是官网有客户入口，但是不太明显。微信的客户回复不及时，咨询了没收到回复。", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "service is insufficient to meet your needs", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "health information insurance, there is no guide how to approach to selected university with such health insurance, many university dont list selected health insurance on their list.. it leads big confusion on health insurance.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Even though the entire amount was transferred (confirmed by the bank too), my Expatrio balance showed 25 Euros less, which delayed my amount confirmation form!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Worst experience...I had with expatrio", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Horrible customer service. All services provided by Expatrio are smooth and convenient, as long as FAQs cover your queries. Because there is no way to contact a human representative in time and all their AI support is useless. Poppy is useless and keeps asking questions in circles. Their AI assistant on WhatsApp is even worse and hallucinates. It took me a week to get in touch with a human (if they were one) via email to have my health insurance changed. Such delays are disastrous for students trying to align everything with their visa process. Everything else is fine, but I pray to all gods I never need customer support ever again from Expatrio.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It’s good that this self-insurance scheme comes with a recommendation for state-funded health insurance, but I’ve noticed that some people can opt for lower management fees. However, I’ve only been able to find this package with relatively high management fees. There are clearly other options available, but I can’t find them!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Not responding to the mail and it's been 3 days i have asked them to add unblock amount but still they have not responded.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am trying to renew my blocked account and have already initiated the transfer. It has been three days and no confirmation has been sent to their side, and I cannot access the 05 document as it is now available in the app, though I got a link to download the document from their user page, which does not function.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The customer service response was not very good. The lack of human interaction and a hot line made my process longer than I expected. Besides the long waiting time for emails’ responses.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "tl;dr - Customer support is shit.\n\nI took the complete package from this website (Blocked Account + Private health insurance).\n\nThe account was provisioned quickly and smoothly. \n\nHowever sending the insurance confirmation was a nightmare. The customer support docs told me that confirmation would be sent within a month of account provisioning.\n\nI setup the account transferred the blocked money, bought the insurance and basically did everything, in the first week of July. \n\nHowever, it is currently the first week of August, and I have gone back and forth with support multiple times yet nothing is happening.\n\nThere is that stupid AI bot, which keeps telling me that it has escalated my request to the customer support team, yet no confirmation is sent to my university.\n\nThe university has given me a deadline of next week to send the insurance confirmation, and I don't know if this scam of a website will even send it.\n\nThe life of an international student is fairly stressful, you are searching for accomodation, figuring out all the basic necessities in this new country you are going to and the last thing you need is an insurance provider which doesn't even care to do its part. \n\nI wouldn't recommend this website to anyone. \nFor anyone reading this please use Fintiba, it will be less stressful.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I gave clear instructions that the blocked account should be created according to the requirements of the Foreigners' Authority of the City of Amberg.\n\nYour agent assured me that the requested content would be included in the \"06 Blocked Amount Confirmation\" document and stated:\n\n\"The content you mentioned will be included in the 06 Blocked Amount Confirmation document.\"\n\nHowever, after reviewing the documents, I could not find any of the requested changes. \n\nCould you please explain why the requested changes were not made and update the documents accordingly?", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Your customer support is so bad takes three days to answer and my information is wrong\n\nUpdate it’s been 2 week now just for them to change my information. Ridiculously horrible service", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am disappointed with Expatrio’s service.\n\nFor a long time, I was told that my account was “not activated,” even though I had already completed all the required steps. Now the activation option has disappeared, which clearly indicates that my account is activated. However, my documents have been “under review” for more than a week with no progress.\n\nThe biggest issue is the lack of communication. I have contacted support multiple times, but I am not receiving any clear response. As a student relying on this money for living expenses, this delay is extremely stressful.\n\nThere is no transparency about:\n\n* When the review will be completed\n* When I will receive my first payment\n* Whether anything else is required from my side\n\nThis kind of uncertainty is unacceptable, especially when people depend on these funds urgently.\n\nI strongly urge Expatrio to improve their response time and provide clear updates. Right now, the service feels unreliable and frustrating.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Issues that are caused by expatrio such as incorrect blocked account confirmation are not resolved sooner.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "App bug is threatening to block my bank account in 2 days despite showing full access. Customer support doesn't reply via email/Instagram. Ticket ID: 1260627", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Unfortunately I cannot reach any person when I have a problem on my account. That was the urgent situation but I could  not find any Expatrio person thereby I rate it 1 star.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I haven't gotten my insurance confirmation yet and it's delaying my visa process", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "TK overcharged me, and as my block provide Expartio did nothing! Worst service.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Terrible support. Avoid it if you can. I'm trying to unlock my account, and it's been a struggle.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Today is July 24th, my payout day, but I received nothing. Your automated chatbot is trapped in a useless loop, and even the automatic confirmation email for customer service is not working. It seems your entire system is crashed. I am in Germany and I have zero cash for the weekend. Check my account immediately.\nUser ID: 1169343", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have been experiencing issues with the finally activation step of my bank account in the app for several days now, and I’ve reached out to support. After hearing back with recommended troubleshooting tips, implementing them with no success, and replying back to support with immediate urgency, they have gone completely silent despite saying they will escalate due to my urgent need to access my account. I have done every step and submitted every required document successfully, yet I am now stuck due to a technical bug on the app with no other alternative platform to perform the required video activation. I need to urgently activate my account to access my funds, and I have completely no means of support or way to get further assistance. Please, please help me resolve this issue, so I may proceed! :(", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The user experience is so bad because there is no notification of direct debit cuts. No security features. Why do I have to download a PDF to view my transaction? The UI is also so bad: no insights about sending patterns, monthly budget, and so on", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "My early enrollment at Universität Bremen is blocked TODAY because of Expatrio. Every single checklist item is done – documents, semester fee, everything. The ONLY missing piece is the M10 health insurance notification, which EXPATRIO must send.\n\nI spoke to ottonova on the phone minutes ago: they confirmed the notification must be sent BY EXPATRIO via the public insurance channel. The university confirmed in writing it was NEVER received.\n\nI've sent countless emails to Expatrio. ZERO response. Total silence while my enrollment sits blocked and time-critical.\n\nExpatrio – SEND the M10 to Universität Bremen \n(H0002687) TODAY:\n\n- User ID: 2081339\n- University application: 607067\n\nThis is urgent. I will update this review the moment it's fixed – but right now a student's enrollment is stuck because nobody at Expatrio answers.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Expatrio has been withholding my €2,576 blocked account funds for nearly 3 years despite my official German visa rejection (Ref: DEU/503000/20230713/001540748).\n\nWhat is even worse: Expatrio’s own dashboard explicitly states: \"In case of visa rejection, the rejection letter is sufficient.\" However, when I uploaded my official rejection letter, they arbitrarily set it as \"rejected\" in their system and kept deducting monthly fees from my money, draining it down to €2,434.37.\n\nThey refuse to apply their own written rules and ignore basic consumer rights. An official complaint has now been registered with the German Federal Financial Supervisory Authority (BaFin) under Beschwerde-ID: 213507.\n\nI demand the immediate release of my full original deposit of €2,576.\n\nUser ID: 440795\n\nUPDATE:\nUPDATE:\n\nExpatrio responds with standard PR excuses claiming \"higher volume of requests\". Claiming a backlog for a case that has been dragged on for nearly 3 YEARS after an official visa rejection is completely unacceptable.\n\nThis is not a support delay; it is an unlawful retention of my €2,576 deposit in direct violation of your own written terms.\n\nMy official complaint with BaFin (Beschwerde-ID: 213507) remains ACTIVE. I do not want automated apologies on Trustpilot—I demand the full refund of my €2,576 to my bank account immediately.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It was good experience but I faced some delay and some site problems", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Kein schneller antworten keine telefoniert erreichen  nie wieder bei euch Kunden nie wieder", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I opened a blocked account with Expatrio and transferred my money as required. However, I have been unable to access my own funds because of a verification issue caused by the way Expatrio handles my name.\n\nTo my first name they added my patronymic (father's name). During the POSTIDENT identification process, Deutsche Post correctly identifies me, because their system automatically reads only the first name and surname from my passport. Expatrio, however, insists that my patronymic must be included in my first name, making the verification impossible.\n\nI have exchanged numerous emails with customer support over several weeks, but the issue remains unresolved. Because of this, I cannot access my own money, which has caused serious financial difficulties.\n\nP.S. It is not a fault of Deutsch Post. They identify me as in passport. It is in a first place identification problem from Expatrio that identified me wrong.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Da es nur der einzuge Weg hier, Sie zu erreichen komme ich zurück auf die Bewertung von meinem Neffe von 9.7 Chris Ulrich. Er hat sich beschwert weil Sie ihm seit Geld immer noch nicht zurück überwiesen haben und Sie geben als Antwort dass die Sache inzwischen gelöst wurde. Wann denn? Nichts ist gelöst, bitte überweisen Sie sein Geld zurück. Das kind braucht es um zu leben. Sie sagen immer er soll sich melden mit der registrierter E-Mail in ihrer System. Wie oft hat er das schon gemacht? Gestern hat er auch nochmal eine E-Mail geschrieben und  immer noch kein Geld. Das ist wirklich nicht in Ordnung. Seit Januar haben Sie das Geld und das Kind braucht kein Sperrkonto mehr... warum behalten Sie denn sein Geld ?", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Terrible service , with just automated replies and no answers from anyone even after cc with formal complaints. I’ve been trying to release my additional basic sum for my semester fees payment for re registration and I’ve submitted all the proofs needed and still get ghosted after a copy pasted automated reply from the agents . Worst experience in my life . If I don’t get any response in few days then I have to legally file a notice for holding my funds even after submitting the proofs for the release as my deadlines are near and you all playing around with the service . If I miss my registration period due to this irresponsible service then Expatrio will have to be responsible for that .", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The customer service and overall product experience at Expatrio are exceptionally poor. I firmly believe they only manage to survive because there are currently limited alternatives in the market. Once similar services become more popular, Expatrio will undoubtedly be forgotten.\nI opened a blocked account with them to extend my visa in Germany. After my visa extension appointment, the Ausländerbehörde issued me a temporary document (Vorläufige / Fiktionsbescheinigung) while I wait for my physical card to arrive, which takes about a month. I requested Expatrio to release my monthly payout because I am actively living in Germany, this temporary document legally confirms my status, and I urgently needed the money to cover my living expenses.\nInstead of receiving help, I had to wait an incredibly long time for their response. Despite multiple back-and-forth emails, my funds were still not released. The financial strain was so severe that for weeks, I literally had to survive on drinking milk because I couldn't afford food, and I couldn't even pay my rent. I had no choice but to borrow money from friends just to get by.\nRecently, I finally received my physical residence permit card (Aufenthaltstitel) and verified it immediately on the Expatrio app. I emailed them right away, explaining the urgency and hoping for a swift payout to resolve my financial crisis. It has now been 4 days, and I have received absolutely zero reply.\nBecause of Expatrio's negligence and agonizingly slow support, I am about to borrow money for a second time from other people and am facing the very real risk of being evicted by my landlord.\nUser ID: 1218417\n\nUPDATE (July 20, 2026):\n​Expatrio replied to my review claiming their support team would assist me via email. However, the email I received from them is completely useless—it is absolute garbage.\n​They simply sent a generic, copy-pasted message telling me to \"log in to the Expatrio App and activate your Bank Account.\" The ridiculous part is that my bank account has ALREADY been activated long before this! When I log into the app, there is absolutely NO BUTTON to click for a payout, neither in the \"Bank Account\" tab nor the \"Blocked Account\" tab.\n​They clearly didn't even bother to check the actual technical status of my app or account before sending this automated nonsense. My problem is STILL not solved, I still have zero access to my own money, and I am still facing severe financial distress and potential eviction because of their glaring incompetence.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I appreciate Expatrio's services for international students, but I am currently facing a challenge with my blocked account transfer. My bank in Cameroon requires the beneficiary bank's identity details and an official attestation confirming that the account has no irregularities before they can authorize the international transfer for compliance purposes.\n\nI kindly ask Expatrio to assist by contacting their partner bank or providing these documents if possible. This is the only remaining requirement preventing my bank from transferring the funds. I hope the support team can help resolve this quickly. Thank you.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have been waiting for my health insurance confirmation for 8 days now. I am currently in Germany and need this document urgently for my upcoming appointment at the local Ausländerbehörde (Foreigners' Office) to apply for my residence permit.\nI have sent 5 emails to the support team, including urgent requests, but I have received zero response. I have been in direct contact with the insurance provider (DR-WALTER), and they confirmed that my data has not yet been transferred from Expatrio's side. This lack of service is putting my entire residence permit process at risk of being rejected or delayed.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "My Visa appointment date is July 20, 2026. I didn't get insurance till now..\nI got the insurance documents today. Thank you for the response.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Hi Expatrio Team,\n\nI raised my request regarding the additional €400 transfer last Friday, but I am still unable to complete the payment.\n\n Although the payment section has been enabled, the portal only allows me to transfer amounts between €1,141 and €12,447, so I cannot transfer the required €400.\n\n I have already shared the screenshot of the error and all the requested details (country: India, currency: INR, amount: €400).\nThis payment is very important for my student visa application, and my visa process is currently pending because of this issue. I kindly request you to review my case and resolve it as soon as possible so that I can complete the payment today if possible.\n\nThank you very much for your assistance.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Extremely stressed. My visa came late, so my Aion account was suspended. I extended my blocked account, and my last two months of payouts were sent, but they went to an unknown IBAN in my portal that I cannot access. I tried to change the payout IBAN to my personal account, but the portal blocks me with a 'name doesn't match' error. I have sent multiple emails and WhatsApp messages but get only automated bot replies. My Expatrio ID is 1037663. Please, I just need a human agent to contact me so I can send my bank statement and get this manually updated.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Expatrio is withholding my legal visa funds across two unmerged blocked accounts. An agent confirmed the merger on July 6, but they have ignored all emails for weeks. My visa extension expires. Their lack of response is actively putting my legal immigration status in Germany in jeopardy. User ID: 1286997.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Unacceptable withholding of funds : \nNo solution despite full validated documents.\n\nMy cousin,  is currently facing severe financial hardship in Africa because Expatrio is refusing to release his Funds immediately.\n\nHis account closure has been fully approved, and Expatrio has confirmed that all documents and evidence are validated. Despite this, they are keeping his money and delaying the transfer back to the originating bank account. \n\nOur repeated follow-ups have led to absolutely no resolution.\n\nIt is completely unprofessional and legally questionable to hold a customer's money when all compliance checks are completed. We demand an immediate escalation to senior management and the payout team. If a SWIFT transaction receipt is not provided within 24 hours, we will file a formal complaint with the German Federal Financial Supervisory Authority (BaFin).", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The support is very slow to respond. I cannot connect with humans at all. Everything is by a chatbot. I need to add additional unblocked amount to my blocked account urgently for my visa, they told they will verify and get back, its been more than 5 days. Haven't received any update", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I sent an email for clarification of the issue I'm currently facing and for now I haven't heard from them yet. I only got AI generated response which wasn't that much helpful. Aside from that, everything is fine.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Too much e mails just to give a feedbackw", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have been trying to resolve an urgent issue with my blocked account since 9 July 2026, with my German visa deadline on 14 July 2026. The problem was entirely caused by Expatrio's own team — an agent set up an Additional Basic Sum (ABS) of €5,500 in my account without my request, which changed my account status from \"Awaiting for Activation\" to \"Insufficient Funds\" and made my account completely invisible on the Expatrio authorities verification portal. This means the German Embassy cannot verify my blocked amount online.\nDespite this being Expatrio's mistake, getting help has been a nightmare. The AI bot \"Poppy\" is completely useless — it loops the same automated responses endlessly and refuses to connect to a human agent unless you give it specific keywords. When I finally reached a human agent (Michelle) via live chat, she removed the ABS but the \"Insufficient Funds\" error and authorities portal invisibility remain unresolved. My emails are met with automated replies saying high volume may cause delays.\nMy account is fully funded — €17,661 received, €0 pending — and I hold a valid 06 Blocked Amount Confirmation dated 07.07.2026. Yet the portal still shows errors caused entirely by Expatrio's internal mistake.\nThis is unacceptable for a service that students rely on for life-changing visa applications.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Their customer support is almost non-existent. I received health insurance through Expatrio (who state on their website that they shall send the notification to the university directly. However, my university emailed me to state that they have not received any confirmation. I have contacted Expatrio through email, local representative, and even Reddit, and am either met with a chatbot or generic replies that direct me to their FAQ. Very disappointed and worried so far.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "You need quick response to Email", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "As an Indian student, I had a good overall experience using this service for my blocked account. The website is easy to use, and once everything was in place, my payment was processed and my blocked account was opened within 2–3 days, which I found quite efficient.\nHowever, there are a few areas that need improvement. The biggest issue was passport verification. It took around 3 days before I was allowed to send my money, whereas I believe this process should ideally be completed within 24 hours. This delay was stressful because blocked account documents are often time-sensitive for visa applications.\nI was also disappointed with the customer support. I tried using the call service, but there was no response, which made the situation even more frustrating when I needed urgent assistance.\nAnother issue is the website's session management. It logs users out too frequently, even while they are actively using the platform. Having to repeatedly log in, retrieve the OTP from email, and authenticate again is time-consuming and frustrating. It would greatly improve the user experience if active sessions remained logged in for longer.\nOverall, the service is reliable and the blocked account process itself is straightforward, but improving passport verification times, customer support responsiveness, and website session handling would make the experience much better.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The worst customer support. The slowest procedure. Took more than 2 weeks just to verify a single document and Got rejected without any given reasons. No one responds from the customer support or reply to contact forms. Even after response the person just ghosts and does not give you any proper answer or solve your issue", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am currently in Germany and facing a severe financial emergency. My online verification failed due to my passport. Expatrio customer service told me to use the offline Post Office method, but they DID NOT send me the required coupon or barcode.\n\nI have no money left, and nobody is replying to my emails or answering the phone. I cannot even go to the post office without this barcode. Please send my coupon immediately so I can activate my account.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Ich warte seit über sechs Monaten auf die Rückzahlung meiner Kaution. Trotz mehrfacher Nachfragen habe ich das vollständige Geld bis heute nicht erhalten.\nDiese Kaution ist für mich sehr wichtig, da ich auf das Geld angewiesen bin, um meinen Lebensunterhalt zu bestreiten. Es ist enttäuschend, so lange auf eine Rückzahlung warten zu müssen, ohne eine zufriedenstellende Lösung oder klare Informationen zu erhalten.\nIch bitte dringend darum, meine Kaution endlich zurückzuzahlen und mein Anliegen ernst zu nehmen. Ich hoffe, dass dieses Problem schnell gelöst wird.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I had selected value package, transferred funds, received 06 blocked amount confirmation and blocked account statement, however I don't see any insurance under my products and no insurance letter under documents to download. Now waiting since yesterday for a reply from support to get this sorted so I can go ahead with my application to be on the waiting list.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "my stament account and blocked amount letter amount has a varition of 300 dollars", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Expatrio have become greedy. I just wanted to extend my existing block account but was unable to do so. I had to pay unnecessary set-up fee which is for new users. \nExpatrio should understand that its customers are immigrant students who are financially vulnerable and should act fair accordingly. \nEven the banks in Germany do not take monthly fee from students, but greedy Expatrio does.\nThe greed of owners to loot vulnerable communities runs deep.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I Smooth but delayed response and Euro 5 monthly deduction without active Bank account.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "When urgent matters need to be resolved immediately, your response time takes an unforeseeably long time.\nHowever, when it comes to basic small matters that require no thought, you can reply instantly.\nShame, do better on your customer service", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "After following explicit instructions from your team regarding my blocked account setup, I am now receiving completely conflicting information. To make matters worse, your automated systems are preventing me from speaking to a real person. I have tried calling and using your support chatbot multiple times, but it completely refuses to transfer me to a live agent or escalate my case to a supervisor. Instead, the bot loops me back to an email address that does not reply.\nYou are holding my blocked account funds, yet you are blocking all human communication channels to resolve a mistake made by your own team.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Title: URGENT: Visa deadline July 10th at risk due to support error - ID 1341943\n\nReview: My German visa deadline is this Friday, July 10th. The Embassy has strictly mandated that my TK Insurance Certificate reflect my university address (ISM Frankfurt Campus). Your support team incorrectly told me to contact TK, but TK confirmed that only Expatrio has backend system authority to modify unactivated profile data.I have sent a formal escalation to formal-complaints Because time is running out, I need a supervisor to manually update my profile address and regenerate my TK certificate today. My Expatrio ID is 1341943. Please help.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I believe that if you will have and application for international people or for traveling or for international studies, you may have a better and updated system that may work with Safari and Google Chrome to avoid misleading information and misunderstandings. I try to get help several times and it makes you wait for an email that is barely answered with very important information and assistance from the AI and the agent.  I understand that rules and loss from the hosting country may ask for requirements and military actions to be taken, but it will be also the reason why Expatrio should have a better and quick quicker customer service response.  Instructions are clear, but not easy to follow. But once you get used to it and you arrive to your destination, the activation, the confirmation, the transfer of funds is very intuitive and systematic, which I love and made me change my mind from a one star to a three stars rate on my experience.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "A real disappointment! I’ve been using Expatrio regularly for my blocked account for the past two years, so I’m a long-term customer. The moment I had a problem, absolutely no one was there to help.\n\nThere isn’t even a customer support phone number you can call. When you send an email, you only receive replies from an AI bot saying that someone will contact you—but that never actually happens.\n\nIf you ever experience an issue with Expatrio, like I did—where your money is deducted but the payment is declined—there is simply no one you can reach to resolve the problem.\n\nIn my case, the money was deducted from my account twice, even though both payments were declined.\n\nIf you value your money and don’t want to risk being left without support when something goes wrong, I cannot recommend using Expatrio. NEVER CHOOSE THEM otherwise you MUST say Goodbye! to your money (TWICE AMOUNT)  like I have to do now", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I transferred funds from my bank account in Vietnam to my blocked account. After the transfer was initiated, I was informed by customer support on June 19 that UniCredit, the banking partner, required proof of the relationship between me and the account holder of the sending bank account. I provided the requested documentation promptly.\n\nDespite submitting the required document, the transfer was still rejected and the funds were returned. However, I was not informed of the specific reason for the rejection. When I contacted my bank in Vietnam, they also confirmed that they had not received any detailed explanation from the receiving bank.\n\nAs a result, I incurred international transfer fees and now need to resend the funds. Before making another transfer, I would like to understand the exact reason for the rejection to ensure the issue is resolved and to avoid the same problem occurring again.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am a U.S. citizen who legally entered Germany and applied for the Opportunity Card (Chancenkarte) from within Germany, which is permitted under German immigration rules. To complete my residence permit application, my Expatrio blocked account must be activated.\n\nHowever, my blocked account has still not been activated.\n\nI have submitted all requested documentation and have spent weeks working with Expatrio's support team. Throughout this process, I received contradictory information. On multiple occasions, I was informed that my issue had been resolved or that my blocked account had been fixed, only to discover that nothing had changed. At other times, I was asked to submit additional documentation after having already provided the requested documents. This made it extremely difficult to understand what was actually required to move my application forward.\n\nAs of today, my issue remains unresolved. The repeated delays, inconsistent communication, and lack of clear guidance have unnecessarily prolonged my immigration process.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I submitted a transaction dispute on June 11th because €18.94 was debited by Aion Bank for a failed food order (Transaction ID: 219c9d22-9445-43a0-9715-2baec8e0d920). The restaurant never received the order. I have sent multiple emails to expatrio support email and messaged on WhatsApp with the official UniCredit PDF confirmation, but I have received absolutely zero responses. Please have a human agent contact me immediately to resolve this.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Absolutely ridiculous the amount of steps you need to go to just to open your bank account. Not only is there a video verification for your face and passport but further documents are required. Worse is the documents are reviewed by AI!! And the AI screener isn't reading my documents correctly at all. I've provided my rental agreement and Meldebestätigung but neither are being recognized as proof of address. My documents have been refected 4 times. Another option is to upload a letter from my health insurance. But my isurance is tied to Expatrio!! If I had know the amount of hoops I needed to jump through just to open my bank account with my own money in it I would never choose expatrio. I am stuck in limbo because I need an IBN to pay for a phone bill, internet, and my insurance. I feel like I've been left out to dry with an emptyimg American bank account. What's the point of a block account if I can't even use it", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Overall, the experience was smooth and simple, very clear and streamlined. But my issue is mainly with the fees charged by Flywire (their only exchange rate processing partner now) for processing the Blocked account amount. For me it was almost ₹7.5K (~70 euros) higher than what was charged by WISE for the same transfer amount. In that sense, what I feel personally is that it's better for and in Expatrio's interest to partner with WISE for offering students a better value than with Flywire. \nAlso, on another note Expatrio is 50 euros costlier than Coracle overall, mainly due to their monthly service fee, although their initial setup fee is 10 euros lesser. Now, its set to increase further by 78 euros from 7th July 2026. (JFYI Coracle has paused onboarding new applications currently (June 2026) due to their stated banking infrastructure upgrades. \n\nOverall hope to see Expatrio offer more value to students at a much more competitive fare compared to their peers. (btw they are much cheaper than Fintiba at least)\nThanks & All the Best", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It's been 22 days passed since I Raised the closing request but haven't received my funds back.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "A legalised scam.\nNo one is available for customer support. They take your money, charge you for it, and do not give it back for months. The number does not work, neither does the live chat. Look for other alternatives", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Awful service, bad application, and delays on money transfers.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Customer service response time, and no compassion.I paid twice for a block account 89+30 & 89+30 due for a single visa extension, due to confusion in visa and activation process.\n\nI would recommend if you are in Germany and need block account. search better options. First of all there response time is super late no direct contact via email or etc just a AI Robot and some fixed templates.\nBanking and a Visa processing both are time critical processes so timing is important and a physical human unfortunately they don’t have both.\n\nI had a far better experience with Coracle, Sparkasse Sperkonto and Fintiba. \nI perfer Sparkasse sperkonto they charge you once, for openings etc, here you need every time 89 euros. Too expensive and sorry for services. \n\nIn my case I had a visa extension and applied for blocked account so even though it was a 6 month process they charged me full price. After that, I had some issues with visa so VO asked me to resubmit it due to some issue due to threshold requirements, I requested them I didn’t received my VISA, please send a new letter with given requirements, and kindly redeem my double fee because the purpose is not served. They told me first do this procedure extend this,  and after that they issued me letter of 56 euros monthly payout for 6 months and 89 euros fee and 30 euros for further processing.\n\nWell I requested them but they said we can’t waive this, until you send that your visa is rejected etc I am already in Germany how my visa is rejected, nevertheless, I had worse experience with them.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am extremely disappointed and stressed by the absolute lack of professionalism from this company. I opened a blocked account with them for my German visa process, and their system errors are currently jeopardizing my entire legal status in Germany.\nTwo major issues have completely stalled my immigration process:\nDeficient Documentation: The blocking confirmation (Sperrbestätigung) they provided completely omits the start and end dates of the blocked period. The German Embassy/Ausländerbehörde strictly requires these dates. Because of this missing information, the embassy rejected my document.\nSystem Error & Financial Deficit: During the first month, they made a double deposit/payout mistake on their end. This internal error artificially depleted my balance. Instead of taking responsibility and fixing their own technical glitch, their support team told me that I have to pay extra money to extend the account just to get a corrected document.\nTo make matters worse, their customer service is incredibly slow, taking more than 5 days to reply to urgent emails with generic answers that offer no real solutions. My visa is about to expire, and I am facing a critical deadline.\nDo not trust this service if your visa depends on it. They make automated mistakes, deplete your funds, give you incomplete documents, and expect you to pay for their errors while ignoring your urgent emails.\nI demand that management looks into my case immediately, fixes my balance, and issues a proper confirmation with exact dates.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "their customer service is very slow. their poppy agent keeps replying with the same replies over and over again. it took them 5 days to respond to me", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I requested to get an additional document for transferring my Tuition fees. I tried many time but my issues not yet solved\n\nSorry to mention it. If possible, Please help", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I get my Monat after 3 months!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I contacted Expatrio several times regarding my queries, but unfortunately I did not receive responses to the questions I raised. I was informed that the standard processing time would take between 3 and 6 days; however, in my case, the process took nearly 20 days without a clear explanation for the delay.\nAlthough my case was eventually approved, I still did not receive satisfactory answers to my concerns or sufficient clarification about the process. This was disappointing, especially since many students highly recommend Expatrio and I expected a more transparent and responsive experience.\nI appreciate the final approval of my case, but I hope communication and customer support can be improved for future applicants.\nThank you.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "At first I thought it was a scam but now am confident about it.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The decision to make flywire mandatory for transfer is not good because it's 2x expensive than other competitors. It's like forcing students to pay through them. when I did my first transfer I had freedom to choose the sending method but at the last transaction I was forced to pay 2x fees because your your rule.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "My transfer to my Expatrio blocked account has been unresolved for more than 3 weeks despite several complaints and almost daily emails to support.\n\nI’m an international student applying for Studienkolleg in Germany, and I need my Blocked Account Confirmation in order to apply for a visa.\n\nOn May 22, I transferred the required money to my Expatrio blocked account: one transfer via an international bank transfer from South Korea and another via Wise. Both of them were confirmed by the sending institutions on the same day. But I still cannot get my Blocked Account Confirmation document because the funds are simply not reflected in my Expatrio account.\n\nI contacted support multiple times. At first, my emails were simply ignored. Eventually, I received a response requesting transfer documents, which I provided immediately. Then, on June 2, one Expatrio support agent explicitly confirmed in writing that both transfers had been received:\n\n\"We received two incoming transfers in your Blocked Account, one for €5040 and another one for €1581, both on May 22nd.\"\n\nWell, where is the money then? How am I supposed to obtain my blocked account confirmation? Another week of being ignored.\n\nSuddenly, another support agent directly contradicted this statement and claimed that no transfer had been received at all. Like ????\n\nAt this point, I genuinely have no idea what is going on here. One person says the money is there, another says it isn’t. Emails go unanswered for days, and even formal complaints seem to lead nowhere.\n\nComplete lack of coordination, transparency, and actual support.\n\nI really hope Expatrio resolves this soon because right now, the experience is far from positive. This is not how a company handling something as important as student finances and visa-related documentation should operate.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I liked the fact that I got my receipt on time.\n\nI disliked the fact that the contact was slow to respond to my inquiries.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I struggled with Expatrio to activate the blocked account. I have visited post office 3 times and i could not. It was not a good start as i was struggling for money. Some of my friends got compensation gift for this issues happened, but i did not received that.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Customer Service is awful! It took 10 days to transfer my money. There is no way to reach out to a Human Agent! AI Agent is sometimes not helpful, especially when technical support is needed. Thank you", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Ich bin am 04.05 in Deutschland angekommen, meine Monatliche Zahlungen sind immer noch nicht da und wir haben schon 11.06. Kundenservice telefonisch nicht erreichbar und wenn sprechen sie so einen Englisch dass man nichts verstehen kann. Auf Emails wird nicht geantwortet. Ich würde jedem davon abraten.\nMuss jetzt wohl Anwalt einschalten um an mein Geld zu kommen.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Their customer supports are very worst. Everything they manage through an AI agent. Mostly that agent understand wrong. and they don't have any help line number either.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Need better accessibility for customers to contact customer care. I fond it difficult to find the CC mail id and find a human support. It took me more than 1 week to resolve my issue. This may improve your service.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Everything is good; however, I believe there should be support available for customers who have queries. The chatbot was not always helpful, and it took me considerable time to figure out the transaction process on my own. Since this was a high-value transaction, I expected to speak with one of your agents before making the payment", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I’m extremely disappointed with my experience with Expatrio’s blocked account support.\n\nI am a student at FH - Dortmund University of Applied Sciences and Arts \n\nI completed my PostIdent verification at the post office, but due to issues on the post office side, my verification did not go through properly. Since then, my blocked account activation has been stuck.\n\n\nWhat has been most frustrating is the lack of real support throughout this process. Most of my emails were answered with automated or bot-like responses, with no clear resolution or proper escalation.\n\nAfter multiple attempts, I finally managed to reach a support agent last Friday. I immediately offered to travel to Frankfurt for an in-person verification to resolve the issue as quickly as possible.\n\n\nSince then, I have received no response, no appointment, and no update at all.\n\nThis situation has become very serious for me, as I am currently unable to access funds needed for basic living expenses. The delay and lack of communication have made an already stressful situation much worse.\nI understand that technical issues can happen, but the absence of timely communication or a clear resolution path is unacceptable for a service that is essential for international students and visa holders.\n\nI hope this feedback helps improve their support process, but based on my experience so far, I cannot recommend relying on their customer service in urgent situations.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am not happy with the deal and the mechanism regarding the buffer transfer.\n\nIt is unfair for the people transfer the blocked amount from Germany or EU because we technically don't get deduction on our 100 euro buffer during the remittance. Even if so, I don't understand why Expatrio don't send the buffer in the first month when all the charges including initial fee and account management fee are transferred already. \n\nYou are nearly a monopolist in the market, the initial fee is getting too expensive while no extra services actually included for the past few years. Application only for the \"extension\" of the block account cost 89 euro initial fee doesn't make sense. Recommended to provide discounts price for old user as we already pay the monthly service fee. Else I would really go for Coracle once they are back with their service.\n\nTwo stars are for the easy use interface and fast confirmation of the required documents. \n\nAdding one more drawback, when it comes to activate the blocked account, it requires identification check in order to open the the bank account. However, there's no option at the first place for people who hold the resident permit, instead, all the options are different type of Visa. The instructions and potions are not compressive enough, so it takes longer to actually activate the account. Again, this is not friendly for the old user or whoever already lived in Germany.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Late response", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am extremely frustrated with the service regarding my blocked account activation.\n\nI completed my PostIdent verification 5 days ago, and my blocked account is still not activated. This delay is causing serious inconvenience, especially since this is a time-sensitive matter for international students and newcomers who depend on timely access to their account status.\n\nWhat is even more disappointing is the complete lack of communication. I have contacted Expatrio customer support multiple times, but I have not received any response, update, or explanation regarding the delay. As a customer, I expect transparency and professional support, especially when important financial services are involved.\n\nI chose Expatrio because of its reputation and expected reliable service. However, my current experience has been extremely disappointing. Waiting for more than five days without any update is unacceptable, and the absence of customer support only makes the situation worse.\n\nI urgently request that my case be reviewed immediately and that I receive a clear update on the status of my blocked account activation. Customers should not be left waiting without information or assistance.\n\nI sincerely hope Expatrio improves its communication and customer support processes to prevent other customers from facing the same frustrating experience.\n\nAwaiting an urgent resolution.\nsubramanya cm\nsubramanyabharathi77@\n+4915216603245\nMagdeburg, Germany", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Overall, my experience with Expatrio was mixed.\n\nOne of the positive aspects was the health insurance service. The insurance process was completed very quickly, and all required documents were provided on the same day.\n\nHowever, I was disappointed with the blocked account transfer process. According to the information provided, transfers are expected to be completed within 1–5 business days. Unfortunately, my transfer took longer than 5 business days, which caused significant stress because my visa appointment was approaching.\n\nIn addition, communication during the process was difficult. Customer support responses often seemed automated, and it was not always easy to obtain clear information about the status of my transfer. Since the payment provider required additional verification, I had to spend considerable time contacting both Flywire and Expatrio.\n\nAlthough the issue was eventually resolved and my funds arrived successfully, the delay meant that my blocked account confirmation did not arrive before my visa appointment. As a result, I had to submit the document to the consulate afterward as an additional document.\n\nI believe the customer experience could be improved by providing more transparent transfer tracking and faster, more personalized support when delays occur.\n\nThank you for your attention to this feedback.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Need to improve on your service's", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "No response at all", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Estoy intentando tener acceso a mi cuenta desde abril 2026. Y todavia no he recibido mi dinero.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "no response for query", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Service is quite slow.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am writing to provide feedback regarding the identity verification process, as my experience has been quite frustrating.\n\nYesterday, I encountered several issues while trying to verify my document. The first specialist told me that my name was missing and that I needed to enter it before logging in. However, I could not find any section in the application to provide this information. After restarting the app, I was able to proceed without being prompted for a name.\n\nThe second specialist I spoke with asked for my name and information while viewing my ID. During the call, she mistakenly asked me to type in a code meant for a different type of verification. But she apologized so everything was ok. It is very disappointing to learn that my name was recorded incorrectly despite the specialist having my details, especially since I was not asked to verify the spelling during the process.\n\nI find it unprofessional that I now have to repeat the entire verification process due to these errors. I hope you can take this feedback into account to improve the service.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Extemely slow responses, AI chat bot replies which are useless , Not paying attention to an urgent matter ! I am stuck at my visa renewal process and i am trying to add a new blocked account to my already existing Expatrio account which has my old Blocked account as closed.\n\nI am in Urgent need of attention , My document verification is pending ( Certificate of Matriculation which previously got done in just 1 day) I am deeply concerned about my application and my Residence Permit extension here .", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It is impossible to get personal assistance with anything from Expatrio. They made me aware 10 days ago that I would need to submit visa documentation. I submitted it exactly as requested, the automated service rejected it citing that I needed to submit it in the exact way that I submitted it. To be sure I also submitted it in the exact opposite way thinking that they may have just worded things poorly. My document was never reviewed and they have now suspended my bank account. I now have no money, and if I wished to return to the US at this time I would have no financial way to do so. I have had to take over three days off from the reason I am in Germany just to deal with this issue and wait on hold for hours with no answer. I have never before dealt with a support system this incompetent.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Iv been reaching out to Expatrio support for 3-4 days but Iv got no reply", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Service. Im trying to get my account verifired for my payouts from last 4-5 days. No response. Uploaded all documents, sent per email also went for postident verification also. No response no customer service support no reply to emails  \nThey have 1 phone number i called 11 times it was always. There is no agent available to take your calls and their phone support is knky for 3 hours.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I‘ve applied for my Blocked Account since 25th of May, 2026 from Myanmar. My passport has been approved, but my blocked account has been awaiting verification and is in Review for 11 days. I have my Visa appointment on the 9th of June, and I still have to transfer money into the bank account once I get my Confirmation Email. My University program starts on 15th June so it is putting me in a tight spot.\nUser ID - 1426223", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "very bad services.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I tride to activate my block account from last 20 days and still not activate i went duech post with 2 3 time and still not active. I try to contact customer service no response my fund is freez in account. Dont use this", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "My account is not het activated", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Useless customer service. I transferred my blocked account funds to Expatrio, but their app is completely glitched on the document review screen and locks me out of finalizing my activation. To make it worse, their customer care only sends automated AI replies telling me to wait or travel 5 hours away to Frankfurt for an in-person verification because their PostIdent partner is broken.\nI live in Schweinfurt and cannot make a 5-hour trip just because Expatrio's digital system fails. I have already sent email copies of my passport and both sides of my German residence permit (Aufenthaltstitel).\nI need a human manager to manually review my case under my name (Nikhil Moolekkadan Padmarajan), bypass the app glitch, and release my 3 months of backdated payouts from March, April, and May 2026 immediately. If this is not resolved, I will file a formal complaint with the BaFin regulator for withholding my funds.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am currently experiencing a serious issue with my blocked account verification process.\n\nI completed the POSTIDENT identity verification twice at a German post office using two different reference IDs generated by Expatrio. After completing the first verification, my account continued to request identity verification and generated a new reference ID. I then completed the verification a second time, but my account is still asking me to verify my identity again.\n\nAs a student in Germany, I urgently need access to my blocked account funds to pay rent and cover essential living expenses. I have already spent significant time traveling to the post office multiple times and following all instructions provided.\n\nThe most frustrating part is that I have not received a clear explanation as to why the completed verifications are not being processed or why new verification requests continue to be generated.\n\nI hope Expatrio reviews my case promptly, provides a clear update on the status of my previous verifications, and resolves this issue as soon as possible.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Hubieron días que ni pude consignar y la respuesta que me daba soporte era leer el instructivo", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Expatrio’s support service is very very poor. But you are ready to always send me messages to put my hard earned money in the blocked account. I have been unable to submit my visa application since yesterday thanks you your poor service. The health insurance certificate issued to me does not fully support my application and I need a travel insurance certificate alongside. I have mentioned it in the help support ticket. No one is yet to address my issue and this is stopped me from submitting my online visa application. Expatrio needs to employ more hands of the current support team are unable to address customers issues under 24 hours. \n\n\nThanks for letting me know never to choose Expatrio again.\n\n\nI was trying to reply to your message but I couldn’t. Well, Expatrio claimed my issue was resolved. It was not by the way, until I withdrew my application for that particular purpose. \n\nReiterating again, my issue was NEVER resolved. Shitty customer service.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "They told me to come to Frankfurt for in person verification. I went there and done with my verification. but here comes the twist They said  ”I should wait. Within 24hrs I’ll get a mail about my passport being verified, if i didn’t get any mail they told me to mail you them”. Its already been 48hrs and still no they didn't revert back to my mail. Students were struggling due to this situation by Expatrio.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Really bad experience, I came to Germany 2 months ago nd I didn’t receive money from my blocked account. As an Indian I didn’t had a video identification option and I had to go to DHL to verify myself . But even after verification I waited 2 days to activate my account , but it asked me to go to post office again to verify myself. Until now I have been to post office at least 5 times and when emailed them an AI respond the same thing and no resolution was given until now", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "CRITICAL UPDATE June 3rd: Your system is a total nightmare! After my urgent request to change the monthly payout to 0.00 EUR for the German authority, your incompetent support completely messed up my account.You automatically changed my account to a student account and are now demanding a completely wrong payment of € 10,338! This is absolute nonsense. My required € 3,378.00 is ALREADY FULLY PAID and received by UniCredit since days!Because of your massive system error, my partner's visa application next Tuesday is in extreme danger. I need a HUMAN MANAGER to immediately fix this mess, reverse the € 10,338 demand, and issue the correct 06 Blocking Confirmation with € 3,378 total and € 0.00 monthly payout. Fix your IT error right now!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Very disappointing experience with Expatrio.\n\nI carefully followed every instruction in the app to unlock my blocked account and open the bank account. I uploaded all required documents successfully and completed every step exactly as requested.\n\nThe app then instructed me to download the PostIdent coupon and verify my identity at a Postfiliale. I completed this process multiple times over 5–6 days, visited different post offices, generated new coupons repeatedly, showed my identification documents, signed where required, and each time the staff confirmed that the verification was completed successfully.\n\nHowever, nothing was reflected in the application. The app continued showing the same instructions and repeatedly asked me to verify again as if the previous attempts never happened.\n\nAs an international student, this delay has had real consequences. I have spent time, money, and energy repeating the same process with no progress and very limited communication or resolution.\n\nI understand that technical issues can happen, but asking users to repeat the same completed verification process over and over without clear updates is unacceptable.\n\nI hope Expatrio reviews and improves this process for future students.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "When trying to update my information on the app and website (arrival/departure dates, addresses, nationality) there are areas that explicitly state under the box that only Support can update this information. However regardless Support will say to simply click and update it myself and when I reply stating it is not possible and something only Expatrio can update, there will be several days without a reply and said email reply will avoid addressing the issue, instead closing the conversation and asking me to review the application.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It was decent experience not bad but not good too.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I’ve been trying to unblock my account and its been hard. It failed and I don’t have any support by the expatrio team. I need access my money to buy food and my basic needs but no one has halped me.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I think e very thing ist good", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Should give the user freedom of choosing their own way to transfer money to blocked account rather than forcing them to use flywire", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The account review took so much time, and now verification system is so dumb. you should work on review and verification process alot.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "On May 14th i reached in Germany, still now I didn't get my blocked account money to use. The problem is Personal identity verification didn't completed. But 3 times I go for personal identity verification to post office, and purposefully completed the all procedures in Post office for 3 times. Still the expatrio side saying didn't completed identity verification. Here I struggling each day's my hand money is getting over. I don't know what to do there is no reply from expatrio side. If I get any trouble or problems it's full responsible for expatrio.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Hi Expatrio\n\nMy name is Mohith Kolli \nDOB: 08.June.2000\n\nI'm facing the issue of activation of my Blocked account. \nAfter that I went to postident office, verify myself. Even on the postident app, It says my verification process is completed. But just after doing the verification status changes to awaiting activation with the activate button ( which makes no sense ) I thought it's some kind of bug. Then again I went for the verification in postident office and it still shows the same. \n\nPlease Help me with this because I have to pay my rent and also my semester fee for my next semester.\n\n\nThanks & Regards\nMohith Kolli.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "My overall al experience is good, but  sometimes. I need urgent documents or made some mistakes the expatrio takes very much time to resolve the issue. As I am facing issue of value package. I made blocked account without taking value package. I need value package because I want health and travel insurance both from expatrio for my visa process and enrollment in my University. Neither my health insurance was confirmed to university nor my travel insurance issue was resolved. \nI really want these issues to be resolved. Expatrio is very cooperative but sometimes very slow.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Please please do not use Expatrio services if you wantto save yourself the trouble of your funds being stuck with them for months with no response from anyone from customer care.\nI have my funds with them even after providing them necessary doumentation and no one from customer care responds. The only next option for me to go is legal.\nI am waiting for my funds to be release from the last 3 months even after giving them the necessary documents\n\n5/6/26- They have put a response after this review about submitting a document which is not true. I had already submitted the document and it took them two months to tell me that a signature is missing . Two months to tell me that they need IBAN number instead of account number and I am still waiting. This is definetely a spam where the money is locked.They do not have an escalation point and I am still waiting for one\n7/6: Still waiting with no response to my last email after updating everything they wanted for second time", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "My block account is not activating at all,when I asked for the reason they didn't even reply back.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Still now the activation issue is not resolved from your end. \nVery bad experience with expatrio, please try to resolve it", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "This is really frustrating to see that no one is replying to my mails for days and not giving proper resolution to my issue..", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I had a bad experience with this app.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am facing a lot of trouble with the verification process in order to get my monthly payouts started. After my city registration as per the instruction I did my verification by visiting nearest post office for postident on thursdays 7th May, I got an email on the same day saying \"your block account is confirmed and we have received your transfer\" this mail has been already sent to me when I tranferred the money in month of march. And the verification process gets back to the visting post office phase in the application. I though maybe a glitch so I waited a 3-5 business days as per other students experience to receive money in the account, but nothing, I sent an email stating this issue and asking for a solution, they sent me a response after 48 hours which is not within the time frame they have given on website, then in that email they ask me to visit their office in Berlin, how is that feasible for a student leaving in Kaiserlautern to travel to Berling and handle the hight cost of travel and other associated expenses, and they gave one more option that is to change the block account provider and that will refund my any fees charged as well. Changing provider will cost me 3 weeks of more time in order to get my money how is this an acceptable response. I tried to do my verification again in case that could work and I can get my monet without the hassle, so I went today to the postbank for my postident again, and within 2 hours received the same email stating, \"your block account is confirmed and we have received your tranfer\" and the application status went to pending verification again. I now accepted to come to Berlin as my only option to get my money faster, but the new problem is I am not getting any fixed appointment date now, I have replied since Sunday to your email that I can come visit the office, please give me the appointment but no response, how much do I have to beg and follow up for my own money? Is this a joke to you, I trusted you with all my money that is supposed to help me survive here and you are now behaving as such you are giving me the money(as if its yours) and I have to cry to get it.\n\nPlease I request you give me an appointment and get this sorted our quickly.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Response to Expatrio's reply -\nAtleast have some courtesy to notify the customer that your team is planing to cancel my existing digital debit card and reissue a new debit card for the suggested reasons. As a customer, I have some auto debit service features which has been affected due to this sudden change without notification. PLEASE DO NOT MAKE CHANGES TO MY ACCOUNT WITHOUT NOTIFYING ME, NOR WITHOUT CUSTOMERS CONSENT.\n\n______________________________\n\nI am extremely disappointed with my experience regarding the physical debit card service.\n\nI applied for a physical debit card and paid EUR 10 for it more than a year ago. Despite multiple follow-ups and repeated assurances that the card was “out for delivery”, I never received it. Several replacement cards were reportedly dispatched, yet none ever reached me.\n\nThroughout this entire period, I had to rely only on the digital card while the paid physical card service was never fulfilled. What is even more frustrating is that after I requested a refund instead of further delivery attempts, I was informed that refunds are not possible as per policy.\n\nCharging customers for a service that was never successfully delivered and keeping them waiting for over a year is unacceptable. I hope this issue is reviewed seriously and handled better for future customers.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "We are facing a horrible experience with Expatrio.\nWe completed verification at the designated post office and each time we were asked to do re-verification. Obviously the error is with Expatrio.\nAs a result, my son is deprived of his funds and is finding it difficult to manage expenses.\nExpatrio is not offering any solutions nor letting us know what needs to be done.\nThey are enjoying interest on our funds while my son is struggling to manage expenses.\nExpatrio need to pay back our money in case they are unable to credit our money.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "My blocked account is not active and a lot of people i know who are stuck said me to go to berlin for this", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Very disappointing experience with Expatrio blocked account activation.\n\nI successfully transferred the blocked amount and completed the POSTIDENT verification at a Deutsche Post branch. My passport was scanned, my signature was taken, and the process was confirmed at the branch.\n\nHowever, despite completing the verification correctly, the account activation failed afterward in their system. I was then told that the only remaining option was to travel from Trier to Berlin for a 15-minute in-office verification appointment or open a completely new blocked account with another provider.\n\nAs an international student, this creates unnecessary financial burden, travel expenses, missed university classes, stress, and delays in accessing my own funds. The issue appears to be affecting multiple students, not just me.\n\nWhile the support team replies politely, the verification and activation process feels poorly coordinated when technical issues occur. Students should not have to spend additional money and time travelling across Germany to access funds that were already transferred successfully.\n\nI strongly recommend future students carefully compare blocked account providers and consider customer support quality and verification reliability before choosing Expatrio.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Dear Expatrio Support Team,\n\nI am writing to express my concern regarding the delay in resolving my blocked account verification issue.\n\nI have already completed the POSTIDENT identity verification process twice at a Deutsche Post office and submitted all the required documents. However, my account status is still not updated, and I continue receiving emails asking me to repeat the verification process.\n\nAdditionally, I contacted support regarding this issue, but I have not received any response even after 4 days. This delay is causing serious inconvenience, especially since the blocked account activation is important for my stay and financial access in Germany.\n\nI kindly request you to urgently review my application manually, confirm the verification status, and resolve this issue as soon as possible.\n\nMy details:\nName: Surigi Yashwanth\n\n\n\nPlease treat this matter as urgent and provide an update at the earliest.\n\nBest regards,\nSurigi Yashwanth", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "worst customer service in any app i have used ever, run.away.from.it.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I still haven't able to activate my blocked account. I did my postident but then now again it shows i have to complete the pestident again and its been weeks still haven't got any proper update from the support team as well. Im struggling without the money.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "They took my personal information to solve my issue and after all the validation steps they just replied they are not going to solve it. This was the second time I was complaining about. Definitely stay away from this company, no contact support and no efforts to solve complaints at all.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Whenever someone emails you or tries to reach you, it takes a long time to get any reply. You should really focus on reducing this response time.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have been living for more than 5 years in Germany ,and the process for opening a new account is same as for a new comer , waste of time and take long time .", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Since 3 weeks I don’t have satisfaction and I ´ve been ignored", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Very bad, unable to unblock my account even after 20 days in Germany, asking me to travel to Berlin from Paderborn", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I arrived in Germany 3 weeks ago and my blocked account is still not activated. I already tried completing the verification at the post office (PostIdent), but the issue is still not resolved. Because of this delay, I am facing serious problems with accessing my funds. Please resolve this issue as soon as possible.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Hi this is Sandeep Joshi Tirumalasetty.\nI am trying to activate my expatrio account in germany and i scanned the postal code and all procedures but again it restarts from starting. And I did this for more than five times. Just solve this issue and try to understand my current situation, and I am struggling with some financial aids.\nPlease solve as soon as possible.\n\nThank you.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The tie up with flywire makes very tough for indian students for transferring maney with very huge transfer charges i personally transferred 14600 euros where i have got only 14049 euros to my account which is 50,000 in indian rupees for 15,64,000/-, which is 2% interest for the amount for 3 moths. \n\nAll this happened just because you guys tied up with flywire which is not accepting indian rupees to convert to euros, so the flywire is taking rupees from students converting them to dollars with 2 rupees extra for converting rupees to dollars and the converting dollars to euros for depositing into expatrio which comes around 5.25/- rupees extra per euro, which is a very huge margin for students to transfer money to expatrio", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I went to activate my account to postident and the employe told me my passport is not verifiable????\nBut it's my passport.\nHow am I supposed to activate my account now?", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have completed the post office address verification \nBut it still says i have to do it again \nAnd its seems to be very tedious processes and timing taking", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Absolutely terrible experience with Expatrio.\n\nTheir verification and account activation system is completely broken. My blocked account has already been opened, and yet I still cannot access my own money from last one week because their system keeps failing again and again.\n\nThe app constantly redirects me in circles asking me to activate an account which I have already did multiple times. I visited multiple DHL/PostIdent branches, followed every instruction, uploaded documents, and still received almost no real support.\n\nWhat shocked me the most was their response to the situation. Instead of actually solving the issue, I was told to come to Berlin even though I live all the way in Krefeld. They also suggested opening another account somewhere else. What kind of solution is that when a customer already cannot access their own money?\n\nCustomer service responses are slow, confusing, and completely lacking urgency for serious financial situations. Because of their faulty system and poor communication, I am almost left with no money for basic expenses at this point.\n\nFor a company focused on international students and blocked accounts, this experience has been unbelievably stressful and disappointing.\n\nI would strongly advise others to be very careful before trusting Expatrio with something as important as your finances and visa-related banking.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I didnt recieved my blocked amount till now Totally disappointed.\nI've already done the activation procedures and verification in the post office \nBut still it redirect to the activation page and I didn't received my blocked amount", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "No proper response from your customer service side. For more than one week", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I arrived in Germany just before April 2026 with an Expatrio blocked account. It is middle of May now and my blocked account still hasn't been activated. \nI am extremely frustrated and disappointed with the way my blocked account activation has been handled. I completed the PostIdent verification in the post office successfully three times, yet my account is still not activated because of your incompetence. The Expatrio app is stuck in a loop of asking for the same verification which I had already completed.\n\nBecause of Expatrio's delay and lack of support, I am now struggling to pay for basic necessities like food and rent. I have tried every possible way to contact the Expatrio team, but the human on WhatsApp support chat disappeared without replying, there has been no response from the contact form on the website, and even the WhatsApp bot is not working for me anymore.\n\nAt this point, I am even willing to personally go to Expatrio's Berlin office because I have been left with no other option, but the support system even failed to provide an appointment to me. The way vulnerable international students are being treated in such situations is unfair and cruel. An appointment in the Berlin office would greatly help me to solve the issue. \n\nI demand an immediate resolution of my case.\n\n\nExpatrio User ID:  1268545", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have gone to the post office twice to verify my identity, but my blocked account is still not activated. Is this the experience you are giving to your customers? How can we live abroad without money if you've kept ours? Not recommended.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am struggling to activate my expatrio blocked account.Iam not satisfied by your service", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "1. My passport was reviewed 4 days (from May 4 to May 8). But you say you can review it in 24 hours.\n2. Everytime I log in the website (even in a few minutes), I have to receive one spam email.\n3. The flywire payment is very unfriendly to Chinese. However, you could have made a clear direction for direct remittance as before.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I completed the DHL PostIdent verification process successfully three times at a DHL branch in Kronach, Germany. However, after each successful verification, the application returns to the activation page and asks me to complete the verification again. My blocked account status still shows “Awaiting activation.”\n\nI kindly request you to check my verification status and activate my blocked account or help resolve this technical issue as soon as possible.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "As an international student newly arrived in Germany, I am writing to express my deep frustration and mental exhaustion regarding the absolute failure of your verification system. It is unacceptable that the technical breakdown of your PostIdent and IDnow platforms—services that are entirely your responsibility—has become my personal burden to solve. I am currently living in Wiesbaden with restricted access to my own funds for food and rent, yet your only \"solution\" is to demand I spend my remaining money on a 10-hour round trip to Berlin for a 15-minute appointment that should have been completed digitally. Suggesting I change providers is an insult, as that would leave me without insurance or money for another month. It is honestly traumatizing to be in a new country facing such systemic incompetence without any offer of travel reimbursement or remote alternatives like Zoom. Expatrio needs to stop offloading its technical failures onto vulnerable students and should, at the very least, have verification hubs in major cities like Frankfurt or Munich to prevent this kind of physical and financial hardship.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have big problems regarding my Blocked Account activation", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have completed the DHL verification 2 time again I am getting the mail like I should do verification one More time and still now I didn't receive the money", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Not responding to mail or whatsapp support", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The helpline takes so much time to reply the mails", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "too slow to respond to questions and inquiries, only chatbot is responding", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am extremely disappointed and frustrated with Expatrio's service. My bank account was suspended despite me providing proof that I have applied for my residence permit at the local authorities in Bremen. I sent multiple urgent emails and support tickets explaining that the delay is on the government side, not mine.\n\nI received ZERO human response. Not a single person reached out to help me or offer a solution before shutting down my account. Now, I am unable to pay my rent or my health insurance, which is causing me a massive financial crisis.\n\nThis company clearly does not care about the students they serve once they have their money. If you are a student moving to Germany, be very careful their support system is non existent when things get complicated. I will be taking this matter to BaFin if it's not resolved immediately.\n\n\nUser ID: 953925", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I can't activate my blocked account after reached Germany and I went 3 times to post office verification and it is a loop", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "They didnt help me", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Das Überweisen von China auf ein Sperrkonto geht ziemlich schnell. Aber die Gebühren zur Kontoeröffnung werden immer teurer. Schon direkt nach der Eröffnung wird die monatliche Gebühr fällig. Ich will ein Chancenkarte-Visum beantragen. Bis ich das Visum habe und nach Deutschland komme, vergehen etwa 5–6 Monate. In dieser ganzen Sperrzeit muss ich auch die monatliche Gebühr zahlen – das schmerzt schon. Ich hoffe, dass das Konto reibungslos aktiviert werden kann, und vielleicht gibt es noch ein paar Kundenvorteile", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I still cannot activate my account.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Simply awful.\n\nI've now waited for two weeks to transfer funds from my blocked account to my bank account and have been stopped at every point.\n\nI've had long email correspondence with them during this time, but unfortunately they only reply once every few days, which is extremely irritating.\n\nI've tried calling them but I only ever get an automated response. There is never anyone I can personally talk to about this as this option doesn't seem to exist. The chatbot function is also useless as it is just a picture. I've tried pressing on it on several devices, both on the website and the app just like it suggested and still nothing happens.\n\nI've made it clear to them that this account is my only source of funds and because of their failure to respond in a timely manner, I've missed rent payments and currently owe money to several people as I have no choice but to beg them for money as I simply do not have any right now.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I completed the POSTIDENT verification at a Deutsche Post branch, but the activation page still shows the “Activate” option as if the verification has not been completed.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Unable to activate blocked account and to complete the PostIndent verification and update on expatrio takes 4hrs minimum and by the the I face issue support time gets over by 12pm and Unable to connect any support team over call", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I still did not get the confirmation for my appointment in Berlin tomorrow. Your WhatsApp bot is useless", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I reached Germany 3 weeks before but still my blocked account not activated.. i done all the documentation and verification but my account is not activated.. i submit many request but no response to customercare team and they didn't solve my problem.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am impressed see your service", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I’m facing issue with activating my blocked account, I have tried twice but physically going to Deutsche post for verification but its not working. I have raised an email regarding the same with the customer support team but I haven’t yet received the confirmation regarding the appointment to the Berlin’s office.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Even after doing postident for 5 times my account was not activated and last option given to me is to visit berlin, which 900 km from my area , i did not havemoney for db ticket or anything, and after asking for reason behind this i am mot getting any rational answer because expatrio support dont know why its failing. Worst service ever.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have been activating my blocked account since 2nd May. And I have done post office verification 5-6 times till now and they have verified my passport and have uploaded every document. Everything has been done very smoothly but till yet I have not received an activation email. In the app it still shows \"Identity verification waiting\"", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I transferred 13700 euros but I received only 13249 euros, and I don’t know why", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am still waiting for them to answer my question which they haven’t answer. It’s like a loop. They don’t have the phone number to contact. The email ID is very slow. I still have not received anything. The application is like 10 years ago all the application still trying to figure out how to contact them, but they are slow.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "My problem haven't been solved", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The format of the website was very easy to navigate. I wish there were better options for questions and help.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "We haven’t received proper information about my M10 certificate Whether it is send to University or not.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "There is no immediate response from expatrio in case of technical issues. We are trusting you with money and the least you can do is to provide immediate support for people in need. I have been going to different post offices to complete my verification and each time the verification is completed, the activation process starts from the beginning. I talked to people at the post office but they said it is completed from their side, im sure it is a technical fault internally. Not at all happy with the experience. Other nationalities can verify online via video call but not Indian nationalities.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Trying to resolve my query from last 2 days, but nobody revert me. Even i contacted to local Expartio person but he also not given any response. Really very bad experience.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have been asking to activate my account i emailed many time that i already did verification but still status shows pending no emails nothing i came here now i don’t have money what should i do ? Your work is to activate it as soon as possible your system can’t work thia sliw", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Worst experience ever, did not help me in anyway. First they did not help me in verification when i mailed them they are saying to come to berlin from frankfurt which is not yet all helpful. \nAll of this for simple identity verification. Now they want me to shift to fintiba so frustrating for students", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "This is absolutely the WORST service! 😡 I have completed my verification at the post office TWICE, but my app is STILL stuck showing the QR code. I’ve reached out to customer support multiple times and have been completely ignored with zero response. This is unacceptable. Someone needs to look into my account immediately!\nMy User ID is:1251191", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "One of the worst company i have seen. After arriving in Germany i want my block account for my expense and i completed all process of verification even i dod not receive Video call verification option so i went to the post office and completed my verification. Even after post verification they again tell me to complete the verification. I contacted customer support since same reply. Dont go with them. Account opening is easy and withdrawal is just awful. \nI edit my review i complete post verification second time and the link shows that you are already verified but they again reset that verification for no reason. Such a shame for a big company. My biggest mistake is choosing you.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "My queries is not taking seriously by your team and I'm not satisfy with your services.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "No response waste of taking expatrio blocked account still my problem didn't resolve in activating my blocked account I went to postal twice  n done with\nverification   but expatrio till now didn't activate my blocked account", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Thinking of going with Expatrio’s blocked account bundle with Ottonova? Avoid it.\n\nFirst and foremost, medical institutions do not interact directly with Ottonova. You are entirely in the middle—handling submissions, follow-ups, and communication yourself—and that’s where the biggest gap lies.\n\nPre-approvals take months. In May 2026, they were still reviewing requests submitted in February. That leaves you stuck—either delay treatment or go ahead without approval and take the risk.\n\nIf you proceed without pre-approval, you’re exposing yourself to a high likelihood of denial. And once that happens, the process becomes a full-blown administrative battle: repeated document requests, long delays, and intense scrutiny of your case.\n\nEven for genuinely new medical issues, it can feel like the process is geared toward identifying any detail that could be used to cast doubt and reframe the condition as pre-existing—giving grounds to deny the claim.\n\nThe result is constant uncertainty. You never have real confidence that your treatment will be covered, even when you’ve done everything by the book. Instead of security, you get stress, delays, and endless back-and-forth at a time when you should be focused on your health.\n\nIf you’re a student, this is the last kind of burden you want while trying to stay on top of your studies and settle into a new country.\n\nThink very carefully before choosing this bundle. You may end up spending more time fighting your insurance than focusing on your studies.\n\nAnd if this is not enough also read Ottonova's reviews on Trustpilot.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Until now I mostly have an unpleasant experience. My verification if failed because suddenly verification don’t work with Israeli passport and nobody told me about this. I get one answer per day if I’m lucky, I still can’t redo my verification. It’s not the service you expect from the company that supposed to keep your big amounts of money for the whole year or maybe longer", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "After my blocked account 06 confirmation, since my university doesn't allow paying fee of 1 year in advance I needed to provide proof of my sem 2 fee by means of an unblocked deposit. I asked via the expatrio customer support. They responded by adding wrong amount with even carefully reading the mail. Customer response time is really high. Worse customer service. It's really hard to get a response for our issue. Total ambiguity.\n\nI wonder how people get response for full refund, except service charges in case of visa rejection. If this is the case, how assured we are about their claims \n\nTotally a bad experience", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Application is horrible, can't even unpair my device. I had a problem with blocked account activation and they still didn't help me to solve it.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Finger weg – lieber zur Konkurrenz gehen, selbst wenn es teurer ist!Ich habe noch nie einen so schlechten Kundenservice erlebt. Auf E-Mails wird lediglich mit Standardvorlagen geantwortet, ohne überhaupt auf die konkreten Anliegen einzugehen.\nIm Rahmen einer Verpflichtungserklärung bei der Ausländerbehörde (Einladung eines Verwandten aus einem Nicht-EU-Land) benötige ich ein Sperrkonto mit entsprechendem Guthaben. Vor der Ausstellung der „Blocked Account Confirmation“ habe ich mich intensiv mit Expatrio per E-Mail abgestimmt (über zehn Nachrichten), um sicherzustellen, dass die Formulierungen den Anforderungen der Behörde entsprechen. Erst nachdem mir dies bestätigt wurde, habe ich das Geld überwiesen. \nDas Ergebnis war katastrophal und zwecks befremdet: Statt der benötigten Bestätigung wurde mir ein Dokument ausgestellt, das offensichtlich für internationale Studierende gedacht ist – also ein Sperrkonto, bei dem nach Ankunft in Deutschland monatlich ein bestimmter Betrag freigegeben wird.Dadurch ist mir erheblicher Zeitverlust entstanden, und es kam zu Problemen bei der Terminwahrnehmung bei der Ausländerbehörde. Der Prozess dauert weiterhin an, und das Problem wurde bis heute nicht gelöst. In der Bestätigung wird  eine Telefonnummer für den Kundenservice angegeben – diese ist jedoch faktisch nutzlos. Der Service soll angeblich zwischen 09:00 und 12:00 erreichbar sein. In der Praxis landet man jedoch in einem endlosen Menüsystem, das letztlich immer mit einem Abbruch und dem Verweis auf die Website endet. Selbst wenn man es schafft, in eine Warteschleife zu gelangen, wird nach über 21 Minuten das Gespräch automatisch beendet mit der Aufforderung, es später erneut zu versuchen.\nNie wieder!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "They should have time in assisting students step by step in block account activation or better still they should tell students they location of they office for one on one assistance.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Very poor service . Totally dissatisfied", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "We had two accounts.  They were put I two accounts.  Not individuals..", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Customer support just doesn’t exist. I have problem with paring my device with the expatro bank account, which is stupid and nonsense.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have been emailing you for the past 5 days to change my email address. I have uploaded all the documents and information you requested. I also created two separate requests through your website and sent five emails including all the required documents and details.\nHowever, I have still not received any response. Unfortunately, this has been a very poor experience, and I have been negatively affected by this situation.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It took approximately 10 days to receive the blocked account opening confirmation. As I had limited time to transfer my blocked funds to Germany, I decided to use another blocked account service provider, which completed the entire process quickly and efficiently.\n\nAdditionally, the communication process was not very efficient, as I had to wait around 2–3 days to receive a response from a support representative, which was quite frustrating.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "​I had already provided my Deutsche Bank account details in the app. Today, I successfully completed my PostIdent verification, and the PostIdent app clearly shows my verification was successful for the first QR code.\n​When my Expatrio app finally updated to \"Awaiting Activation,\" I clicked \"Activate\" to finalize my payouts. Instead, the system glitched and looped me entirely backward to the \"Identity Verification Waiting\" screen. It is now asking me to go to the post office and verify all over again.\n​My money is completely stuck behind this system error. I have an urgent deadline to pay a €750 deposit for my Studentenwerk dormitory, and I urgently need my funds released to my DB account for my daily living expenses. I need the Expatrio support team to manually check my successful PostIdent file and unlock my payouts immediately", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The response is delayed, and it is still hanging, which is really painful cause when I mailed it was about a refund, and I was about to get cardiac arrest.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "You should identify support special passport as well because there are lots of Turkish people who have special passport and you’re making this process harder than it already is.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Thủ tục phức tạp cho phần gọi video thì không có ngôn ngữ để chọn phù hợp tiếng mẹ đẻ .Đâu phải ai cũng nghe và làm theo được kính mong ngài điều chỉnh lại không mỗi nước có phiên dịch phụ trách 1 nước ạ", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Juste Perfect  I am satisfied", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "This time the service or process did not meet expectations. There were delays and some confusion in communication. The company can improve by providing clearer instructions, faster responses, and better customer support.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I chose Expatrio based on a cashback offer of €69 clearly stated in their email during the application process. The message indicated that the cashback would be received after completing specific steps (opening and activating the blocked account and insurance).\n\nHowever, after I fulfilled all the required conditions, I was informed that I was not eligible due to an internal deadline (August 1st, 2025), which was never mentioned in the original communication.\n\nFrom a customer perspective, this is highly misleading. The email created a clear and reasonable expectation that the cashback would be granted upon completion of the stated steps, without any indication of additional eligibility restrictions.\n\nI have contacted customer support and requested escalation, but the responses relied solely on internal policy without addressing the lack of transparency in the original communication.\n\nThis experience raises concerns about how promotional information is presented and whether all relevant conditions are clearly disclosed to customers at the time of decision-making.\n\nI hope Expatrio can review this case fairly and improve the transparency of their communication.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have a deposit since April 7, 2026 but until now, April 16, my deposit is still not cleared. It has been 10 days since then and my still not cleared.\n\nBut my 2 earlier deposits were cleared in 2 hours last March. Please support.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Very slow process", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "These Blocked account services are very Bogus as the Funds are held by the company for 12 Months. We pay the setup Fee, earning no interest on our money, plus the Buffer amount is also kept till the very end plus a monthly service charge is to be paid by the students too. How is this even fair? It is worst than paying an education loan on high interest rates. Also, the sad part is that the Foreign Government bodies and authorities also promote such exploiting activities by tagging it as a Compulsory criteria.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I liked that the amount got into the account quickly, but there are no customer services based in India. And Ahalia Finforex services is not upto the mark, they don't have a proper customer   service, when called there is  a lot of noise and the A2 form is Horrible. Other than that I liked your service.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It is hard to contact with the staff. I waited lots of time…", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am writing to suggest a correction to your website's regional settings. Currently, Taiwan is labeled as a 'Province of China.'\n\nPlease note that this designation does not align with the official administrative practice of the German Federal Foreign Office (see the Verzeichnis der Staatennamen), which recognizes Taiwan as a distinct economic and value-based partner.\n\nFurthermore, from a consumer perspective, such a label may be considered misleading under § 5 of the Act Against Unfair Competition (UWG), as it creates confusion regarding the actual jurisdiction, customs regulations, and geographical origin of the user. To ensure consistency with German standards and ISO 3166, I strongly recommend updating the label to 'Taiwan.'\n\nThank you for your commitment to accuracy and for supporting a clear user experience.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am asking for incoming travel insurance several times. But  Didn't received yet.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I opened 3 time account but when I transferred money I had come to know that my account is closed and funds were held by the supportive bank due to the blocked account closure  that's why I lost my summer intake due to this issue  and further more I charged transection fee of money on every transection, kindly  work on it and faster your customer support service", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I had do Video Verification once and it did not work since I have a special Turkish passport. Then I had to do Post Identification 2 times because first one did not work neither due to my passport again. At the it worked out finally. However the problem is that before the verification and throught the registration process, it was already obvious that I have a speacial passport. So, I think it is a system error that these passports are not registered in the system. Thank you.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Mein Neffe ist schon seit 2 Jahre in Deutschland.  Musste ein Sperrkonto bei expatrio aufmachen was gut geklappt hatte und die Auszahlung auch. Jetzt wollte er sein Visum verlängert und die Behörde haben noch nach einem Sperrkonto gefragt oder Verflichtungserklärung.  Da der Antrag für die Verflichtungserklärung dauerte, haben wir angefangt noch ein Sparkonto zu öffnen und 6000€/12000€ schon eingezahlt. Aber inzwischen hat es mit der Verflichtungserklärung geklappt sodass wir das Konto nicht mehr brauchen. Dann haben wir einen Antrag gestellt um das Konto zu schließen. Da fing unsere Probleme an. Erstmal bekommt man keine Antwort,  est gibt keine Telefonnummer wo Man expatrio kontaktiert kann, es wird inzwischen von uns Dokumente von den Bebörde verlangt was der Behörde selber keine Ahnung davon hat. \nWir haben den Beweis dass wir Geld in ihre Bank haben warum ist das denn schwer das Geld zurück zu zahlen? Bis heute haben wir keine Antwort,  kein Geld.. und das finden wir sehr schade, denn sas Kind braucht auch sas Geld. Aber wenn es so weitergeht,müssen wir ein Antwahl einschalten. Sorry..", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have been trying every possible way to activate my account for over a week, and the experience has been extremely frustrating.\n\nPostIDENT failed multiple times despite visiting different post offices across the city. The support I received was not helpful, as my issue remains unresolved.\n\nI am an ESN student with a valid German visa, and I urgently need access to my money to pay my rent. Instead of resolving the issue, I was asked to travel from Gießen to Berlin just for identity verification. This is completely unreasonable, especially since my account is still deactivated and I cannot even afford the ICE train ticket.\n\nThis situation has caused unnecessary stress and wasted a significant amount of my time.\n\nYour system needs to support green passports. Many students from Turkey are facing the same issue due to this limitation, and it is unacceptable that such a simple technical gap is creating serious problems.\n\nThis issue needs to be addressed urgently!!!!!!!!!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Terrible service that outsource all their customer support to AI.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Impossible to download the current bank state but the reply of email was not helpful as well", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "My card is blocked. I contacted the support team but I havent gotten any replies. It has been over 24 hours. Since there is no number to call, I cant use my money. I need it urgently", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Your identification system is not compatible with all passports, such as those issued by Guinea. Moreover, you have made the identification process unnecessarily complicated.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Expatrio recently implemented a sudden, unannounced policy change that specifically targets Chinese students. They blocked the standard SWIFT EUR transfer option and are now forcing students from China to use Flywire, mandating payments in CNY at an absolutely terrible exchange rate.\n\nIf you already bought Euros, you are out of luck—they force you to convert it back and lose hundreds of Euros in the process. This bundled Flywire policy is a blatant money-grab, and the fact that it specifically targets certain nationalities is completely discriminatory and unacceptable.\n\nDo not use Expatrio. They do not care about students; they only care about squeezing extra hidden fees out of you through forced third-party platforms. Choose their competitors instead!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "中国区不支持欧元打款！必须手动更改为其他国家才能打款。而且是上个月临时起意，太不负责，欺负中国用户。Euro payments are not supported in the China region! (must manually change to another country in order to make the payment). And it was a last-minute decision last month, too irresponsible to Chinese users.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "89 euro platform fee and 5 euro monthly fee is a large amount should be lesser than this amount, otherwise expatrio services are good and quick.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am extremely disappointed with the lack of professional support from Expatrio. I purchased the Value Package and successfully funded my blocked account with €23,808.00. However, my health insurance documents (both Dr-Walter Incoming Insurance and TK Public Health Insurance) have completely disappeared from my user dashboard for no reason.I have a critical visa appointment for TU Berlin, and I cannot proceed without these documents. Despite my numerous attempts to contact customer service over the past few weeks, I have received nothing but automated responses. It is unacceptable to hold such a large amount of a student's money while providing zero human interaction or technical fixes.User ID: 1329247 \nIssue: Missing Insurance Certificates from DashboardPlease assign a human agent to restore my documents immediately. This delay is putting my entire Master's degree and visa process at risk.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Einrichtung lief sehr gut... Visa hat nicht geklappt.... Rückzahlung des Geldes funktioniert vielleicht mit vielen nervigen Hindernissen.... ich warte immer noch. Muss wohl klagen.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I had problems opening an account, but there was no one to talk to, so it was bad.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I submitted my request on Thursday to modify the monthly amount of my blocked account. I was told that I would receive a response within 24 hours, which unfortunately did not happen, then proceeded to send another message, and I was asked to provide the request from the embassy, which I did. However, more than 24 hours have passed again and I still have not received a response.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "dislike: \nThe review process of the blocked account is tooooooooo slow. Said it's within 24h to check the passport but I wait until the next day, and my friends told me they waited for 4 and 5 days. This indefinite time factor is very unfriendly to those who are applying for a visa, which are the most people that are using Expatrio.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I can not transfer by EUR in China", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The service was great, the app feels a bit behind. \nI was only able to do my first payment with the app. The rest, it kept asking me to go to the web page. The app was really slow, and the web page is not really convenient. Everytime I wanted to log in, they sended me a code I had to wait to arrive in my email. It felt as the password was there for nothing.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Too slow to reflect amount in account...", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I’m just Starting. It seems okay to use", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Can not receive verification code", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Mostly easy to use, but the processes of transferring funds to the blocked account and verifying your identity can be very convoluted and hard to follow at times.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have very good experience with expatrio. Within no time , I got confirmation of my account.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "89 Euro Service charge is somehow high in addition to 5 euro per month for students like us.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "payment delays because of flywire", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Sehr schlimm", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "the 5 euro monthly charges is not good as to coracle... because coracle is totally give their service totally free", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have not received any response to my questions until now. My issue remains completely unresolved, and my health insurance is still not active.\n\nI expected clearer and more timely communication.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I opened a blocked account, bank account and health insurance in order to obtain a language visa in Germany. I transferred the money to the blocked account which was a very smooth experience. After Expatrio received my money, however, it became impossible to activate my account. For the last step, they are supposed to call you to verify through a video call, but I was put on hold for hours and no one ever called me. Since I cannot verify my account, I cannot access my money. Expatrio seems to be set up just to make money off the people who trust them with no intention of disbursing the funds.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have followed all the troubleshooting steps:\n\nI uninstalled and reinstalled the app earlier\n\nI cleared the cache by holding the “Help” button for 5 seconds as instructed\n\nI tried logging in again and pairing the device\n\nI attempted the process multiple times\n\nUnfortunately, the issue still persists.\n\nIn my Expatrio dashboard, I can see two separate blocked accounts:\n\nMy previous blocked account (opened from India – now expired)\n\nMy new blocked account (opened in Germany for residence permit renewal) Amount : € 6077\n\nWhen I try to activate or pair the account for monthly payout transfer to my Sparkasse bank account, the system redirects me back to the same page without completing the process. No confirmation or error message appears.\n\nThis does not appear to be a cache or phone issue. It seems to be a backend contract-linking or system configuration issue, possibly related to having two blocked accounts under the same profile.\n\nI kindly request that this case be escalated to the Technical/Product team to:\n\nCheck contract linking on the backend\n\nEnsure the expired account is not blocking activation\n\nManually enable payout activation for the new blocked account\n\nThis matter is urgent as it affects my residence permit renewal process in Germany.\n\nPlease let me know if you require any additional information.\n\nKind regards,\nSagar Vinubhai Gajera\nCustomer ID: 824151", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Worst customer service this company is the worst I have ever used they dont reply to customer emails on time they are just the worst I have ever used and it will ge the last I use them I just regret being under such a company don't waste your time i am telling you use another account option", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The app is easy to use and the Value Package is quite good and useful. However, the support team’s responses were slow, and they kept asking the same questions multiple times. Improving response time and communication would make the experience much better.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "What went wrong was about the fast presentation. It was if you were in hurry. Due to that some of us couldn't get the most out of the presentation which resulted in so many questions which you thought  you answered them during the presentation.\nYou need to do the presentation at a good pace.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It was very introductory, not really helpful as someone already going with procedures. So i couldn't get the details or new info i wanted.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Generic, poor and slow customer service", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Repeated service fee to load money is typical cheat even after opening an account before.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am not receiving OTP from expetrio on my registered email ID", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I cannot access my account as I am not receiving my OTP at my registered email and I have tried to email and filled the form as well and nobody came back.\n\nPlease help me out I want to do important stuff", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "My issue has not been resolved. There is no person to speak with; I only receive automated responses that do not understand my problem", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have purchased the value package. Accidentally selected the private health insurance instead of public health insurance. Now I want to change it. I mailed expatrio team but they’re not replying. Now I feel choosing the expatrio was a bad decision.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Simple smooth and easy process and now I’m happy to apart of Expatrio as international student from Pakistan 10/10 \nI give 5 stars", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "This firm is good, offers pretty good services. However there is a issue, for instance, today i wanted to login my expatrio account to download block account confirmation, despite entering correct login details and requesting verification code multiple times, I am not receiving mail, I hope this finds you well and solve the issue ASAP.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It took long for it to reflect", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The responce was fast.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The only stuff I found helpful was the part she said your company can only help with visa", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I completed the Identity verification process when i reached Germany and the App just never allowed me to open my account. After 3 times, i decided to try Identity Verification through PostIdent and the App/System STILL never showed that i completed my Verification process and my money is still locked, even though i am in Germany", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Waste of time. Why offer \"how to study in Germany for free\" if you are going to sell a 12 thousand euros schooltrip.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am very disappointed with Expatrio’s blocked account activation process. Despite completing PostIdent verification twice and visiting the post office on two separate occasions, my identity still could not be verified by Expatrio.\n\nEach time, instead of resolving the issue, I was sent a new coupon and a new activation link, forcing me to repeat the entire process again. This is extremely inefficient, time-consuming, and frankly bizarre—especially for international students who are already under stress after relocating to Germany.\n\nTo make matters worse, I have contacted Expatrio support multiple times, but there has been no meaningful response so far. The lack of communication and poor support quality makes the situation even more frustrating.\n\nFor a service that handles something as critical as a blocked account, I expected a much more reliable system and responsive customer support. Based on my experience, the activation process is not up to the mark and urgently needs improvement.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have been trying to receive my blocked account payout for days, but Expatrio's system is technically broken. The app constantly gives a \"Recipient verification is currently unavailable\" error, preventing me from updating my IBAN.\n​Even though my payout failed because of their own system, they are ignoring my urgent emails and Instagram messages. I have provided all proof of account ownership, yet they refuse to manually update my details and send my money.\n​This is unacceptable and irresponsible. They are withholding my funds without any valid reason. If this is not resolved immediately, I will be escalating my complaint to BaFin (Federal Financial Supervisory Authority).\n​Stay away if you want to access your money on time!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Thanks to automation, the initial setup of the blocked account was very easy. However, once changes are needed, the process quickly turns into a nightmare. The system is not designed to handle even small issues, which require human intervention and unfortunately, this is where Expatrio fails. I sent an email on Friday requesting a very minor change to my account, but I have still received no response. This level of unresponsiveness is unacceptable for a financial service provider. Urgent issues can arise at any time, and due to the lack of timely support, such problems can become irreversible.\n\nI am giving 1 star only because giving 0 stars is not an option. Effective financial services cannot rely 100% on automation without proper and responsive human support.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "This company really showed its tail once major events occurred in my life. For one, the private insurance provided is a scam; they quite literally took a playbook from the American medical system. I required coverage for a dire emergency that was not covered due to \"preexisting conditions\". The insurance is only there for lining the pockets of those at Educare24, the insurer. Do keep in mind that you will be met with hostility and passive aggressive behavior should you inquire with Educare's support. \n\nThe second most notable time was when I needed to close my blocked account. It took me less than a week to transfer all of my savings to this institution with no enlisting of assistance or requirements for me to do so. Once it came to transferring my money back, it meant that I was met with incompetence, unreasonable requirements, conflicting information, and a two month delay. \n\nDo not work with this company unless you want to experience loss and deep tissue aggravation.\n\n\nEdit to add: I do not need further correspondence from Expatrio. My blocked account is closed and settled, at the time of typing this.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "ok thank you for your follow-up so, expatrio is doing a good job but for my side what I disliked on your service is how you provide documents without a stamp or Qr code or a bar code this has affected me many times when I was going to transfer funds cause there was a confusion on the authenticity of your products.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Hello Team Expatrio,\n\nThank you for organizing the webinar “How to Study or Work in Germany.” \n\nIt was informative and well-structured.\n\nI had posted a couple of questions during the Q&A session regarding Ausbildung and career pathways for experienced professionals, but unfortunately they could not be addressed due to time limitations.\nI just wanted to share this as feedback, as many participants like me attend such sessions hoping to get guidance on more specific and practical career-related questions as well.\n\nOverall, it was a good session and I appreciate the effort of the speakers.\n\nKind regards,\nMohit Sharma", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "One of the worst customer supports. They can't fix basic things.\n\n1. Not changing insurance provider. The app only leads you to private insurance company. No option to change it.\n2. Misleading and non-existed approach to fixing the problems.\n3. Support team is repeating the solutions that doesn't work repeatedly.\n4. Furthermore, app let you create a second account but crashing in a point. So, there's many loopholes to fix.\n5. Currently, I have 2 account 1 is that I requested it  delete another one is stuck in the completing  personal info. Error is \"BAD_DATA\nPease review your application and verify all the data provided is your own it is, please contact Expatrio customer support\"", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Very poor response\nMy emails are being ignored\nI had transferred 156€ from my Indian Bank account which I needed as unblocked amount but it is showing as 146€ in additional basic sum and 10€ as unblocked amount\nI need it for my university but such a delay is not acceptable", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "You have asked me to give a review of expatrio and I gave an honest review that I had an AWFUL experience. Now you are forcing me with further information by asking things like reference number or else threatening that the review is not genuine. It is the customer who decides the review as it is his own experience. Who are you to decide? Are you trying to act smart? Even now I say I have a terrible experience. Your customer care representatives answer very late and they never are available for help. I have raised a query almost 2 days back and they are still investigating. I am unable to use google wallet that I linked to expatrio. what is so hard to understand? Expatrio customer care are lazy people is what I understood.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Its a lot of painful experience.\n\nFirst thing is, you should let people use desktops and laptops and not force them to install an app. Loading documents visa app is such a painful experience.\n\nSecond thing is, you should have a live support agent to address problems of users. AI chatbots are useless.\n\nI am still unsure of how to use the account as I do not have an ATM card", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "so expensive, the \"free\" bank acc is only free for 12 months and monthly gebühr should only be taken after the acc is activated", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "This is a bank, not free, I am paying for the service that you have not even provided yet! Forcing me to give a review with your constant reminders is nothing but lack of professional business manners.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Attığım maillerin hiçbirine içeriğine uygun cevap verilmedi. Ne yazarsam yazim klasik yapay zeka asistanlari gibi: “sayfamızdaki şu başlıkları okuyun” a yönlendirdiniz ve sorumun içeriğinin cevabı orda yoktu. Bu yüzden işlem süreci çok pahalıya mal oldu bana. Geri dönüş yapan ekiplerinizinde  aynı şekilde davranmaları fazlasıyla üzücü, ilgisiz bir tavır, en kötü en can sıkıcı husus bu. Müşteri temsilcisi, geri dönüş konusunda 0 puan veriyorum. Bu hususun iyileştirilmesi lazım. Bu haliyle müşteri temsilcisi yok, olası bir aksilik yaşanması durumunda şansınıza sığınmak zorundasınız.  Onun dışında  aynı gün bloke onayı belgem geldi. Memnunum.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Overall Experience was good but needs some improvement in handling foreign payments.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Timely response was lacking but overall your service was ok", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It was good experiance but you are so much expensive than coracle i would have gone to coracle but it was close thats why i choose expatrio", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "My appointment got cancelled i didnt recieve any call \nI called the number and the guy didnt come back with an answer. Where can i find travel insurance!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The experience of dealing with expatrio is nothing but horrible for me. I started opening the blocked account and it had a hello sign saying that it is being verified. The message on the website said that I can send the money to the account and that will assist in verification. I sent the money and it was received in full. After that I contacted support because account was still yellow and being verified. Support told me that I did not pass verification and was rejected. Well ok. Support emailed me and said the will refund the money. I provided the information they asked - official document from my bank stating my name, address, amount, my account, account money was sent to, date. Everything that was required I provided. Then began the back and forth. Now finally after a week of back and forth support ask ME how to input my account information to refund the money. Excuse me. How am I supposed to know how to fill in the form from the side of Expatrio. I provided everything required from me. And now they don’t even know how to send money to me? It’s a lot of money, now it’s going to get lost along the way because they don’t know how to send it?   ???", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Till now not used it and don't know how it works. I can provide better experience as soon as I use it. Too early for sharing an experience.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I was fascinated by  the  speed of transaction. It was quick and efficient. However, I have one feedback; while transfering blocked amount i transferred the amount in the IBAN which the portal suggested but the account was already closed because it was inactive for more than 90 days. It should be informed to the users while sending the payment information. \nI had to reopen the account in order to complete the transcation.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Before opening the blocked account it did not informed me that i have to verify my self inorder to unblock my account. This was not included in the previous procedure. This has changed without giving any instruction. \n\nDue to that as soon as a got my blocked account i sent that to my visa officer for my visa extention. And when i done with that i caught my flight, after landing to my native country i got to know that i have to be present at DHL station for verification for my blocked account activation. This is just drove me crazy.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have goodexperience because i request for private health insurance certificate and received my private health insurance.\nThank you", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Email responding was good and fast, the process was also efficient hope I will have better experience afterwards", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It’s taking a long time get reply from customer support.\nFor me, i sent a mail regarding my block amount payout still i didn’t get any response from customer support even it’s so urgent for me", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "So many times repeating the same request.. but not clear answers from you..", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "They are not understanding my issue and not giving me a clear solutio.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Your services are too clumsy. Another people needed to understand the whole thing.and your response time...! Oh God! Just hopeless. \nBased on my experience it’s a great mistake choosing Expatrio for health insurance.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "AI Customer service is really bad, therefore, find a way to call them to solve very important issues that their AI chatbot can't solve. Not gonna lie, the idea of the product is very attractive and convenient because everything is online, plus they offer you to open a German bank account for you, but so far I'm not getting the money after 2 weeks in Germany.\n\nThey probably made a mistake with my accounts passport so they switched me one of their partner's bank.\n\nThey solved the mistake, but now I'm not able to have a free bank that they offered in the service, therefore I have to find myself a new bank and do all the process by myself in order to receive the funds from Expatrio.\n\nCustomer Service (AI) :2/10\nCustomer Service (Human): 9/10\nReliability 2/10\nService Speed 9/10", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Bad experience", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The response are mostly auto generated mails, it doesn't give me any true feedback nor humane answers regarding my concerns. Moreover, no time is given in order to check the status of the updates or steps. Very unprofessional", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The dashboard was so critical,  i used before coracle it was so easy, but expatrio isn’t easy to understood.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I need urgent help and they take lot longer to give support or reply my queries and solve my issues", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "How come there's no instant support via phone? Urgent stuff is sometimes needed in dealing with embassies! I once entered a name wrong and had to send for the support and wait a lot just to change a name and was very much in a hurry. Have Instant Support!!!\n\nEdit: this was in the past and there's no open tickets now. I was frustrated at that time because I sent for the support and it was close to the weekend and I really wanted to deliver the blocked account before the end. I kept searching for a phone number to contact but wasn't successful. And as i expected the support answered me later. This was from another email.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Terrible customer service. I emailed to request an extension for my Blocked Amount Confirmation, and my account had sufficient funds. Yet the representative insisted I transfer money into my account.\n\nI sent an email on November 27th. November to communicate, but as of today, I still haven't received the new Blocked Amount Confirmation.\n\nWhat makes me feel even worse is Expatrio does not provide a direct contact number for customer support. This means I can only wait passively for them to handle it.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am writing this review as a warning to any family member, parent, or sponsor planning to fund a student's blocked account through Expatrio. My experience with this company has been deeply unprofessional, financially draining, and psychologically exhausting.\n\nI transferred over  €12,000 to support my sibling’s education in Germany. The funding process was dangerously easy—they accepted my money instantly without a single question. However, getting that money refunded has become a month-long nightmare of incompetence.\n\nThe \"Bait and Switch\" Experience:\nExpatrio is happy to take third-party funds (via Wise/Wells Fargo) to open an account, but when it comes time to refund that exact same money to the original source, they suddenly feign blindness.\n\nWhy This Has Been Torture:\nFor over 30 days, my sibling and I have been battling their support team to simply return my own money to me.\n*   Forensic Proof Ignored: I have provided a complete, verifiable audit trail. I submitted my Wells Fargo bank statements side-by-side with the Wise transfer receipts. The dates match exactly. The amounts ($3,000 per transaction) match exactly. My name and address are on both documents.\n*   Incompetent Review Process: Despite providing a \"1:1 correlation\" where I even highlighted the specific line items in yellow, their team repeatedly replies with generic copy-paste rejections claiming \"insufficient documents\" or that \"references don't match.\" It feels like no one is actually reading the files we upload.\n*   Gaslighting: They keep telling us to \"refund to the student's personal account for simplicity,\" completely ignoring our repeated explanations that this is not an option for us.\n\nThe Bottom Line:\nThis company operates with a double standard: Zero scrutiny when taking your money, maximum obstruction when returning it.\n\nWe are not asking for a favor; we are asking for them to read standard financial documents (Bank Statement + Transfer Receipt) that prove the money came from me.\n\nIf you are a parent or sibling funding a student, do not use Expatrio. They will hold your significant capital hostage behind a wall of robotic support emails. We are now facing severe financial strain because they refuse to acknowledge plain evidence.\n\nTo Expatrio Management: Review case. Stop hiding behind \"insufficient docs\" and look at the evidence provided. Release my funds.\n\nNote: This case has been open since the end of October. And I am still fighting to get my money back.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I liked Expatrio overall, especially when compared to other blocked account service providers. Previously, they charged a €69 setup fee, which was later refunded as cashback. I already had an account with you, which was later close without any prior notice, and now I had to pay the €89 fee as a new account opening policy — which is not refundable as cashback. As a customer, the only thing that bothered me was that before closing my account, you should have at least informed me by email or asked me about the status.\n\nAnd honestly, I believe convenience should be offered to customers, not taken advantage of. You knew very well that other service providers had temporarily suspended their services due to maintenance — and that’s exactly when you decided to increase your fees. Instead of supporting customers during that difficult time, it felt like you took the opportunity to benefit from the situation.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Hi, I really need urgent help. I’m completely stuck on the “pairing of device” step. I’m entering all the correct information exactly as it appears in my account. The system shows that the pairing is completed, but when the app refreshes it goes straight back to saying I haven’t paired anything.\n\nI have screenshots to prove it. I urgently need access to my money, but I’ve been stuck in this loop for days.\n\nI’ve already sent multiple emails and the replies I’ve received are just generic instructions from your website that don’t address the actual issue. On top of that, support only responds once a day at around 3 am, which is making this process even harder.\n\nPlease, I need someone to look at this properly and help resolve it as soon as possible.\n\nUser ID: 1143247", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Their service is an absolutely scam , I can’t belive how bad it it’s. It won’t let me access my money from my blocked bank account, nor even let my phone pair with the app!! And no support from you?!!!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "That's a terrible service! My money are in their correspondent bank CREDIT MUTUEL ARKEA ( SWIFT Code CMBRFR2BXXX) since 6th of November, more than 3 weeks and has not reached my blocked account. Support doesn't help, doesn't answer and only the bot responds. What I need to do?! Why you don't answer and help?? Because bank to which it is indicated to transfer money says to contact you, but you ignore it!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "You have just stolen my money. I have provided new documents and am still getting the needs to reviewed message. I have to get additional money just to pay my bills here because the money I sent you guys is still not reviewed to payout.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I would like to share my extremely disappointing experience while opening my blocked account with Expatrio.\n\nI followed the instructions provided by your representative in a Facebook group and opened a blocked account with the amount for 12 months as guided. However, according to the official regulations of the State Bank of Vietnam and the German Embassy, Studienkolleg students are only allowed to show financial proof for 9 months, with €1,091 per month.\nBecause of this incorrect guidance, the invoice created for me was wrong and caused a major delay in my visa application process. I transferred the money on Sunday, yet I had to wait an entire week to receive my refund. This shows a serious lack of responsibility in updating accurate information for your customers. As a financial proof service provider, it is essential that Expatrio stays aligned with the official requirements from the embassy and banks.\n\nSecondly, I am also dissatisfied with the customer service. I had to repeat my issue multiple times over three days before I finally received support. This was extremely stressful and time-consuming.\n\nI sincerely hope that Expatrio will improve both the accuracy of its information and the quality of its customer service to provide a better experience for future students.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Really slow response time for activation", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "You suck, your service is terrible. The PostIden didn't work and the VideoID as well. Charging 5 euros per month+90 euros opening fee while profiting from my money by lending to others at a higher rate, as in contrary to a normal account, my withdraws are restricted is simply outrageous.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The FlyWire exchange rate was so high that I paid 1000 Norwegian Krones extra as compared to my colleagues who preferred bank transfer. You recommended FlyWire for payment because it was safe. Based on you recommendations, I chose this payment method and it cost me 1000 NOK. \n\nI am highly disappointed.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "very bad experience, very slow transfer and request would never be solved!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Inability to call you on the phone, even though this is a service that should normally have an assistant available 24/7, because it concerns the money we need to live on here in Germany.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Expatrio serves well the purpose for blocking account. I'm impressed with the service provider's promptness in responding Emails. However the costs for the service  are too high", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Very poor service on block account retrieval \n\nThey make it near impossible to retrieve that amount even after uploading all the necessary documents. They fail to reply early and when they eventually do it’s always excuses.. therefore extending the supposed duration it takes to get one’s money out.. please release my funds. I regret using expatrio at this point..", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Pushes additional products aggressively. Not particularly great user interface. Small nitpick, but: Website and app don’t work well with iOS and MacOS Password vault.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Despite entering the activation code three times, joining the live verification three times, and uploading all my university documents correctly, your system still gave me an error. Then it redirected me to the help center, and I have been waiting for a response for an entire day with zero feedback. This experience has been extremely disappointing. Please fix this issue immediately. If you can’t solve it, then shame on you.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Im Online-Chat sind niemand da, lange Wartezeit für das Telefonat und die Mitarbeitende sprechen überhaupt kein Deutsch. Bei Mail ist es gleicher Fall, Deutsch hingeschrieben und Englische Antwort erhalten.\n\nMan kann es kaum anders als \"lächerlich\" beschreiben, insbesondere wenn es um Geld geht, wo exakte Kommunikation notwendig ist.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The verification process takes quite some time and can be a bit complicated. Activating the blocked account is also not very easy. It would be great if these steps could be made simpler and faster", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am extremely disappointed with Expatrio Germany. I opened my blocked account with Expatrio almost one and a half years ago to go to Germany for my studies. I have already submitted all the required documents to close my blocked account, yet every time I contact Expatrio, they come up with some new issue or excuse and keep holding my money without any valid reason.\n\nI have reached out to their support team multiple times, but I have not received any clear or helpful response. It feels like they are intentionally delaying or holding customers’ funds unnecessarily. This is completely unacceptable, especially after I have fulfilled all the legal and procedural requirements.\n\nI expected professionalism, transparency, and timely service from an international platform like Expatrio, but their handling of my case has been very disappointing. I urgently request Expatrio to release and return my funds immediately. If this issue is not resolved soon, I will have no choice but to take further legal action and share my experience publicly to warn other students about such delays and poor customer service.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It’s very messy how to actívate you account. My country (Chile) has a new passport format and expatrio doesn’t have it in their database. Its been very stressful all this situation and after a month arriving to Germany, i still can’t have access to my money", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "UPDATE: January 2026.   It has now been two more months and Expatrio continues to come up with excuses on not returning our money.  I see that many other reviews are stating similar stories.  Do not use this provider for blocked account services!! \n\nExpatrio was easy to work with to recieve our funds and set up the blocked account.  However since that time they have made excuses to not release the money to my daughter while she was studying abroad and is still making excuses for not returning our money now that she has been back for more than 6 months.  Do not use this service.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have worked many years in different organizations. This is one of the worst organizations I have ever encountered. The customer service is very bad (e.g., full of chatbots with useless email replies) and it seems no one knows what is going on there. They know it is all their fault and still they didn't give back the buffered amount. I think they look for ways to keep your money and charge you more at the end.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "My experience with Expatrio has been extremely frustrating. I applied for the Chancenkarte visa, and my application was denied. Naturally, I reached out to Expatrio to request the closure of my account and a refund of my blocked funds.\n\nI was asked to provide a rejection letter from the German Consulate, which I did. Unfortunately, the consulate’s response was phrased awkwardly instead of explicitly stating visa rejection, it said no visa application. Despite my clear explanation and supporting evidence, Expatrio refused to proceed, hiding behind semantics rather than applying reason or common sense.\n\nLater, I was told I could provide a written closing reason myself. I did exactly that, yet the request was still rejected. This has been going on for weeks now, with nothing but repetitive automated responses and no meaningful engagement from a human support representative capable of resolving the issue.\n\nAll I have asked for is simple — close the account and refund my money. Instead, I’ve been caught in an endless loop of poor communication, inefficiency, and unnecessary bureaucracy.\n\nFor a company handling international students’ and applicants’ funds, this level of disorganization and lack of accountability is unacceptable. One star is generous given the experience I’ve had.\n\nDo your possible best to avoid this company and everything it offers, also worth noting, there are no customer service agents available in-person at their office (they do not entertain walk-in appointments)!!!!!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Not help me any employer", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "My blocked account is not getting activated.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Wish I could give zero stars.\n\nI had to close my blocked account and transfer the money out. The first transfer bounced because of a wrong IBAN — partly my fault — but since the account was already closed, I couldn’t fix it myself.\n\nThe worst part? Nobody told me the transfer failed. I spent two weeks emailing support, getting vague replies like “we’re following up with Aion Bank.” When I finally pushed for proof, they admitted it had bounced weeks earlier. They knew and never said a word.\n\nThere’s no phone number, no way to actually talk to a human. Just slow, copy-paste email responses. I asked five times to speak to a manager — ignored until I got angry enough. When someone finally replied, she said support was “best equipped” to help me. Yeah, right.\n\nThree weeks of stress and emails over something that could’ve been fixed in one phone call. Never again. If something goes wrong, you’re on your own.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "My insurance was given only for 11 months instead of 12 months.\nI have already raised this query and yet to receive answers.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "the user experience of web platform (dashboard) can be better despite of that well done it works", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "they will not let you know about the insurance things, i faced a lot of issue because of the Insurance as a student in Germany. Expatrio support is very best not answering your  questions", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Monthly expenses can be reduced or exceempt.for being first preference for the students", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I liked the company’s friendly service and quick response. However, they could improve by communicating updates more clearly and offering more personalized support.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The charges are little high", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Der von ihnen angebotene Sperrkontoservice ist sehr unzureichend.\nDa ich ihn nicht mehr benötigte, habe ich am 7. Oktober einen Antrag auf Kündigung gestellt und trotz wiederholter Versuche, in der folgenden Woche Kontakt aufzunehmen, keine einzige Antwort erhalten. \nWenn Sie Geld einzahlen, erhalten Sie möglicherweise einen akzeptablen Service, aber wenn Sie Geld abheben möchten, verzögern sie die mittlerweile sehr schnellen Bankgeschäfte um etwa einen Monat. Auch wenn sie es bei der Registrierung nicht erwähnen, kann die Rückerstattung nach der Kündigung bis zu einem Monat dauern, und ich vermute, dass sie Ihr Geld nicht vor Ablauf eines Monats auszahlen.\n \nSie halten es nicht für notwendig, sich bezüglich der Zahlung bei Ihnen zu melden. Selbst wenn Sie das Geld dringend benötigen, weiß ich nicht, was passieren würde, wenn sie antworten würden. Der Service ist nicht akzeptabel. Ich möchte keine Erklärung hören, sondern lediglich mein Geld zurückerhalten.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Very bad customer service", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The system is pretty easy and good to use there were some bugs that confused me when I reported them to the customer service they didn't understand what I’m talking about and they answered with something else no related to my question, but that's fine I'm good now.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I tried to activate my blocked account and couldn't; I managed to do the identification process successfully, but my account was never activated. I have done this identification process over seven times now, always with the same result.\n\nI tried to ask for help and decided to write an email (they don't have a phone number). After that, I was ignored until I published a negative review. They replied to my review, saying someone got in contact with me. Someone did get in contact with me and replied twice before ignoring me again.\nSince then, I have written to the support staff four times in several days and haven't heard back. \nSince this seems to be the only way to get in contact with them, I am once again writing this review. I am running out of money, and they are either refusing or unable to provide the service I paid for. It really feels like a mockery and an insult that they think a chatbot and an FAQ page will be enough to solve all their users' problems.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The app in itself is good. there is no issue with it. However, it could have been much better with a developed customer support system.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have been trying to activate my blocked account for a while now and nothing works. \nI have been through the identity verification process with ident over five times and nothing changes, despite being “successful”. Whenever I try to contact customer support I get a chat bot that doesn’t help, or I have to send an email that goes unanswered. (They don’t have a phone number)\nSo far I have only gotten information from ident saying they are a third party provider and can’t really help beyond their service.\nIf a company is using a third party provider, I expect them to communicate with them and enable problem solving instead of denying responsibility and leaving the customer alone.\nWe are talking about a lot of money that is necessary to be able to start the new life in Germany and not about joining a fitness center. \nI am running out of money and don’t know how to get through the next days if this is not resolved asap.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Buggy Identification Process.\nMost of the app works ok it's just buggy. The identification verification process is extremely buggy, it keeps crashing the application. The application also crashes randomly and requires a PIN *AND* an email code verification every time you get back into it. An experience that should have taken 10-15 minutes took almost two hours.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Apologies for earlier comment.\nIt was given by mistake. I wanted to give feedback to Exness Trading but mistakenly, it was uploaded here.\nPlease ignore the first one.\n\nI would like to give feedback for Expatrio.\nIt is my first experience and I found it very costly. There are other options like Fintiba. I could save more than 1000 Euro by Fintiba if I just wait for 3 to 4 days to confirm Fintiba account. Because, it takes a bit more time than Expatrio.\n\n\nFirst Comment:\nUseless, Always taking my money. Always manipulating while I start trading.\nA big fraud. I do not recommend Exness to my friends.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I didn't see a prompt update when I sent the money. It took me to send email after 24 hours of sending the money before my account was updated, meanwhile I sent the money from a Germany. Please can't there be a system where accounts will be updated as soon as the money hits the account.\nAlso sending a confirmation receipt I think is also a problem because Sparkasse my bank does not issue transaction receipt in the mobile up.\nI think you should have a system that will capture all these and give students prompt outdate to save students from further stress", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Worst service and not satisfied, they dont return my money back, so slow reponed, stay away from them besides 15 Days not transfered my money back and ı have be in Germany next week", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I’ve been stuck in a nightmare with Expatrio for more than a week. I uploaded my documents five times already, and every single time they reply with the same robotic email: “Your documents are verified, you’re ready to proceed.” But when I open the app for the video verification, nothing is processed. The app still shows my proof of address pending, and I’m stuck in an endless loop.\n\nI even explained multiple times that my residence permit is about to expire and I don’t have time to waste. Do they care? Not at all. No sympathy, no actual resolution, just the same copy-paste nonsense that sounds like it’s written by a bot.\n\nThis is beyond incompetence—it’s negligence. They are holding people’s futures hostage with their broken system and useless support. If you need reliable service, do NOT choose Expatrio. They will waste your time, your energy, and put you at serious risk.\n\n⭐ If I could give zero stars, I would.\n\n\n🔄 Update – Still No Refund and No Resolution from Expatrio!\n\nAfter my previous review, nothing has improved. My account was closed by Expatrio, and despite multiple emails and explanations, they still haven’t refunded my money.\n\nI made two transfers, one of which was already requested back, and the second transfer of €1300 remains locked in their system. They are holding my money even though the account is closed, and this delay has now put my residence permit at risk, since I can’t open a new blocked account without my own funds.\n\nThis situation is not only unacceptable but deeply irresponsible. Their slow, repetitive, and robotic responses have caused me weeks of stress, and I’m still waiting for a proper human reply and my money.\n\n⚠️ Expatrio needs to take accountability — you cannot close someone’s account, keep their money, and leave them in legal jeopardy in a foreign country.\n\nUntil my full refund is processed, I will continue to update this review to warn others about this experience.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Toutes les etapes sont compliquées et prennent beaucoup de temps!! Je suis arrivée en Allemagne depuis 15jrs et j’ai toujours pas mon argent !!! Activation lente, maintenance, erreurs…..!!! Par mail un certain m. Ali m’aide beaucoup mais l’application ne facilite pas du tout la tache !!!!\n\nMerci", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I ordered a physical bank card and was immediately charged a hidden fee that was not advertised or made clear up front. When I realized within minutes and tried to cancel, support refused, stating that the order could not be canceled once placed. There's no grace period, no warning, and no way to reach a real person in time before their system auto-processes it. On top of that, support responses will give you copy-pasted answers that provided no effort to help or acknowledge the situation. For a company that advertises itself as student-friendly, this practice feels very predatory. Just be warned - they offer unclear fees, no flexibility, and no real customer service. This is by far the worst banking experience I have had", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I cannot recommend Expatrio for Japanese students who hold the new Japanese passport style issued from April 2025. I was unable to activate my blocked account using this passport, despite trying many times—through video calls and even visiting the post office. For a long time, I didn’t understand why the activation kept failing.\nAfter many contacts with customer support, I finally learned that the new Japanese passport is not yet supported for activation. In other words, it was “too new.” Honestly, I couldn’t believe it. Because of this, I couldn’t activate my blocked account or open the free bank account that was supposed to come with it.\nEventually, I was advised to switch my blocked account provider from AionBank to Mangopay. However, Mangopay requires you to provide a SEPA bank account. Fortunately, I had a Wise Euro account, so I could use that. But if you don’t already have a Euro account, opening one in Germany takes time—especially because most Japanese students receive their visa after arriving in Germany. Without a visa, you cannot open a SEPA bank account, which means you cannot receive your monthly payout from the blocked account.\nThis situation can cause a lot of anxiety. Most international students need to pay dormitory fees and insurance every month, and not having access to your funds can be very stressful.\nI gave 3 stars because a customer support staff member named Taha responded politely and patiently every time. That was one positive point.\nStill, I believe this is a very serious issue. I truly hope Expatrio will solve this problem soon—for the sake of future students.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "You should give discount / vouchers to Students it will be beneficial for them.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Aun no recibo respuesta sobre el envio del formulario M10 a la Universidad JLU H0001711.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "They are not allowing me to activate my blocked account.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "feedbacks takes a lot of time", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The app doesn't give the right instructions you have to guess, also there's no one to communicate your AI chatbot doesn't is useful", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "During the process of activating the account, there were two things that made me quite dissatisfied. One was the video identity verification section. The first staff member I connected with was a young woman. She kept turning her chair and had an extremely arrogant tone, as if she didn't like her job very much and was eager to leave. Her English was poor, with a trilled \"r\" sound, and her microphone made it impossible for me to hear what she was saying clearly. After I asked her to repeat her question, she hung up on me and marked the verification as failed. This left me completely bewildered and at a loss. Fortunately, the second staff member I connected with was more patient and helped me verify my identity. She also told me how to use my passport. The second thing was that after the video identity verification was successful, I still had to answer three questions to use the account. This step was completely unnecessary. I had forgotten my answers earlier. At first, I didn't know the answers could be found in my personal information, so I tried several times and ended up blocking my account. I wrote an email for help, and the reply was very prompt. I'm very grateful to them, but they still haven't solved my account problem. I can only try again the next day. The reason I think this is a double-edged sword is that since I had already passed the video identity verification, why would I still have to answer these meaningless questions? In a more extreme case, even if a stranger got my phone to answer the questions, she could find the answers from my personal information. The result was that the person using the account was restricted.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "V.bad experience until with this platform \nI applied for block account and send to locked amount, but still my insurance M10 notifications is not received by uni. I wrote every one expatrio team and TK insurance but my issue is not solved and my enrollment is still pending. No one is trying to solve the issue. \nIt seems to me to choose expatrio is wrong desicion for me.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Time was ok but presentation was rushed", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "€89 got deducted and they are not refundable now", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "EDIT: The embassy said you should release the money. It was clearly written in the mail, i can send a screenshot of the mail. \n Dear Sir / Madam,\nThe Consulate General of the Federal Republic of Germany Lagos does not have a current registration for an appointment nor a current visa application with the passport number B******** in the system.\n\nPlease forward this email to your bank where you have your blocked account, as well as your university.\n\nIf you need a certification of your signature, please get in touch with your responsible bank.\n\nUsually, you can get a certification of your signature from any responsible authority in Nigeria, i.e. local banks. \nSo you should stop lying.  \nEDIT END**\n\n \n\nMy sister used them for her visa, unfortunately the German embassy asked her to withdraw her application as she did not complete the tuition fee for school which is now a requirement for my country. We applied for a refund citing visa refusal as the embassy refused to process her visa. Expatrio said they cannot release the money until they get a mail from the embassy. \nThe German embassy sent a mail on my sister's behalf directly to them and yet they have refused to release the money claiming that my sister said her visa was rejected so she must provide a visa rejection. Or she should choose another reason.  \n\nThey want her to choose another reason so that they can take all the monthly service charge and other hidden charges.  They are not to be trusted. RUN.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Charges are so high", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Overall process is good, just transfer took time to show block account amount, which delay my visa process.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Still my bank account is blocked, saying under document review.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "If you are considering Expatrio for your blocked account, save yourself the trouble and look elsewhere. They do not care about their customers, and the frustration they have caused me is beyond words.\nI currently have nearly €4,000 at stake, and instead of clear answers, I keep receiving copy-paste template emails that dodge my actual questions. In fact, one of their “responses” was sent to me twice and what the email said was that they could confirm my email had been responded to. Not once have they directly addressed my concerns about what happens to my funds, how I can reopen my account if it’s closed, or why the money can’t simply be transferred to my newly extended blocked account WHICH IS ALSO UNDER EXPATRIO!\nThe stress this has caused me is immense, especially as I am waiting for my visa process and need these funds for enrollment and legal stay. And this isn’t new — even from the very beginning, when I first arrived in Germany and opened my account, the level of confusion, delays, and lack of real support was unacceptable. Countless emails, many attempted calls all ending up failed, and a lot more struggle led to no solution at all but somehow one honest review magically resolved all the issues in no time. \nExpatrio’s service has been nothing short of negligent. They repeatedly ignore direct questions, send irrelevant generic replies, and act as if no one is actually reading the emails. For a company handling international students’ money and futures, this behavior is reckless and unprofessional.\nIf you are a student looking into Expatrio: DON’T DO IT. Find a provider that actually values its customers and understands the responsibility of holding their money.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I transferred over 12000 euros to my Expatrio blocked account - one week after the transfer service (flywire) has notified me that the transaction was successful, my money still does not show up in my expatrio account. \n\nThe customer service is practically non-existent, since I haven’t received any answer or help in 6 days. \nThis is not serious, as not knowing what is going on with such an amount of money is causing me worries. \n\nWith the hope that the issue will be solved, I still regret having chosen this service because of its lack/slowness of support", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "My Blocked account, Health insurance and German Bank account are now ready but not activated because I'm not in Germany yet. The process so far has been somehow uncertain. The info in the website is good, yet generic, which makes sense. As I was going through the process I would've liked to have more human interactions. The bot chat was redundant and never gave me a choice to talk to a person about my specific questions.\nAs I was going through the transfer of funds, I learned more about how to activate and get my funds once in Germany.\nI was aware then that I would need a german phone and Anmeldung, which takes having long term accommodations which I haven't secure yet.\nSo, now I'm in the need to have funds ready in the meantime I can access my blocked account.\nI wished I had these details way in advanced, not discover this on the go.\nAgain, your customer service relies heavily in your Beta chat bot which is redundant and does not identifies when the customer has a questions beyond the generic info in the website.\nAt some point, I think some one replied to my email, but honestly, it did'nt \"sound\" human, just a cheerful \"have a great day\" and no answer, just \"go to flywire\" who didn't respond either. Only generic info in their website.\nFor such an important part in the already stressful process of moving abroad, I was expecting more support.\nI hope all goes well once in Germany. You make it look so smooth but in reality there are a lot of bumps in the road, and all you offer is a very limited customer support.\nYour business model, for my experience, reflects how disconnected you are from people, makes me think you hate humans for some reason.\nRemember is people, who need services, not machines. People have fears and insecurities when taking big steps, for ourselves or our loved ones.\nSome reassurance and answers for particular questions could improve the experience. Invest in people.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Everything eventually went smoothly with Expatrio, but I really want to highlight the importance of having a customer service representative you can reach right away. Currently, the only way to contact Expatrio is via email, and it usually takes about a day to get a response from them. Your main competitor offers a phone number that one can actually reach, and honestly that almost made me choose them instead.\n\nIf phone support isn’t possible, please at least consider adding a live chat option with a REAL person. We’re sending a significant amount of money to these services, and it’s stressful to think something could go wrong with no immediate help available. Knowing that no one is there when you need urgent assistance is, at the very least, frustrating.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It’s been 3 days and I still did not receive a reply to my email regarding an issue on my blocked account. Response times needs to be improved.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I want maintenance and get back 252", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "1.微信的帮助功能回复时间太慢了，人工要等5个小时左右才会回复\n2.转钱的方式少，不喜欢，没有中国银联，没有微信转账，没有支付宝转账，每次国际转账银行要收一大笔手续费\n3.我的医疗保险啊，德国大学没收到呢", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The process of opening JUST a blocked account and not the whole package is unnecessarily convoluted. Expatrio keeps spamming me with annoying emails and I just want access to an escrow account. They use AI for their support team and the company feels like a janky start up that's trying to sell an image of a quirky, fun business. I don't want emails with emojis in the headers, I don't want to be forced to use an app, I don't want empty AI generated text to pretend to be my friend -- I want to be able to find out how to access my money without having to run around the entire website. They should employ more software engineers to figure out how to make a more user friendly product instead of the messy frontend they currently have.\n\nEdit: The account is finally accessible, but to complete transaction, I need to enable notifications. I'm now getting notifications to invite my friends to use Expatrio and I can't disable spam in the app settings so I've had to block app notifications entirely.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Do better please", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I liked the swiftness of their services; however, the service charges are too much.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Its impossible bureaucracy", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Overall experience was good, but transferring the funds is little cumbersome, and insurance documents are not well understable i feel. \n\nSupportive team deserve appreciation for their timely support.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The worst blocked account you can have here in Germany. They'll give you all the products in your hand ready but without security most of the times not working,. There is also no easy and quick accessible support system you need a information immediately no way you can get it quickly. I live in Berlin they are giving bank account from Frankfurt. Not even contact of bank other than a email. Choose other blocked account while entering Germany as a student even as a working employee.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Process was good, but i did not get response to my query i had to wait for more than 4 days.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It was a lie that FlyWire is quick. It is a regular wire transfer, not a card payment as was advertised.\n\nIt was a lie that FlyWire coukd be made in Eur. It can only be made in USD at an exchange rate 4-5% higher than the interbank rate, a huge markup.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I had a very negative experience with Expatrio. While they promote their blocked account as simple and transparent, the reality is very different. Apart from the clearly advertised €69 setup fee, there are additional hidden charges that are not clearly communicated at the beginning — for example, the monthly €5 service fee, which is charged even before the account is activated.\n\nTheir customer service is quick to respond, but unfortunately lacks the knowledge and clarity needed to resolve issues. It took multiple emails and back-and-forth communication just to get a vague explanation of why part of my blocked funds were missing. The explanations were inconsistent and unclear.\n\nAlso, their health insurance packages are noticeably more expensive compared to other providers on the market. More expensive than many better alternatives.\n\nIn short, the whole process was unnecessarily stressful and time-consuming. What is advertised as “easy and smooth” turns out to be frustrating and opaque. I would not recommend Expatrio unless they significantly improve their transparency and customer support quality.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I received a notice that my remaining blocked account funds would be suspended if I did not provide an IBAN number in the response form for my home bank account. The US does not use the IBAN system, so the form would not take my response. I sent an URGENT inquiry to customer support to provide alternative bank information, but have yet to receive a response and run the risk of losing my remaining funds. THIS IS UNACCEPTABLE. THEY NEED TO HIRE MORE PEOPLE>", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Other than late customer support it's good, the ai bots are useless and human operator number should be provided.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I had a great experience with Expatrio! The blocked account and health insurance setup were smooth and fast. I received my confirmation within 24 hours.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "We had a terrible experience with this digital bank in summer 2024.  Never, ever again. Customer service is an email address and for every single question you must wait 24-48 hours for a reply.  The company is probably just a couple of clowns working out of a bedsit in Berlin getting rich on German visa requirements. Even more disappointing is how Expatrio quickly got TrustPilot to suppress our review, simply because it didn't favour them.  This therefore makes TrustPilot equally untrustworthy too. Business should not be able to gag a review just because they know which buttons to press with TrustPilot.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Seit 3 Wochen ist mein Freund nun in Deutschland und möchte ihr Leben und Arbeiten. \nLeider funktioniert trotz extrem starker Bemühung das verifizieren der Post ID nicht. \nAbsolut schlechter Service und Erreichbarkeit der Firma. Das Geld wieder zubekommen, welches auf dem Sperrkonto liegt, ist auch super schwer.\nWir raten dringend von der Firma ab und werden uns nun Anwaltlich Beraten lassen.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I activated my blocked account on the 14th of July and in their E-Mail it said that I would receive the first payment within 24 hours. I attempted to change the recipient IBAN to another IBAN, as I already had a bank account in Germany by the time I activated my blocked account. I then sent Expatrio an E-Mail that i still haven't received the money on the 16th of July. They told me then that the IBAN i selected was wrong, so I promptly changed it. After that I sent them another E-Mail notifying them I changed the IBAN. They then sent me an E-Mail on the 18th of July, saying that the transfer would be made within 2 business days. It has since been almost 4 business days since that E-Mail. Due to delays regarding the transfer, I am at risk of not paying rent on time and not enrolling to my University.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "No option for adding beneficiary account in blocked account", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I think they need to work on their customer support section. Usually they are using AI chatbox which is not much efficient. There are many issues which need personal response.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I signed up with Expartio recently, and the health insurance was issued immediately after account creation. Yes the processing was quick, but I ran into an issue. I wanted to edit my date of arrival afterward, but there was no option to do so. It would be really helpful if Expartio allowed users to modify their arrival date even after the insurance is sent. Please consider fixing this. Otherwise, a smooth experience overall.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I chose Expatrio over other providers specifically because of their promise that monthly service fees would only be charged after account activation. That was literally the only reason I picked them instead of competitors. During my onboarding in May, the total service fee was clearly listed as €30 for 6 months (€5/month) — and it was meant to be deducted after activation, not before.\n\nDespite this, Expatrio started charging me monthly fees even though my account is not yet activated, and I cannot even access my Blocked Account Statement. I only noticed the deductions after checking my bank statement manually. There was no explanation, no warning, and no visible breakdown in my user account.\n\nWhen I contacted support, I received contradictory answers. One agent told me “we do not withdraw any fees before activation”, while another said, “we do not refund the setup fee as it was charged according to the regulamin”. A third support agent finally said that fees are charged from the moment funds arrive, not from activation — which completely contradicts the onboarding information and chatbot responses that clearly say fees only begin once the account is activated.\n\nAdding to this confusion, a previous €5 charge was automatically refunded last week, without me even contacting support — clearly indicating it was wrongly deducted in the first place. Why is the same mistake happening again now?\n\nIf Expatrio’s fee policies have changed since I opened my account, it is deeply unethical to apply them retroactively without informing existing users or updating documentation. What’s worse, I am being charged for a service that I literally cannot use — I can’t activate the account, can’t view statements, and yet money is being deducted behind the scenes.\n\nThis experience has caused me a huge amount of stress and anxiety, especially since I am going through the stressful visa application process. Instead of making relocation “simple and stress-free” as they claim, Expatrio has done the opposite. Their support system is broken, their communication is unclear, and their actions are misleading.\n\nPlease be very cautious when choosing this company — read every document, take screenshots, and prepare for inconsistency.\n\nUPDATE (End of July):\nI just reviewed my account statement and confirm that Expatrio charged me twice in July (€5 on both the 15th and the 23rd), even though my account is still inactive.\nThey also backcharged a monthly fee for May — despite previously stating in writing that monthly fees would only begin after activation.\n\nThis contradicts both their website policy and what multiple support agents personally told me.\n\nAt this point, this feels like intentional misinformation and extremely poor handling of user trust. I strongly advise others to stay away from this service.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Complicated and difficult to reach - I suggest you choose a different provider.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Expartio does not have any local on call customer support. In case of urgency I have to wait to get reply through mail communication.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It was easy to set up a blocked account with Expatrio, but after that initial step, the ease of use and trouble shooting was really poor.  There were no instructions provided before attempting to access your funds, just that you can do it once you are in Germany.  We learned that you must have a German mobile telephone number, and it must be unique to your account.  (For example, a wife and husband cannot share a mobile phone number and have it work when you both have Expatrio accounts that you need to access.)  Secondly, the app appears to be a beta version that has not been fully tested or documented.  It is buggy and the error messages are either missing or are not helpful.  They keep referring users to their Help FAQs, but they are sorely lacking in the subject matter areas.  It is impossible to reach a human by phone for help, but after submitting a help request to their support team via email, I did get a response, usually within 24 hours.  They do not appear to have a case management system that tracks the history of the case, as I had to resend the same data more than once.  When I was unable to pair my cell phone with the app, which is required to access your funds, the customer support team kept assuming I was entering the data incorrectly, as I never received a text message with the authorization code.  I finally had to ask them what cell phone number they showed in their system.  Even though I had the correct cell phone number in my profile, their banking partner had my home country mobile number, which was initially used to set up and fund the account.  It took them a week to update this telephone number and over two weeks to resolve the issue all together.  This is unacceptable when needing to access your own money for payment.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Couldn't talk to an agent", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "UI is not that good. And Things are not mentioned properly. You need to see all the options to find anything. Please make UI simpler and provide everything in few steps", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I was told by the host that I was not in the list for the webinar when I had clearly signed up for it.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Very very hard to use", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "deducted 55 euro of my total amount and Expatrio don't have any info why the deducted it", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Good that you are creating my health insurance, travel insurance, and chequing account for me, but there were LOTS of buggs. The biggest problem is with Aion bank. Despite transferring EUR 12133 to my account (full amount), Aion bank is only showing EUR 1052. You (expatrio) sent me confirmation that the amount has been received in full and even gave me my 06 Blocked Account confirmation and told me that the issue will be solved promptly, but it has been 2 business days since then, nothing has changed. I am not comfortable with proceeding with my visa application when the bank says they only have EUR 1052 of my EUR 12133. And there were other glitches as well. Like when we upload A2 form, it does not change from \"upload\" to \"update\". There is no way to see the changed progress. I had to email Cohort Go to confirm that.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I made the last payment for my blocked account but its been 2 days, that the amount has been cleared by freewire but still it hasn't shown on the aion bank", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I didn’t like that people only download important documents by having a computer.sometimes it would be easier to do all the process on the phone", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It seems like the customer care does not even read the questions before replying. There is a long list of problems for a customer who has only just started using your service. I genuinely expected better support and reliability. The nature of your service is based on trust and financial care, and unfortunately, I have not experienced either so far. It is really concerning, and I feel I made a wrong choice selecting expartio as the blocked account service.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "On the morning of June 25th, around 11 AM, I tried to access the “Banking” section in the Expatrio app and was suddenly shown a message stating that my account had been temporarily blocked for 12 hours. I immediately reached out to the support team via email.\n\nHowever, when I tried again after 12 hours had passed, nothing had changed — I was still unable to access my account.\n\nOn the morning of June 26th, I received a response from Expatrio stating that the issue was not on my side, but due to a technical problem in their system. I deleted and reinstalled the app. This time, I was prompted to re-pair my phone with the app, but after tapping \"Continue\", I never received any SMS, and the app kept timing out and restarting the pairing process.\n\nAs a student temporarily staying in Germany, I have urgent financial responsibilities — including rent and health insurance payments. I submitted a second email and also posted a review on the Google Play Store explaining my situation.\n\nOn June 27th, I received a reply via email that the issue had been forwarded to the responsible technical team, and I also saw a comment under my Google Play Store review stating that the problem only affects a small number of users, and a new app version fixing the issue would be released on the same day (27.06.2025).\n\nAs of now (June 28th, 12 PM), absolutely nothing has changed.\n\nSo I must ask: is it acceptable for a person to be locked out of their bank account and funds for over 3.5 days?\n\nI don’t even know how much money I have in my account, let alone how to send payments without access to the app. While I trust that the technical team is doing their best, I believe such fundamental, prolonged issues are unacceptable in a platform that handles people’s finances.\n\nBest regards,", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Latest update: it's been 2 months of using the blocked account. Expatrio is still actively trying to scam me. First, right after activation, I've found out that my balance is short of 69 euro. Turns out, they've charged me twice (!) for both accounts that they've tried to open for me. \nLater then, I did not receive my cashback in time and had to again email them and ask for it.\nAnd just now, I've discovered another shortage of 138 euro on my current balance. Expatrio doesn't even care to reply on my emails anymore, even their team lead. At this point I have no idea how this company is not under criminal investigation still. It's wild\n\nNotice how all the good reviews on them are from the profiles with literally just 1 review. Once they receive a bad one, another 2-3 positive \"reviews\" from empty profiles appear, to cover it. Isn't it just genius? \n\nThere is no right of withdrawal in their Terms & Conditions. So be aware, once you send your money to them, it's gone, they've taken it. Also note, that \"Expatrio does not accept and is not obliged to take part in the online dispute resolution procedure of the European Commission\" - meaning you'll have to take them directly to court. You even can't open a changeback case in your bank, because it's a transfer, not a payment for a service, which it clearly is. They receive the money and provide no service.\n\nSo Expatrio tried to open account for me with their partner AION Bank S.A. German Branch. The AION received my €13321 and 2 hours later refused to open it for me, even though they've literally received it from my normal German bank account. Expatrio support then offered another solution for me, which is another partner of them, MangoPay. The agent said that they will transfer the money in 1-2 business days. I almost begged them to do it asap and explained that the embassy has not given me too much time, but somehow I've managed to ask for 48 hours, because that's exactly what Expatrio has promised me. Guess what? Nothing! Absolutely nothing. The transfer has not been made. I've just received another letter stating that \"the issue has now been escalated to the Supervisor\", which is just marvelous. I've just lost an appointment I've been waiting for 7 months. I do not have a bank account. They took all my money. I don't have another 13k to open with another provider. I regret ever coming across Expatrio and strongly recommend that you avoid it at all costs. It's also clear that they get away with it because the target client is a young student without a lawyer or lawyer insurance in Germany. \n\nOn Monday 23rd of June I was told \"1-2 business days\". \nOn Thursday 26th, exactly 4 days later, they've actually started a transfer (or not) and I was told to wait another \"2-3 business days\". \nUpdate 15:30 Tuesday 1st of July. Another 2-3 business days, promised by the support agent, passed by. No service provided. My money is gone.\n\nIf you find yourself in a similar situation, be sure to post about it everywhere in your local communities. Especially if you speak Hindi, Turkish or Russian, post about it everywhere to avoid more people getting ripped off and their lives ruined. I wish there was a single warning about Expatrio before I've sent them all my money! But there wasn't. I'm only discovering it now - hundreds of people missing their appointments, getting their visas rejected, surviving without their money already in Germany, and just a week ago Expatrio blocked tons of people out of access to their own accounts. If you dig deeper, you'll be shocked. \n\nAvoid like plague.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The hidden fees with Expatrio are absolutely awful. What started as $962 quickly jumped to $1,166, and then to $1,360 — seriously, where do these fees even stop? It ended up costing way more than expected. On top of that, their customer service is painfully slow. I had to message them multiple times just to get my money in my account ASAP. And get this — they even had the nerve to question if I actually sent the payment! Totally unacceptable experience. \n\nOverall, the hidden fees and poor communication made the experience frustrating. I recommend potential users be cautious and prepared for delays and extra costs.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Your bank provider took too long to verify my funds for me to receive my proof of funds document. Your team was slow to respond. It was almost three weeks for me to get the document. There was no phone number/call center to speak to a human, only FAQ which NEVER helps on specific cases. Never again working with Expatrio.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "issue with my activating my block account, its about 12 days i am trying to activate my block account, but facing various issues, as a student who saying in germany with empty packet, i faced may problems regarding to my life expences here, there team does not provide clear instruction and also they dont have a physical address that you reffer to them and solve your problem.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Very late response in my view", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Customer Service is helpful but didnt have the best experience with your website. It kept locking me out despite typing in the right code. I had to reset my pw multiple times. Very annoying.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I disliked how you don’t give clear cut instructions.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I open on this platform because it was supposed to be easy and faster than anything else and then, I already uploaded everything and I can’t have my account because I have an Ecuadorian passport? Like make it make sense bro, and the solution they gave me is changed to another bank which I know nothing about with some tricky email and doesn’t explain anything or give some kind certainty.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Complaint 1: The Blocked Amount provided by Expatrio does not comply with the official requirements for the German intensive language course residence permit. The actual legal requirement for 12 months is €13,094 (€1,091.17/month), as confirmed by the Munich Foreigners Office. \n\nExpatrio only allowed me to deposit €12,133. After transfer fees, the confirmation they issued showed just €11,904 (€992/month), which is below the legal threshold. You can verify this on their own calculator Expatrio's website. \n\nAs a result, the Foreigners Office contacted me, stating the amount was insufficient and requested an additional deposit along with a new confirmation.\n\nWhen I contacted Expatrio about the issue, they told me I had to extend the blocked amount and pay a mandatory €69 fee — a charge that would have been unnecessary if they had requested the correct amount in the first place. This feels like a fraudulent and unfair practice.\n\nComplaint 2: They also refused to refund the €69 “Initial Set-up Fee”, even though I activated all required products (bank account and Dr. Walter insurance).\n\nComplaint 3: Expatrio charges €10 for the debit card. You are required to use it once and activate it with a PIN before you can add it to your digital Wallet. However, even after following all the steps, it still can't be added to the Wallet.\n\nFinal advice: Think twice before opening your account with Expatrio. Poor compliance, hidden fees, and non-functional services are not what you expect when moving to a new country.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "In December 2024 I arrived in Germany. I waited a long time for the Christmas weekend, then the weekend in January, then I waited a long time for the term to register here, then I waited a long time to open my bank account in Germany, and when everything was ready, in the first days of April I submitted the documents to Expatrio to activate my account. But unfortunately in the application you can only select payments for the current and previous two months, so I could only select February March and April, December 2024 and January 2025 were not automatically selected. I then wrote an email to support explaining all the reasons, I was told that if I wanted to receive a payment for more than three months I had to send a passport stamp to enter Germany, I did this immediately, but no response after that. Then I wrote again to the support, where I was told that in order for me to receive a payment exceeding three months, I need to send a confirmation from the German authorities that I am in Germany from December 2024. Then I had a long correspondence with them, about seven eight letters, where I was always asked for confirmation from the German authorities, and when I tried to find out what specific document they need, they could not specifically answer, it seemed that it is just a robot all the time responds to my letter, with the same set of words. In the end I wrote letters to Zoll and Bundespolizei, where Zoll replied that it does not issue such certificates, and Bundespolizei replied that their confirmation is a stamp in the passport. I sent a screenshot of the responses from Zoll and Bundespolizei to Expatrio today. I will wait to see what they say. But I am extremely dissatisfied with the cooperation.\n\nВ декабре 2024 г. я прибыла в Германию. Впереди были рождественские выходные затем выходные в январе я долго ждала термин для того чтобы прописаться здесь, затем долго тянулась процедура открытия моего банковского счёта в Германии, и когда все было готово, в первых числах апреля я подала документы в Expatrio для активации аккаунта. Но к сожалению в приложении можно выбрать выплаты только за текущий и предыдущие два месяца, таким образом я могла выбрать только февраль март и апрель, декабрь 2024-го и январь 2025-го автоматически не выбирались. Затем я написала письмо в поддержку с объяснением всех причин, мне ответили что если я хочу получить выплату превышающую три месяца, то мне нужно отправить штамп паспорта о въезде в Германию, я это сделала незамедлительно, но никакого ответа затем не последовало. Затем я снова написала в поддержку, где мне ответили что для того чтобы мне получить выплату превышающую три месяца, то мне нужно отправить подтверждение от немецких властей о том, что я нахожусь в Германии с декабря 2024 г. Затем у меня с ними была долгая переписка, около семи восьми писем, где от меня все время требовали подтверждения от немецких властей, а когда я пыталась выяснить какой конкретно документ им нужен, они не могли конкретно ответить, создалось впечатление что это просто робот все время отвечает на письмо моё, с одним и тем же набором слов. В конце концов я написала письма в Zoll и Bundespolizei, где Zoll ответил что не выдает такие справки, а Bundespolizei ответил что их подтверждением является штамп в паспорте. Скриншот ответов от Zoll и Bundespolizei я отправила сегодня на почту Expatrio. Буду ждать что они ответят. Но я крайне недовольна сотрудничеством.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have a blocked account with Expatrio and urgently needed support last week. I sent an important email, but I received no reply at all. This is unacceptable, especially considering the financial importance of this account.\nI hold a Fiktionsbescheinigung and was unsure which visa type to select in the system, as mine was not listed. There was no guidance or help provided.\nWhen I tried to complete the PostIdent verification at the post office using my passport and Fiktionsbescheinigung, the employee said the passport alone would be sufficient. Of course, the verification failed later and again, no support from Expatrio to clarify or help solve the issue.\nI urgently rely on access to my money and cannot afford to waste more weeks waiting in uncertainty. The lack of communication and clarity is extremely frustrating. I cannot recommend this service to anyone who is in a time-sensitive situation.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Die monatliche Verwaltungsgebühr ist zu hoch.\nBitte ziehen Sie meine monatliche Verwaltungsgebühr nicht ab.\nIch liebe dich über alles 🙏🙏🙏😭😭😭", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I recently changed my address. I want the same to be reflected on my Aion Bank statement as it still shows my previous address. I have been calling Expatrio customer service since past one week and everytime the response I get is, we have requested Aion Bank to make the changes, but to no avail nothing has been done. There is no physical location where I can visit Aion Bank and Expatrio is my only point of contact. I need this document immediately to apply for my Residence Permit and things are getting extremely delayed. I wish Expatrio sees this review and provides me a solution immediately.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "They lied to me when they said that I can withdraw money from \"any\" ATM for \"free\" 3 times in a month. I just withdrew money for the first time this month at Sparkasse, and was charged a €6 fee. I asked for a refund, but to no avail. Hence this bad review!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Ich habe das Geld eingezahlt, Sperrbestätigung bekommen (06 Blocked Amount Confirmation), die Daten lassen sich auf der Seite für Behörden nicht verifizieren - es kommt eine Fehlermeldung, dass der Kunde gar nicht in der Datenbank existiert 🤡🤡🤡 das ist doch euer Business, eine vernünftige Sperrbestätigung in kürzester Zeit auszustellen! Wie kann man es so verkacken?? Jetzt muss ich noch weiter warten, bis sich euer Support diesbezüglich bei mir meldet - die Zeit habe ich in der Studium-Abschlussphase nicht und die ist ohnehin stressig genug!!! So eine nutzlose unverifizierbare Bestätigung kann ich nicht an die Ausländerbehörde schicken, ich kann nicht riskieren, dass gegen mich wegen des Verdachts auf Urkundenfälschung ermittelt wird!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Unnecessary money", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The platform presented the option of opening the blocked account by credit card payment, but this alternative did not work. After several emails they admitted that due to a problem with their payment platform, then if they have a problem with that, it would be best if they did not present that option so as not to waste time and that customers solve their needs with traditional means of payment.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "No contact phone number, chat pot is not helpful, slow response", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Costly. Charging 60£", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have been a customer of Expatrio for several years because of their reliable and effecient process, untill this recent case, my dissapointment is beyond words.\n\nBy 25.02.2025, I have obtained Block Account confirmation letter to proof that I have sufficient fund for to cover 5 months of my living expenses. I used this letter to apply for a visa extension (aplication was handed in weeks before the visa expiration date - we all know it takes long for the officers to reply). So the amount in the block account was for April to August 2025. \nTo my previous knowledge and expierence with Expatrio, the fund in my block account should always remain BLOCKED till I upload a proof of new visa. But this time Expatrio started deducting monthly Subscription fee and even Extension Fee from my account since Feburary - which leads to a result of the incabability of paying out. \n\nI have contacted Expatrio via their Help Center a few times, they told me it's a \"technical issue on the part of Aion Bank\" and \"This issue has been identified and is being resolved. You should have already received your funds back in your account!\" WELL, it is NOT! Also they never replied me again regarding a real solution.\n\nSo here I am, having to borrow money from friends to cover living expenses, when my own money is being held due to Expatrio's technical problem. This is really frustrating, I don't know how much longer this situation will last. BE CAREFUL GUYS, DON'T FALL INTO THE SAME PITFALL AS I DID!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Avoid them. I've sent multiple emails over the last week and it's all bots and second-rate AI with no follow-up available. Hire some humans please, and do your job.  - Now, WATCH. A poorly paid staffer (or \"manager\") is going to write below some kind of meaningless garbage about how they \"strive\" for customer service. It's just garbage. AVOID THEM.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have tried to reach out to Human customer support via email and chatbot, every time I get automated respond from chatbot (Poppy). In case of certain unanswered question and in any emergency to expedite the matter, it is impossible to reach out to Human support of Expatrio.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "late replies", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I tried a lot but in Zoom app, when I entered the webinar ID, i just repeatedly got an error message. \nI missed the webinar, unfortunately.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have lost almost EUR 400 using this shitty platform. Expatrio lies about how it receives money, and there is LITERALLY NO REAL TIME SUPPORT. Expatrio does not have a reliable product, and several people who have used Expatrio experience numerous difficulties transferring money from the global south. They are stealing people's hard earned money due to numerous technical glitches as a result of their badly designed platform and faulty codebase, which they will NEVER OWN UP TO.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "UPDATE:They made my cashback payment after several emails,calls and reviews on Trustpilot and google.\n\nThey deleted my previous review from TrustPilot\neven though the most of my experience was smooth with expatrio, they never deliver the promises they make about the cashbacks and special offers. I used expatrio for blocked account-current account and health insurance and received special offers such as 110 euro cashback for health insurance with expatrio. But they didn't give the cashback at all even though i called and asked 10+ times. Go use a cheaper provider and don't fall for expatrio's fake promotions.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "communication is bad and chatbot chatting make me angary", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Hi am really want to apologize expatrio team that i didn't not attend or join your online classed of study to Germany am was busy in my college exams bcz that my last year of electrical engineering couse of three year's am sorry but next it not going to be happen again", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Exact point of information not received", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Overall it was Good. The products and services provided by Expatrio are very good, especially for students going abroad for higher studies. I faced some difficulty with the fund transfers to my blocked account. The initiate payment part was a bit confusing for me as I made more than 1 transfer because I had a transfer limit when transferring from my bank. For me, it was not clear if I had to initiate a second payment for a second transfer. I think maybe a short video within the Expatrio app in the blocked account section showing how to set up and how to make single and multiple transfers could have helped me. This video could also be made a mandatory watch for anyone using the blocked account service before transferring money. One more thought I would like to add to this is that, although I kept emailing the Expatrio team and yes they did reply within 24 hours in most cases, I still felt like the replies from the team were not 100% helpful for my concerns. Everything did work out quite fine in the end but I felt the process could be eased a bit more.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "To time taking", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "For God's sake, please, it is my humble request — please give me my M10 certificate. I am using your blocked account service along with health and travel insurance. My enrollment is halted just because of this please", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have one serious issue ,there was health insurance offered with value package,i have recived a private one but i need publichealthinsurance. In germany public insurance is a popular choice and i would like to go with it .Also my university needs m10 conformation from insurance company assuring university that , i am insured through them . Please help me with getting tk public insurance , i already have got my value package blocked account . I have a deadline to meet . Can you please email me procedure to apply for tk public health insurance and also let me know , after getting one can they mail my university,  regarding it", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Still don’t know about my incoming insurance!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am really disappointed because at the time of need their is no one to reply. normally it take at least 2 days to expatrio to reply back.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Please make sure the Muthoot Forex send people the correct tax amount.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "최악입니다 환불을 원할 정도입니다", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Pedi para liberarem o meu pagamento mensal e, na validação do passaporte, dizem não reconhecer o documento. Não consigo contatar a empresa porque a única (péssima) forma de atendimento é enviando e-mail e demoram um dia útil para responder. Enquanto isso, tenho que esperar.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Expatrio Telegram Group makes sale not supporting!!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "travellers insurance came through after  after a long wait. Response to any email seeking any clarification takes more than 2 days. I am short on time and any contact number I try does not work or get through. Email addresses are hard to come by unless you are contacted by the team.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Card is not accepting the payment as there are no options left for the insurance payment to be done.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I liked expatrio service but I didn't like the fact that my travel insurance documents were removed suddenly all of a sudden without any notice. Please make sure that travel and health insurance documents as well as blocked account documents are not removed as this mistake could prove to be detrimental to somebody's visa process which can prove to be fatal for someone's future.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Very delayed service and mail. Not providing proper solution on time. Now please provide me the final health and travel insurance certificate in which the coverage price and date is mentioned.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Poor service from expatrio customer care , i was trying to change my health insurance from private student health insurance TO public health insurance but they are doing this for me....  i want to opt to public health insurance not private health insurance . Regards RAJU YADAV KUTLA", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Worst experience, only got automated replies throughout my queries. Would have to face issues in my enrollment.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It’s a platform\nBasically to help yourself. Funds transfer for opportunity card is very difficult to make from India no forex exchanges will do it for you with the expatrio payment info available. Need a customer service team if not 24/7 at least for 7 hours rather then mail and just wait for the response any other doubts we would have to send a mail again. While dealing with huge funds it’s always better for more clarity with a love agent. Otherwise the site is more user friendly and easy to understand. Kudos to expatrio in helping many.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Please reduce the processing time for transferring the amount to blocked account. It took way too much time for us, a lot more than 5 to 6 business days.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I need to upload a document in order to maintain bank account access. In other words, this is TIME SENSITIVE. There is no provision in the app for uploading this particular document. I sent an email FOUR DAYS AGO and there has not been a response. Expatrio is clearly understaffed to handle customer service enquiries and they don't seem interested in doing anything about it. Once you can get an actual response, the service is usually ok, but getting the response takes an unreasonably long time. HIRE MORE PEOPLE!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I’ve been trying to log in for days and haven’t been able to access it", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "My issues have not been resolved yet", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Customer service", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Refund process is very slow.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "All blocked accounts are expensive and one might think that blocked account has to be activated before you see the startup and monthly service fees in your balance. However, you may see all the accumulated monthly fees of 2 years deducted in your blocked account balance in a minute 2 years later, like it happened to me after opening my blocked account 2 years ago. It was hard to figure out what was happening and I thought it was a technical issue after seeing 209 euros less in my balance in a minute. The Expatrio customer team told me that it was because of the monthly service fees and account opening etc. and they sent me an account statement so I can see in detail. Expatrio gives you umbrella when it's sunny and takes back when it's rainy.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Please focus more on establishing call assist as the most important feature or service. Emails are great but not when financial things come into consideration. Money always is such where confusion, fear arises during hard times and panic is inevident. \n\nMostly hearing someone out over a call and getting assured is far better than waiting for 2-3 days for a response over email. Hence 3 stars.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The bank is never reachable by phone and if you write an email you only get an automatic reply and your request is not addressed. I am totally disappointed and advise against this bank and this website!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Payment got reflected very late.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Terrible service !!!, My visa got rejected in november and from start of december i am contacting them for funds. Its been more than two months and i have still not got my blocked amount back. Its really frustrating why it is taking too long to just send my own money back.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "customer service is really bad", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "customer service is poor", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "everything is so complicated and it is really hard to communicate with you because you take too long to respond to emails.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am waiting for the activation of my blocked account. I am asked to upload my Residence Permit for the same. However, my Residence Permit has expired and I have Bescheinigung (Not Fiktionbescheinigung). There is no place to upload Bescheinigung and hence I merged my expired Residence Permit and Bescheinigung in a single PDF and uploaded it. However, I have received rejection multiple times for the verification of the documents. I have emailed several times to solve my query but did not get any solution (only got generic automated replies). My funds are stuck in the blocked account. What do I do?", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The account was opened in October 2024, the Visa was denied in November 2024 and immediately filled out the form to close the account, but our refund has not come yet. We have already lost close to $800 in exchange rate differences. It sucks. Easy to take money and a nightmare to get it back. Even after proving (including sharing personal bank statement) that I am the one who paid for the blocked account for my son they still don't want to communicate with me. when my son sends emails and copy me they take me off the email chain. I better stop here before I say regrettable things.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The customer service is too slow, takes a whole day for an email, and several days to sort out a problem. The app is very buggy.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I opened a 1 year blocked account with Expatrio. Since they work with a bank called Aion Bank, we made the transfer to that bank (23.01.2025). My money was deposited into the blocked account and I received a confirmation, the PDF was uploaded and I printed it to use for my visa appointment. However, 1 week later on Friday (31.01.2025) at 5 pm, I received an email from customer service, the email said \"We cannot open your account with Aion, we will open it with Mangopay, write that we have informed you and that you approve the terms of use and we will open a new one\". I have a visa appointment in 2 days (03.02.2025). My blocked account is currently closed, and the newly opened account says \"Awaiting deposit\". Is this done during the weekend? Firstly, do I have to live for 2 days without knowing where my 18 thousand Euros are? Thirdly, if you can't open it, why was the PDF sent to me 1 hour after we deposited the money? If I had used this PDF long ago, my visa would not have been issued due to false documents at the consulate and I would never have been able to cross the German border. There is no one I can talk to about this disgrace. They have been using it for 4 years. My friends have never experienced anything like this with this bank. They do not respond to my e-mails.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Some student have to face issues in different questions but your customer services response are very late like in my case", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "You have extremely slow costumer service. I emailed two days ago but haven’t received response so far.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Government wants 1091€ for monthly for blocking but your system misguided me by making me transfer 992€", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Everyone has different problems or issues. It would be better if you posted the different issues and solutions, how long it will take to resolve the issue, in the FAQ section. It will make the procedure easier for us. It would be better if the response and the time taken to solve the issue is faster.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Offer decent services, but they need to have a number that people can call. My bank account got raided by scammers and I have to wait ages for them to respond to a contact sheet. In urgent situations customers need faster alternatives", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Hi Team, I have send 2 emails on my blocked account queries and requests. But I haven't heard back on the email and also when tried to calling your customer service, the call was automatically transferred to Voice email.. Why it's so ?  Could you please get back to me as soon as possible.?\nThanks,\nSarala Devi K", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am an international student at IU on the Berlin campus. I have already opened an account at Expatrio Global Services, which is physically located on Linienstrasse 156-157, 10115 in Berlin, Germany. I fulfilled all the requirements for my blocked account activation. I mean I have a signed rental agreement, a city registration and a post box address in a co-living area. When I email them to activate my account after I uploaded all the required documents. They sent me a postident QR code for verification, which is the alternative method of account activation. When I got to the post office / postbank they couldn't verify my passport because my passport was extended on the other page, which is a technical issue in the German system. So, as a student, I went to their office in Berlin to show them that I was physically present. First, Expatrio refused and insisted that you must be in Berlin. Actually, I was there and once I went, I took a selfie picture of mine and my passport with a visa on it and sent those pictures to them as proof of existence. So, when I call their phone number, the machine tells me to wait for 2 minutes. Indeed, it doesn't work if you call them several times during the day and no one is answering the call. I don't know what they want by such delaying and not replying to my emails and not giving a physical appointment to solve this issue. I am writing this comment because I am here in Berlin city and I have lots of proof. If someone from the expatrio service team replies here, I will ask what you want from a student and what you believe in ? How much proof do you want and for how long will you keep my account inactive? Every student around the world has trusted this financial body regarding blocked account. If they realize that they will face such a problem in the future and no one will care about their financial problems, then this  organization will never be trustworthy. They won't open an account on this platform because you only care about money, and you don't care about the students' financial problems here in Germany. So why are you doing this to me ? ? ? This my right to ask for my money to support my education. I will never give up...", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have been asked to transfer an initial amount to an block account, and 2 weeks after the sum has been transferred with domestic transfer, they still haven't update the payment status.\n\nEverytime I try to contact Expatrio with an email with regarding to the situation, they will only reply in AI and the information is completely USELESS.\n\nThis is a non-trustworthy organisation with virtually no Customer Service! Using this service is like gambling for not being scam for thousands of euro.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "TOO MANY ADEVERTISING E-MAILS!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Slow service and takes alot of time for one simple question", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "im facing some tectincal issues with creating the password of the account", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "At the moment I'm waiting on call for 20+ minutes for customer service to answer. I need to enhance my blocked account amount to comply with regulations that have kicked in. Ive been emailing and calling expatrio service for a week now, they agree to make the changes but do nothing afterwards. All emails go unanswered. Pathetic, pathetic experience.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am Yusuf İmdat Ceylan, User ID: 985963. I have successfully transferred €12,135 to my Expatrio blocked account; however, only €12,105 was credited to the account.\n\nCould you kindly clarify why there is a €30 deduction? I have already paid the transfer fees to my own bank.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Jan 15, 2025 - Sharing my pretty unpleasant Expatrio experience here - hopefully the customer services sees this and improves their record.\n\nI opened a blocked account in July 2024 with Expatrio in the anticipation of my German study visa. Opening the account was seamless. I deposited a significant amount close to Eur 11,000.\n\nAs things happen in life, my visa was rejected for some reason. \n\nNow I start the refund process to reclaim my money in November 2024 and this started my ordeal with Expatrio. After a few email exchanges, I figured out that in addition to uploading the Passport and the Visa rejection letter, a document containing the proof of the original transactions from the original bank accounts has to be submitted to get the refund of the money in the blocked account. \n\nFor some reason, the app says \"Insufficient documents\" - which was cleared up with Expatrio confirming a check had been done. As requested by Expatrio, I resubmitted these documents two more times, only to be greeted by the \"Insufficient documents\" message.\n\nNow it is already 15 January 2025, and I have no proper way to contact Expatrio - the emails go unanswered or I get a delayed response and the Chatbot on the website just reflects the process to close the account without any option for human intervention, and calling them diverts me to a mail box. \n\nAnd of course, there were no replies to my voice message. This is pretty unpleasant to say the least. This delayed refund process is causing endless problems, as this amount would solve personal issues I am facing, just because Expatrio is withholding my funds.\n\nCan anybody from Expatrio suggest on how to go about the refund process? A delay of 3+ months is absolutely unacceptable, especially when you just asking for your own money to be returned! \n\nThis is definitely not earning any goodwill for Expatrio. I hope the folks at Expatrio wake up and do the needful.\n\nGiven the service I have received so far, I will give zero stars as a super unhappy customer.\n\nI appreciate your earliest response in resolving this matter.\n\nFeb 09, 2025 - I have had a pleasant experience with Expatrio as far as the features they offer. And I received my refund after a significant delay. Expatrio had tried to make the process simpler, but red tape issues made it very difficult. Thanks to the Expatrio team who made it possible to get the refunds done as soon as possible.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I had some difficulties about my money transfer. And could  not contact to your experts in time.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Since I have lost my access to my email which is registered to expatrio, I have completed all the steps they want and send all the information that they want. Although they say that they will respond the tickets in 1 business days, it has been 4 business days and still nothing! They did not do anything. I have 20.000 Euro inside and I cannot neither withdraw it nor do anything!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The current account balance in the app and the amount shown on the blocked account bank statement are not the actual amount transferred, there is a short of money. Even after submitting the complaint for this issue, there is no real human reply, instead, I only received the bot answer. Please look into this matter.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I submitted a request to add additional basic sum for my university fee but there is no human response from the team.\n\nPlease fix this issue.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "1. Expatrio stole 10€ from me. They have an option to order a physical card. I clicked on it and then proceeded to select free shipping. Problem is, they charged me 10€ an hour later  apparently this was fees for the card order that was placed. They never disclosed there was any charge. Luckily it was just 10€, what if it was more? They should disclosed it clearly. There are dozens of online bank options in Germany everyone offers free physical cards I assumed it was the same here because no charge was mentioned.\n\nWhen I wrote to customer support immiditaly on the same day, they responded 1 week later that the order was processed and hence no refund can be done. Both the undisclosed charge and the delayed response on my ticket for cancellation was their fault but I had to bear the losses.\n\n2. They have the worst customer support staff. The agents themselves might not be bad at their job but expatrio probably has them overworked or mismanaged. They reply very late often 1-2 weeks of waiting for simple query. Even when they do write back they give useless information that is either something you already know or irrelevant. Once they replied with completely wrong info regarding tax id number. If they are themselves not clear on what to do how will they help us? Still waiting for the simple tax id query to be solved, it's been weeks.\n\nMy friends used fintiba and I'd recommend that to you if any of these sound like problems to you too.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Support is not at all good. Service is okay. Overall just a okayish service. Neither anyone answers your call nor a agent chat with you.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Customer service was responsive without even the swift copy of 2nd transaction they were tracked and issue my funds. After I wrote them a email with my emergency situation of next day visa appointment. Good Team.\n\nUpdate:\nI have requested for refund with Sperrfreigabe, it has been over 10 days, there has been no clear update on where the refund process, it just says 1st verification completed (10 days after update) and refund is under process.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I’ve been trying to activate my account for weeks now. I first contacted customer support about the issue with insufficient documents on 30/12 and it's now 10/01 with no reply or resolution. I uploaded all the required documents, but the transfer proof document doesn’t show any status ( like \"pending\")  On the website  there is a pop-up confirming the upload  but in the app nothing appears. And in both cases the document doesn’t seem to upload which seems like a glitch.\nAlso the visa document requested doesn’t apply to my case since I’m already in Germany and this is not my first blocked account.\nI URGENTLY need this resolved because it's really frustrating, and i need to access the money as soon as possible !!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I didnt have the support with changing my insurance coverage with Dr. Walter. I want the provisit studet and the system only gives me the EDUCARE24. The expatrio support team have not give me a solution since december 19, last year. I still trying to have this resolution fixed.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Customer service is too bad.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "My experience has been terrible because you are not providing my travel health insurance even if I’ve selected that as my product.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The interface is fine, but the step from payment to uploading payment receipts is unclear, which delays the process. It could also be in Spanish since they supposedly have a large Latin American audience. \n\nThe worst part is that the currency exchange process is not transparent. The amount I was supposed to deposit was €6,151, which at any exchange rate equals approximately CLP 6,300,000. However, I had to pay CLP 6,700,000, and there is no explanation of the reason, rates, or exchange calculations.\n\nThey claim to be the cheapest (Expatrio), but after comparing options, I found that while Fintiba has higher maintenance fees, they clearly state the exchange rate. Additionally, the total amount to pay with Fintiba was €200 less.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The company needs an emergency call center/mail. I´ve been trying to get in contact with someone regarding an issue with my incoming insurance but no one has responded yet. Additionally, I missed my visa appointment due to an error on the website.\nBesides that, everything was very easy.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Respected sir/Madam,\nMy name - Ganesh Vitthal Thorbole\nExpatrio No.- 808323\n\nSir/Madam on 27.12.2024 there were 6 consecutive unauthorized transactions were been made of worth € 500 from 9.02 PM to 9.07 PM. I lost €3000 euros all at once I am been a victim of financial fraud .I didn't withdrew all this money as well as I reported this matter to BERLIN POLICE regarding this issue. I am attaching the written POLICE complaint which I filed and I expect to get all my money back from the aion bank which is partnered with expatrio. Sir/Madam I will attach the copy of POLICE COMPLAINT in the contact form as well as the the copy of unauthorised transactions.So it is my HUMBLE request you to take immediate action and please return all of 3000 € money back into my account.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Hice la transferencia a la cuenta bloqueada de expatrio. Todavía no recibo el email de confirmación. La transferencia se realizó hace diez días y no me llega el email. Lo peor de todo es que al querer contactarme con los servicios al cliente me responde un BOT al email. Me están retrasando la aprobación de la visa debido a esta empresa.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I liked the Blocked Account, the Travel Insurance and all but the thing I didn't like is the lack of options of  communication. There is no Indian customer care number, and the online complaint services are also not up to the mark and often delayed.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Worst experience ever customer service is very poor my problem is they didn't give me travel insurance yet and ihave to submit on vfs at 2 jan 2025 please solve my problem", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Does not tell me what I need to do until it is immediately required. \nTried to activate my blocked account, found out I need a german phone number first. \nTried to activate my insurance, found out I can not use a US bank for this. \nAll of this would have been good to know so that I could have prepared these things beforehand. Expatrio leaves a lot of information out so that this process appears simple, but in practice they just make it very frustrating. I wish I could switch providers but it is too late.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I experienced overall expatrio good service but one thing expatrio must improve reply any questions immediately in case of emergency i.e,missing any deadline like visa appointment. Expatrio don't reply before 1or 2 days .\nThey should make policy in case of emergency reply as soon as possible.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Very smooth process but Customer service response is slow and don't care about their client problem", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "No replay from support and even profile data updation doesn’t reflect in the newly generated certificates", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have been in Germany for 2 months, I started the process of activating my health insurance, they told me that they would send me a letter of activation and my card, but more than a month has passed and I still do not have my health insurance, also my bank informs me that they are asking me to pay too high a fee and expatrio does not inform me about anything, it is not the first time I have had a problem.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I'm still waiting for an Answer for a Message that I send on Wednesday asking about what to in case renewing my passport!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I must say its fine.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I sent many emails but didn’t had any answer", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "More fast answer the emails and i have a Problem with my block account and i don’t receive answers", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Too much delay", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "No immediate coustomer support, delay in response. Even there is chance of visa rejection if i didn't get documents within time.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "J'ai aimé votre Professionnalisme auprès de tout nouveau venu dans Expatrio.\nMerci !", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I still have some unanswered questions but opening the account was a breeze!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I didn't get Travel Insurance with value package. Everything else was easy and smooth.\n\nAlso, no response yet after contacting the customer service.\n\nUpdate:\nI contacted Customer Service on December 5th. I received the initial reply with instructions on December 10th. I followed the instructions and completed the necessary steps on the same day. \nNow, I don't know when the next step is going to be.\n\nI can't believe this service is included in a value package. I need it tomorrow for my visa application, so I'm probably going to have to opt for another provider since I don't expect a reply before that.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am extremely disappointed with the customer support experience I’ve had with Expatrio. I reached out to request an adjustment to my payout schedule due to an issue with the start date I mistakenly set. I was told that the matter would be resolved within 48 hours, but it has now been well beyond that time frame, and I have received no updates or response.\n\nThe only way to contact support is via email, and even though I provided all the necessary documents (including my registration certificate, entry stamp, residence permit, and passport copy), my emails seem to be ignored. Every time I reach out, I am reassured that a customer agent is looking into the issue, but there’s no follow-through or resolution.\n\nThis lack of communication and accountability is frustrating, especially since this matter is time-sensitive. I hope this review encourages Expatrio to improve their support process and provide more reliable and responsive customer service.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "it has been 2 weeks I have raised an issue with their team to update my passport number on my block account confirmation letter but there is no update.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Muy mal servicio. Llevo más de 8 días exigiendo mi transferencia mensual desde que recibí el correo de liberación del pago. Al consultar por ello, sólo me responde un robot. soy estudiante y no he recibido mis pagos de este mes cuando ya subi todos los documentos.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Late reply.i will apprisiate if you reply timely", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Dear Expatrio Support Team,\n\nI hope this message finds you well. I am writing to express my concern regarding a support request I submitted on November 28, 2024, which remains unresolved. Despite reaching out to your team to clarify certain matters, including my decision not to proceed with insurance through TK and Dr. Walter, I have not received a response.\n\nTo further emphasize the urgency of this matter, my friend, who submitted a similar inquiry around the same time, received a response within a day, while I have been waiting for over a week without any feedback.\n\nGiven the time-sensitive nature of this issue, I kindly request an immediate update or resolution to the matter. Your prompt assistance would be greatly appreciated.\n\nThank you for your attention to this urgent issue. I look forward to your swift response", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "TERRIBLE. AVOID!!!!!!!!\nI have had ongoing issues with Expatrio - and the only way you can get any reply is by writing a bad review here. What kind of company is this?? I need to change my monthly payouts - I have emailed and called for days but have not gotten any reply. This is the worst interaction I have EVER had with a company. I would never recommend them to anyone.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "AVOID EXPATRIO: COMPANY DOES NOT WORK FOR STUDENTS \n\nI am an international student who needed a blocked account in order to apply for my VISA/ residency permit, which Expatrio EXPLICITLY ADVERTISES for. \nHowever, when I try to access the money in my blocked account, which I need to pay rent and feed myself, their identity verification process asks for a copy of my visa, which the website says for TEMPORARY ACCESS YOU DO NOT NEED. Why does the app and website say two contradicting things? I now have to wait the amount of time it takes to receive a VISA in Germany (which is multiple months)  to access this money, and am now having to consider leaving due to being unable to sustain myself. This is a ridiculous flaw in their app, and judging by other reviews left, MULTIPLE other students have had to face this issue, with a complete LACK of customer service or care from Expatrio's end. I just want to be able to access my money which I deposited, but have had no help or clarity in resolving my issue, just obviously AI replies that hold no relevance.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Worst is a very small word, it's very worst support", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It’s now been over two months that Expatrio has failed to find a solution to the issues blocking me from accessing my money. I have expressed this in emails and attempted to make telephone calls and none are answered. Trust Pilot is the only way you can get in contact with their support team. I cannot imagine what is more important for the support team than fixing a fundamental flaw in their technology that is preventing customers accessing their money, and yet it has been over two months and not been resolved. I would be fascinated to hear how large the department is, and the amount of requests they actually resolve in a day.\n\nOne star is far too high for the abhorrent service I’ve had in the last three months. Please save yourself the financial stress and choose another service.\n\nAnd to the member of staff who reads this review - don’t waste your time trying to justify this issue with how busy the team is. The team has had over two months to fix this issue. You can’t be that busy. Your time would be better spent finding the extensive records of my issues and Expatrio’s inaction in your email account (sent by James Clark - user ID unknown because my app is not functioning).", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Hi team it's been more then 10 days with 6 working days I have made my funds transfer and my visa slot was also done with pending blocked account documents till now there is no update in the app nor any reply to my mails if u give update atleast i can attach to mail and submit to embassy my id is 963873 .", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The customer care although quite fast in reply via email(1-3days),  the support number is basically useless . You call , they say average wait is 6 minutes and 20 minutes later , you have no operator to answer your call.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The customer support doesn't reply to the mails and there is no communication and coordination between the service provider and customer \nI wanted to get my health insurance canceled and i still didn’t get any response from their side", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Das ist unerhört!!! Ich habe bereits ein neues Foto von meinem Passport mit den angegebenen Bedingungen hochgeladen. Expatrio hat mir immer noch keine Blocked Amount Confirmation gegeben!!!\n\nDas ist nicht in Ordnung. Sowas habe ich noch nie erlebt. Ich habe bereits Jobinterviews und muss alle Termine verschieben, weil Expatrio nicht auf meine Nachrichten antwortet oder das Problem nicht klärt!!\n\nGeht gar nicht!!!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Need more support for Customer when we face anything while opening blocked account , and Faced delying response from you , Please improve support throught person to person chatbot or direct call .", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am a student in Hamburg, I had transferred 7148 Euro of amount to expatrio in October 2024. Expatrio had confirmed that their banking partner(AION bank)had received the amount but expatrio was yet to receive the amount . on October 17th I asked expatrio to resend the amount back to the original sender(The amount was sent from my mothers account). for which they agreed and told it might take up a month, but now even after 5 weeks I haven't received the amount. Expatrio isn't solving the issue and AION bank says I need to contact Expatrio. never trusting Expatrio again", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Extremely stressful experience as a student needing to pay bills, no access to my own money for well over a month now. Seems to be one document holding up my activation which I have clearly queried in my emails but either received a completely irrelevant reply or no reply at all.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Hi! \n\nEverything went smoothly, as I opened my blocked account and transferred the funds. After that, I went through the first Postident Verification Procedure -- everything was fine, but they didn't receive it. The status of the account in the app went from. \"activating\" to \"awaiting activation\". I thought that smth must have gone wrong at the post office, so I did the procedure again, and the same thing happened. I then tried repeatedly to contact customer support, but they answered very randomly -- for example, they didn't answer a single email last week. There isn't any other way to contact them, unfortunately:(\n\nI am stuck with no funds now (my own money), cause the customer support just doesn't seem to care", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I didn’t receive the answer that I wanted", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I liked how fast the process was, but still there should be someone like call centre who can reach out to students for help with some details like beneficiary details and late response also", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Expatrio does not reply on time. More than 1 month they have held my money. Each email takes ages to get a reply from. My Anmeldung was completed in the first week of October and its November 23 and they still have not released my blocked account money. This company does not care about customers at all. Cannot call them, they do not respond to emails. The international students will be left crying without their money. There is an error on the app and they just have not fixed it nor provided any support.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Support is zero", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "My complain about account activation and access to funds is yet to be resolved. We are approaching the weekend and I will appreciate if this doesn’t extend to another week. \n\nA quick update on this complain… my account has been activated.\nThanks Expatrio for taking actions and listening.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have been waiting for a week for the money that was transferred to an account that is not mine. They said they would resolve it in 2 days to be transferred to my account and it's been 5 days and they still haven't done it. it's R$992. completely tiring and frustrating.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "always have problem when i activate my blocked account.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Hello, would you be able to solve my issue regarding failed identity verification? Its been more than 2 weeks since I had this issue, and I have not received a proper instruction from Expatrio. In the app, it says I will soon receive an email from your team with further instructions, but there has been nothing until now.\n\nThe only feedback that I received was that they are waiting on Aion Bank's further instructions. I sent an email to Aion Bank directly to help me assist with this issue, but the response that I got was to contact Expatrio customer service.\n\nUser ID: 913145", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have been trying to activate my blocked account so I could access my funds but just automated response. It will be nice if there’s a customer care number one can speak to.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Ich habe meinen Sperrbetrag ausersehen doppelt überwiesen. Der Betrag ist angekommen, das sehe ich auf meinem Account. Ich habe nach 2 Wochen immer noch keine (06) Blocked Amount Confirmation erhalten. Ich habe um eine Klärung gebeten, ob man den einen Überweisungsbetrag wieder an mich überweisen kann oder meinen Remaining Months auf 2 Monate ändert.\n\nIch bin zutiefst enttäuscht, dass sich nach 2 Wochen immer noch keiner gemeldet hat.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Subject: Urgent Assistance Needed for Blocked Account Activation\n\nDear Expatrio Team,\n\nI am reaching out for urgent assistance regarding my blocked account. I arrived in Germany this month and have been trying to activate my account. The first step required me to upload a photo of my visa, which I did. However, it has been more than two weeks, and the status still shows \"Activation in process,\" with my visa photo remaining pending.\n\nI am extremely stressed about this situation as I need to pay my rent by the end of the month, and my funds are running low. I am ready to complete the verification process, but I am unable to do so because I am stuck at this stage. When I attempt to access the banking section of the app, it automatically redirects me to the blocked account section.\n\nI have sent multiple emails and tried to contact support, but unfortunately, I have not received a response.\n\nPlease provide me with a way to proceed with activating my blocked account urgently. If this issue cannot be resolved, I may feel compelled to consider my rights regarding this situation. Expatrio has provided excellent service until my arrival in Germany, but now I am facing significant difficulties.\n\nThank you for your attention to this matter. \n\nUser ID: 916643", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I was sent a block account activation email with statement that you will receive first monthly payout soon. They haven't sent me my 1st payout since 45 days I have landed in Germany. I wrote multiple emails to them but didn't get any reply from them. They also don't pick calls which shows annoying customer support. Please don't go with their services. There are multiple option out there who'll make processes easier for you instead of adding on to your initial struggles.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I haven't been able to connect on call with customer support for a week!\n\nI can't activate my account and nobody tells me what to do! Literally living with no money.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Tried four straight hours yesterday and now another three hours to reach them out over phone line, nobody picks up the call. \n\nNever replied to my query in contact sheet, it's been three business days passed already. \n\nNot sure what's going on!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Pésimo servicio al cliente. Llevo más de 12 días hábiles exigiendo mi transferencia mensual desde que recibí el correo de liberación del pago. Al consultar por ello, sólo me responde un robot. No puede ser que una entidad no cumpla sus responsabilidades ni de explicaciones de qué sucede con el dinero de estudiantes, sobre todo si es para mantenerse en un país extranjero.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I signed up with Expatrio to open a blocked account and secure health insurance for my stay in Germany. However, I’ve encountered a number of frustrating issues. I attempted to transfer funds from my UAE bank account to my German blocked account with Aion Bank, but the payment was rejected either by Aion Bank or the intermediaries involved. Unfortunately, no reason was provided for the rejection.\n\nSince the relationship with the AION bank is handled through Expatrio, when I reached out to Aion Bank’s agents, they simply redirected me to Expatrio. Sadly, Expatrio has been unresponsive to my queries, and their customer support is virtually impossible to reach. Despite numerous attempts to contact them by phone, I was left on hold until my call time ran out—international calls are expensive, and I ended up getting nowhere.\n\nBefore attempting another transfer, I need to understand the reason for the rejection to avoid making the same mistake. However, Expatrio has not been helpful in clarifying the issue. To make matters worse, I am unable to cancel my previous payment or initiate a new one through Expatrio’s platform(so that i can try sending a small amount first and if it is successful then transfer the rest of the fund). This has left me in a deadlock situation, where my application process is delayed and I am unable to proceed.\n\nExpatrio suggested I try using WISE or similar third-party services to make the transfer, but unfortunately, these platforms are not available in the UAE region. As a result, I am left with no choice but to attempt another bank transfer.\n\nOverall, my experience with Expatrio has been extremely disappointing. The lack of support and communication has created unnecessary delays in my process, and I am now stuck with no clear solution in sight. I would not recommend their services based on my current experience.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I recently went through the interview process for a Senior Product Designer role at Expatrio GmbH, and unfortunately, the experience left a lot to be desired in terms of professionalism, respect, and transparency.\n\nThe process started with two initial interviews, which went fairly well. However, I was then assigned a design test task on a Friday, with a deadline to complete it by Monday. The assignment was a full audit and redesign of one of their actual existing products—essentially, a free UX/UI consultation. Despite this extensive workload, I completed the task within the timeframe, expecting feedback and further instructions soon after.\n\nHowever, after submitting the assignment, I didn’t hear back from Expatrio for nine days. After I followed up, they still didn’t respond for another two days. I reached out again, this time to inform them that I was disconnecting the Figma file due to the complete lack of communication. Only then did I receive a vague response asking me to re-enable access to the file and to “please wait” an additional five days—without any explanation for the delays or silence.\n\nThis experience highlighted several red flags for me:\n\nLack of Respect for Candidates' Time and Effort: Expecting candidates to complete unpaid, real-world product work on such a tight deadline is unprofessional, especially for a senior-level position.\nPoor Communication and Transparency: There was no clear timeline or communication about what was happening after each stage, and I was left in the dark for an extended period.\nLack of Process or Professionalism: The vague, “fluffy” responses I received didn’t inspire confidence, and the unstructured nature of the process raised questions about how the company operates internally.\n\nAfter the long delays and lack of feedback, I decided to withdraw my application. The experience made it clear that this was not an environment that valued transparency or trust—a deal-breaker for me as a senior candidate.\n\nFor others considering design roles here, I would strongly advise confirming up front how any design assessments will be used and what the expected timeline is. In the future, I’ll be more careful about agreeing to unpaid work on actual products during interviews, and I’d suggest others do the same.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am feeling ax trimly bad experience because I didn't receive my block amount still now.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have been trying to resolve an issue with my blocked account for over 1.5 months, and despite my countless attempts to contact customer support, I have not received any reply or solution. This is causing me serious stress and financial strain.\n\nLast month, I was unable to pay my rent because of this blocked account. Thankfully, I had a friend to help me out, as I didn’t carry enough cash with me. I shouldn’t have to depend on others to cover basic needs due to an issue that’s entirely beyond my control.\n\nI received an email saying that my account can be reactivated if I verify my identity via PostIdent and that I would receive a coupon via email to help with this. However, when I try to activate my account now, the activation option has disappeared from the app, leaving me stuck without any way to resolve this.\n\nI have sent multiple emails seeking help, but have yet to receive a response. This situation is completely unacceptable, and I am requesting immediate action to restore my account. Furthermore, given the inconvenience and financial strain this issue has caused, I believe I am entitled to compensation for the delay and lack of support.\n\nI sincerely hope that this issue can be resolved within this week. If not, I will be forced to take legal action to get the attention I need.\n\nPlease resolve this as soon as possible!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I faced some issues while i tried to activate my account u should evolve and develop your platform so people don’t have to face this kind of technical issues thank you and don’t get my comment wrong it’s just to make you improve", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "EDIT (13/11/24): I had to take drastic action and guess the email addresses of Expatrio's managers to finally get help from their team. Only after sending an email explaining how urgent my situation was and exposing how much I was being ignored by Expatrio's customer support did I immediately receive my refund. I am grateful to the person who finally listened to me and helped (likely those who received my email), but I still maintain my criticisms of Expatrio's customer service. They urgently need a support center with more people and better qualifications to resolve our issues.\n\n[ORIGINAL REVIEW BELOW]\nI initially left a negative review for Expatrio due to problems with their Portal but ended up deleting it when the Portal finally worked. However, I now feel forced to leave a one-star review again because of how I've been ignored in my recent attempts to contact them.\nIt all started when I tried to request the closure of my account, and I was instructed to do so through the Expatrio Portal. I couldn't immediately close the process due to an error, so I reached out to the Expatrio team on Instagram to try to resolve the issue. The problem was only resolved a week later, which caused me to lose valuable time in starting my account closure process. Since then, I've been contacting Expatrio, explaining how urgent my situation is and how I desperately need my money refunded. Yet, my messages are often read and ignored, and no one can give me a real and clear timeline for when EXACTLY I will receive my money.\nThe refund process is a simple bank transfer that takes, at most, 24 hours. Why is it so difficult to return my money when I am clearly stating that I urgently need this amount? Even if a document review is required before the transfer, it is certainly done by a human being. So, what is the difficulty in asking this person to prioritize my case? What is the difficulty in showing empathy and compassion for the customer and helping them in a delicate moment? I am literally having daily anxiety and crying attacks because of this.\nCuriously, Expatrio took only two days to review my documents and block my money when I opened the account. So unfortunately, at this point, it seems to me that Expatrio is just another bank purely concerned with profit, like all the others.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "They did an app this year, and you are forced to use their application for everything, to open a blocked account, upload documents. But their application is not working at all, I couldn't do anything for a month after arrival in Germany, the made my life harder and don't even answer support messages anymore. It was a good company before, but really went bad, be careful with them.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have made an activation process 4 days ago and on the app has been mentioned that it will take one business day. However, 4 day have passed and I see only one sentence \"Activation is under review\" . I have already sent several emails, but only AI sent me automatic reply. I wanted to contact a human colleague, however failed. I called the telefon nummer of the bank, I heard only auto reply. I am upset for using Expatrio \n\nP.S. Now I have a new problem. I want to close my blocked account. As an instruction, I am on my Blocked account and as said there must be \"Close\" button. But there is no \"Close\" button. There is only \"Extent\" button. What should I do?", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "They give trustworthy services but they take too long to reply their mails", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Opened a blocked account and it went very smoothly. However, it took over a month for me to close the account when my visa was changed, even after providing all the requested documentation and confirming details they requested. Every time I contacted support, my messages would go unanswered for over a week. This left me in an incredibly tough financial position as it is obviously a lot of money they would not release. Even after it was finally released (over a month later), no acknowledgement was made about the incredibly poor service.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I had submitted my Fiktionsbescheinigung for review, which I was given at the last moment due to an emergency. It had been four days since I've submitted it and three days since I've sent an email and I'm still being show a notification saying that my bank account will be closed in one day if I don't submit the document. I really don't know what to do. Every single time I've reached out to expatrio with an emergency via their customer support email, they get back to me with two emails, both automated, one from a bot poppy and the other from their team both saying the same thing, \"we will get back to you in one business day, please don't send more emails with the same reminders.\" And the number of times they have gotten back to me in one business day is none. But for some reason every time I write a bad review about just ONE of the many experiences then they are quick to respond. Maybe if the speed at which you guys respond to your emails were the same as how you respond to your bad reviews, you wouldn't get any. Honestly it's really stressful to be worried about my bank account, money, insurance, all of which are under you surveillance and if you can't get back to people in a short time then maybe don't say that you will get back in a short time.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Terrible service! How can a large bank not have a call center for customers to call? \n\nI don't care if the company is busy or full of demands, that doesn't interest me, but how can it take more than 2 days for an account to be unblocked when they themselves say that the account will be unblocked in one day? \n\nIt's absurd that a company of this size doesn't have a competent team that serves the customer.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It’s too slow to review my blocked account activation, which seriously affected my rent payment!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am disappointed with my experience with Expatrio so far. I completed my identity verification at the post office, uploaded all necessary documents, and have been waiting for my account activation. It's been two days since then, but my activation is still under review. Despite reaching out for support, I received generic AI response that didn’t provide any real solutions.\n\nAs a student relying on timely access to my blocked funds, this delay has been rather inconvenient.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have previous complained about Expatrio on TrustPilot. Absolutely nothing has been done Two months into my stay in Germany I cannot use or transfer any money from my blocked account. Nobody has made any effort to help. I cannot contact Expatrio support. They do not respond to emails and are practically unreachable via telephone. The way I have been treated by Expatrio is a complete disgrace. I have had to take on a significant overdraft just to pay my rent for this month, for which I am sure I will receive no compensation. If Expatrio takes half as long as they have done to solve my issue again, I will have to leave Germany. It is beyond me how this company has accrued so many positive reviews. Please do yourself a favour and avoid using this service at all costs.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I like the company.\nEverything is just awsome.\n\nwhat i dont like is their customer support through emails, it is ridiculous i have been asking one doubt many times but not proper reply or not on point", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Totally unacceptable level of customer support, was told by the app to contact customer support in order to finish activation process however have received no response for over 7 business days.. writing this review is a last resort as desperately need access to my money.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The customer service is really really bad. I have sent emails to update my bank account. There’s no response at all. I have tried all the way to get in touch with you, WeChat, Email or other social media. Nobody has answered me. And there’s no telephone number either. What are you doing????", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The User Interface is a bit clunky.  The user has to figure out which menu to go to.  A lot of changes need to be made in the User Interface so that people can see it easily.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "My account is stuck in a can’t activate but also can’t add more money state. I have been trying to get ahold of someone for a month and have received nothing but not emails. Genuinely an awful service save yourself the stress.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Well, if I had an option to choose less than one star – I'd definitely do that. \n\nFirst, once I opened my account it didn't pass the activation for 2 days, and was activated only after I called to support, during the call within 30 seconds. Why was I waiting for 2 days? IDK.. \n\nThen I made a SWIFT transfer from my Georgian bank account. It was made on 10/14/2024. \n\nNext week, on 10/21 I wrote an email with an ask to share a status, there was no response for 5 days, and I finally called to support and it turned out that your partner bank needs an additional information to be provided (about a type of relationships between the money sender and blocked account holder). I provided this information immediately and you again disappeared for several days. \n\nI pinged on Tuesday by email – no response. I called to support on Wednesday, the support specialist said that it turns out that the bank needed some other information to be provided and seemed she did it during the call, she responded to the bank only because I made a call, so I had to manually push the process on your side which is mind boggling... In the evening after the call the money appeared on the account. It took 13 business (17 calendar) days. \n\nIt's okay, I understand that sometimes international transfers take long time, but what makes me angry is the fact that apparently in my case it was just because you didn't do your job timely. \n\nI am a Product Manager and have been developing software products for 10 years and I know very well how complicated it may be, but really.. I'd be ashamed if my product provided such a poor user experience.\n\nHope you will consider this feedback and will try to make the experience better.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am not at all satisfied with your service and the customer support you provide. It has been many working days since I requested to sent my health insurance information to my university electronically. However I haven’t got any updates on the my request.\nThis is not the kind of customer support I was expecting and I believe this is unacceptable.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "We have been trying for more than a month to get Expatrio to release funds to allow for the rent of a flat in Munich to be paid.  We have provided all the account information Expatrio has asked for.  I have been rerouted off of calls with very lengthy on hold times many times, having tried to speak to someone and been directed instead to a voicemail that no one ever replies to.  The one time I have managed to speak to someone from Expatrio the employee confirmed that we had given them the information they needed but that there was some 'technical issue' that was preventing payment. \n The employee promised that this would be dealt with quickly and we would receive our own money promptly.  That was more than a week ago and we are, once again, facing an impenetrable wall of silence from Expatrio 'customer care'.  Woeful performance.  Outrageous that we are forced to use a system that locks our own money into the account of a firm exhibiting this level of contempt for its customers.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Like some others here, I activated my account weeks ago and have not received any payment from Expatrio. I contacted their support who provided irrelevant information and then completely neglected to follow back up with me when I reiterated my issue. I am unable to access any of my money risking my ability to survive, and Expatrio has left me without support, communication, or recourse. I'm literally only leaving a review here since it seems to prompt responses.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It's extremely challenging to get assistance from Expatrio. They lack a customer support hotline and don’t offer a chat option, leaving email as the only way to reach them – which is slow, with long response times. I'm currently facing an issue with an international bank transfer held by Expatrio's partner bank, Aion, and I urgently need help to meet an upcoming deadline. The lack of timely support has been frustrating and stressful. I hope Expatrio addresses these issues to improve the experience for their users.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Hello,\n\nI am currently following the account closure process but a \"bug\" on the Recipient address country field prevents me from submitting the form. Each of my emails take on average 10 days to be responded. Is this an intentional delay of the account closure process? Please fix this and allow me to close the account and get refunded. Thank", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Despite jumping through all the required hoops and completing account verification several business days ago, they aren't disbursing my funds. Their customer service is non-existent. Avoid this company", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Transfering blocked account was very easy and convinient. But customer support for queries through emails or calls  need improvement", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Very slow resolution of queries", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It has been 12 days since I’ve activated my blocked account and they still didn’t send the first monthly payment. Can’t reach them via e-mails or voice messages. Very bad experience, i don’t know if they will gonna ever reach to me.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Good but customer service can be better.\nI have sent emails about changing my insurance company but no response.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Their services are good, but getting in touch with them is extremely challenging! Before I opened a blocked account, response times were typically 1-2 days. However, since opening the account, response times have stretched to over 5 days.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Response time is quite slow and the BOT generated responses are not that accurate to the issue mentioned.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Not responsive at all on email", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I didn't got any response from the customer representative or anyone else for my query.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The service itself functions as advertised. It allows the user to open a bank account and get insured. I would rate the product very highly if I was actually able to access it.\n\nThe issues begin when you need support from the company. I have been unable to transfer money from my blocked account due to an error code and have asked for help multiple times. A member of the support team would eventually respond after nearly a week and share links to information that is readily available on their website. They have so far not provided any actual support, leaving me unsure as as to whether or not I will be able to make my rent payment next week. Expatrio's customer service needs thorough work.\n\nEdit - as of 28/10/2024, I have still had no support from the customer service team besides a quickly sent email following the posting of this review. Given how much of my money the company is responsible for, I find this quite unbelievable.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "the app is not working properly, i deposited all money and the money reflected in my expatrio account but its been 2 weeks and the document 06 is no where to be found. i sent multiple emails for support  but only generic response and i tried calling the hotline but was waiting for 30mins no one is picking the call even i tried multiple times. really disappointed. \nBecause of this i had to reschedule my interview with the emabassy  and it cost me alot of waiting time again. my user id is 936709\n\n*****************\nUpdate (after 16 hours after i posted this Comment), because of Trustpilot comments, in just hours there has been an action on my case. I am very grateful for the moderator of trustpilot expatrio, without this i will still be stressed and begging for an action from expatrio Support team.\n\nThank you Trustpilot", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Can't solve my problem. I requested the PostIdent code for the activation of the account, and my status is frozen as if I had submited the documents. I repeat, I didn't send the documents yet! Just requested the code! Now my status is stuck like this and I can't proceed to activate my account. It has been 1 week already and the support keeps on providing the same answer for me to activate it again but it is not possible because of the problems of the platform. I am very frustrated with the experience, because I finally have the documents to activate the account but can't do it due to the problems with Expatrio. The next month is coming and I still can't activate my account and no support is capable of helping... I make this review as the last hope Expatrio will finally help me for real to activate my account. It is unethical to put your customers through these experiences! \nThe message says \"We are processing yout activation data, it must take a few minutes\"... Since the 18th of october. I still didn't upload any documetns and just requested for the post ident code to do the activation and now it is frozen with this message!! please help me solve my problem.... I delete this review\n\nEduardo Volskis de Carvalho", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Hey my name is Muhammad hassan.I have transferred my funds and it has been a week.Im from Pakistan and its taking too long. If they could have responded to me i would have change the bank and use services of other platforms. Very disappointing and will not recommend anyone to use their service.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "so slow to reply my email!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Account opening and funds transfer were super easy. Required to submit minimum documents with ID and Address proof which was hassle free.\n\nFound difficult to obtain details account for fund transfer . Need to enter fund transfer amounts and country then downloads the bank details -account number and IBAN which took some time.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have requested several time that I want my disbursement in different account still no one responded and send money on different account \nI don't wanted to create expracrio bank account still due to UI I created it mistakenly and unable to close it nor update it.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The support team is exceptionally inadequate. I wish I had known how challenging it would be to work with Expatrio from the beginning—I would have opened my account with another bank. I've never encountered these kinds of issues with any other platform. Every time I need assistance from the support team, it feels like seeking help in a dark room.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have done my offline identification and it is successful, but it's not reflecting in my Expatrio app. It's been 1 week, I tried contacting costumer care for 4 to 5 time but no response from them. My Expatrio number is 826645. Respond and clear it soon.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "ID: 901393\n\nMy activation documents have already been verified for over a week now and I still have not received my first disbursement", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "You took more than 5 days to answer a question about an important issue.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Overall My experience with expatrio was great. On 14.10.2024 I activated my private health insurance two days later on 17.10.2024 I received a message from expatrio stating that all your documents had been uploaded and I reuploaded my immatrikulationbescheingung on 17.10.2024 it's been two days till now still I am not been able to get any update regarding my private health insurance activation.I contacted them once,twice still no response PLEASE HELP ME OUT ITS URGENT HERE'S MY EXPATRIO NO.-808323 and my private health insurance number is - EX-PVST-0001420", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Not all schools can be found in their options and not all courses  tooo", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Some days ago i wrote a review here. They so called activated the insurance but didn't give me insurance number. I have called , email until i am tired. I have asked for m10 to be sent to my University but nothing. I sincerely cannot advise and will warn any of my friend from using your services if they are to come to Germany.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I don't even want to give 1star to it. But my money is with them so I have to give atleast one star. \n\nExpatrio's Application - not working properly\n\nExpatrio answers to email? - Never \n\nExpatrio receives call? - once in a month (if you are lucky enough)\n\nI don't know why they are charging services fees of 5 euros. It's my duty to ask them that please tell me what should I do after blocking the amount. How will I get my first month money.\n\nThis is my 3rd experience with blocking the money with Expatrio. First two experiences were not so bad. But this time.....I'm done... I need money but they don't receive calls, don't answer emails... don't answer after felling the contact form... Don't know how to get my money back.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have a data change and I've emailed expatrio .\nI have been waiting for a week now, still no response and I need to access blocked money soon.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am super stressful right now as i have to go for my visa appointment soon but i have yet to hear back from them as i contacted them for customer service. Called them multiple times as i am really urgent right now to set up my incoming insurance. I am really praying hard that expatrio can get back to me asap as this is giving me anxiety ( i am afraid i am unable to get my visa on time) I have contacted them a few days ago, called them etc but still silent .. it is worrying 😭😭😭", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I can not see , my transfer document", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Lograr contactar a los agentes de ayuda es una odisea por casi que imposible. Los email son respondidos por un Bot. En un mes recibí dos depósitos de mi cuenta bloqueada lo que hizo que los documentos que prueban mis ingresos se redujera a un mes y ahora tengo que pagar ese mes con todos los costos de servicios de la página.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "AVOID! HORRIBLE EXPERIENCE\nThe website says you can get temporary access to your blocked account without a visa, but the app doesn't allow this. Now many students, like myself, have to wait months until they can access their money. Expatrio's customer support is the worst I have ever encountered. Over the last week I have called over 20 times, have emailed, and have shown up to their offices in Berlin but have not gotten a reply. This experiencing is ruining my year abroad and I can't access any of my money so don't even know if I can stay here.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have never in my life seen a service without customer support. If you use them and arrive in germany, prepare yourself to be stranded for months. I have email them and called till i'm tired. I and some other users recenlty visited their physical location, there is no body there. You are just stranded. I sent my rental agreement for my health insurance to be activated more than 2 weeks ago, no reply. They don't even bother replying to users. I will strongly advise to use other services . Expatrio services are too poor.\n\nPS: My insurance has been activated. Its surprising to see i needed to write a review here before getting a reply. Dear Expatrio Please send my M10 certificate to my University.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "For true expatrio experiences go check the comments on their publications on their Insta account, wish I had done the same.\nI applied for my german visa with the Expatrio blocked account and the process there went smooth, hence the 2 star review. Can't say the same of other people's experiences. \nArriving in Germany was a completely different story. It's been a full week in business days since I went through with, allegedly, quick way of activating my blocked account and there has been no word on any front I've contacted (e-mail, query on the site, phone) ever since. I can't access MY money.\nThankfully I was able to get enough money from savings to pay for rent and Kaution for my apartment. So at least I'm not in such a bad position. Consider using other providers. Don't hope for things to go smooth for you.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "There was an issue and it got solved the next day when I wrote a review on Trustpilot. But before writing a review on Trustpilot, no human agent responded to my emails and phone calls. So I initially gave them 1 star but because the issue got solved the next morning after writing a review, I am leaving 3 star now :)", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "In the first step when I try to sign up for my new user account, an email was sent to confirm my email. But when I click \"Confirm my email\" link/button in the email I faced an error and I couldn't proceed with that anyway. I could be able to sign up only with using my google account.\nThis is the main reason for low scoring of my experience.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Dear customers, I am giving my email address (vaneetshahi88@ gmail.com). Let's see, how Expatrio can return my setup fees 69 euro for making my account with Mangopay without my consent. When I get my setup fees back and interest rate of 7% interest rate on my block amount for holding it for nearly 2 months, I will give positive review of their service...... Review: Expatrio service is too slow. Without my consent, Expatrio has opened my account with their other partner Mangopay (proof:  email communication with Expatrio) and charged 69 euro as setup fees so setup fees is not free as company claims. I think they do this scam also with other customers for their dishonest profit. Plus, they have hold my money for 2 months but did not activate account. It is clear here that the main purpose of not activating my account was to use my money for their profits. Who will pay interest rate @7% for 2 months for holding such a big amount? It is unethical. My honest advice to everyone is that please stay away from expatrio and get service from other customers such as CORACLE or FINTIBA. If expatrio really care about me as customer, they should return my set up fees 69 euro as compensation because I have suffered a lot with their bad service.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I wrote an email to request for travel health insurance certifiate. But the support team didn't even bother to reply even after 8 days. They could have simply said no if they were not able to reply.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have had issues with the activation of my blocked account from this company for over half a month now, despite trying to contact them through all means - I have been writing multiple emails, called them more times than i can count (without answer), and in the off chance that they do answer the emails, they never get back at me if I write them back because the problem is persisting. The only way i got through to them last time was by writing a negative review as I am doing now, to which they answered in a heartbeat. Their new app (which they force costumers to use as the new account activation system) being glitchy, I'm appalled at how slow they are to respond to issues, especially considering how this is after all a banking app specifically for international students, which is a population that already often struggles financially and has less access to help since they're on foreign territory. Me not having access to my blocked account due to activation issues since the end of last month (by now almost three weeks), has put me late on rent and put my family into financial distress. I hope that my issue gets solved quickly, and that no one else has to go through these problems again. I've already written this last time, but I do not recommend this service.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am from a third world country but have a residency permit for an European country meaning I can move to Germany without needing Visa. In trying to activate my account, I am still required to present a Visa which I obviously do not have to have access to my money. This has left me stranded as I haven't got my residency permit yet to continue the activation process.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The process of creating my blocked account was easy and quick. However, the process of un blocking it and opening my bank account has been awful. I am trying to finish the process of activating my account so that I can receive my first monthly payment. I am being asked to connect my phone, but when I click on the button, a message appears saying I've been blocked out of my account and to come back 12 hours after the initial block time. It's been more than a week, and I still can't access my account, and therefore can't receive my payment.\nI've been trying to contact expatrio by phone everyday for a week but nobody answers the call.\nI sent an email 6 dass ago, and still I have no answer.\nIt has been 16 days since I started the process of activating my account and still can't do it because of some problem or other.\nI am very worried by this lack of response. All I know is expatrio has my money and I don't.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "while it is not a scam, this will single handedly ruin your experience and make your first months in Germany miserable. they don't respond to emails or calls, THERE IS NO CUSTOMER SUPPORT.... despite it being one of the most expensive out of the competitors. Absolutely horrendous", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Try to contact them during almost one week: calls, emails, chat on the site, contact form on the site - nothing works. I need the account for a declaration of commitment and chose this option when opening it. This type of account doesn't need to make monthly payments until authority allows and there's no option to change it manually in app or on site. I sent then a document from the authority but no answer, just silence. I need to get the declaration of commitment asap but I cannot change parameters of the account, ID 943575\nLater they answered me via email, instead of to change parameters of the account they suggested to close the account, pay them almost 100eur and get money back in 1 month. Looks like scam. You open an account and then they suggest you to let you earn money on your by closing it without usage the account. They opened account in a such way that cannot be used for a declaration of commitment, it's just useless.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The problem are not been resolved\nAnd they are not replying to my mail", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Terrible customer service, I've been waiting for more than a week and I haven't checked the response. My money is blocked and they won't activate my account even though I do everything they tell me.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "\"Everything was great—the money transfer was fast, and the processing speed was efficient. However, there was one thing that made me extremely upset. The first person who did the video verification with me was very rude. When I didn’t fully understand what he was saying at the beginning, he immediately questioned my English proficiency in a very impatient manner, which I found completely unacceptable. This curly-haired man and I ended up having an argument. Fortunately, after that, a different representative, a woman, took over, and she was very patient and kind. I hope you can better manage your employees; otherwise, I won’t recommend your services to anyone around me.\"", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The support is non existent \n\nI tried raising issues multiple times and still haven't received any response from you guys. I would not recommend this service to anyone.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am a Brazilian Expatrio user with a blocked account and a bank account in Expatrio. I arrived in Germany two weeks ago and ever since I have been trying to activate my account with little success. \n\nI already have the Meldebestätigung  for the city im at and have already applied for the Student Visa, but as a brazilian citizen, I'm allowed entrance to Germany without Visa up to 3 months, as is the situation with citizens from Australia, Canada, Israel, Japan, the Republic of Korea (South Korea), New Zealand, and USA.\n\nTherefore, I should have already been able to activate my blocked account. However, everytime I started the identification process my passport wouldn't be recognized by your identification system. The agents responsible for the identification informed me that my passport was a more recent model of the Brazilian passport (i got it in 2023), and that model wasn't in their database. Due to such a astonishingly trivial problem I haven't been able to proceed with the identification, and I still could not activate my account.\n\nImportant to mention that all my savings for my stay here in Germany (circa 6.000 euros!) are in the blocked account. I'm currently relying on money I brought in case of an emergency, which won't last for more than 1 week. I have also sent e-mails to your customer support, but none of them were responded to, even though the automatic message I received said they would be replied in 1 business day. I also called your customer support number several times the last few days, waited for more than 20 minutes each call and received no answer. \n\nThis whole situation is absolutely unacceptable. I signed up for Expatrio with the sole expectation that the company would provide me with a blocked account I could use after arriving in Germany.  Not only has this simple expectation been frustrated, but I also could not even get any feedback from any of the contacts I tried with you. I don't even know how to proceed from here and whether I will be able to access my money, which makes me deeply unsatisfied with your service.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I send an inquiry since 7 Oktober. I would Like to Open Block Account. Iam currently in Germany and first question what are you doing in Germany? What should be the answer from selected choice since I'm in process of regonized my medical certificate no reply until today. Which make me wonder is it good choice ?\nMy email polatgernasgmail.com", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Slight improvement\nI finally got a direct human response from someone and he was very helpful and gave prompt email responses to each of my replies. This is the kind of service that should be available from the beginning without having to blow up social media. All of these issues could have been solved within minutes if it were possible to get this kind of response by email or phone immediately. Instead it took almost 5 days of anxiety being in a foreign country with no access to my funds. I implore Expatrio to examine the manner in which they respond to customer concerns, as further investigation indicates that my experience is not unique. Kudos to the gentleman who assisted me. If this kind of service was available to all from the very first enquiry, it would save you a lot of work and your customers a lot of stress.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am having the worst experience with Expatrio. It's been more than a week that I am trying to get in contact with the support team via phone, online formular, email, and my case have been neglected, I don't have an answer. My account activation process went wrong in the app, I couldn't finish my ID Verification. This means that my month payments are not happening, my money is locked in the app and I don't even see to each bank my expatrio account is connected. I tried to finish the ID verification but it's not possible neither in the app or in the website. The support does not exist, I can't access properly my account or my money. The amount of money that I have trusted and deposited in this platform is huge and considerable and now nothing works, causing insecurities and a total lack of trust from me towards expatrio. \nUpdate: Expatrio got in contact with me and they fixed the problem quickly after this review. I am satisfied that my problem got a solution, but it’s really annoying that I only had their attention to my case by publishing it here, since I never got a reply before using the official communication channels from the company.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Hello,\nI`m trying to activate my blocked account for some time already, but unfortunately it didn`t work out:\n- 08/10/2024 I upload proof of address to the App and got POSTIDENT coupon on 09/10/2024.\n- I verified my id in post-office in Berlin on 09/10/2024. I haven`t received any emails (including confirmation that data was send to Expatrio) and in couple hours status in App changed to square one - waiting for me to arrive to Germany.\n- I tried one more time with POSTIDENT coupon on 10/10/2024, but the result was the same.\nAll these days I was trying to reach out support team via email and phone number. All attempts were useless, during 2 business days nobody texted me back or answer any of my calls – their line is always busy.\n\nI`m already in Germany and I can`t get access to my account and money which is literally blocked. This situation is really stressful for me and so far experience was really disappointing. \n\nCould you please address this issue as soon as possible? \n \nMy user ID: 933775", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Expatrio closed my bank account 15 days ago and still haven’t transferred my money to new nominated account. I was advised it could take up to 5 business days to complete and yet 15 days later I am still without my money and without any contact from the support team. I have tried in vain to contact the support team only to be responded to by AI bots. No luck with ringing them either. \nPoor service and poor communication. Very disappointed as I was hoping to continue using Expatrio’s services going forward but after this experience, I will be looking elsewhere.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have been trying to contact your customer service for the past three weeks due to my inability to access my account and the issue of not being able to link my bank account through the app. Despite my daily attempts to reach your customer service via phone, I have unfortunately been unsuccessful in doing so.\n\nAlthough I finally received a response via email after several attempts, I was asked a few questions to help resolve the issue. I promptly responded six days ago, yet I have not received any follow-up since then.\n\nAt this point, I am unsure of what other options are available to get in touch with Expatrio and receive the assistance I urgently need. I sincerely hope that this message can help expedite the resolution of my problem.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I was able to gain access to link my bank account to the blocked account, but now the system is again insisting on verification when I try to make a payment, and it again insists that my details are incorrect. I have tried logging out and repairing my device TWICE, which fixed the problem the first time, but it now does not work. THIS IS INEXCUSABLE. The fact that there is no live assistance for a matter such as this is very distressing. Is this what I am to expect every time I try to make a payment? DO BETTER!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The employee who helped me activate my account online spoke very inaccurately and was completely unfriendly. Account activation failed and I plan to go directly to the post office. In the past, when I activated my bank account online, there were similar problems such as poor communication, but they kindly told me to try again, but this employee just hung up.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I (user id: 159573) have received 0 euro (yes, I repeat, 0 euro) buffer out of 100 euros, and your explanation was very much surprising!\n\nYou're deducting money from the day I transferred the amount, which doesn't make any sense. I started receiving payouts in October 2023, but you charged me fees from the day when I transferred the amount to Expatrio, without any prior notice, and then suddenly deducted everything from the buffer. This seems very much unethical, unfair and feels like a misleading tactic to take money from the students. And please don't forget that I won't suggest you to the upcoming students as much as possible only because of your behavior including hidden charges and unfair means of taking money from the students. Actually you deserve 0 rating (yes, I repeat, 0 rating).\n\nChoosing Expatrio over others like Coracle, Fintiba was the biggest mistake of my life. I would never recommend Exptrio to anyone, never! \n\n\n\nEdit: Today is 07.11.2024, no response from them till now, after their reply on 10.10.2024 and you can read their reply here!\n\nPathetic, too pathetic service received! Shame on you!\n\nHonest advice: Save your hard earned money and avoid Expatrio strictly. \n\nThank you.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "My travel insurance document is not issued", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I'm trying to active my expatrio blocked account in germany with a brazilian passport and it doesn't work. When the confirmation call contact me they say that my passport is new and the don't have it in the system.\n\nThe same is happening with my girlfriend that is with me.\n\nWe have no more money and we have no idea about what we will do for living here. I will sleep in a square maybe, just because expatrio don't want to send me back MY OWN MONEY.\n\nI would never recommend this bank for anyone. It doesn't work. They receive our money but doesn't sync with the nowadays passport.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Worst app ever, I cant access to my money and the customer service team doesnt answer. \nThe problem for the baking part persist and then a letter appears and tells me \"Please come back in 12 hours, if the problem persist contact our Customer Support Team\" \n\nI have called the number for more than 30 times and nobody answers the phone.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I'm having trouble making calls. No one is answering me. It's been 4 days and I've spent hours trying to contact you. I need to activate my account. The app didn't work for video calls and I don't receive the QR code either. I need help and I need my money. This is not fair. It's my money. I'm paying for the service. And you don't want to give me what is rightfully mine. I've already explained a thousand times. I've tried calling several times. You don't answer anything I ask. You don't help at all. Only robot answers. And that's it. And I'm the one who gets screwed. I'm begging to get my money back and for the service I paid for and I'm not getting.I've been trying to activate my account for a week and it's not my fault, but the app's fault. I couldn't activate it online via call. The app kept turning off and it wasn't just me. Friends also had the same problem. And now I need my money and you guys are holding it like I'm a stranger who has to prove it's me. Where do I live? And they won't activate my account. They've been sending emails and calling without getting a response. And we paid for the service.\nIt's not just one or two people who said they just called and activated their account with just their passport. But many people did it that way. In fact, even people who went in person didn't need these documents that practically everyone doesn't have when they arrive here. And even so, they had their accounts activated. I'm not making this up. I have friends who did it that way. They received the QR code without having proof of address, went to the specified place and there they just showed their passport and had their accounts activated.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Customer service is hard to get in contact with and when you get a response it's the same response found on line. I called 5 times and was on hold for 20 minutes and never got to speak to a person. You advertise yourself as the best for incoming student but can not provide help when someone actually needs it.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "My blocked account hasn't been activated in 8 whole days. All the documents have been submitted and the status is always shown to be under verification. I've written countless emails reaching out to the customer support team and although they say they'll get back in 1 business day, they never do. I haven't gotten a single follow up. I am in urgent need of the money for my visa extension and there's nothing I can do.\n\nUPDATE:\nAfter 8 days of not receiving any emails that are not automated or from an inefficient bot, my blocked account activation was finally followed up with just 4 hrs after this review was posted. Seems like the only way to get a reply from expatrio's support team is by writing reviews. I had to pay a lot of money that was overdue and after the first payment, that is, after money had gone out of my bank account, i get an email from expatrio asking for detaiks aboit my recipient, no explanations given. And yet, I gave the details that were asked of and I didn't receive any follow back till now. I was recently contacted by the recipient that the money that had gone out of my account was not received by him. If expatrio says that they don't handle the bank account, AION does, and so not responsible for such a mistake, then that would be a huge fail from their part. If you cannot have trusted and efficient partners to deal with money affairs, what promises can you make when it comes to less important things? I have lost 49 euros, which might not be a huge sum, but it is to me, when I'm living in a whole new country away from my family for the first time ever. None of the emails sent to expatrio are EVER replied to.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Changing the policy and taking money from blocked accounts that are not activated yet without notifying the customers.\nHow can we trust a bank that do such thing?", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I was sent a false blocked account activation confirmation email even though my documents weren't verified then. They also delayed my first ever payout. I wrote multiple emails to them but didn't get any reply from them. Please don't go with their services. There are tons of better options out there who'll make this process easier for you instead of adding on to your initial struggles.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "too much waiting time for contacting customer care.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am unable to speak to anyone in customer service over phone. You need to improve that aspect", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have opened a blocked account with Expatrio this month for the third time. While my previous experiences were smooth and I received good support, this time has been absolutely horrible. After transferring funds and receiving confirmation, my account was in \"Awaiting activation\" status. I attempted to change the number of months before activating and didn’t even save the changes. suddenly my account status switched to \"insufficient funds,\" even though it clearly has all the required funds.\n\nThis situation appears to be a technical glitch, and I'm unsure how to get it resolved since customer service is non existent . All my requests were met with irrelevant responses from a chatbot, and none of my calls were answered. I was put on hold for over 15 minutes, and to this moment, I haven’t received any resolution.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have tried to contact Expatrio's customer support through Zendesk and call service. However, I have not gotten any response yet regarding my issue...\nI have used Expatrio extensively for 4 years now, but this year is a huge disappointment.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Worst Service...20 minutes waiting to reach agents and extra charges without any reason and also waiting to get my money from 5 days after activating because of their faulty app where you get an error without any reason while activating an account and It's funny because we have to try and update you about current situation while you are charging month service fees and also I have to wait for 1 hour to reach your agent to explain that I need MY MONEY as soon as possible. will not recommend anyone in the future. go for Fintiba or Coracle if you love your money and time.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have been stuck on the activation in review step for a long time now. I already did my Postident verification and all the necessary steps. I have tried calling the customer service for days but I only get to the mailbox at the end. I urgently need access to my monthly payout because I need to pay my rent! I need a response soon!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "When I opened the blocked account, they promised me that the activation would be quick. I have been in Germany for a week and they still haven't unlocked my account. For a week now, my verification has been under review and they haven't given me any solution from their customer service. I really need the money to survive here, pay rent, insurance and food. IT'S URGENT!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I recently made a new blocked account with this company, but have been having trouble activating it with their new app. I rely on the money on that account to pay rent and eat (as any student would), so I needed a very timely response to my problems. Sadly I haven't been able to reach customer support through call despite trying numerous times since the end of last month and leaving voice mails - and the only other way of contacting them is through a form - which they promise to only take 1 business day to answer, but has also been taking weeks.\n\nI don't think I'll make a blocked account with this company again in the future, as their issues put me in a very tight spot. I also won't recommend it further.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "My blocked account is still under review even though II completed the identity verification process with videocall and uploaded all the necessary documents for the activation.  Therefore I cannot get my money. This morning Expatrio support replied my e-mail and he says that my account is active now and all I need to do is add my current account. But when I checked the status of my blocked account in the app, it is still in review(my proof o address under review). I also checked on my laptop and it says \"Your identity verification process has been finalized. You will soon receive your first month disbursement.\" But there is no IBAN section and the status of proof of adress is the same.(still pending and under review) It is impossible add my iban. It is obvious that Expatrio has some technical issues currently. Please can you fix this problem? Support replies e-mails so late. My user id: 197561", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "In the article \"How can I activate my account?\" it's written: \"If you already have other German bank cards to activate your Blocked Account and do not want to open an Expatrio Bank account, do not click \"I confirm\" and click \"Start Account Activation\" directly. In the next step, enter the IBAN and BIC of your own German bank account to complete identity verification and complete the Blocked Account activation process.\" \nIt is stressed twice that customer's bank account should be German. \n\nIn the article \"How do I get an IBAN to activate my Blocked Account?\" it is written: \"You can find useful information and account set up tips for the banking providers we recommend here (including how to open a German bank account product* via Expatrio!), but you do not have to choose from this list. If you already have a SEPA account (for example a German bank account) set up in your name, you can use it for Blocked Account activation.\" \nOnce again it's twice stressed that it can/should be German bank account.\n\nBut SEPA account means that the bank account for payouts can be opened in any bank/country of the SEPA. \n\nDear Expatrio Support Team let's clear it out. Can one use activated Latvian Revolut IBAN for monthly payouts from one's own blocked account?", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Terrible customer service. When people are in a foreign country and need to access their funds and can't because YOUR system does not function properly, you need to have something in place besides a chatbot to help. It is impossible to get anyone on the phone. I am locked out of my account due to your system's errors and unable to access my funds that I urgently need.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am writing to express my frustration and disappointment regarding the issues I have encountered while trying to extend my blocked account for an additional two months. According to your website and application instructions, this process should be done using the \"Apply/Extend\" button. However, no such button is available on my account, making it impossible for me to resolve this issue independently.\n\nDespite reaching out to Customer Service multiple times, I have repeatedly received automated messages with the same instructions, which do not address my specific problem. I have been unable to connect with a real customer service representative to assist me in resolving this technical issue. Even after calling your contact number and waiting on the line for around 10 minutes, I was redirected to voicemail, again without speaking to an actual employee.\n\nWhile attempting to resolve the problem, I also modified the \"planned stay\" section, thinking this might be the issue. However, this did not help with extending my account, so I reverted the dates to their original state. Now, I am receiving an \"insufficient funds\" warning, which I believe is another technical issue, as the amount in my blocked account is more than the required amount. Unfortunately, I continue to receive automated responses about potential delays in funds arriving, which is not relevant to my situation.\n\nMy visa appointment is in 17 days, and if this issue is not resolved promptly, I risk facing serious complications during my appointment, possibly resulting in visa denial. I find it highly unprofessional that, for such an important service, I have been unable to speak with a real customer service representative who can assist me.\n\nI urgently request that you resolve this issue immediately. Should I not receive a response within the next 7 days, I will be forced to take legal action with my lawyer to resolve the matter.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I’m having trouble connecting my phone to the app to enter my IBAN. When I click 'Connect Phone,' I’m asked to provide my passport number, the city where I was born, my postal code, and phone number. However, after submitting the answers, it tells me that the information is incorrect. I’m certain I entered everything exactly as it appears on my passport.\n\nOn 02/10/2024, I sent you an email explaining my issue (User ID: 779391), but I received no response. I followed up with another email on 04/10/2024, yet I still haven't heard back or received any support. Today is 07/10/2024, and no one has contacted me.\n\nThis situation is very stressful. I just want to receive my money because I have many responsibilities, such as my rent and studies. Unfortunately, your service has not been helpful so far.\n\nPlease address this issue as soon as possible.\n\nMy user ID: 779391", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Not upto the mark and delayed service. Also I want a customer agent to contact me during my question arises. So I think you people should provide that kind of service. Coz people are worried due to the delay and most of the times they are out of time. So please do understand and implement in the future.\nThanks.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "UPDATE ON 24th October 2024\n\nExpatrio free bank account never materialised in my case, despite so many emails and one unhelpful conversation with their helpline executive. I had to open an account in a German bank myself and only then did my Expatrio account get activated finally on 21st. I am now waiting for the monthly payment to reflect in my bank account. Needless to say that the whole point of going with Expatrio was defeated because of this month long horrible experience.\n\n\nUPDATE ON 19th October 2024\n\nMY BAD EXPERIENCE WITH EXPATRIO CONTINUES...No solution or help forthcoming.\n\nIt is now over 3 weeks that I have been seeking help from Expatrio to deliver on their promise. But every time they send a standard email with FAQ. I cannot get through to them and make them understand that the Activation page on the Expatrio APP is not allowing me to proceed with the activation because the APP is not recognizing that I am supposed to have a free German Bank account from Expatrio. \n\nTHIS MEANS THAT EVEN AFTER 21 DAYS OF ARRIVAL IN GERMANY I DO NOT HAVE ACCESS TO MY MONEY AND TO HEALTH INSURANCE.\n---------------------------------------------------\n\n[Original REVIEW - 6th October 2024]\n\nIt has been 5 days and I have not been able to activate my Expatrio blocked account because despite the promise of a free bank account their app keeps asking me to provide IBAN and Bic to sctivate my account. I have been writing emails asking for help but I only get automated reply which repeats FAQs. After holding for 25 minutes I spike to a human helpline person who flatly refused that I had a free bank account. This despite me having emails that say otherwise. I have been left in a lurch, my money is stuck and there is no resolution forthcoming from Expatrio. \nPlease think twice before going in for an Expatrio account.\n\nUPDATE ON 8 Oct\n\nExpatrio got in touch, on email, after the above review but despite explaining the issue once again and even sending screen shots and video no solution was provided. I am still without access to my money. And Expatrio has not responded in over 24 hours now.\nThis is my ongoing terrible experience with Expatrio.\n\nUPDATE ON 9th October 20:40\n\nStill no response, no resolution from Expatrio. No attempts to even contact me. I do not understand why they are doing this, why am I being made to suffer? Why are they not interested in solving my problem?", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I previously shared my frustrations with Expatrio regarding a delay in my fund transfer, which has now been ongoing for several weeks. Despite their response, I am still waiting for my funds and receiving replies after 4-5 days, which is incredibly stressful.\n\nDue to the missing funds in my blocked account, I missed my study start date on October 1st. I’ve emphasized multiple times that this is an urgent matter, but I still haven’t received a clear answer about where my money is.\n\nI hope this situation can be resolved quickly, as it has been extremely disappointing and has impacted my ability to begin my studies.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I would like to inform you that I'm having a very hard time pairing my mobile number with the Expatrio app as the last step to complete my Blocked account activation process.\n\nI am experiencing issues with the security questions as everytime I answer them I get incorrect responses and get locked out. I am entering them correctly as per my documents but it's still saying that my input is incorrect.\n\nIt has been a week and still I'm stuck in this particular step. This is very frustrating as my Blocked account money is stuck and I'm not able to access it.\nI started the entire Blocked account activation process more than 2 weeks back and it's still not completed, looks like you have no SLA for this.\n\nAlso, I have been consistently trying to call you all on +49(0)3025557415 but no one is picking up. Even though it says the waiting time is 4-5 mins I am held up for 30 mins without any response.\n\nI even contacted you guys via the contact sheet but the response from your customer agent is not helping. I request you to please call me and get this issue sorted asap because I can't wait for 24-48 hours for each reply via email.\n\nI have to pay my room rent and most of my processes are stuck because of this blocked account activation. Hence, please understand my problem and get my issue fixed. Resolving device pairings takes hardly a few minutes for which I'm unnecessarily stuck.\n\nTo be honest, my experience with you has not been so great. I would have better gone with Coracle as they don't even have the Postident verification and their customer support is faster and seamless. All my friends enrolled in Corale and even Fintiba got their Blocked account activated within a week.\n\nPlease call me and fix my issue by today, I will be very grateful.\n\nMy UserID is 800807.\n\nMany thanks.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Se realizaron transferencias/pagos sin mi autorización. \nMis datos personales fueron vulnerados y mi dinero fue sacado de mi cuenta sin mi autorización, de modo que no se respetó ninguna medida de seguridad y he perdido mi dinero. No he podido comunicarme con la empresa para desconocer esas transferencias, no responden el teléfono (centro de atención), ni los mails, ni el Instagram, ni tengo respuesta de ningún tipo por ningún medio. \nLo peor de todo esto es que no sé cómo pasó, no brindé mis datos bancarios a nadie, y tampoco tengo respuestas de Expatrio. Estoy intentando contactar con el centro de atención al cliente hace tres días, cuando fue el hecho, para poder reportarlo, desconocer, pedir otro número de tarjeta o algo que devuelva la seguridad a mi cuenta bancaria que fue vulnerada. Además necesito mi dinero de vuelta, soy una estudiante de intercambio que confió que con este servicio mi dinero estaría a salvo, pero mi cuenta fue vulnerada, mi dinero tomado sin mi autorización y ahora no tengo dinero siquiera para subsistir aquí en Alemania.\nEn conclusión, la plataforma no es segura, y si tienes un problema nadie te ayuda a resolverlo. Pésimo servicio", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "its been more than 24 hours and you guys have not yet responded \nthis is unacceptable i was not hoping to get this type of service", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I’m writing to share my frustration with the service I’ve been experiencing. I chose Expatrio based on the positive reviews I read, but unfortunately, my experience has been quite the opposite.\n\nIt’s been over two weeks since my sender bank confirmed that the funds are in the receiver bank, but I’m still getting no resolution from your team. The wait times for urgent inquiries are incredibly long—often 4-5 days—which is really stressful for me since I need those funds to access my blocked account and apply for my student visa.\n\nI’ve also struggled to reach anyone for help. Your team doesn’t seem to answer calls, and my sister in Germany has been trying to assist me, but it’s frustrating that there’s no WhatsApp support or live chat option available.\n\nI really hope this gets sorted out soon, as it’s been an incredibly disappointing experience so far. Thank you for your attention to this matter.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Good application but tedious to enter, every time you need to open the app, Expatrio needs to send you a code though your email to get to open the app and it gets annoying very quickly, apart from that its easy to use and reliable.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The app does not show me my card number and cvv on my digital bank card on the app. It has been 4 days since this issue and my email has not been replied yet. Expatrio app wont even let me order their physical card as there is some stupid bug. Please fix this.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I opened value package and I didn't get my travel insurance,I have contacted your customer care and no use,so I book an zoom meeting also but it is postponed continuously..", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Your customer service is pathetic. I am trying to reach someone on the phone but it stays on standby forever. Happened two days in a row. Even over the email there are no replies for weeks. I need get an issue resolved but I don't how to contact someone who can help.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Quick service but response time could be better for queries.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "After block account is activated, I cannot log in to the app. My password is wrong and when I try to change my password to a new number I get an error and I really don't understand why the automatic login system doesn't work. Please solve the problem as quickly as possible so I can spend my money", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Sıkıntı yaşadığımda maillere geri dönüş çok uzun sürdü", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Expatrio is fast in everything but their customer support sucks. I have to take out 2 stars due to their customer support. For everything else, i would give 5 stars", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I (User ID: 159573) am extremely dissatisfied with my experience with Expatrio. Their service has been deteriorating over the past few months, and I feel compelled to share my frustration. I have been waiting for my earned referral bonus (110€) for the last 3 months, but despite multiple inquiries, the response has always been the same: they are \"trying to contact their finance team and the management team for further clarification.\"\n\nIt’s disheartening to see such a lack of urgency and communication. Actually they are misleading students for their own interests. I expected a more professional approach, especially given the promises made when I first signed up. I hope they can improve their customer service and resolve these issues promptly, but for now, I cannot recommend them at all.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I'm trying to cancel my private health insurance from expatrio and to opt for a public one since my university require public one for enrolment. I have been trying to get in touch with the expatrio team via mail as well as email since the last 3 days. This is even causing my enrollment to be delayed. Very slow customer service.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I just want to use the customer portal to access my payments and ADD MONEY to my blocked account (to reflect the new 992€/mo requirement), but I can’t find the “my payments” option under my blocked account like the TUTORIAL online says to do. I can’t find it on my app on my iPhone, Android, or desktop. I’ve been trying to be patient with customer service, but this is delaying my temporary permit process (which is delaying me from uploading my document within 180 days).", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "My bank transferred the funds quickly once after my request. But on expatrio it showed after so much of delay.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Very bad service", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Did not get my health insurance certificate after 4 days from applying although it was stated that it will take 24 hours only", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Even though I changed date of arrival in profile, Still it is not reflecting in travel health insurance", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Couldn't get response of my email on time, still waiting.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have not had access to my bank account for a whole week. Despite calling and leaving 2 voicemails after waiting on hold for 20 minutes each time, and sending two emails to their support team. Appalling service as I have not had access to my money for the whole week right as my rent is due. I hope to be proven wrong with a solution ASAP but at this point I believe this company is effectively running a scam. Avoid at all costs.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It’s easy enough to set up an account but all feels a bit dodgy as you do it. It also doesn’t help that their customer service is extremely poor. You give your huge sum of money through a transfer to a business account that doesn’t match the name of Expatrio. It does work though but is a weird start to the process. You then have to wait until you’re in Germany to activate it. Seems simple enough until you try and do that and discover you also need a German number. Since the UK have just left the Erasmus countries, the need for a blocked account to do an exchange is new. I don’t remember seeing anywhere about needing a German phone number to unlock the account. Thankfully it wasn’t urgent since it took 5 days for customer support to respond to my question, as well as 2 unanswered phone calls (one said immediately that they were too busy and the other said it was a 3 minute wait but made me wait 20 minutes before telling it it was too busy). They also sent me a link to good phone providers but all of them were contracts when all I needed was to get an PAYG SIM card just for the account to be activated. The best one is ALDI TALK. After that though it’s almost instant the set up. It’s all very secure with video calls to check you are who you say you are. I had very few doubts about Expatrio before the really poor customer service but other than that the account works well and it gave me health insurance and you can also get travel insurance. This is good value for money. Just don’t ask any questions!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Me habían recomendado mucho Expatrio por ser una empresa que te facilitaba todo este proceso, hasta antes de mi llegada a Alemania todo iba bien, sin embargo, ya tengo tres semanas en Alemania y aún no me desbloquean mi cuenta y mucho menos me han dado mi cuenta de banco. Hace ya dos semanas mi verificación aparece en revisión y no me dan ninguna solución en su servicio al cliente. Realmente necesito el dinero para subsistir aquí, pagar renta, seguro y comida. ES URGENTE!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "You want me to submit new documents for activation for my health insurance but there is no option to submit this documents how will you expect to to upload those documents! Your customers service will took 1 business day to answer my problems you should have physical office to visit this is important documents. Your customer service sucks!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I needed the Blocked Account Confirmation for my Visa-application and although the money had transferred, Expatrio officials were too lazy to hit a button and confirm, so I had to call and personally demand that I need it for the day after, as I waited until the last day, and the first thing they said was to wait and it will eventually be confirmed. If I had the time to wait, I would've waited. Instead, I had to worry about the money through all the process and personally deal with the situation, which was very unprofessional.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Delayed response & communication errors.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I had some problem with the M10 process (process of sending insurance certificate directly to university). It took way longer than I expected for the university to recieve. Also, the support center does not exist. I have called the phone number, was put on wait for 20 minutes, and was then cut off.  Many times, I was left anxious because of lack of update about the process. I wished expatrio could have given more explanation on what was going on each time they texted me.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am writing as a user with the ID number 460455, and I would like to explain my issue in detail. Despite numerous attempts to resolve this matter, I have yet to receive a satisfactory resolution, and I am now deeply frustrated with the situation. \n\nI emailed you two days ago as well. It has been almost 10 days since I arrived in Germany, but I still cannot activate my account.\n\nWhen I click on the \"Banking\" section, the \"Activate\" button appears, but when I click on it, it doesn't proceed and remains stuck. Please reset my account and let me go through the verification steps from the beginning. I am also requesting a new video verification appointment.\n\nI have been dealing with this issue for 10 days now, and I cannot continue another week without access to my funds. My payments are overdue, and I am in a difficult situation.\n\nIf my problem is not resolved this time, I will have to consider legal action.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Whenever I have to log in to my account, it asks for OTP to be delivered via email. This is too much of security and it reduces the ease of use. Also, the session expires every 5 mins, so I again have to repeat the login procedure. \n\nMoreover, activating the blocked account is a hassle. It is not possible to do it on a laptop or PC, it has to be done on a mobile device. All the documents that are required to be uploaded are generally on the laptop. Uploading documents through Android File Explorer is a hassle and not at all easy. Plus there is no camera option while uploading the documents. That means each time the app asks for a document, I have to exit the app and click an image, then locate that image in the file explorer through expatrio app (the most difficult part). Please improve user experience.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I sent the money from the bank in my own country to create a blocked account in expatrio. since I did not have an account in that bank before, I sent the amount to be blocked through my friend who has an account in that bank. but although the money left our bank on the day we sent the money (september 11), the money has still not been deposited into my expatrio account and I have a visa appointment on september 18. I request that this situation be resolved urgently.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The user interface is not easy to use, and it is very frustrating. I only wanted to get the blocked account, but it forced me to add the insurance to the cart each time, which required me to contact customer service, which was very, very slow (like 3 days slow). The money transfer process was not clear enough, and since it was a big amount, it was very stressful for us. I don't think I am getting my money's worth. For next year, I don't think I will continue with this company for my finances in Germany.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I didn't get my travel insurance .", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Sitede dili çevirince ilerletmiyor kayıt olamıyorsun ve sürekli bir sorun çıktı diyor", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have been emailing about an urgent matter for 3 days now and The only reply I got was from an inefficient bot by email. It said to email back with a reply and the website said that I'll get a reply within 1 business day. However, I still haven't received anything. There are no live chat agents as well, it's just an inefficient bot that can't help. \nAll I'm asking for is a new confirmation of my blocked account that I haven't even used at all since I'm still waiting for my visa which needs the new confirmation to be processed since the current letter i have ends in less than a month!!!!!\nThis is my worst customer experience yet!\nI expected much more from the company. This is horrid. just super bad.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Unfair fees and hidden charges\nI only received an 90 euro buffer out of 100, and your explanation was surprising.\nYou're deducting money from the day I transferred the amount, which doesn't make sense. I started receiving payouts in October 2023, but you charged me fees for July, August and Septemer 2023 without any prior notice, and then suddenly deducted everything from the buffer. This seems unfair and feels like a misleading tactic to take money.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I got rejected at vfs appointment centre because I failed to give Tk insurance.\n \nAfter taking Value of Expatario, however Expatario failed to provide essential document.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The only thing I really disliked is the help centre. They either don’t reply to important queries or reply extremely late. There are lot of app glitches too.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Pésima experiencia.\nAcudí al banco con el formato de transferencia y van dos ocasiones en que no pasa. Me cobraron una comisión por aprox 450 dolares en cada una, es decir que he perdido 900 dólares y nadie se está haciendo responsable.\nTrato de contactarlos y no responden por teléfono, me bota la llamada al esperar al asesor en Alemania.\nY por correo responden una frase y hay que esperar días de nuevo hasta que se comunican.\nPerdí mi cita de la visa y hasta este momento 18 mil pesos por su pésima asesoría y gestión.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "No response to our queries.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The support is crazy, and it's the worst", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I applied for refund to expatrio, and then got an e-mail in 15th of August that says it may take up to 4 weeks. Tomorrow will be 4 weeks.\nIn the 3rd of the September, i wrote them for the process, they said in the 8th of the month, they controlled my papers, and reviewing them again for anti money laundering process. I sent my money to my account with swift in one night and there were no problem, but while you are paying back, you say you are controlling for anti money laundering, is this identical? \nIn addition, for the refund process i kindly ask for a fast process since i need this amount asap for my other applications, but they did not helped me.\nIT IS ENOUGH PLEASE GIVE MY MONEY BACK", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "When we contact Expatrio's support team, they don't respond even after one business day. Their service is very poor.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I had some issues with Expatrio service last week, but I appreciate them responding to my review. I now have 3 stars because I still had massive difficulty calling their helpline. I tried 4 times and collectively, waited over 55 minutes on hold, but never once reached a representative. For an institution that handles large sums of money, I would expect better phone service and hope this issue can be addressed internally.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have uploaded the required documents on 30th August. According to the process the document review should take upto a week but more than a week have passed and as expected the blocked account closing documents(visa rejection letter and bank document) are still under review.\nThere is no update or progress from Expatrio and no reply to my emails either. I am sure the documents that I uploaded are okay and the refund should have been initiated by now. \nExpatrio has yet again made it painful for me. You guys should understand that customers like me have a lot of other important work to do and it is very difficult for us to follow up at every step of the closing process.\nI am very very disappointed with the customer support from Expatrio", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Not good customer service is pathetic they never try to understand our query and don’t reply on time which waste alot of time", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Payment never on time , it's been four months, they have stated payment will arrive every first week of every month but this seems never to be the case, i receive it nearly at the end of every month.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have transferred funds 2 times to my one transfer on 31st August and on 3rd sept today is 8th still the second payment didn't get updated and funds didn't credited in my account", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Expatrio did nothing about giving cashback after I decided not to get health insurance", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Customer service was very slow and the instructions were confusing.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I contacted customer service via email three days ago, but I have not yet received a response. I have been unable to reach anyone regarding an urgent matter. I had a visa appointment yesterday and could not submit the 06 document. Despite their promise to respond within one day, I have been waiting for three days.\n\nI got an answer but their answer did not solve my problem.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Issue was not resolved. Worst customer support ever. Please don’t dupe people like this", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Their support is non-existent. They have given a number to contact but good luck trying to find an agent to connect with you. I am facing an issue since Monday and have waited patiently for them to reply to my mail but I don't get any help. I just get automated mails that my issue is resolved but it is not resolved yet. I have my visa appointment on Wednesday and these guys are making sure I will get rejected. Worst service everrrr\n\nEdit: Got a reply on trustpilot saying that team has promptly responded to update my details. Yes I have already updated my details in the personal data section but still my health insurance certificate shows the wrong university. That part is still not fixed. If it gets fixed I am willing to leave a better review :)", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have completed the full transfer for my amount required for my blocked account and the funds have arrived in my account and they show on my profile. But formore than two weeks now but you guys have still not verified my account and you have not send me the 06 Blocked amount opening confirmation. Neither have you informed me as why this delay is happening.This unreasonable delay from your side has caused me big problems with my visa, studies and everything. Please send me the opening confirmation as fast as possible.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It should be more specific that the benefitiary of the transfer for the blocked account must be a member of close family or yourself. Its not enough with the given information in the website.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The application processes is very smooth. However, the app designer should simplify the interface i.e. more easy to access to key features such as blocked account and health insurance certificate. Moreover, biometric login should be allowed.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "My initial deposit was €11437 and I had my visa appointment on 17 July post which there was a rumour about increased block account amount. So, 4 days back I edited the details in my account to increase the amount by €700. \n\nMy problem - dashboard is not getting updated since last 4 days. It says initial amount of €11437 as yet to be transferred in Form 05. However, at one place it says amount received as €11432 which is 5 euro less than what I transferred. Please help to get the dashboard updated so that I can increase the amount by €700 and also, sort the difference of 5 euros between transferred and available amount on my dashboard. I need to submit the same to embassy ASAP", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I contacted you regarding the extension of health insurance for 365 days from 185 days ,after writing a mail and tried to reach out to you regarding the same via phone,I've been waiting for 18 mins on hold and later you redirected me to a voice mail.Neither your got back via mail nor to my voice message.\nThis is a high priority thing for me as my visa was held in the consulate and I see you are responding for review but not for the raised concern.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The application is easy to use. But when something is wrong and I want to cancel, it takes 2-3 days to get reply from the service team. I think every thing is okay expect the late reply .", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I received only an 85-euro buffer out of 100, and your explanation was surprising. You’re deducting money from the day I transferred the amount, which doesn’t make sense. I started receiving payouts in September 2023, but you charged me fees for June, July, and August 2023 without any prior notice, and then suddenly deducted everything from the buffer. This seems unfair and feels like a misleading tactic to take money.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "They say that they automatically send the M10 notification but my university hasn’t received the M10 notification and when i tried to contact expatrio via email all i got was an automated reply. Its been 2 days and they say they will contact within 1 business day , still havent been contacted by anyone from the side of expatrio.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I had sent a Blocked Account closure request 2 days ago because my visa was rejected. Expatrio was supposed to reach me within one business day and today is the 3rd business day without any response. I do not know when I will receive the closure initiation mail or my money. Blocked account opening was smooth and fast as was the case with me as well (and is evident in the good reviews) but the problems start right after it seems.\nI have submitted the contact form as per process and waiting to upload the required documents after the close button is enabled.\nI am really disappointed with Expatrio customer service", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I received my final payout this month, but my buffer still hasn't been returned to me. Many of my friends are facing the same issue. I don't see the point in holding 100 euro buffer for so long and then not even disbursing it after the last payout.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Everything was great, but it was really difficult to locate the IBAN number.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Slow responses", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "instructions are hard to find", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Misleading about the bank account being \"free\" and the bank account not needing an address. People's lives get ruined through such lies.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The information I requested was not given in the way I requested.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I will be coming to Germany with my husband but I could not find any information on how to add him to my insurance. I have sent multiple e-mails but my questions are not answered.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "had trouble signing in and receiving security emails, app has some problems", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Very false advertising on the period of the process. I had to wait for the review of my application for 5 days even though on the website it says within 24 hours, I sent the request for the extension of the blocked account still have not responded me back within 24 hours (I have waited for 2 days).\n\nVery slow on customer service, take a long time to respond.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have been sending emails after emails to send electronic insurance notification to  H0000481 (Ostfalia University of Applied Sciences), even TK has not informed me till now if its send or not", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Payment options should be improvised, losing lots of money on exchange transactions due to currency fluctuations.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I gave it 5 stars before, but now I regret.\nThink twice if you want to open a blocked account with this company.\n1. Very slow customer service, they need weeks to reply to you but the replies weren't helpful.\n2. Their phone service is very difficult to reach while they don't have any walk-in service or appointments.\n3. They cannot handle issues after you transfer money to them. And you bear all the consequences.\n4. Technical errors usually appear on their platform.\nExpatrio should become a competent company before doing business.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "have to wait too long for the response", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Someone has emailed me that the unblocked amount can be added under blocked account then payments. \nBut I am not able to see this and no help from customer service", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It would be great if you guys could implement a live chat for helping abroad students, some times its hard to make time lines due to the mail waiting issue", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Some times there is a delay in login..", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I emailed them and I didn’t get a response back. Luckily I do have time but you need to keep that in mind. Plus they assured me that they would send my M10 document to my university and they didn’t", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The overall interface design is very attractive and simple, which I really like. However, I’m not sure if it's an issue with my operation or a system bug. I applied for a transfer three times in total, and it was quite troublesome. The first time, after the application was successful, there was no 05 file available below, which prevented me from going to the bank to complete the transfer. Despite several days of communication with customer service, the issue wasn’t resolved, so I had to reapply. The second time, the 05 file appeared, but it took several days to show up, and by the time it did, it was almost expired, leaving me no time to go to the bank. Finally, the third time was successful, but it took nearly half a month in total just to complete one transfer. I find this process extremely cumbersome and hope for improvements. Thank you.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am trying to get the documents done before my appointment for a visa in Germany. It is said that I will get my verification in at most 24 hours. It has been 36 hours, and I couldn't transfer my money to my blocked account since it has not been approved yet. Also, I mailed them about my circumstances, but no response. My visa appointment is on Monday; it is Friday night now. I cannot transfer money in time. I hope everything goes well and Expatrio validates my account before my visa appointment. I will update this comment once everything settles.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Funds transfer was quick but there was a lot of delay in releasing 06 blocked account document. The customer service was hard to reach and there was added delay from expatrio to share details asked by bank.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Well to me i think theyre doin a fantastic job together as a team..more kudos.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I like the ease of using the service.. i don't like the customer service", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "No spanish available \nNot easy to understand the process\nFees", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Worst experience of my life with Expartio customer support, they are not answering mails for 2 days. I just wanted to add unblocked deposit for that I tried contacting them for 3 days, they just have to initiate my new transfer request. For this they took 3 days. \nStill bad experience is not over...\nI paid full amount for 11417 Euro, which they have asked in INR 1069206.65, still they are massaging you made partial payment. I already escalated this issue, let's see if it resolves or not. This is just beginning, I fear what will happen after I land in Germany.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "My money 2617 euros was returned to Nigeria since 1 August, I need the document proof of return please, I have not seen this money.\n\nI don't like your service", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Envie los fondos, se tardaron una semana en avisar de que estaban teniendo problemas para crear la cuenta bloqueada, desde el 29 de julio de 2024 que me informaron de esto, hasta el día de hoy 5 de agosto de 2024, no han resuelto el problema y el día de mañana es mi cita con la visa, y no me repsonde de cuando van a entregar el documento.\nLas respuestas son las mismas, autogeneradas, encima me despierto en las madrugas para estar al pendiente de un servicio al cliente pobre y lento", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Sorularımın yavaş cevaplanması ve müşteri temsilcisinin eksikliği dolayı kırdım", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Esperé demasiado tiempo para que se abriera la cuenta bloqueada. Perdí la cita de la visa por ello.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Please ensure that response time are within SLA.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The support team didn't provide a definite answer to the inquiry, and I thought Expatrio's work was a little late.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The waiting times could be shorter, especially after the money transfer", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "There is customer service, very inconvenient. And the instructions are not very clear. Really a bad experience.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am going to Germany for my Master's degree and I chose to work with Expatrio to open a blocked account. I purchased the Value Package to also use the insurance. I initiated the transfer of funds to the blocked account from my own bank, but it still hasn't been credited to the blocked account. When I contacted the bank I sent the transfer from, they said they have already initiated the transfer.\n\nI have a visa appointment in two days, and I need the document for my blocked account to be ready. I emailed Expatrio, but I haven't received a response. I need support for the problem I am experiencing. I have limited time left.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It might be ideal that the support team could provide prompt and accurate answer to the client, especially in the urgent situation.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "You kept the first transaction waiting for 10 days and then refunded it from a different bank and I suffered a loss without doing anything and you do not take care of it.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Very slow response. Took atleast 24hrs for a response for each reply.\n\nBut the resolution is good.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Took too much time to get amount confirmation after transferring the amount. Many of the my friends faced this issue. Visa deadline will be nearby, soo if we get amount confirmation soon it will be helpful. But for me amount confirmation was received very soon.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The process is complicated, especially when you come from a country where making international transfers is difficult.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have already created a blocked account and transferred the money. Now i wamt to create an unblocked account to transfer my second sem fees which i can show as proof during visa appointment. But expatrio is not respomding to the mail where i requested the same. Kindly help as soon as possible as my visa appointment date is nearing.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "the service team responded super slow and didn' really answering my questions. Appearntly they didn't read my email.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I dont like their android app. It feels outdated and sluggish. Otherwise service is good.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Like the user interface and easy to use. On the other hand, I dislike the transfer guidelines. I transferred the amount requested for the blocked account. And I separately paid the transfer fees so that the full amount is received without any shortage. Surprisingly, I noticed that the amount received in the account is less by approximately €22. That’s what I dislike.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "All issues require atleast one day to solve even if they are urgent. Can be made still more faster", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Die Rückgabe von Geld von einem Sperrkonto ist sehr bürokratisch. Sie müssen nachweisen, dass Sie nach Deutschland gekommen sind und eine Reihe von Dokumenten vorlegen, an die sehr strenge Anforderungen gestellt werden. Zum Beispiel ein Wohnsitznachweis, der ausschließlich aktuell ist, auf Ihren eigenen Namen lautet und aus bestimmten Quellen stammt.\n\nUpdate:\nEven after I proved my place of residence, the expatrio writes that the verification process has been failed and says “wait for instructions.” In general, I got the impression that their main goal is to get money (because this is a very fast process), but they very much delay the payment process for various reasons.\n\nMy advice: choose another service. The one I interacted with before had no such problems at all.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Guten Tag,\n\nich bin nicht nicht zufrieden, obwohl mir von meiner Bank mitgeteilt wurde, dass ich meine Überweisung in Euro tätigen könne und der Screenshot so aussah, erfuhr ich, dass dies nicht möglich sei. In der Zwischenzeit hatte ich mein Geld in Euro umgerechnet und hatte es dann getan Um es in USD umzurechnen, bin ich ein Opfer. Ich habe finanziell Geld verloren. Ihr Bildschirm und Ihr Team haben Sie nicht richtig geführt.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The intermediary bank transfers could be notified to the customers.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "So many back and forth emails was required to align blocked account.\n\nAfter receiving the payment, you realised that partner bank has declined the account verification.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Vey bad respond. Slow", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Instant processing but a little disappointed just discovered service fee applied even before activating blocked account. So if visa rejected you will lose money here too. Also better add more money so it is as per accepted guidline during visa processing which takes 3-4 months. I.e. 4×5 more euros.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "A lot of steps. It must be easier.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "No specific warning mentioning the USD is more expensive than the Euro....\nI didn't realize until I ask my friend about the price. \n\"It's usually faster and cheaper to send money to your account in local currency\" is A SCAM...\nI'm actually sad now", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Even though I was using one of the biggest banks of my country, their account of my local currency wouldn't accept my payment. I had to convert my Euro into my local currency and then back to Euro because of their inabilities and lost money. I would not recommend using it if you have any other options.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have an extremely negative experience with Expatrio. On May 7, I registered an account at Expatrio and uploaded a scan of my passport. Only on May 15, after my reminder, they opened a blocked account for me! On the same day, May 15, I transferred money to my blocked account. The transfer was in Euros from Poland to  Mangopay Bank in Luxembourg. So far the money has not been credited to my blocked account (June 5). Apparently, the money is stuck in Mangopay Bank in Luxembourg. But the Expatrio support service does not want to take any action to find my money. So I am left without money and without a visa to Germany.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Site does not show transactions and dates. Only shows balances. All banks should show itemized transaction. Site then sent me two payments in first month and insufficient funds now remain in my account to apply for my residency permit. I might be able to prove to german government that set up account correctly and was over paid in first month but this is not possible without a list of itemized transactions listed by date. Specifically the transaction showing the correct amount of funds received and the date received. I have my receipt from my bank showing transfer but german government will want to see receipt for expatrio receiving the money. I have no idea how to correct this problem.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "You have not replied to my request for help concerning activation of blocked bank account.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Çok kötüydü. Çok Ağır ilerledi.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Primero que todo escribir en español porque es mi idioma materno, encuentro que la plataforma no es tan amigable con el usuario y que podrían trabajar en ello, es un poco difícil saber dónde encontrar los datos para transferir luego de haber sido aprobada la cuenta, creo que quizás en la página o la aplicación podría haber un apartado donde diga donde transferir los datos y así sería mucho más amigable o podría haber un botón de pago como las tiendas comerciales o PayPal, en el que uno pueda pagar directamente desde la página. \nMuchas gracias por leerme.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "You don't have a support team in India", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Me and my friend tried opening account with expatrio. There was a technical issue because we opened the account using same computer. I even transfered my block account money and my block account was opened but later after few days I had a mail stating that the account information was mixed with my friend. It wasted almost 2 weeks of time and the customer support team is also very slow in solving queries.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I had terrible experience activating my blocked account and still i couldnt get my money from my blocked account yet. I have tried and follow the steps two times with video identification process. Still they have my name wrong and result in identification failed. \n\nI have told them my first name and sirname and this is really upsetting me because i need to pay my rent and pay for my food. How can i pay for my rent and food if my money is still in blocked account?? \n\nI have tried and call expatrio customer service and no one picked up. I have waited a long time just to speak to the person who can help me out. No one picked up and the call was 2 hours!! Ive waited 2 hours just to see if anyone responding but turns out no one attended to me. \n\nI have followed the proper instructions and still they have got my name wrong and saying it was the bank fault as well. I dont get it. Dont we have the iban and swift code number that can be used as referances. I need to pay for my rent and buy food because i have no cash left. This is really concerning", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The request for tax identification number (TIN) from applicant who have not yet arrived Germany from their home country, appears not to be ok with me.In developing country like mine,we are mostly tax indirectly and as such many do not have (TIN)", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Not all the id verification specialists are friendly. Some don't even know how to explain to verification procedure. And one of them even told me that I don't speak english nor German while she was the one who couldn't speak proper english! I found that very disrespectful. But the last one was very friendly and her steps explanations were clear.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I didn't get the payment confirmation certificate during my visa submission", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Good aspects:\n1. Once the deposit is made, documents can be automatically generated for visa extension.\n2. A customer service named Angela is very nice, reply to emails in a timely manner, for my questions answered succinctly, effectively; while also standing in my point of view to provide me with actionable advice, very good customer service staff, recommended promotion and salary increase, haha.\n\nBad aspects:\n1. Due to the fact that I had to send money offshore（to Luxembourg）(the German bank account collaborated with you refused my request to send money), the arrival time seemed to be about 3 days later than that of the German account. It is recommended to set up additional German accounts for the convenience of customers who are in Germany.\n2. The service of WeChat Chinese customer service and the customer service I contacted by writing emails is terrible, they don't read my questions at all, they just answer mechanically, the customer service experience is very poor.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I took insurance of dr walter but TK has not yet informed my university the same and did not send electronic notification owing to which I am suffering and enrolment is pe ding", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "1- for the initial payment of my bank account, due to the option being there i tried sending the money in liras however the transfer wasn’t possible due to the banking system. I lost a sum of money to conversion rates due to their lack of explanation.\n2- during the identification process (via IDnow) the first person was very rude and didn’t speak proper English, tried to rush me and eventually declined without further explanation, i sensed a discrimination based on my nationality. The second person was great and helped me identify in a few minutes.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Activation process is so hectic.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I would also expect your web page in German Language.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I liked everything about the insurance and blocked account. But if I want to pay in dollars then I have to pay 200 dollars more. And my biggest disappointment was to find out that Expatrio is misleading about the current account. They say they help to open it. But after I transfered my blocked account money and asked them about current account they said they can only give me tips how to do that.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I landed in Germany and now unable to activate my account. I have a Canadian passport that was released in June, 2023. This company and it's unqualified customer support does not know how to validate this over the video call. This is the same passport that was provided while opening an account. I was asked to go to the Post office in Germany and they could not validate the new passport either. For those who are not familiar, the photo page of the new Canadian passport is a plastic card and the the post office needs MICR which is there on other passports. Now I'm stuck in a new country with all money locked up. Their support people are useless. I hope someone from this company reads this and help resolve.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I'm frustrated with expatrio, I've been trying to unlock it for 20 days and I can't because there are no people available to unlock it.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "My transfer failed with expatrio. The banks that they work with are not collaborative, especially for the students who come from Turkey. I would definitely not recommend. I waited for 2 weeks and their bank still say they don't know where my money is, while my bank says they successfully transfered my amount.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "For the verification i tried 3 times and finally finished\nThe first man wrote my name wrong, the second man has no patience and cut off our connect directly!!\nThanks to the third man, patient and skilled.\nThe experience was really bad! For the third man i would like to give one more star.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The process of setting up the blocked account is not quick or smooth as advertised. I'm basically stuck now waiting for feedback after a failed identity verification due to an unexperienced agent. It doesn't make sense asking me twice to give a review before I finish setting up my account so this is my initial review which I will update later. \nUPDATE: Everything is running smoothly now so I have to adjust my previous rating of the service. My advice to new customers is not to worry in the beginning as it might take some time to set up your accounts as the process involves third parties.\nUPDATE: Stay away!!! There is no real customer support. They just send you generic responses, so if you have any problems you will be left without any way to access your money or knowing why some of your money is missing from your account in my case. Save yourself from this horrible experience!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Customer Service is not qualified.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Not a convenient process for adding Additional Basic Sum money.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Although the money reached the receiving bank the day after I sent it, it was held at the bank for more than 2 weeks. And there was nothing wrong or incorrect. For days I sent emails to expatrio support to contact the bank, but there was no solution. Finally, I contacted the bank myself and the problem was resolved within a few days. However, due to this disruption, I could not submit my blocked account document at my visa appointment. I sent it as an missing document. You should choose the banks you work with better and communicate better.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I sent second wrong transfer. So I sent my dekont by bank. I wrote a email but no reply me yet. Didn't send back me . Please help me. Ahmet BAKIR", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I had done full payment but the gap between the payment was only one day but the only one payment is showing in blocked account statement another is still pending and I had visa application within one day.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Expatrio has given my blocked account confirmation after 4 5 days. I wasn't able to give document at visa appointment.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "THE WORST SERVICE EVER!!!!! \n\nIt's been over 6 months my sister's education in Germany has started. Despite multiple attempts to resolve the issue through emails and phone calls, she hasn't yet to receive a single disbursement.  They are giving non-sense reasons and their internal conflicts. They can't even give the timeline to solve the issue and don't know how long she need to wait to get money from them. As an international student, her primary focus should be on her studies, not on navigating financial uncertainties caused by poor service. \n\nYou guys deserve minus review. DO NOT TRUST THIS SERVICE.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Costomer support option should have call option instead of email support", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am dissatisfied with the recent service I received. There was a significant delay in crediting the amount to my account, causing inconvenience and additionally the provided travel insurance only covers me from 11th March, while my masters program commences on the 15th of March. Traveling on the available date would result in my arrival in Germany on the 14th of March, just a day before my studies begin. This timing is not ideal, as it should have allowed for a more comfortable margin of at least 10 days before the start of my academic program.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "This is the possible worst service to use if you are making block account for extension of your residence permit. They ask you for documents that makes no sense if you are creating block amount for just extension purposes.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Money transfer allocated but you didn’t inform us until we sent you messages and we were waiting for your mail", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The transaction took too much, almost 8 days", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "El servicio al cliente ha retenido mi dinero durante dos meses. Abrí una cuenta bloqueada, y poco tiempo despues tuve que cerrarla la, desde entonces comenzó el martirio. Expatrio no solo ha sido incapaz de devolverme el dinero en más de dos meses, sino que su servicio al cliente es negligente. Me responden con mentiras, no solucionan nada y no ofrecen alternativas ni compensaciones. Tengo una cantidad de dinero congelada por ellos en plena necesidad de fondos. Gracias a esta situación, he perdido muchos recursos ya que Expatrio no ha cumplido con sus compromisos. Me he comunicado de manera oportuna y amable en varias ocasiones durante todo este tiempo, pero después de dos meses, esto me parece un robo oficial. Solicité oficialmente una compensación por la situación y me respondieron que no habían hecho nada malo. Es increíble. Ahora estoy buscando la forma de demandar a una compañía tan irresponsable.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Assalamualaikum everyone hope you all are fine.\n\nI’m sharing an experience of my blocked account with Expatrio, I processed my amount which is 11,417 euro on 02.01.2024. I received an email from Expatrio on 09.01.2024 that my payment has been rejected by the intermediary bank, I called Expatrio on their Helpline number I asked them why they reject my payment. So, then they said we are not accepting funds from your country bank or your country(Pakistan) is a blacklisted country. \n\nAfter that, I changed my blocked account Expatrio to Coracle I opened an account on coracle and they send me the opening confirmation of my account instantly and I processed my Amount which is 11,387 euro on Thursday and received swift code on Friday. I emailed to coracle and attached my swift code and tell them that I have to submit my block mount confirmation on Monday. \n\nCoracle send me the confirmation of my blocked amount on Saturday night and with coracle my experience are really impressive, their reply timing are very quick. \n\nI recommend you all always doing research before processing your payment to any Company or organization. \n\nCoracle really has a great team to communicate with all the international students and specially representative of Coracle from Pakistan AHTASHAM brother. He is very understanding, understand all the situation and give his precious opinion, if you are about to open blocked account go for coracle 100% sure.\n\nThanks.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Hello,\n\nI recently encountered an issue during the identity verification process. Regrettably, I mistakenly began the verification with my wrong passport. As a result, the verification failed.\n\nI've been trying to correct this situation by contacting the support team, but I'm not getting any replies. I would greatly appreciate your guidance on how to correct the initial mistake and successfully complete the verification process, as this will affect my financial situation in Germany.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I had a problem with my blocked account my bank transfer the money 7 December, even though i provided proof sent by my bank. Expatrio support  team did nothing to solve my problem, they only sent emails for me to solve it with my bank here in Chile. A month had to go by  in which i tried to contact cohort directly because when they contact it it was always the same answer no posible solution , to later they found the money that was always there in cohort as I told them, due to a mistake made completely by them and the lack of communication between cohort and Expatrio. I could not apply for my visa and I almost lost my trip. Terrible experience I dont wish it on anybody.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I haven't got any informations about my travel insurance .there is already information about my block amount confirmation and health insurance but there is information about my travel insurance .I have asked but your reply is slow ,my interview is on 16 of Jan and recently i am really worry about waiting for response from you about my travel insurance", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "They are a lot of questions to open the account. It should be easy, but it was more time and work as expected.  It should be in 24 hours give a answer and it takes more time because of Christmas. At least I have to call them, to get an answer. The callcenter woman was very nice and helped me, but after that I sent the money and they make the payment into the wrong account. I tried to call, machine says 2 minutes, after 1 hours they says I have to leave a message and someone will be answer. No body answers. I call on Friday 29.12., all the time says I call outside of work time, but in internet says they are open. Also until know no answer and not solution.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Delay of the payouts for more than 3  weeks . But Expatrio customer service  has helped me  and solved the problem \nThanks Daniel", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I liked the extreme fast processing of the funds to my blocked account which was very convenient and quick than expected. I didn't like the customer support which is not slow but the medium to contact.\n\nI think it should be on chat services and call basis,according to country,for the customer services work.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The process of sending my money to your organization was basically online, and I assumed that your organization is very professional, but unfortunately, you have a very unprofessional person with the IDnow (video) verification.\nThe lady lacks empathy and rudely shuts you down. She speaks like a dictator because she does not allow clients to make further suggestions. She speaks like a programmed robot, ( constantly saying \"I am sorry the system does not support this\"). The next thing she ends the call without educating you properly. \nThis is a very big organization, you should have more professional people like MONICA and Jimmy from the customer care unit to handle your many clients.\n  Monica is a very fantastic and nice person. She is softly spoken-and has lots of encouragement to clients. She spent lots of time on the phone to educate me on the process leading to this success.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I made two payments, one was perfect and at next day it was transfered to the blocked account.( via Cohort). However,in the other payment I couldn't send the total ammount so I asked how should I send it. They were extremely late to give me an answer, a week later, so I could send the remaining money a week later. But the worst of all is that from Cohort it was transfered to my blocked account a week further again. So the whole process took two weeks, and I warned them that it was urgent because the embassy was waiting for it. I trusted it was going to be fast but it was not.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Dear sir,\nDear team hope you are doing well\nHere i am writting the mail to extend my incoming health insurance as per the German consulate,mumbai.\n\nThe earlier embassy issuing 6 months validity for students that 185 days insurance is enough.\nNow the German embassy is giving visa validity for 1 year in the context embessy is asking for 1 year of incoming insurance.\nSo please provide 1 year  incoming health insurance.My colleague insurance extend from your side.no one can short out my query ....you  gave185 day to my colleague and after you gave him 1 year validity on mail...so why I cant as same...", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It's really helpful ,  you can save in it🙂", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "This is a terrible service. My experience starten in November 2022, I had deposited money in my blocked account through a transfer from my uncle. It all went smoothly. Then 2 months later my Visa application was rejected. Between February 2023 and May 2023 I have not heard a word from Expatrio about a refund. Then they started asking for document after document (information about me, information about my uncle who depositied the money for me, copies of passports, etc.) I have provided all the information required, week after week I was informed that they asked their banking partner to transfer my money back to where it came from. Weeks later they decided the money cannot be sent back to its owner, it has to be sent back to an account under my name. I opened a bank account under my name in a country where there is no functional banking sector since 2019 (Lebanon). I have explicitly told Expatrio that it is unlikely a correspondant bank processes a transfer to Lebanon but they insisted. 4 weeks later they inform that they cannot send money to Lebanon and the money has to be sent back to where it came from, meaning my uncle's account in Saudi Arabia. Then they started another round of asking for information that took another 2 weeks. Today they tell me they can only send the money to an account under my name in a country other than Lebanon. Expatrio is asking me to emigrate to get my money refunded. And the adventure continues.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Until the activation process of my blocked account, everything went well with Expatrio. However, I made the mobile video verification three times and they were not successful. Expatrio did not even provide the reason for that. What is more is I'm unable to use the other verification option since the documents that Expatrio requires almost impossible to have if you are new in Germany. I'm stuck with this problem. Expatrio provides no solutions for this and I really need that monthly pay back.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "seit dem 11.10.2023 versuche ich mein gesperrtes Konto zu aktivieren. Ich habe versucht, mich per Videocall zu identifizieren, doch die Mitarbeiter zeigten weder Geduld noch Respekt gegenüber uns Kunden. Sie beendeten den Anruf sofort, ohne eine Begründung zu geben. Nun kann ich mein Konto aufgrund dieses Vorfalls nicht aktivieren und habe kein Geld mehr. Die Art und Weise, wie ich als Kunde behandelt werde, finde ich inakzeptabel.\nEinfach Finger weg", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am writing to report a serious issue that has happened with my son after transferring the blocked account money. The money was delivered to Mangopay, the partner bank, but for unclear reasons they are still blocking the amount. They have asked for certificate of residence and passport copy and all documents were provided promptly, but there is still an unjustified block on my son's already-existing account and the extended one. Now my son cannot renew his residency because he needs the confirmation letter and does not have the monthly payment to pay for his accommodation and living expenses. He is a student who is studying language and is still not permitted to work. Instead of facilitating a student's life, expatrio is playing a destabalising role in a poor student's life. Lots of anxiety and lots of follow up and the only result is waste of time and unjustified delay. We trusted our money with you and we trusted our children's lives in a foreign country with you. Please act accordingly and cooperate with your clients who are helpless students that have no choices but to be at the mercy of banking transactions. Many emails were sent to customer service who respond nicely but no action has been taken to expedite the process. I refer the matter to your management to provide effective solutions in cooperation with your partners.\n\nIt has been four days since I have posted this review. I am updating my review again hoping to receive prompt action to salvage the situation.\n\nAs a follow up of my earlier reviews of the issues my son faced in extending his blocked account, I would like to add that the issue was resolved yesterday and my son received an email from Expatrio team confirming the unblocking of his account and processing of his monthly payouts over the next few days. Also, the extended account will be activated soon. I am writing this to all those who might face the same issue of putting hold on their blocked account. I myself was looking for answers from earlier reviews that reported the issue but did not follow up on the result. Finally, the problem is solved. It took about six weeks since the transaction has taken place with constant follow up with Expatrio customer service by both phone and email. I am writing this to assure those who encounter similar disruption that it will be eventually resolved, but you have to keep in mind that you always need plan B to pay for your rent, bills and daily expenses if this happens to you, God forbid. May God bless our children everywhere.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The employee did not explain to me what the problem was, and the call was cut off until the second time. The second employee explained to me what I could do to get a better view of the passport.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I came to Germany on October 5th. After completing my bank transactions, I completed all my information and went to the ID verification stage, but during our interviews, they said that your passport is not supported. However, my friend had completed the transaction with the same passport type last week. After uploading all the visa and passport information to the Expatrio Support section, no one answered to help. I lost 100 euros in transfer transactions during this process and my terrible time-wise process is now causing difficulties again when trying to get my money.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Video Call Identification did not work since my Turkish Passport was a newer version. I had to make postident identification which I had to go to the post office face to face. The responsible person on the video call told that he could not continue with identification due to my passport having a newer version and this version is not registered in their system. This was an unpleasent experience. My Passport is official and valid so I should'nt have faced this issue. The system should be updated to recognize newer versions of passports so nobody faces this issue again. Postident identification process was smooth and I faced no issue.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I got a mail on 22nd that my payout is being processed. It's been 5 days and I didn't get the amount yet", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Hi, I think your service for transfers etc is very good. However, I referred a friend who made a total of 40 but, only 10 ended up hitting the account", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "i've been trying for months to get my money back....\nat the beginning i didnt get any usefull information about how could i receive the amount of money that was in my blocked account. After that i continued digging after it until they told me that i can get it done in a post bank office. they sent me a postident copoun in order to verify myself there and get the activation done.\nunfortunatly without any justifying reasons it didnt work out and until now i have no access on the money...\ni have no idea how to get my money back!!!!!!!!\ni think that now you have a resonable and logical  reason not to trust them...... DO NOT MAKE ANY DEAL WITH THIS COMPANY.... YOU'RE GONNA REGRET IT!!!!!!!!!!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The bank is still trying to send me my money back \"as they say\" and every time they use the same language that sending the money failed for no reason.\n Frankly, the matter is suspicious, as several months have passed and the year is almost complete and this money has not been returned.\n I think that this bank does not intend to return my money to me, and because of my difficulty in reaching them and the lack of a legal mechanism through which we can reach them and recover our rights, they are exploiting the issue and may never return my money.\n Rejecting a visa application gives them the ability to procrastinate endlessly.\n I am completely convinced that the issue involves a scam, especially for those who cannot reach European Union countries.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Finger weg ... ist nicht in der Lage trotz 7x komplette Durchführung einer Identifikation das Konto zu aktivieren.  Antworten gibt es nur auf Englisch oder Chinesisch obwohl in Deutschland alles konfiguriert und bestellt und die Ansprechpartner angeblich in Berlin sind. Keine Kommunikation in Deutsch oder Französisch möglich. Du bist verloren! Mieser service ... keine konkreten Anweisungen nur Ablehnung.  Geld offenbar verloren ... seit über 4 Wochen bin ich blockiert ohne ersichtlichen Grund.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It was all good until I started writing emails to the support team! I always got a reply after at least 3 days. When I updated from 861€ to 934€ after coming to Germany no form 06 was generated with the updated amount, this affected me during my Residence Permit appointment.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I've tried transferring to their block account for 3 times already and all have failed thus far. Customer support was insufficient throughout this period, unable to provide me with the right account details + slow response. Overall wasted alot of my money and time", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "After 9 months of payout from my blocked account, I am asked to do identify verification again. It’s a long and complicated process where you have to download their stupid app, do a video call and scan your documents. A complete waste of one’s time.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have been with Expatrio for almost 2 years. It is actually easy to open a blocked account with them. I usually get my monthly payout by the end of the month. From the past months everything was alright. \n\nBut it is now 11.08 and I haven’t received my payout yet. I emailed both Expatrio and my bank regarding this issue. My bank told me they cannot locate the transfer as it appears no one is sending me yet. It only takes 2-3 days to receive my payout. No one is telling me what seems to be the problem. It’s clear that it is not my bank.\n\nEventhough I have work to sustain my daily needs, it is not right to delay your client’s monthly payout unless you informed me of some issues. Expatrio’s service is actually good but at least find out what’s causing the delay or atleast informed your client if there is an issue.\n\nUpdate: 18 August now, I haven’t received my payout yet. Again, my bank said there’s no transfer yet.\nAnd yes I’ve been emailing Expatrio since 1st wk of August.\n\nUpdate: 21 August, I am now giving it 2 stars, I hate to give bad reviews but this is unfair. I haven‘t received a notification yet from Mangopay. The delay is too much. I will edit this review once they give me my own money.\n\nEdit: 25 Aug. Finally got my monthly payment.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am waiting for my money to be transferred for more than 6 working days and I need to get document 06 for my visa interview on Tuesday. The money I sent from Turkey reached the intermediary bank on the first business day, but I am still waiting for the transfer to be completed. I can't get an answer to the question I asked through support. In the document you sent, it was stated that it took 3-5 working days and I threw it out 7 days ago despite that. My school opens in September and I have a visa appointment on Tuesday. Please can you at least follow up my transfer with my name and receipt? Waiting for your reply, thank you.MY TRANSFER WILL BE CANCELED IF MY MONEY DOESN'T RECEIVE TO MY ACCOUNT UNTIL 17th AUGUST!!!!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Ich habe seit November 2022 ein Sperrkonto benutzt, alles war in Ordnung, aber im letzten Monat gab es Probleme. Seit fast zwei Wochen kann ich meine monatliche Zahlung noch nicht erhalten.\nIch bin allein in einem fremden Land, ohne Geld, ohne Rechnungen bezahlen zu können, für die ich bereits Strafen erhalten habe, ich kann meine Wohnung nicht bezahlen, ich werde bald auf die Straße gesetzt, meine SIM-Karte wird bald wegen Nichtbezahlung gesperrt und ich werde ohne Kommunikation sein.\nGleichzeitig hat der Support seit einer Woche nicht auf das Schreiben geantwortet, niemand geht ans Telefon, ich bin jedes Mal 15-20 Min. in der Warteschleife, danach wird die Verbindung unterbrochen oder ein Anrufbeantworter eingeschaltet.\n\nIch bin mir absolut sicher, dass Expatrio nach dieser Situation nicht mehr als einen Stern verdient hat.\n\nP.S. Sie antworteten mit einem Standardkommentar. Gleichzeitig habe ich in der Rückmeldung meine ID angegeben und zweimal an die angegebene E-Mail-Adresse geschrieben.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have been a customer with Expatrio for 2 years now, and am extending my account for the third year in a row. My account is stuck on the \"awaiting activation\" page and no payouts have been sent out for this extended account. I am dependent on this money to pay rent, bills etc. The customer support team is nowhere to be found, cannot reach them on call or get a response via the contact form. Really disappointing after 2 years of smooth service. Not sure what to do now as I cannot reach them at all.\n\nUpdate: I did not have an \"activate\" button on my profile until I sent them several emails. After that I finally got the option to activate and then followed a simple ID procedure at the post office. While I have my payouts set up now, really disappointed how we were not given any heads up about these new procedures, timelines, and delays. Would hope Expatrio steps their game up before their reputation takes a hit in the internationals students community.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Unable to log in to my expatrio account- tells me 'somethings wrong' every time I try and if I try to change my password it says I don't have an account. \n\nI have emailed them and had no reply and can't get through to anyone over the phone either. Need to access my account urgently for my visa application and am losing all hope/ beginning to regret I ever made an account.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I can't log in to my account. I keep getting \"something wrong try main page\"\n\nNow I can't even pay into my account. Now I'm stuck. If no change by the end of the day I will probably have to use a different provider.\n\nQuite shambolic!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I had a terrible experience with Expatrio. I needed to open a blocked account for my visa application, but the application keeps rejecting my passport photo. I tried contacting support, but their instructions were repetitive and unhelpful. What's frustrating is that my classmates, who uploaded low-quality scanned photos, had their photos automatically accepted. It's been days, and I still haven't received a response from the support team.\n\nThis constant rejection of my passport photo and the lack of response from the support team have caused significant delays in my visa application process. This has created a lot of stress and uncertainty for me, as I am on a tight timeline to secure my visa and make the necessary arrangements for my relocation. I understand that technical issues can arise, but the lack of effective communication and assistance from Expatrio has been extremely frustrating. I hope that the company can address these issues promptly and provide the necessary support to resolve my situation.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have successfully transferred the funds and received the 06 file, but my account shows 0. The customer service responded very slowly and did not solve the problem.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Customer service is very poor, I am trying to open my blocked account and have few queries, I sent an email and there was no response, i have been calling them for 4 days continuously and no one picked the call even once. Disappointed!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "No tuve ningún inconveniente para abrir mi cuenta bloqueada y seguro médico, pero desde el viernes pasado estoy enviando correos para ampliar mi paquete integral por 1 mes más, por solicitud de la embajada alemana y no ha sido posible obtener respuesta, lo cual me pejudica enormemente. \nLo he intentado modificar varias veces desde la página y no funciona.\nLes he enviado correos electrónicos  y no he obtenido respuesta pese a que dicen que se comunican en maximo 24 horas.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Their applications are not working, my account was not activated even though I verified with video verification. I haven't been able to activate for almost 3 weeks. They want me to try the other method, so I'm expected to adress proof. Why do I have to provide proof of address when there was video verification? I need to withdraw my money to rent an apartment, but I am expected to submit an address record to receive the money. Tiring cycle.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "There was a bit of a problem in making a Girokonto in Germany. Commerzbank and ING are 2 of the 4 recommended by Expatrio to activate the Blocked Account but application to open a Girokonto in these 2 banks were rejected. In the end, a Girokonto from the local Sparkasse was opened and the activation of the blocked account proceeded without a problem.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Pros: the application process is easy and can be completed remotely.\n\nCons: The online system has many glitches that are pretty annoying and unnecessary.\n\n1. I added money to my account in installments. These arrived and were reflected in the balance. However during this process the 'transfer status' did not update to 'complete'. The result was that I could not initiate a transfer for up to the final amount until I contacted customer service and had them update the status of these transfers manually. This took about three days.\n\n2. I got the blocked account coupled with Dr Walters health insurance. I activated the insurance through Expatrio. Expatrio did not pass on the complete details to Dr Walters. Specifically they did not pass on the intended end date of the contract. I am waiting 1.5 weeks for confirmation from Dr Walters, while they are evidently waiting on this information. In the end I called Dr Walters directly them and they straighten it out immediately.\n\n3. Right now I have just completed the identity check through the app via a video call. After the video call I am sent to screen that says the identity check was successful. Now under the 'account activation status' it says the identity check failed. So I really don't know if it has been successful or not or what I need to do.\n\nCustomer service takes (based on my 3 experiences) ~ 3 business days to respond, not one. So Expatrio should not say they aim to respond within one business day.\n\nThis could be a really good service if these glitches were fixed.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "This is unbelievable really! I need my funds now and this can not be tolerated! The blocked account is supposed to be ready from 01.04.23 and till now I can't receive the funds! I don't know how you are doing this to your clients and it directly damages my life and I can not accept it. I don’t know why you don’t reply I don’t get it even when I call you no one answers. I have the complete right to know where is my money and why I’m not getting it all this time. \n\nI'm living the worst days of my life because of your issue. I don't know what living in the streets, not in your apartment, is worth to you???? How should I study and succeed??? I'm broke because of your issue and you are providing some change as a compensation. This is definitely destroying my life and everything about being here in germany. I'm still figuring up my options as a legal approach to this.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I've a blocked account by expatrio ,but the last two months I'vent bekomm my transfer und they say that my transfer ist by mangopay blockiert und they trying to contact mangopay .i made a kontakt with mangopay und told that the problem is by expatrio und thanx to them i have no money now to pay my apartment und in 10 days I'll be living in streets HOMLESS", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Is Expatrio a Scam company? Where do money saved in an account mysteriously vanished to. After Keeping my account frozen for a whole month, my account is now showing 0 balance. I am a student depending on the monthly payouts for survival. I have been in Germany since April 4,2023 and today is June 6, 2023. This only mail i have gotten fro expatrio regarding my blocked account money has been that they are are chasing their banking partners to return my money to my original blocked account. I have thrown out of my house because I do not have cash to pay my rent. I have to beg before I eat. Why are you guys so wicked expatrio. Where did you send my money, where did all my money go to?", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "My Son Credentials are as under:\nName: Sarim Ahmed Kola\n\nThis has reference to below exchange on subject long pending issue I am writing to inform you about a matter of utmost importance that requires your immediate attention. It has come to my attention that your organization, Expatrio , seems to be involved in alleged money laundering activities, in violation of various local and international laws and regulations.\n\nIn light of the seriousness of these allegations, I demand that you immediately refund my amount without further loss of time. \n\nI urge you to take the necessary steps to rectify the situation, including conducting a thorough internal investigation into these allegations and implementing robust compliance measures to ensure that your organization is fully compliant with all relevant laws and regulations.\n\nFailure to comply with this long pending request will leave me with no choice but to pursue all available legal remedies to protect the interests of the affected parties. This may include reporting the matter to law enforcement authorities, cooperating with regulatory agencies, and pursuing civil litigation seeking damages for the harm caused.\n\nForgery (Section 267, German Criminal Code)\n\nIf a criminal investigation has been initiated against you on suspicion forgery in Germany, applies all the more to document forgery offences, as the police clearance rate is above average compared to other offences. The punishability of document forgery results from § 267 German Criminal Code. According to § 267, paragraph 1, German Criminal Code, anyone who produces a false document, falsifies a genuine document or uses a false or falsified document in order to deceive legal transactions commits forgery. Even the attempt to forge a document is punishable. The German criminal law provision serves the security and reliability of legal transactions with documents.\n\nI strongly advise you to seek legal counsel to understand the gravity of the situation and to ensure that you take appropriate actions to rectify this matter promptly. It is in your best interest to cooperate fully with any investigations that may be initiated as a result of these allegations.\n\nI trust that you will treat this matter with the utmost urgency and seriousness it deserves. I look forward to receiving written confirmation from you within 24 hours and resolve this and to take immediate corrective actions.\n\nPlease be advised that this letter is not intended to be a complete or exhaustive statement of all relevant legal rights and remedies available to the affected parties. I expressly reserve all rights and remedies available at law or in equity.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I was asked to update my expatrio account while still in my country. I updated my account since march1, 2023. I got to Germany since April ,2023. I opened a bank account and when i went to my expatrio portal to start my activation process i realized that i did not have an activate button. I emailed Expatrio customer service May 3, 2023 and i was told that the uppdate process would be completed within two business days. Fast forward to today May 24,2023 i still do not have an activate button and i have not gotten any befitting reply from expatrio support team. I am a student and a stranger here, i need my money to pay my house rent and get basic need for myself. I need to eat to survive. People can not send their hard earned money for a purpose and when they need it the most expatrio starts to play deaf-ear!! The Month od May is about to end and i dont even have money to pay reng or even afford food to eat. This a very bad way of responding to customers. And reading the amount of bad reviews on this website, if i had known i would have used another blocked account. I know you are about to reply and tell me to send message to your customer support team and you will solve my problem. Like you have not seen the countless mails that i have send your support team. Your just give me access to my activation buuton!!! And now my account that showed my balance is now showing a 0.00 balance, and i have not received a dime from expatrio as monthly payment. I do not even have an activate button so where did my money go expatrio? I need response urgently!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It has been almost 2 months since I arrived in Germany and I still haven’t received a single payout from my Block account. I opened a block account using expatrio for my studies in Germany and now I have been here for 2 months and still haven’t received a single payout from my block account I can’t even activate my block accounts and now my funds aren’t even showing up on the application I have been talking to there customer support via call and email and all their response is that they are facing some issues with their banking partner and the issue should be resolved in the next two day and they have been saying the same thing over to me for a month now I can’t even pay my rent or my\nbills my landlord has given me an eviction notice for non payment of rent.This is one of the most pathetic and disrespectful thing a company can do to a consumer and as an international student travelling abroad this is a really huge level of a problem to me but I don’t think expatrio realises or acknowledges that which very disappointing and frustrating I feel like this might even be grounds for illegal activity and I will be talking to the proper legal authorities for the best interest of my finances.\n\nUpdate: There has been still no update or progress in this issue which is very pathetic and disappointing you guys are responsible for ruining peoples lives by doing stuff like this my land lord has evicted me due to non payment of rent I dont have any money left with me at all now I am going to file a police report against this company as I am left with no other choice I made the worst decision to open my block account with expatrio this company shouldnt exist they ruin peoples lives.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It's the worst experience. It's been several months now and I still haven't been able to get my money back, because my visa application was rejected. In March, Expatrio informed me that they had returned the money, but this did not happen, and no amount has been deposited yet. Although I contacted them a lot and left them several emails asking for clarification, but their response is rare, in their last response in 1st May they said ( we contacted our banking partner and asked them to find out where is the transfer pending. We will let you know when we have an update for you ) but it's more than two weeks now and no update. I am thinking that it may be some kind of fraud , I can find no other explanation, all I know is that I have not received my money back until today.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Terrible customer service. Why do you guys promise to reply within 24 hours when you can't do it. I have transferred money to my account and for a whole week now, I haven't heard anything. I am stressed, frustrated and feel scammed. I don't even know what to do now. Nobody should trust this company.\nEdit: They finally replied. I think it's probably because I posted a review. Not good.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I thought it should be \"fast money transfer\" but I've been waiting for 10 days. (Still no contact from expatrio.)", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I just read a previous comment quite similar to my situation. I have been trying to activate my blocked account for almost three weeks now. First two times I even went to the Post Ident and without giving me any response as to why it did not work, finally they replied to my email. They moved the funds to another blocked account, meaning I had to verify myself. It’s been already three whole business days since I updated my documents and no one has checked on them. I have had several blocked accounts with Expatrio over the years, never had I experienced such a bad customer service, lacking on responses and response time almost a week! Please help me fix my issue, it is literally been adding more unnecessary stress to how I am supposed to pay my rent, insurance and food!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Como puderam verificar, responderam meu post original após 5 dias, e com a mesma resposta padrão que dão a todas as reclamações, pedindo contato pelo e-mail do SAC da Expatrio, o qual os relatos aqui de TODOS, é de que não se tem retorno nem suporte. Lamentável", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I'm for almost a month trying to activate my blocked account. The process has failed twice and at the third try expatrio don't know what is going wrong with their bank partner. Every time they take a long time to answer my emails and all the times that I tried to make a phone call it didn't work. I'm almost running out of money and they apparently don't care to solve it fast. I'm still waiting to a solution after many and many attempts of contact by email.\n\nI will not recommend this service to anyone who will depend on their payout to survive in a foreign country.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have been trying to activate my blocked account since last two weeks. First they asked me to verify me personally after that no updates from their side. I'm still confused and not able to activate my account. This was an unexpected experience from Expatrio.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Expatrio NÃO RESPONDE EMAIL\nMeu filho completou 30 dias na Alemanha e o dinheiro completou quase 45 dias na Expatrio, porém após 3 vezes no correio para validar documentos, e-mails diversos, a conta não libera o recurso. No telefone ninguém atende e a promessa de resposta ao e-mail no atendimento ao cliente de até 24 horas não se cumpre e as respostas são subjetivas e vagas. Um absurdo um serviço tão ruim em um pais tão organizado. E pelo que vejo nesse site de avaliações, os problemas se repetem com outras pessoas e as respostas também são padrões (mesmo resposta e pedindo contato pelo email, que eles não respondem).", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "No pensaba escribir una reseña aquí, pero al haber recibido tan mala atención espero que mi experiencia ayude a alguien más especialmente si son de algún país en Latinoamérica. Expatrio tiene el peor servicio al cliente, los correos te responden despues de mas de 4 dias, ni siquiera te lo responden o a veces simplemente te envían un correo automático sin resolver tu problema. Hice la transferencia de mi dinero con más de 2 semanas de anticipación y al llamar siempre me decían que el dinero no había llegado, me vengo a enterar más de 1 mes después de que el AION BANK había rechazado la transferencia y nunca me dieron una explicación razonable del porqué. Casi ocasionan que pierda mi cita en la embajada, es una cantidad exorbitante de dinero y no les importa, lo único que saben decir es que su banco aún no ha recibido los fondos incluso cuando era mentira. Tuve que abrir mi cuenta con Fintiba que al menos fueron un poco más rápidos en su servicio al cliente. Si quieres comunicarte con su operadora de Expatrio tienes que levantarte a las 2 de la madrugada para hacerlo que es el horario en el que abren ya que si te comunicas más tarde simplemente te tienen en espera por como 30 minutos y nunca responden, ningún tipo de empatía con sus clientes sabiendo lo costosas que son las llamadas internacionales. Elegí expatrio pensando que sería una buena opción frente a la competencia y fue la peor de todas. La falta profesionalismo es increíble y mas aun el poco apoyo que brindan. No recomiendo a nadie que utilicen esta empresa, pensé que serían rápidos y ayudarían en caso de problemas y no fue asi, pésima experiencia y espero nunca más tener que repetirla.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I created the account a couple of weeks ago but had a terrible experience with the process. There were delays in the money's arrival, and they have not responded to my inquiries or calls. I didn't know where my money was for almost two weeks, and I had yet to receive a response from Expatrio. In the end, due to the delay in the money's arrival, the account was automatically closed, and the money bounced back to the origin account, and I lost more than 150 euros in commissions. I do not recommend this company for their poor customer service", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Please reply me Expatrio... It's been 2 weeks since I activated my account but you guys rejected saying it's an issue of name order. Nobody has gotten back to me even after multiple emails... I need my money to survive!!!\n\nUPDATE: Funds are in 3 days after review on trustpilot :D Their response seems to be more active on Trustpilot than their mail", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It took three days to activate my blocked account.\nfirst I uploaded a wrong file but after I re uploaded the missing file I waited two days with no response.\nI called them and they immediately activated my account.\nI guess they have forgotten my request.\n\nThe App also not very smooth but it's enough.\n\nWhen it comes to money transfer it's better than other services.\n\nOne last thing they do not accept syrian passports anymore and that is quiet disappointing.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "From my point of view, expatrio is not the best but it is a good option. When I landed in Germany I activated the blocked account but it got updated after 3 weeks compared to people in Fintiba who got their accounts activated in the same week. The response time is prolonged and the app is also not a good support.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I arrived to Germany 1 month and a half ago, so far I have done the activation process 5 times. At first I used video-call method to verify my identity, they claimed the system could not read the new version of the passport, I have a mexican passport and in recent years a \"new version was issued\", the funny part is that I have an old version passport. After that I tried the post office verification, and did not work. They told that my birth place in my passport does not match the one written on my personal data. The customer service is useless, since you have to wait at least one week to get answers. They have never notified any updated about my problem, it is me who has to get in touch to know the recent news. Also  their phone number never picks up, the waiting line has finished my call more times, than the times I have talked to a person. I wished they have the decency to at list give a good customer service", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Expatrio no me ha dado MI DINERO. He intentado verificar mi cuenta 3 veces de la manera correcta y con las instrucciones que ellos brindan en la página, sin embargo su sistema es tan malo que no han podido resolver los problemas por los cuales no han podido desbloquear mi cuenta. Su atención al cliente es pésima, tardan varios días en contestar los correos (en ocasiones ni los contestan) y al llamar por teléfono te tienen más de 20 minutos en espera, al final ni siquiera te brindan una solución. En mi caso reconocieron que yo había realizado el procedimiento de manera correcta y supuestamente ellos se contactarían directamente con el banco, han pasado varios días desde que esto comenzó y no han resuelto nada. Mi experiencia ha sido terrible, ya que ellos son los que tienen mi dinero y yo no he recibido nada, no recomiendo expatrio para nada, su interés en ayudar a sus clientes es nulo.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Because of passport printing issue my blocked account got delayed. Finally expatrio staff helped me after some follow up. Thanks Expatrio", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I transferred the money to Expatrio at January, got my Working Holiday Visa and now that I need to activate my Blocked Account, the Activation button doesn't show. I sent an e-mail for their support, with the transfer proof and telling everything and had no answer, then I called and they kept me in line waiting for half an hour and nobody picked up. I don't what else to do, I need this money to survive in Germany.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "A month in Germany and having did the verification twice and still hasn't got my first batch of money which they claim is \"1 business day\" to process. Gave no reason for that and endless waiting. Wrote by email but did not reply to me lately and no one's on the phone to listen. Rubbish.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am here to express my extreme dissatisfaction with the level of service I have received from Expatrio. Everyone, please think twice before you open an account with Expatrio\n\nAs an international student in Germany, I have been using your company's services for the past few months, including the opening of a blocked account for my financial needs.\n\nHowever, I have been facing significant difficulties in accessing the funds in my blocked account since 1st March 2023, despite following all the necessary procedures and submitting all the required documents. I have been to the post office for identity verification FOUR times, as instructed by your staff, but still cannot activate my account and receive my first payout. It is almost April now, and I am extremely frustrated and anxious about my financial situation.\n\nWhat is even more disappointing is the lack of useful solutions provided by your customer service staff. Every time I contact them, they simply ask me to keep going to the post office and try again and again, without any clear explanation or indication of when I can expect to access my funds. This has caused me a great deal of stress and inconvenience, and I feel that your company has failed to fulfill its obligations to provide timely and effective support to its customers.\n\nI strongly urge Expatrio to take immediate action to resolve this issue and release my funds as soon as possible. (I communicate with the staff via WeChat and the staff replies to my message slowly. They said that they are communicating with the bank which takes a really long time, more than 2 weeks to confirm there is a problem with postident.....Until now 30 March 2023, I still haven't received any solution regarding the problem). I also request that you improve your customer service by providing clear and specific guidance to customers who are facing similar issues, rather than repeating the same ineffective instructions.\n\n I expect better communication and support from a company that claims to specialize in helping international students in Germany.\n\nI totally have no idea when I can receive my funds as it has been 1 month since my arrival in Germany........\nFor Expatrio, Please take action instead of replying to a useless\"thank you\" message.\n\nUpdated: \n2023/04/06\nFinally, I received the email from expatrio and they reviewed my submitted documents which I received the funds on 6th April.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The worse service ever! I'm one month alread in Germany, i can not cativate my account! The answer onle \"we will fix your problem soon\". And this \"soon\" already lasts 4 weeks. Fortunately I have some money with me. I tried to call to support team, but they didn't pick up the phone. Totally don't recommend this service!!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have been trying to open my blocked account since March 1. Since the passport, I have been new and the verification company they have contracted does not have a system suitable for this, I verified my identity by going to the post office. 2 TIMES! I sent a lot of e-mails with this (with screenshots), and they answered me only once. When I call by phone, for some reason they are always busy and never open. It directs you to voice mail. That answer is also a 1-sentence mail. There cannot be such a disgrace.\nPeople trust you and deposit that money into that account. My Current Account and everything else is ready. You have to answer the emails. March is about to end, and I have no money in my account. Don't force people to take legal action. I want my account to be activated as soon as possible because I have sent you every activation path you want with evidence. I want to see my money in my account before 31 March. \n\nNote: Don't send a message thanking you for your feedback, just solve the problem. I have been receiving that \"thank you\" message for 1 month already. Everyone wants results, nor thanks from you.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Such a pathetic service ever. I don't recommend it to anyone. It's been half a month that I have been contacting the Expatrio team via Mail, +49 3025557415.About the Email, they are giving answers to the questions that I don't ask for and about the call, they don't have a proper help line. Because of their mistake my visa extension is at stake. Don't don't goo for Expatrio.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I never go out of my way to upload a bad review but am left with no choice. I have been trying to unsuccessfully activate my account for the past few weeks and each time I try to contact a team member for more information or help on this, it takes them days to get back to you. When they finally get back to you, they reply with a canned response I can find from the FAQ. If you try to call, you wait in line, and it's impossible to get a hold of anyone, probably because they have so many customers stuck in the same situation. Meanwhile my visa application has been approved since March and it's already almost April and I still haven't received any funds. I would not recommend Expatrio to anyone.\n\nUpdate as of March 22,2023: I've finally received my first disbursement. My visa was approved in March and it took 3 weeks to receive funds. The stress was really not worth it.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "This is literally the first time i leave a review on internet, but this is honestly the worst experience i ever have,no one,ever,answer the customer hotline, i have been calling every day in a week, each time took me 20 mins wait time and then they just told u to leave a voice mail,the activation steps are a joke,it didnt work,it wont send u the disburstment,it wont notify u until u send them a email to ask whats wrong, and then u have to constantly waiting for their reply,and they will say the most standard procedure which u did 1000 times already.Nothing,Literally ,Works.The staff doest work, the bank doesnt work ,the customer hot line doesnt work,If u send the money u are basically just like a cuck , hopelessly waiting for mercy of their hands to reply u.Things that can be done in a week can probably take half year to finished. \n\nThis is some next level of bad service,its like the most trauma thing u can have if u use expatrio.\n\nupdate:AND THEY CHARGED U MONEY FOR WAITING IN THE PHONE.I SPENT LIKE 120 MINS AND ALL MY CREDITS RAN OUT", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "By far the worst", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Your connection with TK was very slow and because of it I had difficulty to get my international student ID card on time. If I knew it would take so long I would not have signed in for the Value package.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I hardly write any review anywhere. But I am only doing this because the way expatrio treated my funds and monthly payout is beyond me. I did not receive my payout for this month and it is already 15th of March. They had turned me into a ‘Karen’, they hardly pick up their phone and answer their email. If there is no response, I will follow suit to others people who are in same situation as me; legal pursuit. \n\nPlease do not tell me to email your service dot com. I had emailed a dozen of them and expatrio did not take any responsibility for what is happening to my funds nor taking any proper action to resend my funds to me. \n\nI will not recommend this service to anyone who will depend on their payout to survive in a foreign country.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "This service should be a very simple affair. You transfer the money, activate your account and get a part of your money back every month. It really is not rocket science. However, Expatrio managed to fail at every step of the way until now.\n\nWe have verified our identity online. Got an error message saying support will contact us and provide help. Never happened. Got back to us 5 days later (Quintupling your promised response time), switched the verification method to postal identification. We successfully verified ourselves once again. Again, same error. \n\nYour customer service is the worst I have ever seen. No one ever answers the phone, I have been in your queue every day for 5 days straight, never talked to any of those elusive agents. Nobody responds to emails, and if they do, it is usually a one-line response. Remember, this is only a glorified bank account! How you can screw that up is beyond me. Now we are stuck waiting for your support crew to respond, which will probably take another 5 days.\n\nWe are currently pursuing legal action and have contacted the authorities in Belgium. Hopefully this will stir something soon", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I write this so no one else needs to be in the same situation as I do. I will write my experience everywhere and post updates on the situation. Credited the money in September 2022. Account activation didn't work, no follow-up from customer service. No one answers the phone, and no one replies to my emails sent. Their claim of \"response in 1 business day\" is imaginary. It's completely unacceptable! Consumers pay for your service and your consumers are international students who depend on the payouts to survive. Expatrio fails in the main service it provides. Legal action will be pursued.\n\n\nUpdate: I was asked to redo the verification process for the THIRD TIME. Blocked account got activated and received my funds more than 2 weeks after the initial activation attempt.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "He tenido muchas dificultades porque informan que hay un problema del sistema y no solucionan. Solo dicen que enviaran un recordatorio para que el area encargada arregle el problema. Llevna 3 semanas enviando recordatorios y no he accedido al dinero.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "First of all, its a shame that a big company like Expatrio doesn´t answer phone calls! I tried to call them a many times and they made me wait for around 20 min and at the end they said I had to leave a voice message. I left the voice message and until now I have no answer. That happened several times! I called them because I have sent some e-mails and my problem is still not solved. By the way, they say they usually answer e-mails in 24 hours. Not mine!\n\nMy problem is: I set my blocked bank account  in February, but I have not received my first month's disbursement yet and all the money still in my Expatrio bank account. I read some articles in their website and it was written that after activating your account, \"You will receive your first monthly payment within 2 business days\" and other that said: \"After the verification is complete, the first payment from the Blocked Account will be sent to you. Please note that the money transfer can take up to 3 business days, depending on the processing times of the recipient bank (your bank).\" \n\nSo the deadline is up and i still don´t have my money. Right now, I wouldn´t recommend Expatrio.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I've transferred the funds and got confirmation from the bank that the money was credited. Still no confirmation from them. And they're just ignoring my emails. I Don't recommend them at all.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I opened a blocked account with Expatrio for my studies in Germany. It has been over three weeks since I have attempted to activate it, but I have not yet received my first monthly payout. I strongly advise anyone considering Expatrio as a blocked account provider to look elsewhere.\nEdit: It has now been five weeks since activating my account, and still nothing has occurred. Do not trust Expatrio with your money. I will update this review once the issue has been resolved.\nEdit #2: I have finally received the monthly payouts for my first two months here.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Changed policy mid service and closed all Iranian student accounts. Caused A lot of trouble in the middle of this hardship for our people. Thank you for the support of freedom and humanity!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I cannot log in from my computer even though I have the correct username and password.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have written three emails about three different problems but none of them are not reply until now although I wrote them on weekdays not on Friday or Holiday. The 24-hour support is so bad.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Im having the worst experience with expatrio.\nI opened an account and they approved my details and passport, after that i transferee all the required money for my visa application. Then they said our bank has a problem with your nationality and we cannot process your application. Now after a week i cannot even get my money bank and it is going to cause my visa rejection!!!\nUpdate:\nGot my money back after 1 month, it costed me a lot of time and stress", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Expatrio doesn't share a statement of transactions with its customers.\n\nAfter Expatrio opened my blocked account with Mangopay in Luxembourg, I did multiple transfers and kept uploading the transfer proofs on my user portal simultaneously. However, after alerting customer care about the difference in the amount shown on Expatrio's portal and, subsequently, my repeated request emails for the statement of transactions of the account opened in my name in Luxembourg, Expatrio didn't share proper data. Surprisingly, Expatrio is not able to provide something very basic like a 'statement of transactions' to its customer, which nowadays is easily obtainable with just a few clicks on the user portal of most of the fintech companies/banks.\n\nAlso, it is almost impossible to talk to a customer care representative on their phone support. I often couldn't reach a human representative, despite waiting for almost 20 minutes. Firstly, calling them on their international numbers is so expensive, and getting no resolution, even after spending so much on phone calls, makes me feel so cheated. \n\nThis is sheer unprofessionalism and inefficiency on their part.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I would like to give it a 5 star but unfortunately I had been waiting all day to transfer money to my blocked account. They are claiming to get 06 document for visa on the same day even though they can't verify an account. Which they claim it takes only minutes to be ready. Well it's hard to get 06 document on the same day if I can't transfer any money. The sole reason I choose Expatrio. I e-mailed and ask what is taking so long they said it takes 24 hours to confirm. I'm very disappointed. I don't think they deserve all those comments about how fast and thrust-worthy it is.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I'm not getting my refreal code to share with my friends so I'm not happy really disappointing.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Не вникли в тему. Не посмотрели приложение. Не помогли(", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I haven't received my first pay in my bank as of now", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I had opened a Blocked Account with their Health Insurance benefits package in September 2020. In this package the company had promised a refund of 49€ if I opened a Blocked Account with TK Health Insurance membership. I started my membership with TK after I reached Germany in April 2021 and activated my blocked account. They did not process my refund automatically. I had to hassle with them even for that and my Current account showed 49€ credited at the end of May 2021. I thought that this was the end of it but after I looked at their blocked account disbursal after they paid my last installment, these fraudsters had debited the same amount of 49€ again the same day. I was aghast and wrote two emails to their customer service and still haven't received any response. I guess when they have screwed you anyway why bother with the customer right? In effect they charged me 109€ (approx. 9,500₹) for this effing blocked account even after fulfilling their conditions! Take my word, don't look at the rosy reviews here. It is better that you take another service provider from Germany or open a blocked account with Kotak Mahindra. You will save a lot of money and disappointment. After this, I am going to complain at a German Government Agency that looks after consumer protection.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The services are good, but they reply really slowly. Customer support in special cases is at a snail's pace. They open an account really quickly, but take almost a week to reply to emails? And I am always unable to reach them on the given phone number, despite waiting for half an hour on call. \n\nI would recommend Expatrio only to people who do not have any hiccups in their journey and don't necessarily need a good customer care experience.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "They are THIEVES. I opened an account with them in August to request my visa in September. \n\nI had to go to the embassy before receiving the result of my German exam, due to COVID the response times of the embassy were very long and I was not going to arrive on time at the start of classes. I already had conditional admission to the University and the only thing missing was this exam. Unfortunately I did not get the necessary score and I lost my place at the University. I had to ask the embassy not to continue with my visa process because otherwise it would be denied. \nI asked EXPATRIO for a refund of the money and they removed 109Eur from my money  (49Eur for the currency exchange fee) and then monthly charge of 5euro (which they NEVER notified me that they were going to withdraw). I paid (5541Eur which corresponded to 6678.32 USD and they only returned me: 5959USD). It's unbelievable how much money they STEAL. I lost 718USD just for making a MONEY move. When I write to customer service no one seems to care and they just tell me that those are their policies and fees.\n\nThey are not trustworthy, they are fraudulent, they have hidden charges and NO ONE SEEMS TO REALLY CARES.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "too much fees for students.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I hated Dr. Walter insurance. I had a terrible tooth pain and my tooth had to be extracted. I couldn’t get any support from them, neither could I have my money returned; I couldn’t even activate my travel insurance due to bureaucracy. Dr. Walter barely respond and unreachable through email. They're attitude is autistic and they’re are absolutely ruthless when it comes to the deadlines. I would never recommend this insurance company to anyone, and I feel frustrated how this company was enforced on me through expatrio.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The insurance activation has not happened even after 1 week of providing details. Also there is no way to reach anyone telephonically everything is over email and takes 24-48 hours to get an answer . I am still waiting on the problem To be resolved.\n\nUpdate- I had to finally call the dr.Walter insurance company for activation. And they did it within 30 seconds . Why it was not done after expatrio  sent my details i do not know .", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "After one week of activation of health insurance I didn't get any email from DR Walter. I keep on emailing still no response. I have to submit certificate to college to get my student card.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "They are thieves.  I opened an account with them in February and unfortunately the German embassy didn't give me a date for visa interview until my enrolment passed. When I tried to collect my money in may.  They removed 109 euro from my money claiming it is for closing the account. Meanwhile the charges they announced on their site was 49euro and then monthly charge of 5euro. Going by that they still owe me 45 euro but because they think am not in their country and don't have access to them that they will eat my money.  They are not trustworthy,  they are fraudulent and they have hidden charges. THIEVES", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I havent received my 49 euro cashback yet.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Everything is good except customer service. I had to change my blocked amount from 861€ to 947.10€. I tried 2-3 times and even wrote some mails to which I didn’t receive any response. I had also attached the email I received from embassy in my email. Then I came to know from their website that the maximum amount that can be requested is 947€. Then, i requested them to change the amount to 947€, which the expatrio team swiftly changed it within a day.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I opened an year long blocked account  with them last year. Account opening and the process of providing additional documents such as health insurance went smoothly. \nBut problem started afterwards, they initially promised to offer a lot of freebies, such as liability insurance, ISIC card and repatriation insurance in the so called “Value Package” but later refused to provide these additional services. \n\nIf I ignore the case of this aforementioned false advertising, the experience with blocked account was rather smooth. I received all disbursements on time except the last one, which they sent few days early and closed my account. \nI intended to extend my blocked account, but when I opened the expatrio portal few days before the usual disbursement date, to my dismay, the account was already closed from their end. And for the extension account, I would have to pay additional 49 Euros and set it up as a new account. No thanks! \n\nAnother negative aspect of this company is their predatory business practices. Through articles on Degis, same founder as Expatrio, they oversell their product, and try malign other blocked account providers. “Degis” claim other operators  use banks outside of Germany, and that isn't in accordance with German residency law(False information). All fully licensed Banks in EU have a license to operate in Germany and are perfectly fine.\nAnother outrageous claim is that they open the account in Germany in student’s name in BNP Paribhas or Commerzbank(False, they open it with a Fintech company(Mangopay) in  Luxembourg, which doesn’t even have a full banking license and obviously no deposit insurance to speak of). \n\nRecently, a scam by the blocked account provider, BAM has been uncovered. Given the many shady business practices of Expatrio, I highly doubt I would consider them for another term.\n\nPS: Still the best blocked account provider though,", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It is all good but, there is no interface to deal regarding the errors. My address is wrong in the documents. There is no one to be contacted.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Quick and easy process, BUT when it comes to transferring money be careful what option you choose. Choose the option of transferring EUR not your own currency it will save you a lot money. Make sure you calculate which option is the cheapest because the are big differences in the exchange rate depending on what option you choose. So pay attention to save yourself from paying too much.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Expatrio system has put wrong DOB on both travel health insurance of mine and since i logged a ticket it's been more than 48 hrs, but no response. Very disappointed in their service when customer's visa is on the line because of the system mistake which has not been recorded and correct as of now.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Very very slow service. They don't reply to mail.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Transaction fees are high\nI sent 10541 and 31.55 € in total 10572.55€ excluding the fees charged by the sender bank. Now, I have 10516€ in my account. I think you should inform users about how much the transactions will cost in total beforehand.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Return my friend's hamis Shareef Khan money back.  He has been waiting a month now.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Didn't give pay out from the starting of visa. Only gave for 3 months", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Fast response by the call center, but a bit expensive in my opinion", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "In general the service is fine but I did not was satisfied with the info. offered regarding the emission of the confirmation PDF and the process between the senfmding of fund and arrival of them to the blocked account. The information is not clear enough (timing, waiting time...)", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I was in the trouble for verifying my visa.\nIn my case, there is no need to get a visa in advance, but it was compulsory to upload the visa scan.\nI stuck in 3day on this issue but there was no advice or helps.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The customer service is very bad. I have asked at least three times by email to know the status of my insurance application, and they have not answered. I still don't know if I'm covered by the insurance after applying 2 months ago.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "PROS:\n- They respond to emails faster than their competitor.\n- They made a mistake but at least solved it after some back and forth communication.\n\nCONS:\n- They keep making mistakes.\n- They run a referral scheme so a lot of the reviews and referrals you see are financially motivated. \n- They host a fishy site called DeGiS which does comparisons between Expatrio and its competitors where they subtly make Expatrio come out as the better deal. I gotta give to them, I fell for it! They're good!!\n- They'll try to sell you services like CohortGo during your registration process. More ways this broker tries to get any penny they can. Brokers be broking.\n\nOVERALL TIP:\nAvoid them. Do your blocked account with another competitor and get your health insurance directly from the health insurance company! CUT THE MIDDLE MAN.\n\n______________________________________________\nDETAILED REVIEW:\nWhere do I start? Expatrio are so good at incorporating scam-like yet legit marketing methods that I can't really help but respect their efforts and skills.\nThey got me real good with their DeGiS comparisons because they seemed so genuine and accurate.\nHowever, the best comparison I found was that of my own. I used Expatrio and another competitor (check my other review) and after 2 months in Germany, Expatrio seems to be the worse out of the two.\n\nThe first issue I had with Expatrio was when I tried to open a blocked account. I had the money and I wanted to do it quickly, but they tried to sell me a payment service called CohortGo as a \"faster and cheaper\" way to pay. It was anything but. If not having expatrio as a middle man, imagine if that broker himself had another middle man! But they just try to get as much money from you as possible by getting you to use CohortGo.\nI fell for CohortGo at first but when it came to actually transferring my money, I emailed them and requested to transfer directly. They reset my account.\n\nWhile waiting for their reply though, I used the service of another competitor and opened a blocked account with that competitor instead. I'm in Germany now and have had no problems with the competitor's blocked account, even though Expatrio claimed in their DeGiS comparisons that the competitors has problems A, B and C. Quite misleading indeed because none of these problems were true for said competitor based on my experience.\n\nI still however used their TK insurance and they made another mistake and they sent TK a false university start date so I got overcharged for a month (other trustpilot reviews seem to have the same issue!).\nI didn't bother to contact Expatrio at this point because a classmate of mine had several issues with Expatrio and advised me to contact TK directly. Cut the middle man!\n\nTo conclude, Expatrio is a broker and just like any other broker, you'd think they're provide you with services and products when in fact YOU are the product. They make money from commissions when they bring you, the customer, to a company.\n\nI'll say it for the third time; CUT THE MIDDLE MAN!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Its good for people below 30years of age as everything is smooth. However if you are above 30 years and a student, value pack is not recomended. The reason is the certificate which they provide for private health insurance was rejected by my university and i had to urgently buy Mawista insurance seperatly. There is very little and uncleared information availible in their portal about Dr walter health insurance. If you contact for clarity, they take ages to respond. After all this unclear information if you choose to buy any other private insurance, in that case they will not give you 49euro cashback as promised.\nSo if you are above 30,value pack is not advised.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Verification is not done in 24 hours after uploading my passport.Contact support didn't also answered to my requests yet.When I am calling their contact phone, it is always busy", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The service itself is good, but activation of Blocked account requires a proof of address, which is unreasonable requirement for students with unstable accomodations or traveling between Universities in the first weeks.\nMonese is not a German bank so the IBAN was rejected in some cases.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have been trying to reach one of your help desk agent for weeks. But unfortunately no one is answering my calls. I know you are too busy but in my opinion you have a great issue with your help desk department.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Too much time for responding, processing and update each step. Nobody answers the phone also, so support is only by email. In the end all the services fulfilled but after long time. I would recommend to be prepaired with money for one month at least.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Mixed feelings / 2.5 stars.  \n\nThe customer service is fast but not always effective. I sent over a years worth of funds for my blocked account in order to study in Germany. Expatrio gave me the impression that I would have access to them right away (as soon as I was in Germany). It took almost 3 months, and several emails before I finally got my first disbursement. Luckily I have other savings. If I was relying on my blocked account for those 3 months I would have been screwed. \n\nI already lived in Germany at the time that I applied for my blocked account and instead of this speeding up the process it seemed to slow it down. All of the instructions on their website assume you are outside of Germany and don't have a VISA at the time of applying. \n\nDisorganization: \n\nThe links they send in their emails are broken - like the link to the user portal that they include in every email just opens into a broken link. I emailed to tell them and no one did anything to change it. The FAQ's did not address my issues and I had to email several times to get updates to figure out why it was taking so long to access to my own funds. \n\nThe website and email interactions were disorganized. I was asked to send the same document multiple times. I had to upload it to the website and then email it again.  They asked me to upload a bank statement when there was already one uploaded. \n\nThe positives: Expatrio has a quick customer service response and are recognized by the German visa office when applying for a student visa. \n\nTheir business partner in disbursement, Monese unfortunately has literally zero customer service. Monese never answered a single phone call or responded to a single email (I called and emailed several times). I questioned if Monese is a scam service at some point because they have an automated chat but seemingly no human people working for their customer service department. I really question why Expatrio chose them as a partner as it makes everything seem more like an untrustworthy scam to take your funds. I was prepared to get a lawyer to seek legal action against either Monese or Expatrio because it was taking so long to get access to my own funds and no one was updating me on why it was taking so long. I wondered if I just lost a years worth of money to these websites. \n\nThe good news is, you can link your blocked account from Expatrio to a Germany bank and not Monese, which may be easier since most Banks will at least respond to your emails if there is a problem. \n\nFinal Verdict: Expatrio is functional but takes much longer than I expected to get the job done, and is pretty disorganized at getting the job done if you already live in Germany.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Account opening and transfer of money was very smooth and easy. Got everything at a single place for a decent price but the problem was unblocking the account which took very long because monese current account wasn't being activated.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Expatrio team is wonderful, but the package that i brought is included Monese. Monese app and team are unresponsive, take a month to reply without helping solve the problem.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It was fast but everything was not clear but also automatic system could be even faster", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I'm still waiting for my blocked bank account. I will update my review if it will be fast as they say 😎", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Every service has at least a problem. Slow response. I still have not receive any feedback regarding my issue with Monese.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Initiating transfer to the INR account (both online and offline option) kept getting failed, multiple times over multiple days. The error only shows \"something went wrong\" and offers no useful information on how to even attempt a solution. Contacting the service centre was not also helpful.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Transferred the money on Monday and never got the confirmation letter within 24 hours as advertised or within minutes like the other reviews and they never reply my email. My visa appointment is tomorrow morning and I'm frustratingly waiting for the letter. Chose Expatrio over other service provider because they seems to be the most reliable and the quickest, but now I'm just disappointed.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Pros:\nMoney transfer and confirmation of block account is very fast.\nCons:\nBut they usually reply very late even in case of urgency.\nFastest money transfer option(In india, local transfer with Electronic Aa2 form) incurres high conversion rates as compared to other conpetitors. \nTheir FAQ section has very little information.\n\nNote:i do not have any experience with other BA providers.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The package they are offering within the amount is alluring. But it also comes with a loophole that is, they have horrible customer service. I've waited 5 days to get an answer to my query before I switching to another provider, but unsurprisingly Expatrio never replied. The claim they make in their website is absolutely bogus, they will never reply within 24 hrs.\nI would have given a negative star but sadly it's not an option...", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have decided to go with Expatrio rather than Coracle or Fintiba, as it seemed the quickiest one. On their website it is written \"We give you confirmation documents as soon as we receive the money transfer\". Don't buy it, it is not true! \n\nMy experience so far is a lot different than what I expected. I have successfully transferred the money to my blocked account using Transferwise (which is their recommended partner). And I am still waiting for confirmation!\n\nI can't get answer to my e-mails. The questions I've sent 2 days ago are still not answered.\n\nI have bought international phone call package, just to call Expatrio's customer services. But they don't bother to answer the phone. I have a visa application in 2 days, and I have to get the confirmations ASAP. \n\nWhen I was talking to other companies, their customer services was A LOT quickier than this. It was not what I expected with Expatrio. Unfortunately, I regret choosing Expatrio. They are not there to help you when you need the most.\n\nI still hope to get the confirmation before my visa appointment. Otherwise, I will really be in trouble..\n\nEDIT: Soon after my review, they reached out to me and fastened the process. I specifically would like to thank Gabriella from customer support, who was very willing to help me.\n\nEDIT2: After my arrival to Germany, I have applied to activate my current and blocked accounts. It's been 3 days, but my activation request is still in review. \n\nMy landlord is waiting for my payment, I am waiting for my current account to be opened to make my transactions! \n\nFor a fresh expat, you need things to be quick! But Expatrio is again very slow!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I opened a blocked account for my visa application as a student. Until covid 19 crisis all was good. Due to covid I didn't travel to Germany and I've been struggling trying to close my blocked account and get my money back. I've to wait for 5 months until the german embassy reopen again, to ask for a permission to close the account.However, despite of I sent all the documents more than 1 month ago, I hadn't received my money back, and they didn't gave any explanation. I'm still waiting to get my money back.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Bad service. I have waited more than 2 weeks and couldn't get proper blocked account confirmation document which could be accepted by the visa Personal. The call support works only at morning or afternoon, exactly do not know when.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "A nightmare initially. All has been resolved amicably now.\n\nI opened a Blocked account for my father-in-law, after being asked to do so by the local Ausländerbehörde. He is already resident in Germany, and is living here legally. Due to the COVID situation his \"Aufenthaltskarte\" is already expired and the office is behind with its backlog of work. \n\nI opened the blocked account no problem, but now Expatrio won't activate it because his residence card is expired. This despite the fact that the German alien authorities have released a press release to say that anyone who applied to renew residence card before the lockdown is legally here, until a decision is made. For him, as a dependent of an EU citizen, only the security of livlihood is needed. I gave Expatrio this evidence, and pleaded with them to activate his account, as he needs the money!! After speaking to a customer service rep last week, no reply, I cannot get through and when I leave answerphone messages to call back, nothng happens.\n\nThe processing time for residence cards in Germany is 3 months upwards. He cannot access his money until they activate his account, and that requires that the new card arrives!!! Crazy!\n\nOur case has well-and-truly \"fallen through the floorboards\". Feel let down, that no one there cares less, now that the money is securely in their account. \n\nNo idea when he will have access to the money that by right he should already be able to access!!!!\n\nUpdate on 21st July 2020:\nA friendly lady from customer relations called me, and listened to my experiences with Expatrio. She apologised on behalf of of the company, and assured me that lessons will be learned (and this should not recur). Thankfully account activation has happened and the first disbursement has been made. Thank you Expatrio for following up with me. Faith has been (partly) restored.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "some marginal expense that charged me more", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "the speed to open a blocked account is ok, but the speed to get a reply from customer service to activate the account is unacceptable.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Never buy the value package\nThe monese they provide said my account no problems, TK said  cannot directly debit account. \nAnd i think Expatrio should be responsible for this situation.\nThen i contact Expatrio and after two weeks they told me to contact TK by myself (?) \nSo regretful", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "If you are planing on using expatrio as a blocked account to apply for a Visa in Germany, I highly recommend you to reconsider. I chose expatrio believing it would mean a quick and simple process I could do from my home country before going to germany and it has been the complete opposite. I'll try not to get into details, but the highlights of my issue with expatrio are:\n\n-It works with Mangopay, a bank located in luxemburg. Not being a german bank, a certificate from this bank requires a clarification that they have a partnership with a german bank. The blocked account confirmation does not provide such clarification.\n\n-Instead of solving the problem directly, expatrio told me that my university should solve the problem for me. My university had never had anything to do with my visa aplication\n\n-I was transfered three months at once on my first transfer, before being able to solve the problem, so now when I ask for the residence permit, the certificate will show three months less than what I had originally transfered to expatrio.\n\n-Closing the account and opening another one in a german bank would take around a month, time in which my current residence permit would not be valid anymore\n\n-Customer service hasn´t really been helpful, just redundant and without providing a clear solution", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have issues with :\n1. Activating my current account. Took 1 month for just activation.\n2. Activating my blocked account. Took 1 week after activation of current account\n3. Transferring of the monthly blocked account amount to the current account. Took Another 3-4 days to just transfer the amount from blocked account to current account. \n4. Yet to get Insurance health card from TK. The process is delayed due to whose fault is still unknown.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "They have worst support and they don't understand what is meaning of 48 hours, they think 48 hours = 2 weeks.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Expatrio is the worst amongst all the blocked account providers. They don't care about their customers and their customer care is pathetic.\nPlease don't take expatrio's service, or else be ready to regret later.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I really had great expectations from Expatrio. And when I was in my country the application and transfer of the funds to my blocked account was swift and filled me with confidence that the procedures in Germany will be simple and swift as well. But all of my services were delayed to a limit where I was totally helpless and had barely 25 Euros left in my wallet. Even though everything was done on time on my behalf. The products are really good, no doubt but in the way they were provided it was really poor. \nPlease don't do this to students who had left their homes to a far away foreign land to be able to study. It's a serious issue and I am saying very sincerely.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The process of blocked account activation could've been better. I still haven't received all of my product such as the stay safe insurance(liability insurance).", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "very slow reply and poor customer service via phone and email. i opened account on 31 july, but done on 27 august, in between i need to wait for few days for each reply, and expatrio gave me a wrong IBAN which caused me 10 days for 06 block account confirmation. until now i did not get a free ISIC, monese also cannot be set up. what a mess. kindly hire more people to improve your business service,", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I am so frustrated with Expatrio, I really do not recommend getting any kind of insurance through them, only the blocked account if you must. I have never received any of the student ID or other insurance cards that I got as a part of my package with them. For the health insurance, they give you a piece of paper that says you are insured by TK with a \"personal ID number\" that actually was refused at doctor's office because they called TK who said this number did not exist. After over 2 months of emailing with Expatrio about getting my insurance card, they finally said they would send my information to TK to activate my insurance. Over one month after that, I never received my card in the mail, and called TK directly, who told me that Expatrio actually never sent any of my information to them to activate the account. When I called Expatrio helpline, they were so unhelpful and told me all these things weren't their problem and they don't know anything about TK, they just sell their insurance, and hung up the phone. So incredibly frustrating and incompetent...I will make sure to keep my friends away from this company and their problems.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It took a lot of time after my arrival in Germany to get the first disbursement.\nReally disappointed, big time.\nCustomer support is not satisfactory at all.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "My first experience with Expatrio was good, I had no problems setting up a Blocked Account and received my money quite easily and on time. However, when I had to extend my blocked account for a second year, it was complete chaos! The instructions to extend the account were unclear and when I transferred the money they said I transferred it to the old account (even though I followed the instructions by downloading the documents with the account number) and it took them almost a month to give me a solution. That meant I had to figure out where to get money from for an entire month, the same month I was to ask for the renewal of my visa (which I was carrying around expired for a week because of the delay on the Sperrkonto documents)... That was no fun.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Slow service. I still haven’t received many services like ISIC card and the travel insurance denied my claim for lost items. Where is my ISIC card and why was my claim of lost items denied by ONE", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The services are cost efficient and well planned.Thanks\n\nBut the processing time and people Behind the customer services are not empathetic or responsive at all.\n\nI mailed you in the situation of emergency and you have replied me next week saying that I will be getting my own money next to next week.\n\nGod .I even can't express it in words.\n\nExtremely frustrated by the irresponsible behavior.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Dint get the disbursement of my first block amount on time even uploading the documents on time.\n\nI am suffering from few health issues and cannot go to the doctor as I did not get my health card on time even after uploading documents on time.\n\nWhenever called the helpline usually it was busy.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Slow processing times. The customer service it’s hard to contact and they often take “longer than usual due to high amount of applications”. They are holding all the money that you will use for your payments once you arrive in a foreign country. Never again", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It took more than a month to unblock the money!!  N I hvnt got my health insurance card yet... While blocking the money Expatrio suggested transferwise to transfer money which took hell lot of time and that lead to problems in my visa process.. Also expatrio suggested Monese current account and then after 2 weeks of opening the Monese account, expatrio said they r facing issue with monese so go for another bank which again takes time as, German banking system is too slow.. In a nurshell I will say Expatrio should never promote vendors about whom they don't have clear idea because I faced lot of issues by trusting expatrio for transferwise n Monese.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I have been in Germany for about a month now and I was given my two (first) payments (September and October) well into October. I arrived to the country on September 16. The documents needed to start the process for transferring were given to Expatrio two weeks ago. Now, whenever I called I would be told that they had too many applicants. I don’t know how that can be an excuse given the fact that all the money is transferred to Expatrio in advance and they know they amount of applicants they will get per semester. It’s a great paid service, a cheap service, but still paid, they should know better.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It took a lot to have my money for september and october. Also, I called a lot to ask and they said something first and then the opposite so I’m not really happy with the services. The only thing they said was: “there’s a lot of costumers waiting just like you” But if you know that on September/October a lot of costumers or students will come and ask for their money, you should be prepared because I’m paying for a service.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I haven't received my first month block account money !!!!!!! it almost been a month, and i didn't get a reply email !!!!!!!!!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Honestly I am not having a good experience with the company. Payments are not well organized and more than once I had to remind you to make the monthly deposit. The first payment of my account extension took one more month, even though you confirmed me two months before I was getting the money by first days of September. Lack of professionalism as well, need more formality if you are managing other people's money.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Expatrio forgot to review my documents somehow, so I could't get my first money. The problem was solved after I called them personally. They were nice and then processed the problems quickly.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Everything was fine, until the first disbursement transaction, since they said it would take 3-5 days since the day they confirmed my activation documents and it actually took more than 2 weeks.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Now I am living in Germany and I needed a blocked account to renovate my residence permit, so I decide to open with Expatrio because it was suppose to be quickly. The problem is that to active the blocked account I need to submit the visa, so I sumbitted my residence permit but is going to expire in 1 month, because of the sooner expiration date I was asked to submit my new residence permit but it is going to take 1 extra month to arrive.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Too slow to get my first money and I haven’t got it now", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I've sent the money. and waiting to get the confirmation more than 2 weeks.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "I still didn't receive a blocked amount confirmation of receiving the fund", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Opened my account, they can't locate my transfer after multiple calls I still have not received anything and my appointment is on the horizon, tried to contact Mangopay and could not get anything from them. I hope they will be able to solve my issue soon!!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Expatrio recommended using a money transfer partner called TransferWise. TransferWise debited $9,500 from my account then deactivated my account. My $9,500 has gone missing and TransferWise hasn't responded to multiple emails. Please save your money and don't use Expatrio or their partners or your money may go missing as well! I have opened a dispute with my bank and hopefully the money can be recovered. But why risk it? Use a more reputable bank and transfer partner!\n\nUpdate: In response to the comment below, I have tried several times to call your number but it doesn't accept calls from Skype or Google Voice so I can't actually speak with anyone. I will attempt to resolve this over email.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The blocked account part was easy and smooth, but activating the health insurance and Dr. Walter insurance is taking a long time to get a response from the people asking for information. Also, expatrio informed me that I can use a copy of the health insurance certificate at the doctor so\nI don’t have to pay, and this did not work. Meanwhile it is taking a long time to get my insurance card and I have not been given any info about how to get reimbursed for my medical expenses.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "The mail promise is seriously inconsistent with the actual situation.  The mail promises that the remittance will arrive in two days, but in fact far exceeds this deadline.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "They take very long to respond and never answer the phone.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Took almost a week to get my 05 account opening confirmation. The service team even only replied me once a day, and the reply was totally useless.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Service reply is slow, and the reply for cancellation request is too bad to convince customers.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "Not good. not profi", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Expatrio", "t": "It was kind of hard to do the money transfer through transfer wise, and through the bank i sent it, it arrived almost 2 weeks after i has sent it.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "One of the worst companies I have ever dealt with. They keep deducting monthly fees under the description “Account Maintenance Fee,” and the amount is different every time. When I contact them and ask for an explanation, they do not respond to my emails.\nLast month, they deducted €20, and this month they deducted another €10. My friends are experiencing the same issue, with some of them being charged even higher amounts, reaching €70 per month.\nI gave them a one-star rating, and if I could give them less than one star, I would.\nI am not responsible for maintaining your service or account, so why should I be paying maintenance fees? There is no clause in my contract stating that I am required to pay such fees.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Dear Fintiba,\n\nI am following up regarding my withdrawal request and the emails, tickets, and inquiries I have submitted, none of which have received a response.\n\nIt has now been 53 days since the initial payment, and I have still not received the Confirmation Letter. Therefore, I kindly request the immediate withdrawal and refund of my funds to the original sender’s account.\n\nFurther delays are unacceptable. This situation has caused significant stress and has negatively affected our student’s personal and academic circumstances. Please treat this matter as urgent and confirm when the refund will be processed.\n\nI look forward to your immediate response.\n\nFintiba Tickets:\nAug 28th -> 1344984 (Formal Complaint and Urgent Request for Withdrawal of Funds – Account 862-062-871)\nAug 11th -> 1325152\n\n\nFIB tickets with no response received yet: \n\nJul 23rd -> 7965 (Follow-up on “Mittelherkunftstransaktionen” and Withdrawal Request), \nAug 10th -> 10099 (FIB Formal Complaint and Urgent Request for Withdrawal of Funds – Account 862-062-871)\nAug 28th -> 9011 (FIB Formal complaint and urgent request for Fintiba Account withdrawal and full refund (Account Closure - OTP verification issue)), \nSep 1st -> 10279 ([FIB Frankfurt International Bank AG] Re: Re: Follow-up on “Mittelherkunftstransaktionen” and Withdrawal Request)", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "They did well. But didn't like the procedure of the webinar. Questions and Answers session should have come after the compressive lecture but in this case it was questions from the beginning of the webinar to the end.\nThough my own questions were not even attended to.\nBut generally Fintiba tried by putting up such a Webinar.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I absolutely do NOT recommend Fintiba. Their service is a complete disaster. Despite contacting them multiple times and submitting the required documents through three separate requests, they failed to provide me with the document I urgently needed for my German student visa application. Their terrible communication, lack of responsiveness, and sheer incompetence caused completely unacceptable delays.\n\nBecause of Fintiba’s failure to do their job properly, I missed my university intake and now have to start the entire admission process again, losing months in the process. When you handle services that are essential for international students and visa applications, this level of incompetence is simply unacceptable. Stay away from Fintiba. I strongly advise students not to trust this company with anything related to an important visa deadline. I would never use Fintiba again and I absolutely do not recommend them.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Extremely disappointing and frustrating experience with Fintiba.\n\nWe have been waiting for more than 45 Days for the confirmation of the blocked account documents. Despite repeated phone calls and emails, we received little to no meaningful response or timely support.\n\nToday, my sister went to the German embassy for her visa appointment, and her visa was ultimately rejected because the required blocked-account confirmation was not available. This situation has caused serious stress, wasted time, and potentially significant consequences for her plans to come to Germany.\n\nWhat is especially unacceptable is that we repeatedly tried to contact Fintiba and asked for help, but our concerns were not handled with the urgency such an important immigration document requires.\n\nWe are now considering filing a formal complaint with the relevant regulatory authorities, including BaFin where applicable, and exploring all available legal options.\n\nI strongly recommend being extremely cautious and making sure you have sufficient time before relying on Fintiba for documents that are critical to a visa application. In our experience, the communication and handling of this matter were completely unacceptable.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I opened a Fintiba blocked account on 08.08.2026 (Order ID 2063571) and transferred EUR 14,059.00 by SWIFT on 12.08.2026, fully traceable via UETR. My complete Source of Funds documentation was submitted on 24.08.2026, at which point the portal status changed to \"Approval Pending - Your documents are in review\" and no further action was possible on my end.\n\nSince that date, despite multiple emails and phone calls, I have not received a single substantive update, not even confirmation that my complete file was received or forwarded to FIB. A call on 25.08.2026 revealed my file had not yet even reached FIB. A follow-up call on 28.08.2026 was told it has now been sent, but with no written confirmation or expected date. Three separate support tickets (1331283, 1340064, 1341086) remain open with only automated replies.\n\nI understand enhanced due diligence applies to my case and I am not disputing that. My concern is the total absence of communication or a stated timeline, well past Fintiba's own published 1-2 week guidance for this step. I have escalated formally to FIB directly and will pursue BaFin and the Bundesbank Schlichtungsstelle if this remains unresolved.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "My experience with Fintiba is too bad.\nI transferred €12,170.00 to my Fintiba blocked account on July 9, 2026. It is now August 31, 2026 — nearly 2 months — and I still have not received my blocking confirmation. Fintiba requested additional Source of Funds documents. I submitted everything immediately and completely and still didn't receive my blocking confirmation. This delay is now directly endangering my student visa and my Bachelor studies at TU Dortmund, which start in October. The university is waiting for me, but without the Blocking Confirmation I cannot complete the visa process. in addition to that my language certificate will not be accepted by the embassy by November 1st.\nI kindley request releasing the needed Blocking confiramtion.\nSupport Code at Fintiba: 704-990-269\nTicket at FIB bank: 9097", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Disastrous 2-month delay! Funds held since June, jeopardizing my Visa interview!I am a professional Dentist whose life savings (€13,343) have been completely held up by Fintiba and Frankfurt International Bank since June 18th, 2026. My transaction shows \"Expired / Approval Pending\" for no reason, and nobody is responding to my urgent requests. My official German Visa interview is on September 22nd, and this administrative neglect is destroying my future. I need my Blocking Confirmation (Sperrbestätigung) ISSUED IMMEDIATELY.Ticket Number: 1291843", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "52-Day Delay: Source of funding and blocked account documents completely stalled.\nNo Communication: Team refuses to answer phone calls or reply to direct emails.\nUseless Bots: Customer service relies entirely on automated bots repeating generic scripts.\nVisa Risks: Unacceptable processing times cause extreme stress and threaten strict deadlines.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Fintiba is a nightmare. Never use them! I transferred my money on June 30th from Russia. They did not say anything for the first 3 weeks. After that, they asked for 2–3 new documents every week to check my funds. I sent the last documents on August 16th, and now it is total silence again.It is impossible to talk to a real person. I am almost kicked out of my university because I cannot get health insurance without the block confirmation. They do not give any deadlines for the check. Nothing is clear. This is the worst service ever.Because of this, my visa documents are stuck at the consulate since July 1st. I do not know when this will end. All my plans are ruined. Even if the university keeps my place, I cannot arrive in Germany on time for the semester. I wrote a complaint to their support, but it is useless. Tomorrow, I will write an official complaint to BaFin (the German financial regulator) and put Fintiba's office in copy. They cannot work like this. They should close down or start working normally. I have no patience and no energy left! \nMrs./Ms. Anna Shagina\nSupport code:  913-967-361", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ticket 1334500 – Dringende Mitteilung über Betrag für das Sperrkonto\n\n\n\n\nSehr geehrtes Fintiba-Support-Team,\n\nich beziehe mich auf das Ticket 1334500, das seit dem 18. August offen ist.\n\nIch habe mich heute Morgen telefonisch bei Finiziba erkundigt. Dabei wurde mir mitgeteilt, dass die Bearbeitung des Sperrkontos bislang nicht abgeschlossen werden konnte und ich mich bezüglich der weiteren Vorgehensweise direkt an den Support wenden soll.\n\nDer für das Sperrkonto bestimmte Betrag ist bereits bei Fintiba  eingegangen. Da die Eröffnung des Sperrkontos weiterhin nicht abgeschlossen werden kann, möchte ich Sie hiermit freundlich, aber dringend bitten, meine Situation   schnellstmöglich zu bearbeiten , da das Geld sogar aus Frankreich stammt und entpricht nicht der Überprüfung der Geldquelle , die Sie zwingend vorführen möchten \n\nDa das Ticket bereits seit dem 18. August offen ist und wir den Vorgang dringend abschließen müssen, wäre ich Ihnen sehr dankbar, wenn Sie die so schnell wie möglich veranlassen und mir kurz bestätigen könnten, wann diese erfolgt.\n\nVielen Dank für Ihre Unterstützung und die schnelle Bearbeitung.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Fintiba is ruining my studies. I am already enrolled, and my classes start on September 7, 2026. Their support team told me that a routine \"Source of Funds\" check takes up to 2 months! They are holding my money and refusing to issue the Blocking Confirmation, which makes it impossible to get my visa on time. I have officially submitted a formal complaint to BaFin against Sutor Bank/Fintiba regarding this unreasonable delay. My Fintiba ID is 2029314.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I’m a student from Russia who just wants to go study in Germany. Let me tell you about my \"fantastic\" experience dealing with Fintiba.\n\nFriends who moved last year recommended Fintiba to me — back then everything went smoothly. I trusted them and didn’t bother checking the current state of affairs. Turns out that since April this year Fintiba introduced strict rules for verifying the origin of funds for people from ‘high-risk countries’ — AND SAID NOTHING ABOUT IT ANYWHERE. So if you think you’ll just quickly deposit your savings, get approved in no time, happily apply for your visa, and fly off to study on schedule — think again! Instead, they’ll first demand proof of the origin of your funds, and once you provide it, a long and agonizing silence begins. Meanwhile, you’re rapidly losing your chances at both the visa and your studies. And it’s painfully obvious that nobody cares — not about your plans, not about your life, not about your money. Oh, but don’t worry, they’ll still charge you the fee — apparently that money is perfectly legitimate to them.\n\nI can understand it when you’re HONESTLY warned that document review will take several months. But when Fintiba cheerfully sends you notifications saying “hurry up and deposit your money into your account” — that looks like deliberate deception and theft.\n\nAfter reading through chat forums and learning that Fintiba doesn’t approve submitted documents for months on end, I started to panic. My money was taken and blocked, and I couldn’t apply for my visa. Thankfully, my parents were able to lend me money, and I opened a blocked account through a different company (starts with “Edu”, ends with “Bao”) — they got everything done in a single day.\n\nI’ve been trying, unsuccessfully, to close my Fintiba account and get my money back, but:\n1.\tThe button in the phone app simply doesn’t work (lol)\n2.\tWhen I try to close the account on the website, a message pops up saying “Can’t close account right now, please try again later” — and this has been going on for almost THREE WEEKS\nNaturally, emails to support don’t work either — just endless silence. They simply stole the money and went quiet.\n\nI WOULD NEVER RECOMMEND THIS COMPANY TO ANYONE, EVER!\n\n* If any Fintiba representatives happen to read this, here’s my Support code: 794-595-463 — in case you’d like to actually respond to my inquiries before I file a complaint with BaFin.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Too much charges", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "My blocked account confirmation has been pending for over 70 days, and I still have not received anything.\nMy ticket number is: 1344448", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ich habe vor 20 Tagen Geld auf mein Fintiba-Sperrkonto überwiesen. Obwohl die Überweisung von Berliner Sparkasse kam und ich habe alle benötigen Unterlagen hochgeladen, wurde plötzlich ein Herkunftsnachweis verlangt. Der Support meinte nun, dass die Prüfung 1 bis 2 Monate dauern kann. Für ein digitales Konto ist so eine lange Wartezeit absolut inakzeptabel, besonders wenn man auf das Geld angewiesen ist. Sehr enttäuschend.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "This is my third and last review of Fintiba.\n\nNot because my problem was solved — it was not, even after multiple calls, emails, Instagram comments, and reviews here.\n\nIt is because I am giving up on communicating with this company. They do not respond via email, and their answers over the phone or in replies here are just brushed off. I am filing a complaint against them and FIB (who are not answering either) to BaFin in the middle of next week, demanding a full refund. This includes the €159 Fintiba service fee; I am not going to pay any fees to a company that has only caused me stress and panic attacks.\n\nThey do nothing to improve their support, and most of the positive reviews here are from their free webinars, not from actual usage of their services. Think twice, three, ten times before choosing Fintiba — choose another service instead, as there are plenty of options available. \n\n(long story short: they are holding my money for 2+ month without any adequate reason and do not release my blocking confirmation, which is essential for my visa)", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am currently in a serious visa situation because of Fintiba. I finished my studies and urgently need my blocking confirmation for the Ausländerbehörde. My account contains the full required amount of €13,092, but I cannot obtain the necessary document.\n\nI have sent multiple emails in German and English and called multiple times. Every time I call, I am simply told to “write an email,” but my issue remains unresolved while my visa application is being delayed.\n\nFor a service specifically used by international students for residence permits, this is extremely disappointing. I urgently need Fintiba to properly review my case and provide a solution.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Sehr enttäuschende Erfahrung mit Fintiba\n\nDie von Fintiba angegebene Bearbeitungszeit von 3–4 Wochen ist inzwischen abgelaufen, trotzdem habe ich noch immer keine Sperrkonto-Bestätigung erhalten.\n\nDie Botschaft verlangt dieses Dokument ausdrücklich für meinen Visumantrag; die von Fintiba vorgeschlagenen Ersatzdokumente werden nicht akzeptiert.\n\nMein Studium an der TH Deggendorf beginnt am 1. Oktober 2026, sodass jede weitere Verzögerung meinen Studienbeginn gefährdet.\n\nIch erwarte von Fintiba endlich eine konkrete Lösung und die unverzügliche Ausstellung meiner Sperrkonto-Bestätigung. Andernfalls werde ich mich erneut an die BaFin wenden und die Schließung meines Kontos prüfen.\nTicket Nummer: 1346244", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "They took my money and won't give it back. Zero support.\n\nFintiba literally took my money and locked it up. I haven't received my money back.\nI’ve been submitting support tickets for over 3 months, but I have never received a single reply from a real human. There is basically zero customer support.\nTheir document upload system makes no sense:\n To unblock the account, they demand both the front and back of my visa document.\n But their app only lets you upload ONE photo.\n If I upload just one side, an automated bot rejects it for missing the other side.\n If I combine both sides into a PDF, the bot rejects it for being a PDF.\nThey offer no actual solutions and just keep spamming automated bot rejections. I’ve reached out dozens of times, and nobody ever answers. Do not use this company.\n\nTicket 1346167", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "My experience with fintiba is very bad I am waiting for the blocking confirmation more then 2 months now because of source of fund is pending no approval although I have submitted necessary documents to the case \nTickets 1339211", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Fintiba took my Money and refuses to send them Back. I would like to share my experience with Fintiba. After i transfered my blocked amount, fintiba intitated Moneylaundering Check (altough i did Transfer from Germany!). I refused to give ans documents (because this Check can lasts multiple months), and wanted to Open a blocked Account with other firm. But now Fintiba refused to give my Money Back (As they emloyee Said, because of some \"Bug\"), and they Just hold my Money without any explanation. I dont understand, if they suspect something about Money laundering, Fintiba obliged by the law to Transfer Money Back. But now my life can be ruined because of this company. You Play with peoples lifes! My support Code is 1341709, maybe someone from Fintiba team still has some Heart in them.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Order ID: 1968101\n\nMy funds have been on the Fintiba blocked account since the end of June 2026. All Source of Funds documents were submitted long ago. \n\nDespite multiple follow-ups, Trustpilot complaints, and even a formal complaint to BaFin, I still have not received the Blocking Confirmation.\nThe only replies I keep receiving are generic messages that the case has been forwarded to FIB Compliance. No concrete timeline, no clear status, and no decision.\n\nThis delay is now directly endangering my student visa and my Master’s studies at the University of Jena, which start in October. The university is waiting for me, but without the Blocking Confirmation I cannot complete the visa process.\nAfter more than two months this is no longer acceptable. I urgently need either the Blocking Confirmation or a full refund and account closure.\n\nSofia Plakhina", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Your team promised to review my case, but I still haven't received any response.\nI provided all the necessary documents confirming the legal origin of the funds back on July 30th. More than a MONTH has passed since then, and no decision has been made.\nI have written again and again, but I still haven't been able to get a response. The situation is becoming very critical: my studies begin in September, and this delay is directly threatening my plans. Without confirmation of the block being lifted, I cannot obtain a visa!\nI urgently request that you escalate my case and provide a resolution.\n\nSupport Code: 932-776-105", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Открыла блокированный счет для ребенка, отправила 13251 евро в июне 2026 года. С 16 июня отправила три пакета документов для прохождения так называемой \"проверки происхождения денежных средств\". Никакого результата за два месяца не получила и 13.08.26 написала письмо о закрытии счета и полном возврате денежных средств в течение 14 календарных дней. На 27  августа деньги не были возвращены, я не получила на моё письмо никакого ответа, ни о получении моего письмо Fintiba, ни сроков возврата. Просто тишина. Прошу всех очень хорошо подумать прежде чем связываться с Fintiba, чтобы не оказаться без денег и полностью сорванными планами. Сейчас мы без визы, без понимания что делать ребенку в этом году и с рисками потери денег, оплаченных за год языковых курсов, простаивающей квартирой в Германии и рисками потери денег отправленных в финтибу.\nI opened a blocked account for my child and transferred €13,251 in June 2026. Starting on June 16th, I submitted three sets of documents to complete the so-called \"verification of the origin of funds.\" I received no results for two months, and on August 13th, 2026, I wrote a letter requesting the account be closed and a full refund within 14 calendar days. As of August 27th, the money had not been returned, and I have received no response to my letter, no indication of receipt from Fintiba, no refund deadline. Just silence. I urge everyone to think very carefully before contacting Fintiba, to avoid being left without funds and completely ruined. We are currently without a visa, with no idea what to do for our child this year, and are facing the risk of losing the money we paid for a year of language courses, an unused apartment in Germany, and the risk of losing the money we sent to Fintiba.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I don’t know what to do, it absolutely nightmare! The verification and response times are horrendous. They don't reply to my messages for two weeks, which is why everything is dragging on so long, I'm absolutely exhausted! My mother LEGALLY receives her salary in cash. You need to verify ONE document to confirm this, close all the verifications, and give me blocking confirmation! Please!\n\nTicket  1292501", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "ich habe ein Sperrkonto bei Fintiba eröffnet, Mein Cousin hat zwei Überweisungen getätigt  aber die zweite  wurde blockiert mit der Begründung ich müsse die Verwandtschaft nachweisen.  Ich habe alle Dokumente geschickt, Ausweise, Gehaltsnachweis , alles von meines Cousins.\n\nDas ist jetzt  mehr als einen Monat her, Nichts passiert! Ich habe mehrmals geschrieben und darum gebeten entweder  endlich zu prüfen oder Geld zurück an meinem Cousin zu schicken, Fintiba reagiert nicht.\n\nIch bin wirklich verzweifelt.  So etwas habe ich noch nie erleb", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Dear Fintiba \nI hope you reply to this review \nI have been waiting the confirmation of my \nblock account for 3 months and i got nothing \nI sent all the documenta you asked for , all the documents that relate to the funds and i got nothing \nMy sister and my brother in law transferred the money to my block account since 03.06.2026\nAnd i had my interview at the German embassy\nIn Jordan in 24.06.2026 they told me they will wait me to get my confirmation till 10.07.2026\nAand i got nothing, i email the support team in fintiba  alomat every day and they tell me to wait more , the german embassy gave me another deadline to get the confirmation till 23.08.2026 and still the same i got nothing \nMy brother travelled from Hamburg to Frankfurt \nJust to get some information  they told him you have to wait \nMy visa is about to get rejected and i’ve been stressed out for almost 3 months please help me ,my study journey is on the edge because of this, i had my language course already booked in germany and spent already alot of money there , and the amount of money in my block  account is complete i’m just waiting the confirmation. \nTicket\n1340470\nThanks you so much \nI hope i got your answer soon", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "No support. I couldn’t send my transfer receipt and helpless support.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "One week ago, I wrote a review regarding my concern with my blocked account and the pending Source of Funds verification. At the same time, I also contacted Fintiba Support by email to explain my situation.\n\nI received a response from the support team informing me that the verification process could take 3–4 weeks. They also advised me to provide the transfer receipt and account opening confirmation to the German Embassy as supporting documents, which I did.\n\nUnfortunately, the embassy informed me that these documents were not sufficient and that they specifically require the official confirmation of the blocked bank account, as well as the insurance confirmation.\n\nI am therefore writing this updated review because I have also sent another email to Fintiba explaining the latest situation with the embassy, and I am hoping to receive an update as soon as possible. My studies and visa application depend on receiving the necessary confirmations.\n\nI would kindly like to know:\n\n* If any additional documents are required from my side for the Source of Funds verification.\n* Whether the documents I have already submitted are sufficient.\n\nI completely understand that compliance and verification procedures take time, and I am willing to provide anything else that is required. However, because my visa application and studies depend on these confirmations, I would really appreciate it if the support team could review my case and provide an update as soon as possible.\n\nI hope Fintiba can help resolve this matter soon. Thank you to the support team in advance for your assistance.\nTicket number : 1324132", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I transferred the required funds to Fintiba/FIB on 10 July 2026 for my German student-visa application and completed the requested verification process. However, after 46 days, I still had not received my blocked-account confirmation or been able to recover my money.\n\nI attempted to use the withdrawal function several times, but the process repeatedly failed during OTP verification and displayed an “invalid” error. I also contacted Fintiba through its support channels, but I did not receive a satisfactory response or a clear explanation of the delay.\n\nThis has seriously affected my German student-visa application and put my Master’s programme, scheduled to begin on 1 October 2026, at risk. The blocked-account confirmation is an important part of the visa process, so delays of this length can have serious consequences for international students.\n\nI have submitted a formal complaint to BaFin and am seeking an urgent resolution. I hope Fintiba will improve its communication, restore a functioning withdrawal process, and resolve affected customers’ cases promptly.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Hello,\n\nYou replied to my previous Trustpilot review stating:\n\n“Hello,\nWe’re sorry to hear about your experience and completely understand your concern.\nOur team has responded regarding your case. Please check your inbox (and your spam folder, if necessary). If you have any further questions or need additional assistance, please don’t hesitate to reach out.\n\nBest regards,\nTeam Fintiba”\n\nHowever, I have carefully checked both my inbox and spam folder, and I have still not received any response regarding my case.\n\nFor identification:\n\nName: Emiliia Dantsker\nDate of birth: 21 October 2003\nTicket: 1293210\n\nI have now been waiting for the cancellation of my insurance for more than one and a half months. Please review my case again and provide me with a clear and substantive response.\n\nFor context, this is the message I previously sent:\n\nDear Fintiba Team,\n\nI have been trying to resolve the cancellation of my insurance for more than a month and a half. Despite repeatedly providing the requested documents and following your instructions, the issue is still unresolved.\n\nMy TK public health insurance has been valid since 1 April 2026, while I only entered Germany at the end of June. I have already sent the official TK confirmation several times. Your employee specifically told me that proof of alternative insurance was required to cancel MAWISTA Visum, and I provided this as soon as it became available.\n\nDespite this, €95 was already charged for August, even though I informed you at the beginning of July that I no longer needed this insurance and asked for the matter to be resolved before 1 August. I am now also being asked to pay approximately €170.\n\nThe private insurance was originally arranged for me by mistake. From the beginning, I clearly stated that I was a Master’s student at a German university, yet I was provided with private insurance that did not meet my university’s requirements.\n\nI only discovered this at the end of the enrolment deadline, when my university informed me that the required statutory insurance confirmation had not been received. I then had only one day to arrange statutory insurance with TK in order to protect my enrolment.\n\nThis was also not the first serious issue I experienced with Fintiba. My source-of-funds verification took around three months, with repeated requests for the same documents and documents that do not even exist in my country. My parents and I spent more than €600 on translations and related documentation, and these delays significantly affected my relocation and the beginning of my studies.\n\nThroughout this process, I responded promptly, provided all requested documents and followed the instructions given to me. In return, I experienced long delays, repeated requests for documents already submitted, template responses, an incorrectly arranged insurance policy and now additional financial demands.\n\nTo summarise: my source-of-funds verification took around three months, delaying my relocation and studies; I was provided with private insurance that did not meet my university’s requirements; and I had to arrange statutory insurance within one day to protect my enrolment. I then followed your instructions regarding cancellation and repeatedly provided proof of my TK insurance. Despite this, the cancellation is still unresolved, €95 has already been charged, and I am now being asked to pay approximately another €170. I do not understand why I am expected to bear the financial consequences of problems that were not caused by me.\n\nIf this issue is not resolved correctly, I will submit formal complaints to the relevant authorities together with the complete correspondence, submitted documents, insurance confirmations and payment records. I will also submit a complaint to BaFin regarding the handling of my source-of-funds verification.\n\nI have treated Fintiba and its employees with patience and respect throughout this process. I now expect a clear, substantive response and a final resolution of this matter.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Update: Das Problem wurde endlich behoben, dank der herausragenden Leistung seitens von Sutor Bank, und des Fintiba Customer Support Teams. \n\nIch nutze Fintiba seit Jahren und war immer zufrieden. Aktuell ist es leider ein Desaster.\n\n​Seit fast 30 Tagen warte ich vergeblich auf die Auszahlung. Hab jetzt mehrere Mails geschrieben. Jedoch gar keine Antwort bekommen. Hoffentlich wird man nicht rechtlich eskalieren müssen um das eigene Geld ausgezahlt zu bekommen. Somit 1 Stern. \n\n​Standardisierte PR-Antworten von Fintiba unter dieser Bewertung bitte ignorieren. Ich werde hier selbst explizit ein Update geben, sofern das Problem gelöst wird.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Honestly i liked how exact every important information about transfer details are shown in the app. But the speed of transferring the money into my account is pretty low. It's almost 2 business days that my account balance isn't updated. I hope your team will find a solution to that.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Please Resolve My Case\n\nVery disappointing experience with Fintiba.\n\nMy name is BRIAN SHOKAH FONYUY. My support/reference number is 751-100-871.\n\nI am currently waiting for source-of-funds verification . I submitted the required information on 7/8/2026, but I am still waiting for the matter to be resolved.\n\nThis is particularly stressful because I am a student preparing for my German visa application, and delays with the blocked-account documentation can directly affect my visa timeline, and my extend into my university enrollment date if something is not done urgently.\n\nI have already contacted support, but I need this case to be properly reviewed and resolved rather than receiving generic responses.\n\nFintiba, please locate my case using the information above and contact me with a clear update and resolution.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have now been waiting for almost two months for my compliance review to be completed, despite having submitted all the requested documents.\n\nThis situation is extremely stressful because I need my blocked account confirmation to proceed with my visa application for Germany. Such a long delay is particularly difficult for a student whose study plans depend on this document.\n\nI understand that a verification process is necessary, but almost two months of waiting is far too long without any concrete solution.\n\nI sincerely hope that Fintiba will finally review and complete my case as soon as possible.\n\nTicket: 1276707", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "​I am writing this review out of utter frustration. I returned to Bangladesh and requested Fintiba to close my blocked account, providing my Abmeldung and Passport Exit Stamp. They informed me that they couldn't release the full remaining funds without the Sperrfreigabe.\n​Right after receiving their response, I immediately emailed them back asking to at least continue my regular monthly payouts until I could arrange the Sperrfreigabe.\n​It has been almost 2 months now, and I have received NO proper response from human support. I have not received my July monthly payout, nor any update on my account. Whenever I email them, I only receive automated generic replies. I have sent multiple follow-up emails, but my urgent requests are completely ignored.\n​This level of delay and lack of communication is unacceptable. Please look into my case urgently and resume my payouts at least.\n​Name: Meherun Nessa\nFintiba Support Code: 284-560-285\n​", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I transferred and blocked my money (12500 EURO)on 30 July 2026, and it has now been 26 days without any confirmation of my blocked amount. I have never experienced this level of mental stress in my entire life.\nFor international students, this confirmation is essential for visa applications and university deadlines. The continued delay, uncertainty, and lack of communication have left me extremely anxious. I am now genuinely afraid that I will miss my university enrollment deadline because I am still waiting for the final blocked-amount confirmation (Sperrbestätigung). \nWhat makes the situation even more frustrating is that Fintiba has not replied to any of my emails and has not answered my calls. I have sent multiple emails, included my ticket number, and provided the requested information, yet I have received no clear update, explanation, or support. \nTicket Number :1311912, 1313994, 1323207, \nNew update(27.08.2026): Finally received the block account confirmation.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Hallo,\n\nseit mehr ein 8 Wochen warte ich immer auf die Bestätigung des Sperkkonto. Mein Studium Start ist für Oktober geplant und bis jetzt keine Rückmeldung.\nTrotz mehrerer Anruf wurde mir immer gesagt, zu warten.. !! Das geht überhaupt nicht !! Aktuell ist mein Studiumstart gefährdert!!! Ich erwarte eine schnelle Rückmeldung ihrerseits, sonst muss ich leider eine Klage gegen Sie einstellen... Das geht Überhaupt nicht..\nMeine ID Nummer : 585-569-261\n\nGruß", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I deposited the required funds to my Fintiba blocked account on 11 August 2026 for my German student visa. Today is 25 August. Fourteen days later, my account is still not verified, and Fintiba is now the sole obstacle to my visa application for my Bachelor's studies at starting in Ocotber 1st.\n\nThe facts, in order:\n\n• 11 Aug: Funds transferred.\n• 12-14 Aug: All requested documents uploaded, and proof of source of funds demanded despite the funds coming from a European country.\n• 14, 17, 19, 22 Aug: Four separate follow-up emails to support. Zero substantive replies.\n• 15-24 Aug: My university admission letter was rejected FOUR TIMES for \"verification\" — despite being an unconditional admission accepted by the university, and despite my subsequent proof of full enrolment, which I also uploaded. As I had to contact health insurance without their support, I couldn't depend on them.\n• 25 Aug (today): Fifth call to support. After I gave the agent my ticket number and it looked as if she was going to help, I was put on hold for 8 minutes and then the line was disconnected.\n\nI still have no blocked account confirmation nor travel insurance and no updates. Both documents are legally required for my visa file. Both are entirely blocked on Fintiba's side.\n\nFintiba markets itself as fast, reliable, and student-friendly. The reality is that the funds are sitting untouched at your partner bank for two weeks, silence from support, opaque document rejections, and 5+ phone calls with no help whatsoever. And I can tell I am not the only person facing this.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "They didn't even open my documents 🤬", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "am a student preparing to move to Germany, and my visa is currently being delayed only because Fintiba has not completed my Source of Funds verification.\nThe full €4,063 has already arrived in my blocked account. My sister funded the transfer, and I have already provided all the documents requested for the verification.\nIt has now been more than three weeks. I have emailed Fintiba multiple times, and my sister has even called them from Germany several times. They respond to other emails, but whenever I ask specifically about the pending verification, I get no meaningful response.\nI understand that compliance checks are necessary. I'm not asking them to skip the process. I just want my documents to actually be reviewed and to be told if anything is missing.\nMy visa, university plans, and entire move to Germany are now depending on this one document.\nLiterally the money is being held hostage right now. I am so speechless.\nSUPPORT CODE- 225-504-056", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have been waiting four weeks for Fintiba to complete the Source of Funds verification for my blocked account.\n\nThe funds were credited to my account on 22 July 2026, and I submitted the complete set of requested documents on 27 July. Fintiba stated that the verification would take 1–2 weeks. Four weeks later, I still have no decision and no clear indication of when the process will be completed.\n\nI have contacted Fintiba support several times and asked for the case to be escalated. I also contacted the bank responsible for the account directly. Despite this, I have not received a clear explanation for the delay or a concrete timeframe.\n\nI understand that Source of Funds checks are necessary and that compliance reviews can sometimes take longer than expected. However, when a company states a processing time of 1–2 weeks, waiting four weeks without a meaningful status update is difficult to accept, especially when the service is being used for a time-sensitive visa process.\n\nThe main issue is not simply that the verification is taking longer than expected. It is the lack of transparency and the inability to get a concrete answer about when it will be completed.\n\nSupport ticket: 1328104", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Hallo Fintiba-Team,\n\nleider bin ich sehr enttäuscht von Fintiba. Der Kundenservice ist sehr schlecht und überhaupt nicht zufriedenstellend.\n\nIch habe bis heute keine Bestätigung bzw. die erforderlichen Unterlagen für mein Konto erhalten, obwohl ich diese dringend benötige. Mein Termin bei der deutschen Botschaft ist bereits morgen früh, und durch diese Verzögerung könnte meine berufliche und persönliche Zukunft erheblich beeinträchtigt werden.\n\nIch habe lange gewartet und immer wieder auf eine Lösung gehofft, aber bisher wurde mein Problem nicht zufriedenstellend gelöst. Für mich ist diese Situation sehr ernst, da eine solche Verzögerung direkte Auswirkungen auf meine Zukunft haben kann.\n\nIch erwarte eine sofortige Lösung und eine schnelle Zusendung der fehlenden Bestätigung bzw. Unterlagen.\n\nBitte kümmern Sie sich dringend darum. Diese Verzögerung ist für mich nicht akzeptabel.\nAbd Alkader Ahmad\nGeburtsdatum: 15.03.2000\nPassnummer: N03119122", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am extremely frustrated with the complete lack of responsiveness and urgency from Fintiba's compliance team.\n\nOur funds were transferred on August 3rd and credited to the account on August 10th. On the exact same day, we uploaded all required \"Proof of Source of Funds\" documents. It has now been two full weeks, and our files remain unreviewed while our Blocking Confirmation is withheld.\n\nWhat is outrageous is that you are holding nearly €12,000 of our money while citing a multi-week refund timeframe, effectively trapping us and completely blocking our ability to switch to another service provider. Our visa appointment and relocation timeline are now at severe risk solely due to this internal backlog.\n\nHolding critical funds while refusing to process submitted compliance documents in a timely manner is unacceptable for a service handling time-sensitive relocations.\n\nI demand that senior management or an escalation specialist review my uploaded documents immediately and issue the Blocking Confirmation without further delay.\n\nTicket 1320094, 1340432", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "They are so slow.\nSo many people had problems with the embassy because of Fintiba", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Am unable to proceed with the deposit.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Dear Fintiba Team,\n\nI have been trying to resolve the cancellation of my insurance with you for more than a month and a half. Despite repeatedly providing the documents you requested and following your instructions, the issue is still unresolved.\n\nI have already sent my TK insurance confirmation several times. My TK public health insurance has been valid since 1 April 2026, while I only entered Germany at the end of June. Therefore, I was already fully insured with TK at the time of my entry into Germany.\n\nYour employee specifically told me that in order to cancel MAWISTA Visum, I needed to provide proof of alternative insurance. As soon as I received the official TK confirmation, I sent it to you. Nevertheless, instead of receiving a proper decision, I continue to receive repeated requests for the same documents.\n\nBecause the cancellation has still not been processed, €95 was already charged for August, even though I informed you at the beginning of July that I no longer needed this insurance and asked for the matter to be resolved before 1 August. I am now also being asked to pay approximately €170, and I genuinely do not understand why I should be financially responsible for a situation that was not caused by me.\n\nThe private insurance was originally arranged for me by mistake. From the very beginning, I clearly stated that I was a Master’s student at a German university. Nevertheless, I was provided with private insurance that did not meet my university’s requirements.\n\nI only discovered this at the end of the enrolment deadline, when my university informed me that they had not received the required confirmation of statutory health insurance. Until then, I had been informed that everything regarding my insurance was in order.\n\nAs a result, I had only one day to arrange statutory insurance with TK. Fortunately, TK provided the necessary confirmation within one day. Otherwise, I could have lost my enrolment for that semester and potentially my opportunity to study in Germany.\n\nThis was also not the first serious issue I experienced with Fintiba. My source-of-funds verification took approximately three months, with repeated requests for the same documents, template responses and requests for documents that do not even exist in my country. My parents and I spent more than €600 on translations and related documentation, and the delays significantly affected my relocation and the beginning of my studies.\n\nThroughout this entire process, I acted responsibly and promptly. I answered your requests without unnecessary delay, provided documents as soon as they became available, followed the instructions given to me by your employees and always communicated with your team respectfully and patiently.\n\nIn return, I received long delays, repeated requests for documents I had already submitted, template responses that did not properly address my case, an incorrectly arranged insurance policy, and now additional financial demands.\n\nI have fulfilled my responsibilities as a customer at every stage. I therefore expect the same level of responsibility, attention and professionalism from Fintiba.\n\nInternational students already face a stressful relocation process and rely on services like Fintiba for professional support. Unfortunately, despite doing everything required from my side, I have experienced months of delays, repeated errors and additional charges.\n\nTo summarise: my source-of-funds verification took around three months, delaying my relocation and studies; I was provided with private insurance that did not meet my university’s requirements; and I had to arrange statutory insurance within one day to protect my enrolment. I then followed your instructions regarding cancellation and repeatedly provided proof of my TK insurance. Despite this, the cancellation is still unresolved, €95 has already been charged, and I am now being asked to pay approximately another €170. I do not understand why I am expected to bear the financial consequences of problems that were not caused by me.\n\nIf this issue is not resolved correctly, I will submit formal complaints to the relevant authorities, together with the complete correspondence, submitted documents, insurance confirmations, payment records and other evidence. I will also submit a complaint to BaFin regarding the handling of my source-of-funds verification, which involved repeated requests, significant delays and substantial additional expenses.\n\nI have treated Fintiba and its employees with patience and respect throughout this process. I now expect Fintiba to treat my case with the same seriousness, responsibility and respect.\n\nI expect a clear and substantive response regarding this matter.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "A terrible experience with this bank so far; I have been waiting for two months, and the proof of funds has not yet been verified", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Unacceptable Delays Jeopardizing My Visa Timeline\n\nI transferred the full required amount to my closed blocked account and uploaded all requested documents and proofs immediately. However, I am still waiting for the crucial confirmation of funds.\n\nMy file cannot withstand any further delays. I have a language certificate timeline of 5 months, and every day wasted here threatens my entire schedule. I have invested significant money and effort into preparing everything for my embassy appointment, and I cannot proceed without Fintiba's confirmation.\n\nFintiba must take the urgency of these situations seriously. They need to adhere to their stated processing times and expedite their reviews. We, as customers, have no more time or energy to waste on these unnecessary hold-ups. This is extremely frustrating.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I'd like to share my experience with Fintiba.\nI used this company to open a student account for my studies in Germany. Initially, I encountered no problems with either registration or sending funds to the account. A real nightmare began after money reached my account. The company began verifying the sources of my funds instead of confirming the account block. Of course, I provided them with all the requested documents without any questions. However, Fintiba refused to even provide an estimated timeframe for document verification. Fintiba’s employees assured me that I simply had to wait. The contract with the company specified a maximum document verification period of three weeks. Two months have passed since then, and I still haven't received confirmation of the account block. I can't find out the status of the document verification, becuse technical support responds only a month after sending them an email. There are also no stated verification deadlines, and there's no way to find out. I've tried every possible way to contact the company, but the situation hasn't changed or any information has been obtained.\nThis situation threatens to disrupt my student visa application process. I consider Fintiba's actions fraudulent. I particularly highlight the incompetence of their customer support and the inadequate verification timeframe. I do not recommend using this company, as there are organizations that can resolve all account opening issues within 24 hours.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am extremely disappointed with my experience with Fintiba.\n\nMy Source-of-Funds verification has been delayed for weeks, despite the fact that I have already submitted the documents requested by Fintiba. My visa appointment is approaching, and my university semester starts on 1 October 2026, yet I still have no concrete solution.\n\nWhat is particularly frustrating is that I keep receiving responses that do not actually resolve my problem. In their latest response, Fintiba told me that the verification could take another 3–4 weeks and suggested that I present my transfer receipt and account-opening confirmation to the German Embassy.\n\nThe problem is that these documents are not the official proof of a sufficiently funded blocked account that I need for my visa application, and I am concerned that the Embassy will not accept them as a substitute for the required Sperrkonto confirmation.\n\nI have repeatedly explained the urgency of my situation, but I still have not received a concrete, visa-usable solution from Fintiba. I cannot simply wait several more weeks while my visa process and university enrolment are at risk.\n\nIf this situation is not resolved urgently, I will have no choice but to file a formal complaint with BaFin and provide the relevant documentation concerning the delays and the handling of my case.\n\nFintiba needs to understand that this is not just an ordinary customer-service issue. The delay is directly affecting my German visa procedure and my university studies.\n\nTicket: 1339195", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I submitted all the required documents on July 17, 2026. After waiting for about a month, I was informed that additional documents were required, but they did not specify which documents were missing or what exactly I needed to provide.\n\nI have sent several emails asking for clarification, but unfortunately, I have not received any response so far. The lack of communication and the long waiting time have been very frustrating.\n\nI hope Vintiba can improve its communication with customers and provide clear information about any missing documents and respond to emails in a timely manner.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Six weeks and still no refund of my own money\n\nI closed my blocked account on 11 July 2026 and was told it would be refunded. It is now six weeks later and I still don't have my €6,958.70.\n\nI opened three separate support tickets (#1291092, #1300468, #1309747) between 11–28 July with no real answer. On 29 July I was told the reversal failed due to a missing account number on their end, and was asked to sign and return a payment order — which I did the same day. Since then: silence. I called the hotline repeatedly and only got through after two weeks, on 14 August, and again on 19 August — both times I was told an \"escalation email\" would be sent to the technical team. Nothing has changed.\n\nI've now filed a formal written complaint (Ticket #1335950) with a documented chronology. If this isn't resolved by 28 August, I'll be filing with BaFin and the banking Schlichtungsstelle.\n\nIf you're considering Fintiba for your blocked account: ask yourself what happens when you want your money back, not just when you're paying it in.\n\nUpdate 22-Aug-2026: With remarkable nerve, Fintiba is now acting as though my payment transfer order — sent to them weeks ago on 29 July 2026, and which they simply never processed — only reached them on 22 August 2026, testing their customer's intelligence in the process. As of 22 August, they are claiming by email that they need two more weeks to process it. However, as proven by the recorded call center conversation dated 14 August 2026, that same order was already in their system as of 14 August 2026 — and I'm not even claiming it was in their hands earlier than that, because for weeks they simply refused to respond to my emails, precisely so they could never have to acknowledge it and could legally delay starting the process! I hope they put their business acumen to better use. 28 August 2026 — marking two weeks from the aforementioned 14 August call — is the final deadline for my money to be sent to my account, as also stated in the formal complaint letter I sent them. Any information, claim, or action communicated in writing or verbally after this date will be handled by the official authorities in Germany.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I opened blocked account at Fintiba for my son who was minor at that time, when he turned 18 which is majority age he opened his own Fintiba blocked account and i transferred funds to his account. But since then his payouts have been frozen yet money is blocked to his account. Fintiba system keeps rejecting documents due to address verification failure witout further guidance. Yet, they may be able to see that account was opened on behalf of my son and that address evidence should not be in my name. And in my view, they can contact us and do it manually. Every issue is not solved by AI bot!!!human interaction is necessary sometimes depending on issue. But no clear guidance provided!  I found Fintiba support very weak to resolve that issue and my son even went to their office making a travel of more than 5 hours in train but they didn't assist him till now. Money is sitting on account for two months now. And he is a student totally depending on that money sitting in account.\n\n I advise other parents not to use  Fintiba if they find other options/alternatives. Very weak customer support!!!!!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I opened a blocked account with Fintiba on June 28, 2026, with great hope that everything would go smoothly and that I would be able to submit my visa documents on time. The required amount of 12,000 euros was fully credited by July 24, but I was then asked to provide documents proving the origin of the funds. In response to that request, I submitted all the necessary documents on July 30, there was no delay whatsoever on my part.\nMore than three weeks have passed since then, and I still have not received a decision or even an approximate timeframe. I have called and written again and again, but have not been able to get a decision. Meanwhile, time keeps passing, and I have a strict deadline for submitting my documents to the embassy. If I don't make it in time, I risk losing the university place I have worked toward and hoped for, for so long. I have spent a great deal of money and resources to pursue this goal, and now only this single issue stands between me and my dream. It would be extremely painful if this one problem were to derail all of my plans.\nI'm completely desperate and truly do not know what to do. I sincerely ask someone from your team to look into my case. My entire education is genuinely at stake right now. \n\nMy Support Code: 705-218-367", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Extremely slow and unclear source-of-funds verification.\n\nI transferred my funds at the end of June 2026 and submitted the requested proof of source of funds on July 7.\n\nUnfortunately, the required documentation was not clearly explained from the beginning. The support team was also very slow to respond to my questions, and when I did receive replies, the answers were often unclear and did not fully explain what was required.\n\nAfter waiting for about a month, I was asked to provide additional documents. I submitted the requested information, but I am still waiting for the verification to be completed.\n\nThis delay has had a serious impact on my plans. All my other documents were ready, but without the required blocked-account confirmation, I cannot proceed with my visa application. As a result, I have already had to postpone my travel plans, and there is now a real possibility that I may not be able to travel during 2026 at all.\n\nI understand that source-of-funds checks are necessary for compliance reasons, but the process should be transparent from the beginning, and customers should not have to wait weeks only to discover that additional documents are required.\n\nVery disappointing experience.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Sehe gehrate damn und haree \nIch war mit dem Webinar zufrieden, es hatte aber keinen Bezug zu meinem Fachgebiet. Ich hatte es wegen dieses Gebäudes ausgewählt. Ich stellte einige Fragen, erhielt aber von den anderen Teilnehmern keine Antworten, die sich auf dieses Gebäude bezogen. \nQais", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Unklar, wann die Bestätigung eingeht, da die überweisende Bank die Zahlung bereits bearbeitet hat.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am extremely disappointed with Fintiba’s handling of my payment. I transferred EUR 10,900 on 07 August, but the amount has still not been credited to my Fintiba account despite having valid SWIFT payment proof.\n\nThe payment is still showing “Not Started” at the beneficiary bank, and the delay is creating serious problems with my German student visa process and university enrolment. For international students, these payments are time-sensitive, and such delays can have a major impact on their future plans.\n\nI have requested Fintiba to trace the payment and provide a clear update, but the situation remains unresolved.\n\nI understand that bank processing can sometimes take time, but when such a large amount is involved, customers deserve clear communication, transparency, and timely support.\n\nI sincerely hope Fintiba improves its payment-tracking and customer-support process and resolves my case urgently.\n\nPayment: EUR 10,900\nDate: 07 August\nTracking Number: b98a4165-c997-46a7-ba97-dbfd00495f98\n\nI would not recommend Fintiba to students until they improve their handling of payment delays and communication.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have been trying to resolve a critical technical issue with Fintiba since July 24th, 2026. My app interface contains a system error where my payout start date has been mistakenly set to 2028 instead of starting immediately, completely freezing my blocked account payouts.\n\nI have already submitted my official residence permit (valid until February 2028) via email. However, I have received no meaningful response to my support ticket (#1329811) for weeks. Furthermore, the \"Book a Call with an Expert\" link in the app throws a \"Bad Request\" error, leaving me with zero customer support.\n\nI am currently in Germany without access to my living funds due to this internal bug. I need an operator to manually fix my payout schedule and release my funds immediately.\n\nUPDATE:\nSince there has still been no resolution or response to my ticket (#1329811) and I remain without access to my daily living funds, I have officially submitted a formal complaint against FIB Frankfurt International Bank AG / Fintiba to BaFin (Federal Financial Supervisory Authority) under Complaint ID No. 222652. I expect an immediate manual correction of my payout start date and the release of my pending funds.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I transferred the money for my Fintiba blocked account so they have not yet released the blocked account confirmation. They asked me for documents on verification of funds and I sent them. It took like two weeks before they answered by the compliance team telling me the documents are incomplete. Later I sent the documents the compliance team asked me through the ticket number they gave me. I sent the documents and the compliance team has not replied to me for more than two weeks now.So I called the support team and they asked me to send some documents through the support team email, but I did not include the ticket number which the compliance team gave me. A new ticket was made and only automated emails have been sent asking for more time and it has been over one week now.I need a manager to manually pull my documents from the new ticket, apply them to my original compliance case, and release my official Blocked Account Confirmation immediately.\nOriginal Compliance Ticket: [8344]\nNew Support Ticket: [1328964]", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I’m really disappointed with my recent experience with Fintiba.\nMy last payout was due on 31 July, but I still haven’t received it. This was supposed to be my final payout, and the Fintiba app currently shows “No next payout registered.”\nI have contacted Fintiba several times by email, but unfortunately, I haven’t received any proper response or meaningful update. I also called their support team multiple times. Every time, they simply opened a ticket, but there was no follow-up, explanation, or solution.\nI understand that payment issues can sometimes happen, but the biggest problem for me is the lack of communication and customer support. When someone is waiting for their final payout, having no clear information for weeks is extremely frustrating.\nI have already provided my details and information to Fintiba through their official support channels. I would really appreciate it if someone from the team could properly review my case, provide an update, and resolve the issue as soon as possible.\nOverall, this has been a very frustrating experience, especially after using Fintiba and expecting a smooth process until the end. I hope Fintiba takes this feedback seriously and improves its customer support and communication regarding payment issues.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ich bin leider sehr enttäuscht von Fintiba. Ich habe ein Sperrkonto für mein bevorstehendes Studium in Deutschland eingerichtet und benötige die dort hinterlegten Unterlagen für meinen Visumsprozess.\n\nFintiba hat leider einen falschen Geburtsort in meine Unterlagen und der Bestätigung geschrieben. Seit mittlerweile drei Wochen versuche ich, meine persönlichen Daten korrigieren zu lassen. Trotz täglicher Anrufe beim Kundenservice wurde mein Anliegen bis heute nicht gelöst. Statt einer konkreten Lösung werde ich immer wieder vertröstet und an andere Stellen verwiesen.\n\nDas Problem mag auf den ersten Blick wie eine kleine Datenkorrektur erscheinen, hat für mich jedoch gravierende Konsequenzen: Mein Visumsverfahren hängt davon ab, und dadurch ist inzwischen sogar mein Studienbeginne in Deutschland gefährdet.\n\nBesonders frustrierend ist, dass ich mich täglich bemühe, das Problem zu lösen, die benötigten Unterlagen mehrfach eingereicht habe und trotzdem seit drei Wochen keine zufriedenstellende Lösung erhalte. Gleichzeitig sind Termine bei der Deutschen Botschaft sehr schwer zu bekommen, sodass jede weitere Verzögerung für mich erhebliche Folgen haben kann.\n\nIch hätte von einem Anbieter, dessen Dienstleistungen ausdrücklich für internationale Studierende und deren Visumverfahren gedacht sind, deutlich mehr Unterstützung und vor allem eine schnelle und verlässliche Bearbeitung dringender Fälle erwartet.\n\nIch hoffe weiterhin, dass Fintiba mein Anliegen schnellstmöglich löst. Zum jetzigen Zeitpunkt kann ich den Service aufgrund meiner Erfahrung jedoch leider nicht empfehlen.\n\nUPDATE 26.08.2026: Auch wenn Fintiba behauptet, dass das Problem gelöst ist, ist es immer noch nicht. Im System wurde es nun geändert, aber nicht in dem wichtigen Dokument für das Visum. Ich hatte bereits 2 Termine in der Deutschen Botschaft verstreichen lassen bzw. bin extra 12 Stunden zur Botschaft gefahren um dort abgewiesen zu werden, weil das Dokument von Fintiba immer noch falsch ist. Trotz weiteren Versuchen die Situation zu klären, hat sich immer noch nichts getan. Mein Studium ist nun wirklich in Gefahr.\n\nUPDATE 31.08.2026: Es wurde nun im System wieder in den falschen Geburtsort geändert. Ich verstehe nicht, dass irgendein Mensch sich meinen Fall angenommen hat, aber immer noch die falschen Daten drinstehen bzw. sogar bereits korrigierte Daten wieder in die falschen geändert wurden. Der Telefon-Support kann immer nur vertrösten, per Mail passiert leider gar nichts. Ich bin wirklich verzweifelt.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Sehr enttäuschende und äußerst unprofessionelle Erfahrung mit Fintiba.\nIch kann Fintiba aufgrund meiner bisherigen Erfahrung absolut nicht empfehlen. Es geht hier nicht um eine einfache Anfrage, sondern um mein eigenes Geld auf meinem Sperrkonto, auf das ich dringend angewiesen bin.\nSeit über einer Woche wird mir versprochen, dass das Problem schnellstmöglich gelöst und die ausstehende Überweisung durchgeführt wird. Bis heute ist jedoch nichts passiert. Trotz mehrfacher Kontaktaufnahme erhalte ich keine klare und verbindliche Auskunft darüber, wann ich mein Geld tatsächlich erhalten werde.\nDurch diese Verzögerung bin ich inzwischen mit finanziellen Verpflichtungen konfrontiert, die ich aufgrund der ausstehenden Auszahlung nicht rechtzeitig erfüllen kann. Die daraus entstehenden Probleme und der finanzielle Druck werden offenbar nicht ernst genommen.\nBesonders enttäuschend ist, dass ich immer wieder selbst nachfragen muss, anstatt eine klare Information und eine konkrete Lösung zu erhalten. Wenn es um das eigene Geld der Kunden geht, sollte Zuverlässigkeit und schnelle Kommunikation selbstverständlich sein.\nEine Woche lang auf eine zugesagte Lösung zu warten, ohne dass das Problem tatsächlich behoben wird, ist für mich absolut inakzeptabel.\nIch erwarte von Fintiba eine sofortige Klärung, eine transparente Kommunikation und vor allem die unverzügliche Auszahlung meines noch ausstehenden Geldes.\nNach dieser Erfahrung würde ich Fintiba definitiv nicht weiterempfehlen", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Hello @Fintiba team, again there are problems with the blocked account. First, I didn't receive 3 months of money from you guys at the beginning, and now it is almost August 20th and I didn't receive the payout for August that should have come at the end of July. Even though I wrote an email, I didn't get a response. This is my minimum subsistence level to live on, and I need it as soon as possible. If I don't get it in the next 48 hours, I will need to take further steps and inform official authorities about these problems. I already had problems in the beginning for 3 months, and now you don't give me the money for the current month. Why is there always a problem, and why aren't these issues solved after over a year?! Please help.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am writing another review because this situation has now gone far beyond what I consider a reasonable delay.\n\nMy final blocked account payout was due on 31 July 2026. Today is 20 August 2026, and I still have not received my money. My current remaining blocked account balance is €884.70.\n\nI have contacted Fintiba repeatedly by both phone and email.\n\nAfter the payout initially failed, I was told on the phone that there were technical problems and that the money should be transferred soon. Nothing arrived.\n\nThen, on 11 August 2026, Fintiba Customer Care told me under Ticket 1314434 that they had initiated a manual transfer request and that I would receive my remaining funds within 3-5 business days.\n\nThat deadline has now passed.\n\nI still have not received the money in my registered German bank account. Even more importantly, the €884.70 still appears as remaining in my Fintiba blocked account, which raises serious concerns as to whether the promised manual transfer was ever actually executed.\n\nDespite all of this, my previous case was treated as resolved, and Fintiba even publicly replied to my previous Trustpilot review saying:\n\n“We’re happy to inform you that your query has been resolved.”\n\nNo, it has not been resolved.\n\nThe entire issue was that Fintiba had failed to send my final blocked account payout. The money has still not reached me. Calling the case “resolved” while the payment remains outstanding is extremely frustrating and unacceptable.\n\nI sent another escalation to Fintiba today and have now opened a new support request:\n\nPrevious Ticket: 1314434\nNew Ticket: 1336471\nSupport Code: 158-271-771\n\nAt this point, I am asking Fintiba to resolve this immediately and release my remaining blocked account funds.\n\nThis is not simply a minor customer-service inconvenience. A blocked account exists so international students can access money for their living expenses according to a scheduled payout. Students should not have to spend weeks repeatedly calling, emailing and publicly complaining just to receive their own money.\n\nI have already waited since 31 July, waited through the technical-problem explanation, and then waited through Fintiba's additional promised 3–5-business-day manual-transfer deadline. That deadline has also passed.\n\nIf this is still not resolved promptly, I will have to escalate the matter formally through the responsible bank's complaints management and, if necessary, BaFin and other appropriate complaint channels. I would much rather Fintiba simply resolve the issue and transfer the money that is outstanding.\n\nI will update this review when the outstanding funds actually arrive in my bank account.\n\nUntil that happens, this issue is not resolved.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I‏ transferred money to Fintiba on May 29 for my Sperrkonto (German visa). The money arrived June 1, but I was asked to provide proof of source of funds. My embassy interview was on June 4 – leaving me very little time.\n‏When I went to declare the source, I noticed the \"Friend\" option – which had been available before – was no longer there. This added to my confusion during an already stressful time.\n‏I uploaded all required documents promptly. Unfortunately, I didn't receive any response for over 6 weeks. The embassy had given me a 2-month deadline, and most of it passed without feedback.\n‏When I finally received a reply, it was a general template, not specific to my situation. Later, I was asked for additional documents that hadn't been mentioned initially.\n‏I also struggled to reach customer support – emails and calls went mostly unanswered, with only occasional generic apologies.\n‏What made it harder is that several friends of mine transferred the same amount to Fintiba after me, from outside Germany, and were never asked for proof of source – which felt inconsistent.\n‏Now I'm past the embassy's deadline, and my visa application is at serious risk. I respectfully ask Fintiba to urgently review my case and issue the Sperrkonto confirmation so I can submit it before my application is rejected.\n‏I hope they understand how stressful this situation has been, as it affects my future and my studies.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Been waiting for proof of source of funds verification for over weeks now. I could loose my admission spot because of Fintiba", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "During the registration and the setup process, I was never informed that the confirmation of Source of Funds would take this long.\n\nIf I had known from the beginning, I would have changed my plans accoirdingly, but even their own website says that it takes 7 days, 2 weeks at most.\n\nIt has now been more than 4 weeks since I've sent all of the documets, and the results are still pending. My visa deadline is coming up, and without all the necessary documents it's almost certain that my visa application will get rejected.\n\nThe worst part is that Fintiba support themselves, who are nearly impossible to reach, cannot even tell me how much longer it will take to process this. I was told to contact the bank directly, but FIB has seemingly stopped taking calls whatsoever, just redirecting me back to Fintiba's support.\n\nI am using Fintiba to get a German student visa, and my future will likely be ruined if the documents don't get processed as soon as possible and the verification of Source of Funds doesn't get completed.\n\nAt this point I am very desperate, but I don't ask Fintiba to skip any steps of the process, just to handle it quickly and responsibly and tell me if any additional documents are needed and to finish the confirmation urgently.\n\nOrder ID: 2003842\nSupport Code: 675-308-473\nAleksandrov Evgenii\nPlease, Fintiba, I really need your help, or I won't even make it to Germany. For the past few weeks I've been living in constant stress and I would greatly appreciate any meaningful update on my situation.\n\nI have also made a formal complaint to BaFin regarding this situation and will press it further if my situation does not get resolved.\nComplaint Number: 222068", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "If a minus rating existed, I’d give it without hesitation. Extremely unprofessional service. Support does not pick up calls, especially in English, and ignores emails for weeks. Agents seem unaware of basic processes, give inconsistent information, and leave urgent visa/finance issues unresolved. I cannot recommend Fintiba to anyone who needs reliable, timely support. When Fintiba worked with Sutor Bank, the process was smooth and predictable but now switching to FIB, everything has been delayed and handled unprofessionally.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I honestly did not expect the Source of Funds verification with Fintiba to take this long.\n\nMy funds were transferred successfully, and I have provided all the documents requested by Fintiba, including documents confirming the source of the funds and the financial situation of the person who made the transfer. However, more than three weeks have now passed, and my verification is still pending.\n\nWhat is particularly stressful is that I was never informed beforehand that this process could take several weeks. If I had known that the Source of Funds verification might take this long, I would have opened my blocked account much earlier and planned my visa application accordingly.\n\nThe estimated processing time has also changed several times. Initially, I was told that the verification would take around two weeks. Later, I was informed that it could take up to three weeks. Now, after already waiting for more than three weeks, I am being told that the bank may need up to four weeks to review the documents.\n\nThis situation is making it extremely difficult to plan my visa process. I am applying for a German student visa and urgently need my Blocking Confirmation. I am genuinely worried that I may miss my visa timeline because my blocked account verification is still not completed.\n\nI completely understand that Fintiba and its banking partners have to carry out compliance and anti-money-laundering checks. I am fully willing to provide any additional documents or information if necessary. However, after waiting for so long, it is extremely frustrating not knowing whether everything is in order, whether something else is required from me, or when my verification will finally be completed.\n\nEvery time I contact support, I am told that the case simply needs more time. Meanwhile, my visa deadline is getting closer every day.\n\nI really wish the possible duration and requirements of the Source of Funds verification had been communicated more clearly from the beginning. Knowing that the process could take up to four weeks would have allowed me to plan my finances and visa application much earlier.\n\nI am not asking Fintiba to bypass any required checks. I am simply asking you to review my case as soon as possible, clearly inform me if anything else is needed from my side, and complete the verification without further unnecessary delay.\n\nAt this point, I am extremely worried and would be very grateful if my case could be escalated to the responsible team and treated as urgent.\n\nOrder ID: 2006753\nArtem Guselnikov\n\nPlease, Fintiba, I really need your help with this. I just want to receive my Blocking Confirmation and continue my visa process without constantly worrying that I will miss my deadline.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I honestly never expected the Source of Funds verification with Fintiba to take this long.\nMy funds were transferred successfully, and I provided all the documents Fintiba requested from me. I also provided documents confirming the source of the funds and the financial situation of the person who transferred them. \nAnd yet, more than three weeks later, my verification is still not completed.\n\nThe most stressful part is that I was not informed in advance that this process could take several weeks. If I had known beforehand that the Source of Funds verification could take this long, I would have planned my visa process completely differently and opened my blocked account much earlier.\n\nWhat makes the situation even more frustrating is that the estimated processing time kept changing. At first, I was told that the verification could take around two weeks. Then I was told it could take up to three weeks. Now, after I have already been waiting for more than three weeks, I received another message saying that the bank may take up to four weeks to review the documents.\n\nThis makes it extremely difficult to plan my visa process. If I had known from the beginning that the verification could take up to four weeks, I would have planned everything differently and opened my blocked account much earlier.\n\nI am a student applying for a German student visa, and I urgently need the Blocking Confirmation. I am now genuinely scared that I may not be able to complete my visa process on time simply because my blocked account verification is still pending.\n\nI completely understand that banks have compliance and anti-money-laundering requirements. I have no problem providing documents or answering questions. What I find extremely difficult is waiting for weeks without knowing whether everything is fine, whether another document is missing, or when the process will finally be completed.\n\nEvery time I contact support, I am told that the case needs more time. But meanwhile, my visa deadline is getting closer every day.\n\nI wish Fintiba had made the possible duration and requirements of this verification much clearer from the beginning. This would have allowed me to plan my finances and visa application properly instead of finding myself in this situation at the last moment.\n\nI am not asking Fintiba to skip the required checks. I am simply asking them to review my documents as soon as possible, tell me clearly if anything else is needed, and finally complete my verification.\n\nAt this point, I am extremely worried and would be incredibly grateful if my case could finally be escalated to the responsible team.\nPlease, Fintiba, I really need your help with this. I just want to receive my Blocking Confirmation and be able to continue my visa process without this constant fear that I will miss the deadline.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I'm stuck on the source of funds review part of my procedure and my program starts at the end of next month (28 September) which is very close at this point and i can't proceed with my student visa without the blocking confirmation.\nI provided the documents around 25 days ago and from what i saw online it shouldn't take that much, i've seen many people facing such an issue which made me concerned and afraid of not making it to Germany on time.\nMy case number is: 1332769", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Fintiba is not just a financial company; it’s a true school of patience! They take their own deadlines very seriously—or rather, they don’t just miss them, they ignore them with inspiration!\nIt has been about five weeks since we opened a blocked account for our son and transferred €12,170. He needs to be in Germany by September 15th, and his studies begin on October 1st. However, Fintiba keeps sending polite, empty replies stating that they are 'looking into the matter' and that we need to wait again. How much longer are we expected to wait again and again?! Please, escalate our case!\nFintiba Order ID: 2015461", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I posted my review several days ago and received a standard reply saying that your support team is “looking into the case” and that I would get an update by email soon.\nUnfortunately, nothing has changed.\nNo concrete update, no timeline, no decision from FIB Compliance.\nMy funds have been on the blocked account since the end of June. All Source of Funds documents were submitted long ago. The verification has now been ongoing for almost two months. Meanwhile the German consulate is pressuring me to submit the Blocking Confirmation, and my study plans are at serious risk.\nA generic “we are working on it” is no longer acceptable after such a long delay.\nI urgently request either:\n1.  Immediate issuance of the Blocking Confirmation, or\n2.  Clear confirmation that the account will be closed and the full amount refunded without further delay.\nPlease stop sending template answers and provide a real status update.\n\nOn 31 July 2026 I already filed an official complaint with BaFin regarding this unacceptable delay. BaFin confirmed that they have opened a case and are currently reviewing it.\n\nSofia Plakhina\nOrder ID: 1968101", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Karega Chris Shami\nI opened fintiba blocked account and made a deposit got Blocking confirmation on 14th July and I upgraded to Fintiba plus to get health insurance on July 21st since then haven’t heard any updates been a month its only showing PENDING nothing else no nothing I wrote several emails to their support team ticket#1317131 but no help from them yet my studies are being put at risk because the dates are close and this is an a document i need am not requesting to be put before others but \n\nI hoped that this was a service that can’t take more than 3 working days and the prolonged silence has become extremely stressful and frustrating\n\nIf there are some missing documents causing delay please lemme know but if we are all good please get it resolved.\n\nBut hopefully they might look into it and get it resolved as soon as possible \nTo know the next step i can take", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am extremely disappointed with my experience with Fintiba.\n\nI am trying to open a Blocked Account for my wife, who will be accompanying me to Germany as a family member. Unfortunately, I have encountered technical problems during the application process, and the system keeps sending me back to the first step instead of allowing me to complete the application.\n\nWhat is even more frustrating is the communication with customer support. I contacted Fintiba several times, but instead of receiving a clear and practical solution to the technical problem, I kept receiving generic responses that did not address my specific situation.\n\nMy account has not been funded, I have not transferred any money, and I am simply trying to complete the application correctly. I also offered to provide the necessary passport and verification documents to resolve the issue.\n\nI expected much better support from a company that provides an essential service for international students and their families. When dealing with a visa application, these kinds of technical problems and delays create unnecessary stress and uncertainty.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The timelines of Source of Funds verification are insane. I'm waiting for 2 months and the only thing that support says is that they don't know the status - the verification is holding by FIB Bank and they can't do anything. However, Fintiba took my money and get their 159 euro commision for doing nothing. This is a reason to start an official lawsuit against Fintiba due to improper provision of contract services. \nIt was the worst experience of intaraction with financial organization in my life. I reccomend every student to choose other providers because Fintiba ruin my visa process. Now I face the risk of missing my opportunity to arrive to the uni at the start of the year or even don't obtain the visa at all.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Sehr geehrtes Fintiba-Team,\n\nich möchte mich hiermit ausdrücklich über die erneute Verzögerung bei der Überprüfung meiner Source-of-Funds-Unterlagen beschweren.\n\nIch habe die von Ihnen angeforderten Unterlagen bereits eingereicht und warte seit längerer Zeit auf den Abschluss der Verifizierung. Nun wurde die verbleibende Bearbeitungszeit erneut zurückgesetzt bzw. neu gestartet. Für mich ist diese Situation äußerst problematisch, da ich die Bestätigung meines Sperrkontos dringend für mein Visumverfahren benötige.\n\nIch habe alle von Ihnen angeforderten Informationen und Nachweise nach bestem Wissen und vollständig zur Verfügung gestellt. Trotzdem wird die Bearbeitungszeit immer wieder verlängert, ohne dass ich eine klare Erklärung darüber erhalte, warum die Überprüfung weiterhin nicht abgeschlossen werden kann.\n\nIch bitte Sie daher dringend:\n\n1. meine Verifizierung schnellstmöglich abzuschließen,\n2. mir den aktuellen Status meines Falls mitzuteilen,\n3. mir zu erklären, warum die Bearbeitungszeit erneut gestartet wurde,\n4. und mir schnellstmöglich die erforderliche Sperrkonto-Bestätigung zur Verfügung zu stellen.\n\nDie wiederholten Verzögerungen bringen mich in eine schwierige Situation und können meine weitere Visaplanung erheblich beeinträchtigen.\n\nIch bitte um eine konkrete und zeitnahe Antwort und nicht lediglich um eine allgemeine Mitteilung über die Bearbeitungszeit.Persönliche Daten\n\nVollständiger Name: Evrad Belvin Djomo Dactouo \nSupport ID : 408-344-405 \n\nMit freundlichen Grüßen\n\nEvrad Belvin Djomo", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Very horrible service \nI started the funds verification process three months ago and until now there is no solution for my problem, the delays from Fintiba's side had costed me my first college semester and visa, and in the last three emails that Fintiba had sent me they asked for the same two documents that i had already provided to them.\nI do not suggest their service to anyone.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Very horrible service \nI started the funds verification process three months ago and until now there is no solution for my problem, the delays from Fintiba's side had costed me my first college semester and visa, and in the last three emails that Fintiba had sent me they asked for the same two documents that i had already provided to them.\nI do not suggest their service to anyone.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Fintiba doesn't give me my money back\nOn the 3th of August I contacted Fintiba support regarding the return of funds that were transferred to my blocked account. Today is the 17 th of August and I still haven’t received a single proper reply.\nIt’s a shame there isn’t an option to give zero stars here – otherwise I’d do just that. \nAnd, dear Fintiba, if you’re reading this review, you can save yourself the trouble of writing yet another comment telling me that the team is working on my case, because that’s a lie :) This review is exclusively for those planning to open a blocked account for a visa. Don’t use Fintiba – they’re scammers. Use Edubao instead.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Update: My Source of Funds verification is still pending after almost 4 weeks. All requested documents were provided, the verification countdown in my account has expired, and I still have no Blocking Confirmation.\n\nI submitted my German student visa application on 26.08.2026, with the Blocking Confirmation to be submitted afterwards. This delay is now directly affecting my visa process and university enrollment.\n\nMy previous support request #1326965 was closed without resolving the issue. I have now opened a new urgent request: #1346259.\n\nCurrent support code: 520-996-621\n\nI urgently require Fintiba to resolve this case and issue my Blocking Confirmation. If this matter continues to remain unresolved without a concrete explanation or timeframe, I will escalate the complaint through the appropriate formal complaint and regulatory channels.\n\nAt this point, I need a resolution, not another generic request to wait.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Honestly, I’m really frustrated with Fintiba right now. I’m a medical doctor from Lebanon, and I waited 5 months just to get my German visa appointment. I finally had the appointment and submitted my visa application, but I’m now stuck waiting for my Fintiba Sperrbestätigung because the Source of Funds verification is still pending.\nI’ve already uploaded the documents they asked for and explained exactly where the money came from. I understand that these checks are necessary, but I’m now stuck waiting with a deadline from the German Embassy. If I don’t get the confirmation in time, I will end up with my visa application being rejected because of this one missing document.\nAfter waiting 5 months for the appointment, this is honestly incredibly stressful. I’m not asking them to skip the verification ,I just wish there was better communication and some way to handle cases like mine when there is an actual visa deadline.\nI really hope Fintiba can resolve this soon.\nTicket number : 1328065", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "chose Fintiba because of its good reputation and the services it offers international students. Unfortunately, my experience with the Source of Funds verification has been quite stressful.\n\nI submitted all the requested documents on 4 August 2026, including the documents showing the source of the funds and the relevant bank accounts in Kuwait. I have also contacted Fintiba several times by email and telephone.\n\nI understand that compliance checks can take time, and I am completely willing to provide anything else that may be required from me or my sponsor. My concern is simply that I still don't know what is actually happening with my case.\n\nI have received responses saying that my case is being reviewed and that I need to wait, but this doesn't tell me whether something is missing, whether there is an issue with my documents, or whether everything is complete and I simply need to wait for the verification to finish.\n\nMy German visa appointment is very soon, so I would really appreciate some clarity. I am not asking Fintiba to skip any necessary checks. I just want to know the actual current status of my verification and whether there is anything I can do from my side to help resolve it.\n\nI hope someone from Fintiba can look into my case and provide a specific update rather than another general response that it is under review.\n\nTicket Number: 1324132\n\nIf any additional information is needed to identify my case, I am happy to provide it privately.\n\nI would really appreciate Fintiba's assistance in resolving this as soon as possible.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Extremely disappointing experience with Fintiba — one month of waiting with no meaningful update\n\nMy experience with Fintiba has been extremely disappointing and stressful.\n\nI opened a Fintiba blocked account for my German student visa and transferred the required funds from my own bank account in Kazakhstan on 15 July 2026.\n\nOn 23 July, Fintiba informed me that my funds would undergo an additional source-of-funds review because, according to them, the transaction was somehow connected to a country affected by sanctions. However, the transfer was made directly from my own account at a Kazakh bank, and I have still not received a clear explanation of what specific sanctioned-country connection Fintiba believes exists.\n\nNevertheless, I fully cooperated and provided extensive documentation covering the entire source-of-funds chain, including:\n\n1. an official employment certificate from my employer, signed and stamped, confirming my employment period and salary;\n2. an original English-language bank statement from my salary account showing regular salary payments and their amounts;\n3. officially certified and notarized documents confirming the transfer of my funds to my bank account in Kazakhstan;\n4. official documents confirming the subsequent transfer from that account to my Fintiba blocked account.\n\nIn other words, I provided documentation tracing the funds from my employment and salary all the way to the transfer into the blocked account.\n\nWhat is particularly frustrating is the way the estimated processing time is displayed in the Fintiba app. Initially, the countdown indicated approximately two weeks, so naturally I expected the review to be completed within that period. Instead, after those two weeks passed, the countdown simply reset and started another two-week period.\n\nAs of today, 15 August 2026, exactly one month has passed since I transferred the money, and more than three weeks have passed since Fintiba requested the source-of-funds documentation. I have received no meaningful update about the status of the review, no indication of whether additional documents are required, and no realistic estimate of when the process will be completed.\n\nI have also uploaded my official university enrolment confirmation (Immatrikulationsbescheinigung) to Fintiba. Even this simple one-page PDF document has apparently been under review for around two weeks.\n\nThis is not merely an inconvenience. I spent approximately a year preparing for my master’s studies in Germany. I have been admitted to the university and officially enrolled, but this unresolved blocked-account verification is now putting my student visa timeline and my ability to begin my studies in Germany at risk.\n\nI completely understand that financial institutions have compliance obligations and may need to verify the origin of funds. What I find unacceptable is the combination of extremely long processing times, a repeatedly resetting countdown, and almost complete absence of communication while a student’s visa and university plans depend on the outcome.\n\nFor a company whose core customers are international students dealing with strict visa deadlines, I would expect a much more transparent, predictable, and responsive approach.\n\nI am asking Fintiba to review my case urgently and contact me with a concrete update so that I can proceed with my visa and finally begin the studies I have worked so long for.\n\nFintiba Support Number: 090-649-815", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Funds were credited to account 16 July 2026, with account opening fee charged and Source of Funds proof requested the same day. Those documents were submitted in full on 17 July, ticket 1298978. Since then I have received no questions, no correction requests, and no status updates.\n\nFintiba's own Help Center states this verification normally takes 1-2 weeks for high-risk countries, and that period ended on 1 August.\n\nI have written three times. Two replies asked me to \"allow a little bit more time\". The third, on 28 July, set out my fixed, unchangeable visa appointment date and asked either for the confirmation or for one line telling me what was missing. It was never answered.\n\nThe only document you have issued, the monthly statement, is printed with the words \"This document is not a blocking confirmation\".\n\nToday I finally reached your support by phone and was told the review sits with your partner bank, FIB Frankfurt International Bank. Seventeen minutes later I called FIB. A recording thanked me for calling, said all blocked-account matters must be directed to Fintiba, and ended the call. So there is no way to reach a human being at the bank holding my money.\n\nMy formal complaint to FIB on 7 August so far resulted only in an automated reply with no reference number and no content. On 14 August (today) I filed a complaint against FIB with BaFin.\n\nMy national student visa application was filed on 3 August, and is incomplete for exactly one reason. The winter semester begins on 1 October.\n\nI paid in advance, in full, for a product with a single function, and that function has not been performed for a month.\n\nMy support code (it has changed recently without explanation), current:  044-894-636\n\nPlease reply with a date. \"Under review\", \"our team is working on it\" and \"we will email you as soon as possible\" are what I have been given since docs upload day. Anything without either the blocking confirmation or a specific completion date will be added to my BaFin file as it stands.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "vollständige Rückstattung meines Geldes . \nZwecks eines Studiums in Deutschland habe ich am 24 Juni ein Speerkonto in Fintiba geöffnet.und da Sie mir bis heute keine Speerbestätigung zukommen gelassen haben und mein Semester nicht mehr gewährleisten kann , verlange ich eine sorfort vollständige Rückstattung meines Geldes . Sie haben mein Projekt verhindern. So eine äußerst schlechte Erfahrung", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The worst nightmare of a last few months, nearly driven me to the suicide.  The money were transferred and than CONFIRM YOUR SOURCE OF FUNDS came up, although all possible documents were provided (tons of them, they are all more than clear). I had to apply for a visa cause I don’t have much time left. And still the third month goes by with no result. And now I risk of not getting and ruining my dream, whole year and more than that just because Fintiba does nothing to check the documents (it would take idk, 15 minutes?). \nPlease, do something. Please. \n\nOrder id is 2017852", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "On behalf of Polina Nadobenko\nFintiba Order ID: 1987876\nCustomer number: RU1097662\nBlocked Account number: DE0850...9300\n\nFor more than 35 days, we have been attempting to obtain clarification and a status update regarding the source of funds verification process.\n\nBlocked account was opened in June and money was transferd to blocked account on 25th June. On the 29th June requested documents for source of funds verification have been uploaded. \n\nDespite multiple emails to different Fintiba addresses, repeated attempts via support chat, and several phone calls, we have not received any response.\nDue to this prolonged delay and lack of communication, we were unable to submit the outstanding documents required by the German Embassy in Moscow. As a result, our visa application process has been stalled for over four weeks since submission and five weeks since the money transfer and source of funds verification began.\n\nFinally we lost hope and requested withdraw of the funds, stop of source of funds verification and close blocked account with Fintiba.\n\nRequest was placed 4 Aug 2026 to reimburse the full amount but till now neither progress nor updates from Fintiba. Application and website still shown Expired/pending source of funds verification although in Telegram chat, Fintiba support confirmed recieveing our request and processing it.\n\nAbsolutely weak customer service, lack of  communication and no transparency to funds movement.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "NO MONEY RECEIVED AFTER ONE MONTH!\nIt has been one month since I requested the closure of my blocked account with Fintiba. There are thousands of euros in the account that I urgently need, but no action by Fintiba.\nTwo weeks ago, I wrote on Trustpilot, and they immediately replied that we closed the account, but what's the use? I want the money back, not just the \"closed account\" status.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "1-Star Review\nAccount Number 2051770300\nUnacceptable delay in Source of Funds verification – visa appointment at risk\n\nI transferred the required funds to my Fintiba blocked account and submitted all requested Source of Funds documents on 16 July 2026.\n\nToday is 13 August 2026, and my account is still under review. I have not received a clear update explaining the status of my case or whether any additional documents are required.\n\nMy German Embassy appointment to submit the missing documents is on 17 August 2026, and this prolonged delay is putting my visa application at serious risk.\n\nI completely understand that compliance and Source of Funds checks are necessary. However, keeping a customer's case under review for almost a month without providing a meaningful update is extremely stressful, especially when the customer has an important visa deadline.\n\nI am not asking for special treatment. I am simply asking Fintiba to either complete the verification or clearly tell me what additional documents are required.\n\nFintiba needs to significantly improve its communication and processing time for compliance cases.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ich kann mein Sperrkonto seit einem Monat nicht freischalten.\n\nObwohl ich mich bereits in Deutschland befinde und meinen Aufenthaltstitel erhalten habe, versuche ich seit einem Monat, Zugang zu meinem Geld auf dem Sperrkonto zu bekommen. Am 18.07.2026 habe ich meinen Aufenthaltstitel in der Fintiba-App hochgeladen. Nachdem zwei Wochen lang nichts passiert war, habe ich Fintiba mehrfach per E-Mail kontaktiert und zusätzlich beim Kundenservice angerufen.\nAm Telefon wurde mir zunächst versichert, dass alles in Ordnung sei, mein Aufenthaltstitel bereits geprüft worden sei und in meinem Account nur noch „irgendein Problem“ gelöst werden müsse.\n\nEinige Tage später habe ich erneut bei Fintiba angerufen. Dieses Mal wurde mir gesagt, dass das Problem behoben sei und mein Aufenthaltstitel – ausdrücklich – bereits GEPRÜFT worden sei.\n\nMein letzter Anruf bei Fintiba war am 13.08.2026 um 09:27 Uhr. Ein anderer Mitarbeiter des Kundenservice behauptete plötzlich, mein Aufenthaltstitel sei doch noch nicht geprüft. Als ich fragte, worin genau das Problem bestehe und warum auf meine E-Mails nicht geantwortet werde, HAT DER MITARBEITER EINFACH AUFGELEGT!!! Ein solches Verhalten empfinde ich als unglaublich unhöflich und respektlos.\n\nMein Fazit: Fintiba hat innerhalb eines Monats auf keine meiner E-Mails gar nicht geantwortet. Bei jedem Telefonat erhalte ich von unterschiedlichen Mitarbeitern des Kundenservice widersprüchliche Informationen. Gleichzeitig habe ich keinen Zugang zu meinem Geld für meinen Lebensunterhalt und befinde mich dadurch in einer sehr schwierigen finanziellen Situation, für die die anhaltende Verzögerung bei Fintiba verantwortlich ist. Zusätzlich muss ich als Kundin ein respektloses Verhalten einzelner Mitarbeiter hinnehmen.\n\nIch hoffe sehr, dass Fintiba diese Bewertung zur Kenntnis nimmt, den Fall endlich ernsthaft prüft und mein Sperrkonto unverzüglich freischaltet.\nMein Account Nummer: 2026953300\n\nUpdate: endlich ist mein Problem behoben, zwei nette Mitarbeitern im Fintiba Büro haben vor Ort mein Problem gelöst.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ich bin extrem enttäuscht von dem Service. Mein Geld ist bereits seit Ende Juni vollständig auf meinem Fintiba-Konto eingegangen. Seit fast zwei Monaten warte ich nun auf die Bestätigung (Blocking Confirmation) für mein Visum, da mein Profil in der Prüfung zum Herkunftsnachweis (Source of Funds) festsitzt. Es gibt absolut keine Rückmeldung oder Updates vom Support, obwohl alle notwendigen Dokumente hochgeladen wurden. Am 17. Juli musste ich bereits meinen Visumstermin im Konsulat ohne die Bestätigung wahrnehmen und konnte nur die restlichen Unterlagen einreichen. Mittlerweile werde ich vom Konsulat mit Aufforderungen bombardiert, die Blocking Confirmation endlich nachzureichen. Mein gesamtes Studium in Deutschland steht auf dem Spiel!Da Fintiba und die Sutor Bank überhaupt nicht reagieren, habe ich bereits Ende Juli eine offizielle Beschwerde bei der BaFin eingereicht. Ein solches Verhalten ist für ein offiziell vom Auswärtigen Amt empfohlenes Unternehmen absolut inakzeptabel. Ich fordere das Fintiba-Team auf, meinen Fall umgehend manuell zu prüfen, freizugeben und mir das Dokument auszustellen! \nIch werde meine Bewertung hier gerne ändern, sobald ich endlich eine Antwort und die Kontobestätigung bekomme.  \nMeine Order ID: 1968101", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have been in Germany since the end of June and I still cannot receive a single payout from my blocked account.\nFirst there was a long verification delay. Now I cannot register my IBAN for payouts at all - the app shows an error and tells me to contact support. I did exactly that, immediately (ticket 1301620), and again with more details (ticket 1320062). It has now been over three weeks and I have not received a single reply to either ticket. Nobody picks up the phone either.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I uploaded all the documents regarding the funds verification issue almost two weeks ago and still haven't received any response! Totally I've been waiting for the blocking confirmation since June 16th!\n\nMy tickets is 1293122", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Hey everyone,\n\nI wanted to share a nightmare situation I am dealing with right now and warn any incoming international students: whatever you do, DO NOT block your funds with FINTIBA.\n\nLike most non-EU students, I had to open a blocked account for our visas. I made the mistake of trusting Fintiba.\n\nNow, they are completely refusing to release my monthly payout money. I have hit a wall communicating with them, and they are holding onto the funds with no valid justification.\n\nI have already called and emailed BaFin and the Versicherungsombudsmann for help, but shockingly, both organizations told us that this blocked account and this company are unknown to them.\n\nBecause of this, I've realized it is better to contact the Ausländerbehörde directly. I am going to explain the situation to them that companies like Fintiba are running a scam on people like us and ask the authorities to give us another solution to show we have enough funds to support our lives in Germany at least for the students to come in the future.\n\nDealing with this level of financial uncertainty while trying to focus on our studies is incredibly stressful. If you are in the process of planning your move, please save yourself the anxiety, the risk, and the potential legal fees. Choose a different provider for your blocked account, or just explain the situation to the Ausländerbehörde and ask them to give you another alternative, and DO NOT BLOCK YOUR FUNDS.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I contacted Fintiba support regarding the return of funds that were transferred to my blocked account. Due to a change in circumstances, the purpose of opening the account is no longer valid, and I requested that the money be returned to the original sender's account.\nUnfortunately, despite contacting support, I have not received any response. For a company handling significant amounts of customers' money, timely communication and support are essential. I hope this issue will be addressed as soon as possible.\n\nAccount Number 2055929300", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "My monthly payout for August from my blocked account was due on July 31st, 2026. Today is August 11th, and the money has still not arrived.\n​When calling support, I am given excuses about the weekend, but a SEPA bank transfer does not take 11 days. Worse, customer support has been completely ignoring my written emails for weeks.\n​This blocked account is my sole source of living expenses in Germany. Due to this unacceptable delay and lack of support, I have filed an official complaint with the Federal Financial Supervisory Authority (BaFin).\n​Customer ID: IR01082169\n\nUpdate (14.08.2026):\nAfter posting this review, the payment for August was finally processed. I am updating this to confirm receipt of funds, but I will keep monitoring the performance for upcoming months to see if payments are made on time without needing public complaints.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "UPDATE August 19th: STILL NO SOLUTION. My acquaintance contacted your call center on behalf of my son, and your team confirmed that you received our 12,093 EUR transfer but held it. Your agent promised to send instructions to my son's email to unblock the profile and issue the Blocking Confirmation. We have been waiting, but no email was received, and our support tickets remain unanswered. My son's official visa deadline at the Ausländerbehörde passed yesterday, so the situation is very urgent. Please contact me via Trustpilot direct messages (DM) immediately so I can provide my son's account details privately and we can resolve this together today. Thank you.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I opened a blocked account, and the full amount of €12,063 was transferred from a German bank account to the blocked account on June 22, 2026. The €159 account-opening fee was charged immediately. Shortly afterwards, I was informed that, as a Russian citizen, I was required to provide additional documentation to verify the source of the funds. I provided all the requested documents the very next day, on June 23. After that, however, there was no meaningful information about the progress of the verification. I contacted customer support several times via chat and phone, but unfortunately received only generic responses such as “We do not know when there will be a result” and “There is nothing we can do.”\nAfter waiting 38 days, I received a further request for additional documents. I provided everything again the following day, hoping that submitting the documents promptly would help move the process forward. Unfortunately, I am still waiting.\nAs of today, more than 48 days have passed since the funds were transferred to the blocked account, and I have provided the requested documentation twice. I still have not received a final decision or any meaningful update regarding the status of my account.\nThis is particularly frustrating because Fintiba recommends opening a blocked account 3–4 weeks before applying for a visa. In my case, that period has already passed by a considerable margin, while I still have no clear indication of when the verification will be completed.\nI also expected better communication from customer support. The chat support has mostly provided repetitive and generic responses without any useful information. Today, for the seventh time, I received the same answer from support: \"wait a little longer.\" I understand that support teams can be under pressure, but I found this response disappointing and inappropriate.\nI completely understand that source-of-funds checks can take time and that additional verification may sometimes be necessary. My main frustration, however, is that there appears to be no clear timeframe for completing these checks, while the lack of meaningful updates suggests that Fintiba’s operational processes for handling such cases may not be working effectively.\nI sincerely hope that Fintiba and FIB Frankfurt International Bank AG will eventually provide the service and support they advertise and that this long and stressful process will finally come to an end.\nAt the same time, I would like to warn other customers, particularly those from countries subject to additional verification, to think carefully before opening a blocked account with Fintiba. Based on my experience, you should be prepared for the possibility of a very lengthy verification process and limited information or assistance. Once the verification process begins, it may be very difficult to obtain a meaningful update about your case or even an indication of when the process might be completed. This can be particularly problematic when the blocked account is connected to important deadlines, such as visa applications.\nBased on my experience, I would strongly recommend taking the potential delays and uncertainty into consideration before choosing Fintiba.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Delayed payout for August.\nVery disappointing experience with Fintiba. My August 2026 payout from my blocked account has still not been received, despite contacting Fintiba several times. I want to emphasize that this is my own money that is being held by Fintiba and not payed to me. \n\nThis is a serious issue because I rely on the monthly payout for essential expenses, including my health insurance contributions. A delayed payment can therefore cause significant financial and administrative problems.\n\nI have now sent a formal reminder and requested that the outstanding amount be paid by 15 August 2026. If the issue is not resolved, I will consider further steps, including contacting the BaFin.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I wrote many mails to gmail Fintiba support no responses and also for phone calls", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Extremely disappointing experience with Fintiba\nMy sister and I opened blocked accounts with Fintiba for our visa applications. The required funds were transferred on July 7, and all requested documents were submitted on July 10.\nDespite this, we are still waiting for the Blocking Confirmation, which is essential for moving forward with our visa applications.\nWhat is particularly disappointing is the complete lack of clear communication. We have tried to contact Fintiba through different channels, including customer support through our personal accounts, email, and phone.\nUnfortunately, neither of us has received a single proper or substantive response. The only messages we have received have been generic or automated replies confirming that our requests were received. No one has provided a clear explanation of what is happening with our accounts, whether anything is missing, or when we can expect to receive the Blocking Confirmations.\nGetting any useful information by phone has also been extremely difficult. Even when contact is finally established, the issue remains unresolved, and no clear information about the status of the accounts or expected processing time is provided.\nThis delay is creating serious difficulties with our visa applications. The funds were transferred and all required documents were submitted weeks ago, yet we are still waiting for confirmations that are necessary for the next stage of the visa process.\nWe expected a much more professional level of service and communication from Fintiba, especially when dealing with documents that are so important for visa applications.\nVery disappointing experience and customer service.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Very disappointing experience with Fintiba\nMy brother and I opened blocked accounts with Fintiba for our visa applications. The required funds were transferred on July 7, and all requested documents were submitted on July 10.\nWe are still waiting for the Blocking Confirmation, which is required to proceed with our visa applications.\nWhat is especially frustrating is that we have repeatedly tried to contact Fintiba through different channels. We contacted customer support through our personal accounts, emailed their support address directly, and also tried reaching customer service by phone.\nUnfortunately, the only responses we have received have been generic or automated messages confirming that our requests were received. We have not received a single substantive response explaining what is happening with our accounts, whether anything is missing, or when we can expect the Blocking Confirmations.\nIt is also extremely difficult to get any clear information by phone. Even when contact is finally established, the issue is not resolved and no clear information about the status of the accounts is provided.\nThis lack of communication and the delay are causing serious problems with our visa applications. The funds were transferred and all required documents were submitted weeks ago, but we are still waiting for a confirmation that is essential for the next step of the visa process.\nWe expected Fintiba to process the documents in a timely manner and, at the very least, to provide proper and meaningful support when contacted repeatedly.\nVery disappointing customer service and communication.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Following the positive reviews about Fintiba, we decided to open a blocked account (Sperrconto) with them for our daughter's enrollment at Studienkolleg. We transferred the funds as required, and they requested documents to confirm the origin of the funds. The documents were provided, after which, supposedly, a verification process began. Two months passed, and the verification status remained unchanged. When we began to worry and wrote to them, they responded with contradictory and varying information, each time stating: « need to wait longer», or «send additional documents», or «pay more», etc. As a result, exam dates were missed, and our daughter's trip, which our whole family had been preparing for the past couple of years, fell through. To say that she was upset would be an understatement.\n\nNow we're trying to get at least the money back, but Fintiba is sending us the same familiar, formal replies: \"We will review your request within 4-6 weeks,\" with a disingenuous signature about how much they love us in Frankfurt. Meanwhile, I see dozens, if not hundreds, of stories online from other families similar to ours. \n\nTheir support claims they are forced to comply with strict banking requirements. This might be true, but we quickly found another provider, where we received the same service in half a day!\n\nFurthermore, even those who managed to open a Sperrconto with Fintiba are experiencing problems accessing funds from their accounts for their children, who are already studying in Germany.\n\nEveryone talks about the famous German «ordnung». However, it remains a mystery how a company that has orchestrated an obvious money trap right in the center of Europe continues to fleece unwary clients and hasn't encountered any problems with regulatory authorities.\n\n\nUpd from August 17, 2026, in response to Fintiba's response: the brazen hypocrites who shamelessly stole a year of our family's life and our dream of a modern education assure us that \"our support team is actively reviewing your case\" and thanks us for \"patience and understanding.\" I don't even know what could be more vile.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "It has now been almost a week since I published my last review, in response to which I was promised that the issue would be resolved. Unfortunately, the problem has still not been resolved, and I have not received the payment.\n\nPlease help me resolve this issue as soon as possible. I urgently need these funds to cover my living expenses, so the continued delay is causing me serious difficulties.\n\nI would really appreciate it if you could look into this matter and ensure that the payment is made without any further delay. Thank you for your attention and assistance.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "We opened a blocked account for our son for his studies in Germany and transferred 12K Euro to his account. According to Fintiba’s documentation, the 'Blocking Confirmation' should have been issued as soon as the funds were received. But no! Fintiba did not send the blocking confirmation after the funds were received in the account. However, as our son is a Russian citizen, we were asked to provide proof of the source of funds. We submitted the requested documents immediately. It has now been over three weeks since we provided the documents, and we have received no response from Fintiba. Every time we inquire, we are told that the verification process is still ongoing. \nIt is nonsensical that the funds are considered 'unverified' for the purpose of issuing the Blocking Confirmation, but 'verified' enough for the company to deduct their fees. The funds have been held in the account for weeks, and there is no indication of when the verification process will be completed.\nHonestly, I’ve never seen anything like this in terms of customer care.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I've been a Fintiba customer since summer 2023 and during this time I observed how a quality of their services drastically downgraded. My current complaint is about a failed payout for August 2026, which I still didn't receive, even though today is August 10th. On August 3rd, I created a ticket for this issue and since that time I called their support 3 times just to hear from them that they are working on that. Absolutely, there is no care for their customers, international students, who pay now 9.9 euro monthly and depend on the punctuality of the payouts to pay for rent, insurance, etc, and not even getting their money back.\nMy number ticket is 1316061", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "My name is Sergey, and I am an international student who was admitted to Julius-Maximilians-Universität Würzburg for a Master's programme. I chose Fintiba for my blocked account because I had heard good things about the company from other students. Unfortunately, my experience has been extremely stressful and has put my visa process at risk.\n\nI opened my blocked account around 20 June 2026 and transferred the required funds shortly afterwards. The very next day, Fintiba requested additional AML documentation. As I understand it, residents of Russia are currently subject to enhanced checks regarding the source of funds.\n\nI want to be clear: I do not object to the AML procedure itself. Given the current regulatory environment, I understand why such checks may be necessary.\n\nThe problem is the processing time and communication.\n\nI provided the requested documents by the beginning of July. These included the passport of the person who transferred the money, confirmation of their relationship to me, documents explaining the source of the funds, employment/income documentation, and bank statements showing the movement and origin of the money.\n\nAfter that, I waited.\n\nI repeatedly contacted Fintiba by email, by phone through contacts in Germany, and through their Russian-language Telegram support. I also repeatedly asked for my case to be escalated. Despite this, I received no substantive response for more than a month.\n\nOnly on 5 August did I finally receive a response informing me that additional documents were required. I was then given until 19 August to provide translated bank statements, even though the statements I had previously submitted were bilingual.\n\nI can accept being asked for additional documents. What I cannot accept is waiting more than a month just to be told that something else is required.\n\nIf my documents had been reviewed within a reasonable timeframe — for example, within several days or a week or two — I could have immediately provided anything that was missing. Instead, the delay itself has become a serious problem.\n\nI have already applied for my German visa, and Fintiba may now be unable to provide the necessary blocked-account confirmation in time. For an international student, this is not a minor inconvenience. The blocked account is an important part of the visa process, while university start dates, visa appointments, accommodation and travel arrangements all operate on fixed timelines.\n\nThe most frustrating part is that this situation could potentially have been avoided through timely communication. If Fintiba had reviewed my documents promptly and told me in July what was missing, I would simply have provided the additional documents at that time.\n\nInstead, I lost more than a month waiting, repeatedly contacting support and worrying whether I would be able to complete my visa process in time.\n\nThe issue is therefore not that Fintiba performs AML checks. The issue is the combination of an understandable compliance procedure with extremely slow document processing and customer support.\n\nA company providing blocked accounts specifically for international students should understand that time is critical. A delay of one or two days is one thing. A delay of more than a month before identifying missing documents is something completely different.\n\nI am submitting the additional documents today. At this point, I can only hope they will be reviewed considerably faster than the documents I submitted in July.\n\nMy chances of starting the Master's programme I have worked hard to get into have already been seriously affected by these delays, although the situation is not yet beyond repair. A prompt response from Fintiba could still make a difference.\n\nFintiba still has an opportunity to fix this. I sincerely hope they take it.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Critical Delay! \nVerification timer expired, German Embassy is waiting!\n My name is Daria Roban. I uploaded all source of funds documents weeks ago. The internal verification timer expired 5 days ago, and my profile is completely stuck. I have already submitted my documents to the German Embassy, and the visa officers have been waiting for my Sperrbestätigung for over a week now! Fintiba's standard support is completely ignoring my urgent emails. Because of this artificial delay, my student visa and university enrollment are under immediate threat. Please verify my account immediately!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I decided to go with Fintiba Plus, partly because they assured me that even though I’m from a high-risk country, the verification process would be quick – no more than two weeks, they said.\n\nI transferred the money on June 22nd and submitted all required documents on June 30th. Then came the waiting. After an entire month, on July 28th, they finally reached out – but only to request additional documents. I sent those promptly on July 30th.\n\nThe problem is, I’m working against a tight deadline: I now have only 3 days left to provide my blocking confirmation. I politely asked them to expedite the review, but my message was simply ignored. No response, no update, no sense of urgency.\n\nAt this point, it feels like I’ve wasted both time and money. And what’s most frustrating is that Fintiba doesn’t seem to care about resolving the issue in time. It's been a month and a half, I remind you. \n\nMy support code: 872-870-009", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am writing this review after more than two months of waiting for my Source of Funds verification to be completed.\nThe review process has now been ongoing for approximately two months. For a service specifically designed for international students with strict visa deadlines, such processing times are simply unacceptable.\nThe requirements are not transparent. First, one set of documents is requested, then additional documents are requested later, even though the initial package already addressed the stated requirements. My source of funds is my own officially declared salary from regular employment at a non-sanctioned international company. I am not a business owner, investor, or politically exposed person. It is difficult to understand why verification of standard employment income should take this long.\nAt no point during the account opening process was I informed that Russian citizens may be subject to an extensive Source of Funds review lasting several months. Nor was there any indication that the process could take more than two months with no predictable completion date. The only place where such experiences are discussed is in informal student chats. I received no warning from Fintiba before transferring my funds.\nWhat I find particularly concerning is that account-opening fees are charged immediately after the transfer is received, while the actual verification of the source of funds takes place afterwards. If the compliance review is considered essential before the account can be fully used, customers should be clearly informed about the expected timeline and verification requirements before transferring their money.\nAs a result of these delays, my German student visa application and my admission to a Master's programme are now at risk. I have spent the last two months dealing with uncertainty, preparing additional documentation, paying for translations, and waiting for updates instead of focusing on my relocation and housing search.\nIf I had known in advance that this process could take several months without any clear timeline, I would have chosen a different blocked account provider.\nI sincerely hope that Fintiba and FIB Frankfurt International Bank AG improve transparency, communication, and processing times so that future students do not face the same situation.\nFrolova Kseniia\nTicket #1244597", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Avoid this company at all costs! I transferred money to my blocked account on June 22nd. It took them six (!) whole weeks and multiple support tickets just to send me the list of documents required for the source of funds verification.\n\nTo make matters worse, they finally sent this list the exact day AFTER we had already submitted our visa applications. Because of Fintiba's unacceptable delays, we were forced to open a second blocked account with another company (EduBao) just to meet our visa deadline.\n\nSince the Fintiba account is no longer relevant, we are now trying to get our money back. However, their customer support completely ignores us. Heaven only knows how much more time and effort it will take to get a refund.\n\nNever use this company under any circumstances! They will ruin your schedule and ghost you when you ask for your money back.\n\nUPDATE:\n\nToday, August 31, support replied that we need to upload documents in the app 🤦‍♂️.  The button in the app is disabled and we’ve already uploaded all documents, and we don't have any others! For a month now, we've been asking them to stop the verification process and refund our money!\n\nAll their replies here and over the phone saying that they are \"looking into the issue and will contact us soon\" are just pure lie! If you want to end up without a blocking confirmation and no money - Fintiba is your choice!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "UPDATE - 18 August 2026:\n\nUnfortunately, this issue is still not resolved.\n\nFintiba has publicly replied to this review stating: “We’re happy to inform you that your query has been resolved.” However, I still have not received my remaining €894.50.\n\nOn 11 August 2026, Fintiba informed me by email that they had initiated a **manual transfer request** and that I should receive the remaining funds within 3–5 business days. That timeframe has now passed, and as of 18 August 2026, the money has still not arrived in my registered German bank account.\n\nI find it very concerning that my case has been publicly described as “resolved” when the actual issue this review concerns - receiving my outstanding blocked account funds - remains unresolved.\n\nI have contacted Fintiba again today and requested confirmation of whether the manual transfer was actually executed, as well as the transaction details.\n\nI will update this review when I actually receive the outstanding funds.\n\n---\n\nORIGINAL REVIEW:\n\nExtremely disappointed with Fintiba’s handling of my final blocked account payout.\n\nMy final payout was due on 31 July 2026. It is now 9 August 2026, and I still have not received the money that I need for my living expenses this month. My Fintiba account shows that my payouts have expired, while €894.50 of my money still remains in the Fintiba account.\n\nI have contacted Fintiba multiple times regarding this issue, both by email and phone. On the phone, I was told that they were experiencing technical problems and that my final payout should be transferred soon. Despite this, the money has still not arrived, and I have received no meaningful resolution.\n\nThis is especially unacceptable because a blocked account is specifically intended to provide students with money for their living expenses. Customers should not have to repeatedly chase a financial service provider simply to receive their own scheduled payout.\n\nI am asking Fintiba to release my remaining €894.50 immediately and confirm the transfer.\n\nSupport Code: 197-784-503\n\nI will update this review if and when Fintiba actually resolves the issue.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Update as of August 10: My file has now been pending for over a month and a half.\n\nI still deeply discourage anyone from using Fintiba. \n\nTwo weeks ago, the FIB compliance team contacted me requesting additional documents. However, here is the real issue: I had ALREADY provided those exact documents from their checklist back in June through the official Fintiba form. Where are these documents? Why did they fail to reach the FIB team? Why does this company allow such catastrophic internal delays and a rude, unacceptable violation of their own processing deadlines stated on the website?\n\nI have been unable to receive my blocking confirmation for 1.5 months. This extreme bureaucratic stress has severely impacted my health, causing panic attacks and fainting. I have spent months preparing my move to Germany, investing significant time, effort and money into the process. It is extremely frustrating to see the visa timeline put at risk because of administrative delays that appear to be outside my control.\n\nLatest support ticket number: 1299401", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I would also like to make a complaint about the whole procedure of confirming funds with Fintiba and the bank they work with.  My name is Alisa Gafarova and support code 509-082-704 in my Fintiba account. I have transferred my money on the 25th of June, after that I received a request of confirming the source of my funds. All documents were attached on the 2nd of July and I am still waiting for the outcome. I got a request for additional documents on the 30th of July, it took some time to prepare new documents. The whole procedure of confirming funds is awfully long. Okay, I acknowledge that there is a law and the bank is obliged to confirm where the funds come from but it is unbelievably long. How can it take 2 months? How? I haven’t got an eternity ahead of me as many other people. The translation of documents is also pretty expensive taking into consideration that they ask to do a certified translation in Germany in the majority of cases. I have wasted a lot of money on that. Fintiba either rarely answers requests or it takes a lot of time for them to answer.  VISA depends on the the blocked account.\nIt is really complicated to do something without this confirmation of my blocked account. It is crucial for VISA approval. Please finish checking my documents. I am out of power and all resources. It is so nervous and devastating waiting for the outcome for such a long time. I would not want any other person to go through it. Many other people also complain about it. All this is just crazy. The amount of money lost is not meaningless. I am highly disappointed.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Hello, my Account ID is 145-454-587. The compliance timer reached 'Expiré' 3 days ago. Could you please escalate this to the team for immediate manual approval? Thank you!\"", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Dear Fintiba Support Team and Management,\n\nI am writing to formally reject the unauthorized opening and activation of my blocked account on August 7, 2026.\n\nI strictly object to your instruction to close the account manually through your portal. Doing so would unfairly trigger the €159 Fintiba Plus setup fee and monthly administrative fees for services that you failed to provide when they were legally and contractually required.\n\nPlease note the following critical facts:\n\n1. Gross Operational Delay: My verification process was completely frozen by Fintiba from June 11, 2026, until August 4, 2026 (nearly 2 months). This completely violates your advertised processing times.\n\n2. Prior Cancellation: On August 4, 2026—while my profile was still unverified—I sent a formal request to terminate our relationship and demanded a full refund. You completely ignored this legal communication and proceeded to retroactively activate the account 3 days later, on August 7, 2026.\n\n3. Severe Damages: Because of your 2-month delay, I was unable to obtain my visa. My presence was mandatory at the Berlin campus on August 6, 2026. Due to your failure to deliver the Sperrbestätigungin time, my educational plans have been severely disrupted.\n\nYour package premium services (including the health insurance component of Fintiba Plus) are now entirely obsolete for me. Your retroactive activation of the account on August 7 is a clear attempt to enforce unjust fees (€159 setup fee + monthly fees) for a contract you breached through severe operational negligence.\n\nMy Demands:\n\n* Do NOT force manual portal closure: I demand that your management team closes this account internally as a \"Service Failure / Cancellation prior to activation\".\n\n* 100% Full Refund: I demand the immediate return of the full €12,073 without any deductions or withholding of the €159 fee.\n\nIf you do not confirm the waiver of all fees and the initiation of the 100% refund within 48 hours, I will immediately proceed with:\n\n1. An official complaint to the German Federal Financial Supervisory Authority (BaFin).\n\n2. A formal dispute submission via the European Online Dispute Resolution platform.\n\n3. Escalation to the Verbraucherzentrale (German Consumer Protection Agency) regarding unfair business practices and systemic delays causing financial damages to international students.\n\nI expect a response from a senior supervisor or compliance manager immediately.\n\nSincerely,\nSofiya Kh. \nFintiba ID: 1968423", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Fintiba is failing to meet the deadlines for providing the Blocking Confirmation, which is required to obtain a visa. The Agreements and Declaration of Consent state that we will receive the Blocking Сonfirmation  immediately upon receipt of funds. After the funds are deposited, Fintiba demands documents proving the origin of the funds but doesn't send a Blocking Confirmation. So the process isn't proceeding as described in Fintiba's documents! Fintiba doesn't set any time limits for itself. It takes weeks or even months for the funds to be verified. This is nonsense! I don't understand how unverified funds can sit in an account for so long.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "C'était pas vraiment ce que je recherche. Je suis déjà Docteur et chercheur et les questions était liés plutôt au Master ou moins. Je voulais savoir est ce que je peux relancer un doctorat même si je suis âgée... donc C'était autre chose.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The call centre waiting time is unacceptable, and the treatment from the agents has been unacceptable. I have not received my money for 2 months now, they said it is a problem with the bank. And the transfer needs to be done manually, but it has been months, and they cannot give me a date to expect my money back. I am in financial and emotional distress thanks to this.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Absolute Nightmare – Left Without Money or Food for a Week Due to an App Bug\nI am a 22-year-old girl who just arrived in Germany alone. I chose Fintiba expecting a smooth process to unblock my account and access my funds, but it has turned into an absolute nightmare.\nIt has been a full week, and I am completely stranded without a single cent. I cannot buy food or pay for public transport. I have successfully completed every single step, including the video legitimation. However, due to a technical bug in their app, it keeps displaying a warning saying I still need to complete video legitimation—even though it was already passed successfully!\nThis is a minor glitch that an IT technician could manually fix in 5 minutes, yet I am left calling customer support every single day only to be told to \"just wait.\" It is Friday, and office hours are about to end for the weekend. How am I supposed to wait when I don't even have money for basic food?\nI never imagined a bank would leave people starving in a foreign country with zero support. If I had known they were this irresponsible, I would have never trusted them with my money. Unacceptable service.\nticket number- 1320107\n\nTitle: WebID Re-completed – Ticket #1320107\nBody:\nI have just re-completed my video legitimation via WebID.\nMy funds are already received (confirmed by phone support today), and ticket #1320107was internally escalated.\nPlease sync the new status from WebID immediately and manually approve the legitimation on my Fintiba account so the \"Pending\" status changes and I can access my blocked account for payout setup!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am writing this review out of absolute desperation. I live now outside Germany, and my funds were transferred locally from within Germany to my Fintiba blocked account. I uploaded all the requested \"Source of Funds\" documents more than 60 days ago, Then, I received a response from the Compliance Team at FIB Frankfurt International Bank AG requesting additional documents. I submitted the requested documents 21 days ago, but I have not received any response since then.\n\nThe German Embassy already gave me a final extension until August 2th to submit my Blocking Confirmation, but that deadline has now passed. If this document is not issued within the next few days, my visa will be officially rejected, and my entire future will be ruined due to this unreasonable delay.\n\nCustomer support on the phone and via email keeps telling me to wait, but I am running out of time. I urgently request the management or a compliance supervisor to look into my file and approve it immediately.\n\nKonto ID: 1932453\nParty ID: 2042526", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Full scam. The Worst blocked provider. After getting your money they will not start payouts on time. Every payouts are delayed by more than 5 working days, their actual claim.\nFor me it took more than 2 weeks to get the first payment after they had confirmed my payouts were intiated. The second payout has still  not arrived and today is the 5 working day, the maximum time they claim for sending payments.\nWhen i called them their agent simply said to wait until 5 days to check if i receive the payment. I must inform them only if funds are not received with in5 working days so that they can escalate and execute the transfer again, which will take additional 5 working days. So they are telling me to wait 10 working days in total to get the payout of the current month. Its 6 august and I have already missed to pay my house rent, and other utility bills solely due to their delay. Even if I receive the money in the coming days, after half of the month gone, i have to pay fines upto hundreds of euros for late payment of rent and other bills due to their delay.\n\nEvery call and every email will end up in frustration and disappointment. I have been aware about their ill business practices overtime, so I kept BaFin informed about about my entire experience using their poor services. Fintiba will keep using all the ways to delay your payments and earn as much interest on your money, until they are legally obliged to return. So, avoid Fintiba whatsoever, dont get scammed.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Leider kann ich Fintiba nicht empfehlen.\nDie letzte Auszahlung meines Sperrkontos ist auch nach über einem Monat und sechs Tagen noch immer nicht erfolgt. Trotz zahlreicher E-Mails und mehrerer Telefonate habe ich weder eine Lösung noch eine klare Auskunft erhalten.\nBesonders enttäuschend ist, dass weiterhin Kontoführungsgebühren berechnet werden, obwohl die vertraglich geschuldete Auszahlung aussteht. Als Kunde erwartet man einen zuverlässigen Service und eine zeitnahe Bearbeitung, vor allem wenn es um existenziell wichtige Gelder geht.\nDie mangelhafte Kommunikation und die lange Verzögerung haben bei mir zu erheblichen finanziellen Problemen geführt.\nIch hoffe, dass Fintiba seinen Kundenservice und die Bearbeitungszeiten künftig deutlich verbessert", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Am 30. Juli 2026 wurde das Geld für mein Sperrkonto überwiesen. Obwohl die Überweisung rechtzeitig erfolgt ist, wurde der Zahlungseingang erst am 03. August 2026 bestätigt. Diese Verzögerung hat mich bereits erheblich belastet und mir große Sorgen bereitet.\nNachdem der Zahlungseingang bestätigt wurde, wurde ich aufgefordert, Unterlagen zur Überprüfung der Herkunft der Geldmittel (Source of Funds Verification) einzureichen. Ich habe alle angeforderten Dokumente sofort vollständig hochgeladen.\nTrotzdem warte ich bis heute auf die Bestätigung meines Sperrkontos. Diese lange Bearbeitungszeit bringt mich in eine sehr schwierige Situation. Ich benötige die Sperrkontobestätigung dringend für meinen Antrag auf ein deutsches Studentenvisum. Jede weitere Verzögerung gefährdet meinen Visumsantrag und damit auch meinen rechtzeitigen Studienbeginn im Wintersemester 2026/2027.\nIch habe den Kundenservice bereits mehrfach kontaktiert, jedoch bisher keine zufriedenstellende Lösung oder verbindliche Auskunft erhalten. Ich bitte daher dringend darum, meinen Fall schnellstmöglich zu bearbeiten und mir die Sperrkontobestätigung auszustellen.\nSollte ich in den nächsten Tagen keine Rückmeldung oder keine Lösung meines Falls erhalten, sehe ich mich gezwungen, eine formelle Beschwerde bei der Bundesanstalt für Finanzdienstleistungsaufsicht (BaFin) einzureichen. Dies möchte ich eigentlich vermeiden, hoffe jedoch auf eine schnelle und faire Bearbeitung meines Anliegens.\nSupport Code: 408-344-405", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The acoustics were terrible - a constant echo in the background from the presenter and I could not hear what was being said.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I requested you to update my transfer document as my name first name is missing  and my first name is written in my surname. You have not corrected it.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I thought writing here would help them realize how poor their support system is and encourage them to improve it, but unfortunately, nothing has changed. They replied by saying that their team had already responded to my case. However, that response did nothing to solve the actual problem. \n\nIn their reply, they claim that the fee has already been reduced, but it has not. The fee is still being added to the amount I have to transfer. I honestly don’t understand how a support system can be this ineffective. The only issue that needs to be resolved is removing the fee that I should not be paying. It is that simple, yet after weeks of emails and phone calls, nothing has been done.\n\nI am really tired of this support system that doesn’t provide any actual support. I am also tired of constantly emphasizing how urgent my case is, only to realize that it seems to mean nothing to them. The issue is still exactly the same, yet they keep sending responses that do not match what is actually happening with my account.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Worst service ever. It’s been more than 25 days, and I’m still waiting for my source of funds to be verified. There has been no clear explanation of how long this process will take.\n\nThis has been a nightmare for me. The embassy appointments are being booked up quickly, and I’m afraid I won’t be able to secure an appointment because of this delay which is not acceptable.\n\nThe customer service is even worse. I keep sending emails and making phone calls, but I haven’t received any helpful response or solution that addresses my case.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "They don't talk about uni assist which is the most important factor", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Not much time is given to all participants to ask questions", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I opened my Fintiba account around July/August 2025, but I did not fund the blocked account because there was a long visa appointment backlog in my country.\n\nThis year, in July/August 2026, I was ready to begin my visa process. When I logged into my Fintiba account, I discovered that it had been suspended due to inactivity. I was advised to create a new account using a different email address, which I did.\nDuring the verification process, I uploaded my passport, but it was rejected twice. I later realized that I had uploaded it as a PDF instead of an image. After uploading the correct image format\nHowever, it has now been 2 weeks and 3 days, and my account has remained stuck on \"Verification in Progress.\nI have contacted your support team multiple times, but I have not received any response. I have been left in the dark, and I urgently need to complete my blocked account verification so I can apply for my German student visa before my studies begin in October.\n\nI would greatly appreciate it if you could review my verification as soon as possible or let me know if you require any additional documents from me.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Fintiba lies on this website. In reply to my latest complaint here (the only way to communicate with them is by righting comments on this site), they say the following: \"However, a follow-up email has been sent with a comprehensive explanation outlining the exact document required. Once our team receives this document, we will be able to proceed further. They asked for the requisites for a refund, which I sent them in an email on 29 July.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Me and tens of other people were supposed to receive our August payout since 31.07\nThey didn’t send anything, they don’t say why, and contacting them is harder than reaching Messi. They don’t answer emails and answer the phone after a very long wait with no use and keep saying today or tomorrow. This is my money in the blocked account and I want it", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Terrible customer service and endless delays!I am extremely disappointed with Fintiba. The waiting times are unacceptably long, and their customer support completely ignores emails and queries. Because of their lack of response and total neglect, my visa appointment and travel plans are now seriously delayed. If you are on a tight schedule, avoid this service. They do not care about your deadlines.They have been delaying the verification of my source of funds for over 50 days now.Fintiba is a Nightmare.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Thank you for your public response. However, I am disappointed that you reply here while my emails and important questions remain unanswered.\n\nI contacted your support on 10 July 2026 regarding my daughter’s blocked account, but I have received no reply. I was also informed that the delay with my blocked account was due to a technical issue being handled by your IT team. More than 10 days have passed without any solution or meaningful update.\n\nPublic replies are appreciated, but what I really need is a real solution. Please respond to my emails and provide a clear update on my case.\n\nSupport Ticket: #1289775", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "My experience with Fintiba has been extremely disappointing, and I would not recommend this bank to anyone.\nOpening the blocked account was already a frustrating process. It took three days because I was repeatedly asked to submit the same documents. I had to send a selfie with my passport twice and my verified passport copy twice before the account was finally opened.\nAfter the account was opened, I transferred the required funds. Shortly afterward, I was asked to provide proof of the source of funds. I submitted all requested documents on 22 June.\nFrom that moment, everything stopped. The first review period expired, and despite sending multiple emails to the support team, I received no meaningful response—only automatic replies. Then the second review period also expired. My application became invalid while I continued emailing support, and even a close friend of mine in Germany contacted them on my behalf to ask about my case. We received no useful response.\nFinally, on 3 August, after about 45 days, I received another email asking me to submit additional documents. To my surprise, they requested the very same documents that I had already submitted weeks earlier.\nThis unacceptable delay has put my university admission at serious risk. I may lose my university place because I have been unable to book my visa appointment without the source-of-funds verification.\nThe customer service has been extremely poor, communication has been almost nonexistent, and the entire process has caused unnecessary stress, wasted time, and put my future studies in jeopardy. I strongly advise others to think carefully before choosing Fintiba.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "\"Terrible experience. I transferred €12,211 on 22 June 2026. They requested source of funds documents, which I submitted immediately. After more than 40 days of waiting, they asked for additional paperwork. I provided everything again. Still no response, no approval, no update. My visa and study plans are now at serious risk because of their endless delays. Their support team is unresponsive and unhelpful. I do not recommend Fintiba to any international student.\"", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "This is the second time I am writing here after another extremely frustrating day filled with unsuccessful emails and phone calls. I honestly cannot understand how a customer service system can be this ineffective.\n\nThe worst part is the email support. I have explained my problem in detail every single time, trying my best to avoid any confusion, but the replies I receive are completely unrelated to my actual issue. It feels like I am not communicating with a real person, but just receiving copy-pasted automatic responses from a robot. Instead of solving a simple problem, every interaction creates even more frustration.\n\nI never wanted to have an account with Fintiba. The first time I tried to use Fintiba, I already had problems sending my money, and the issue was never properly solved. I decided to use another blocked account provider, where I was actually happy with the service. Unfortunately, because of a technical issue, I was transferred to Fintiba.\n\nAs an international student trying to complete my residence permit process, time is extremely important. But now, months later, I am still dealing with the same problems caused by this transfer. I cannot even move forward with my residence permit process because of these unresolved issues.\n\nI was told that because I was transferred from Coracle, I would not have to pay any fees. However, the first time I was transferred, the app still charged a fee. After weeks of waiting and countless attempts to get help, the fee was finally reduced somehow.\n\nNow the exact same problem is happening again. The app is asking me to pay a fee that I was clearly told I do not have to pay. I have been trying for months to get this fixed, and nothing happens. Every email leads nowhere. Every phone call ends with the same sentence: “Your case has been escalated, please wait.” But waiting is not a solution when there is a real problem that needs to be fixed.\n\nIt should not be this difficult to remove a fee that should not exist in the first place. Being told that I do not need to pay a fee while repeatedly being asked to pay it, and then receiving no real support to correct it, feels extremely unfair and unacceptable.\n\nIf you are an international student coming to Germany and you need a blocked account, think carefully before choosing Fintiba. The biggest problem is not only the technical issues that can happen and perferctly understandable but it is the customer service. When you actually need help, you find yourself completely stuck with no effective support.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Their website is so bad and slow they didn’t even give me the chance to become their customer. The sign up flow is filled with bugs, reset password emails take a full day to land in your inbox. Very slow and inconvenient website overall.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am writing to complain about my inability to get block account money from Finbita for more than a year! \nLast time, you said my residence permit must contain both front and back cover. I sent you both front and back cover of the residence permit again, but this time, you said my residence permit is about to expire. If that's a problem, why didn't you mention in your first email? Your company gave me an impression that it's just fabricating different excuses to prevent me from getting money from my block account! that is very very poor customer service! And I demand a detailed explanation on how and when I can get my money from my block account? Why is your company holding my block account money for so long? Your company shd tell me when I can start getting the block account money once all the requirements are fulfilled and all the requirements shd be listed in one single email, not in countless separate emails.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Fintiba paid, after four months, what it was supposed to pay every month. Thank you for your concern. However, it is already August 4, and the next payment has still not arrived. Please resolve this issue, as customer support, as usual, is unable to do anything", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am an international student who chose Fintiba for my blocked account while preparing for my studies in Germany.\n\nAfter a prolonged Source of Funds review and multiple requests for additional documentation, I decided to close my case and request a refund because I am unable to provide further documents that are not accessible to me.\n\nI have emailed both FIB and Fintiba requesting the closure of my case and the refund of my funds. My latest support ticket is #1313012. Unfortunately, I have not received a response regarding my request.\n\nIn addition, I am currently unable to complete the account closure process because the OTP verification required for closing the account is not working, leaving me unable to proceed with the cancellation myself.\n\nThis situation has become extremely stressful. My university enrollment and student visa process depend on having access to my funds, and every additional delay increases the risk of losing my academic year.\n\nI fully understand the importance of compliance procedures. However, after deciding to close my case, I simply expect timely communication and a clear refund process.\n\nI respectfully ask FIB/Fintiba to:\n\n* Respond to my refund request (Support Ticket #1313012).\n* Resolve the OTP verification issue preventing me from closing my account.\n* Confirm the account closure.\n* Process the refund of my funds as soon as possible.\n\nI sincerely hope this matter can be resolved promptly.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "DRINGEND: Visum gefährdet aufgrund einer Compliance-Verzögerung von über 20 Tagen – Account-ID: 1962930\n\nIch schreibe diese Bewertung aus völliger Verzweiflung. Ich lebe mittlerweile außerhalb Deutschlands, und meine Gelder wurden innerhalb Deutschlands auf mein Fintiba-Sperrkonto überwiesen. Ich habe bereits vor mehr als 20 Tagen alle angeforderten Unterlagen zum „Source of Funds“ (Herkunft der Gelder) hochgeladen, jedoch bis heute keinerlei Rückmeldung oder Update vom Compliance-Team der FIB Frankfurt International Bank AG erhalten.\n\nMeine Frist bei der deutschen Botschaft, um meine Blocking Confirmation (Sperrkonto-Bestätigung) einzureichen, endet am 15.August. Wenn dieses Dokument nicht innerhalb der nächsten Tage ausgestellt wird, wird mein Visumantrag offiziell abgelehnt, und meine gesamte Zukunft wird aufgrund dieser völlig unangemessenen Verzögerung zerstört.\n\nDer Kundenservice teilt mir sowohl telefonisch als auch per E-Mail immer wieder mit, dass ich warten soll, aber mir läuft die Zeit davon. Ich bitte dringend die Geschäftsleitung oder einen Compliance-Vorgesetzten, meinen Fall zu prüfen und die Freigabe sofort zu veranlassen.\nAccount-ID: 1962930", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have had a very disappointing experience with Fintiba. The advertised monthly account maintenance fee is €9.90, but I was charged €19.80 one month and €29.70 the following month. I opened my account in May 2026, so I don’t understand why I was charged the equivalent of two months and then three months of maintenance fees.\n\nI have contacted customer support and hope they can explain these charges, but until then I find this billing very confusing and concerning. I expected transparent and predictable fees, not unexpected charges that are much higher than the stated monthly amount.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The only thing I can recommend is reporting Fintiba's actions to BaFin and the police. They have stolen my money. I have been unable to get a refund for months.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Arbeiten da eigendlich nur begriffsstutzige? Ich habe ein Sperrkonto für eine Verpflichtungserklärung beantragt. 3000 € für 3 Monate.  Trotz zweimaligen anschreibens und zweimaligen telefonierens ist man nicht in der Lage ein \"Blocked Amount\" über 3000 € (zzgl Gebühren) auszustellen. Das Ganze geht jetzt schon über eine Woche, das Versprechen ein Sperrkonto ist in wenigen Minuten eingerichtet ist schlicht unwar. Ich brauche das jetzt und nicht irgenwann mal.\nWeder im Browser noch in der App lassen sich die korrekten Zahlen eingeben. \nHeute bekomme ich neue Dokumente, ein leer(ohne Zahlen) und eins wieder mit den selben, falschen Zahlen wie gestern.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ich weiß nicht, was mit diesem Unternehmen los ist, wenn Sie nicht in der Lage sind, die angeforderte Arbeit zu erledigen, die Leute freizulassen oder günstige und klare Informationen zu geben, werde ich Sie noch dazu bringen, meine Situation in den kommenden Tagen zu regeln, sonst würde ich wirklich bei BaFin beschweren \nFranck Soh wandji", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Sehr geehrtes Fintiba-Team,\n\nich habe heute eine Aufforderung erhalten, die Zahlung für mein Sperrkonto durchzuführen.\n\nDie Zahlung wurde jedoch bereits über TransferMate getätigt und registriert. Könnten Sie bitte prüfen, ob der Betrag meinem Konto zugeordnet wurde?\n\nVielen Dank.\n\nMit freundlichen Grüßen\nEVRAD BELVIN DJOMO DACTOUO", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I genuinely cannot believe I am writing another review.\n\nMy June and July blocked account payouts were severely delayed, leaving me without access to my own living money for two months in a row. I spent an unbelievable amount of time calling, emailing, opening tickets and escalating the issue before I finally received those payments.\n\nAfter that experience, I specifically contacted Fintiba about my upcoming August payout because I was afraid the same thing would happen again. On 23 July, Fintiba assured me in writing that they would personally follow my August payout, monitor it closely and ensure it was processed smoothly and on time.\n\nIt is now August 3d. My August payout is late too, I was supposed to recieve it on July 31st.\n\nTheir response? My case is being treated “with priority,” my payout is “being processed,” and I will receive it “as soon as possible.”\n\nAs soon as possible is not an acceptable answer after what happened with June and July.\n\nThis is now three consecutive months of problems accessing my monthly blocked-account funds. The entire purpose of this service is to ensure an international student receives their monthly living allowance. These funds pay for accommodation, health insurance, food and basic living expenses. Students cannot simply go indefinitely without them.\n\nDuring the previous delays, my bank account went into debt, my cards were blocked, and I had to request extensions for essential payments because I could not access my own money.\n\nI have heard enough apologies, explanations, technical issues, promises, escalations and requests for ticket numbers. I need my monthly payouts to actually arrive on time.\n\nAfter everything that happened with June and July, and after Fintiba explicitly promised to monitor August personally, allowing the exact same situation to happen again is absolutely unacceptable.\n\nThree months in a row is no longer an isolated technical problem. Something is fundamentally wrong with the service I am receiving, and I do not recommend fintiba to anyone based on my experience.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ich bin derzeit etwas enttäuscht über die langen Bearbeitungszeiten bei der Verifizierung. Obwohl das Geld von einem deutschen Konto überwiesen wurde, dauert die Prüfung sehr länger als erwartet. Gerade bei zeitkritischen Angelegenheiten, wie einem Visumantrag, können solche Verzögerungen problematisch sein.\nIch hoffe, dass die Bank ihre Prozesse zukünftig beschleunigt und die Kommunikation mit den Kunden verbessert. Mit einer schnelleren Bearbeitung und mehr Transparenz könnte das Kundenerlebnis deutlich verbessert werden. Wenn diese Punkte optimiert werden, würde ich die Bank gerne weiterempfehlen, denn ein zuverlässiger und effizienter Service ist für viele Kunden ein entscheidender Faktor.\n\nTicket: 1309493\nUnterstützungscode: 048-672-258", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "After transferring the funds to my account ,they needed a source of funds, which is totally fine by me.\nThe problem is that I've been waiting for a reply for more than 55 days,\nand now I can't start my semester in time which means I need to wait one more semester to travel .\nThat was not a very good experience for me.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The customer service has been extremely disappointing. During my last phone call, when I explained that the same problem had happened again and how serious the consequences were for me, the representative suddenly acted as if he could no longer hear me and then disconnected the call. Whether it was intentional or not, that was my experience. When I immediately tried to call back, I waited for about over 20 minutes without anyone answering. \n\nThis has been one of the most frustrating customer service experiences I have ever had. I cannot recommend Fintiba to anyone who may need timely support. If everything works perfectly, you may never have a problem. But if something goes wrong, don’t expect quick or reliable assistance.\n\nI have been trying to resolve a simple issue with Fintiba for almost a month, and despite countless emails and waiting, the problem still has not been fixed. This has caused unnecessary stress and put my residence permit application at risk because I cannot complete the required blocked account transfer.\n\nThe customer service has been extremely disappointing. Responses are slow, and even when they do reply, the issue remains unresolved. I have repeatedly had to explain the same problem and wait for updates, yet nothing has been properly addressed.\n\nWhat is most frustrating is that this is not even the first time this exact issue has happened. It was supposedly resolved before, but now it has occurred again, leaving me in the same situation despite previous assurances.\n\nI cannot recommend this service to anyone, especially if your situation involves strict deadlines or immigration matters where delays can have serious consequences. Based on my experience, you should be prepared for long waiting times, poor communication, and unnecessary stress.\n\nThe service may seem fine until you actually need help. Once you have a problem, don’t expect much support.\n\nI have been trying to resolve the same issue for almost a month, yet it still hasn’t been fixed. The delays and lack of effective assistance have put me under enormous stress, especially because this issue affects important deadlines in my case as an international student.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I extended my account in August for 12 months. I already had the money needed for 2 months, and they asked me to pay the needed amount for the remaining 10 months.\n\nSince last October, I have received no money at all, and I have been contacting them to resolve the issue since February with no clear answer and no one helping me to this day. I tried asking for a supervisor or someone who could solve my problem, but they always say they can't do it or find some excuse.\n\nThe customer support is one of the worst I have ever experienced. It takes them at least 20 minutes to answer, and sometimes they just hang up. The employees are impolite and sometimes shout at customers, even trying to shift the blame onto me.\n\nTo resolve the issue quickly, I asked them in May to extend my account for a 9-month period, thinking I might be able to get my money back this way. Instead, they sent me an extension for 12 months, asking me to pay for the whole duration even though I already have enough money for 10 months in my account.\n\nFor anyone considering opening an account with Fintiba, I would not recommend it at all. It might all go smoothly, but the moment you have a problem, you will have to go through one of the worst customer support systems ever.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Not satisfied! It has been more than two weeks since I requested the closure of my blocked account, and I have submitted all the necessary official documents. Still waiting for the payout of the account balance, which I need urgently.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "It has been more than 1 month that i am waiting for my blocking confirmation even after everything completed they are still not providing me blocking confirmation \nMy ticket no.-1295394\nemail:- aryanfg011@gmail", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "worst experience with fintiba.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "A completely irresponsible bank that has put international students’ educational lives at risk due to a lack of customer support. They ignore even the smallest feedback and fail to respond to repeated complaints sent by email, ticket, or phone. No matter your situation, or how close you are to deadlines or appointments, you won’t receive any response after 3 weeks at the moment.\n\nI strongly suggest everyone to review their negative comments and to check other people’s experiences on Google or Reddit before choosing them.\n\nI genuinely haven't got any response almost for one month for none my tickets below from the bank side:\n\nFintiba Ticket: 1308355 *, 1299963, 1311436\nFIB Ticket: 9011 *, 7965\nBaFin Complain ID: 21***4 (In progress)\n\nUPDATE (Aug 25, 2026):\nThere has still been no update from Fintiba Support. The refund/withdrawal process remains unavailable, and none of my OTP-based withdrawal attempts submitted over the past 15 days has been accepted. BaFin is following this matter, and I hope it will soon be resolved following a thorough review of the case.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "URGENT: Extremely long Source of Funds verification – My studies are at risk\nI am writing this review because I have been waiting for a very long time for my Source of Funds verification to be completed.\nI submitted all the requested documents, including additional documents requested by the Compliance Team. Despite my full cooperation, my verification is still pending, and I have received only automatic replies asking me to wait.\nThis delay has already caused serious problems for my study plans in Germany. I have already missed valuable time and even lost the opportunity to book an earlier student visa appointment because my blocked account has not yet been approved.\nI fully understand that compliance checks are important and necessary. However, I believe that applicants deserve clear communication and a reasonable processing time, especially after providing every requested document.\nI kindly ask the Compliance Team or a supervisor to review my case as soon as possible.\nI sincerely hope this review helps bring attention to my case and encourages a faster resolution.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "فتحت حساب اول مرة من ٧ اشهر و انتم لم تساعدوني في استعادته تتأخرون دوما في الرد لقد أجلت سفري بسبب إهمالكم للعملاء", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I do not recommend Fintiba at all.\n\nWhile opening a blocked account was relatively straightforward, getting my blocked money back was an extremely frustrating and stressful experience. It took several months after I submitted my refund request before I finally received my money. During that time, Fintiba continued deducting account fees, even though I was waiting for the refund process to be completed.\n\nCustomer support was one of the biggest disappointments. Most of the time I received generic template responses that did not address my questions. In some cases, different agents repeated contradictory information, making it clear they were not familiar with my case or its history.\n\nAnother major issue was the paperwork. Although Fintiba states on its website that everything is handled online, I was instructed to send a legalized document by postal mail. After waiting for weeks, I contacted them several times and received different answers from different agents. Eventually, it became clear that my document had either been lost or never successfully received. I had to complete the entire process again, pay for postage a second time, and spend even more time following up.\n\nThe whole experience was mentally exhausting. At one point, because of the lack of transparency, inconsistent communication, and endless delays, I even started wondering whether I would ever get my money back.\n\nIf you're considering Fintiba, keep in mind that opening a blocked account is only part of the story. If you later need to close the account and have your money refunded, you may face a long, stressful, and poorly managed process.\n\nThankfully, I eventually received my money, but only after months of persistent follow-ups. Based on my experience, I cannot recommend Fintiba.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "For reference, my Fintiba customer ID is 615-974-461.\n\nMy experience with Fintiba was fine until I had to extend my blocked account. That's where everything started to fall apart.\n\nThe extension itself was confirmed by email, but my app still showed that no next payout was registered. I contacted support because I wanted to make sure my monthly payout would actually arrive. Instead of looking into my account, I kept receiving the same basic instructions. I was told to register my payout myself, even though I had already sent screenshots showing that this was impossible because the entire payout page was greyed out and there was nothing I could click or edit.\nI tried everything. I used the AI chatbot, which was only able to repeat general instructions. When I followed those instructions, they simply did not match what was actually shown in my account. I emailed support multiple times, and my replies either went unanswered or ignored what I had actually written. I even had to email the CEO's address just to get a response. When I called customer support, I waited around 40 minutes, only to be told that my money should arrive automatically. That wasn't my question. I wasn't asking what should happen. I was asking someone to actually look into why it wasn't happening.\n\nThe biggest problem is not that technical issues exist. Technical issues happen. The problem is that nobody seemed willing to spend even a few minutes checking my account. I spent about a month trying to resolve this. Every time I explained the situation, I was sent back to the same generic instructions, the chatbot, or told to wait.\nBecause of this, I have been left without access to my own money. I have had to postpone my appointment with the immigration office, I have not been able to switch to public health insurance, I cannot pay my rent, and I cannot cover basic living expenses. This is a company that manages blocked accounts for international students. When something goes wrong, there needs to be a reliable way to reach someone who can actually investigate and solve the problem instead of sending the same instructions over and over again.\n\nI was patient for a month. At this point, I simply can't afford to keep waiting.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Hello, Sir, You only allowed the questioning and answered of knowing people or Related to your country people not to other countries people like, Pakistan etc. \nBut Your provided information Better 🙂.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I previously told about my experience with their team and now the people who had the same issue their issue is getting fixed but even after 1 month i stand where i was last meanwhile people who faced this issue 10 days ago for no blocking confirmation their issue is solved when will i get my issue fixed give me a damn date \nTicket No. -1295394\nemail id -aryanfg011@gmail", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am writing this review out of utter frustration with Fintiba’s customer support and lack of internal coordination. My blocking process and account status are completely stalled, and no one is taking ownership to resolve my open issues.\nKey Issues & Ticket References:\n * Admission Letter Delay (Ticket #1292810): I inquired about uploading my admission letter back on June 30th. It was uploaded on July 16th, but support replied claiming I was missing a photo for health insurance. They completely failed to clarify that this photo issue was directly holding up my Block Confirmation. I only found this out after having to call them directly on July 28th.\n * Double Charge & Block Confirmation Pending (Ticket #1296595): On July 14th, I initiated my main bank transfer, which arrived on July 16th short by €318 (transferred €12,163, net received €11,845). I immediately paid an extra €59 via the app and filed a formal complaint. The €59 cleared on July 20th, yet the deducted amount is still missing, and I have NOT received my Block Confirmation or any resolution on this double charge.\n * Unresolved Support Requests (Ticket #1309680): Despite multiple attempts to follow up and submit requested information, my photo status remains unresolved, my double charge is ignored, and my critical visa documents are missing.\nCurrent Status:\n * Block confirmation: NOT RECEIVED\n * Health insurance photo: NOT RESOLVED / NOT UPLOADED\n * Missing/deducted funds: UNSOLVED\nIt is unacceptable that students dealing with strict visa deadlines are forced to jump through hoops and make international calls just to get basic clarity on disconnected support tickets.\nI demand immediate attention from management to reconcile my funds and issue my Block Confirmation right away.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "It was more informative. And my most of the questions about study visa in Germany was cleared.Thanks", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am extremely disappointed and stressed by Fintiba’s terrible compliance processing times, which are now putting my entire university admission and visa at risk. I am a student, and my father is fully funding my education and blocked account.Here is the timeline of our ongoing issue:\n- June 8, 2026: My father transferred the funds to open my blocked account.\n- June 11, 2026: We uploaded all required documents for the Source of Funds (SoF) verification, including my father's financial proofs.\n- July 15, 2026: After more than a month of silence, the compliance team claimed the documents were insufficient. They mistakenly stated that my father's bank statement didn't show his employer transfers, even though they were clearly visible! On the exact same day, we immediately re-uploaded the existing documents. My father then obtained and uploaded new additional proofs as soon as he received them.\n- Today is July 30, 2026: Still no response, no blocked account confirmation, and total silence.\n\nI must be on my university campus by August 6th. The German Embassy is ready to issue my national visa but is strictly waiting for Fintiba’s blocked account confirmation. Because of your severe delays and oversight, my academic future is on the line.Please review my case immediately and release my confirmation!\n\nFintiba ID: 1968423\nRegistered Email: vaskes dot valmos at gmail dot com", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am writing this review out of absolute\ndesperation. I live now outside Germany, and my funds were transferred locally from within Germany to my Fintiba blocked account. I uploaded all the requested \"Source of Funds\" documents more than 23 days ago, but I have received absolutely no response or update from the compliance team at FIB Frankfurt International Bank AG.\n\nThe German Embassy already gave me a final extension until August 8th to submit my Blocking Confirmation. If this document is not issued within the next few days, my visa will be officially rejected, and my entire future will be ruined due to this unreasonable delay.\n\nCustomer support on the phone and via email keeps telling me to wait, but I am running out of time. I urgently request the management or a compliance supervisor to look into my file and\napprove it immediately.\n\nAccount ID: 1899025", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I DON'T WANT THE INSURANCE, THEY DIDN'T GIVE ME AN OPTION TO CHOSE AND NOW I CAN'T HAVE THE NORMAL BLOCKED ACCOUNT", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Is it finitiba plan to kill people’s dream?? Is fintiba a racist company?!!! All funds transferred and source of funds uploaded yet no letter and embassy is strictly asking!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "My documents verification for blocked account activation has exceed 4 business days and still there is no response from their side, neither they are asking for documentation correction.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I completed my payment of blocked account on 2nd june and now it’s been a month but still i haven’t received my blocking confirmation. I have raised so ticket but from the last 1 month they are saying we are working on it even though it is a priority ticket but no response. \n\n\n\nWorst customer care they have 0 idea how long it will take to solve the issue they are only there to make you feel even worse and not to help \n\nI have called them multiple times but same response we’ll solve it “asap” bro i mean comeon how long asap doesn’t mean 1 month for your fault\n\nTicket No. 1295394", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I asked such a simple task of how to change my current foreign address and no one can help me. You chat bot does not do anything. No one replied to my issue, I has been 3 days now and you advertised that your staff will get back to me within 24 hours. That is such a lie.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ich bin wirklich enttäuscht von dieser Einrichtung und Sie gefährden mein gestrebtes Semester und falls diese vorkommt, werde ich verpflichtet, mich bei BAFIN zu beschweren \n\t1.\t**23.06 -**Das Sperrkonto wurde vollständig mit 12075 EUR aufgeladen. Der Geldeingang wurde bestätigt.\n\t2.\t**24.06-**Ich wurde darüber informiert, dass aufgrund meiner Staatsangehörigkeit eine erweiterte Prüfung der Herkunft der Geldmittel (Source of Funds) durchgeführt wird.\n\t3.\t**24.06 -**Alle angeforderten Unterlagen wurden eingereicht.\n\t4.\t22.07. – Der Kundenservice bestätigte mir per E-Mail, dass die Prüfung insgesamt 3 bis 4 Wochen dauern werde.\n\t5.\t28.07. – Fünfte Woche. Noch immer keine Entscheidung, kein Update und keine Antwort auf meine E-Mail.\n\nIch würde mich gern auf Ihre baldige Rückmeldung freuen , damit ich mit meinem Visiumantrag fortsetzen kann \nFranck Geovannie Soh wandji ( Referenznummer : 979-964-129 )", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "It's almost two months now and yet no one replies to our emails. It is frustrating.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Update (31 July 2026): Fintiba replied on Trustpilot claiming that my issue had been resolved. Unfortunately, this is not correct. According to your latest email regarding Ticket #1289775, I was informed that this is a technical issue. However, three full business days have passed since that email, and the problem is still not resolved. I am still waiting for my blocked account confirmation. You have already received my payment, but I have not yet received the service I paid for. I have fulfilled all of my obligations, and I kindly ask Fintiba to fulfill theirs. I sincerely hope this matter will be resolved as soon as possible. Thank you.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I cannot change the dates of the inssurance", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Katastrophaler Support! Mein Geld ist blockiert und mein Visum in Gefahr!Seit über einem Monat ignoriert Fintiba meine Tickets. Auf meinem Sperrkonto befindet sich noch mein Geld, aber ich habe keinerlei Zugriff darauf! Aufgrund eines App-Fehlers kann ich das Konto nicht verlängern: Es wird fälschlicherweise „bereits verlängert“ angezeigt, obwohl seit dem 30. Juni keine Auszahlungen mehr erfolgen. Trotz 7 Telefonaten hat mir niemand geholfen.Wegen Ihrer Trödelei muss ich jetzt eventuell ein neues Sperrkonto bei der Konkurrenz eröffnen. Das kostet wertvolle Zeit, die ich nicht habe. Wenn Sie nicht sofort handeln, kann ich meinen Aufenthaltstitel nicht rechtzeitig verlängern!Sollte der Fehler nicht bis zum 30.07.2026 behoben sein, geht eine offizielle Beschwerde an die BaFin.Fall sofort prüfen!Name: Mokhisorakhon AvazkhonovaPassnummer: FA9521302", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "​I am issuing a final warning before escalating to BaFin. I transitioned my Minor blocked account to an Adult account. The internal transfer of €12,004 and my additional SWIFT transfer of €159 have both fully cleared. My dashboard explicitly shows a balance of €12,163 and \"0€ to transfer.\"\n​Despite having my funds in full, Fintiba's system has failed to generate my Blocking Confirmation (Sperrbestätigung). I have been waiting 12 days, called 10 times, and sent multiple emails. Support only offers automated excuses and refuses to manually trigger the document.\n​I have exactly 10 days left to submit my visa application to the German Embassy, or my application will be discarded and my university semester ruined. Withholding legal financial documentation when funds are fully cleared is a massive compliance failure.\n​If my Sperrbestätigung is not in my portal until July 29,2026, I am filing a formal regulatory complaint with BaFin for withholding funds and documentation.\n​Ticket: 1297984", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "It was bad. They are not sending the bank details..", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Because did not get my mail reply", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ich bin äußerst enttäuscht vom Service von Fintiba. Meine Frau und ich erleben derzeit eine sehr belastende Situation, da die verzögerte Bearbeitung durch Fintiba unseren bevorstehenden Botschaftstermin direkt gefährdet.\nHier ist der Ablauf unseres Falls:\nAm 22.06.2026 haben wir Geld auf unsere Fintiba-Konten überwiesen. Am selben Tag wurden wir aufgefordert, Nachweise über die Herkunft der Mittel einzureichen. Dies habe ich umgehend am selben Tag erledigt.\nErst nach 14 Tagen und erst nach meiner aktiven Kontaktaufnahme mit dem Support erhielten wir überhaupt eine Rückmeldung – mit der Aufforderung, weitere Dokumente einzureichen. Meine Frau hat die geforderten Unterlagen am 10.07.2026 hochgeladen, ich meine am 13.07.2026.\nUnser Botschaftstermin ist bereits in wenigen Tagen (am 03.08.2026). Ich habe Fintiba mehrfach per E-Mail darauf hingewiesen, dass unser Fall dringend bearbeitet werden muss. Wir haben 8 Monate lang auf diesen Botschaftstermin gewartet! Fintiba zeigt jedoch keinerlei Verständnis für die Belastung und das Risiko, dass unser Antrag wegen dieser Verzögerungen abgelehnt werden könnte. Bis heute gibt es keine angemessene Reaktion.\nZusätzlich gibt es ein technisches Problem mit der Krankenversicherung in meinem Konto: Ich habe diese vor etwa 10 Tagen beantragt, aber weder die Unterlagen erhalten noch wurde sie aktiviert. Auch hierzu habe ich den Support kontaktiert, jedoch ohne jegliche Rückmeldung oder Lösung.\nReferenzdaten zu unseren Konten:\nMein Konto:\n  (Party ID): 2038901\n Ticket-IDs: 7914, 7752\nKonto meiner Frau:\n  (Party ID): 2038904\n Ticket-IDs: 7913, 7751\nIch fordere Fintiba dringend auf, unsere Fälle und das Problem mit der Krankenversicherung vor unserem Botschaftstermin am 03.08.2026 zu lösen. Sollte dies nicht geschehen, werde ich eine offizielle Beschwerde bei der Bundesanstalt für Finanzdienstleistungsaufsicht (BaFin) einreichen.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am honestly beyond frustrated and angry with Fintiba and FIB at this point.\n\nI have been waiting for weeks while my blocked account verification has been delayed, and throughout this entire process I have provided the documents requested and cooperated with every requirement. Yet I am now suffering the consequences of what appears to be a failure to properly read and understand the documents I submitted.\n\nWhat makes this especially infuriating is that the document clearly explained that the money bounced back because the bank was refusing the transfer. Instead of properly understanding what the document said, it appears that the fact that my name was mentioned was interpreted as me having sent money to my sponsor so that he could then send it to my blocked account.\n\nHow does that interpretation even make sense when the document clearly explains that the transaction was rejected/bounced back?\n\nAt this point, it honestly feels like nobody cares about the fact that there is a real person on the other side of this case whose visa and future are being affected. I have even found myself thinking, “Do they just see me as a problem and decide to make me suffer until I lose my chance?” I genuinely hope that is not the case, because it is difficult to understand how something this important could be handled with so little urgency.\n\nHuman beings are supposed to understand that their actions have consequences for other people. I have a visa application, a course start date and an entire plan depending on this process. I am the one paying the price for the failure to properly review my documents in the first place.\n\nIf additional documents or clarification were required, they could have simply asked me earlier. I have repeatedly shown that I am willing and able to provide whatever is required immediately. Instead, I have been left waiting week after week while my visa opportunity gets closer and closer to being jeopardized.\n\nAnd to be completely honest, the damage has already been done. The delays and mishandling of my case by FIB and Fintiba have already cost me valuable time and have put my visa and course start date in serious jeopardy.\n\nIf my case is delayed one more time despite everything that has already been submitted and explained, I will have very serious reason to question whether this is still simply an oversight or administrative mistake, or whether my case is being deliberately left unresolved.\n\nAt this point, I have done everything expected of me. I have provided the documents, responded to requests and waited patiently for weeks. I cannot continue paying the price for mistakes and delays that were not caused by me.\n\nThis is no longer just an inconvenience. There is a real person behind this case, and real consequences to these delays and incompetence. I sincerely hope FIB and Fintiba finally take responsibility, properly review everything that has already been provided, and resolve this without putting me through yet another waiting period.\n\nI have been patient. I have cooperated. I have provided what was requested. At this point, I need action — not another request to wait.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am an international student applying for a blocked account for my studies in Germany.\n\nMy application has now been under compliance review for approximately one month. Throughout this process, I have fully cooperated and submitted every document requested.\n\nOne week ago, after being asked for additional source-of-funds documentation, I submitted a comprehensive package containing all the documents I am reasonably able to provide. Since then, I have not received any meaningful update confirming whether the documents are sufficient or whether anything else is required.\n\nI have contacted both Fintiba Support and the Compliance Team multiple times regarding my case. My support tickets are #1271207, #1286906, and #1299537, and my compliance case reference is #7615. Despite these follow-ups, I have not received a meaningful response regarding the status of my verification.\n\nI completely understand that compliance reviews are necessary. However, the prolonged silence has become extremely stressful. My university enrollment and student visa application depend on the completion of this verification, and every day of delay increases the risk of missing my visa timeline and potentially losing an entire academic year.\n\nI am not asking for special treatment—only for clear communication and a timely decision. If the documentation I have provided is sufficient, please proceed with the verification. If there are specific additional documents that are genuinely required, please let me know exactly what they are. However, if my application cannot be approved based on the documentation I have already submitted, I kindly ask that you inform me as soon as possible and arrange a refund of my funds so that I can make alternative arrangements before it is too late.\n\nI sincerely hope this matter can be resolved promptly. At this point, I simply need a clear decision so I can move forward with my academic future, whether through an approval or, if that is not possible, a timely refund. Thank you.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "For standard application process, its very simple and straight forward but if we have some questions or other special request, it is very difficult to get the answers we need.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "​I have been waiting for over 12 days for customer support to update my health insurance plan from Mawista Comfort to Mawista Classic under my Fintiba Plus account. I sent multiple emails and follow-ups, but I haven't received any resolution or response. This delay is affecting my visa application process and account transfer. My name is Majd Alhasan. Please resolve this issue as soon as possible. \nticket 1288532\nUPDATE: Fintiba has now resolved the issue and updated my insurance plan to Mawista Classic after this review was posted. While the initial 18-day delay was frustrating, the requested change is finally completed.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ticket #1302691 and #1276983\n\nTimeline of the things happened:\n1. 19.06 - Blocked account funded in full (11.993 EUR). Transfer confirmed.\n2. 22.06 - Informed that an enhanced Source of Funds review applies due to my nationality.\n3. 23.06 - All requested documents submitted.\n4. 03.07 - Support confirms via email: review will take 3–4 weeks in total\n5. 22.07 - Week five. No decision, no update, no reply to email\n\nThe deadline was not mine. It was Fintiba's own. It expired and no one has communicated anything. What makes this hard to accept is how one-sided the arrangement is. My money was accepted immediately and without friction. Confirming that it exists - the single service I paid for - has now taken longer than the entire review period you yourselves specified, with no communication whatsoever. My residence permit application depends on this document \n\nI am fortunate to be inside Germany already. I can appear at the Ausländerbehörde in person, submit my application before my visa expires, file a complaint with BaFin, and instruct a German lawyer if necessary. A student waiting abroad for their visa appointment has none of those options and simply loses the semester.\n\nUnless I receive a substantive response and a firm date, I will be filing a formal complaint with BaFin and obtaining legal representation regarding the release of my funds and the damages caused by this delay.\n\nAll correspondence is saved. I will update this review the moment the matter is actually resolved.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Technical support based on a very limited AI  creating case assigning a support ticket number with a message that within 1 working day they might take care of the inquiry, then a few days later: (Hang in  there sorry for the delay in answering quickly, please give us more time to process your ticket),then International phone calls to the +49-69204342620 are placed on a long wait (15 + min. in my case) without anyone attending the call. This is really frustrating when time frame is very constraint. I read a few bad reviews before choosing FINTIBA, but I decided to follow the advise of our educational advisors based on their good past experiences with this provider. Verification time for the source of funds took longer than 30 days and so far no news on the process. I hope this Provider improves its services and customer support and feedback.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I will tell right away to anyone who, unlike me, decided to read the reviews before using the service: DO NOT USE FINTIBA. Your money will be locked, the customer support will not give you proper answers, clear deadlines, or reasons for the delay, ignoring the criticality of my timing and providing only automated templates. Your time and nerves will be wasted, and your future in Germany will be put at risk.\n\nAbout my situation: I am from a high-risk money-laundering country, so my sponsor, even though he is from Israel, was absolutely ready to provide all the necessary documents for verification. Almost exactly 4 weeks ago, I received a request to submit these documents—and we provided them immediately. Tomorrow it will be exactly 4 weeks that my documents have been \"pending.\" I haven't been asked to send anything else, clarify anything, nothing—my funds just arrived in the account (the cleared and uncleared balances matched perfectly), but I still haven't received the final Blocking Confirmation from Fintiba, which is strictly required to get a student visa. Due to this extreme delay, the Embassy has already set a deadline, causing an imminent risk of a visa rejection due to operational negligence.\n\nToday I am writing a review here, and at the end of the week, I am involving BaFin and legal representatives. I am not going to allow some shady financial companies with a good reputation that is left in the past to ruin my future, for which my father and I have worked so hard.\n\nLatest support ticket number: 1299401\n\nUpdates: they answered me here and via email (which is already a big deal), but nothing specific: no deadlines, no reasons of delay, nothing. The only hopeful thing is that they said they WILL CONTACT (when? oh, right, as soon as possible) with FIB about my case, but again, nothing specific.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am writing this out of sheer desperation as Fintiba and FIB Bank have missed all the deadlines of compliance review, putting my university admission and visa at direct risk.\n\nChronology of Events:\nMay 15: Funds were successfully received by Fintiba.\nJune 26: FIB Compliance requested additional Source of Funds verification, setting a deadline of July 10.\nJuly 2: I uploaded ALL requested documentation (8 days BEFORE the deadline).\nIt is now July 22. FIB compliance remains completely silent, and Fintiba support now asks for another 2-3 weeks of waiting. \n\nUpd: 2 days after this review, I finally got the compliance completed on July 24, but I'm still not sure whether the embassy will manage to issue my visa on time because of the delay.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I opened a Fintiba account at the beginning of 2026 and have been trying to close it and get my money back for over seven months. My issue remains completely unresolved: account not closed, funds not returned.\n\n“Your account has been successfully closed! Thank you for being our customer!”\n\nI received this message on 20 June 2026. Then, on 11 July 2026, I received another document stating that my account is still open and that a fee of €44.10 has been deducted for the past 7 months.\n\nThis reduces the blocked account balance I have been trying to close and retrieve my money for over seven months- unjustified fees eating into my own funds while I wait.\n\nFintiba refuses to provide clear answers to the following questions:\n- What is causing the delay ?\n- Why is the blocked account still active?\n- Why are fees being taken from my money?\n- When will I get my money back?\n\nThis ongoing delay has taken a severe toll on me mentally and on my family. I’m experiencing intense anxiety, sleep disruption, and constant worry. the stress has become so overwhelming that I’ve started feeling like there’s no way out anymore.\n\nTickets: 1228929, 1168775, 1173909, 1233623, 1285628.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am extremely disappointed with my experience with Fintiba.\nFor over two months, approximately €720 of my money has been stuck in my account despite my requesting its return multiple times. I have contacted customer support by both email and phone at least 10 times. Most of the time, I either received no meaningful help or my issue remained unresolved.\nEventually, I was told that I needed to close my account in order to receive my funds. I agreed and followed the instructions immediately. However, I still have not received my money, nor have I received any confirmation that my account has been closed. I continue to be left without answers while my funds remain inaccessible.\nWhat concerns me the most is how little urgency this situation has been treated with. If I had been someone who urgently depended on that money to pay rent, buy food, or cover an emergency, I would have been left in an incredibly difficult position. The lack of communication and accountability throughout this process has been unacceptable.\nAs a student, this money is important to me, and waiting months for funds that belong to me is simply not acceptable. I hope Fintiba seriously improves the way it handles customer support and cases like mine. Based on my experience, I cannot recommend this service.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "​I have been waiting for 7 days regarding my ticket #1296057. I also called your support team today, but I am still receiving generic automated emails with no actual update or progress on my issue.\nPlease escalate this ticket to a manager or senior support specialist immediately as this delay is impacting my visa/travel timeline.\n​Regards,\nMd Kamrul Islam", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am writing this review out of absolute desperation. I live now outside Germany, and my funds were transferred from Norway to my Fintiba blocked account. I uploaded the required 'Source of Funds' documents. After waiting for 19 days, the Compliance team at FIB Frankfurt International Bank AG sent me an email stating that the submitted documents were insufficient and requested additional paperwork. I promptly sent those additional documents 12 days ago. However, I have not yet received any response from the compliance team at FIB Frankfurt International Bank AG.\nThe German Embassy has already granted me a final deadline until July 26 to submit my booking confirmation. If this document is not issued within the next few days, my visa may be officially rejected, and my entire future will be ruined due to this unjustified delay.\nTime is running out for me. I urgently request management or a compliance supervisor to review and approve my file immediately please.\nMy order ID on Fintiba: 1959190", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I received the Source of Funds verification request because Nepal is listed as a high-risk country. However, the funds transferred to my Fintiba account were not sent by a private individual; they were transferred by a registered charitable organization in Germany that is sponsoring my studies.\n\nThe current Source of Funds form appears to be designed only for individual senders, as it requests details such as the sender’s personal ID, date of birth, and private bank statements. These requirements do not apply to an organizational sponsor.\n\nCould you please advise how I should complete the form in this situation? Alternatively, may I submit the sponsor’s official confirmation letter, registration documents, and other relevant organizational documents manually for verification?\n\nThe 2-week submission deadline is approaching, and I urgently need the blocking confirmation for my further processing. I have already contacted your support team via email but have not yet received a response. This issue is linked to ticket 1299032 (from the email thread under ticket 1280597).\n\nI would really appreciate it if you could at least guide me quickly in the reply to this review so that I can proceed with the required steps on time.\n\nSadly, I am having horrible experience with Fintiba, but I sincerely hope this can be resolved quickly with your support and guidance. Thank you.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have been dealing with Fintiba’s Source of Funds verification for almost three months. I submitted all the requested documents, including additional documents they asked for several times. Today, I received another email requesting five documents that I had already sent a long time ago.\n\nAll the money was transferred through German bank accounts, yet they continue asking for more Source of Funds documents without clearly explaining what is still missing or why the documents already submitted are not sufficient.\n\nI also requested a refund, but I was told that I first need to wait for confirmation from FIB and then wait another three to five weeks to receive my money. However, customer service previously told me that the refund would take only two weeks.\n\nIt seems that every employee gives a different answer, while nobody provides an actual solution. The communication is inconsistent, the process is extremely slow, and customers are repeatedly asked to submit the same documents. This has been an extremely frustrating and disappointing experience.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Fintiba is withholding my funds. I withdrew from the embassy queue before applying, so no application exists. Fintiba demands a document (Sperrfreigabe) or an email from the embassy that the embassy cannot physically generate for a non-existent case. I send them a message, and an email, and called them twice, support refuses to help, giving only robotic frustrating replies.\n\nThis is NOT a strange case, if they don't have a process in their system for such a case, and if me sending the money to them is not as easy as they sending it back then something is terribly suspicious here, as the more time they have the  money the more they take fees. BaFin complaint filed. \n\nTickets numbers: 1275712 , 1280910\nWaiting for the normal reply \"We sincerely apologize for your experience and completely understand your concern.....\" which is another robotic reply, I've been in this for 3 weeks and I can see other people for 10 months now.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have seen that you guys do not reply to any emails or pick up calls that we make. I am a student and I had to put my important priorities aside and go to Frankfurt to your office just for you to reply to my email there??? You could have done that without having me to travel 4 hours and spending money. Reply to my concerns ASAP. Or I will have to find some other way that will not be very beneficial for your trashy and irresponsible staff and company.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Stay far away from this online bank you will save yourself days of headache trying to reach their so called \"customer support\" and a lot of money.\n\nFirst of all the only real support you will get is in the form of an ai bot that is incompetent and never answers your questions, you cannot contact a real agent to assist you nor can you call them as their phone number just straight up doesn't work, your only option is to send them an email and wait for a response.\n\nI sent an email nearly a month ago and I still have not been contacted by the support team (1276789), and now I submitted another ticket (1299516) to close and refund my blocked account which had a large sum practically all my savings and they are playing the same game and not answering me which is leaving me in a desperate financial situation.\n\nTo sum it up you will never get any kind of support, they will gladly take your hard earned savings but if you ask for account closure and refund you will never hear from them. AVOID AT ALL COST.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I opened a Fintiba account at the beginning of 2026 and have been trying to close it and get my money back for over seven months. My issue remains completely unresolved: account not closed, funds not returned. I keep receiving automated replies and false \"resolved\" claims, but no real human help and no funds.\n\nWhat I did NOT get:\n\n- An exact date when my money will be returned\n- A clear timeline or written escalation plan\n- A single human agent who took ownership of my case\n\nWhat I DID get:\n\n- Automated/bot replies (multiple times)\n- Fake \"case resolved\" comments with no action\n-Vague promises that changed and were never met\n\nThis ongoing delay has taken a severe toll on me mentally and on my family. I'm experiencing intense anxiety, sleep disruption, and constant worry, the stress has become so overwhelming that I've started feeling like there's no way out anymore. \n\nExperiencing this company has been hell. A seven-month nightmare with no transparency, no humans, and no accountability.\n\nTickets: 1228929, 1168775, 1173909, 1233623, 1285628.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have been waiting for 20 days for my documents to be reviewed, and I still haven't received any response. My embassy appointment is getting closer, and this delay is causing me a lot of stress. The customer service has been very disappointing. I hope my application will be reviewed as soon as possible.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Completely unresponsive and irresponsible! I've been uploading my selfie for the verification process for a whole month, and Fintiba hasn't given me a single response. Neither a positive nor a negative answer! It is unacceptable for a service that deals with blocked accounts and visas to be this careless and slow. Zero communication, zero support. Do not trust them with your time or money.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "nur Katastrophe. wenn man ein Sperrkonto eröffnen lassen möchte, wird unterstützet und begleitet. sobald man das Geld raus möchte, wird immer ignorieret. kein IT support, kein Unterstützung, nix. ich versuche seit zwei Monaten mein Geld raus holen, kein Erfolg. man fühlt sich irgendwie, die möchten einfach nur Geld behalten oder wie spät wie möglich das Geld zurückzahlen. unfassbar!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Schrecklich. Das Geld vor über einem Monat überwiesen. Wo ist das Geld - keine Ahnung. Wo ist die Sperrkontobestätigung? Keine Ahnung. Mehrmals angerufen ohne jeglichen Erfolg. Als Ergebnis heißt das unzureichende Unterlagen bei dem Konsulat sprich kein Studiumvisum. Ich bin bei mehreren Unis angenommen worden, wollte die Forschung machen. Viele Dank an Fintiba!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I opened a Fintiba Plus blocked account on 24 June for my German student visa. Funds fully deposited since June (€12,193, confirmed on my FIB statement) everything on my side is done.\n\nSix weeks later, still no blocking confirmation. My documents were submitted over a month ago, the deadline they set themselves has already expired, and my status now just says \"expired\" with zero communication. Phone calls unanswered. Emails get only auto-replies. Ticket 1257286  still no response.\n\nHere's the worst part: when Fintiba replies to reviews here, they're just lying. They publicly told me \"check your inbox and spam folder, our team responded.\" I checked both. Nothing. No email ever came. You hit a new low every time.\n\nI have 10 days before my semester starts on 1 September. Because of this one missing document, I can't finish my visa process and I could lose an entire year despite doing everything right and on time.\n\nI've filed a complaint with BaFin, and I've contacted my country's student union to warn other students not to open accounts with Fintiba. Order ID: 738569.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Zwecks meines Studiums in Deutschland habe ich am 24 Juni die Geldüberweisung im Rahmen der Eröffnung eines Sperrkontos durchgeführt, Leider habe ich bis heute sogar noch zwei Anrufen keine Bestätigung bekommen, um mit meinem Visuimantrag fortzusetzen , ich bitte Sie darum , meine Situation schnellstmöglich nachzuvollziehen. Ich würde gar auf keinen Fall meinen gestrebten Studienbegimn zu verpassen", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Leider könnte man nicht wirklich die Moderatorin hören. Man hat sich manchmal gefragt auf welche Sprache sie gesprochen hat, Englisch? Arabisch ? Keine Ahnung! Die Antworte auf gestellte Frage waren oft nicht genug informative, uninteressant und ich konnte wirklich keine klare Antwort an meine Frage haben. Ich möchte gerne Fintiba benutzen für meine Tochter, aber habe ich Angst davon,weil ich  nicht genau weiß, wie das Sperrkonto funktioniert bis jetzt,wir haben auch in Webinar gesehen im Chat ,jemand hat geschrieben dass er Geld Transfert gemacht hat ,aber bis jetzt keine Auskunft davon hat. Betrug !?. Es ist etwas unmotivierend,  Webinar Zeit war  zu kurz für so ein Thema leider. \n\nViele Dank", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I closed my Fintiba blocked account months ago, but I still haven't received my refund. The transfer was supposedly initiated on March 6th, 2026, but the funds never arrived at my bank. When Fintiba finally sent me the transfer details to verify, the account formatting was incorrect and could not be processed by my bank.\nI provided the correct, complete international details of my OTP Bank account weeks ago. Since then, I have been repeatedly asking for the standard MT103 document or UETR code so my bank can help locate the funds, but Fintiba's support ignores my requests and keeps sending automated replies. Holding a customer's money for 4 months without providing any tracking document is unacceptable. I demand immediate escalation of Ticket #1248980.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Cannot choose if I want a health insurance. Is this a money trap? Additionally the AI assistant only talks in my local language and I could not change that. Therefore my support request got declined just because there is no option to change that. Terrible system. Only opening an account was easy.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Let me tell you about my nightmare with this bank. It's been eighteen long months since they froze my funds without any reason. My latest ticket number is 1291309, I say latest because I've lost count of how many I've opened. Since February 2025, they've been deducting monthly fees from that account but have simply refused to resolve the issue. I guess that’s too much to ask. \n I've called them countless times, and every single conversation is a battle. The agents are rude, dismissive, and frankly, insulting. The moment I ask to speak with a supervisor or someone who can actually help, they flat out refuse to transfer me. Their response is simply \"brush off and wait.\" That's not customer service: that’s contempt. And wait for what? I've already waited a year and a half. How much longer do they expect?\nEmails are no better. I send a detailed message, wait two weeks, and get a vague one-liner that addresses nothing. Then they go silent. I have to chase them again, reopen the same issue, and the cycle repeats. The only consistent communication I receive from them is a heart emoji. A heart emoji! \nInstead of helping, they've reduced me to begging friends for loans, borrowing just to get by, while my own funds sit frozen in their system. They don't see the dignity they're stripping away, the humiliation of asking people around me for money that I shouldn't have to ask for. \nHere's what I've learned the hard way: patience is a trap with this bank. They count on you getting tired, giving up, and going away. Don't do that. If you sense even a hint of trouble, do not wait like I did. Do not beg. Do not hope. Go straight to legal help. Because this bank does not value you, your time, or your hard-earned money. They will take your fees, dodge your calls, and leave you stranded. \nIf anyone out there is considering legal action, let's join forces. They need to be held accountable: not just for the money they've trapped, but for the psychological toll, the humiliation, the financial strain they've inflicted. They can't keep getting away with this. It's time they pay for every single thing they've put us through.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Despite being told by Fintiba support that the Source of Funds review usually takes 5–10 business days, my case has now been under review for approximately one month, if not longer.\n\nI understand the importance of compliance checks. I am fully prepared to provide any additional documents required and to wait for a reasonable processing period. The main problem is that I receive no meaningful feedback about the status of my case and no clear guidance on how to interact with the service, avoid further problems, and complete all transactions in accordance with Fintiba’s own requirements.\n\nThe only response I received was a generic template sent after I posted a review on Trustpilot. It stated that my case might take 3–4 weeks to process. My follow-up questions in the same email thread remain unanswered.\n\nSince posting publicly on Trustpilot or Facebook appears to be the only way to receive attention from Fintiba support, I am posting this update as well.\n\nI have now submitted a detailed formal complaint to FIB Frankfurt International Bank AG, describing my entire customer experience with Fintiba from the beginning until today. I included Fintiba's support in copy. Fintiba assigned the complaint ticket number 1298297.\n\nIf Fintiba is genuinely interested in improving its customer experience, this complaint should provide a detailed and useful account of the failures in communication, guidance, and case handling.\n\nI am still waiting for clear answers to the questions that support has repeatedly left unanswered. All of them are included in Ticket 1298297.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "30th July Update: I uploaded my proof of source of funds on the 22nd of June and got approval more than 5 weeks later on the 30th of July. It was a distressing process as there were no clear timelines about how long the process would take. Clearer information would make this process more bearable.\n\n\n17th July: I am extremely disappointed with my experience with Fintiba.\n\nTicket number: 1288332\n\nMy account has been pending since 18 June, and I submitted all requested proof of source of funds on 22 June. Since then, I have repeatedly been told to wait with no clear timeline for when my account will be active. \n\nThese delays are now putting my student visa appointment at risk. I worked incredibly hard to secure admission to a Master’s program and it is deeply frustrating that administrative delays on Fintiba’s side and their banking partner could prevent me from starting my studies, despite having fulfilled all of my own requirements promptly.\n\nBeing told that Fintiba has no control over its banking partner’s timelines feels like an attempt to shift responsibility rather than solve the problem. As a customer, I chose Fintiba, not FIB, and I expect the service to be managed end-to-end. If this is a recurring part of your business, there should be systems in place to streamline compliance reviews and provide transparent, reliable timelines instead of leaving students waiting indefinitely while their visa deadlines draw closer.\n\n\nTo make matters worse, emails go unanswered, making it nearly impossible to get clarity or reassurance about the status of my application.\n\nI sincerely hope my case is reviewed as soon as possible and that Fintiba improves its customer support for future students who come from countries who require visas.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Fintiba has been withholding my legally mandated student living funds (blocked account) since April 2026. I have been left with no money to survive. I was promised my €2,000 payout would be released on July 9th, but it never arrived. On top of that, I am locked out of entering my IBAN by a portal error, and they have charged me a €89 reactivation fee. My emails are ignored and the phone queue is unreachable. I have officially escalated this case to BaFin. Kindly resolve the matter immediately.\n\nMy active support ticket is #1280755.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Many irrelevant questions were asked and time was wasted. I left after 1 hour. got some good info regarding types of visas especially I didnt know about Chancenkarte visa.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Fintiba, this seems to be the only way I can reach your support team unfortunately. You wrote on trust pilot that you would email me but you didn't.\n\nI need to conclude this matter. If the bank is unwilling to approve my funds I would like to close this account and receive my money back. \n\nIt's been a month since I sent these funds. Please respond with a conclusive answer by the end of day tomorrow, 7/16/26.\n\nTickets: 1251953, 1269505, 1289218, 1290590", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The customer service did not help me at all. I tried to get a blocked account without the insurance and they told me that they don’t have that option and they will downgrade me once I set up everything. Then another person told me it was my fault for choosing the insurance... when there was no choice for me not to choose it. Terrible customer service, super rude, the girl hung up without thank you, goodbye or anything. It was such a stressfull experience and specially when you want to make sure your money is safe. If you have to do a blocked account, do NOT go with Fintiba.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Fintiba, when are you going to answer my emails or my calls?\n\nI have noticed you're doing this inhumane thing not just to me, but to everyone. Your social media pages are full of people begging you to answer their emails, process their requests, or release their monthly blocked account payments, yet you simply don't care.\n\nYou ask people to open support tickets, but then you do absolutely nothing with them.\n\nIt's been 1 month and 16 days since I submitted my source of funds confirmation. The first time it was rejected because you said it wasn't enough. Fine—I uploaded the requested document again. Now I have no idea whether it's correct or not because nobody answers. My deadline expired 4 days ago, and I'm still waiting.\n\nBecause of this one document, I can't even book my visa appointment. You guys are literally holding my future hostage. I have only 14 days left to attend my visa interview, receive my visa, and make it to Germany before my semester starts on 1 September. If I miss this because of your delays, I will most likely have to wait another entire year.\n\nHave some shame. If you have even a little dignity left, start treating your customers like human beings instead of ticket numbers. You are literally playing with people's lives and their time, and you act like none of it matters.\n\nMark my words: I will do everything I can to tell future students to stay away from Fintiba. No one should have to beg a company for weeks just to get a response while their future hangs in the balance.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The service has been unacceptable I have been waiting for my issue to resolved to almost 3 weeks now and still no resolution for my visa extension with regards to extending my blocked account I am really angry as this is unacceptable. They keep on saying I must wait for a certain time period but still nothing. It is absolute nonsense and I demand my issue to be resolved immediately now!!!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have been trying to reach out to the Fintiba team for the last 3 weeks regarding my refund update, but I have not received a valid update from the team. I just received, 'We are so sorry for the delay in responding to your request.'\nPlease give us just a little bit more time to process your ticket.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am extremely disappointed with how Fintiba handles account adjustments. I transferred my full blocked amount of €12,163. Because I tried to adjust my account settings yesterday and changed them back, Fintiba's system automatically double-charged me for the setup fee. This created an artificial shortfall of €59 on my dashboard.To save myself the hassle of waiting, I paid the extra €59 via credit card, only to find out that TransferMate will take 3 to 5 days to clear it—even though card payments should be instant. Now my visa confirmation is stuck because of a duplicate system fee. Fintiba needs to fix these glitches, stop double-charging students, and expedite my blocking confirmation immediately!\nmy ticket number: 1296595", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I want to warn everyone who is planning to use Fintiba. My recent experience with them has been an absolute disappointment and a source of immense stress.\nI used a Fintiba blocked account for one year, and everything was fine. Now, I need to renew this account to extend my stay in Germany. There is a corresponding \"Renew\" button on the website, but clicking it simply redirects me to the \"Contact Support\" page.\nAnd this is where the fun begins: support claims that it is impossible to renew the account! Why? There is no clear explanation. At the same time, the account already physically exists in their system; it just needs to be prolonged. Because of their incomprehensible refusal, I found myself in a dead-end situation, as alternative services (such as Expatrio or Coracle) also do not allow opening a new account in my situation right now.\nMain issues with the service:\n * Complete lack of feedback: It is impossible to reach customer support by phone.\n * Ignoring customers: They do not reply to written inquiries for weeks. A total information vacuum.\n * Technical and organizational glitches: The system sends you to support, and support sends you nowhere.\nI demand that Fintiba contact me and resolve this issue. I only need to renew the account I already have with you. Please look into my request!\nMy ticket/inquiry number: 1275128", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have been living in Germany for three and a half months, and I need money to cover my living expenses. I have €12,000 in my blocked account, yet I still cannot access my own funds.\n\nThere is a technical issue preventing me from receiving my money, but it has still not been resolved. As an international student, I depend on these funds to pay for rent, food, and other basic necessities. Without access to my own money, it is becoming impossible to support myself.\n\nThe customer support team has already created countless support tickets for my case. They know my email address by heart because I call them regularly to ask for an update. Despite all of this, absolutely nothing has changed. Weeks and months go by, but there is still no solution, no progress, and no access to my own money.\n\nAs an individual student, I feel powerless in this situation. I believe no student should have to struggle just to access their own legally deposited funds. I sincerely hope Fintiba resolves this issue as soon as possible and treats affected students fairly\n\nUPD.: Fintiba resolved my issue, but that doesn't change the fact that I had to go through hell to get it resolved\n\nUPD. 03.08.2026: Fintiba still hasn't sent the money this month. Nothing has changed.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ich habe bei einer Option einen Fehler gemacht, und seit ich ihn korrigieren wollte, warte ich nun schon einen Monat. Der Kundenservice antwortet nicht auf meine E-Mails und bietet mir keine Lösung an. Mir wurde vor einiger Zeit zugesichert, dass die Änderung vorgenommen würde, aber es ist so viel Zeit vergangen, und ich warte immer noch. Das ist dringend für mich.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Es un quilombo para tranferir mi amiga me quiere transferir yenes y no puede. Tiene que ser desde una cuenta mía. La verdad nose que hacer. Proque tengo solo cuentas argentinas tengo que hacerme otra cuenta extranjera para transferir una decepción", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have been unable to receive my payment for more than two weeks. As a result, I have no money to pay my rent or health insurance. That could also cause problems with the immigration authorities and may affect the renewal of my residence permit, as they strictly require all blocked-account payments to be made on time.\nDuring these two weeks, I contacted the company three times by email and called customer service three times, yet nobody was able or willing to resolve the issue. One of the responses I received was simply with “God help you”.\nMy tickets: 1281174 and 1288594 but both were merged into another ticket as I know", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Unfortunately, the experience has become the worst for the last months. \nIt's been more than 40 days since I requested reverting my money back cause my visa has expired. \n\nFintiba promised fast solutions for any request, but in reality nothing happens from their side. You send messages to Support, they send you kind email in response: we're working on your issue, and then just fade away. \nYou may make phone calls, they'll promise you that they'll solve your issue just within a day, and then...nothing happens and fade away! \n\nFor now, I am waiting for the reversal transfer form. But according to the experience of the other fellows even after submitting this form I won't know when money will be reverted. \n\nPlease help return my money back! \n\n\nUPD from 19/08/2026. After three weeks since submitting reversal transfer form, I finally received my funds. In my case, it took almost three months from the initial request to complete the return.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "FINGER WEG! Bloß nicht nutzen!\nDer Service ist eine absolute Katastrophe und der Kundenservice schlichtweg unverschämt. Sie behalten Ihr Geld ein und verweigern die Auszahlung. Wenn man versucht, jemanden zu erreichen, wird man nur mit der Ausrede abgespeist, man sei überlastet und solle eine E-Mail schreiben. Ich habe bereits fünf E-Mails geschickt – und bis heute keine einzige Antwort erhalten!\nSeit nunmehr zwei Monaten wartet meine Tochter vergeblich auf das Geld, das ich ihr überwiesen habe. Die Ausreden, die man zu hören bekommt, sind völlig haltlos: An einem Tag heißt es, das Geld sei auf dem Konto sichtbar, am nächsten Tag ist es plötzlich wieder verschwunden.\nDies ist ein absolut unseriöses Unternehmen, das die Gutgläubigkeit der Menschen ausnutzt und sie eiskalt im Stich lässt. Sparen Sie sich diesen Ärger und Ihr Geld – machen Sie einen großen Bogen um diesen Anbieter!\n\nUZAK DURUN! Sakın kullanmayın!\nServis tam bir felaket ve müşteri hizmetleri kelimenin tam anlamıyla rezalet. Paranıza el koyuyorlar ve ödemeyi reddediyorlar. Birine ulaşmaya çalıştığınızda, sadece çok yoğun olduklarını ve e-mail yazmanız gerektiğini söyleyen bir bahaneyle geçiştiriyorlar. Zaten 5 mail gönderdim – ve bugüne kadar tek bir cevap bile almadım!\nKızım, gönderdiğim parayı tam iki aydır boş yere bekliyor. Söylenen bahaneler tamamen asılsız: Bir gün paranın hesapta göründüğünü söylüyorlar, ertesi gün para bir anda ortadan kayboluyor.\nBu, insanların iyi niyetini suistimal eden ve onları soğukkanlılıkla mağdur eden kesinlikle ciddiyetsiz bir şirkettir. Kendinizi bu dertten ve paranızdan kurtarın – bu sağlayıcıdan fersah fersah uzak durun!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am very disappointed with my experience with Fintiba's customer support.\n\nI have been waiting for a resolution to my issue for quite some time, and despite opening a support ticket, I have not received a meaningful solution. This delay is affecting an important process, and the lack of communication has been very frustrating.\n\nTicket Number: 1286613\n\nI would greatly appreciate it if someone from the Fintiba support team could review my case as soon as possible and provide an update. I chose Fintiba because of its reputation, and I sincerely hope this issue can be resolved promptly.\n\nThank you.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "My visa was rejected, and I have been waiting for my blocked account refund (€11.885,80) for exactly 10 months. I submitted all requested documents, including the 'Reversal Transfer' form on June 18, but they keep ignoring me. Worse, they are still deducting monthly fees from my money! Unacceptable service. I have already sent a final warning and will proceed with a BaFin complaint against Sutor Bank if it's not resolved immediately.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have been a Fintiba customer since June 2026 and this has been by far the worst customer experience I have ever had. Despite my family making enormous financial sacrifices to wire over €12,150 from the United States into my blocked account, exceeding the required €11,904 blocking sum, I have been unable to receive my blocking confirmation for almost a week due to a Payment Information Error on their platform.\n\nI am a young Ghanaian student trying to secure admission to a German university and this document is critical to joining the visa appointment queue. Every day without it puts my February 2027 intake at risk.\n\nI have raised a support ticket (1289355), emailed the ambassador team, attended their webinar, connected with their team members directly, and even made an additional payment via Fintiba Transfer, all with little to no meaningful response. The replies I have received have been generic and unhelpful.\n\nFor someone who has worked so hard to gather these funds, this experience has been deeply disappointing. I sincerely hope Fintiba takes this seriously and resolves it urgently.\n\nOrder ID: 1977331", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "After my first blocked account expired, I had to open a new one with Fintiba (and pay the account opening fee again). Despite already being a customer, my documents and selfie verification could not be completed. When I called customer service, I was told my account needed manual review, but no one could do this directly, and that an email response could take 3-4 weeks. This is a serious problem if you have an urgent Ausländerbehörde appointment. I ended up using Expatrio instead, who verified my account in 3 days and also offered a free bank account option, which was useful as a newcomer. Do your own research and decide what works best for you.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ich habe vor fast einem Monat einen Antrag auf Änderung meiner Krankenversicherung gestellt, und Fintiba hat meine E-Mails immer noch nicht beantwortet. Sie haben ohne meine Zustimmung den teuersten Tarif aktiviert, und bald wird die zweite Zahlung fällig, die fast 100 Euro für eine Versicherung abbucht, die ich nicht beantragt habe.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Honestly forcing students to a specific insurance is not ethical at all, I didn't want the insurance provided and only wanted to open the blocked account, but apparently it's not an option!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "very slow , no options for above 30 students, and all above this the worst cs ever", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have been waiting for over one month for Fintiba to complete the review of my blocked account transfers, but I still have not received any clear written feedback.\n\nI am a student admitted to a German university. My studies start on October 1st, and my visa appointment is on July 22nd. All my visa documents are ready except the final Fintiba blocked account confirmation.\n\nMy transfers are still stuck in Fintiba’s Source of Funds review. All requested Source of Funds documents have been uploaded, but the transactions are still marked as “Approval Pending”. The review timer has also been reset multiple times without any clear explanation.\n\nThe transfers were made from Portuguese and Georgian bank accounts, not from Russia. I hold Russian citizenship, but I have not lived in Russia for more than four years. During the transfer setup, the portal did not clearly warn me that citizenship could affect whether my transactions would be subject to additional review. The interface only indicated that the country from which the transfer is made is relevant.\n\nThis is especially frustrating because Fintiba had my passport from the beginning, and the chatbot, which was the only immediate source of information, did not provide any useful warning or clear guidance.\n\nI have contacted Fintiba repeatedly through tickets, emails, and phone calls. My ticket numbers include 1289553, 1283121, 1273696, and others. I was told by phone that requests had been sent to the bank and that my case had been escalated, but I still have no clear written update.\n\nIt is unacceptable for a financial service handling thousands of euros of students’ money to leave customers without transparent information for weeks, especially when their visa process and university admission depend on these documents.\n\nFintiba, I urgently need you to manually review all my transactions and uploaded Source of Funds documents, confirm whether anything else is required, and provide a clear written response.\n\nPlease check Ticket 1289553 and reply immediately.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am writing this review out of absolute desperation. I live now outside Germany, and my funds were transferred locally from within Germany to my Fintiba blocked account. I uploaded all the requested \"Source of Funds\" documents more than 22 days ago, but I have received absolutely no response or update from the compliance team at FIB Frankfurt International Bank AG.\n\nThe German Embassy already gave me a final extension until July 30th to submit my Blocking Confirmation. If this document is not issued within the next few days, my visa will be officially rejected, and my entire future will be ruined due to this unreasonable delay.\n\nCustomer support on the phone and via email keeps telling me to wait, but I am running out of time. I urgently request the management or a compliance supervisor to look into my file and approve it immediately.\n\nAccount ID: 1937119", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The identity verification process incorrectly recorded my passport number and swapped my first and last name in the system, which has resulted in my visa documents being incorrect. \n\nI have opened three tickets through their AI chatbot, called their hotline regarding this issue, as well as sent an email containing all required documents and instructions to fix the issue in accordance with what was mentioned in the phone call. \n\nFor more than a week till now, no meaningful responses or updates have been provided by Fintiba to the tickets or email other than automated responses. This has been extremely disappointing.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The FIB statement is not received from visa submissio", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Fintiba is playing with people's lives and wasting their time.\n\nIt took almost three weeks just to update my passport number on my insurance. I also transferred €800 to my blocked account, and it has now been one month and fifteen days without receiving a source of funds confirmation.\n\nEvery time I email your support team, I either receive delayed responses or advice that makes no sense. Telling me to take the transfer receipt to the embassy if you cannot issue the confirmation is absurd. If the blocked account cannot be confirmed, the solution is apparently to wait another 3–4 weeks. How is that acceptable when students are facing visa deadlines?\n\nGetting support from Fintiba has been incredibly frustrating. Phone calls go unanswered, emails take far too long, and customers are left feeling like they have to beg for a response.\n\nMark my words: I will do everything I can to warn future students not to fall into the same trap. No student should have to risk their admission or visa because of such poor customer service.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Conferencists, Personas q hablen un ingles elocuente, mas limpio estandard para mejor entendimiento", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I was just the Q/A session and did not get answer to my query", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I transferred the required funds to my Fintiba blocked account. My initial transfer was made on 9 June 2026, and I sent an additional transfer on 16 June 2026 to ensure the required amount was available after transfer fees.\n\nI submitted all requested Source of Funds documents on 16 June 2026. I was informed that the review usually takes 2–3 weeks, but I am still waiting for my blocked account confirmation.\n\nI have contacted support several times regarding my case (Tickets #1271207 and #1286906), but I have not received a meaningful update or a realistic estimate of when the review will be completed.\n\nWhat makes this especially difficult is that my German student visa application cannot move forward without this confirmation. Every additional week of waiting increases the risk of missing important university and visa deadlines. After working hard to secure my university admission, prepare every required document, and complete every step requested by Fintiba, it is incredibly stressful to feel that everything is on hold because of a compliance review with no clear timeline. I am genuinely worried that this delay could force me to postpone my studies and lose an entire academic year despite having completed everything required from my side.\n\nI fully understand that compliance and Source of Funds reviews are necessary, but clearer communication and more transparent updates would make a huge difference for students whose futures depend on these documents. I sincerely hope my case can be reviewed as soon as possible.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am extremely dissatisfied with Fintiba's poor operating and support system. I honestly no longer know where to submit my complaint.\n\nSince July 2, I have sent nearly 30 emails regarding both the cancellation of my travel insurance and the issue of being unable to upload my blocked account confirmation document, even though my blocked account has already been verified. I have attached screenshots to my emails as evidence. I have also called your support team multiple times, but I honestly cannot understand what your support staff are doing. It is unclear why they are there if they are unable to resolve even the simplest issues.\n\nI requested the cancellation of my travel insurance before it was confirmed. However, without even reviewing my ticket, you charged €159 from my account for the insurance. This is highly unprofessional.\n\nIn addition, my account is not functioning properly. Many buttons and features are unavailable, and I cannot edit anything in my profile. The buttons that your support team refers to in their instructions simply do not exist in my account.\n\nThis situation is unacceptable and extremely disappointing.\n\nMost importantly, my visa application is now being delayed because of Fintiba's failure to resolve these issues in a timely manner.\n\nI urgently request that my case be reviewed and resolved without any further delay.\n\nMy ticket numbers include: 1279851, 1285465, 1285439, and others.\nUpdate 13.06.2026: Fintiba claims that my issue has been resolved. However, this is not true. My issue is still unresolved, and my visa process has already been negatively affected by the delays. I will update this review once the matter is fully resolved.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I transferred my funds to Fintiba almost 4 weeks ago for my German visa application. My funds are reflected in my Fintiba blocked account statement, but I still have not received my blocking confirmation. I also purchased the insurance package through Fintiba, but I have not received the required insurance documents either.\n\nThe Embassy has now reached out to me because these documents are still missing. My entire visa application is now at risk of being cancelled because I have not been able to provide the blocking confirmation and insurance documents, even though I paid and transferred the required funds through Fintiba weeks ago.\n\nFintiba, please put yourselves in my position. This involves a significant amount of my savings and directly affects my livelihood and future plans. How can it be acceptable to put another human being through this level of turmoil by holding their funds, not providing the required documents, and giving no clear information?\n\nIt is deeply unfair and distressing to leave a person in silence when their money, visa process, and important life plans are involved.\n\nMy previous tickets, including 1269505 and 1251953, remain unanswered after my follow-ups. I have not received a clear written update explaining when my blocking confirmation and insurance documents will be issued. I have also tried calling, but no one is answering.\n\nThe timer in my Fintiba account keeps resetting without any clear explanation or proper update. This makes the process even more confusing because I am being left to rely on a timer that does not appear to give a reliable or transparent status of my case.\n\nI am asking Fintiba to issue my blocking confirmation and insurance documents without further delay. If there is any reason these documents cannot be issued immediately, Fintiba should provide a clear written explanation and confirm exactly when I will receive them, or whether I should proceed to close this account.\n\nI also appeal to the relevant German authorities and banking partners to review how Fintiba is handling international applicants and customers. Many people appear to be stranded, whether because they are waiting for blocked account documents, refunds, or payouts, and they are unable to move forward because of these delays and poor communication.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ich habe vor fast einem Monat einen Antrag auf Änderung meiner Krankenversicherung gestellt, und Fintiba hat meine E-Mails immer noch nicht beantwortet. Sie haben ohne meine Zustimmung den teuersten Tarif aktiviert, und bald wird die zweite Zahlung fällig, die fast 100 Euro für eine Versicherung abbucht, die ich nicht beantragt habe.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "My money is stuck in their account. They won’t reply and won’t give a payout. They have all of my documents and everything . They randomly stopped after second month! \nI would never recommend it to someone.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Another promised deadline has passed. Last week fintiba saw my reviews asked for my tickets and said my issue had been resolved and I would recieve my money it three working days. Its been two weeks .It has now been more than two months, and I still have not received my June or July blocked account payouts.\n\nI have spent weeks calling, emailing, opening support tickets, and escalating my case. Every time I receive a new explanation. Now I am being told that the bank keeps returning the money to Fintiba and that they are “trying to resolve it.”\n\nTrying to resolve it for two months is not acceptable.\n\nI don’t care whether the problem is with Fintiba or the bank. As a customer, that is not my responsibility. My responsibility ended when I deposited my money and fulfilled all of my obligations. Your responsibility is to ensure I receive my monthly allowance.\n\nBecause of this failure, I have been left without access to my own money for over two months. I have had to request payment extensions for my accommodation and health insurance, my bank account has gone into debt, and my payment cards have been blocked.\n\nThis is no longer a delay. It is a complete failure to provide a customer with access to their own funds. I hope no international student ever has to experience what I have been through.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Your support is non-responsive. My account is frozen after a 50% transfer from Angola, though ALL Source of Funds documents are uploaded.I was told on the phone I should have paid in one transaction due to my Russian citizenship, but this was NEVER stated beforehand. The funds did NOT come from Russia.My visa appointment is on July 22nd. This delay is ruining my visa process. I demand an immediate manual review of my documents and the unblocking of my account so I can transfer the rest.Please check Ticket: 1289609 and reply today!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Another one star review because why not. 10 days ago i made a review mentioning that they do not give a shit about my finances and how they are dealt with and guess what, they still do not care :). They are horrible. Would not recommend.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "-100000/10", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Your health-/travel insurance in the Fintiba Plus package starts on the wrong date. \nI complained about it 4 weeks ago (inquiry 1257353) and you still have not dealt with it.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Fintiba bietet Sperrkonten für ausländische Studenten und Verpflichtungserklärungen. Wir benötigen ein Sperrkonto für eine Verpflichtungserklärung und es läuft alles schief: keine passende Maske bei der App für Verpflichtungserklärungen, Mitarbeiter ohne Ahnung, lange Bearbeitungszeiten, Änderung der falschen Sperrsumme (verursacht gemeinsam mit dem Mitarbeiter, der es auch nicht wusste) dauert nach Angaben der Mitarbeiterin 3 Wochen. Fast tägliche Telefonate bleiben erfolglos. Leider bieten ortsnahe Banken keine Sperrkonten für Verpflichtungserklärungen an. Wir sind ratlos bei so viel Inkompetenz!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "It is now the 5th working day since I was promised that my June and July payouts had been manually initiated, and I still have not received a single cent.\n\nToday, for the first time, I spoke to a support agent who genuinely tried to help. She contacted management, IT, and informed me that three separate requests had already been sent to the bank to manually release my funds. I appreciate her efforts.\n\nHowever, after two months, I still have no access to my own money.\n\nEvery time I leave a review, I am asked to provide my ticket numbers. I do. Nothing changes. More tickets are opened, more promises are made, more deadlines pass, and I am still left without my June and July payouts.\n\nI do not care whether the delay is caused by Fintiba or the bank. My money is my money, and no customer should be left without access to their own funds for two months while different parties pass responsibility between each other.\n\nBecause of this, my bank account has gone into debt, my payment cards have been blocked, and I have had to ask my accommodation provider and my health insurance provider for payment extensions just to avoid falling behind on essential living expenses.\n\nThis is not just poor customer service. This is a complete failure to provide access to a student’s own money. I sincerely hope no one else has to go through what I have experienced.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Update:\n\nI would like to provide an update regarding my case with Fintiba.\n\nThe reverse transfer process has now been initiated, and I have completed all the required steps and submitted the requested information through the Fintiba app. My case is currently waiting for approval from the Fintiba support team so that the transfer can be processed.\n\nI kindly ask the support team to review my request as soon as possible, as my situation is extremely urgent. I have been waiting for a long time, and I urgently need access to my funds to meet my financial obligations.\n\nMy case is linked to Ticket #1268527. I would greatly appreciate it if the approval and reverse transfer could be completed without any further delay.\n\nThank you, and I hope my case can be resolved as soon as possible.\nTickt : 1284517", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am very disappointed with my experience with Fintiba.\nAbout one month ago, I submitted the blocked account closure document issued by the German Consulate, exactly as requested by Fintiba. However, I still have not received my refund.\nI have sent several messages to customer support, but I have not received any response. I paid service fees for this blocked account, yet I am now struggling to get my own money back.\nFintiba promotes itself as a trustworthy banking service, but my experience has been very disappointing. I sincerely hope my refund will be processed as soon as possible and that Fintiba improves its communication and refund process for other customers.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Fintiba is by far the worst service provider I have dealt with here in Germany. I am in the middle of extending my residency permit. 3 weeks ago when I attempted to extend my blocked account a second time, they told me it had to be done from their side. So I sent an email, and I waited. Then I sent another and another and then I called again and again.\nAs of the time I'm writing this, i have sent 6 emails and called 5 times. Its been 3 weeks and not only does it take 30 minutes to get someone on the line, everytime I do they all say \"be patient\",\"be patient there's still time\". How condescending!!!!!!!!!!!!!\n\n\nMy permit expires next month, my blocked account expires this month, and I have received ZERO responses to my request from Fintiba, ZERO progress. I am an international student, my focus should be on my studies, not chasing after a service provider so I can have their permission to put money in my account!\n\nTicket: 1272508\nName: Sherif Elmeehy", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "\"We hereby confirm that we have submitted your documents to Banking Partner for further processing of the closing transaction and to execute your payment to the account where the deposit came from.\n\nThank you for being our customer.\n\nPlease note that, according to the contract, it can take 5-6 working days until the money is back on your account.\"\n\nThis message was sent to me on 20 June 2026. Today is 7 July 2026 , that’s 17 days later, and I still have not received any money. The 5–6 working days they promised have passed, and there has been no update, no correction, and no funds. \n\nAfter six months of waiting (since the beginning of 2026), with only automated/bot replies and no real human escalation, this false timeline is the latest example of Fintiba’s unprofessionalism and lack of accountability. My issue remains completely unresolved: funds not returned. This delay continues to cause me serious psychological and mental stress.\n\nTickets: 1228929, 1168775, 1173909, 1233623.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "No comments", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "This is my 5th review here, and I will not stop writing until fintiba gives me an answer. I have spent the whole june & now july with ZERO access to my money. Fintiba makes empty promises saying they will deliver it in 3 working days mind you its almost been two weeks. They keep saying technichal issue but clearly there is no issue to take my maintanence fund and even release documents for it. They keep seeinf my reviews, asking for information and apologizing for the delay yet they give no actual solution. This is absolutely unnaceptable not to mention my barmer health insurance payment is coming up, and sparkasse has even blocked my cards from use due to the debt fintiba has put me in. An account thats supposed to support a students living abroad. One of their agent has even been extremely rude telling me “ Well welcome to Germany, maybe where ur from the system is better there bye bye”. Absolutely ridicilous. I absolutely do not recommend fintiba to anyone unless you want physcilogical stress and no acces to your funds for two months with no response :).", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Delayed blocked account closure since April 2026 – serious communication and process failures\n\nI applied to close my unused blocked account in April 2026 and submitted the Grenzübertrittsbescheinigung and official documents from the German authorities.\n\nSince then, the process has been delayed for more than three months due to unclear communication, changing requirements, and a lack of transparency in Fintiba’s verification process.\n\nTimeline of my experience:\n\nApril 2026:\nI submitted my account closure request with the required documents. The online portal showed only “Pending” for almost two months. There was no clear notification that my documents were incomplete, rejected, or required further action.\n\nEnd of May 2026:\nOnly after I repeatedly contacted customer support myself did I learn that the submitted documents were considered insufficient. I was told that I needed further confirmation from the Ausländerbehörde.\n\nI immediately contacted the German authority and provided the requested documents.\n\nJune 2026:\nThe Ausländerbehörde provided official confirmation regarding the release of my blocked account. However, Fintiba continued to raise new issues, including requesting a handwritten signature on an officially issued digital document and repeatedly asking for a valid visa, although my residence status had already ended and I had been required to leave Germany.\n\nThe requirements changed repeatedly, and the online system did not clearly explain the actual reason for rejection. Only after further enquiries did I receive clarification from support.\n\nI always cooperated and provided every requested document as soon as a new requirement was communicated. The delay was not caused by my lack of cooperation.\n\nFinancial impact:\nDuring this entire period, my own funds of more than €10,000 remained inaccessible. Because I urgently needed access to my money in June, I had to arrange alternative financing and suffered additional financial costs.\n\nLatest update – July 21, 2026:\nMy documents have finally passed review. I have now submitted a formal complaint to Fintiba Management and Compliance, with the complete timeline and supporting evidence.\n\nI have requested:\n\nimmediate release of my remaining blocked account balance;\na full review and refund of monthly fees charged after the account no longer served its original purpose;\nconsideration of the financial impact caused by the prolonged delay.\n\nFintiba has been given 5 business days (until July 28, 2026) to provide a final resolution. If this matter is not resolved, I will submit the complete documented case to the relevant supervisory authorities, including BaFin.\n\nI hope Fintiba will resolve this matter professionally and fairly.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Overall bad, on the surface they look awesome, great feedback everything until i tried it, they don't respond to email, their is literally no button to upload any additional files that they are asking for + they didn't reply to my messages for like 3 days now+ their ai bot is the worst AI I've ever seen, never again, only good thing that earned them the extra star is that they accept passports or nationality that expatrio doesn't normally accept", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I would like to share an update about my experience with Fintiba.\n\nWhile I appreciate that my passport-related issue was eventually resolved, my case is still far from finished. I have now been waiting for over two weeks, and I am still unable to access my own funds.\n\nMy current case is linked to Ticket #1268527. Despite several follow-ups, I am still waiting for a final solution. The lack of timely communication and the long delays have caused me significant stress and financial difficulties.\n\nAt this stage, I am simply requesting that the full amount of my funds be transferred back to my active Sparkasse bank account so I can access my money and move forward. I have communicated this request to the support team and hope it can be processed without any further delays.\n\nThis situation has become urgent, as I have outstanding financial obligations, including rent, and I cannot continue waiting indefinitely for access to my own funds.\n\nI sincerely hope Fintiba will review Ticket #1268527 as soon as possible, process my request, and improve its response times and communication with customers facing urgent situations.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I migrated from Coracle to Fintiba due to the issues with coracle. The main reason for the migration was because I wanted to add more funds to my block account, after the entire migration was done, Fintiba informed me that I CAN NOT add more funds, despite having cleary communicated to them, that I would need to add funds. \n\nRight now I am dealing with an EVEN BIGGER problem that is causing so much stress. I have already been in germany, and the automated visa check keeps rejecting my visa start date as it is older than the block account confirmation. There is no way to get a human to check it, I have gotten no response on my email, chat support is useless, and calling them just means wasting your balance because no one ever picks up. \nI am genuinely appalled by how these services are being provided.  \nKindly resolve my matter QUICKLY. \n\nmy id: 1954454", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "It is July 6th and I have had zero money on my account for the whole june, and now july. My cards have been blocked from use due to the debt fintiba has put me in, I have no cash, and my health insurance payment is coming up this week. As a student abroad you can Imagine how critical of a condition I am in.  I have wrote previous reviews here and while fintiba has asked for my ticket ID and said they initiated the payout, it has been absolutely untrue.One and a half week ago they told me my june payout would be sent to me in three working days and they did not stay true to their word. Last week I contacted them AGAIN,(after sending hundreds of emails and calls) requesting my june & july payout immediately. They told me due to technichal issues again the money hadnt been transfered, mind you they keep charging me for account maintanence and even releasing document proofs so CLEARLY there is no technichal issue. On July 1st,(3days late to my july payment) they told me again they would send my money in 3 working days. I emailed them again they pushed it to 3-5 working days. It is July 6. I truly hope by wednesday to see my money or this is no longer acceptable. I simply cannot recommend fintiba based on my experience.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "They ignore Emails. Kundenservice are incompetent and lie all the time, AND they blocked the rest of our blocked account without any way of returning it. And on top of that, they keep trying to delete any negative review I write! Is this a legitimate company or a legalized scam? \nI would never want anything to do with them ever again AS SOON AS THEY RETURN THE REST THE MONEY THEY ARE KEEPING HOSTAGE!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Why do we think an ai assistant can solve any question. Is very difficult to contact support, almost impossible.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "it was nice the speaker doesn't check the Q and A questions", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Nothing was usefull most of things are already on chancenkarte site i joined webinar so i can ask questions and clear my confusions, but only one question got answered, other were not even considered, so it was a waste of time for me", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Very difficult and complicated", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Sehr einfach und praktisch", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "NO support services at all", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The organisation has requested documents to verify the source of funds, as I am a resident of a so called \"high-risk country\". \n\nThe documents were submitted on the same day, yet I have been waiting for the review for a week and a half now, which is significantly delaying the process of applying for a residence permit.\n\nAll this despite the fact that I have been living in Germany for a year now and had no problems with another similar service previously. I tried to contact customer support, but didn’t get a clear answer; it’s a shame that such a simple and routine problem requires me to be constantly on edge.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The worse service ever. \nI have been in Germany and waiting to get my payouts over a month but no genuine response from them. I gave them all documents and bank details but their helpline says it will take 3 weeks to get an answer and 5 business days after to get the first payout. I am failing to pay my rents and other bills due to the delay in their processing and having to my fines for late payments.\nDon't use this platform if you never want to find yourself in my situation. Due to the interest, it definitely makes more sense for them to hold your money as long as they can before they are legally obliged to return. You wont get their response because delaying the process generates their income to sustain the business.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Hello Fintiba, my case has been pending for weeks. I have already completed the reversal transfer process and sent multiple emails, but 1 am still waiting for a response. Please check my emails and help resolve my case as soon as possible.\nThank you. \n- Mohammad Abdulrahman\n10.11.2005", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Overall, the experience has not been the worst, but I've had several issues with payouts that couldn't be resolved quickly, which made me VERY stressed and frustrated. The quality of customer service really depends on the agent, their attitude, experience, and even their mood. If you contact them by email, don't expect a solution within one business day (as promised); in my experience, responses have taken anywhere from 7 to 10 days. If you call them, the agent may or may not be helpful; some are very sweet, while others can be really rude. On top of that, you may have to wait up to 30 minutes on hold before someone answers.\n\nCurrently, I'm dealing with yet another payout issue. It's causing me a lot of stress, and I have to keep pushing them to take action and resolve it. Otherwise I cannot pay my rent, health insurance, etc", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "get an EXPATRIO account , fintiba is slow and you won t get your money.\n\nYou can do everything right, do two different types of legitimation, contact them via email or call and they will take months getting to you while you run out of money instead of activating your account and allowing you to have access to your money. \n\nCalled them multiple times every week, did everything in my power to access the funds, did every single step they suggested and still nothing has happened, the people on the phone will tell you \"its going to be done by tommorow\" , \"it's going to be done by next week\" I have been hearing the same thing for MONTHS and nothing has changed .", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I recommend everyone read this! This \"wonderful\" service promises customer support but actually lets its customers down.\nI needed to extend my blocked account. I clicked the button, and the waiting process began. I submitted an inquiry on June 15th—almost three weeks ago—and received this reply: \"Just a little longer | Your inquiry 1256045 will be dealt with soon.\" Naturally, there has been no further response. A week ago, I noticed a request for proof of address in the documents section, even though I hadn't received any notification about it. I uploaded the document; a week has passed, and it’s silence again. Today I called Fintiba support, and they simply told me to wait. Wait for what?! It’s madness! Why should we pay monthly maintenance fees if the world's worst service provider can't even organize its own operations?\nYou know what the most interesting part is? If you read the reviews, you'll notice that Fintiba often refuses to extend accounts altogether, suggesting customers open them with other companies instead. But here's the thing: the other two companies (Expatrio and Coracle) aren't actually competitors—they all belong to the same parent company, CHAPTERS Group AG. It seems like a way to line their pockets at our expense by making us pay for account setup fees over and over again.\nOne can only hope a competitor emerges that can drive all three of these services out of business within a year; after all, a business with this kind of attitude toward customers, IT systems straight out of the last century, and abysmal support won't survive long in a competitive market. Unfortunately, like other customers, I’ve been unlucky...\nSo, what can we do in a situation like this, friends? Personally, I’ve identified the following options:\n1. File an official complaint with the partner bank (Sutor Bank).\n2. Complaint to the federal regulator (BaFin)\n3. Notification of your local Foreigners' Registration Office (Ausländerbehörde)\n4. Federal Cartel Office (Bundeskartellamt)\n5. Consumer Protection Agency (Verbraucherzentrale)\n6. German National Association for Student Affairs (Deutsches Studierendenwerk — DSW)\nI feel that simply staying silent is definitely not an option. We need to insist that our rights are respected.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am extremely disappointed and stressed with Fintiba's customer service. My money of EUR 12,063.00 was successfully credited into my FIB Frankfurt International Bank account on June 3, 2026 (Account No: 2043032300). On the exact same day, I uploaded all the required documents for the \"Source of Funds\" verification.\n\nIt has been nearly a month now, and I have not received a single update or reply from their compliance/support team, despite multiple emails and tickets sent. They never reply to anything. My German student visa appointment is approaching very soon, and this unacceptable delay is putting my entire education and future at risk.\n\nI know that I am not alone, as there are many other people facing the similar case like me and the exact same stressful situation with Fintiba right now.\n\nMy money is already inside your bank, so why is it taking a whole month just to review the documents and issue the Blocked Confirmation? Please escalate this issue immediately! If you do not want to approve my funds, please refund my money right away.\n\nMy Fintiba Support Code: 364-817-309", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Die Auszahlungen kommen viel zu spät (30.4. für März und April, 19.6. für Mai und Juni) Nach mehreren Telefonaten und EMails wird man nur vertröstet; der Support hat keinen Zugriff auf das Konto und kann nichts erklären. Angeblich gibt es „technische Probleme“, aber unerklärliche Gebühren können abgebucht werden: 49,50 und 3x 9,90. Hierzu gab es nach 6 Wochen eine „Antwort“ über 4,90, die gar nichts erklärte.\nFür unsere Beschwerden haben wir mittlerweile 4 Tickets, aber außer dass „es noch ein paar Tage braucht“ kommt nichts. (Tickets  1246022, 1254676, 1254752 und 1270121). Wenn alle Ticketnummern Fragen und Beschwerdeschreiben sind, müsste man die ganze Fintibank wirklich hinterfragen….\nWir reichen morgen Beschwerden ein bei der BaFin und bei der Schlichtungsstelle der Deutschen Bundesbank.\nDem Ausländermeldeamt haben wir es schon gemeldet und wir werden auch die Botschaft informieren. \nEs ist absolut nicht hinnehmbar, dass das eigene hartersparte Geld nicht ausgezahlt wird und dass junge Menschen damit in erhebliche Zahlungsnot geraten.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ticket 1267337\nI am waiting for a response to simply change my plan from Basic to Plus for 2 weeks. Why isn’t it just a button in the account in the first place? I can’t delete my account, I can’t recreate it using other email, to just faster getting to deposit. This constant email replies “please wait a little bit longer” without any context are very frustrating. As a experience as whole so far.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Soll mein erste Payout seit 3 Wochen bekommen, jedoch bis jetzt hab ich nichts. Die Kommunikation ist unmöglich, seit 2 Wochen bearbeiten die mein Ticket! Auf Anruf kriegt man keine vernünftige Infos. Bin richtig in so ein Dilemma mit dieser Bank und wollte nur mein Geld! Überhaupt nicht zu empfehlen", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Transferred funds pending since June 3rd. Support is ignoring me!\nI transferred my blocked account funds on June 3, 2026. It has been nearly a month, and my account status has still not been updated. I have received absolutely no updates, and your contact support is only giving me automated bot replies with no real human intervention. My German visa appointment is approaching very soon, and this delay is causing extreme distress.\n\nI am not posting my personal account details here for privacy reasons, but I have already sent multiple emails and directly messaged your official LinkedIn page with my Fintiba Account Number, Passport Number, and the official SWIFT transfer receipt.\n\nPlease have a REAL HUMAN AGENT check your LinkedIn DMs or support tickets and resolve my issue immediately!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Einfach nur nervig!!! Ich habe vor einer Woche versucht ein Konto für eine Verpflichtungserklärung anzulegen. Der Betrag wurde hier falsch übertragen und es bestand ein Ladefehler in der App. Somit konnte ich die Einzahlung nicht machen. Ich habe den Kundenservice kontaktiert und mir wurde gesagt, dass das Problem darin besteht, dass es den Fall derzeit nicht aktualisiert. Es wurde ein Ticket eröffnet und das Problem würde behoben werden. NICHTS ist passiert. Der geplante Einreisetermin nähert sich und es hängt weder an Behörden oder sonstigem, nur an dieser Bank hier. Ich versuche seit einer Stunde den Kundenservice zu erreichen (innerhalb der vorgegeben Zeiten) und entweder bekomme ich zu hören „try later again“ oder ich stecke 15 Minuten lang in der Warteschleife um dann, ohne Antwort, rausgekickt zu werden. Diese Art der Bearbeitung und Service- Erreichbarkeit, macht wirklich Angst dieser Bank sein Geld anzuvertrauen. Wer nach schneller Bearbeitung und auch Service sucht, sollte sich ggf.  nach Alternativen umzusehen. Bisher ist meine Erfahrung hier eine Katastrophe!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "**Extremely Urgent – My Student Residence Permit Is at Risk**\n\nI have been waiting for a long time for Fintiba to issue updated **Blocked Account** and **Health Insurance Confirmation** documents. These are the only documents I need for my residence permit renewal.\n\nDespite sending multiple emails and repeatedly calling customer support spending money I can barely afford as a student I have received no resolution. My immigration deadline is approaching, yet Fintiba continues to ignore my requests.\n\nThis level of customer support is unacceptable, especially when students' legal status depends on receiving these documents. I urgently ask Fintiba to address this issue.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Update regarding my last review, It is now June 30, and I have spent the entire month without access to my June blocked account payout.\n\nFintiba promised me in writing that my transfer had been initiated and that I would receive my money within 3 working days. That deadline has passed, and I still have not received a single euro.\n\nI was left without access to my own money for an entire month while still having to pay health insurance, bills, and other essential living expenses. Every time I contacted support, I was told only to “wait.”\n\nThis is unacceptable for a company managing students’ living funds. Broken promises, no accountability, and no resolution. I simply cannot recommend Fintiba based on this experience.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Horrible. They are so irresponsible with the payments, the inquiries I have for them. They ignore me, do not give me my money in time (at this time it has been 16 days since I should've received the money btw). Words cannot describe how shitty the experience you have with them is. Being able to do nothing while they hold your money for reasons they do not make clear. Leaving Fintiba as soon as I am finished with my first year of using it. (Had to use Fintiba for blocked account by circumstances, not by choice.)", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have been using Fintiba for more than a year now. Everything went well, and everything was okay. Until April, I received an email saying that a passport update verification was required. Now that I have uploaded the passport details, I have had this page for more than 1 month. I can't see my account details, and I am not sure whether it would affect my monthly payment as well.\n\nOne thing is for sure, I've contacted them by both email and Phone call, but all I get is basically either \"we will go with you again\" or just a polite reply saying \"we are sorry for the delay in answering you quickly.\nPlease give us a little bit more time to process your ticket XXXXXXX adequately \".\n\nThe tickets that I have were 1261323, 1273729, 1275797,", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": ":I have been trapped in a complete nightmare with Fintiba since April 2026 due to a visa rejection. My account closure was officially confirmed on May 28, 2026. Instead of refunding my money, Fintiba is literally stealing from my account.Even though I explicitly ordered them to close my account, they have repeatedly and wrongfully charged me 4.90 EUR management fees. To make matters worse, they also illegally charged me a \"bank change fee\" during this period without my consent! My account status still appears as \"Suspended\" in the app instead of \"Closed\" because they are intentionally delaying the process to milk my money with unauthorized deductions.This is not a professional financial service; this is financial misconduct. If my main funds and ALL illegal deductions (management fees + bank change fee) are not fully refunded immediately, and if the official MT103/SWIFT document is not provided today, I will file an official complaint with BaFin (Federal Financial Supervisory Authority) and take legal action. Stop hiding behind automated bot replies and fix this robbery now!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Fintiba Ticket Nr. (1125341)\n\nLiebe Leser\n\nihr dürft 3 Mal raten, wo sich das Geld, also das Eigentum meiner Freundin heute befindet? \n\nJAAAAAAA  RICHTIG - das Geld ist immer noch bei FINTIBA - wo denn sonst. Jedes Mal wenn ich hier wieder eine neue, miese Bewertung über Fintiba schreibe, antworten diese hier jeweils zuverlässig, entschuldigen sich artig, und freuen sich wahnsinnig, dass sie jetzt DIE Lösung gefunden haben. \n\nUnd es ist tatsächlich wahr - der Fintiba Support hat uns eine neue E-Mail geschrieben am 23. Juni 2026. Der neueste Scherz vom Fintiba Support ist, dass wir nun ein allerletztes Formular ausfüllen müssen - dann werde das Geld innert 3 bis 4 Wochen bei uns eintreffen - wird vollmundig in dieser E-Mail versprochen. \n\nTatsächlich handelt es sich lediglich um einen weiteren, schlechten Scherz des Fintiba Supports, denn GANZ GENAU DIESES FORMULAR \"FIB_ReversalTransfer_Blank (1).pdf\" wir am 19.02.2026 bereits ausgefüllt, unterzeichnet und dem Fintiba Support zurückgeschickt haben. Wir erleben also eine weitere Runde KUNDENVERARSCHUNG vom Fintiba Support. \n\nMeine Freundin und ich haben in unserem ganzen Leben noch nie so ein meisterhaft, schlechten Support erlebt. Und meine Freundin stammt aus Russland - das sagt doch alles über den FINTIBA-Support.\n\nWir werden euch, liebe Leser, hier weiterhin auf dem Laufenden halten hier.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I need to open a blocked account for German visa application for only one month for a sum of €3100. Fintiba insisted minimum for two months hence doubling the deposit sum to €6200. Unfair.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I'm an international student who needs a blocked account set at €1,309/month to meet Austria's publicly known financial threshold. Fintiba's default is €992/month (calibrated for Germany). My account is inexplicably locked at €1,295, not the default, not the amount I need, and I cannot change it.\nWhat makes this worse is the system asks for a justification to exceed the default, but the justification is straightforward and publicly available, Austria's minimum financial requirement is €1,309/month, my sponsor wants to send exactly this amount into my blocked account, and I need it to meet the visa requirement. There is no way to attach supporting documents. The AI support bot collects the information, then closes the ticket with a generic, incomplete message: \"you have entered a monthly sum significantly...\", without resolving anything. No human follow-up. (Ticket #1274135, Support id:  774-122-248)\nFor Austria, Fintiba simply does not work. The amount is wrong, locked, and unsupported. Very frustrating experience.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Die Leute, mit denen wir unterwegs waren, hatten keine Ahnung, konnten niemandem Auskunft geben und verbreiteten falsche Informationen. Sie waren nicht einmal qualifiziert; sie waren einfach nur gereist, mehr nicht. Sie waren so ungebildet wie Kinder. Es gab keinerlei Zusammenarbeit; jeder kritisierte den anderen und versuchte, ihn zu übertrumpfen, jeder dachte: „Ich verstehe mehr als du.“ Keiner von ihnen wusste irgendetwas und sie waren völlig nutzlos. Der Vortrag war reine Zeitverschwendung. Ich hätte Gemini oder GPT fragen sollen; das wäre einfacher gewesen.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "i called severral time because i had questions regarding to my inquiry from ABH. and no one gave me a clear answer, yet they just said different things which made me confused. also, i felt like i am not listening and my inquiry is nothing. still made the blocked account but i just did it because fintiba was the only option since i already use expatrio.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I arrived in Germany on 5 May 2026 and had already opened my blocked account with Fintiba before travelling. Immediately after my arrival, I completed all the required formalities and submitted every document requested for account activation.\n\nUnfortunately, more than two months later, my blocked account is still not activated. During this period, I have contacted Fintiba's customer support numerous times by email and phone. Every time, I receive the same response—that my request will be processed manually as soon as possible—but nothing has changed.\n\nBecause my account has not been activated, I have been unable to access my own money for essential living expenses such as rent, food, transportation, and other daily needs. This has caused significant financial hardship and unnecessary stress while trying to settle into life in Germany as an international student.\n\nI expected a much faster resolution for such a critical service. While the support team responds, they have not provided any effective solution or realistic timeline for resolving my issue.\n\nI sincerely hope Fintiba resolves this matter immediately. If not, I will have no option but to escalate the matter to the relevant regulatory authorities.\n\nUpdate: If Fintiba resolves my issue promptly, I will gladly update this review to reflect my experience.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "أتمنى أن تناقشنا في المرات القادمة التحديات الخاصة بتوفر السكن تكلفة المعيشة الاختلاف الثقافي وأثره على الأبناء", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "i had waited for 2 +hrs and there is no opportunity for talk at all !!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I need an actual human being support to speak to", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Cok gec geri dönüs yapiyorsunuz durumumun cok acil olduğunu söylememe ragmen", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "They scanned my passport and still they put the wrong passport number, place of birth and my name. And it’s over 2 weeks now issue is not resolved. Poor service", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am writing to express serious concern regarding the activation process for Fintiba blocked accounts. My account has been stuck in 'Pending' status for over two weeks despite the full submission of all required documents, leaving me without access to my own funds for essential living expenses. \n\nUnfortunately, this does not appear to be an isolated incident. I am aware of multiple other students facing similar, prolonged delays, some waiting as long as two months for their accounts to be activated. This suggests a systemic breakdown in Fintiba’s verification and customer support operations that is causing significant financial hardship for many international students who rely on these accounts to meet visa and residency requirements. While I understand that verification takes time, the current lack of communication and the excessive, multi-month wait times for many users are unacceptable. \n\nI urge Fintiba to address these operational bottlenecks immediately and provide transparent timelines for those currently stranded without their funds.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "My issue is extremely urgent. I have been trying to contact support by email regarding my account renewal, but unfortunately nobody has responded yet.\n\nMy account renewal is very important and time-sensitive, so I would greatly appreciate a prompt response and assistance as soon as possible to get my payout. \n\nTicket Number: 1262636\nName : Mohammad Abdulrahman \nSupport code : 099-993-452\n\nPlease review my case and get back to me as soon as possible.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I would like to update my review regarding Fintiba.\n\nAfter experiencing significant delays in communication, the team has now helped resolve my passport-related issue, which I appreciate. Thank you for taking action on that matter.\n\nHowever, my case is still not fully resolved. I am currently waiting for approval of a second account extension, which is very important for my situation. Due to a misunderstanding of the renewal process, I transferred my funds before extending the account, and I am now relying on Fintiba’s assistance to resolve this issue.\n\nMy situation remains urgent, as I am facing financial pressure and have outstanding rent obligations. I would be very grateful if my request for a second account extension could be reviewed and processed as soon as possible.\n\nI appreciate the support provided so far and hope the remaining issue can be resolved quickly so that my case can finally be completed.\nName : Mohand Omran Abd Alrahman", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "after 3 days, still there is no response to my request", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Update: This issue is still unresolved.\n\nAfter my earlier review, Fintiba responded and referred me to the timer displayed in my account. At that time, the timer showed 8 days remaining, so I continued waiting and checking the timer.\n\nThe timer later reached 0 days on my end, and I contacted Fintiba to ask for an update. I did not receive a timely reply. Later, the timer appeared to reset, and by the time Fintiba responded, they said they were seeing 12 days on their end.\n\nThis does not make sense to me. If customers are being told to rely on the timer displayed in their account, then Fintiba needs to explain why the timer reached 0 days on my end and later appeared to show a higher number. This also does not clearly align with the 15-working-day timeline I was previously given.\n\nFintiba is holding a significant amount of my savings for a blocked account, and I still do not have a clear written update, timeline, or confirmation of what is happening with my case.\n\nI am asking Fintiba to provide a proper written response confirming:\n\n* whether my source of funds review is complete or still pending;\n* what exact step is outstanding, if any;\n* whether any further documents are required from me;\n* the expected date for issuing my blocking confirmation;\n* why the timer reached 0 days on my end and later appeared to reset;\n* how the current displayed timer relates to the 15-working-day processing timeline I was given.\n\nIf I do not receive a clear and substantive response by the end of the stated processing period, I will have to escalate this formally through the appropriate complaint channels.\n\n---\n\n\nI am deeply frustrated with Fintiba’s handling of my account.\n\nI submitted all the required Source of Funds documentation, and the blocking confirmation is the only remaining document I need to proceed with my visa and travel plans. Yet I have received zero communication regarding my account status, the review process, or the expected timeline.\n\nI sincerely wish I had read these reviews and considered other providers before transferring my funds. Fintiba does not make it clear that obtaining a blocking confirmation may become significantly more complicated depending on a customer’s location or the source of the funds. If the country or location entered by a customer is likely to trigger additional compliance requirements, the system should flag this clearly before accepting such a substantial transfer.\n\nInstead, Fintiba has accepted and is holding my money while leaving me completely in the dark.\n\nThis complete lack of communication is unacceptable and deeply concerning. If Fintiba is entirely non-communicative at the very beginning of the process, how can customers trust the company to release their monthly funds reliably later?\n\nI now have very little money left to live on, while my visa and travel plans remain on hold. A company entrusted with large amounts of other people’s money has a clear duty to communicate promptly and transparently.\n\nI need an immediate status update on my open inquiry, (Ticket #1269505). I need a clear explanation of what is happening with my account, whether anything further is required from me, when the blocking confirmation will be issued, and what options are available to me. Continuing to ignore my inquiry is unacceptable.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ich bin wirklich enttäuscht von Fintiba. Die Überweisung wurde angeblich vor 12 Tagen von Fintiba getätigt, aber meine Bank hat das Geld nie erhalten. Ich habe E-Mails geschrieben, aber keine einzige wurde beantwortet. Als sie mich anriefen, meinten sie, sie würden per E-Mail antworten?! Ich bin verzweifelt; mir droht die Zwangsräumung und horrende Strafen wegen ausstehender Miete. Ich habe nicht einmal Geld für Essen oder den täglichen Bedarf. Fintiba macht mein Leben in Deutschland zu einem wahren Albtraum.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ich bin seit Anfang April in Deutschland. Ich habe alle Unterlagen zur Auszahlung (Payout) uploadet. Leider wurde keine Auszahlung bezahlt.  ich habe Support geschrieben und angerufen. Es wurde nichts gemacht.  Ich brauche Geld um die Sprachkurs Miete und Essen.  Ich dachte Fintiba ist da damit ich monatlich Geld bekomme für Miete, Sprachkurs, Essen, Zug ... Bitte aktivieren Sie mein Konto", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Die Seite hat mich immer wieder zur Versicherung geleitet, obwohl ich mich ohne registrieren wollte.\nIch brauche nur ein blocked account.\nJetzt habe ich aus Frust mit Versicherung den Account geöffnet.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am writing this review to highlight a significant delay regarding my urgent support case, Ticket 1238778. It has been approximately one month since I received an update requesting additional time to process my account. Over the course of this month, I have placed more than seven telephone inquiries to customer support. While the representatives have consistently been polite and assured me that the matter would be resolved, no progress has been made on the account profile.\n\nThe issue stems from a technical limitation within the web interface that prevents immediate passport verification, thereby necessitating a manual review. Although the required documentation was provided, the passport has not yet been uploaded to the interface, which continues to prevent access to the necessary payment details.\n\nWith a master's program scheduled to commence this October, these unexpected administrative delays are now severely impacting a critical university visa timeline.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "After my previous review, Fintiba contacted me and asked for my ticket ID. I provided all requested information, but I still have not received my money or a real solution. I even called them again today and they had the audacity to tell me and I quote“ Well, welcome to Germany this is how things work, I dont know where you are from maybe the system is better there but you can’t do anything just wait. Bye bye.” And he ended the call without even allowing me to respond. I found this EXTREMELY rude. \n\nMy June blocked account payout is still missing. This means I have been left almost the entire month of June without access to the money that is specifically meant for my living expenses in Germany.\n\nI have called multiple times, sent emails, and opened support tickets. The only answer I receive is “please wait” or “as soon as possible” — but nobody can tell me when I will actually receive my own money.\n\nA blocked account is required because students depend on these funds for rent, health insurance, food, and daily costs. Keeping someone without access to their monthly allowance for weeks, with no timeframe and no proper escalation, is unacceptable. Not to mention I have health issues and could not even pay for my pills and I told them im not in a good heath condition, still didn’t care :).\nI am still waiting for Fintiba to resolve this immediately.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am extremely disappointed with Fintiba’s customer support. I have sent multiple emails regarding my issue and have received no response. My emails have been completely ignored, and I have been left without any update or assistance.\n\nMy ticket number is 1233335, and my issue remains unresolved. This lack of communication is unacceptable, especially as my situation is urgent and time-sensitive.\n\nI urgently need a representative to review my case and contact me as soon as possible. I have been waiting for days without any meaningful response, and I cannot continue facing these delays.\n\nI expect Fintiba to respond promptly, address my case, and provide a clear solution without further delay.\nMy name is Mohand Omran Abd Alrahman\nDate of birth : 01.07.2005\nTicket number is : 1233335", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Extremely urgent! Support ID: 099-993-452 / Ticket Nr: 1262636. My account Mohammad Abdulrahman has been blocked for a month. Fintiba says they sent emails, but I receive absolutely nothing. I am calling daily and agents just open useless tickets. I cannot pay my rent, I received a Mahnung, and I am facing eviction. Change my email or clear my payout manually NOW!\"", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Title: Account blocked despite official Bürgeramt manual verification - BaFin Case GZ: VBS 13-QB 4301/00195#15291\nReview:\nFintiba is completely ignoring my official manual verification documents, leaving me stranded without access to my money. Following their direct alternative verification instructions, I went to the Berlin Bürgeramt, got my identification documents officially verified, signed, and stamped with the German state seal (Bezirksamt Tempelhof-Schöneberg).\nI sent clear photos of these state-verified documents, my Meldebescheinigung, and my O2 phone bill via email days ago, and the original physical paperwork is already delivered to their Frankfurt office by mail. Yet, my account remains blocked, and there is zero response from customer care.\nThe financial regulator BaFin is already actively tracking this under case number GZ: VBS 13-QB 4301/00195#15291. And my support code is 775-384-632.Fintiba compliance management needs to manually bypass the PostIdent screen and unlock my IBAN entry screen immediately. This is an absolute nightmare for international students.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have a Blocked Account in Fintiba GmbH. I send twenty time reminder for closure account and send me return back Money. I also send Official letter of German embassy (Uploaded on app Dated: 28-02-2026). This is not good behaviour of Fintiba. Please release my Money.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Keine Antwort , alles so kompliziert", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am extremely disappointed with my experience with Fintiba. My blocked account payout for June 2026 has not been received, even though this money is specifically intended to cover students’ living expenses in Germany.\n\nIt is now 18 June and I still have not recieved monthly payment. I have contacted support multiple times, sent emails, opened tickets, and spent a long time waiting on calls. The only answer I receive is that I should “wait” and that they will respond “as soon as possible” — without any clear timeframe or solution.\n\nA blocked account is not a regular service. Students depend on this money for rent, health insurance, food, and basic necessities. Leaving someone without access to their own funds for weeks with no explanation is unacceptable.\n\nI understand technical issues can happen, but the lack of urgency, communication, and a clear resolution process is very concerning. Customers need transparency, especially when their essential living funds are involved.\n\nI hope Fintiba resolves this immediately and improves their handling of urgent payout problems.\nPs. I even have health issues and need money to pay for my pills, called them telling them I am in urgent need, even at extremes they dont take action :) great way to go fintiba!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "لقد طلبت أكثر من مرة للسوال ولم يتم اجابتى \nفى كتير من الأحيان كانت الاسئلة خارج نطاق الموضوع الرئيسى", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am a student in Germany and use Fintiba. My monthly payments go through on time, but I am unable to transfer the €2,000 \"bounce payment.\" I get a server error whenever I try to do it manually. I have emailed the support team twice, but despite nearly a month passing, I still haven't received a reply. I am a student and have run out of money, yet no one is addressing the issue.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "August 1st UPDATE: Unacceptable service. STILL NOT SOLVED\n\nUnacceptable service. Do not trust Fintiba to help you with your visa --  they will make every mistake possible and take forever to fix it. WE ARE MISSING OUR VISA APPOINTMENT BECAUSE OF THEM.\n\n1. They made two basic mistakes when opening the account: the name and place of birth were wrong. This information should have been verified against the passport, but clearly it wasn’t. Their support team did not care at all. It took more than a week to fix, and we had to chase them everywhere --  Instagram, Facebook, multiple emails, and calls -- to get any attention at all. \n\n2. Then, after we transferred the money, they displayed the WRONG amount on the visa document!! This document is incorrect now -- we cannot use it at the embassy, so we are missing our visa appointment..\n\nA financial service that is supposed to help with visas shouldn't work like this. Do not trust them!! AVOID by all means", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "**Subject: Extremely Disappointing Experience with Fintiba Services for an International Student**\n\nMy child, Anchit, travelled to Germany for higher studies after completing all the required formalities through Fintiba, including opening a blocked account and obtaining the insurance package offered by the company. We chose Fintiba because it presents itself as a reliable and trustworthy partner for international students.\n\nHowever, upon arrival in Germany, my child faced a serious issue when attempting to activate and use the services linked to the blocked account. Fintiba informed him that the insurance associated with the account was not operational. While the problem was acknowledged, no clear guidance, support, or practical solution was provided to resolve the matter.\n\nThis experience has been extremely stressful and disappointing. International students arrive in a foreign country with limited local support and depend heavily on service providers such as Fintiba for smooth settlement and compliance with legal requirements. Instead of receiving timely assistance, my child was left confused and uncertain about how to resolve an issue that was beyond his control.\n\nA company serving international students has a responsibility not only to identify problems but also to provide prompt, effective, and customer-friendly solutions. Unfortunately, Fintiba failed to meet these expectations. The lack of proper guidance and support at such a critical stage has caused unnecessary anxiety and inconvenience.\n\nI strongly urge Fintiba to improve its customer support system and ensure that students facing similar issues receive immediate assistance and clear instructions for resolution. International students place their trust in your services while starting a new life abroad, and that trust should be respected through professional and responsive support.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "\"Hello,\nThank you for bringing this matter to our attention. We’re pleased to inform you that your case has been reviewed and the issue has now been resolved.\nWe appreciate your patience and understanding. If there is anything else we can help you with, please contact us\"\n\nThis reply was sent six days ago as a response to my previous review. It is clearly false. My issue remains completely unresolved: I opened a Fintiba account at the start of 2026 and have been trying to close it and get my money back for six months. Despite submitting four support tickets (1228929, 1168775, 1173909, 1233623), I receive only automated or bot messages with no clear timeline, no human escalation, and no accountability.\n\nThis ongoing delay has caused me serious psychological and mental stress, including anxiety, sleep disruption, and constant worry about accessing my own funds. Fintiba’s false claim of resolution is unacceptable and shows a lack of genuine support.\n\nTickets: 1228929, 1168775, 1173909, 1233623.\n\n⚠️ Update: Fintiba replied claiming the case is \"resolved,\" but my issue is NOT resolved. I’m still waiting for  my funds. I will update this review once the matter is actually resolved.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "After more than two months of pure psychological distress, over 20 emails, 20 phone calls, 4 Trustpilot reviews, and 2 formal letters, my issue has finally been resolved, and I have received my first payout.\n​While I am relieved to finally access my money, my overall experience with Fintiba has been profoundly negative. For two months, I was left without a single cent, unable to pay my health insurance, and forced to accumulate debts just to survive and all of this because of ( small Technical Issue)\n​Students come to Germany to focus on their studies and future careers; we should not have to waste our energy and mental peace worrying about whether we can access our own money.\n​I sincerely hope that future payouts will arrive smoothly and without the delays that many others have unfortunately experienced. I cannot recommend this service based on the immense struggle I had to go through, and I truly hope Fintiba takes immediate action to fix their system and resolve everyone else's pending issues.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Fintiba Ticket Nr. (1125341)\n\nzunächst mal - wir haben das Geld immer noch nicht zurück erhalten. Es geht also weiter. Fintiba hat hier auf meine erste Bewertung vor 7 (!!!) Tagen geschrieben:\nHello,\nThank you for your patience. We’re pleased to let you know that your query has now been resolved.\nWe sincerely apologize for any inconvenience caused and appreciate your understanding throughout the process. If you have any further questions or need additional assistance, please feel free to contact us at support(at)fintiba.com.\n\nAlles nur dummes Gequatsche. Was nützt uns diese Entschuldigung, wenn wir das Geld immer noch nicht haben. Ich habe mal den Namen \"Support\" aus Spass gegoogelt - da heisst es wörtlich: Unterstützung, Hilfe oder Rückhalt.\n\nLiebe Fintiba - wie wäre es, wenn SIE das mal googeln. Ihren Support zu kontaktieren, ist verlorene Zeit. Es kommen nur dämliche Antworten.\n\nIch warne jeden Interessierten nach wie vor - seien Sie vorsichtig bei der Auswahl dieses \"Dienstleisters\"!!! Sie werden ihr Geld nie wieder sehen. Wir sind nun bei sage und schreibe 76 E-Mails - und ich betone - meine Freundin hat ihr Geld immer noch nicht zurückerhalten. Die Anrufe, wovon etwa drei Viertel davon einfach seitens Fintiba-Support aufgelegt bzw. abgewürgt wurden, habe ich noch nicht einmal mitgezählt. Mit unserer E-Mail von heute sind es TATSÄCHLICH 76 E-Mails - UNGLAUBILICH wie ineffizient dieser Laden (nicht) funktioniert.\n\nAktuell geht die Diskussion um folgendes: Der Fintiba Prozess bietet beim Schliessen des Kontos zwei Optionen an: Das Geld auf das \"Ursprungskonto\" zurücküberweisen, oder ein anderes Konto anzugeben. Wir hatten die Wahl - und wir haben ein anderes Konto angegeben. Und dann geht es wieder los mit unsinnigem E-Mail Verkehr. Wir haben dann eine E-Mail von Fintiba erhalten, dass es laut \"Geldwäscherei-Gesetz\" nicht möglich sei, das Geld auf ein anderes Konto zu überweisen. Versteht ihr - wir drehen uns mit diesem Fintiba-Support immer im Kreis. Sie erfinden immer wieder neue Gründe, um das Geld zu behalten. \n\nIch denke - ich werde hier nun wöchentlich Bericht erstatten. Ich bin gespannt, wann wir mit dem E-Mail Verkehr die 100er Marke knacken.!!!!!!!!!!!!!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Der Kundenservice ist völlig unbrauchbar.\n\nUpdate: Finger weg!!!\nSie wurden erneut kontaktiert – leider wieder ohne Antwort.\nEine Bank, die keine direkten Ansprechpartner oder Telefonnummern hat? Es gibt lediglich die Kundenservice-Hotline, und die Mitarbeitenden dort können nichts veranlassen. Das ist wirklich ein Witz.\nSelbst auf gesetzte Fristen wird nicht reagiert. Die Überprüfung dauert mehrere Wochen. Absolut nicht empfehlenswert.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ich habe ein Sperrkonto bei fintiba.com⁠� eröffnet und versehentlich „Visum zur Arbeitsplatzsuche“ ausgewählt, da es bei der Antragstellung keine Option für ein Ehegatten- bzw. Familiennachzugsvisum gab. Ich habe den Kundenservice sofort kontaktiert und um eine Korrektur gebeten. Trotz meiner Anfrage wurde seit über einer Woche nichts unternommen.\nAls ich den Kundenservice telefonisch kontaktierte, wurde mir mitgeteilt, dass die Bearbeitung drei Wochen oder sogar länger dauern könne. Außerdem empfand ich das Verhalten des Mitarbeiters als unhöflich und wenig hilfsbereit.\nDurch diese Verzögerung kann ich mein Visum nicht rechtzeitig beantragen, was zu unnötigem Stress und einer möglichen Verschiebung meines gesamten Visumverfahrens führt. Für einen Dienstleister, der für internationale Visa-Angelegenheiten eine wichtige Rolle spielt, hätte ich einen deutlich besseren Kundenservice und eine schnellere Bearbeitung erwartet.\nInsgesamt bin ich mit der Kommunikation, der langen Bearbeitungszeit und dem Umgang mit Kunden sehr unzufrieden. Ich hoffe, dass der Kundenservice und die internen Prozesse künftig verbessert werden.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have filed a support ticket. They say it takes them usually 1 business day to return. However it has been a week and i am yet to get a return.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I chose Fintiba Basic for block account; I don't know why after registering ,it turn into Fintiba Plus.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I contacted Fintiba support by email on 09.06.2026 and until now I have not received any real response.\n\nMy request is very simple and clear: I only want to change my health insurance from Mawista private health insurance to Barmer public health insurance.\n\nI also tried to call them several times, but I still did not receive any actual support or solution.\n\nUnfortunately, I only received automatic replies and no actual support or solution. This delay is very stressful because I need the documents for my student visa process.\n\nMy ticket number is #1256128.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I read a Reddit post recently where a girl shared her terrible experience with Fintiba support, mentioning how a guy named Alex yelled at her and was extremely rude. Well,  Alex is still at Fintiba support and he is still yelling at customers. I had the exact same experience today and I was really disappointed with their customer service.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have been a Fintiba customer and the account worked fine until approximately one month ago, when I uploaded my visa document as required to access my blocked funds.\n\nSince then, my account has been permanently stuck in \"we are checking your information\" status with no progress or timeline provided.\n\nI have sent 3 support emails (ticket nums: 1243266, 1246546 and 1253947) and received only generic \"we need more time\" responses before being completely ignored.\n\nI am now unable to access my funds despite having completed all required steps on my side. This is causing significant financial disruption.\n\nI am requesting that Fintiba or their banking partner Frankfurt International Bank (FIB) contact me urgently to resolve this verification deadlock. My next step will be a formal complaint filed directly with FIB and BaFin.\n\nUpdate: Issue was resolved on next day after this review was submitted. I just wish Fintiba didn't use this tactic to keep our money longer or just hire enough support people if this is a case..", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Seit nunmehr einem Monat habe ich keinen Zugriff auf mein Geld aus dem Sperrkonto.\n\nMein Konto wird als aktiv angezeigt und das Guthaben ist sichtbar, dennoch kann ich die Auszahlung aufgrund technischer Fehler nicht einrichten. Dadurch habe ich bereits meinen ersten Mietzahlungstermin verpasst, und der nächste steht in weniger als zwei Wochen bevor.\n\nVor über zwei Wochen habe ich eine E-Mail an den Support geschickt und bis heute keine Antwort erhalten. Mehrfach habe ich den Kundenservice telefonisch kontaktiert. Leider konnte mir niemand weiterhelfen. Heute wurde mir beim Anruf erneut mitgeteilt, dass ich weitere 10–12 Tage warten müsse. Nach den bisherigen Erfahrungen fällt es mir schwer, darauf zu vertrauen, dass sich das Problem in dieser Zeit tatsächlich lösen wird.\n\nAls internationaler Student bin ich auf dieses Geld angewiesen, um meine Miete und meinen Lebensunterhalt zu bezahlen. Es ist für mich nicht nachvollziehbar, warum ich seit einem Monat keinen Zugang zu meinem eigenen Geld habe und gleichzeitig weder eine Lösung noch eine konkrete Rückmeldung erhalte.\n\nTicketnummer: 1251475\n\nIch hoffe, dass sich endlich jemand meines Falls annimmt und dieses Problem zeitnah löst.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I wanted to extend my blocked account, and at first customer support told me that I could do it and that I did not need any specific confirmation from Fintiba. But after the funds were sent on 19 May, it turned out that they could not offer me an extension of my blocked account, so my money was supposed to be sent back to the sender’s bank account.\nSince then, I have repeatedly requested official confirmation that my money was sent back, a SWIFT trace, an MT103, or any other proof of the transaction, but I have received no meaningful response. I have contacted customer support several times by email and phone, but nobody has been able to tell me anything useful. All I have received are useless automated replies saying that they “need more time to solve the problem.”\nFrom my perspective, this looks as if Fintiba and FIB have simply appropriated my money and are refusing to provide any proof of where it is. I have already filed a complaint with BaFin and sent an official complaint to FIB, but I still have not received any proper response. The last time I called customer support, the agent did not even ask for my passport details and simply told me to “wait” because they “could not do anything.”\nI strongly recommend not using this company for a blocked account.\nI also found many complaints against Fintiba on Reddit describing very similar problems. Some users say they did not receive their funds back even after three months of waiting.\nThink twice before using this service.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I opened an account with Fintiba, and it has been downhill since then. They never reply to emails, forcing one to call them on their customer care line. This being an international call, it's can get very expensive very quickly. After deciding to absorb the cost, I keep waiting on the line for over 10 minutes only for the customer care agent to put me on hold while they verify \"somethings\" then just hang up on me repeatedly.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Hello fintiba team,  I am dipali gediya . I have been waiting for long time for payout of my block money in fintiba . Now i am in alot of stress . \nBecause i went fintiba office 10 times and also sent 35 email . \nNow i got notification from landlord i did not pay rent and i have no work . My all money is now in fintiba block account . \nAs a girl i am in stress and i do not know what i will do with my self because of this stress . I am giving you last reminder that please give me my money back . I must need to start lowyer process and i must have to complain with BAFIN .   \n\nnow it‘sbeen pending for over 3 months without resolution.\n\nDespite multiple previous requests, I have not received:\n\nA clear explanation for the delay\nA confirmed payout transaction reference (SEPA/TX ID)\n\nA definitive timeline for the transfer\n\nThis delay is no longer acceptable and is causing serious financial and personal inconvenience.\n\nI hereby request the following information and action within 5 working days:\n\nImmediate confirmation of the payout status\nThe official transaction reference number (SEPA / TX ID)\n\nExact reason for the delay\nA confirmed date by which the funds will be transferred\n\nIf I do not receive a clear response within the stated timeframe, I will proceed with:\n\nFiling a formal complaint with the German Federal Financial Supervisory Authority (BaFin)\nSeeking legal assistance to recover my funds\n\nbest of luck \n\ncontact me on : dipalikachhadiya05@....", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am extremely disappointed with my experience with Fintiba.\n\nI have been waiting for my blocked account payout for more than three weeks. During this time, I repeatedly contacted customer support and was told several times that the payment had already been initiated. However, the funds have still not arrived in my bank account.\n\nI asked multiple times for the End-to-End payment reference or any proof of transfer so that I could track the payment with my bank. Despite these requests, Fintiba has never provided any payment reference, transfer confirmation, or evidence that the money was actually sent.\n\nAs a newcomer in Germany, I depend on these funds for my daily living expenses. The ongoing delays and lack of transparency have caused serious financial difficulties and unnecessary stress.\n\nTo resolve the issue, I traveled to the Fintiba office in Frankfurt twice in person. Despite these visits and numerous emails, the problem remains unresolved and I still have not received my money.\n\nAt the time of writing this review, I still have not received my funds.\n\nFor reference, my most recent support ticket is #1256364. This is only the latest ticket, as I have contacted support multiple times regarding this issue.\n\nBased on my experience, I cannot recommend this service.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I'm following up on ticket #1253719. It's June 15th, and I still haven't received this month's payout despite ~20 calls and 10/11 emails, with no clear timeline given. As an international student, this delay is causing serious financial stress. Please provide a status update and a concrete date for resolution as soon as possible.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Hi team i am really disappointed with fintiba service at the moment its been two weeks now i am stuck on identity verification loosing hope now and my appointment is too close and still i don’t know i will get reply from fintiba or not", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "My experience with Fintiba has been ongoing since March and is still unresolved. This is a factual summary of what has happened.\nI opened my account and completed passport verification in the app at the beginning of the process. After that, I was instructed to complete additional steps including PostIdent and submitting signed legitimation documents by post. I completed every single instruction given to me.\nDespite full compliance, the process continuously failed at different stages.\nI was later told that a passport copy was missing, even though a passport copy was already included in the legitimation documents provided by Fintiba. I immediately sent the requested passport copy by email twice as instructed.\nAfter waiting several weeks, I was then told that my documents were not received or not available at all.\nBecause of continued delays, I was instructed to complete in-person verification at Sutor Bank, which I did. The bank confirmed that the documents would be sent and should arrive within a few days.\nHowever, no progress followed.\nWhen contacting support again, I was informed that my account is actually linked to a different bank (FIB Bank), not Sutor Bank — despite being directed there earlier. This inconsistency is unacceptable given the sensitivity of the process.\nSupport experience has been consistently poor:\nOnly a hotline is available, with long waiting times (often 20+ minutes)\nAgents repeatedly state they cannot see or explain the actual status of verification\nI was repeatedly told “high priority tickets” would be created, but nothing changed for weeks\nI was promised a callback regarding an appointment that never happened\nNo one provides clear timelines, ownership, or accountability for the case\nThe result is a process that has been ongoing for months since March with no resolution, despite full cooperation and repeated submission of all requested documents.\nThis has caused serious financial consequences, including inability to reliably plan or meet essential obligations such as rent and bills due to blocked access to funds.\nAt this point, the issue is not minor delays — it is a complete lack of transparency, inconsistent instructions, and failure to resolve a basic verification process over an extended period of time.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "ich bräuchte Hilfe bei package Wechsel stundenlang gewartet niemand geht ans Telefon.\n\nEmail auch geschrieben keine Antwort.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "First When I call no one attends. Have been waiting 10 minutes multiple time just ringing no one cares.\n\nI have visa change and block account need to be extended when i requested they just said we can not do it use other service , what about my remaining funds here what kind of stupid response is this.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have been waiting for my money to be returned for 3 months, and Fintiba has completely stopped responding to my emails.\n\nI want to warn everyone reading these reviews: do not fall for their comments. When they reply here claiming \"the issue has been resolved,\" it is an absolute lie and just a fake bot response to save their public image. Nothing is actually fixed and they just keep your money. Avoid this company at all costs.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am extremely frustrated with Fintiba. I’ve made a blocked account and asked them via email whether or not I could transfer from a USD account (I’m not in the US), which they never replied to, even after waiting for a month. I sent a follow-up and another, similar email, but those also went ignored.\n\nI then sent a test transfer of €63 and it went through, so I therefore didn’t need confirmation from them any longer, but thereafter I faced another issue – I could only make two more transfers to complete the total transaction amount of €12,100. This was supposedly communicated to me via a transfer information document, but you can’t download this document from the site. It’s only accessible via their mobile app, which I didn’t have.\n\nNow I’m facing another issue. I can’t transfer more than €4,300 from my bank account at a time, and my bank is unwilling to change this limit. This means I can’t transfer the remainder of €12,100 in the two transactions that I can make. \n\nI have emailed and called Fintiba for a solution to this new problem and again I have been ignored. The person I spoke to on the phone advised me to email them as he would “prioritize my request”, but it still has been ignored. I am at my wits end at this point.\n\nUpdate: The issue has been resolved, but now I need to update my passport information and they — you guessed it — haven’t responded to my email.\n\n–Nasif Istiak Remon.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Dear Fintiba Support Team, \n\n\nToday date : 16th june 2026 \nI am making new review that i am seeing FIB iban now why ? Still 1 year i see Sitor bank iban and my account balance like 13231 euro in my account but today account balance is 0 why ? I want answer today and where is my all money i did not get even single installment and now it’s been 4 months . First why account balance is 0 and where is my money tell me this is i am asking last time otherwise i already talked with my personal laywer so let me know i am tired from your service now\n\n13th june \nI am writing again regarding my pending payout(s), which have still not been credited to my bank account, despite completing all required steps, including correct IBAN setup and multiple payout requests.\n\nAccording to your latest message, the payout has already been executed and should arrive within a few working days. However, I have still not received the funds in my account.\nI have also tried contacting your support team via email and phone, but I have not received any clear response or resolution.\n\nAt this point, I need to inform you that if the full amount is not received by Monday, I will escalate this matter further by filing a formal complaint with the relevant financial supervisory authority (BaFin) and will also consider legal action through a lawyer if necessary.\n\nI kindly request you to treat this matter as urgent and provide me with a clear update, including the transaction reference (SWIFT/MT103) for tracking the payment.\nI expect a prompt resolution.\n\nKind regards,\nDipali gediya", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Es gibt keine Professionalität im Umgang mit Kunden. besonders die Mitarbeiter warten nur auf den Moment. in dem sie das Telefon auflegen können.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "It's not clear how I should register if I'm already in Germany and just need a blocked account: I can't opt out of health insurance, I can't choose a month from which to start receiving money (I need July and can only choose the next semester). Support has been ignoring me for more than two weeks (via email and phone)", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Zu langsam , zu kompliziert, und schlechtes Support..\nIch empfehle nicht", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Fintiba’s internal system (Fintiba Transfer) has a severe bug that glitched my name into '???', holding my 96,717.13 CNY visa deposit since May 21st. Their customer support is totally useless, refusing manual intervention for 3 weeks and ignoring urgent timelines. I am now filing a formal complaint to BaFin for unlawfully retaining student assets. Issue my confirmation immediatel", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "\"Thank you for your E-mail. Please note that you have to confirm if the original account where the money came from when it was sent to the blocked account is active or if you would like to receive the funds in another account, so that we can no how to continue next.\"\n\nI received this email three times after already providing the requested information. \n\nThe message contains grammatical errors (e.g., \"no how\"), which undermines confidence in their professionalism. \nI entrusted Fintiba with my funds at the beginning of 2026 and have now waited months with only automated replies and no human escalation.  \n\nTickets: 1228929, 1168775, 1173909, 1233623.\n\n⚠️ Update: Fintiba replied claiming the case is \"resolved,\" but my issue is NOT resolved. I’m still waiting for account closure and my funds. I will update this review once the matter is actually resolved.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am unable to get my payouts despite sending multiple emails and waiting for more than a month. I received roughly 900 euros when I arrived here on the 1st of April, but then the system skipped my May and June payouts. I am currently surviving without funds. The call agents have no authority and cannot do anything to help. Despite sending several emails, I have received no replies at all. I have sent my final warning email and will be complaining to BaFin, as well as going to a lawyer to get my funds back. This is a very stressful situation. I am wasting so much time and struggling to manage my studies with this kind of mental stress.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Unacceptable: Blocked funds withheld for 45days (ID: IN01045866)\nReview: Fintiba and Frankfurt International Bank have been withholding my blocked living expenses for 45 days. I have successfully completed my Post dent verification THREE separate times. Their system is completely glitched and customer support ignores all emails and tells me to \"wait\" on the phone. I have officially filed a formal consumer complaint with BaFin (The German Financial Regulator). Unblock my account (Customer ID:\nIN01045866) immediately.why are you replying with your problem is solved my problem is not solved yet and you give fake information and response so others can trust you.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Dear Fintiba team \nI opened an account with you and the email is Wrong \nPassport number T97658542\nAnd tickets are #1258301 and #1255930\nIt’s one month I call your costumer service and it’s not solving !\nFor God sake \nCorrect this \nMy visa application is one month on hold because of this problem", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have been trying to withdraw my funds from Fintiba for more than 9 weeks now.\nAt first, I uploaded my visa and passport as requested. My account was then activated, and I was informed that my funds would be transferred. However, shortly after, my account was suddenly put into a pending status again.\nMost recently, I was asked to complete a reverse transfer form, which I did. Today, I was again informed that my funds would be transferred. However, later in the evening, I received another email requesting a “Sperrfreigabe” document in order to close my account.\nThis requirement is not possible for me to provide, as I already have a valid visa, I have not received any rejection, and I have already uploaded my visa into your system.\nI have discussed this situation with my lawyer. If my funds are not transferred and this issue is not resolved, I will proceed with legal action.\nI am being left with the impression that my money is being deliberately withheld, which I find unacceptable.\nI expect this matter to be resolved immediately. (My ticket is:1258816 and 1250786)", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Sehr geehrte Damen und Herren,\nich habe die erforderliche Gebühr für mein gesperrtes Konto überwiesen. Es ist nun fast eine Woche her, aber ich habe die Bestätigungsbescheinigung noch immer nicht erhalten. Dieses Dokument ist für meinen Antrag auf eine Chancenkarte wichtig. Ich bitte Sie um eine umgehende Antwort.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I opened a Fintiba account and have been trying to close it and withdraw my funds since the beginning of 2026. Six months later there is still no resolution. I’ve opened multiple support tickets (1228929, 1168775, 1173909, 1233623) and all I get are automated/bot replies with no clear timeline, no human escalation, and no accountability. This has caused significant financial stress and wasted a huge amount of my time. Customer service is unresponsive and the process is opaque - I cannot recommend Fintiba to anyone who needs reliable access to their money. You're Advised to avoid Fintiba until they fix their support and withdrawal procedures.\n\n⚠️ Update: Fintiba replied claiming the case is \"resolved,\" but my issue is NOT resolved. I’m still waiting for account closure and my funds. I will update this review once the matter is actually resolved.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ich bin seit Ende April in Deutschland, ich habe alle benötigte Unterlagen (Visum, zulassung der Uni...) leider wurde mein Payout immer noch nicht aktiviert. Ich kann kein IBAN eingeben um geld zu bekommen. Mein Email an Support wird einfach ignoriert. Ich kann die Sprachekurz und die Miete nicht zahlen und bin gezwungen zu Hause zu bleiben", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Poor service", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Dear Fintiba Team!   \nAfter my repeated emails and complaints, you finally informed me on June 8th that my Mavista insurance had been cancelled.\nI also saw in my Fintiba personal account that both Mavista insurance policies had been cancelled.\nHowever, today I discovered that Mavista has debited my account for the monthly insurance premium of 115 euros.\nHow can you explain this? Furthermore, I had already written to Mavista twice (on June 2nd and 4th) regarding the cancellation of my insurance and provided details of a different policy from the same company as a replacement. \nPlease reply urgently.  \nIf I do not receive a response and a resolution to this simple issue, I will be forced to file a complaint with the Verbraucherzentrale, as I am currently in Germany.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Dear Sir/Madam,I am filing an official complaint against Sutor Bank and its partner Fintiba for the unlawful withholding of my funds.Since November 2025, I have provided the official Embassy release letter (Sperrfreigabe). Furthermore, a notarized and apostilled legitimization document from Peru was physically delivered and accepted at Fintiba’s offices. Despite fulfilling all legal criteria, Fintiba mistakenly processed my account for \"activation\" instead of a \"refund\" due to an internal staff error. They have completely ignored my emails for over a month and failed to reply to my final formal warning sent 3 business days ago. I request BaFin’s immediate intervention to compel Sutor Bank to release my funds and provide the SWIFT MT103 confirmation. Account Number: 976-001-729 Account Holder: Maria Ana Garcia Revilla", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Dear Fintiba Support Team,\n\nI hope you are doing well.\n\nI am writing regarding my ongoing issue with my Fintiba account and Ticket Number #1255930.very helpful representative created this ticket.\n\nWhen I initially opened my account, I accidentally entered an incorrect email address. Following your instructions, I submitted a verification photo of myself holding my passport along with the email address that I wanted to use for my account. I completed all requested verification steps promptly.\n\nHowever, it has now been over one month, and I have not received any update regarding the resolution of this issue. I was later informed that the email address I originally requested might already be associated with another Fintiba account and therefore could not be used for the change.\n\nTo help resolve this matter, I submitted a new verification photo holding my passport and provided a different email address that has never been registered with Fintiba. I have fully cooperated with every request and supplied all necessary documents.\n\nI would also like to formally raise a concern regarding my call with a female customer service representative (Miss Hassan) on 10 June 2026 at approximately 13:44 (Germany  time). The call lasted around 23 minutes, and the ticket number is (1257080) I kindly request that the call recording be reviewed.\n\nDuring the conversation, while I was trying to explain my situation and seek assistance with my long-pending account issue, the representative stated that I was “wasting her time.” I was surprised and distressed by this remark, especially considering that my visa process has been delayed for over a month due to this unresolved matter.\n\nUnfortunately, my visa process has been delayed for nearly a month solely because of this email change issue. This situation has caused significant stress and may affect important deadlines related to my studies and travel arrangements.\n\nI kindly and respectfully ask for your urgent assistance in updating my email address and completing the remaining account verification process as soon as possible. I would be very grateful if my case could be reviewed with priority, as this matter is now directly impacting my visa application.\n\nThank you for your time, understanding, and support. I look forward to your response and to resolving this issue as soon as possible.\n\nKind regards,\n\nSara Nourolahzadeh Kalkhoran\nTicket Number: #1255930", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "UPDATE – ISSUE STILL NOT RESOLVED (NOW EVEN WORSE)\n\nI am updating my previous review because the issue still has not been resolved and the situation has become even more frustrating.\n\nAfter my previous review, I was contacted and informed that the issue had finally been fixed. I logged into my account and at first everything appeared normal again — my balance showed €3,462, which matched the amount that had previously been confirmed as credited to my blocked account.\n\nI proceeded to enter my IBAN in order to start the payout process. After entering the confirmation code sent to my phone number, I received an error message: “Error XG12 – please try again later.”\n\nI tried again, but received the same error once more.\n\nAfter that, my account still displayed the balance, but the next day when I logged in again, the system showed: “Can’t calculate your payouts – please contact support.”\n\nThis is now the third time I have been told that the issue was fixed, only to log in and discover that it still does not work.\n\nPreviously I received replies from support within a day, but now I am no longer receiving responses.\n\nTo summarize:\n• Funds deposited: January 13\n• Visa documents submitted months ago\n• Balance disappeared and reappeared multiple times\n• Balance showed €3,462 after being told the issue was resolved\n• Entered IBAN and payout setup failed with Error XG12\n• “Can’t calculate your payouts” message appeared again\n• Support is currently not responding\n\nI am currently in Germany and urgently need access to my payout documents and funds for my residence permit extension and living expenses.\n\nAt this point, after around five months of ongoing issues, I honestly no longer understand how a system handling blocked accounts can continue showing the same technical problems repeatedly after multiple confirmations that everything was fixed.\n\nI truly hope this situation finally comes to an end, because I am starting to lose confidence that this issue will ever be resolved.\n\nTicket number: 1237245", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I haven't received payouts for the last two months, and they're not responding to my open ticket.\nCalling customer service is pointless; they'll ask you to write an email and spam you with the \"Just a little longer\" replies.\nThe only star earned is because they provide good paperwork and an easy process for depositing and setting up the payouts.\nAlso, they mislead you into thinking they also provide a second account for payouts; they do not offer that service.\nUpdate:\nIt's month 5 now; not a single payment was sent automatically.\nI had to send an email every month to receive my payment at least 6 days late.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Same bad experienced with other people. I've been here in Germany for almost 3 months, everytime I am setting up my IBAN, and then I dont receive any OTP from phone or email.\n\nThis is so frustrating. I can't do my payouts. I saved that money for a year. And I can't used it here in Germany.\n\nSo disappointing Fintiba.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "seit über einem Jahr versuche ich einer Freundin behilflich zu sein, dass sie ihr bei der Fintiba eingezahltes Geld endlich zurück erhält. Ihr Visum wurde von den Deutschen Behörden abgelehnt. Seither versuchen wir ihr Geld zurückzuerhalten. Der Fintiba Support schreibt (wenn überhaupt eine Antwort kommt) Antworten - die keiner versteht. Diese Antworten kommen sehr selten und sehr verspätet. Teilweise haben wir Monate auf eine Antwort gewartet. Wenn man dann anruft und nachfragt, wird man vertröstet, noch eine Woche zu warten - dann käme bestimmt eine Antwort. Und dann noch eine Woche, und noch eine und noch eine. Und nun ist schon über ein Jahr vergangen - und NICHTS ist passiert. Wir tun alles was sie verlangen (wenn man das überhaupt versteht was sie wollen). Sie bekommen Anweisungen wie \"Ana..., du musst in deinem Konto aktiv werden!\". \n\nUnd wenn man den Support anruft und das Problem erklärt, und man dann sagt, das hätten wir nun schon vier mal gehört, dass in einer Woche eine Antwort kommt, dann legt der Support der Fintiba den Hörer einfach auf mitten im Gespräch. Das haben wir nun schon mehrmals erlebt, dass die einfach mitten im Gespräch auflegen. \n\nNiemand wurde von unserer Seite laut - niemand hat geschimpft - wir waren immer höflich, (obwohl das schwierig ist nach so langer Zeit) wir haben einfach nur gefragt, wann wir eine Antwort erwarten dürfen. \n\nWir haben leider den Eindruck gewonnen, dass diese Leute vom Fintiba Support arrogante Leute sind, die mit den Studenten spielen als wäre das ihr Geld. \n\nHier ein Beispiel von einer E-Mail vom Fintiba Support. Wir mussten das Sperrkonto auflösen. Dazu verlangte das Fintiba System ein Dokument, welches beweist, dass das Visum abgelehnt wurde. Wir haben dieses Schreiben der Deutschen Botschaft (einen Scan) hochgeladen. Heute, einen Tag später erhalten wir eine E-Mail von Fintiba mit folgendem Inhalt:\n\"Ihre Verifizierung ist fehlgeschlagen 😞 Hier ist der Grund:\nFolgendes ist passiert: Screenshots, Scans, Bildschirmfotos und Schwarzweißbilder können aufgrund fehlender Authentizität leider nicht akzeptiert werden. Aktualisieren Sie Ihre Informationen\"\n\nDas ist alles. Das Dokument war ein sauberer Scan - kein Printscreen. Aber Scans werden nicht akzeptiert. Was sollen wir den sonst noch machen?\n\nWir bekommen einfach das Geld nicht zurück. Wir haben nach über einem Jahr Ärger mit dieser Fintiba den Eindruck, dass das - (ich will dieses Wort hier nicht schreiben) sind. Die spielen mit den Studenten. Und es geht hier immerhin um eine fünfstellige EURO Summe. Die rücken einfach das Geld nicht heraus. Wir wussten uns einfach nicht mehr zu helfen. Deshalb haben wir nun nach 14 Monaten diese Kritik geschrieben.\n\nWir empfehlen jedem, aufgrund unserer Erfahrungen - seien Sie vorsichtig mit Fintiba - Sie sehen sonst ihr Geld NIE WIEDER..!!!\n\nFintiba Ticket Nr. (1125341) \n\nStellungnahme zur untenstehenden Fintiba Antwort vom 11.06.2026\n\nDiese Antwort strotzt nur so vor Spott und Hohn. Fintiba setzt voraus, dass wir Geduld haben mit Ihnen. Ich kann Ihnen sagen, dass unsere Geduld mit Ihnen schon längst erschöpft ist. Auch dass Sie aus irgendeinem irrigen Grund annehmen, dass wir \"Verständnis\" haben für Fintiba, ist eine Frechheit. Nach diesen vielen Monaten, und den zahlreichen Telefonaten, wo ihr unhöfliches Supportpersonal einfach das Telefon auflegen und absolut NICHTS unternehmen, dass das Geld wieder an die rechtmässige Besitzerin zurückgeht - und Sie wollen Verständnis dafür? Der geneigte Leser soll ein wenig nach unten scrollen hier in dieser Liste. Immer wieder kann man lesen, wie grottenschlecht und unnütz ihr Support ist, und wie ihr Support immer wieder einfach das Telefon auflegt. Wir glauben der Fintiba gar nichts mehr bis zu dem Tag, wo das Geld endlich wieder bei der rechtmässigen Besitzerin ist - und by the way - das ist nicht etwa die Fintiba.!!! \n\nEin guter Rat an die Geschäftsleitung von Fintiba: misten Sie mal tüchtig ihr Support-Stall aus, und ersetzen Sie diese Leute, durch Mitarbeiter, welche ihren Job und ihre Kunden ernst nehmen und auch als solche behandeln! Und schulen Sie ihr Support Personal dahingehend, dass das Geld NICHT Fintiba gehört, und dass WIR die KUNDEN sind! Und mit Kunden geht man nicht so um.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Let me delete my account!!!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "This is my Fourth review on this platform within a single month, as my problem remains completely unresolved. I am writing this as a final warning before taking legal action and filing a formal complaint with the BaFin.\n​For over  two months, I have been trapped in an endless loop. I contact customer service daily, only to receive generic responses. Now, the payout is failing due to a technical glitch: I am not receiving the mandatory OTP via email or SMS to register my German IBAN.\n​As an international student, I depend entirely on this blocked account. Due to your ongoing system failures and total inaction, I am left without a single cent, unable to buy food or pay my rent.\n​I demand a resolution within the next 48 hours. If my account is not unlocked by then, I will proceed with BaFin and legal steps immediately.\nticket Number [1245372]", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I opened the block account in Fintiba during short time but after I decided to upgrade my account to Fintiba plus to include health insurance and travel insurance and they replied that during 24 hours they will do it but passed a week now and still didn't get my request???", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am an international student and have been waiting for more than three months for the monthly payouts from my blocked account to start. All requirements were fulfilled, yet no payout has ever been made.\n\nI have contacted Fintiba multiple times and always receive the same answer: \"There is a technical issue and the IT team is working on it.\" After more than three months, there is still no solution, no timeline, and no clear communication.\n\nThese funds are essential for my rent, health insurance, food, and daily expenses. Leaving a student without access to their own money for months is simply unacceptable.\n\nVery disappointing experience and poor handling of a serious issue. 1/5.\n\nStill waiting !!!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "FINTIBA SCAMMING BANK \n\nTICKET NO.: \n1249434\n1203176\n1222793\n1222811\n1230055\n1204619\n\nINTERNATIONAL STUDENTS PLEASE BE VERY CAREFUL WITH THIS SCAMMER BANK!!!!\n\nI have been trying to set up my Fintiba since March 2026 and it’s been June 2026, they haven’t still done anything to get me my money! I have been stuck in the legitimation phase for over two months and they will basically ignore everything you do!! Their customer service representative Alex will treat you like you owe them money and will basically tell you to come to Frankfurt or you can go f yourself!! I have done 3 post ident identification at the Post Office, went to my local bank, sent them 2 address confirmations and still they told me i didn’t send the correct documents!! \n\nI would advise anyone coming to do their blocked account to avoid this company!! They are not a bank! They will treat you like third world citizens and they will tell you it’s not their problems that you don’t have money! Right now i sit with an eviction letter from my landlord and DB and my phone provider is sending me to court! I sent them the court letter as proof of address and they still don’t think i live at that address!!! \n\n\nIt’s really pathetic! I hope it helps future students! They won’t offer you any help, after telling them your situation the best response for them is to hang up the phone on your face and send you a generic email!!\n\nBEWARE!!!!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ich warte seit fast zwei Monaten auf eine Antwort. Jedes Mal am Telefon wird mir nur gesagt, ich solle eine E-Mail schreiben, aber auf meine E-Mails reagiert niemand!\nIch habe meinen Reisepass erneuert und natürlich eine neue Passnummer erhalten. Obwohl ich alle neuen Dokumente eingereicht habe, werden sie einfach ignoriert oder abgelehnt. Mein Visum und meine Universitätseinschreibung sind jetzt in akuter Gefahr, nur weil Fintiba seit zwei Monaten untätig ist. Ich weiß wirklich nicht mehr, was ich tun soll.\nIch empfehle jedem, lieber über andere Banken nachzudenken, da Fintiba einfach nicht antwortet\n\nUpdate:\nLeider ist mein Problem immer noch nicht gelöst. Der Prozess lief anfangs gut, ist aber jetzt komplett zum Stillstand gekommen.\nMir wurde mitgeteilt, dass ich mein Sperrkonto verlängern soll, was ich auch getan habe. Zudem hieß es, dass das verbleibende Guthaben von 12.000 Euro von meinem alten Konto auf das neue, verlängerte Konto übertragen wird. Jetzt verlangt Fintiba jedoch von mir, dass ich noch einmal 12.000 Euro auf das verlängerte Konto einzahle! Das ergibt absolut keinen Sinn. Sie haben mein Geld bereits (12.000 Euro), erwarten aber nun eine doppelte Zahlung, was ihrer vorherigen Nachricht völlig widerspricht.\nObwohl ich die anfänglichen kleinen Fortschritte schätze, steht der letzte und wichtigste Schritt  die Ausstellung der neuen Sperrbestätigung für meine Visumsverlängerung immer noch aus.\nIch habe bereits angerufen und ein Support-Ticket eröffnet, aber mein Ticket wurde bisher nicht aktualisiert. Ich brauche eine Klärung dieses finanziellen Missverständnisses und meine Visumsunterlagen!(Ticket: 1222647)\n\nTicket-ID: \n\n1203362\n1188050", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "My June payout as of today (9th of June) has not being sent. This is irresponsible. They’re not providing a service they’re advertising. Horrible service. I have been left stranded in Germany without money for almost 10 days now. I have escalated the situation to BaFin and will look into other legal methods. \n\nFintiba gave me a generic response through email but still doesn’t respond to my questions. \n\nIt is impacting my lifestyle, mental health and many other things. They sent me an email saying they’re looking into the situation last week on Friday. At this point it doesn’t even make sense because the next two days were the weekend days. \n\nDon’t trust fintiba, they will not give you your own money on a monthly basis. \nPatience doesn’t solve my problems. I’m extremely disappointed.\n\nThey deducted the administrative fee while still not paying my money. I have been dealing with so much stress. I cannot pay for my DB ticket which leads to legal penalties and impacts my Schufa score.\n\nThe deduction of the fee hints that it is not a technical problem but rather something else. \n\nTicket number: 1248088", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The worst application ever i told him  one hundred time that i have another insurance and they never respect me and they want me to pay for mawista they stole money i send them more than 5 email to mawista and fintiba and they don’t listen or read my messages that totally shit I don’t want this mawista and I’ll never pay for it and if they take money i want to call my lawyer and complain", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "UPDATE – ISSUE STILL NOT RESOLVED (NOW EVEN WORSE)\n\nI am updating my previous review because the issue remains unresolved and has become even more confusing.\n\nAfter my original review, I was contacted and informed that the issue had been fixed. My blocked account balance finally appeared again and showed €3,462, which matched the amount I had previously proven was credited to my account.\n\nI then entered my IBAN to start receiving payouts. However, instead of processing the payout, I received an error message stating: “Can’t calculate your payouts – please contact support.”\n\nI contacted support immediately but received no response.\n\nToday, when I checked again, my balance had disappeared once more and returned to €0.\n\nTo summarize:\n• Funds deposited: January 13  \n• Visa documents submitted months ago  \n• Balance repeatedly disappears and reappears  \n• Balance showed €3,462 again recently  \n• Payout setup failed with an error  \n• No response from support  \n• Balance is now back to €0  \n\nI am currently in Germany and my residence permit is expiring. I urgently need access to my payout documents and funds for my visa extension and living expenses.\n\nAt this point, after around five months of unresolved issues, I no longer understand why my balance keeps disappearing or why payouts cannot be calculated despite the funds appearing in the account.\n\nI am requesting an immediate clarification and resolution. If this continues without action, I will consider escalating the matter to the relevant financial authorities and seeking legal advice.\n\nVery disappointing experience.\n\nTicket number: 1237245", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I do not understand why applicants are required to purchase insurance when opening a blocked account. In my case, I already had valid health insurance coverage, yet I was still required to purchase an additional insurance plan through your platform in order to complete the registration process.\n\nAfter realizing this, I made several attempts to contact customer support and request that the insurance be cancelled, as I do not need it. Unfortunately, despite sending multiple messages and trying different communication channels, I received nothing more than an automated email response. No one reviewed my case or provided any meaningful assistance.\n\nWhat makes the situation even more disappointing is the lack of accessible support options. I spent a considerable amount of time trying to find a phone number or a way to speak directly with a representative so I could clearly explain my situation and resolve the issue. However, I was unable to reach anyone.\n\nAs a customer, I expected a much higher level of support, especially when dealing with important matters such as blocked accounts and insurance services. The overall experience has been frustrating and time-consuming.\n\nI hope you will review my case, cancel the unnecessary insurance policy, and improve the quality and accessibility of your customer support for future customers.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Your service has become too slow. Problems occur at every stage. Your customer support does not work at all.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have held a blocked account with Fintiba for over a year and have generally been satisfied with your service; however, the last two months have been problematic.\n\nWhile my May payout arrived on the 4th, it is now June 8th and I have yet to receive my funds for this month. I contacted support on June 4th and was told the accounting department would reach out, but I have received no response. Today, I attempted to call almost 7/8 times. During around 5 attempts, I waited on hold for eight minutes without an answer, and during the other cases, I was told a connection could not be made.\n\nAs a student, this delay is highly distressing. My rent and bills are due by the 5th of each month, and the lack of communication regarding this delay is unprofessional. If there is a system issue, I expect to be notified rather than being left without information or access to customer support. Ticket number:  1253965\nThank you.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "My experience with Fintiba has been generally positive. Fintiba's customer support was quick and responsive. Although there was an issue with a payment, they handled it professionally and agreed to refund the money after I contacted them.\n\nHowever, I find the €160 initial fee and the €10 monthly fee quite unfair and expensive for the service provided. Overall, the support was excellent, but the pricing could be improved.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am writing to report a false claim made on my recent review regarding Fintiba.\n\nAfter I posted my complaint on your platform, Fintiba responded and claimed that the issue had been resolved. However, more than 4 weeks have passed since their reply, and it was nothing but an empty promise. Absolutely no money has been deposited into my account!\n\nDue to their deceptive behavior and continued withholding of my funds, it is clear that a formal complaint must be filed with the German Federal Financial Supervisory Authority (BaFin).\n\nI want my review to reflect the truth so that other users are not fooled by their fake public responses. Please let me know how I can update my review status to show that the problem remains completely unresolved.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have request for change of address and it has been 4 days and there has been no reply or response from the team.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "DO NOT TRUST THIS COMPANY. I am an international student in Germany and Fintiba has created an artificial financial crisis for me.\nI updated my address details nearly TWO MONTHS AGO, and my profile has been stuck on \"pending verification\" ever since. Because of their extreme administrative incompetence and failure to review a simple document, they have now BLOCKED my monthly payout.\nI cannot pay my rent, I cannot pay my health insurance, and I am left with no money to survive. To make matters worse, their customer service is non-existent. They do not answer the phone, and they ignore all support tickets inside the app. Completely cutting off communication while withholding a student's legal livelihood is unacceptable.\nIf my address is not approved and my funds are not released immediately, I will escalate this compliance failure to BaFin (Federal Financial Supervisory Authority). \nMy ticket is 1246843", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have not received my june payout until now, regardless of sending you multiple emails and you solving them automatically (No reply from you, just closing my ticket). I already put a review here before and you told me that you contacted me with details, but I never got contacted.\n\nIt is already the 8th of the Month,and honestly this is not ok at all.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ich nutze Fintiba seit März 2026 für mein Sperrkonto. Die ersten beiden monatlichen Auszahlungen kamen nahezu problemlos an. Bei der letzten und abschließenden Überweisung jedoch warte ich nun seit über einem Monat vergeblich. Als Grund wird telefonisch ein „technischer Fehler\" genannt – eine Erklärung, die ich in auffällig vielen anderen Bewertungen hier wiederfinde.\n\nFristsetzung ignoriert. Support-Ticket erstellt, Frist schriftlich gesetzt – keine Reaktion außer der telefonischen Aussage, man wisse nicht, wann das Problem gelöst wird. Neue E-Mails, so wurde mir erklärt, verschieben mich ans Ende der Warteschlange.\n\nZur Einordnung: Fintibas Kernprodukt richtet sich an internationale Studierende, die ein Sperrkonto als gesetzlich vorgeschriebenen Finanzierungsnachweis benötigen. Diese Auszahlungen sind keine optionalen Überweisungen – sie sind Lebenshaltungskosten. Wer hier über Wochen hinhält, nimmt billigend in Kauf, dass Menschen in finanzielle Not geraten.\n\nIch bereite derzeit eine Beschwerde bei der BaFin vor und werde diese einreichen, sofern sich Fintiba nicht zeitnah meldet.\n\nIch habe eine Rechtsschutzversicherung und werde rechtliche Schritte einleiten, sofern die Zahlung nicht innerhalb weniger Tage eingeht. Parallel reiche ich die BaFin-Beschwerde ein.\n\nFintiba: Ticket-Nummer liegt vor: 1225973. Ich erwarte eine direkte Reaktion hier oder per E-Mail – keine Standardantwort.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Very disappointing experience with Fintiba. Their customer support is extremely slow and ineffective. Every response takes around 24 hours, so if you have an urgent matter, don't expect timely assistance.\n\nWhat's even more frustrating is that after waiting a full day, you often don't receive an answer to the actual question you asked. The responses are generic, incomplete, and frequently fail to address the issue. It feels like support agents either don't fully read the message or don't understand the problem.\n\nAs a result, even the smallest matters can take days or sometimes weeks to resolve because you're stuck in an endless cycle of waiting for replies that don't provide the information you need.\n\nFor a service that handles important financial and visa-related matters, this level of support is unacceptable. The entire support system is poorly organized, inefficient, and incredibly frustrating to deal with. I would not recommend Fintiba based on my experience.\n\nalso uploading document system is way more pathetic i must say", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "There is still no response from Fintiba. I haven’t got my payout for June and have been left stranded without money in Germany for a whole week now. This is extremely irresponsible. Don’t give your money to Fintiba, because they will not bother to respond but also have extremely rude agents telling you, you are annoying for asking about the whereabouts of your money. \n\nIf you can’t process money and do your job properly then don’t open such a business in the first place. My DB ticket got cancelled, I can’t pay for basic necessities. I’m really glad that this whole ordeal with Fintiba will end in August. I’m no longer planning to actively subscribe and extend my account. \n\nHorrible!\nTicket numbers:\n1248088\n1247706\n1243858", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have been trying to receive my money from Fintiba for more than two months. During this time, I have called multiple times and sent numerous emails, but my issue remains unresolved.\nFirst, my account was activated, and then it was closed again. This situation has caused me significant financial difficulties and a great deal of psychological stress.\nMost recently, I received a reversal transfer form. Unfortunately, I made a mistake while filling it out, which resulted in an error. I immediately contacted your support team by email and asked for assistance, but once again I have not received any response.\nI am extremely frustrated with the lack of communication and the way this matter has been handled. I have been waiting for far too long and have done everything requested of me.\nIf this issue is not resolved promptly, I will have no choice but to seek legal advice and consider taking further legal action. (My Ticket:1198153)", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Fintiba crushed my dream of going to Germany 😭We did everything and they still cannot open a correct account for me. I can't begin my studies at German University and now my life is now ruined 😡. Your last chance to fix this, Fintiba - Ticket 1219288!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Don't bother with Fintiba - they don't have time for old customers, let alone new ones. My ticket 1219288 is still open. Just pick any other provider. Meanwhile BaFin will definitely fine Fintiba or even make it close its business. Fintiba cannot even read things you send them, why would you trust them your money? Avoid at any cost.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "My question about money transfer was not answered for 4 working  days", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I recently migrated from Coracle to Fintiba and was placed into a Fintiba Plus account. However, I am already living in Germany and am fully covered by TK.\n\nI opened a ticket over two weeks ago, attaching my TK insurance card, requesting an immediate downgrade to Fintiba Basic. Fintiba has completely ignored my tickets for over 14 days. Worse, they have now deducted money from my account for the Fintiba Plus health insurance that I do not need, do not want, as I was already enrolled in TK coverage.\n\nThis level of customer service is unacceptable. I expect an immediate response, a retroactive cancellation of the Fintiba Plus insurance, and a full refund of the deducted amount.\n\nIgnored Support Ticket IDs: 1237464, 1247909, 1247939", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Despite repeated inquiries to customer support, I have yet to receive a response. My registered address remains unverified, even though I have repeatedly uploaded the document confirming my registration—I request that you clarify this matter immediately.\nMy account remains inaccessible from my work computer; multiple requests to resolve this technical issue have gone unanswered—I request that you clarify this matter as well.\n\nI am completely at a loss as to why a paid insurance policy from Mavista was issued without any prior notification to me—a policy that entails monthly deductions from my account without my consent.\nWhen I first contacted your team, I was assured that I would not have to pay anything for Mavista insurance, as everything was already included in the comprehensive service package. Moreover, the accompanying documentation contained not a single word regarding any upcoming payments or the fact that €115 would be deducted from my account! I request that you clarify this matter. The documentation provided does not even specify the policy number for this paid insurance coverage. This constitutes a violation of my rights.\n\nI urgently need to cancel this insurance policy. I have already submitted a replacement insurance policy via email to supersede the Mavista coverage, but I have not yet received a response.\n\nI request your assistance in resolving this issue", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I'm really disappointed with Fintiba\n\nI haven’t received my June payout from my blocked account (Today is June 3rd and still nothing) , and unlike previous months, there’s no sign of any processing or transaction at all.\n\nI have an expired Aufenthaltstitel and a valid Fiktionsbescheinigung. I uploaded both, but they were rejected, and I haven’t been told clearly what document I’m supposed to provide instead.\n\nBecause of this delay, I’ve already been charged bank fees due to insufficient funds. I depend on this monthly payout for my basic living expenses, so this situation is really stressful.\n\nI really hope this gets resolved quickly because it’s affecting my daily life.\n\n\nTicket number : 1249985", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Fintiba offers a blocked account for minors and fails to issue a correct confirmation. The minor is as old as the parent?! It takes forever to change a single document!!! We are running out of time. The minor will not get the visa, and it is Fintiba's fault! Never do business with Fintiba! Ticket 1219288", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Worst customer service and no payout!\nI have been trying to contact fintiba through email and obviously they have not responded. I called an agent on the 1st of June, said my payout will be executed. It wasn’t executed so I gave another call on the 2nd of June at 14:27. The operator hung up on me without even responding after 27 minutes of waiting. I had to call again at 14.55, the lady started being extremely aggressive saying that I’m annoying and have no right to call because I opened 4 tickets. The call was recorded by Fintiba as well. My monthly payout has been extremely late now, 4 business days. My DB ticket got cancelled because of this. I have no money left and depend on this money for survival. \n\nTicket numbers:\n1248088\n1247706\n1243858", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I asked for what to do in my particular situation during the blocked account registration process, and after more than a month of waiting and many attempts to re-establish contact, I was simply told: complete the registration process. I am lucky I had *something* to turn to in my last desperations, but the support was unacceptable.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "As usual, payouts are late. We got rent to pay and alot of things! I contact customer support, they ask me to send an email. I send an email, I do not get any reply, the usual way.. I do not know what to say to be honest!!\n\n\n\nUpdate: I did not get a reply from Fintiba's team yet. No one reached out to me.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ticket: 1232490\nI would really appreciate if my request could be taken into consideration. Have been waiting for bussines 10 days for a response.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Fintiba has a horrible customer support. They facilitate everything for you when you want to open the blocked account and transfer the money. But when it comes to payouts, they performed the first pay-out on time, but are delaying subsequent pay-outs! They don’t reply on e-mails and answer the phone after waiting 35 mins. I’m with my kids in Germany and need the payout to pay the rent and they didn’t do the transfer. I don’t recommend their service and will inform the German Embassy in Egypt not to recommend them for coming residents.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "After nearly 4 weeks, the bounced payment can not be redone. When I try to redo the bounced payment after I enter the otp I get the internal server error. \nThe payment for April and May has not yet been transferred to my account. I asked the company many times if this error is something that can not be solved, just transfer the amount to my account manually, but the problem has not been resolved.\n\nTicket numbers: 1243594, 1221690", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I'm a frustrated student.On 5th of May,I sent a request for extension.Since that time I have been following up on emails and calls for my account to be extended so that I can renew my student visa.\n\nThe call center feedback is the same, they don't know what is wrong with their colleagues,emails are unanswered and today?an agent decided not to respond when I asked for escalation procedures.\n\nWho else is experiencing this?", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "UPDATE AFTER 2 MORE WEEKS – STILL NO SOLUTION\n\nI am updating my previous review because nothing has changed.\n\nMy blocked account funds were deposited on January 13, and I have already provided proof that the money arrived successfully. I also submitted my visa documents months ago so that payouts could begin.\n\nOver the last 5 months, my balance has repeatedly disappeared and shown as €0. Every time I contacted support, the issue was temporarily fixed, only to happen again. I was told there was a migration from Sutor Bank to FIB Bank, then after waiting nearly 2 months I was informed that the transfer had failed and the money would be returned. Yet my funds are still not accessible.\n\nI have provided account confirmations showing that €3,462 was credited to my blocked account. Despite this, I still cannot access my money.\n\nI am already in Germany and this situation has caused severe financial hardship. I have struggled to pay for basic living expenses and even had to use my remaining funds for my residence permit extension because my blocked account payouts never started.\n\nTicket: 1232459\n\nFive months without access to my own money is unacceptable. Repeated requests to support have resulted only in the same response: “Please be patient.”\n\nPatience does not pay rent, food, health insurance, or university expenses.\n\nAt this point, I am considering escalating the matter to the relevant financial authorities and seeking legal assistance if this issue is not resolved immediately.\n\nExtremely disappointing experience.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Dear Fintiba Support Team,\nI am writing to express my serious concern regarding the ongoing delay in resolving my support request. For the past 21 days, I have been repeatedly contacting your international support number and submitting support tickets regarding a single issue: correcting the email address associated with my account.\nDespite my continuous efforts, I have not received a clear timeline or a definitive resolution. I have fully cooperated with all verification requests and provided all information requested to prove my identity as the legitimate account holder. In addition, I have uploaded screenshots of the relevant email correspondence as evidence, yet there has been no meaningful update on my case.\nThis delay is now having significant consequences for me. My visa application process is currently on hold because this issue remains unresolved, and my studies are scheduled to begin soon. As an international student from Iran, I have already done everything possible to provide the necessary documentation and respond promptly to all inquiries. The lack of progress is causing considerable stress and jeopardizing my academic plans.\nFor your reference, the support tickets associated with this matter are:\n#1238389\n#1242051\n#1242059\n#1225227\n#1234800\n#1232875\nI respectfully request that this matter be escalated and resolved as a priority. At the very least, I would appreciate a clear update on the status of my case and an estimated timeframe for completion.\nI sincerely hope Fintiba can assist me in resolving this issue as soon as possible, as my visa process and university enrollment depend on it.\nThank you for your attention and prompt assistance.\nKind regards,", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Very disappointed with the service.\n\nMy blocked account was supposed to be closed on May 31, but I still have not received all of my remaining funds.\n\nThe delay is unacceptable, especially as a student who depends on this money.\n\nI expected a faster and more reliable process.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Support team will absolutely lie within their replies to the reviews here telling people that their queries are resolved while they are actually not.\n\nI have been in this fight with the support team for a month now from the 3rd of May, and I have missed my visa appointment due to their ignorance.\n\nI opened my first ticket with the support on the 3rd of May to update my visa documents to a newly issued passport as requested by the embassy, then after ignoring my request for 3 complete weeks, and after extensively fighting back with them, they decided to update only 2 of the 3 visa documents needed, as they only updated the blocking confirmation and the Barmer public health insurance documents, and they completely ignored updating one of the most crucial documents needed by the embassy which is the mandatory travel insurance of Mawista Visum and that made me miss my visa appointment due to incomplete documents, so I opened new tickets on the 21st of May (Tickets 1240069 and 1237236), and till now, they didn't update the document so that I can try and book another visa appointment, and the only thing they have been good at is lying in the replies to the customers' reviews here claiming that the matter or query is resolved, while nothing is resolved in real life with a delay of more than 30 days. Genuinely, a completely useless customer support and service.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Identity verification (WebID) was completed successfully on 25 April 2026. As of today, the application has been pending for six weeks — beyond the maximum processing time stated for even exceptional cases.\nThe timeline:\n— 25 April: video verification completed.\n— 12 May: one human reply, stating the case had been forwarded to the banking partner with a promise of a follow-up.\n— 12 May to today: automated holding messages only. No human response. No status update. No request for any document.\nThe customer portal shows no option to upload anything. No email has arrived asking for additional documentation of any kind. The application simply sits, with no visible path forward and no communication from a person — despite a phone call and a public reply both promising the case was being handled.\nThis is not an isolated case. Other applicants in comparable situations describe the same pattern: weeks of silence after verification, with the real cause never communicated unless the customer initiates contact. For anyone selecting a blocked-account provider on a fixed visa timeline, this is the single most important thing to understand before committing.\nThe account is for a minor and the timing is not flexible. I am ready to provide the Order ID privately so the case can be located immediately. What I am asking is simple: a reply from a person, and a clear answer on what is actually happening.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "My problem still not solven", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Dear Fintiba Customer Support,\nI am writing because I am exhausted from trying to resolve an urgent issue with my blocked account extension, and I am extremely concerned about the time this is taking. My residence permit/visa renewal process depends on this extension, and every day of delay puts my legal status in Germany at serious risk.\nFor more than a week now, I have:\nSent multiple emails\nMade several phone calls\nSubmitted a support ticket (reference number: 1238422)\nDespite all these efforts, I have not received any response or update. The portal continues to show an error and instructs me to contact customer support because of which I am unable to extend my blocked account, but I am stuck in a loop with no resolution.\nThis is not just a routine request; it is a time-sensitive visa renewal matter where missing deadlines can have severe consequences. I urgently need Fintiba’s immediate assistance to:\n- Investigate and fix the portal error preventing my blocked account extension\n- Provide a clear timeline for when this will be resolved\n\nI am at a point of genuine distress and frustration after a week of no response. Please treat this as a high-priority case and get back to me today with a concrete update.\nRegards,\nZibraan Ahmed\nSupport Ticket/Reference Number: 1238422", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "THEY NEVER GAVE ME A SOLUTION TO SUCH A SMALL ,STUPID LITTLE PROBLEM THAT WAS NOT MY FAULT", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Don’t you ever open an account with them, worst support ever.\nI opened my account 1 month before moving to germany and they only verified my data 1 month after I arrive, I tried to call multiple times to access the money because I really needed and they did not help, I had to ask for money from my parents because all I had it was blocked.\nAlso, they did not give me the proper amount, I was aware of the 9,9€ charges every month, but on the second payment they charged me 29,9€ for no reason, they said it was the last charge and there was nothing else booked but then on the 3rd payment they charged me more 9,9€, so they steal money, I called the support again the guy was really rude and said there was nothing he could do and turn off the phone on me. Extremely disrespectful!\nDon’t you ever open an account with them, only problems", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "My last review here got replayed very fast and I am thankful for your consideration. The problem of setting mobile number is fixed, However the original problem of ticket 1221690 is still persisted and I can not redo my bounced payment, and I get Internal server error when I want to redo the payment and input my otp. Still the problem is not fixed and I have asked several times that redo mechnism get done by your team as you can verify the bank information which is under my own name to resolve this issue which took 3 weeks and still not fixed. I send the screenshot replaying to customer care answer from yesterday via Email.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I’ve had such a horrible experience with fintiba. After making my transfer their system just kept a red banner at the top saying that I need to make a deposit. The transfer I sent did reflect on my account balance but they literally couldn’t generate a payment confirmation for me. Their customer care line takes about 1 hour to get someone to pick up and when they so they are very rude— literally dismiss and cut the line saying they can’t help. It’s been going on for two weeks now and I still can’t get a confirmation letter for my visa application whose deadline has passed. It’s so bad and I won’t recommend their services to anyone. Try somewhere else.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "This is my second review. The company's response to my first review on this site is an outright lie.\n\nIt took two months of trying to start receiving payouts to my current account. Unsuccessfully. I tried to close my blocked account then. Their buggy website sent me a confirmation code to my email address and then said that the code was incorrect, however, I received an email saying that the closure procedure had been initiated. I repeated this four times. Instead of closing my account, they issued me a blocking confirmation the next day. Once you have received the blocking confirmation, you can only return your funds if your visa application has been rejected. However, I am already in Germany and need this account to extend my residence permit. So the only way for my money to go is to my German current account, not back to my home country.\n\nIn order to start making payments to a blocked account, you need to upload a visa or residence permit. However, my residence permit has the number of my old passport on it. The Fintiba system requires a new residence permit or a photo of the old passport, and asks you to contact their support team. The support bot is awful. Even if a human answers once a month, it's not much better. \n\nI have already mentioned one rude and unprofessional manager from the compliance department: Lavinia Stan. Here is the name of another incredibly rude and even more incompetent manager: Sahin Koc from the Complaints Management department. I will continue to publicly post the names of these people.\n\nConclusion: AVOID FINTIBA!\n\nTHEY HAVE JUST STOLEN MY MONEY", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The support will not do anything for you.\nAfter 3 weeks of waiting, there is still no answer as to why something this simple could take so long. \nThe problem is just setting a mobile number in my account. I have called many times, making emergency tickets, and no one has answered. Even the company answers Trustpilot faster than their tickets; however, they said that the problem is resolved, but after two days of their reply on this site, I can confirm THAT IS NOT TRUE. There has been no payment since I set up my bank account!!!!\n\nTicket Number: 1221690", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I submitted my blocked account closure request and uploaded all required documents 14 days ago. Since then, I have not received a clear update about the status of my request, what exactly I am waiting for, or how long the process is expected to take.\n\nThe funds are important for me, and the lack of clear communication makes the situation stressful. I would appreciate faster processing and a transparent update about the next steps.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I raised some tickets and didn't get any response after 2 weeks. I will share my experience in social media very soon.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "On the step of registration everything was OK. But in time when I tried to get my money back — everything went wrong. I got a confirmation that my account will be closed and i will get my money in 2 weeks. But since that i still didn't get my money back. It's already 2 weeks delayed and support is not responding on the emails and on the phone. Be aware.\n\nUPD. 29/05/2026 I got my money back.\nBut I still recommend to avoid Fintiba, because of my experience. Support didn't provide any information, just asking to be patient and wait for answer.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "UPDATE — STILL UNRESOLVED. STILL NO ACCESS TO MY OWN MONEY.\n\nAfter my previous review, Fintiba publicly replied with the usual \"a follow-up email has been sent with detailed next steps.\" Sounds professional, right? Here is the reality:\n\nThe \"solution\" was simply linking my phone number to the account. That's it. The actual problem — that I cannot receive the OTP verification code needed to confirm my German bank account and unlock my monthly payouts — is STILL not fixed.\n\nThe OTP code does NOT arrive:\n— not by SMS\n— not by email\n— not in spam\n— not after multiple retries across different days and devices\n\nMeanwhile, every email I send to support gets the same copy-paste template back. No real explanation. No technical investigation. No timeline. No accountability. Just polite words while a student in Germany is left without access to the money she legally deposited with them as part of the visa Sperrkonto requirement.\n\nLet's be honest about what this means in practice:\n\nI am a Bachelor's student in Potsdam. The blocked account exists specifically so that international students can access their guaranteed monthly amount to pay rent, health insurance, food, and university fees. Fintiba KNOWS this. Their entire business model is built on students who legally CANNOT use another provider easily once the visa is issued. And yet, when something breaks on THEIR side, students are left waiting for months while support hides behind templates.\n\nA simple SMS code. That's all I need. A six-digit number. And a multi-million-euro fintech company supposedly specialized in serving international students cannot deliver it after weeks of requests.\n\nThis is not a technical glitch anymore. This is negligence toward customers who have the least power to push back — foreign students, often dealing with visa pressure, language barriers, and financial dependence on exactly this account.\n\nI am escalating this to:\n— BaFin (Bundesanstalt für Finanzdienstleistungsaufsicht)\n— Verbraucherzentrale Brandenburg\n— and I will keep updating this review publicly until the issue is genuinely resolved, not cosmetically patched.\n\nTo other international students reading this BEFORE choosing a Sperrkonto provider: please consider alternatives like Expatrio or a direct Deutsche Bank / Sparkasse blocked account. Once you are locked in with Fintiba and something goes wrong, you will discover very quickly how alone you are.\n\nFintiba — I do not need another templated \"we are sorry for your experience\" reply. I need the OTP system fixed and my monthly payout released. Today's date is on the review. The clock is running.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I've had a blocked account now for approx. 2 years, meaning I extended my blocked account. Now I wanted to re-extend my blocked account for another year. I have sent more emails than I can count, and called them numerous times. Every time, I talk to the same employee with the same demeaning tone and no resolution. It's been 3 weeks since I sent an inquiry for the blocked account re-extension. This is absolutely abhorrent and unacceptable. I have to provide documents for my residence permit renewal as I have to apply, and they have given me 0 assistance with anything and reply with the same corporate reply with no specificity to my inquiry or the same automated email reply to my emails. This is unacceptable. Not to mention the customer service is quite unpleasant and expects you to be 100% okay. I had called and they yelled at me on the phone. \nTill now I have yet to hear ANY updates about my inquiry or anything at all, so all in all, 4 weeks for them to reply or even START.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Initial setup wasn't straight forward but doable. The system is not easy. Their response to support is so delayed and inconsistent. My daughter has been trying to contact them for two weeks for just a renewal of her account. No response. Called the phone service and the guy yelled at her, JUST WAIT.\nSo, if you want a supportive and responsive company, you need to study your options.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "You haven’t responded back to two emails I’ve sent and the service has gotten bad compared to the past three years.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Honestly this is the worst service I've ever had from  financial institution. They do not respond to emails and the customer care are rude. \nSetting up my account for payouts took 2 months. I haven't even received my first payout because they kept pushing it. Upon asking, one customer care on call even laughed it off and said he can't do anything about it. \nPlease don't trust them with your money you will be stranded when you arrive in Germany.\n\nThank you", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "After a whole month of sending the required documents to fulfill my request and creating tickets, they only decided to solve half of the problem, and I am still stuck in the middle and not able to submit my visa documents to the embassy on time with complete ignorance of all of my tickets, 1237236 and 1240069.\n\nA month ago, I requested updating my visa documents from my old passport to my new passport,  and after a whole month of opening support tickets and trying to reach them, they only solved half of the problem and decided to update 2 of the 3 visa documents, as they only updated the blocking confirmation and the Barmer health insurance, but the Mawista Visum Travel Insurance document got ignored and wasn't updated, and it's still showing my old passport number (the update of the 2 of the 3 documents happened in the ticket number 1234963), so I opened new tickets immediately (1237236 and 1240069) to let them know as soon as possible about the ignored outdated document of the Mawista Visum Travel Insurance so that they can just easily update it like the rest of the documents to my new passport, because the travel insurance is very important for the embassy, and till now I have been delayed more than a month in submitting my papers to the embassy just for the sake of these easy updates, and they are just ignoring my requests a week after a week.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "My experience with Fintiba has been extremely disappointing. I transferred funds to my blocked account for my Germany Opportunity Card application more than 10 days ago, and the funds are still not reflected.\n\nMy UK bank has confirmed multiple times that the money was successfully received by Fintiba, yet their customer service has been terrible throughout this process. I have sent several emails, opened multiple tickets (#1240964, #1239492, #1234084), and contacted all their social media pages, but responses have either been delayed, generic, or completely ignored.\n\nFor a company handling such sensitive financial and immigration-related processes, this level of poor communication and lack of urgency is unacceptable. People are dealing with visa timelines, appointments, and major life decisions, yet Fintiba seems to show very little accountability when issues arise.\n\nThis has been stressful, exhausting, and honestly one of the worst customer service experiences I have had with a financial platform.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Opening blocked accounts went more or less smoothly two years ago. Now, however, it is a complete disaster. The site is full of bugs at every step. They discriminate against people of certain nationalities, repeatedly require new documents to prove that your fund are note associated with criminal income.  The compliance separtment, especially a manager called Lavinia Stan, is rude and unprofessional. They do not answer questions. There is no support there at all in reality; of about two dozen emails, not a single one was answered. \nFintiba will cost you money, your German visa and your mental health. Do not open an account with this provider. It is an extremely irresponsible company that you cannot rely on. Their inaction endangered my legal status in Germany.\nI have filed an official complaint with BaFin.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ich warte nun seit über drei Wochen darauf, dass mein Sperrkonto eröffnet wird und es ist immer noch nichts passiert.\n\nAber ganz ehrlich Für mich ist es absolut unverständlich und inakzeptabel, dass sich über so einen langen Zeitraum rein gar nichts bewegt.\nMan fühlt sich völlig im Stich gelassen keine Lösung, keine klaren Informationen, nur ständige Verzögerungen. Für ein so wichtiges Konto, das man als internationaler Student dringend benötigt, ist dieser Service meiner Meinung nach einfach unmöglich und unprofessionell.\nIch bin extrem enttäuscht und würde Fintiba nach dieser Erfahrung auf keinen Fall weiterempfehlen.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am an international student who arrived in Munich on May 22nd. My Fintiba account was opened with my old passport. When I received my visa on my new passport, I uploaded the new passport photo on May 14th as instructed. Since then I have received nothing but automated replies across four separate support tickets (1229054, 1232812, 1233837, 1240140) over two weeks. Phone calls go unanswered. I am now physically in Germany with no access to my €12,063 blocked account, money I need for rent, food, and daily expenses. This is not a minor inconvenience. This is a student stranded without access to their own funds after completing every step Fintiba asked of me. I need a human being to contact me and resolve this passport mismatch immediately.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I opened a Fintiba blocked account in February 2026 for my studies in Germany. The account opening went smoothly - funds transferred successfully and the account was activated. However, from March through May, serious technical issues completely blocked my access to my own money.\n \nCRITICAL PROBLEMS:\n \n1. OTP CODES NEVER ARRIVE (Neither SMS nor Email)\nSince March, I have not received ANY verification codes - neither by SMS nor email. I cannot complete the payout setup without these codes. I have:\n- Checked spam folders multiple times\n- Reconnected my phone number multiple times  \n- Followed EVERY instruction from support\n- Uploaded all required documents\n- Completed video legitimation successfully\nResult: ZERO codes received in 3 months.\n \n2. PHONE FUNCTION INTENTIONALLY DELETED - BUT NO ALTERNATIVE PROVIDED\nIn April, the phone connection function disappeared from my dashboard. When I called support, the employee ADMITTED they INTENTIONALLY removed it so \"the code would go to email instead.\"\nProblem: The code doesn't arrive on email either. The phone function was never restored. I'm trapped with ZERO ways to receive any code.\n \n3. VISA DATE NOT UPDATED\nI provided documentation of my visa appointment date change (May 28 to May 5). The app still shows May 28 - nearly a month later. System not updating despite uploaded documents.\n \nFINANCIAL CRISIS:\n- My personal savings are almost depleted\n- I struggle to pay rent and basic living expenses\n- I have significant funds in Fintiba but CANNOT access them\n- I've warned my landlord I may not pay rent on time\n- I don't know how to pay next month's expenses\n \nThis is not inconvenience - I came to study in Germany but cannot pay for basic necessities because this company won't provide access to my own money.\n \nSUPPORT RESPONSE - COMPLETELY UNPROFESSIONAL:\nI've sent 20+ emails and made 10+ phone calls over 3 months. Every response is the same template: \"IT will fix in 1-2 days\" or \"Your case is in priority.\" Nothing changes. Support never:\n- Checked account logs\n- Gave technical explanations\n- Provided realistic timelines\n- Offered interim solutions\n \nTHIS IS NOT A TECHNICAL PROBLEM - THIS IS NEGLIGENCE.\n \nWhen a financial company takes your money, promises monthly payouts, locks you out for 3+ months, cannot send a simple SMS code, deletes account functions, and ignores all contact attempts - this is not a glitch. This is failure to provide promised services.\n \nWARNING TO STUDENTS:\nIf you depend on Fintiba for monthly payouts while studying in Germany - DO NOT use them. They can freeze your access without warning, take your money, and leave you without support for months.\n \nI am filing complaints with BaFin (German Financial Regulator) and Verbraucherzentrale Brandenburg. DO NOT use Fintiba if you have other options.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have been for more than 2 months  in Germany, my account can't be unblocked therefore no access to my own funds due to some technical issue.\nNo support from Fintiba, no details about how or when I will receive my funds or be able to unblock my account.\nNo replies to e-mails, phone support can't do anything.\nI don't know what to do anymore, I have no money to pay rent or food and no support from no one.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "SO UNNÖTIG KOMPLIZIERT… GAR NICHT WEITERZUEMPFEHLEN. Habe bis jetzt 10 mal meine Dokumente hochgeladen, jedes Mal steht da Verification failed… dass man da kämpfen muss, um an sein eigenes Geld zu kommen… unglaublich, einfach ÄRGERLICH", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am absolutely shocked by the unprofessional and lawless behavior of Fintiba GmbH! We were not even able to submit our documents for the visa application. I obtained the official Sperrfreigabe (blocked account release) from the German Consulate confirming this fact and officially requested to close my account. Fintiba confirmed the closure and promised to return my funds within 2 weeks.It has been 31 DAYS since the confirmation, and Fintiba is still illegally withholding my money — 13,412.00 EUR!What makes it even worse is their customer support. They have completely ghosted me. While they at least replied to my husband on day 28 via social media blaming a \"system failure,\" they are totally ignoring my emails and messages. I receive absolutely no updates regarding my own money. This is a deliberate and unlawful retention of customer funds.A criminal complaint for embezzlement (Strafanzeige wegen Unterschlagung) has already been filed with the German Police, along with official reports to the financial regulator BaFin and Verbraucherzentrale. I demand the immediate return of my 13,412.00 EUR to my IBAN (DE37 2023 0800 0504 925191) plus a 1,500 EUR delay compensation for this stressful ordeal. Return my money now! Unfortunately, I cannot attach any supporting photos. However, if Fintiba starts responding to its customers' incoming emails, they will see that I have sent numerous screenshots and demands for my money back.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "We are extremely outraged by the lawless actions of Fintiba GmbH! We officially closed our blocked accounts after a visa refusal, providing the official Sperrfreigabe from the German Consulate. Fintiba promised a full refund within 2 weeks.It has been 31 DAYS since the confirmation, and we still have not received our money! In total, they are unlawfully retaining 26,830.00 EUR (Evgenii Zlobin — 13,418.00 €; Viktoriia Zlobina — 13,412.00 €).After dozens of messages, they ignored my wife entirely, and told me about some \"system failure\" on day 28, demanding a re-application and delaying the payout for another month! This is an illegal withholding of customer funds. They are clearly working with our money in their own interest. We have already filed criminal complaints with the German Police (Strafanzeige wegen Unterschlagung) and official complaints with the financial regulator BaFin and Verbraucherzentrale! We demand an immediate return of our funds along with a delay compensation of 1,500 EUR for each of us. Return our money immediately!\nMein iban DE80 2023 0800 0504 9236 4..", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "1208415 Finger weg von dieser Organisation! Seit fünf Wochen kann ich auf mein Geld nicht zugreifen. Ich habe E-Mails geschrieben, telefonisch gehen sie nicht ran. Am Apparat wurde mir gesagt, es sei einfach ein technisches Problem, aber ein technisches Problem dauert keine fünf Wochen! Das ist meine Lebenssicherung in Deutschland, wie soll man überleben? Keiner kümmert sich drum. Zum Glück habe ich eine Rechtsanwaltversicherung und am Mittwoch habe ich einen Termin, der Fall wird anscheinend vor Gericht gehen.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Unverschämt! Eine meiner Freundinnen, wie auch andere Nutzer, wie ich sehe, kann ihr eigenes Geld von diesem Unternehmen nicht ausgezahlt bekommen. Sie antworten nicht auf E-Mails, telefonisch sind sie nicht erreichbar. Den Kundenservice konnten wir nur einmal erreichen, und die „nette“ Dame hat aufgelegt, nachdem wir das Problem geschildert hatten. Sie meinten, dass es ein technisches Problem sei, aber ein technisches Problem dauert nicht 4-5 Wochen! Zum Glück ist sie nicht allein, und mein Mann ist ein Rechtsanwalt, und wir kümmern uns schon um diese Situation. Schwer sich vorzustellen, was andere in diesem Fall ohne Unterstützung machen müssen. Wir werden diese Situation so bekannt machen, wie es möglich ist, damit andere Leute nicht darauf hereinfallen!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Horrible customer service. Unfriendly call agents and no reply to emails", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "they are the worst company to open a block account", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "​I have been trying to link my bank account to my Fintiba blocked account for 14 days now (ticket 1228493). The system has a technical error and does not send the OTP code.\n​I already posted a review on this platform previously, and your response was an email instructing me to contact the chatbot. When I did, the bot simply told me to reach out to customer support. I sent an email to support 14 days ago and have received absolutely no reply.\n​I am now calling your support line every single day, and the only answer I get is: \"Your case has been forwarded to the tech department, you have to wait and be patient.\"\n​Until when? How much longer am I supposed to wait?\n​My financial resources are completely exhausted, and I urgently need access to my own money to pay my rent and basic living expenses. It is absolutely irresponsible to leave someone without their funds for weeks due to a system bug, only to pass them back and forth between a bot and unresponsive support.\n​I do not need another automated reply or to be told to wait. I expect an immediate, manual authorization and a real solution today!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "In meinem Leben hatte ich noch nie so schlechte Erfahrungen wie mit diesem Dienstleister.\n\n(Ticket IDs: 1233970, 1229898, 1237827)\n\nEin Bekannter hat einen Blocked Account bei der Fintiba eröffnet. Wir warten nun schon seit 2 Wochen, dass dieser endlich freigegeben wird. Alle Gebühren für den Account wurden natürlich schon abgebucht und einbehalten (das geht technisch offensichtlich noch einwandfrei…). Alles stimmt mit dem Account, mehrfach bestätigt durch den telefonischen Fintiba-Support. Wir haben den Fintiba-Support schon mehrfach per E-Mail kontaktiert und den telefonischen Support mittlerweile fast täglich angerufen (eure generische Antwort mit „kontaktiert den Support“ könnt ihr euch also sparen - ist mittlerweile mehrfach geschehen.)\n\nEs bewegt sich nichts. Die Support-Mitarbeiter:innen dieses Unternehmens reichten bisher von komplett ahnungslos zu regelrecht frech und respektlos. Ständig wird man vertröstet. Es gibt irgendwelche internen IT-Probleme laut eigener Aussage aller Mitarbeiter bisher, das Problem sei schon lange bekannt. Alle sagen einem sie können nichts tun. Man muss warten. Wie lange denn noch? Wenn ich die Google Reviews anschaue, existiert das Problem schon seit mehreren Monaten, ohne dass es gelöst wird. Wie unfähig kann man sein? Ihr spielt und zerstört hier die Existenzgrundlage hunderter Menschen.\n\nDas Visum meines Bekannten läuft jetzt bald aus und weil ihr euch nicht um eure internen Probleme kümmert und seinen Fall sowie den zahlreicher weiterer einfach ignoriert und nicht bearbeitet (was laut eurer eigenen Angabe innerhalb von 1 Werktag geschehen soll), kann er keinen neuen Visumsantrag stellen und wird wegen euch am Ende des Landes verwiesen.\n\nHeute wieder den Kundensupport kontaktiert und mit Abstand mit dem respektlosesten Mitarbeiter bisher gesprochen. Seine Name ist Alex. Er hat mich mehrfach unterbrochen, zurechtgewiesen, als ich ihm mein letztes Gespräch mit dem Support geschildert habe behauptet ich würde die Unwahrheit erzählen, mich am Ende noch mansplained und dann ohne ein Grußwort aufgelegt. Seine Stimme war klar aggressiv. Wenn der Fintiba Support so mit allen Personen weiblichen Geschlechts redet, kann ich allen Frauen nur raten diesen Dienstleister tunlichst zu meiden.\nDas Beste war, dass er mich nicht mal nach der Fall-ID oder sonstigen Daten gefragt hat bis ich selbst angemerkt habe, ob er sich wenigstens den Fall anschauen kann bevor er mit mir spricht als wäre ich der letzte Mensch. D.h. er wusste nicht mal worum es geht. Absolut inakzeptabel, inkompetent und unerhört ein solches Verhalten mit Kunden gleich auf mehreren Ebenen, im Kundensupport als auch der Lösung des Problems.\n\nIch kann nur jedem raten diesen Dienstleister nie in Anspruch zu nehmen. Fintiba ist an Verantwortungslosigkeit kaum zu überbieten.\n\nWir und so viele andere warten, ohne Zeit dafür zu haben.\n\nAn @Fintiba Kümmert euch endlich um unser Kudenanliegen und löst das Problem mit unserem Account!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "​Terrible support! Auto-system rejected my official Fiktionsbescheinigung 3 times. Sent emails, called the hotline, nobody helps. 3-day holiday weekend is starting now in Germany and my rent is due. I am here with my children, my account is frozen and we have no money for rent and food. Please verify my Fiktionsbescheinigung manually today and release my payout! ID: 291-431-126", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I deposited my money on January 13 and uploaded my visa documents so that the payouts could start. Since then, my balance has shown as 0 multiple times. Every time I contacted support, they temporarily fixed it.\n\nAt one point, I was informed that there was a migration happening from Sutor Bank to FIB Bank. I waited almost 2 months for the transfer process, and later I was told that the transfer did not work and that my money would be returned from Sutor Bank. After that, my balance again showed 0.\n\nI am already in Germany and I am facing serious financial difficulties because I still cannot access my money. I even had to spend the remaining money I had for my visa extension because Fintiba is not paying out my blocked account funds.\n\nThis issue has been going on for 5 months. I have contacted support countless times, but nothing gets solved. My ticket number is 1232459. Support only tells me to “be patient,” but institutions and deadlines are not patient.\n\nBecause of Fintiba’s failure to handle this properly, I am facing serious problems in my academic career and daily life in Germany. Extremely disappointing experience.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Very slow customer support i mailed them one week ago and still didn't receive their response..", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Schlechte Kundenservice", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am very disappointed with Fintiba’s support and verification process.\n\nI already submitted all required visa and verification documents more than two weeks ago. I called support multiple times and was only told to “wait” because there are many cases.\n\nI am already living in Germany and depend on these funds to pay rent, buy food, and cover basic student expenses, yet there is no clear timeline and almost no communication.\n\nVery stressful experience for international students.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "​I have been trying to link my bank account to my Fintiba blocked account for 10 days now (ticket 1228493) . The system has a technical error and does not send the OTP code. Instead of fixing the bug or manually authorizing my account, the customer support just tells me to \"wait\" every single day.\n​My financial resources are completely exhausted, and I urgently need access to my own money to pay my rent and living expenses. It is absolutely irresponsible to leave someone without their funds for over a week due to a system bug. I expect an immediate solution!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Support is very bad , I need asap blocking confirmation document and I contacted support a week ago , honestly very very bad", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Worst! I have opened a block account in February to extend my visa in Germany.I have tried to reach them every way possible to get monthly payout but they are not answering emails or not picking up my calls. My data is still under review. 😆", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Alles dauert lange", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "--Update To Reply to Fintiba's Response--\n\nI appreciate your trial in assisting in the ticket of 1234963, however, regarding the same ticket number, unfortunately, the matter isn't still fully resolved, some of the documents got updated and some still hold the old passport information (Precisely, the Mawista Visum travel insurance document was left without being updated and still displays the old passport with the outdated information), so now some documents are with new passport details, and some still hold the old passport details, so if you can fix this mistake as well and adjust the overlooked document of the Mawista Visum Travel Insurance as soon as possible so that all the documents are consistent and full before handing them in to the embassy.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------\n\nDon't ever consider opening your account with Fintiba at all costs as you will never get any support when you urgently need it (Ticket 1217908, and ticket 1234963). Your requests will be ignored for a month without any response and no actual actions to address your problem, and you will be treated with utmost ignorance and they won't care if it would result in severe delays to your visa application, so just search for another provider. \n\nI have opened my account with them a year ago, then my admission got deferred to this year, and consequently, I have been issued a new passport and I have reached the point of almost begging them for a month now (the first ticket was opened on the 5th of May) through customer support tickets (Ticket 1217908, and ticket 1234963) and also through phone calls to just update my passport details and issue new visa documents with the new passport in order not to miss my visa appointment, and all my requests have been ignored for almost a month now and the documents are still missing, and I have been delaying my visa appointments one after another due to the missing documents and the ignorance of their customer support when dealing with their clients' urgent requests.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I've been contacting Fintiba \nsince 11th may \nbefore I opened my account and it was at verification process then when I got my admission offer letter it's 9 days im trying to get the access to my account but they're not cooperating \nkindly check the tickets I'm providing \nalso I just asked them to update my email address \nin terms of having the account again \nI send them my picture holding passport and hand written text even for my email changing \nI sent them the address Registeration data also \ntickets : #1234800 #1225227 #1232875", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Can't setup Sperrkonto payout for more than a month.\nWas urged to do a bank partner migration, and after some time they told that migration is cancelled.\nMy email asking them about timeline for resolving this issue is not answered after almost a week.\nAnd in the phone call today they only said that there is a technical issue, long queue and all I can do is to wait.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Worst financial platform that I ever had to dealt with. The support mechanism is very unclear, a simple ticket is still in progress from 2 weeks and no one is answering clearly and tell just to wait without noticing that the majority of their customers are students living in a new country and need this is their only financial source.\n\n[UPDATE] - On May 26th the company reply that the problem has been resolved, which is a false information but there is no place to replay to that review, and still the problem is not resoved to the date 26-05-2026-15:03 GMT+2 !!!!!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "This has been the most unpleasant experience I have ever had. Securing my Master's admission in Germany as an international student was already an incredibly difficult journey, and Fintiba has only made the process significantly harder and more stressful. I sent my money a week ago, it has officially exited my country, and there is still absolutely no reflection of it on my blocked account dashboard. Worse, I have sent multiple emails to the Fintiba support team over the past few days providing my SWIFT documents, and no one is willing to at least talk to me or assure me that my funds are safe. The complete lack of human communication and support during such a massive financial transfer is unacceptable.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The service is so so bad in this bank", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "One of the worst experiences I’ve had as an international student moving to Germany.\n\nI trusted Fintiba with my blocked account and insurance during one of the most important transitions of my life, but almost every step has been stressful and disappointing.\n\nIt has now been over 2 months, and I still have not properly received access to my own money. On top of that, the customer support experience has been extremely poor:\n\n* Tickets take weeks or sometimes even a month to get responses\n* Calls involve waiting 30–60 minutes with little to no useful information\n* No proper timelines, updates, or accountability are provided\n\nWhat makes this worse is that international students depend on these funds for basic survival — rent, groceries, transportation, and settling into a completely new country. Delays like this create enormous mental stress and uncertainty.\n\nI understand that issues can happen in any company, but the lack of communication, urgency, and support has made this experience genuinely traumatic for me.\n\nI hope Fintiba improves its customer support and operational processes instead of focusing only on expansion and marketing.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am extremely disappointed with the service of Fintiba. My support ticket (#1221276) has been delayed for far too long and I am still not receiving proper answers from the support team.\n\nI was clearly informed that the process would take around 3 to 4 weeks, but that time has already passed and my issue is still unresolved. Despite multiple follow-ups, I continue receiving only generic replies asking me to wait without any clear explanation or actual progress.\n\nI urgently need my money, and these continuous delays are seriously affecting my plans and causing unnecessary stress. I have already submitted all required information and fully cooperated throughout the process.\n\nI request Fintiba to finally take my case seriously, provide a proper update regarding ticket #1221276, and release my funds as soon as possible. Better communication and timely support are expected from a company handling students’ blocked account", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "1,5 aydır bloke hesaptaki paramı almaya çalışıyorum sürekli mail attım ama sadece beklemem gerektiğinin söylenildiği bir cevap maili alıyorum defalarca yazmama rağmen neden hala bir çözüm bulunamadı ne yapmam gerekiyor lütfen yetkili birisi yardımcı olabilir mi?", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Did not answer my emails", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Such a waste of time and money. I can't enter my IBAN to reach out to my funds due to technical issue and their customer support is not helping I can't receive my funds for at least 20 days. definitely not reliable at all.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ich bin extrem enttäuscht vom Service von Fintiba.\n​Vor etwa zwei Monaten habe ich sowohl das Geld als auch die erforderlichen Unterlagen nach Deutschland geschickt, aber bis heute habe ich keine Sperrkonto-Bescheinigung erhalten. Ich habe mehrfach geschrieben und darauf hingewiesen, dass mein Studienbeginn kurz bevorsteht – was Ihnen bereits bekannt war. Die Antwort darauf war lediglich, dass dies nicht Ihr Problem sei, gefolgt von einem „Schade“.\n​Daraufhin habe ich die Rückzahlung meiner Mittel gefordert, aber meine E-Mails blieben unbeantwortet, und sogar die Anrufe meiner Schwester aus Europa wurden teilweise ignoriert. Dann verlangten Sie einen Ablehnungsbescheid der Visastelle für die Auszahlung. Das ist jedoch unmöglich: Wegen Ihrer Verzögerung ist meine Zulassung abgelaufen, ich habe meinen Studienstart verpasst und konnte mangels Sperrkonto-Bescheinigung gar nicht erst zum Visumstermin gehen. Ihre Reaktion? „Das betrifft uns nicht.“\n​Heute stehe ich ohne Geld und ohne Nachweis da. Zwei Monate völlig umsonst. Vielen Dank an Fintiba – das war die schlimmste Erfahrung meines Lebens. Meinen Start in Deutschland wegen Ihres Verschuldens verpasst zu haben, ist inakzeptabel. \nIch bin noch hier in Kamerun und könnte wirklich nicht meine Komilitonen Fintiba empfehleen\nVerbesserungsvorschläge für Fintiba:\n​Erreichbarkeit: E-Mails müssen beantwortet und Telefonate von Angehörigen nicht ignoriert werden.\n​Höflichkeit: Respektloser Kundenservice und zynische Antworten (wie „Schade“) sind absolut unprofessionell.\n​Schnelligkeit: Eine Bearbeitungszeit von 2 Monaten zerstört Zukunftspläne. Die Prozesse für die Sperrkonto-Bescheinigung müssen drastisch beschleunigt werden.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am extremely disappointed and stressed with Fintiba's service. My blocked account contains my essential funds for my living expenses in Germany, yet I have been unable to access them since my arrival in Germany on March 25th (nearly 2 months).\n\nAll my official visa and permanent address requirements have been submitted and verified. My health insurance Barmer has also been officially activated as of 01.04.2026. Despite fulfilling all my obligations, Fintiba refuses to release my \"Setup Payout\" option due to their system delays.\n\nTo make matters worse, customer support is completely non-existent. I opened a ticket on May 5th, and all I receive are automated copy-paste replies with smiling emojis asking for \"more time\" (Ticket ID: 1218112). Meanwhile, I am a student in Germany left with no access to my money for basic living expenses because Fintiba is withholding my funds.\n\nThis is completely unacceptable and irresponsible for a financial institution. I demand that a human support agent looks into Ticket 1218112 immediately and unlocks my payout setup.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Extremely disappointing experience with Fintiba — this has now been ongoing since March.\n\nI opened my account and verified my passport in the app at the beginning. After that, I was asked to complete additional steps including PostIdent and sending signed legitimation documents by post, which I did in full.\n\nDespite that, the process never progressed.\n\nI was later informed that a passport copy was missing, even though:\n\n- my passport was already verified in the app at account creation, and\n- a copy of my passport was included in the legitimation documents they themselves provided.\n\nTo avoid further delays, I sent the requested passport copy by email immediately — not once, but twice.\n\nStill, nothing was resolved.\n\nSince March, I have been stuck in a cycle of repeated delays, conflicting document requests, and zero real progress. Every time I contact support, I wait 20+ minutes on the hotline only to reach agents who have no visibility into the verification process. They cannot provide updates, cannot transfer me to the responsible department, and repeatedly tell me only to “wait” or that a “high priority ticket” has been created.\n\nWeeks pass after each call with no change.\n\nIn some cases, support interactions have also been unhelpful and dismissive, despite the seriousness of the situation. There is no clear escalation path and no meaningful communication from the verification team.\n\nAs a result of these delays, I've been facing serious financial consequences, including difficulties paying rent and bills, as the blocked account funds are not accessible.\n\nThis level of delay and lack of accountability over several months is unacceptable, especially for a service that is critical for international students relying on timely access to their funds in Germany.\n\nI strongly recommend extreme caution when relying on this service for anything time-sensitive or essential.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "AVOID THIS COMPANY AT ALL COSTS! Opening an account and blocking your money takes them only 2 days, but getting your own money back takes more than 2 months!\n\nI have been waiting for over a month just to get a single reply to my emails, but they completely ignore me. Absolutely zero human response! Everything is handled by useless bots that send generic, automated templates. Weeks are passing by, and I am completely unable to close my account and withdraw my funds after my visa rejection.\n\nThis is by far the worst customer service I have ever experienced. They trap your money and then vanish when you need a refund. Do not trust them with your money!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Fintiba took 12,000 euros from me and opened a blocked account. i am no longer moving to germany and they havent given me my money back. theyve sent me dozens of emails that say \"please give us more time\". its been just over 3 months. 12,000 euros have just vanished.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "ZERO stars if I could. Absolutely disgraceful service.\n\nI am an international student in Germany relying on my Fintiba blocked account (Sperrkonto) for my monthly living expenses. My May disbursement has NOT been transferred as of May 18th — I am halfway through the month with no money.\n\nI have sent multiple emails. I have called multiple times. I have heard NOTHING back. Complete silence. No response, no explanation, no solution.\n\nThis is not just bad customer service — this is a serious financial harm to a student who depends on this money for rent and food. Fintiba is trusted by thousands of international students across Germany, and this is how they treat us?\n\nI will be filing a formal complaint with BaFin (German Financial Supervisory Authority) and reporting this case to relevant student support organizations.\n\nDo NOT trust this company with your Sperrkonto. When you need them most, they disappear. Shameful.\nUpdate:::\nThey have responded to me that my problem has been resolved and I wanna say \"No \" you laiers noooo it has been not resolved and no one contacted me ever ..\nDon't trust them guys....", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Website with a lot of problems", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Decent service at the start, pretty straight forward.\nBut I’m having an issue where my account is now verified and I came in Germany in February with a British passport meaning I didn’t need a visa to enter.\nWhen I’m being told to input my arrival date in Germany it doesn’t accept it as it’s in the past.\nI sent multiple emails to no avail.\nI’d like you to review my case as I’ve sent all the relevant documents and I’d like to start received payments.\nWhoever handles customer service needs to completely reconsider their attitude and realize that students completely rely on their services.\nCompletely false advertising regarding maximum 24 hours till a response, honestly it’s a surprise someone has not opened a legal case against this due to false advertising.\nOverall, simple process to setup.\nOverall fast to reflect on their side. \nOnly issue is customer service and their system not being developed enough in regard to countries that don’t require visa’s to enter Germany.\n\nSupport Code: 037-861-490", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I provided my IBAN for the payout on Fintiba\n, but the verification code they claimed would be sent to my phone number or email never arrived. I tried multiple times and received nothing.\n\nI contacted support by email and got no response. Their chatbot was completely unhelpful and only directed me to customer service. I then called customer service and waited for over 30 minutes listening to music without ever reaching an agent.\n\nExtremely frustrating experience, especially when the issue appears to be with their own verification system.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have try to contact multiple times to change my start date, I have multiple times tried help but it doesn't work", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Very extremely poor customer service, so annoying, been writing an email for almost a week now for an urgent issue but no reply yet despite stating on the website the maximum response time is 24 hours", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Seit mehr als 5 Wochen versuche ich, auf mein Geld bei Fintiba⁠ zuzugreifen. Ich habe unzählige E-Mails geschrieben und mehrmals angerufen, aber mir wurde immer nur gesagt: „Bitte warten Sie, das Problem wird gelöst.“ Trotzdem kümmert sich niemand wirklich um mein Problem. Ich wünschte, ich hätte niemals ein Sperrkonto bei Fintiba eröffnet. Falls mein Problem nicht schnellstmöglich gelöst wird, werde ich mit meinem Anwalt sprechen und die Angelegenheit vor Gericht bringen.(Mein Ticket:1222225) Update: It's been over 7 weeks since I tried to access my money and I feel so overwhelmed because of Fintiba. I don't know what to do. If they don't give my money, I'll have to take a legal action. I regret opening Fintiba blocked account so much.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "No one has responded to my email. I have been waiting for almost a week.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "No one has responded to my email. I have been waiting for a week.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I sent an email weeks ago regarding my blocked account and haven't received a response. My issue is urgent and I needed assistance as soon as possible, but I was completely left in the dark with no updates what so ever. The customer service is terrible.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have asked some question on this week Monday morning still no reply. How many business days are gone lol\nYour service is disguisting and you only care about profit.  You take your own sweet time for weeks when we are in hurry. Not having enough people to answer enquries so you can profit well. No customer service at all", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have emailed them sevreral times but they are not responding. I am facing issues with health insurance", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "At first everything went well until I absolutely had to change my IBAN. Couldn’t do it for days, support left my messages unanswered. I managed to do it finally and now it’s been over a week and the money hasn’t even been sent out. The support said it has to be done manually and they can’t give me any timeline. \nThe payment is supposed to be for May and it’s the middle of May. I’m a student and I rely on the money I have on the blocked account heavily. I don’t have access to it, don’t have an answer to when it will be sent. Contacting support has given 0 results. \n\nIt’s seriously affecting my life, my mental health, I can’t pay my rent for this month without the transfer being completed. \nThis is unacceptable, I’m relying on this money for basic living expenses.\n\nSupport code:\n484-920-124\nPlease send the monthly amount as soon as possible.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ich habe für mein Sprachvisum in Deutschland ein Sperrkonto bei Fintiba eröffnet. Nachdem ich nach Deutschland gekommen bin und mein Visum im System hochgeladen habe, erlebte ich einen großen Schock: Statt der auf meinen offiziellen Visadokumenten angegebenen Daten wurde der Zahlungsbeginn plötzlich auf August 2029 gesetzt. Das ist vollkommen falsch und inakzeptabel.\n\nTrotz unzähliger Anrufe und Kontaktversuche über einen Zeitraum von zwei Monaten hat niemand mein Problem gelöst oder Verantwortung übernommen. Der Kundenservice reagiert entweder gar nicht oder vertröstet ständig ohne konkrete Lösung.\n\nEin solcher Fehler kann für internationale Studenten und Sprachschüler schwerwiegende finanzielle und rechtliche Folgen haben. Ich fordere Fintiba hiermit auf, dieses Problem unverzüglich zu korrigieren und endlich eine ernsthafte Lösung anzubieten.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Very disappointing experience with Fintiba.\n\nI extended my blocked account from 6 months to 5 months, but the extension document was never updated correctly and still showed the amount for 6 months. Because of this issue\n\nCustomer support informed me that there was a technical issue and that I would receive a refund. They told me that I would receive my money at the beginning of next week, but I still do not have any exact date or clear information.\n\nEvery time I call support, I am told to wait and that they do not know exactly when I will receive my money.\n\nWhat is even more confusing is that my account maintenance fees (€4.90) were deducted three times, including twice within the same week, even though these fees are usually deducted only once per month when I receive my payout — but I did not receive anything.\n\nI am an international student in Germany and currently I have almost no money left because my funds are blocked. I urgently need this money for accommodation, insurance, food, and daily expenses. Because I could not pay my bills on time, I also received several penalties and late fees.\n\nThis situation has caused me serious stress and financial difficulties.\n\nVery poor communication, no clear answers, and no real solution provided. I do not recommend using Fintiba.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "They consistently fail to respond to emails. For the past two months, I have been requesting the cancellation of my health insurance—sending repeated emails and receiving only automated replies, with no direct communication or updates. Meanwhile, they continue to withdraw monthly payments from my bank account without delay or issue. To this day, I am still waiting for the cancellation to be processed.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Trapped in Fintiba’s “source of funds” verification nightmare. This isn’t anti-money laundering - it’s systematic financial harassment.\n\nHow It Works:\n\t1.\tSubmit documents they request\n\t2.\tWait days\n\t3.\tGet rejection: “We need additional documents”\n\t4.\tSubmit more documents\n\t5.\tRepeat until you run out of money or give up\n\nThe Trap:\n\nYour money is locked in their system. Closing the account means SWIFT transfer back to “high risk” countries with 20-50% bank fees. They know you’re trapped. They exploit it.\n\nLiving on €1000/month while searching for work, I’m supposed to gamble my entire budget on maybe satisfying their next unknown requirement.\n\nWhat Others Should Know:\n\nRussia/Kazakhstan/CIS banking = enhanced scrutiny. Every transaction in your statements will be questioned. Fintiba will demand explanations for amounts as small as €400. Bank statements showing 6 months? Expect questions about every line.\n\nThis Isn’t Compliance:\n\nReal AML compliance has clear checklists. This is moving goalposts. Document theater. Financial exhaustion as a strategy.\n\nTo Fintiba:\n\nPublish requirements upfront. State clearly: “certified translation required: yes/no” for each document type. Stop pretending you can’t provide a complete list. This is cruelty, not procedure.\n\nAlternative: Expatrio or Coracle. Don’t let Fintiba trap your money.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "We are trying to open / renew the closed account (Sperrkonto), yet we got no response back since two weeks. Not even a confirmation or a waiting time or anything.\n\n The Visa is about to run out, and we cant extend it without this closed account.\n\nI would just go to Expatrio or Sparkasse if I were you.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I chose Fintiba over Expatrio because I had heard that Fintiba provides great customer service, but unfortunately my experience has been the complete opposite.I transferred the required amount to my blocked account and submitted all the requested source of funds documents over a week ago. I still do not understand why it is taking so long just to verify the documents. The lack of communication and delay in processing have been extremely frustrating. What makes this even more disappointing is that my friend and I started our blocked account process at the same time. She chose Expatrio, received her confirmation on the same day she transferred the money, and has already reached Germany because of how quickly they processed her application.Meanwhile, I am still stuck waiting for verification from Fintiba and unable to submit my documents to the embassy to collect my passport. I already have my flight booked for May 24, and this entire situation has become one of the most stressful experiences I have had to deal with.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Very disappointing experience with Fintiba. It took more than one month just to update my passport information, and during that entire time the support team was not helpful at all. Every time I contacted them, the only answer I received was “please wait.”\n\nThe delays were supposedly caused by the migration to another bank, but after waiting for over a month, I suddenly received an email saying that my account would not even be migrated in the end. Meanwhile, I added my IBAN more than a week ago and I still have not received my funds.\nand my Blocked Account still says \"Pending\"\n\nFor international students, access to funds is extremely important, and this level of delay and poor communication creates unnecessary stress. I expected much better service and support.\nSupport code:\n 739-121-911", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Firstly, it was never obviously stated anywhere that after extending my blocked account, I would have to have at least around 6000€ on my account to receive my payout. \n\nSecondly, now that I have the necessary amount on my blocked account, I haven't received my money since 2 weeks... I keep calling and sending emails to solve my problem, but no one responds to my emails, and the calls are barely of any help. Everyone just tells me to be patient, while I have payments due, I have rent to pay, and my housing management would terminate my contract if I didn't have friends to lend me rent money.\n\nToday was the last straw. I called customer service again, and an extremely passive-aggressive man took the call. While the other support agents I have talked to before were at least nice and patient, this man said \"there is no magic button I can press to solve your problem\", and while I was still talking, hung up on me!!! That is simply unacceptable. I don't care even if he had a bad day, no person working in customer service should let it out on customers!!\n\nIt seems like no one in this company understands that students' lives quite literally depend on them. I'm happy to have friends and a partner who pay for my day-to-day life for 2 weeks now, but not everyone has that luxury.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The support department is taking a very long time to respond. I submitted a request to cancel my insurance because I already have insurance with another company, yet I haven't received any response in a week. Your performance was excellent until you changed your banking partner; since then, everything has been significantly delayed.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Leider eine extrem enttäuschende Erfahrung mit Fintiba.\n\nSeit fast 2 Monaten (Seit dem 18.3.2026) warten wir auf die „Blocked Account Confirmation“, obwohl alle erforderlichen Unterlagen bereits vollständig eingereicht wurden. Bis heute (11.5.2026) erhalten wir weder eine klare Antwort noch eine Lösung.\n\nTelefonisch wird uns seit Wochen immer wieder nur gesagt, dass sich alles „in Bearbeitung“ befindet. Per E-Mail erhält man größtenteils nur automatische Antworten ohne konkrete Informationen.\n\nDie deutsche Botschaft fordert dieses Dokument jedoch weiterhin ausdrücklich für das Visumverfahren an. Dadurch ist unser gesamter Prozess inzwischen blockiert und verzögert sich massiv.\n\nBesonders frustrierend ist, dass uns bis heute niemand klar mitteilt:\n\nob noch Unterlagen fehlen,\nwo genau das Problem liegt,\noder wann endlich mit einer Bearbeitung zu rechnen ist.\n\nWir haben mehrfach zusätzliche Dokumente eingereicht, amtliche Übersetzungen organisiert und ständig nachgefragt – trotzdem passiert praktisch nichts.\n\nDurch diese Verzögerungen entstehen uns inzwischen sogar finanzielle Probleme und Schulden. Gebühren für Versicherungen, Reservierungen und weitere verpflichtende Kosten in Deutschland laufen weiter oder verfallen, obwohl der Prozess wegen der fehlenden Bestätigung blockiert ist. Niemand ersetzt einem diese Kosten oder übernimmt Verantwortung dafür.\n\nIm Jahr 2026 sollte ein digitaler Prozess nicht fast zwei Monate dauern, ohne transparente Kommunikation oder konkrete Unterstützung.\n\nWir können internationalen Antragstellern aktuell leider nicht empfehlen, diesen Service für ihr Visumverfahren zu nutzen. Der Support reagiert sehr langsam und hilft bei dringenden Fällen kaum weiter.\n\nSupport-Ticket: 1196998\n\nEntweder benötigen wir endlich die Bestätigung oder wenigstens eine klare Aussage darüber, was überhaupt noch fehlt.\n\n----\nUpdate am 19.05.2026:\n\nFintiba hat inzwischen auf unsere Bewertung geantwortet und erklärt, unser Fall werde „mit Priorität bearbeitet“. Leider hat sich in der Realität weiterhin nichts geändert.\n\nDie „06 - Blocked Account Confirmation“ ist bis heute immer noch nicht im Portal verfügbar. Trotz unzähliger E-Mails, Telefonate und erneut eingereichter Unterlagen bekommen wir weiterhin keine konkrete Lösung und keine klare Aussage.\n\nSeit fast 2 Monaten ist unser Visumprozess dadurch blockiert. Die Botschaft fordert das Dokument weiterhin ausdrücklich an.\n\nBesonders enttäuschend ist, dass man telefonisch immer wieder nur hört, dass sich alles „in Bearbeitung“ befindet, während per E-Mail meistens automatische Antworten kommen.\n\nIm Jahr 2026 sollte ein digitaler Service deutlich transparenter und schneller funktionieren.\n\nSupport-Ticket: 1196998\n\nWir hoffen weiterhin endlich auf:\n\ndie Bereitstellung der Sperrkonto-Bestätigung,\noder wenigstens eine klare Information darüber, was überhaupt noch fehlt.\n\n-----\nUpdate vom 01.06.2026\n\nLeider hat sich unsere Situation trotz zahlreicher Kontaktversuche weiterhin nicht verbessert.\n\nSeit dem 18.03.2026 warten wir auf die Ausstellung der „Blocked Account Confirmation“. Alle angeforderten Unterlagen wurden mehrfach eingereicht, darunter Bankunterlagen, Nachweise zur Herkunft der Gelder, Steuerunterlagen, Identitätsnachweise sowie beglaubigte englische Übersetzungen.\n\nZwischenzeitlich hat Fintiba auf Trustpilot geantwortet und erklärt, unser Fall werde mit Priorität bearbeitet. In unserem Portal ist die benötigte Bestätigung jedoch bis heute nicht verfügbar.\n\nInzwischen hat uns das Bundesamt für Auswärtige Angelegenheiten erneut aufgefordert, einen Nachweis über das Sperrkonto vorzulegen. Die fehlende Bestätigung gefährdet nun unmittelbar unser Visumverfahren.\n\nBesonders enttäuschend ist, dass wir seit Wochen weder eine konkrete Lösung noch eine klare Aussage erhalten, welche Unterlagen angeblich noch fehlen. Telefonisch wird lediglich auf eine laufende Bearbeitung verwiesen.\n\nWir möchten andere internationale Antragsteller darauf hinweisen, dass Verzögerungen in diesem Prozess erhebliche Folgen haben können. Neben dem Risiko für das Visum entstehen zusätzliche Kosten für Versicherungen, Sprachkurse, Reservierungen und andere organisatorische Aufwendungen, die niemand ersetzt.\n\nSupport-Ticket: 1196998\n\nWir hoffen weiterhin auf eine schnelle Lösung, können den bisherigen Service jedoch leider nicht empfehlen.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I emailed you but you haven’t responded yet. I wish your bank had a phone so I could able to call and solve my problem. \nBecause my situation is specific and I really need help. \nI moved in Germany a month ago and it’s written in my visa that I need to open a blocked account actually I got my visa before opening a blocked account.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "My account is stuck. I cannot upload my visa or register my address because the menus are missing from my dashboard. I’ve sent all documents to support (Ticket #1212420, 1174398) over a month ago, but no manual update has been made, no answer at all.\n\nIt is very frustrating to have money blocked with no way to initiate the payout because of a system bug. Please have a technical agent look into my account and enable the necessary steps immediately.\n\nMy big money is holding for 4 months without any support so far.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I had already opened a blocked account with Fintiba and decided to extend it for my visa renewal. I submitted my extension request and transferred the required amount on 16/04. I also uploaded my proof of address.\n\nSince then, I have called customer support 8 times. Every single time, I was told: “by the end of the week” or “by the end of April.” Today, on 07/05, I called again and was suddenly told it may take until the end of May.\n\nMy visa expires on 13/06, and I clearly explained that this situation is urgent because I cannot even book my visa extension appointment without the blocked account confirmation. The employee literally told me that this is “not their problem” and that I could withdraw my money and go somewhere else if I was in a hurry.\n\nI also asked for my position in the waiting queue, but they refused to provide any information.\n\nVery disappointing communication, no transparency, and no sense of urgency despite the serious consequences for international students and visa holders.\n\n\nIch hatte bereits ein Sperrkonto bei  Fintiba und wollte es für meine Visumsverlängerung verlängern. Den Verlängerungsantrag habe ich am 16.04. gestellt und den erforderlichen Betrag überwiesen. Außerdem habe ich meinen Wohnsitznachweis hochgeladen.\n\nSeitdem habe ich den Kundenservice insgesamt 8 Mal angerufen. Jedes Mal wurde mir gesagt: „bis Ende der Woche“ oder „bis Ende April“. Heute, am 07.05., wurde mir plötzlich gesagt, dass es sogar bis Ende Mai dauern könnte.\n\nMein Visum läuft am 13.06. ab, und ich habe mehrfach erklärt, dass die Situation dringend ist, weil ich ohne die Blocked-Account-Bestätigung nicht einmal einen Termin für die Visumsverlängerung buchen kann. Die Mitarbeiterin sagte mir daraufhin, dass das „nicht ihr Problem“ sei und ich mein Geld zurückziehen und zu einem anderen Anbieter gehen könne, wenn ich es eilig habe.\n\nAußerdem wollte ich wissen, an welcher Position ich mich in der Warteliste befinde, aber diese Information wurde mir verweigert.\n\nSehr enttäuschender Kundenservice, keine Transparenz und keinerlei Verständnis für die ernsten Konsequenzen für internationale Studierende und Visuminhaber.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I unfortunately have a blocked account with fintiba, as someone who relies on his block amount for monthly expenses, In 2 occasions Fintiba has failed me, once provided delayed payment and now with no payment this month, and no explanation. When called help line they just said that \"You're payment should have gone through, Its been happening with alot of people and Unfortunately I cant help you\".\nI still havent recieved my payout for this month, Im behind on my rent, down to my last 30 euros, and now I have to look to either borrow money or get loans.\nWhile this justifies a compensation, I simply ask for just my money and payout, but I havent recieved any support just some generic emails \"Just wait a little longer\".'\n\nFor anyone else facing this issue, I have written an email, asking them to fix it in 48 hours, If it doesn't I do plan to complain to BaFin, and any legal actions I can take against this, and I urge you to do the same.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I haven’t received my monthly payment for 8 days, even though I had payments due. Because of Fintiba’s unprofessional customer service, I had to pay extra interest on my overdue payments.\nI have also been trying to contact customer service for the past 4 days. They kept telling me that they couldn’t open a ticket, but on the last day they suddenly told me to wait and that they would open one after all. I don’t understand why they kept giving me conflicting information.\nThe service was awful, and the customer service staff were very rude.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I really hated to write this negative review because they were working very well and very smoothly up until the point when I moved to Germany. Unfortunately, it's been a full month without any response from their support team about getting the monthly payouts. I have contacted support around 5-6 times, yet nothing. Additionally, I have attempted over 10 times to verify my identity with them, and that doesn't seem to show progress either - it's stuck on \"verification pending\", even though I went through the entire process with agents via web cam ten times. I'm guessing there's some kind of a mess that happened with Fintiba and their change of bank over the last 1-2 months, which isn't an excuse for leaving people in another country with no money, ruining the relationships with landlords from the start, giving people bad name for no reason, getting people in debt etc. If the issue isn't fixed asap, I will have to escalate with BaFin like others because this is unacceptable. \nMy ticket(s) are 1215305, 1192264, and I'm sure like 15 other tickets that I submitted. \n\nUpdate 12 days later: they responded here but have not actually resolved my case. I'm unfortunately forced to escalate my case. Guys you're drowning in negative reviews. Please at least come out and make a statement on what is going on with students' money for month. at least give minimal respect to customers.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Very disappointing experience with Fintiba support and blocked account management.\n\nI extended my blocked account for 6 months, then changed it to 5 months, but the total amount was never corrected and still reflects 6 months. Because of this issue, my account payouts have been blocked .\n\nI did not receive my payouts for April and May, while the monthly fees (€5) were still deducted from my account last month and again this month. I contacted support several times by phone, including last Thursday and today, but the problem is still unresolved, I was told that they do not know when I will receive my money, and that my case has already been open for 3 weeks, but nothing has changed. I also do not know how much money I still need to deposit in order to receive my payouts because the extension document still shows the amount for 6 months instead of 5 months.\n\nAs an international student in Germany, I need this money urgently to pay my health insurance and accommodation. This situation has caused me a lot of stress and financial difficulties. Very poor communication and no clear solution provided.\noumeyma soukah", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I dont want to make insurance. Only blocked account. But I did not.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Einfach schlecht.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Just a mess of a company and catastrophic communication from customer service. Fintiba has turned my time in Germany into a living hell, from the dysfunctional app providing conflicting information, to the automated emails being irrelevant and causing unnecessary stress, all the way to the lying customer service who is left by the bosses on the front row with very little information and power to act that they start making up things. Fintiba has delayed payouts and I am left with no money in a foreign country where I have no contacts and ruined much of my time here making it very hard to focus on my studies.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "It was extremely hard to transfer money because Fintiba’s system was not compatible with the Turkish banks. They asked us to send the money in TRY, but it was only possible to send in EUR.\n\nThere was an absurdly high amount of cut, and so, we ended up having to send more money during which we were not able to receive substantial and significant guidance and there were obviously associated costs as well. \n\nIt was us deciding to send money under overwhelming stress because they told us we had to do the transfer within that day. And the email responses in comparison to the time pressure were extremely slow. \n\nOn top of it, they told us that they cannot transfer the surplass to the blocked account, which made us lose even more money.\n\nThey also initially tell you that it takes 5-10 mins to verify your ID, but they keep you waiting for a day or two. And they tell you that you immediately get the documents needed for your visa, but I am still waiting for them.\n\nIt was just very stressful and we lost so much money. I am hoping that there will not be any more problems as I feel like I would have to solve them by myself as well. Just very poor guidance and customer service.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Let us all send our complains to BaFin, and Verbraucherzentrale together. It seems, that won't be solved any other way but legal force.\n\nIt has been 20+ days from my first support mail, yet no progress. Think about it, if I hold ~12k€ per user that long, and use it as an investment in any basic investment tool like index funds; I would have ~200€ per user. I do not say that is what they are doing, I am just telling you what we are losing on time.\n\nWe should not allow that. Please all together send our complaints to BaFin and Verbraucherzentrale.\n\nIf any other legal authorities you know, please write it for us.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Very slow customer service response", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "This is one of the most frustrating services I have dealt with. I have been waiting for months for my payout and still cannot access my own money. The system keeps showing errors when I try to add my IBAN and there is no real solution from support, just repeated delays and vague responses.\n\nRight now I am in a very serious situation as a student in Germany because I cannot even pay my rent or cover basic expenses while my blocked account funds are inaccessible. This money is supposed to support students, but instead it feels completely unavailable and poorly managed.\n\nI strongly warn others: do not rely on this service if you need reliable access to your funds. The stress and financial pressure this has caused is unacceptable.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "If you are a student or worker planning to open a blocked account in Germany, do NOT choose Fintiba. Choose any other provider.\n\nFintiba is completely unreliable. Their communication is extremely poor — they rarely answer emails (I sent one over two weeks ago and still have no reply), and when you call, you are given misleading or inconsistent information. Their English support line is useless; no one ever responds. The only way to reach someone is through the German line.\n\nI have been left stranded for a month without access to my money. As a student who relies entirely on my blocked account, this is unacceptable. My April and May payments were supposed to be transferred, but I only received one payment at the end of April (29.04).\n\nWhat makes this worse is the constant false promises. I was repeatedly told my money would arrive in “2–3 working days,” but it arrived literally at the end of the month. Even today, I was told my may payment would arrive — and it didn’t. This creates false hope and puts you in serious trouble when you have rent, insurance, groceries, or other urgent expenses to pay. You end up telling people your money is “on the way,” only to find out it isn’t.\n\nThis is not just poor service — it directly affects people’s ability to live. If you check online forums like Reddit, you will see many others facing similar problems, often waiting for months without clear solutions.\n\nThey cannot be trusted with your money, especially if you are living abroad and fully dependent on it. I will be going to my university’s Rechtsberatung next Monday to explore possible legal action I can take.\n\nAvoid Fintiba at all costs.\n\nTicket #1217568", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Fintiba customer service is getting worse and worse, unresponsive. Since the beginning of the month, I changed my new IBAN for payouts. I received confirmation in my email. But, on the system, still left unchanged - my old closed bank IBAN. I can't receive my monthly payments. Phone calls and emails arw not being replied.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am extremely disappointed with my experience with Fintiba. I am an international student relying on my blocked account payouts to pay my rent and cover basic living expenses, but my payout was not transferred on time.\n\nI contacted support multiple times through emails and phone calls, explained that this situation is urgent, and that I risk penalties for unpaid rent, yet the issue still has not been resolved . The lack of communication and delay in handling such an important financial matter has caused me a lot of stress and uncertainty.\n\nFor students who depend on these monthly payouts to survive, delays like this are not a small inconvenience  they can seriously affect daily life. I hope the company improves its customer support responsiveness and handles blocked account payout issues with much more urgency in the future.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I was trying to connect the support line but they didn’t answer", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Why is it so hard or even impossible to reach for a human to discuss my problems ? \n\nThey let you talk to an AI and when you ask to talk with a human AI tells you it will take them 1-2 days to answer. \n\nyou send an email, and guess what ? they do not answer.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I opened a blocked account with Fintiba to meet visa requirements for my studies in Germany. The verification process for my source of funds took considerably longer than advertised, with multiple emails going unanswered for weeks. Some inquiries received no response at all.\n\nAfter finally receiving confirmation that all documents were approved—and with my visa already uploaded to the platform—I still do not have access to my own funds. There is no clear explanation for the continued hold, no updated timeline, and no proactive communication.\n\nWhen I contacted support by phone, the representative seemed as uncertain as I was. At one point, after I asked a follow-up question that was related but distinct from an earlier one, the agent raised their voice, assuming I was repeating myself. This interaction left me feeling dismissed rather than supported.\n\nThe practical impact is severe: I am currently in Germany with limited cash reserves, unable to budget or plan because my blocked funds remain inaccessible. This uncertainty is affecting my basic quality of life.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Sprichst nicht turkisch hilfe", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Hello, I have a problem and the compliance team answers me once per 2 weeks, but it is urgent. When I opened my blocked account in February, I was not required to provide any proofs of the origin of the money and everything went smoothly. However, now they ask me to provide sworn translation of 10!! documents. I do not have these documents with me as I’m already in Germany + I cannot afford to translate them. I need the money from my blocked account to be able to live in Germany. Why didn’t they ask me for these documents in the very beginning??? What should I do??\n\nCould you please tell me when and how I will receive my money back?", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ich bin von Fintiba sehr enttäuscht, ich bin seit 4 Woche in  Deutschland, und habe leider immer keinen Zugriff auf meinem Konto, ich habe seit 14 Tage Email an Support geschrieben, leider habt bisher keine Reaktion, ich habe 4 Mal angerufen, jeder Support Mittarbeiter sagt dass allles okay ist und dass Ticket geschriben wurde um die Auszahlung(monthly payout) freizugeben, leider kann ich immer kein IBAN eingeben. Albano Kamdem", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ich habe beim Eröffnen eines Sperrkontos in Ihrer App Probleme gehabt. Seit etwa einer Woche versuche ich, über E-Mail Kontakt aufzunehmen und den Vorgang zu klären, aber leider habe ich bisher keine Antwort erhalten. \n\nDurch diese Verzögerung bin ich inzwischen in finanzielle Schwierigkeiten geraten und habe Probleme, meinen Lebensunterhalt zu bestreiten. Ich bitte Sie dringend um eine schnelle Rückmeldung und Unterstützung.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Horrible Experience!\nProblems trying to connect my Deutsche Bank account to my Blocked Account, Problems to get my Health Insurance active and Horrible experience with Fintiba's phone attendant (I think his name is Alex - or something like that).\nHorrible experience overall", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "If you are considering opening a blocked account, please reconsider.\nDo not be misled by their positive ratings. In my experience, they appear to take advantage of German defamation laws to remove negative reviews. My previous review on Google was not published under defamation law, which is why I am writing this review again, even though I wrote the previous review with my account registered at Fintiba.\nAt first, the process seems efficient and straightforward: you transfer the required funds, receive confirmation, and everything appears to be in order. Since I already live in Germany and only needed the blocked account to renew my residence permit, I expected the process to be simple.\nI received my new residence permit almost two months ago. To release my funds, Fintiba required a legitimation document from either my bank or Barmer. My bank sent the requested document before the Easter holidays, and Fintiba confirmed receipt of it on 07.04.2026. They then informed me that my passport and address page was missing. I submitted the missing passport page along with my residence permit (Aufenthaltstitel) on the very same day.\nSince then, I have not received a single response from the company.\nIt has now been over three weeks without any communication. Their automated responses claim that inquiries are typically answered within one working day, but this is simply not true.\nWhenever I call their customer support hotline, I receive conflicting explanations. One representative told me that my funds are deposited with FIB Bank and that there is no way to contact them directly. Another representative contradicted this entirely, stating that this information was false and that the company is facing internal issues instead.\nAt this point, I genuinely do not know whom to believe.\nWhen I asked how much longer it would take before I could finally start receiving my monthly payouts, after already waiting for nearly two months, I was told they had absolutely no idea.\nMeanwhile, as the customer, I am left in complete uncertainty with no access to my own funds.\nIf Fintiba has trouble verifying my identity through this account, they can reach out to me directly and I will provide the necessary information to confirm my account details. Previously, they responded to one of my reviews by falsely claiming they could not locate my account. This excuse no longer applies.\nIt is extremely frustrating that Fintiba seems more focused on responding to and removing public reviews than on addressing the legitimate concerns of their paying customers through proper customer support channels.\nBased on my experience, I strongly advise others to reconsider before trusting Fintiba with such an important financial requirement.​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​\n\n\n.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The reply time is just too much! Been waiting for so many days, and still I have no reply. The service is extremely slow.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "no funcionó la app y es complejo el flujo de transferencia", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Schelcht sehr schelcht", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "All the support ever does is send me automated emails telling me to wait. Never gets any resolution.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Es war sehr schlecht.Ich bin unzufrieden.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Fintiba is the most shit organization ive used in German so far. Their app is so buggy you get error after error. Sometimes it keep spamming the documents when you download 1. I couldn't change my IBAN number because of an error that the system gave 3 weeks ago. Their support team hasn't even resolved the issue they are so shit. Their support is also shit like that org is sub standard", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ich versuche seit drei Wochen, den Betrag der monatlichen Zahlung zu ändern. Dies ist eine Anforderung der LEA. Die Mitarbeiter im Support sagen, dass mein Anliegen hohe Priorität hat, unternehmen jedoch nichts.\nIch bin bereit, mich für kostenpflichtige Unterstützung an die Verbraucherzentrale zu wenden. Einen derart schlechten Service habe ich noch nirgendwo erlebt.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "It's expensive and very long to process the account verification", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Initial rating: 1 star.\n\nDespite claiming to answer support queries within 1 business day, I received no reply within a week. \n\nFor a service on which people's livelihoods have to depend on (because fintiba and Expatio are single-company monopoly) this is unacceptable.\n\nUpd (13.09.26):\nUpdating to 2 stars, as I finally received an answer to my support query - several weeks after the initial inquiry. \n\nClaims to having 1-day support response are still misleading. I wish Fintiba was honest about expected processing times to not cause anxiety in the customers.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Coracle has transfered my money to fintiba almost since 2 weeks and There is a glitch on fintiba page showing I need to transfer another 79 euros. I've emailed fintiba support twice and haven't gotten any response yet.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Very poor experience with Fintiba.\n\nTicket #1201453 was supposed to be resolved within 14 working days, but it has now been over one month with no solution. I only receive repeated generic responses asking for more time.\n\nMy university deadline is 30 April, and this delay is putting my future at risk. Extremely disappointing and unreliable service.\nI strongly urge Fintiba to take immediate action on urgent cases like mine instead of sending automated responses. This level of service is highly frustrating and unreliable for international students.\n\nI hope this review pushes Fintiba to resolve my issue as soon as possible.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ich warte seit Wochen auf die Eröffnung meines Sperrkontos – trotz vollständig eingereichter Unterlagen.\n\nMein Visum ist seit dem 01. April gültig und wurde am 08. April hochgeladen. Seitdem ist nichts passiert. Weder wurde mein Konto eröffnet noch habe ich eine verbindliche Rückmeldung erhalten.\n\nBesonders frustrierend: Ich habe mehrfach angerufen und zusätzlich eine E-Mail geschrieben. Jedes Mal wurde ich lediglich auf „weiter warten“ verwiesen – ohne konkrete Informationen oder eine Lösung.\n\nEin Sperrkonto ist eine zwingende Voraussetzung für den Aufenthalt in Deutschland. Durch diese Verzögerung entstehen mir erhebliche Probleme und Unsicherheiten.\n\n\nIch kann den Service aktuell leider nicht empfehlen.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Everything was OK with this company\nUntil today.\nI just want to learn something from customer service.\nHe answered my phone call and, without offering any greeting, said “Yes, I can speak English” and then asked in a harsh tone, “What can I do for you?”\n\nI explained my issue. He then asked for some information and repeated the same question again in an even harsher tone.\n\nI politely asked him to be a bit more courteous, but he started shouting at me, accused me of being drunk, and hung up on me.\n\nHe probably behaved this way because I couldn’t speak German and because I did not consent to the call being recorded at the beginning. Not speaking German should not be a problem, and if it is, it certainly should not be an issue for an international company.\n\nI just wanted to ask when the €12,000 I sent would be credited to my account. 🤷🏼‍♂️", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Über Trustpilot erhielten wir die Meldung, das die Fintiba das Problem behoben hat. Tatsächlich hat Sie nur zum wiederholten mal per E-Mail mitgeteilt, dass wir uns weiterhin gedulden sollen.\nEs gibt also weiterhin kein Sperrkonto und den Verbleib des am 02.04.26 nachweislich eingezahlten Betrages konnte die Fintiba bis heute nicht klären.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "\"I am a genuine customer (ID: 504434711). My review is 100% real and based on my struggle to get a refund of €11,887.10, which has been stuck since March 12th.\nFintiba is trying to flag my review as 'not genuine' just to hide their poor service. I am providing my Sutor Bank statement (dated 02.04.2026) as proof, which shows they are still deducting €4.90 monthly fees from my blocked account even after I submitted the Visa Rejection/Sperrfreigabe documents.\nI have already reported this to BaFin. I request Trustpilot to verify my documents and keep this review active to warn other students.\"\n\nI am highly frustrated with Fintiba's service. I applied for my blocked account closure and refund on 12th March 2024, following all the necessary procedures and providing the required documents. It has been nearly 2 months, and I have received no refund and no response to my multiple follow-up emails.\nAs per my latest bank statement and app status (Fintiba ID: 504434711), my current balance of 11,887.10 € is still sitting in the account. Shockingly, Fintiba is still deducting monthly fees of 4.90 € (last seen on 02.04.2024) despite the account closure request.\nThis level of negligence is unacceptable. I am being forced to escalate this matter to BaFin (German Financial Regulator) as there has been zero communication from Fintiba’s support team. I demand an immediate update and the full refund of my funds including the wrongly deducted fees. I have the bank statements and visa rejection letters ready. Please provide an upload link or an email address where I can send these proofs immediately to verify my review.\"", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Fintiba is illegally withholding my blocked account funds. I have been in Germany since February, yet I have received ZERO payouts for March and April. I uploaded all documents in March, and support admits there is no action needed from my side, yet they refuse to release MY money due to their own bank migration issues. Ticker Number 1190830\nThis is a total failure of service that has left me in a severe financial crisis with no money for living expenses. I am filing a formal complaint with BaFin. If you are considering Fintiba, STAY AWAY—they will leave you stranded in a foreign country without access to your own money. This is unacceptable,´and the service is non existent.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "If you are not qualified enough to provide the service for which you are charging a fees then at least you need to tell the truth. Your customer agents are useless. Frontend has no communication with the backend and it just a chaos. I am regretting not to use Epatrio and decided to deal with this and neglecting  the  negative Feedbacks. 10 Days for a very simple step to raise the amount of the blcoked account. No more! Ticket Number: 1194270\nI additionally attached the statement of embassy which shows how urgent is this issue which and impact if i missed the examination appointment and the associated booked flight tickets and requested to be called back and no one even cares.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "the support hangs up the phone during the call.\nthe mails are not being answered.\nthe chatbot is not helping at all.\nthe money is not being paid out as it should.\nthe communication is a disaster.\n\nHow am I supposed to give my mail adress to you, Fintiba? I already answered the forms that you were sending through trustpilot.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Avoid Fintiba at all costs.\n\nI have had no access to my money for over a month. I sent emails every day — no replies. Customer service hangs up calls and does not help.\n\nThis is unacceptable for a company responsible for students’ blocked accounts. Leaving people without funds in a foreign country is not just bad service — it is irresponsible.\n\nI strongly advise future students to choose another provider.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Leider war es nicht einfach, online ein Konto zu eröffnen und den erforderlichen Betrag für die Verpflichtungserklärung zu blockieren. Telefonisch konnte mir nicht weitergeholfen werden, und auch per E-Mail erhielt ich keine hilfreiche Unterstützung.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "So bad, first the chatbot is not helpful at all and when I can the customer service the man was very rude and he cut the call while I gave him my passport number.\nAnd they did not respond my e-mail", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Till now no reply for my messages. How can I buy  fentiba plus.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I was wondering if there could be a quicker way to speak to agent online via chat instead of a bot. I need to update my passport on my account asap so I can travel since I just got my visa approval. I would appreciate if there was someone available to help me with this.\nI am extremely disappointed with Fintiba’s support process. I requested a simple passport update in my account and was told it would take 3–5 business days just to process, and potentially another 24 hours just to receive an initial response explaining the delay.\nUnfortunately after speaking to 2 agents today.\nThis is not acceptable given how time-sensitive blocked account and insurance matters are, especially when travel and embassy deadlines are involved. There is very little flexibility or urgency in handling critical updates, even when the customer clearly explains the situation.\n\nFor a service that international students and visa applicants rely on, the communication and speed of resolution need to be significantly improved. I expected much more efficiency and understanding in urgent cases like this.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Worst experience", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am a student in Freising/Munich, currently facing a dire financial situation because Fintiba refuses to release my blocked funds. My rent is due in 9 days, and I am literally running out of money for food and my commute to university.\nDespite the urgency, customer service is dismissive and aggressive when I call for updates. It is unacceptable that I am being treated this way while peers who used EXPATRIO had their funds released within 10 days of arrival.\nFintiba is failing in its primary purpose: to provide students with their own money for survival in Germany. If my funds are not released immediately, I will face eviction and severe consequences. I strongly advise all international students to choose Expatrio over this unprofessional service.\nCase # 1191272", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Guten Tag \nich bin interessiert an ein Sperrkonto bei Fintiba gewesen. Darüber möchte ich direkt mich online Portal melden. Mir gefällt die Gelegenheit zu Hause bequem mein Anliegen zu machen. Aber der Prozesse für  die Kontrollieren die Identität so lange dauert. Es kostet mich sehr viel Zeit darauf zu warten. Ich hatte noch andere Problem um die Überweisung zu bezahlen. Das war schlimm weil ich in der Wartezeit meine Termine mit Ausländerbehöre verpasst habe. Weil der Summe mein Antrags falsch gestellt geworden ist. \nIch hätte gerne noch mal mit Fintiba Team im Verbindung bleiben. Aber hoffe, die Unannehmlichkeiten wird aufgehoben. Ich schätze sehr dass eure Kundenservice Team schnell und kompetent mit meine Fragen reagierte. Vielen Dank wünsche Euch weiterhin viel Erfolg. \nMit Freundlichen Grüßen \nThao Vu", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ich habe zur Unterstützung geschrieben und kann seit 10 Tagen keine Antwort mehr erhalten.  Ich muss die monatliche Zahlung für meinen Visumantrag ändern. Und das kann ich sehr lange nicht tun. Ich rufe an, aber der Bediener sagt auch, dass er nichts tun kann. Es ist ein schrecklicher Service", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Worst experience in terms of payment. They are definitely holding my money. \n\nThe OTP works on anywhere except when it comes to withdraw phase...\n\nI cannot reach MY MONEY for 1 week. \n\nMailed them 3 times and called the support many many times (more than 10 in last 7 days). Support says the ticket is created, you should wait. Meanwhile my rent payment delayed days.\n\nUSE EXPATRIO SAVE YOURSELF", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "A disaster. I have been waiting for more than 3 weeks to receive my monthly payment from my blocked account. I called them and send emails. Costumer support says since week one that the money will arrive in a few days, EVERYTIME. I don’t know if a few days mean a whole month or what in germany, but it’s a very disgusting situation i find myself now. I have literally no money left. Do yourself a favor and never open an account with them. Guten Tag!!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "One of the 3rd class Customer Support one of the 3rd class Block Account Bank Fintiba, I created my account and do everything next day they send me Passport verification failed I need to re-upload I uploaded and today when I'm writing this review believe me or not 19 days have been passed and I'm calling them and emailing them for consecutive 19 day what there Customer support say we can't help you best of luck bye, and Today my visa got rejected just because of Fintiba.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have been facing a serious issue with my Fintiba account.\n\nI requested a phone number change because my previous phone is damaged, but I could not find any solution in the app. I also contacted support multiple times via phone and email, but I did not receive any helpful response.\n\nI have been in Germany for a week and I still cannot access my account properly, which is causing me real difficulties.\n\nI hope this issue will be addressed soon and that better support will be provided to users in similar situations.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Die Fintiba hat sich offensichtlich neu aufgestellt. Es gibt nur noch ein Sperrkonto mit teurer Barmer Krankenversicherung. Wir hatten am 2.4.2026 Geld eingezahlt und dies mit korkten Daten im Einzahlungsbeleg auch nachgewiesen. Die Fintiba vertröstet uns seit dem und weiß angeblich nicht wo das Geld in Ihrer Partnerbank abgeblieben ist. Wann das Sperrkonto freigegeben wird wissen wir bis heute nicht (21.04.2026). Es gibt keine Beschwerdemöglichkeit und Vorgesetzte sind für den Kunden auch nicht zu sprechen. Aus unserer Sicht ist die Fintiba trotz guten Internetauftrittes nicht in der Lage Ihren Geschäftszweck ordnungsgemäß nachzukommen. Der Einzahlungsbetrag ist nicht auffindbar.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "My payment is three weeks late which is putting me in a really difficult situation. I have called Fintiba four times and each time they told me the money will be transferred in a couple of days, which did not happen. They also told me to reach them via email and it’ll be answered in one work day, which I did multiple times and haven’t received any response even after three weeks. Every time i reach customer support they have no idea what is going on and they come up with a different excuse. Today the last time I called they said it is not Fintiba's responsibility and hanged up on me. This irresponsibility is unacceptable considering most their customers are international students who solely depend on their blocked accounts. I’ll close my account as soon as I get all the payments back and will move to another blocked account firm. I don’t recommend Fintiba.\n\nps: even though it seems like my problem is solved from the reply, it is the end of the week and I still haven't received the money. It is not even shown as transferred and customer support can't solve the problem. It has been a month I couldn't pay my rent and bills because of this situation it is really unacceptable and frustrating.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have been trying to set up my payout IBAN for over 10 days, but the app keeps showing an error: ‘There are problems calculating your payouts.’ I have contacted support multiple times and only received delayed, generic responses. I am a student living in Germany and I urgently need access to my blocked account funds for my living expenses. Ticket #1185014 is still unresolved. I expected much better service from Fintiba.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have been stranded in germany for a month now because fintibas verification phase is just not ending so that it releases my own goddamn money, DO NOT OPEN AN ACCOUNT WITH THEM, use expatrio instead atleast its worth the fee. The customer suppport doesnt work nor are they replying to emails. I had to transfer my funds from coracle as they closed off while i was still in germany and now fintiba isnt accepting my visa date either cuz \"it was before account opening\" maybe check these things before you take someone's money?? Trash organization.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Opened an account with Fintiba and moved to Germany, was supposed to receive my first payout on the 2nd of April but it failed due to some credit issue. I call the customer service and they basically do nothing, send two emails with no response. I called again today and as I go to explain my issue the lady just hangs up, avoid this company like the plague!!! They don't care about your money or anything. It's been almost 2 weeks now and I still didn't receive my first payment.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Very disappointing experience with Fintiba.\n\nMy monthly payout is delayed with no clear explanation. I was told multiple times the money would arrive, but it didn’t. Support keeps giving vague answers and no exact timeline. \n\nThis is unacceptable, especially for students who rely on this money for basic living expenses.\n\nit’s been 2 weeks.\nSupport code:\n 965-061-420", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "the fee, even though its monthly payed its way too high, specially for students. I know deutsche bank used to charge 200 EUR for the blocked account but at least it was a well established german bank. For a bank that is practically unknown that runs only online to charge an additional of over 150 euros to just be able to have an account that is unfortunately imposed to foreigner students who often dont come from money to begin with to me is taking advantage of the system and the people that are affected by it.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am extremely disappointed with Fintiba. They are quick to deduct high fees (159€ opening fee + monthly fees), but when it comes to providing the service, they fail miserably. It is already the 14th of April and I still haven't received my monthly payout. As a student, I rely on this money for my basic needs. Their lack of planning for holidays has put me in a serious financial crisis. I would NOT recommend Fintiba to anyone. Avoid them if you don't want to be left stranded without money in Germany!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Fintiba provides abysmal customer service; they simply do not respond to emails. You could be starving without your basic needs being met and they wouldn't care; even then, they won't release your money. They rejected a transfer to my German IBAN and more than a week has passed without them resending the funds or providing any explanation. This service is failing to meet its obligations. If you have other app options, try them instead, because this is just a profit-driven bank. Never again with Fintiba. TERRIBLE SERVICE!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Horrible customer service and they do not answer immediately \nAll the emails are urgent and they do not reply they leave you for weeks without replying\nI do not recommend it its so bad \nI have been calling them for more than a week now they keep telling me they will solve my problems as soon as possible and nothing gets solved \nThe agents have some sentences learned that they all day the same thing \nVery horrible and unacceptable", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "An absolute headache of a company. They haven’t been able to deposit my first payout for almost half a month. Which means I haven’t been able to pay my rent or my food for half a month. They said my issue would be resolved at the latest on Monday and when I called today (on Monday) they told me that it would be resolved during this week. I have no trust left in this company. They also haven’t provided the bank account that was supposed to be included in my plus package. Use anything else so that you don’t have to worry about not having access to the money that you own. This is completely against the point of a blocked account and the German visa process.\n\nMy support code is: 003-364-109\n\nI demand immediate action.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I closed my blocking account with fintiba after my move to Germany fell through.\nThey have apparently refunded the €12.000 that I had with them, but my account now shows €0 on fintibas side and I haven't received the funds. Their email support takes weeks to reply to simple requests and today their phone team hung up on me. No idea what to do. \n€12.000 has just vanished", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I opened a blocked account with Fintiba two weeks ago, and since then I’ve been stuck in the address verification process with no clear resolution.\n\nFirst, I submitted my 3-month bank statement in English, which clearly showed my name and residential address. According to Fintiba’s own guidelines, proof of a bank account with my name and address should be acceptable. However, my document was rejected without a convincing explanation.\n\nThen, I went a step further and obtained an official residence document issued by the Turkish government. I had it translated into English by a sworn translator and submitted it again. This document includes a verification barcode and can be validated online through the Turkish e-government system. It even explicitly states that it was issued for submission to institutions like Fintiba. Despite all of this, it was rejected again.\n\nAt this point, I genuinely do not understand what kind of document Fintiba actually expects.\n\nFor the past 3 days, I have been sending emails but have received no response. I have also called multiple times—either no one answers, or I’m told it will be reviewed “by tomorrow,” which never happens.\n\nThis situation is extremely stressful because I have an upcoming appointment at the German embassy and urgently need my blocked account confirmation. My language course is also about to start, and without complete documents, my visa application is at serious risk.\n\nIf my visa gets rejected due to these delays and lack of support, will Fintiba take responsibility?\n\nAdditionally, your website mentions that rental contracts or utility bills are acceptable documents—but in many cases (like mine), these are not in the applicant’s name, making them unusable.\n\nHonestly, I am exhausted and extremely disappointed. I don’t know what else I’m supposed to provide.\n\nSupport Code: 794-099-020", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Im Prozess hat man zu viel Geld verloren\nzB beträgt die Abrechnung des Evangeliums 150 €, wobei 4,5 € pro Monat einbehalten werden.\nAber Hauptproblem kann man nicht zweite Sperrkonto öffnen \nİch wohne seit 1 Jahr in Deutschland und ich warte meine Termin für Visum \nDeswegen habe ich heutzutage keine Fiktionsbescheinigung \nDann sie sagen mir ,dass sie Sperrkonto nicht aktivieren dürfen.Wenn ich von Sperrkonto nicht Geld bekommen kann,\nWarum meldete ich bei der Sperrkonto", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am writing to formally notify Fintiba that the technical issue preventing access to my blocked account has remained unresolved for over 8 weeks, despite repeated contact with your customer support.\n\nDue to your failure to provide a functioning verification process, I am being unlawfully denied access to my own funds. This situation is causing me significant financial hardship.\n\nI hereby set a final deadline of 7 calendar days from receipt of this email to fully resolve the issue and restore my access.\n\nIf the problem is not resolved within this period, I will take further action without additional notice. This includes, but is not limited to:\n\nFiling a formal complaint with BaFin\n\nContacting Verbraucherzentrale\n\nInitiating legal proceedings with the assistance of a lawyer to claim damages\n\nPlease also note that I expect an immediate alternative verification method to be provided, as your current system is clearly not functioning.\n\nThis matter is urgent and requires immediate attention.\n\nSincerely,", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "While using Fintiba I got a problem with bounced payment. My bank rejected monthly transfer from Fintiba and bounced it back. Fintiba app offered me to transfer money again or to another bank with different IBAN. I changed my IBAN but after entering sms code it says that error server occurred. I tried contacting support, but even after holidays they are still ghosting me after few working days (they say it takes maximum 1 working day). Support's phone number simply disconnecting right after you are trying to call. I am running out of money because Fintiba' support team seams not to exist. That's why I DO NOT recommend Fintiba for people who don't want to stress out\n\nEdited: as you can see they do not care at all suggesting me to contact their support team, that I've mentioned as the worst support service which constantly ignores people", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "very worst experience,\nafter transforming money to my block account, it has been more than a week still my money is in verification. i have uploaded bank statement, our business audit report and bank balance certificate, still no response. my classes have already started from april , and i have mailed them so many time regarding my issue but no response , if the documnets are missing i can provide futher documents , but they are not responding.many others also have said it takes months to verify source of funds.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Mein Problem wurde nicht gelöst.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Sehr enttäuschender und unzuverlässiger Service. Seit über einem Monat versuche ich, mein Konto zu aktivieren – ohne Ergebnis. Als Begründung wird meine angeblich zu kurze Aufenthaltserlaubnis genannt, obwohl ich das Konto mit genau dieser gültigen Aufenthaltserlaubnis eröffnet habe.\n\nDer Kundenservice ist keine Hilfe: immer die gleichen Standardantworten, keine Lösung. Mehrfach wurde mir eine Rückmeldung versprochen, die nie kam. Einmal wurde das Gespräch sogar einfach beendet.\n\nInsgesamt sehr unprofessionell. Absolut nicht empfehlenswert.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Very good fi", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The customer support is slow to reply and doesn't work fast enough. I had requested my transfer from coracle to fintiba on 18th of March and now its 2nd of April and the amount hasn't been reached yet. The deadline is April 10th. I hope it gets transferred soon as I dont understand the delay because both companies are owned by the same group.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "OK, I look forward to your response by email", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Taking way too much time to respond. Very slow service. Disappointed", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Für alle, die ein Sperrkonto bei Fintiba in Betracht ziehen, möchte ich meine persönliche Erfahrung teilen:\n\nDie Eröffnung und Abwicklung des Sperrkontos ist aus meiner Sicht relativ komplex und erfordert mehrere Schritte, die man genau verstehen und korrekt durchführen muss.\n\nDie Bearbeitungszeiten können außerdem recht lang sein, insbesondere bei der Prüfung von Unterlagen und der Freischaltung der monatlichen Auszahlung. Wer dringend auf das Geld angewiesen ist, sollte dies unbedingt berücksichtigen und ausreichend Zeit einplanen!!!\n\nAuch die Auszahlung selbst erfolgt nicht immer so schnell, wie man es erwartet, was in bestimmten Situationen zu Problemen führen kann.\n\nPositiv ist, dass das Konto grundsätzlich die notwendigen Anforderungen für Aufenthalt und Visum erfüllt.\n\nMein Fazit: Man sollte sich vorab sehr gut informieren und sich auf längere Bearbeitungszeiten einstellen!!!\n\nIch hoffe, dieses Feedback hilft anderen bei ihrer Entscheidung.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Hello, my Fintiba support case number is 248-790-731. Our request to change our IBAN has still not been resolved. We are still being kept waiting under the pretext of missing documents. We know they requested these documents from us for security purposes. However, we have already sent our notarized passport information, along with both our old and new bank IBAN details. Additionally, our bank has confirmed and sent the updated IBAN information. We took a selfie with our passport and sent it. We also sent our visa, which has not been approved. \nHow else can we prove our identity? We tried to prove ourselves through a video call. Since we don’t speak the language, they immediately hang up on us. I’m already applying to learn the language. How much longer will this simple issue take? Now Fintiba is negotiating with a new bank. Another layer will be added to our problem. Please, we kindly ask you to finally process this simple IBAN change. Hülya Günay/Turkey", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I asked my cousin in Germany to deposit money into my Fintiba blocked account last Wednesday 18/03/2026.  I made sure he did that using the instant transfer option, yet I have not received my confirmatory letter. All efforts together with receipts sent to Fintiba by mail have proven futile. This is unfair and considering recommendations to use this platform, I am almost regretting my decision.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "At first, everything about fintiba felt straightforward and very direct which is good. However, until now I realised even after months of waiting after providing all the required documents, my account is still on pending (which is dire as my trip is arriving soon). Other schoolmates that registered with fintiba for the same purpose as I did seemed to have no issue getting their accounts. Furthermore, when I try and contact support, first the AI bot was absolutely useless, being unable to answer any and all questions I posed. Then when redirected to email, it has been nearly a week since I inquired yet they not only told me it was taking longer than usual to process, but did not give me any more notifications and updates after that first email (which was 1 day after my inquiry). \n\nAccount support code: 681-849-361", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "أريد السفر والبحث عن عمل", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "My wife and I had our funds blocked through Fintiba for a language course in Germany. However, since our language visa was not approved, we have been trying to close our account since January 2026. The original account we provided to Fintiba had its IBANs changed due to a name change at our bank. We proved this situation to Fintiba with numerous documents they requested and sent them via courier with notary certification. Despite this, deductions from our account have continued for months. They have been unable to process the IBAN change. Every time we call, we end up back at square one, and no solution is found. We are now urgently requesting a resolution to this issue. We ask that you process the IBAN change and finally refund our money. Hülya Günay/Türkei", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Application for Android and all related documents is a complete mess. Amounts to pay in invoices don't match selected amounts in app. Files are downloaded not in the folder that you specify in a dialogue window and you have to search for them, most of the time files are broken and won't open anyway. Blank lines in agreement etc etc. \nEdit: I contacted support  (ticket 1163276) on 25 March. As of April 3 there is still no answer, except for \"sorry for delay, we'll come back to you shortly\".", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Worst customer service ever, have been trying to change my insurance from a higher tier to a lower one, their AI chat bot is useless, you have to send emails, which then they respond to 24 hours later then if u reply instantly to it for a follow up or to provide them info they reply another 24 hours later, and they still have not managed to fix my problem, I contacted them via phone so hopefully my problem could get resolved quicker, the support agent sounded like they do not want to help whatsoever, haven’t even finished my sentence and they’re already trying to end the conversation saying have a nice day, still couldn’t get my problem resolved, they said they raised a ticket and I have still not gotten any update, the only update I got was a “we’d love your feedback” email lol", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ich habe noch 100 Euro Restguthaben, die noch nicht überwiesen wurden.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Don't trust Fintiba, they haven't returned money for months! They're passing the request around in circles.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Die Informationen kommen immer nur in Englisch", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "delay, disappointment", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "delay, disappointment", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ich nutze Fintiba seit mehreren Jahren für mein Sperrkonto und hatte bisher keine größeren Probleme. Nachdem jedoch die Partnerbank zu Frankfurt International Bank gewechselt wurde, war meine Erfahrung sehr frustrierend.\n\nAls ich mein Sperrkonto verlängern wollte, musste ich plötzlich ein komplett neues Konto eröffnen, da sich die Partnerbank geändert hatte. Darüber wurde ich vorher nicht klar informiert.\n\nNachdem ich Geld für meine Lebenshaltungskosten überwiesen hatte, wurde ich erst danach darüber informiert, dass eine Source-of-Funds-Prüfung erforderlich ist. Diese Anforderung wurde vor der Überweisung nicht kommuniziert, wodurch mein Geld während des Verifizierungsprozesses faktisch blockiert wurde.\n\nMir wurde mitgeteilt, dass der Prozess bis zu 15 Werktage dauern könne. Inzwischen dauert die Prüfung jedoch deutlich länger. Zusätzlich kam es zu weiteren Verzögerungen, weil ein bereits eingereichtes Dokument angeblich nicht eingegangen ist und erneut gesendet werden musste.\n\nIch verstehe, dass Compliance- und Geldwäscheprüfungen notwendig sind. Dennoch ist die mangelnde Transparenz, die schlechte Kommunikation und die langsame Bearbeitung sehr belastend – besonders da Sperrkonten für grundlegende Lebenshaltungskosten wie Miete und Krankenversicherung vorgesehen sind.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Very Bad experience and so frustrating. I made a directremit transfer on 14-02 ( this type of transfer should be very fast 1 to 3 days max)\nMy bank already confirmed that transaction was done and money has reached to Fintiba. Now after 3 weeks my money doesn’t appear in my blocked account.After several emails they said may be their partner bank sutor is holding the money. The investigation is ongoing and Now i don’t know what happened to this transfer or if it’s held by sutor or not!!! Totally confused!!!\nNever recommend this poor bank. Honestly you are very far from the standard of customer service.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "very slow customer service, complicated system and expensive products. I am supposed to apply for my visa today and i still could not get the documents for my insurance.\ni have moved to expatrio for their services and it is a much smoother and faster experience. i will not recommend fintiba to any of my friends.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Fintiba offers a fast and smooth blocked account setup with clear guidance, making the process stress-free. However, it is comparatively more expensive than other providers.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Fintiba just decides to not send me my money for the month March and i cant pay my bills and rent and that is a huge problem in Germany. And as if thats not enough their support is literally so bad. They dont respond to your emails,they have the worst chatbot in history which is not able to solve no problems whatsoever.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "- still waiting for the pay out\n- customer service is rude and hang up on me\n- unhelpful email responses \n- worst chatbot out there", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Der Support ist nicht zuverlässig.\nIch habe Fintiba ein Jahr lang benutzt. Die ersten Monate liefen reibungslos, sodass ich keinen Support brauchte und alles mehr oder weniger allein ausführen konnte. Sobald ich mein Konto zum zweiten Mal verlängern wollte, begann das Chaos. Ab diesem Zeitpunkt haben sie mich entweder nicht richtig oder sogar falsch beraten. So musste ich bei einer Kontoeröffnung eine neue Krankenversicherung abschließen, obwohl ich diese nicht brauchte, und kämpfe immer noch um die Schließung dieses Kontos, das immer noch gegen meinen Willen offen ist. Außerdem muss man bei der Eröffnung des Kontos nicht „pflichtende“ Punkte zustimmen, um weiterzumachen. \nAus diesem und weiteren Gründen habe ich einen anderen Anbieter gesucht. Für diesen Preis sollte man zumindest einen zuverlässigen Support bekommen.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Terrible Experience with Fintiba\nI am extremely disappointed with Fintiba. They have refused to process my last payout and have completely ignored all my email inquiries and phone calls. The lack of communication is unacceptable. I am seriously contemplating visiting their Frankfurt office in person due to the sheer inconvenience they have caused. This level of service is frustrating and unprofessional.\n\nUpdate: After endlessly complaining for days, they have reached out claiming that they have technical issues and will make the Transfer in the next few days. I am already sleeping in the streets, begging for food in a foreign country.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I really wish I was writing this with a better review but so far my experience with Fintiba has been lacklustre at best and highly frustrating at worst. Firstly, setting the blocked account up was not as straight forward as it was made out to seem as, if you are like me and come from a so called \"high risk\" country for money laundering, you will have to provide several different documents to prove the funds put in the account are of a legitimate origin. So, in other words, they will accept the transfer but will make you prove the source of funds before they start releasing them.\n\nBecause of this, the payout schedule I needed to have was delayed and my family had to fork out additional funds so I could live for the first month. Whatever fine, the source of funds was finally accepted after many emails and calls (that I had to initiate by the way because Fintiba can't seem to be bothered to tell you exactly what they need and by when) and I started receiving payouts. \n\nNow you would think from here onwards everything would be smooth sailing but no, after four payouts (one of which came late because they took forever to activate my account) I find myself with no money for March because I didn't receive a payout in late February. Did anyone call or email or even alert me in any way in the app/website that this could happen? No, of course not.\n\nSo now I find myself without money to pay my rent or insurance for this month, both of which are due on the 5th of March. I have called twice and still nothing. I called yesterday and I was told I should receive my money by today but my gut told me to just call again and then I was told today that there is some kind of delay in many payments. Where was that explanation when I called yesterday? Now I have to wait until tomorrow to see what can be done and HOPE that I will be able to pay my rent and insurance. \n\nAs an international student coming from a developing country, I do not have the luxury to be inconvenienced in such a way by a service that is supposed to be straight-forward and reliable. I am terrified that I will be penalised by my landlord and insurance company for being late and I am even more so scared that I will have to ask my family to send even more money so I can afford to eat for the month. \n\nI won't pretend to be perfect, I have mismanaged that late payout they sent earlier which I theoretically could have used in this situation, but I did not expect that they would skip a random month to make up for the initial mix up. And what's worse is I didn't expect to not be informed of what they would do with my own money, a simple email explaining the change in payout schedule would have done wonders but no. \n\nI really hope the escalation made today in the form of a ticket will save me otherwise I will have to rely on my family again. I am scared, anxious and terribly de-moralised by this experience. Unfortunately, I don't have the privilege to close the account and open with a new provider so I will continue to be steadfast with Fintiba. \n\nBut if you are an international student coming to Germany considering Fintiba, check if you come from what they consider a \"high risk\" country for money laundering and plan accordingly because dealing with customer service when there is an issue will drive you insane and put you in precarious positions.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ich versuche seit Mitte Januar, mein Fintiba-Konto zu schließen und mein Geld zurückzubekommen. Ich habe alle Dokumente eingereicht, die WebID-Verifikation gemacht und das Formular für die Rücküberweisung ausgefüllt. Mein Konto zeigt immer noch „ausstehend“ und ich habe keine Bestätigung, wann das Geld kommt. Durch die Verzögerung bin ich in einer sehr schwierigen Situation, habe kein Geld für Essen und muss Hilfe bei sozialen Organisationen suchen. Das Ganze ist ein sehr schlechter Erfahrung und eine enorme Belastung für mich als Kunde. Außerdem berechnet das Unternehmen mir weiterhin jeden Monat 5 Euro Servicegebühr für ein Konto, das ich eigentlich seit Januar schließen möchte.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I set up an account and I put money in the account about 2 months ago. A few days afterwards they sent me an email telling me to send documents to prove my source of funds. They put a timer for 11 days to approve your documents but they never do. You will just see pending on your blocked account every single time. The fintibot does not help at all. The customer service is terrible. When you email them they keep asking for the same documents over and over even after you provide them. It's like it's an automatically generated message. I really wish they took this seriously because I'm already in Germany and don't know how to access my funds.\nMy brother also made an account with them the same time I did and he has experienced the same issue. To the point where his visa is being held back because of his blocked account. It's so unfortunate! I truly wish we never used Fintiba to begin with. I have reached out to them with emails after this reply but still no real person is replying it's just an automated message. I wish they understood the urgency of certain matters", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I want to communicate with my bank", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I sent 5 times email regarding to Stop my Barmer Health Insurance and Mawista Health Insurance because I have already Public health insurance in TK but haven't stopped Public Health Insurance yet by Fintiba team. Please stop this Insurance as soon as possible.\nLittrely, It made me disappointed that you are not stopping my Barmer and Mawista Insurance even I attached my TK insurance file here.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "opened a blocked account with Fintiba and transferred the full required amount for my student visa application. The funds have already been credited to my blocked account, yet I have still not received my blocking confirmation.\nMy university courses start on April 1st, and my visa appointment is scheduled for March 12th. This document is essential for my visa process, and the delay is putting my studies at serious risk.\nWhat is particularly concerning is the quality of communication. The responses I receive from customer support are often generic and do not provide clear timelines or concrete solutions. Instead of addressing the urgency of my situation, I have been redirected to contact FIB, even though my contractual relationship and payment were made directly with Fintiba.\nAs a student dealing with strict visa deadlines, this lack of clear communication and accountability creates significant stress and uncertainty. I expected transparent information, realistic processing timelines, and coordinated support between Fintiba and their banking partner.\nI am sharing this experience to highlight the impact that delays and unclear communication can have on international students whose academic futures depend on time-sensitive documentation.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "This is the worst experience I’ve ever had with a financial institution. Their website promises 3-4weeks to issue a refund but it’s been two months and I keep getting the same automated response. \n\nIt takes a few days to open this account but after that, don’t expect any real customer support", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Below zero.my son paid more than 6000 Euro as blocked account and get the conformation but did not get any money because of error in the system since 10 days and IT there did not solve the problem ,very bad communication and i do not know what an IT who cannot solve a problem in the system and who will compensate my sin", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The 29–38 age range has been blocked from creating new accounts without any prior notice or explanation, and no one is taking responsibility for it.\nNo clear reason is provided for this restriction, and no timeframe is given for when it will be resolved.\nCustomer support is practically nonexistent — only automated, repetitive responses with no real investigation or follow-up.\nThis level of irresponsibility, lack of transparency, and disregard for users is completely unacceptable.\nUsers have the right to know why they are being restricted and exactly when this issue will be fixed.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "No real people in real time to help foreigners only German phone number when blocked accounts are mostly a requirement for foreigners", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "my son paid more than 6000 euro, there is a problem in the system, the IT did not solve the problem since 7 days, my son cannot live due to your delay ,", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "URGENT: 4 Months of Contradictory Information! €13,198 Refund Missing! Ticket #1081596\n​@Fintiba officially confirmed on Oct 15 that my refund was executed on Oct 1, 2025. Now, after 4 months, you provide contradictory updates regarding the execution date (Feb 9 and Feb 11) for the same transaction.\n​This lack of transparency and consistent contradictory information is unacceptable. I require the MT103/SWIFT copy within 24 hours. Failure to do so will result in a formal complaint to BaFin including all evidence of these contradictions.\n​Stop the delays and return my money!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I can't use the ui functionality until i make a transfer to blocked account!!. I need to immeadiately close my blocked account and insurance made by fintiba. but they keep auto registrating the insurance. i have insure by TK . They do not close your account or anything. There is just an automated ai bot replying and that's it. NO REAL CUSTOMER SUPPORT.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have been trying to solve a critical issue with my blocked account for over 2 weeks (Multiple tickets sent), and I keep receiving generic or negative responses.\nThe German Consulate has officially requested an increase of my monthly blocked amount to €1,491 (€1,091 for me + €400 for my spouse as a dependent/refakatçi). This is a MANDATORY requirement for our joint visa approval.\nDespite explaining this multiple times:\n1. Fintiba refuses to manually update my monthly limit.\n2. My spouse CANNOT open a separate account because the Consulate currently holds his passport for the visa process, making ID verification impossible.\n3. This is a \"Joint Application\" where the main applicant (myself) is legally allowed to show the total funds for the family unit.\nI am being ignored by the support team while our visa process is at risk of rejection. I need a manual override of my \"Blocking Agreement\" to reflect the €1,491 monthly sum immediately.\nTicket reference: 1114797", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Why i can't i contact I be able to easily contact the bank if a person is depositing such large sum of money...", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Extremely expensive (health insurance)", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have had a very disappointing experience with Fintiba. My MFS transfer was scheduled for 29 January, and over a week later, I still have not received the funds.\n\nTo make things worse, I received conflicting information from their customer service: two representatives told me the IBAN country doesn’t matter, and a third said only a German IBAN works. This inconsistency caused me to waste time and left me unsure if the transfer would ever go through.\n\nEven after being told repeatedly that the payment was released and would arrive in 1–2 working days, the funds have not appeared in my account. The lack of reliability and clear communication is unacceptable.\n\nI strongly advise caution when dealing with Fintiba — this delay has caused me serious inconvenience and stress.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The partnership where you can book your insurance with the block account, was a experience for me.\nI will be cautiously advised others not to do same with like.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Null Service, null Respekt, und niemand versteht mich oder weiß, wie man mir helfen kann.\n\n\nZero service, zero respect, and nobody understands or knows how to help me.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Forced acceptance to apply for Mastercard, unnecessary insurance agreements to be insured under Barmer and also for to accept to apply for Mawista travel health insurance. Give students the opportunity to choose what they like. Lastly, charges are high compared to when the blocked account was opened with Sutor Bank", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The available options aren't very clear unless you look very closely. If you make a mistake, you can't undo your choices, so you have to switch accounts and browsers because the site saves information that prevents you from making other selections. The automated process is slow. I had trouble redoing another selection and had to contact technical support (because the bot isn't very helpful). I've been waiting for several days for technical support to respond and haven't been able to continue the process. If you're in a hurry, I don't think this is the best option.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Payment never Lost by Fintiba.\nI made a International payment for the purpose of Blocked Amount. The payment was deducted from my local bank and the local bank confirmed that the Payment was received by Fintiba's EUR correspondent Bank. However even upon sharing the International SWIFTCODE to the official support email of fintiba but there was no response nor my payments were debited to my Fintiba Account which is extremely frustrating and deploring. To worse the situation when I booked a support phone call so nobody showed up.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Disaster for people who want to get their money refunded!!!!! Technical issues and steps that never end. Just waiting for weeks, months, nobody cares, they only give general information on the phone. Our own money, in our own blocked account will not be refunded quickly, I don't know what to say, it's 2026!!!!!!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have contacted more than 10 times but just I have got an email like:\nafter reviewing your inquiry we've escalated it to the Fintiba IT Support team.\nWe will get back to you as soon as possible.\n\nHang in there! :-)\n\nWith ❤️ from Frankfurt\nYour Fintiba Team\n\n\nThis is a terrible IT support Team.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "How do I know the blocked account  i created is legit. I am indeed sceptical about the blocked account and will want to be certain this is legit", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have blocked for a period that was about 5 months and after that I just want to extend my blocked account while there is an extension option on App but I could not do that. Then I have connected with support Team embarrassedly they could not solve my problem even after 9 days. It seems there is a Bug in their App and Web-site as well.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Iam stuck \n            J no", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "My daughter Nawal Aziz is trying to open a Blocked Account for the study purpose in Germany. She has uploaded her picture with passport. One week has been passed away. Still waiting . I think your process is slow.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Fall 1049009 Sehr geehrte Fintiba, z. Hd. Arnold Sangonda Da Sie die fällige Rückerstattung bis heute nicht bearbeitet haben, informieren wir Sie darüber, dass dieser Fall an die Finanzaufsichtsbehörde BaFin weitergeleitet wurde. Wir weisen darauf hin, dass Sie das Konto eines EU-Bürgers gesperrt haben. Diese Maßnahme ist rechtlich nicht durchsetzbar, da sie gegen EU-Vorschriften verstößt. Bei Bedarf wird der Fall einer Anwaltskanzlei vorgelegt. 16. Dezember 2025", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "You have a major problem: a person cannot send money from America.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I’ve been trying to set up my payout for days, and the system still refuses to work. Every single time I enter my private bank account IBAN and submit it, I get the same error message saying “you’re not allowed to set up your payouts yet.”\nThis makes absolutely no sense, because all my documents are verified and everything on my account is supposedly in good standing.\n\nI’ve contacted support multiple times, and I keep getting nowhere. I’m stuck in an endless loop of trying, failing, and receiving no real explanation or solution. It’s incredibly frustrating and honestly unacceptable for a platform that handles financial information.\n\nI just want my payout set up, and instead I’m wasting time battling a system error that should have been fixed immediately. Very disappointed with this experience.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Once again I'm back with a negative review on fintiba.\nI have suffered with emails and calls to these people.\n\nI have followed my account statements for close to 3 weeks.My visa is expiring and I need to have a student residents permit immediately.\n1st instance they asked me to block more money only to be told that I needed to showcase my account statement as is by the visa application officer.\n\nI have been following up for this and today morning,I met a rude customer support officer who bluntly told me that 'they are busy with new accounts openings' and she couldn't help me get my blocked account statement urgently.\nClose to 3 weeks follow up on an expiring visa isn't urgent enough!!!\n\nThey frustrated me on insurance, withdrawals and now this.\nEmails on this are closed without addressing", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "They removed support email and relying on stupid AI response. When I call support number they promised to write back on email but nothing happened. Totally very bad experience. Ali", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Dear Fintiba Team,\n\nI would like to inform you that I have now received my university admission and have successfully opened my blocked account through Fintiba Plus.\n\nHowever, I am facing an important issue and kindly request your urgent support: my child will accompany me during my studies, and therefore I need to add the required additional blocked amount for my child.\n\nPlease enable the option to increase the blocked amount or provide me with the correct instructions for adding the additional amount. This is urgent as I must finalize everything before my visa appointment.\n\nThank you very much in advance for your assistance.\n\nBest regards,\nMostafa Abdalla Mostafa", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Unfortunately I have been met with constant resistance from Fintiba regarding the “legitimation” of my documents. Beware that there are a lot of hidden procedures that come after you successfully open your closed account, to actually get access to your funds again. I have been chasing around Fintiba support to get my account “legitimated” to get access to my account for about 3 months now, and now I am stranded in a foreign country, with all of my money locked in this bank account. I would definitely go with other providers that provide much more clarity in the procedures and actually provide support. Fintiba mediates support through their Fintibot, an AI service that routes you back to itself when you ask for a human agent… Their email is absolutely unreachable, and the only way to contact them is through a hotline, conveniently nowhere to be found on their website… Be absolutely aware of all of the fake reviews on here, and also be mindful this is coming from an exchange student who otherwise has had a decent experience with German bureaucracy at the Meldeamt and so on… Out of desperation I am writing this review, as I have tried so many different ways to get their attention… My next step I guess is to submit a formal complaint with Sutor Bank and their Ombudsmann…", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Hallo Fintiba.\nIt's been two day i have not gotten a response , could you kindly get back to me with the information for my review please.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Sehr geehrte Fintiba-Redaktion, ich schreibe Ihnen, da ich das genaue Datum der Gutschrift auf meinem Konto benötige, das seit September unberechtigterweise gesperrt ist. Diese Nachricht richtet sich an den Kontomanager, Herrn Arnold Sangonda. Wir benötigen dringend eine Lösung in dieser Angelegenheit. Vielen Dank.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Their 3rd party is very unprofessional. Constantly asking money and delaying the visa process", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I transferred money to my blocked account on 28 November 2025, but the funds still have not appeared. This delay is affecting my student visa process, and it’s becoming worrying.\nPlease check the status of my transfer and update me. Also, I kindly suggest improving the processing and communication speed, as long delays make it difficult for students to plan properly.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I’m extremely worried about the delayed review of my blocked account documents. When I first uploaded them, I had 13 days left—now I’m down to just 7, and this account is crucial for my student visa process. I still haven’t received an update, and missing this deadline could cost me my chance to begin my studies on time. This review is my last hope to reach someone who can help. Please update me as soon as possible.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "So there were a lot of glitches first with the OTP send on the email and send when i tried to download transfer details file it was downloading as a txt rather than a pdf", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Cant contact human and the chatbot is broken. Worse  customer support experience of my life.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Sehr geehrte Damen und Herren von Fintiba, Sie haben uns am 25. Oktober über die Rückerstattung informiert, diese ist jedoch noch nicht auf unserem Konto eingegangen. Die Bank hat Ihnen dies schriftlich bestätigt. Sie haben bereits drei Support-Tickets (1022119, 1044770, 1049009) eröffnet, leider ohne Erfolg. Nächste Woche wird der Fall von auf Finanzbetrug spezialisierten Anwälten geprüft. Wir wären Ihnen dankbar, wenn die Rückerstattung noch diese Woche eingehen würde, um rechtliche Schritte zu vermeiden. Wir erwarten Ihre Antwort. Vielen Dank.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am from one of the countries that allow visiting Germany with no visa and it is taking a while to obtain the documents for the longer visa however I now need access to my money. Therefore I tried uploading the documents I have to the bank to get my own money. However you need a specific stamp / document which I physically can not obtain. \n\nI tried reaching out through the document submittance but I keep getting the same automatic generic answer. \n\nSo I try to message the help bot and they give the same automatic generic answer.\n\nSo I try to call the helpline and they give the same automatic generic answer. They also mentioned they cannot do anything because they are not part of Fintiba.\n\nSo I email the helpline email and they give the same automatic generic answer. They did not even bother to read my issue otherwise they would see that their solution is not possible.\n\nOverall, I would strongly advise to avoid this company as if there are any issues they just cannot help and are unwilling to listen.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Two years ago, I opened a blocked account for my visa, and the whole process went very smoothly. However, it seems that the company has undergone major changes, because now I’m opening a blocked account again and almost nothing works! Fintiba itself is having huge issues with its website. I wasn’t able to link my phone number — I tried for about a week, but the site wouldn’t verify it because the buttons didn’t work. There were also problems with the payment. The thing is, transferring money to a Fintiba blocked account is completely non-transparent: you don’t send the money directly to your blocked account; instead, it goes through several different banks. This shouldn’t matter to you, but it does matter to the bank you’re sending the money from — they need to know where the funds are going. Since the process is completely non-transparent, you will have to spend a lot of time gathering information about the route your money takes and collecting documents that confirm it. I wasn’t able to do this because Fintiba itself does not explain the procedure anywhere — neither on the website nor through support — and for many foreign banks the transaction appears suspicious, even fraudulent.\n\nThere is also an issue with customer support. Most of the time, you’ll be speaking with an AI bot that gives silly, repetitive answers. To contact a real person, you’ll have to find their support email and phone number (it took me three days to find them). When you call support, the operator can’t do anything except submit a request — they have no authority to actually solve your problem. After that, a few days later, you’ll receive a response that doesn’t address your issue at all, because the staff apparently doesn’t even read the requests. The answers are similar to what the AI bot sends, and you’ll have to submit your request multiple times until you finally reach someone at least somewhat competent", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Hello and good time\nI have blocked my money twice at Fintiba. The first time, everything went very well. I have just blocked my money. I tried many times to confirm my account to receive money, but I haven't received a  message from you (mTAN) to confirm my account. I really really really need money. I sent email many times to support fintiba com during the last week, but my emails were not delivered. I sent massage many times on WhatsApp, but someone did not answer me. How can I contact support team? I did not receive any emails from you about confirmation of my account. Send me email send me email send me email. The bot can not solve my problem, it gave me repetitive answers. Send me email. Send email me. I am waiting for you", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Do not recommend Fintiba or any other their services including Isnurance. Be aware\n\nI am extremely disappointed with Fintiba’s support and reliability. A very simple issue with my blocked account documents has remained unresolved for more than two weeks, despite multiple requests and clear explanations from my side.\n\nThe Account Statement and Blocking Confirmation in my Fintiba account do not reflect the actual balance of my account (topped up), and no corrected version has been issued — even though this document is critical for my German visa procedure. I explained it and provided proofs. \n\nWhen visa authorities set strict deadlines, such delays will directly jeopardise the entire application process. I submitted a hundred of inquires to Fintiba within the 2 weeks. Still not solved. \n\nI didn’t not receive any proper replies and resolutions. But at least they started to work on my request. After 2 weeks and 100+ inquiries they started to read and work  \n\nAdditionally, Fintiba has not properly addressed my inquiry regarding my last additional transfer, even though I provided the MT103. I am still without confirmation of where the payment is and whether it was processed correctly by Sutor Bank.\n\nSumming up important point for future applicants:\n\nIf your embassy may require any adjustments to the blocked amount (and you cannot predict that, so it can), the process through Fintiba would be challenging, extremely slow and complicated and with no support. \n\nFintiba may be acceptable if you only need to deposit a fixed monthly amount once (e.g., 1,000 EUR) and never request changes, but if your consulate asks for modifications — whether due to updated requirements or additional financial checks — Fintiba is not the best option. you should consider other providers.\n\nFintiba is not reliable and may ruin your visa application.\n\nCommunication with support in my experience has been slow and non-transparent, and support tickets have been closed without resolving the issue, sometimes they replied to a questions I never asked…never solving my questions. This is especially frustrating because applicants rely on Fintiba for time-sensitive, legally required financial documentation.\n\nWhen I called them, the support manager on a line told me that she is not able to help with anny issue and all support via email. Ok. Why you present telephone of the support line when it is not a support line?\n\nSo bearing in mind how they work with banking issues I am happy I didn’t work with them as Insurance.\n\nConsider any other option for blocked account. Fintiba is not reliable and acts like a fraud", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Fintiba’s bot-based support system is not very effective. Even in the app, there is no phone number or email address provided for contacting real support. This makes it difficult to ask for help when needed.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Send me email\n\nYour company is fraud", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Very poor service, the whole blocked account for students setup is absolutely awful and putting students in a incredibly vulnerable position. I ticked the box that said no health insurance (as this is not required for the country I'm from), and wanted to get the basic cheapest account but found out that Fintiba had purposfully added a very small checkbox that's almost completely unnoticable (obviously on purpose) that meant that I was signed up for extra things that I didn't want and couldn't afford to pay extra for. This is incredibly exploitative and took months to sort out after many calls and emails (I ended up having to pay extra anyway!). Annoyingly, the customer service people kept putting my ticket in as 'resolved' when it obviously was not. This is so frustrating and puts extra stress on an already stressful situation", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have applied for block account today and I have not got transfer Document yet. THERE IS NO WAY I CAN CONNECT WITH THE TEAM. its really frustrating when you try to do things at utmost perfection but didn't get any result", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The service started well. The website is easy to navigate and the initial setup process was clearly guided.\nHowever, serious problems arose during the VISA verification stage. For students who require a VISA to study in Germany, the process is straightforward: obtain the VISA in your home country and upload it to the website. In our case, my daughter comes from a country that does not require a VISA but instead needs a residence permit. Here, the process became unclear and unnecessarily complicated.\nFirst, Fintiba requested an entry stamp in the passport. Since we drove into the Schengen zone via France, this was rejected, and they insisted on a German border stamp — essentially only obtainable through an airport entry. My daughter had to fly in and out just to get this stamp. Even then, we were told it was insufficient and were asked to provide a copy of the Fiktionsbescheinigung.\nI uploaded both front and back sides of the document, but because they were in two separate files, the submission was rejected again. This rigid requirement has caused months of delay, and my daughter has been unable to access her blocked account for over three months.\nCommunication from Fintiba has been limited to automated rejection emails, with no access to a real support person — only an AI chatbot.\nOverall, what began as a promising service turned into a deeply frustrating experience once our case did not fit the standard path. If your journey follows the typical visa process, Fintiba may work for you. But if your situation deviates from the norm, they do not offer the support and guidance you need.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have been a Fintiba customer for a long time and already had an active blocked account. On **17 November**, we transferred an additional amount required by the German Embassy for my visa process.\n\nToday is **26 November** — **10 days later** — and the money is *still not credited*.\n\nFor **three working days**, not a single employee responded to my emails, even though I clearly explained that my situation is urgent and the Embassy requires an updated account balance.\n\nThen on **24 November**, I finally received a message from Fintiba confirming that **the amount had arrived** and that my monthly amount was updated. They also informed me that I would receive my new blocking confirmation within **1–2 days**.\n\nHowever, on **26 November**, another employee replied stating that **the money has NOT arrived** — completely contradicting the previous message.\n\nMy bank confirms that the funds have been successfully sent, and I also attached their official confirmation to my message. Still no clear answer.\n\nThis level of inconsistency, long delays, and contradictory communication is absolutely unacceptable, especially when people depend on these documents for visa appointments. Fintiba’s disorganized support and conflicting responses have put me at risk of missing my visa deadline.\n\nI hope Fintiba will finally take responsibility and resolve this issue immediately.\nFintiba ticket Id 1053407", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Wir haben noch keine Antwort bezüglich einer Lösung für das im vorherigen Bericht erwähnte Problem erhalten.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Dear Fintiba Support Team,\nI hope this email finds you well.\nI am writing to request an urgent update regarding the status of my Fintiba account. I am concerned that the current long-standing \"PENDING\" status is causing a delay in my German visa application preparations.\nThe following items are currently still pending:\n\nBlocked Account (Sperrkonto)\n• Status: I completed the required transfer.\n• Concern: I am still awaiting confirmation of the transfer and the final issuance of the blocked account confirmation document.\n\nThank you very much for your prompt attention to this urgent matter.\n\nName:Koshi Ono\nSupport Code:", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "System suppose.me as a student ..But i am not.System.blocked.my progress. Help desk is just bot account. Reaching.the.support.really though.Bot can not clarify the issue.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I live in Pakistan, they run an ad on YouTube and i joined their zoom meeting webinar. But they were speaking in Russian, so why you sent me the email then for......\nEnglish is the main language and you held webinar in Russian language and send me email.... I don't know Russian....", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Very poor service. I am deeply disappointed and mentally harrased by fintiba and its hidden policies. You said you gave me free travel insurance by the name of \"MAWISTA visum\". But you hid the fact from me that you are also giving me \"MAWISTA Visum Comfort\" which covers liability insurance at the hefty premium of 160 euros that too for just six months. I will have to pay 160 euros again for the next six months. I never ordered this MAWISTA Visum Comfort insurance policy. When I asked MAWISTA to cancel it they say it is part of the package so you talk directly to Fintiba. I already have the \" IAS liability\" insurance with a premium of 60 euros with monthly deduction of only 5 euros. Now I have double liability insurance. Please cancel the \"MAWISTA Visum Comfort\" policy as you forcefully and deceptively gave me this unwanted insurance policy. I just want to keep the \"MAWISTA Student Classic\" health insurance to which I willingly agreed to pay the premium. This is so much exploitation and harassment by fintiba with hidden policies, packages and fees. If you do not cancel the MAWISTA Visum Comfort insurance policy I will have to complain to appropriate german and indian authorities. I am writing you a special email in this regard.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Sehr geehrte Damen und Herren von FINTIBA, ich schreibe Ihnen bezüglich des fälschlicherweise gesperrten Kontos, das Sie angeblich am 24. Oktober 2025 unter der Referenznummer 0119a053304d3pU3 gekündigt haben. Ich möchte Sie darüber informieren, dass die Gelder nicht bei der Bank eingegangen sind. Die offizielle Antwort des Finanzinstituts, die ich Ihnen per E-Mail zugesandt habe, ist beigefügt. Es ist empörend, dass Sie die Verantwortung für die Nachverfolgung der Überweisung bis zum Kontoinhaber nicht übernehmen, insbesondere da Sie irrtümlicherweise das Konto eines EU-Bürgers gesperrt haben. Die Anwälte meiner Familie sammeln derzeit Informationen, um rechtliche Schritte einzuleiten. Sie erhalten eine entsprechende Benachrichtigung. Ich bitte Sie daher, die Gelder umgehend nachzuverfolgen. Ich stehe Ihnen gerne zur Verfügung.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "A month in Germany, PR Emails without activation of my account. Fintiba can do better than this\n\n13th Nov -Hello,\n\nThank you for your E-mail.\n\nAs per our banking partner, you will be legitimated tomorrow and would be able to set up your payouts.\n \nWe appreciate and thank you for your patience and understanding,\n\nWe hope we could help you with this information. \n\nBest regards. \nYour Fintiba Team\n\n\n10th November-Hello\n \nThank you for your message.\n \nYou are in the process of Waiting for legitimation in Germany, you have to finish this step before you set up patouts.\n \nBR\n\n7th November\n\nwe are sorry for the delay in answering you quickly.\nPlease give us a little bit more time to process your ticket xxx adequately 🙂\n\nWith ❤️ from Frankfurt\nYour Fintiba Team\n\n4th November,\n\nThank you so much for keeping in touch,\n \nWe are happy to tell you that we have just received your legitimation document and we have submitted it to Sutor Bank. We now have to wait for them to verify your legitimation. This usually takes 1-2 working days.\n \nAfterwards, you can connect your mobile phone number (if not done yet) and set up your payouts to your current account in the \"Blocked Account\" section of your Fintiba account.\n \nBest regards😊", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "My payment not in account I paid 6 days ago", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Rückerstattung nicht erhalten.\nDie von Ihnen angegebene Frist für die Rückerstattung der Anzahlung, die fälschlicherweise aufgrund meines EU-Bürgerstatus blockiert wurde, ist verstrichen, und wir haben die Rückerstattung nicht erhalten. Wir benötigen umgehend eine Antwort.\n\nVielen Dank.\nSugerencias", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ich brauche das Konto nicht mehr, aber um mein Geld erstattet zu haben dauert es Monate. Die Mitarbeiter sind sehr langsam und jeden Monat wurden EUR20 abgerechnet.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Terrible service experience from Fintiba summarised in 3 key points. \n\nFirstly, poor communication with the customer, my experience with Fintiba when something goes wrong was terrible. For instance, during my proof of funds process, I wasn’t sure what documents to submit because the website was so vague, it wasn’t until after 2 weeks long past the 5-7 working day that I felt that something was wrong and during this time Fintiba NEVER emailed or called me to inform me what was going wrong. Thus I had to email them so they inform me what documents I need to add. \n\nSecondly, Fintiba does not care about it’s customers, for instance my second issue, transferring of funds, I had to email them 3 times to make my case known to Fintiba, but the shocking thing is when I called them only then they have raised my urgent case to their manager. Thus the says if you don’t urge Fintiba they will just simply ignore you until they have some time to solve your case in the next month.                                           \n\nThirdly, Fintiba the time, it atrociously long for any problem to be resolved, as mentioned before, in the website or by email Fintiba says that it take around 2-3 working days but the real timeline is around 14-16 working days to resolve an issue. I might come out as impatient but 14 working days in 7 times the expected time. Utterly disappointing service from Fintiba. \nAdditionally, I’m still waiting for my money transfer issue to be resolved, and Fintiba has the audacity to charge me a service fee when I can’t even access my money. Outrageous. Disappointing. Incompetent. Inefficient.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I got an issue with double charging and mistaken certificates. I emailed the firm but still I have no answer or solution.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Sehr geehrte Damen und Herren, ich schreibe Ihnen, da mein Sohn seine Revolut-Rückerstattung noch nicht erhalten hat und das Geld dringend benötigt. Ich wäre Ihnen dankbar, wenn Sie sich mit der zuständigen Behörde in Verbindung setzen könnten, um die Freigabe seiner Ersparnisse zu veranlassen. Vielen Dank.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "No available guidance and unclear process and not user friendly app", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Email spam and misleading costs\n\nGot like 6 emails within the first 20 minutes of using this thing. Most importantly, they show a money amount for your initial transfer that is supposed to be \"all inclusive\" and after you send the money, you're notified that their fee was not included.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I’ve been facing payout delays with Fintiba almost every month, and it’s becoming unbearable. Every time, the transfer is delayed without any proper explanation, even though this is supposed to be an automated process.\n\nI rely on these payouts for my living expenses, and such repeated delays cause unnecessary stress and financial difficulties. I’ve contacted support multiple times, but the same issue keeps happening.\n\nIf my payout doesn’t arrive today, I’ll be escalating this matter through my lawyer. This kind of negligence is unacceptable for a financial institution. Customers deserve reliability and transparency — not repeated excuses.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Wouldn’t recommend. I’m a student who just arrived in Germany and was sent for Postident verification. It’s been over a week since I sent everything, and when I followed up, I was told it’s always slow and that they can’t influence the process  but then gave me a bunch of other options I could have been told about from the start. When I asked to try online verification again, they just repeated the same physical options, even after I explained that I don’t have time for that. Extremely frustrating, confusing process, and a total lack of consideration for people with limited time.\nAdditionally, I finally submitted the additional documents, was told to wait for a maximum of 2 working days for my account to be activated. I'm on the 3rd day,no email response,getting into the weekend without money in my account.\nThe complacency is a no for me.\n\nIt's a no for me.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am in Germany for almost 4 weeks and it was only yesterday when I found out that my picture and german address were not sent to Barmer. I had to call myself and send all the necessary information for my insurance card myself. Also I sent your Support Team several Emails about this topic and they were not helpful at all.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I bought Mawista Insurance+Fintiba Blocked Account Package. Mawista sent electronic notification to my university through Barmer MONTHS AFTER. My first request on JULY and problem solved on OCTOBER. I missed the enrolling deadline of the university and I had to sent several apology emails to the office. I could get my matriculation 2 months after my classmates. Top of that the hardest one is getting any answer from Mawista. I have sent several emails and I got only three response emails from them. None of them was attempted to explaining the situation OR at least suggesting any solution. All of them directed me to Fintiba Support. Then I wanted to cancel... Then I did not any answer again. Two weeks later I got an email which was demanding payment for insurance. My insurance had been activated finally! Through all this journey, it was not even active! Because I had to get my first PAYOUT from Fintiba. Appearantly nobody EVER CHECKED the situation of my insurance or my blocked account BEFORE RESPONDING MY \"WHAT IS GOING ON\" EMAILS. And nobody inform me about how the process would go on. I will DEFINITELY not recommend Fintiba to my circle. I even do not want to remember huge irresponsibility and ignorance of Mawista but... Weeks after they wrote another insane message: \"Electronic notifications is COMPULSORY ACROSS GERMANY, FOR ALL INSURANCE COMPANIES AND UNIVERSITIES BUT... WE DO NOT DO THAT! Apply any insurance company in person which does this and KINDLY REQUEST them to send M10 to your university\". I stared at the screen a few seconds to digest it.. Why you were so late to respond and why I would COVER YOUR LACK OF ORGANIZATION. I pay money to you for getting your things together! Shame on you!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "It appears that choosing to pay via bank transfer results in an unjustified delay in payment confirmation. This raises the concern that Fintiba intentionally discourages this method, given that it does not yield the additional ~1% conversion margin obtained through other payment options.\nIn addition, the app failed during the “preparing your documents” stage, forcing me to abandon the app and complete the process through the website instead (Pixel 9 Pro — latest Android).\nAltogether, the experience reflects a lack of fairness and insufficient attention to customer usability.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Este 2025, con mi marido nos fuimos a Alemania de marzo a julio con la Chancenkarte y FINTIBA era la cuenta bloqueada que más nos recomendaban. Tuvimos el inicio y durante el proceso, muy mala experiencia. Primero, con el envío y recepción del dinero. Nosotros somos de Chile.\nTransferimos al rededor de 12.000 euros (que es mucho dinero para nosotros) a finales de diciembre, a una cuenta que Fintiba nos decia que era lo más rápido, con datos bancarios chilenos. Entendiamos que por ser fechas de fiestas, se podría demorar un poco más, pero pasaban las semanas, y no teniamos ninguna confirmación de la recepción del dinero. A todo esto, se supone que el trámite es de máximo 2 semanas, 3 en casos excepcionales. Cada vez que preguntábamos, el mail de ellos era como \"les pedimos que tengan paciencia, esto puede demorar, etc.\" Luego de más de un mes, vuelvo a escribir y me dicen que el dinero no ha llegado y que yo tengo que averiguar con mi banco. Fue terrible ya que estábamos a finales de enero y teníamos comprado el pasaje para marzo, sumado a que los trámites de Consulado son lentos y no avanzan sin el comprobante de la cuenta bloqueada con el dinero.\nLuego de hacer las investigaciones pertinentes, donde ellos NO ayudaron, descubrimos que habían 2 intermediarios: uno que recibía el dinero en Chile y lo mandaba a Europa (1), y el otro que lo recibía en Europa (TransferMate) (2) para luego, pasarlo a Fintiba. Sólo escribiéndole a Transfermate que fueron EXCELENTES, pudimos descubrir que el dinero nunca salió de Chile y se quedó estancado más de un mes. No podiamos entender cómo una empresa tan grande como Fintiba, que trabaja con distintos países, no hiciera el seguimiento correspondiente y nos dejara prácticamente solos. Transfermate en 3 dias solucionó todo.\nLuego, al llegar a Alemania (porque sí, lo logramos justo a tiempo), empezó otro problema: el primer pago no llegaba, más de un mes así. Ni a mi marido, ni a mi. Y nuevamente, nos decían que nosotros teníamos que averiguar con el banco qué estaba pasando. Abrimos otra cuenta de banco y ahí ya pudimos recibir el pago, el cual vino DOBLE no la primera vez (que se entendería por el atraso), sino los meses posteriores, lo que generaba un desajuste en nuestro orden. Yo entiendo que esto último puede parecer exagerado, pero ya era la gota que rebalsó el vaso.\nRealmente fue una muy mala experiencia, esto generó mucho estrés y malestar. Uno entiende que pueden ocurrir contratiempos, especialmente cuando se mezcla dinero y otros países, pero lo que más nos frustraba era la poca claridad y apoyo, pues si bien respondían los correos, estos o eran genéricos o nos decían que nosotros teníamos que resolver por nuestro lado.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "In the terms and conditions, I was forced to select that I want to open a bank account on Frankfurt International Bank and I will order a MasterCard and it will be charged according to the bank price list. Before checking them, I called the support that I don't want them, they told me you can check to open the account then you can email us to close the checking account and MasterCard. Then after opening, when I mailed them, they replied that \"It's mandatory and not possible\".", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am quite disappointed that I still cannot access my account details despite several requests raised through your help lines and the email I previously sent.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "i keep on receiving phone verification code after i connect my phone number", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ich danke Ihnen sehr dafür, dass anerkannt wurde, dass das Konto niemals eröffnet hätte werden dürfen, da ich ein europäischer Bürger bin und diese Verwaltung nicht benötige. Ich hoffe, dass Sie die Bankmittel so schnell wie möglich freigeben, da ich sie dringend benötige.  \nIch bleibe aufmerksam, danke.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "1. The software usage process is abnormal and very inconvenient,When I was trying to modify the frozen account balance, I got stuck in a process and couldn't use any other functions.\n2. The customer service staff responded very slowly and could not always give a comprehensive and thoughtful answer. I had to keep asking and waiting, and ultimately I did not get the results I wanted.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "They are not helpful at all. You call them and they be like: \"I'll open a ticket for you and they'll contact you in 24 hours\". After 24 hours, they be like:  \"I'll open an urgent ticket for you and they'll contact you in 24 hours\". After 24 hours, they be like:  \"I'll open another urgent ticket for you and they'll contact you in 24 hours\". This is a one end street, they are useless. Don't waste your time and energy.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Customer service is terrible. No one answers the phone, or they take forever to do so. This is the second time I’ve extended my account, and this time I’ve had to go through a bunch of extra steps that weren’t required the first time.\nOn top of that, they’re not transferring my money, but they are charging the fees — and even charging them twice. It’s simply horrible and unpleasant.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "How easy I can download the files. What really made my experience bad was the fact that I have little time before my visa appointment and processing my documents too long and transferring the money online with visa debit card getting failed and failed for no apparent reason when tho everything is matching \n\nHow it is gonna get fixed and processing documents gets faster", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am extremely disappointed with Fintiba. My name is Dimitri Kakoishvili, and as an exchange student, I rely on my monthly payout to cover basic living expenses. It has now been over a month since I was supposed to receive my money, and nothing has been transferred.\n\nI have sent more than 10 emails and made multiple phone calls, but I keep getting no real answer or solution. Every time I contact support, I’m either ignored or told to “wait,” while I’m literally struggling to afford food and daily essentials.\n\nThis kind of service is completely unacceptable, especially for a company that handles students’ blocked accounts and knows how important timely payments are. I’m honestly shocked at how unresponsive and unhelpful Fintiba has been throughout this entire process.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ive not become my monthly payout and i am trying to communicate with customer service but nobody is answering me either or emails or phone", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Waited whole September for my monthly payout as an exchange student its really hard for me to live like this even if the money comes 1 week later\nIts 1. October still waiting", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "What a waste of time this webinar was, spoke about the usual general headlines of the chancenkarte, didn’t add anything to the topic aside from the known general info \n\nAsked 2-3 questions no reply \n\nDid not discuss opportunities that we can seek \n\nIt was such a disappointment", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Even though transaction was completed and it showed up on the app, there's no transfer shown in an account statement, which is why I'm unable to get visa. I wrote to customer support multiple times, but it has been three weeks and no one helped me", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Negative Google-Bewertungen werden entfernt, dass bestätig wie wenig seriös dieses „Unternehmen“ ist. Leider unflexibel im Service, man kann nur 08/15 Anfragen bearbeiten für bekannte Prozesse. Wenn es um ein spezielles Anliegen geht, welches vom Standart Schema abweicht, meldet sich keiner zurück. Verlängerung des Kontos überhaupt nicht möglich", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "UI didn't user friendly", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Muhattap bulamadım Türkiye’de çalıştığınız (sipay)ödeme şirketi sitenizde bulunan hesap bilgilerinin güncel olmadığını ve yardım edemeyeceklerini söylediler bu yüzden işlerim aksadı çevremdeki insanlara ve sosyal medyada fintibayı önermeyeceğim", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Gave 3 stars because the info could be clearer at the start, maybe with pop-ups like “almost there, just fill this and that.” The worst part was that the payment took over 24h to process with no notice or countdown, the app just stayed silent. Still, the services work fine once ready. In summary, if the app was more user friendly about the process of setting up the account, making the transfer and receiving the money, I would review it as 5 stars", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Previous feedback: /reviews/68b5cb6d34f7aead1123fcbd\n\n\nEnglish:\nEven after all these days, my problem is still not solved. The official blocked account statement, which is essential for my residence permit, remains missing. Instead of real support, I am stuck in a cycle of automated replies and excuses. It is disappointing to see how a company handling such a crucial service for international students shows so little responsibility toward its customers.\n\nDeutsch:\nAuch nach all den Tagen ist mein Problem immer noch nicht gelöst. Das offizielle Sperrkonto-Dokument, das ich dringend für meinen Aufenthaltstitel benötige, fehlt weiterhin. Anstelle echter Unterstützung erhalte ich nur automatische Antworten und Ausreden. Es ist enttäuschend zu sehen, wie ein Unternehmen, das einen so wichtigen Service für internationale Studierende anbietet, so wenig Verantwortung gegenüber seinen Kund*innen zeigt.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Eine der schlechtesten Erfahrungen meines Lebens.\nSeit über einem Monat versuche ich, mein Sperrkonto zu verlängern. Trotz mehrmaliger E-Mails und Überweisungen bekomme ich widersprüchliche Informationen und keine klare Lösung. Jeder Tag kostet mich Zeit, Geld und verursacht Stress mit der Ausländerbehörde. Absolute Intransparenz und fehlende Zuverlässigkeit. Nicht empfehlenswert!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I opened my blocked account on 26.08.2025 and transferred the required amount. Due to a technical error, the balance was displayed twice. Unsurprisingly, this issue – their own financial problem – was solved immediately. Suddenly, everything worked smoothly: no delays, no repetitive responses, just instant resolution.\n\nBut when it comes to my official blocked account statement, the story changes completely. I have been waiting for days, even though I urgently need this document for my residence permit. Each time I contact customer service, I receive the same copy-paste reply: “please wait 24 hours.” These 24 hours keep repeating endlessly.\n\nThe impression is crystal clear: when it’s about their money, things move fast and without obstacles. When it’s about the customer’s needs, especially critical documents, you’re left in a loop of empty promises. For a company that depends on international students, the priorities are clearly in the wrong place.\n\n-----------------------------\nDeutsch:\n\nIch habe am 26.08.2025 mein Sperrkonto eröffnet und den Betrag überwiesen. Durch einen technischen Fehler wurde der Betrag doppelt angezeigt. Dieses Problem – also ihr eigenes finanzielles Problem – war selbstverständlich sofort gelöst. Da ging es plötzlich sehr schnell, kein Warten, keine Standardantworten, alles innerhalb kürzester Zeit erledigt.\n\nGanz anders sieht es bei meinem offiziellen Sperrkonto-Dokument aus. Seit Tagen warte ich darauf, obwohl ich es dringend für meinen Aufenthaltstitel benötige. Jedes Mal, wenn ich den Kundenservice kontaktiere, bekomme ich nur die identische Antwort „bitte warten Sie 24 Stunden“. Diese 24 Stunden scheinen sich endlos zu wiederholen.\n\nDer Eindruck ist eindeutig: Sobald es um Ihr Geld geht, funktioniert alles reibungslos und ohne Verzögerung. Geht es aber um die Anliegen der Kund*innen, insbesondere um dringend benötigte Dokumente, dann zeigt sich eine endlose Hinhaltetaktik. Für ein Unternehmen, das von Studierenden abhängig ist, sollte die Priorität eigentlich umgekehrt sein.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I booked a payment request through Fintiba Transfer, but I would now like to transfer the funds to my blocked account using a Regular International Bank Transfer instead. I have sent email to Finitba and there is no response, it was written on Fintiba website that this booking only remain for 48 hours and more than 3 days passed and the booking is still the same.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Honestly, I make the transfer today for 4 times, every time the transfer is returned to my account, and the bank customer service assured that the problem is with the receiver account, FIB Frankfurt international bank AG, I want to blame on fintiba for this massive mistake, this is a waste our time, money and effort.\nReally the service of fintiba is disgusting", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "My money has been in my account since 8/20 and it has been almost a week (8/26) and you still cannot provide me with a blocking confirmation for my visa procedure while you advertise this only takes about 10 minutes and the longest is 24 hours? When I send email for my problem (several times), Fintiba just send generic template responses instead of reading my email and trying to solve the problem :)", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "They offer good services even though I still wonder why I found it difficult to do some things on the app smoothly. And why I cannot reuse my intact money that I blocked to do an extension without opening an entire new one.\nI understand it's for them to make profit....but that's totally weird.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Horrible transfer company selection, very slow and unresponsive. outdated UI and files on website. Awful customer team with copy paste answers and not even reading questions. I wish I chose Expatrio over Fintiba.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I transferred money from my current account to Fintiba blocked account, but unfortunately it went to their organization TransferMate IBAN. Since July Fintiba has been taking me round about this money telling me that they contacted TransferMate and told them that the money belongs me. The next time Fintiba is trying to force me to close my account with them yet my money is still pending. Finitba themselves also have some of my money. I have been calling Fintiba ever since and they give me same stories, we are working on it. At some point I talked to a very rude lady I can not remember her name. Fintiba please let your partner release my money then you transfer all my money not what you want to do to me.  I am very disappointed with your services.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The insurance coverage didn't start at time, stuck processing. Mawista tried to withdraw 115 euro from me for this insurance that should be free.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "One of the banks for your blocked account, that i would personally not recommend, im so tired of them. You might definetely have problems with them and the customer service was not good in my opinion at all here. They do not care about your problem at all in my opinion. Please do your self a favor and read more reviews. Personally, I was devastated waiting for my money for a very long time without being able to pay for anything.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The were some mistakes, such as the health insurance start date was written 1-11-2025 while my study starts on 1-10-2025. And the M10 notification still hasn't been sent to the University.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The two host provldea datailed Presentation They ansere alltheauestins satisdatorily", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "awesome it is nice experience forme lmeans it acurate and easyto follow back if all the othe apps are desingned this way.everyone will surely.Love to use App like fintiba apps always lappre ciate somuc", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Fees are not stated clearly from the beginning. And the bank details for the transaction are not clear enough.\nI wanted to transfer the money by my euro debit card issued from Egypt but the option wasn't available, the site only provided a transaction with EGP with very high exchange rate", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "En sí es una buena plataforma para la cuenta bloqueada, pero en el momento que hay un problema, algo que no cuadra, es pésimo. Tienen a una señorita que responde el teléfono en inglés que no sirve de mucho y aparte es grosera. No entiende cómo tratar a la clientela. Todo tarda innecesariamente demasiado. Yo estoy sumamante disgustada con la atención al cliente de Fintiba.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I had trouble with:\n1. Creating an user account\n2. Opening up a blocked account\n3. Can't find direct customer support -- all it gives me are chatbots and german numbers/schedules (which are waay out of my timezone).", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I used Fintiba to extend my blocked account, and to be fair — the automated process works well once everything is in place. I eventually received my extension documents and was able to move forward.\n\nBut the customer service experience was a huge disappointment.\n\nMy transfer took 8 business days, which is significantly longer than the typical timeframe for a bank transaction. During that time, Fintiba support offered no real help — just empty affirmations like “please be patient” while showing no real urgency or ownership of the issue.\n\nI don’t expect support staff to fix complex backend problems instantly, but I do expect communication, updates, and some accountability. Instead, Fintiba simply kept pushing the blame to TransferMate — but as a customer, I didn’t choose TransferMate.\nThey are Fintiba’s partner, not mine.\n\nIf something goes wrong in a process that starts on your own platform, you should at least own it and inform your customers properly — not leave them in the dark while their residence permit is on the line.\n\nGlad it worked out in the end, but the trust is damaged.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "WE HAVE ALMOST 1 WEEK TRYING TO GET A \n A BLOQUED ACCOUNT . THE TIME AND THE GUIDANCE IT  IS NOT CLEAR.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Very late response to urgent messages. and the IBan I got shows me error, there is some problem with the iban. I had waited a lot and had to change from Fintiba to another bank.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have a huge problem here. My block account didn't become active yet. My transfer didn't come to my block account. I don't know why but I can not solve the problem. Help me!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The Fintiba app and website are convenient to use. Everything is accurate and fast, but the support group is awful. I have written several emails because I had an unusual situation and had some problems with payment. The answers were rude or it felt that way for me, and I never got a proper answer. My problems were never resolved, so I had to ask ChatGPT for help....", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Next time you can collaborate and bring in representatives from some of the universities to offer more  scholarships tips", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "资金到账太慢了，expatrio上午打款，下午到账。你们同样操作，几天都不能到。严重影响我的签证官进度。", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I been trying to contact you because of the transfer that I need to make but the app keep asking me for my social Security number, which I don’t have because I am not from the US, the person who transfer the money is from the US but I am not, and because of this question of MY social security number (which I don’t have) I can’t proceed to put the info of the person transferring the money, and I got no answer from you.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Used Fintiba for the second time, this time was a disaster. The fee breakdown made no sense, and customer service couldn’t explain it. Worst part: Fintiba Plus advertised cheap insurance with Mawista, but we got stuck with DAK at €139/month before even arriving in Germany. Couldn’t cancel, locked in for 12 months, and now paying €260/month post-graduation. Support was dismissive and unhelpful. Fintiba Plus is absolutely not worth it.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Support people more about transfer progress.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am a Chinese undergraduate trying to get my locked account. I chose this company by the recommendation of Rednote. However, the guidance of app is really horrible and the link is unstable. Although there is a WeChat service to answer my questions, I prefer seeing the guidance directly from the beginning of the process. It indeed solved my problem, but I feel hard and ambiguous finishing all the tasks. Hope your team will improve it.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "If I could give it 0 zero stars I would. Absolute disorganised and horrible treatment of account holders. Delays after delays to release the money. I submitted the documents they require to release the money, then they said actually they need a different document and find some reason to claim that the documents are not enough only after I've provided what they asked for, and kept on raising the bar after I met it again and again.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "After paying Fintiba’s monthly fees since November without complaints, I was shocked by how my experience ended. According to their own policy, the blocked account should automatically close after the last regular payout – in my case, May 31st. Despite this, they delayed the final transfer to June 2nd and used that delay as an excuse to charge me an extra, unjustified monthly fee.\n\nThis is not just poor service – it’s a clear case of manipulation and lack of transparency. They took advantage of the fact that the account still had a small balance to force one last fee without providing any service in return.\n\nSuch behavior shows zero integrity and is the opposite of what international students need when trusting a financial service. I will make sure to warn others and strongly discourage using Fintiba unless no other option is available.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I need a blocked account for a formal obligation (Verpflichtungserklärung). I am not a student, nor am I the one who applies for a visa. The process is not made for my requirements, although the website said it is easily possible. In the end I had to pay another 1700 Euros on top, which I hope I'll get back once my visitor leaves the country.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "You are not responsible. Shame on you", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "You are slow and there is a big problem about your payment methods. Yes, the option to pay in local currency is nice but this is a major disadvantage for currencies with high exchange rates. For example, in Turkey, as long as you apply for a foreign currency account statement from your contracted Turkish bank, you can pay directly in Euros with your credit cards (without converting to Turkish Lira at the current exchange rate). This way, if you already have euros, the current exchange rate does not affect you.\nBut TransferMate only converts to local currency for card payment options. Supporting withdrawals in euros while redirecting to the payment page will make a big difference for your company. I recommend you to take these words into consideration because this is a detail for you to gain a good customer base from Turkey.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ich bin äußerst enttäuscht von Fintiba. Trotz vollständiger Einzahlung meines Sperrkontos und fristgerechter Legitimation wurde mein Geld nicht freigegeben – und das, obwohl ich dringend darauf angewiesen bin, um mein Studium in Deutschland antreten zu können.\n\nMehrere Kontaktversuche blieben unbeantwortet oder führten nur zu automatisierten Reaktionen. Die Bearbeitung verzögert sich seit Wochen ohne nachvollziehbaren Grund. Der Kundenservice wirkt überfordert oder ignoriert kritische Anfragen gezielt.\n\nDas Verhalten ist aus meiner Sicht nicht nur unprofessionell, sondern grenzt an Verantwortungslosigkeit – insbesondere, wenn es um so sensible Themen wie Studienaufenthalte und finanzielle Existenzsicherung geht.\n\nIch kann Fintiba daher leider nicht empfehlen.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "So many awful steps, low quality help along the way, my funds are still freezed, i can't pay my rent. I stareted this process over a month ago and still having issues. worst experience.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I need mail support ID", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Just making excuses not to refund me .I am tired of back and forth with fintiba by email.still not resolving my case 😡😡😡😡😡😡😡😡😡😡😡😡😡😡😡", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Not willing to help me, poor customer service experience in my life ,the worst ever ,only creat excuses to prolong refund. I Will never recommend to any one Fintiba they recive deposits in one day but not willing to refund. Additionally deined my evidence.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "They activated travel insurance with mawista for free and when I changed the insurance to Techniker Krankenkasse and requested the cancellation of mawista health insurance, they said the travel insurance is not free any more and I have to pay 170 Euros for something I did not use and was not aware of having it in the first place.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "my experince about paying system was terrible. Still I am waiting for the amount and I have visa tomorrow", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ich habe bei Fintiba widerrufen,die Registrierung zurueckgezogen.Ich bekomme Zahlungsaufforderungen von unbekannten Absendern  mit der Zahlungsaufforderung ueber die Summe,die ich haette bei Fintiba hinterlegen sollen.Warnung.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The company is doing well in orientation of both existing and potential customers. \nUnfortunately the delay in visa application in my country is 😭\nSecondly the demand for proof for my source of money despite its appearance on the statement of account is discouraging. Was rejected initially until a more stressful and legal validation was used before it was finally accepted.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Time of asking questions is very short", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Please answer my questions from the question and answers", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Your offer:a blocked account for Minors.As a matter of fact:NOT available.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "There is no good info in Russian. Alsovery dificult to find info regarding opening block account for minor by Parent", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "If I could give it 0 zero stars I would. Fintiba has continued to be the most stressful part of my stay abroad — a service that’s supposed to support international students has only caused me unnecessary anxiety, delays, and damage.\nI was left without access to any of my blocked funds for almost 10 days, unable to use my own money in a foreign country. There was no proper explanation, no sense of urgency — just silence, false promises and stress over what eventually turned out to be a “simple IT issue.”\nTheir handling of the health insurance side was just as careless. I signed up for Fintiba Plus —their “all-in-one” service— and got nothing but chaos in return.  From failing to inform me that there was an issue with my health insurance for weeks (until I found out myself), to signing me up with different providers without my consent, to their faulty system messing up my already active health insurance—insurance I had to practically fix myself.\n\nFintiba markets itself as a streamlined solution for international students —but my experience has been the exact opposite.\nFintiba Plus was a huge letdown, and the stress it caused me is something I wouldn’t wish on anyone.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Please specify well that it takes time for CERTAIN HIGH RISK COUNTRIES to get their blocking confirmation. The supposed reason I used fintiba is the speed, this defeats the whole purpose, AFTER making payment then you're showing it may take up to 2 weeks, that's crazy", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "charged me more than 30 month administration fee without asking and my permission, just like a robbery", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Misleading information (just before transferring the money it was clear that it is only for students etc.), no response from service desk", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I wanted to see drop down buttons for the various visa purposes or types. Looks like the platform is specially designed for blocked accounts of international students visa application. I wanted to see the chancenkarke", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "It's been more than 5 business days and my money hasn't appeared in my account.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Very confusing platform with very minimal communication of which steps I should follow. No clear guidance.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I recently had a terrible experience with them. I blocked some money for my residence permit as a job seeker visa and it accidently went into the category of declaration of commitment. I asked them to please allow me to make payouts and despite calling and writing to them several times, they were entirely unhelpful. I would not recommend them at all.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Dear Sir/Madam,\nI hope this message finds you well.\n\nFirst, I would like to thank you for your service.\nSetting up the account was fast and easy but asking the user to transfer a large amount of cash in a single transfer is difficult to achieve and increases risk.\nI saw that the reason for the forementioned condition was to prevent money laundering, but as an economics expert and as someone who lived in a 3rd world country for years, I tell you that this condition does nothing but make the user experience worse.\nI’m happy to discuss this further over a meeting if needed.\n\nKindest regards.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "My request is still pending", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "mein fruher mawista comfort Versicherung falsche Abzueg werden nach viele Tage noch nicht zuruckgegeben.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Das Geld für das Sperrkonto wurde von meiner GmbH überwiesen und das Geld wird nicht freigegeben. Die Bank von Fintiba möchte den Nachweis über die Herkunft des Geldes haben. Ich kann jedoch aus datenschutzrechtlichen Gründen den Nachweis nicht erbringen. Nach langem Hin und Her (Schlechter Service komme nicht klar rüber, was sie wollen, immer der Standard \"bitte laden Sie neue Dokumente hoch\"), habe ich jetzt das Konto gekündigt und ich hab gelesen, vermutlich habe ich sehr viel Probleme bis ich mein Geld wiederhabe wir werden sehen.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Somehow there is a technical issue and the transaction has been sent but I did get only one confirmation for one transaction and the other one not although it shows and reflects in the balance and that issue has delayed the issue of the blocked account confirmation.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Very unprofessional, did not inform me about health insurance regulations , did not add important points into contract ( Visa application document ). So my experience with Fintiba is worst. Better choose Expatrio.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I requested to close my account a long time ago cause I no longer needed to go to Germany. The money reversal it’s a nightmare and the customer support staff is the most inneficient and unprofessional that I’ve dealt with, its been over a month and they do not give me a specific reason why the reversal transfer is not approved\nIn the meantime, they keep charging 5€ a month for “account maintenance”", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Out of service this website", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Nice wow good thanks", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "El servicio al cliente es basura. \nHe esperado semanas en recibir el dinero. Y Servicio al cliente responde en 3 días si tienes suerte.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Suggestion for Improving the FintiI am a user of Fintiba Plus and would like to share some suggestions for improving the platform. Currently, I am experiencing difficulties setting up my account because I am not enrolled in a university but only in a language course at IIK Bayreuth, which starts on March 10, 2025. The system does not allow me to enter this information, causing uncertainty when making the deposit, especially due to the high amount of money involved.\nI believe it would be beneficial for many users to have more flexible and specific options for those attending language courses and not full university programs. Additionally, it would be ideal to receive support in Spanish for those who are not fluent in English or German, making it easier to understand and use the platform.ba Plus Platform", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "It would be better if you give more Details about blocked acount’s and how should we make it or what it need", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I was not able to create two accounts for my two kids, and when my wife tried to make an account with the passport number of my second child, the system wouldn't let her do, because it says that \"the passport is already being used in one account\". We lost some days to fix the problem.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The only problem i faced is am unable to upload my transfer proof in the Fintiba app and website on web as i chose a bank transfer option", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Jedes Mal, wenn ich ein Konto schließen möchte, erhalte ich die Bitte um weitere Dokumente: zuerst einen Kontoauszug und dann eine Online-Passüberprüfung.\n\nBei der Kontoeröffnung wurde mir gesagt, dass ich mein Geld problemlos zurückerhalten würde, wenn etwas passieren würde. In Wirklichkeit verzögern und erschweren sie die Rückerstattung des Geldes so weit wie möglich.\n\nIch habe die Kontobestätigung bereits zweimal eingereicht und wurde online anhand meines Reisepasses verifiziert. Jetzt fragen sie nach meiner Adresse und den Tag des Visumsbeginns. Auf die Frage, warum sie diese Informationen benötigen, antworten sie: Ja, wir benötigen diese Informationen nicht. Wir haben keine Anfrage zur Schließung Ihres Kontos erhalten. \n\nObwohl sie erst vor wenigen Tagen bestätigten, dass sie Dokumente zur Kontoauflösung akzeptiert hatten.\nJetzt fragen Sie endlos nach zusätzlichen Dokumenten.\n\nIch rate niemandem, sich an diese Organisation zu wenden.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "1. I accidentally confirmed the a liability insurance order without reviewing the contract or payment details—The page was misleading — just few words with a \"Confirm\" button, and once I clicked it, the order was immediately processed, leaving me with no chance to check anything beforehand. —everything happened so fast! \n2. Then came the nightmare of trying to cancel. I contacted both Fintiba and the insurance company, but neither was helpful. I ended up sending multiple emails, but no one took real action. After a week of frustration, I finally received an email from Fintiba today: \"Your liability insurance has been successfully activated!\"\n\nThis whole process felt like a scam. What a nightmare!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I already have an another insurance and fintiba give me mawista insurance i don't like to have it and its cost 25€ per month i can't afford that", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Fintiba web page has an error, it took a couple of days to solve it. It causes a delay in my blocked account process. Even though the personal was very kind and very supportive.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "It took around 3 weeks just to link my current and blocked account and they never even followed up if the issue was resolved.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "So bad communication", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Extrem negative Erfahrung, viel Druck wenn es darum geht das Geld auf das Sperrkonto zu überweisen, dann aber langsamer service und es dauert ewig, das Geld wieder aus dem Sperrkonto zu bekommen, fast wie ein Betrugssystem.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Not helpful at all, even make more troubles! I want to close my account, I've written so many emails, however, no solution. I don't understand why you don't help me, I am in trouble and confused every day. What is wrong with you? Or you don't want to reture my money back. Why my problem won't be solved?", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Honest. Good hard work", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "They are faster than the alternatives for student blocked account but still waaay to improve. My process took 10 days including several errors just because they had not noticed a detail in my documents or even didn't see the email attachment!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I haven't recieved the 31. Okt. 2024 13:13 update, I knew about it only by accident from the letter with the rating request.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Inputting my contact phone number is a difficult thing now", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Very poor service and customer service behaviour. I don’t want your block account service I want my money back.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Your services is really good.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "This website is very help full \nAnd  I am very happy to connect\nWith fintiba", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The only problem I had was thé vérification process. It takes too long. You guys could make the vérification a one step thing instead of 4 or 5 steps", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Worst identification process , I kept waiting all day for an employee and when they show up, if they don't hear you in one second they hang up, I still haven't had my identification since yesterday, shame for such a developed company", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I’ve had some troubling issues with fintiba \nAnd bailey in the office tried her best to give us a solution \n\nThe company could be more efficient it has taken me more than 3 weeks of stress and still haven’t got any money in my account yet", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "1- in the registration flow you force the user to register with Fintiba plus by showing two questions about the insurance and giving join with insurance a priority by making it the main CTA\n2- even when the user discover that he can't convert to basic account through the web/Mobile app he needs to contact the support team by Email -not even by support button -\n3- you don't provide CS team in weekend so that's mean if you have short time he need to go with the plus plan to complete his blocked account\n4- if the user forced to pay the blocked account he can't convert to basic anymore he lose this option \nYou use design dark patterns to force the user to pay more to get more profit and you don't care about user time or money", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "because my wife's initial registration was wrongly registered and it was automatically filled in wrongly without our fault", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "How can i cancaled my healt Insurance", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I changed university 2 days ago and they initiated my registration again at the same university", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Conflicting instructions. The application offers and allows you to top up a blocked account to apply for a ‘Chancenkarte’ using Fintiba Transfer, but the instructions on the website and FintiBot on the app state that this solution is only for international students and not available to applicants for job-seeker visas or residence permit applicants.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Fintiba Team generally has been wonderful. However today I got a nasty reception from the person who attended to me when I put in a call to express my frustration about the trial and error account validation process. Instead of highlighting all the issues and getting me to address them at once, the Sutor Bank keep rejecting my account with a different reason very seemingly unjustifiable. I uploaded salary account statement and I was told salary cannot be traced in the statement when flow pattern is highlighted. I uploaded identity documents  documents of my sponsor but because of name ordering, I was told it's a mismatch as if someone can send money to an account and failed to identify himself", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "it takes too long to be verified", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "After signing up they said they need a selfie with holding your passport, but before signing up they didn't mentioned it a little bit. If you ask them that you cannot take it because of the passport is at the embassy, they then revoked your account and you can't using it anymore.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Wir warten seit Monaten trotz Freigabe auf die Rücküberweisung nach Visa -Wechsel.\nBei jedem Telefonat wird versprochen dass es innerhalb von 2 Tagen überwiesen wird. Diese Bank ist nicht seriös und wir warnen vor einer Zusammenarbeit.\nWir warten auf 7000 EUR sein April 2024", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Awful with everthing worst service ever", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Es ist äußerst unangenehm den Antrag auszufüllen, weil man zu Beginn nicht weiß welche Informationen abgefragt werden. Warum sind nicht alle Fragen auf einer Seite? Wenn man diesen Prozess des Ausfüllens des Antrages beginnt, möchte man wissen welche Informationen benötigt werden. Statt dessen tauchen ständig neue unerwartete Fragen auf, so dass man diesen Prozess immer wieder neu starten muss, weil man sich nicht auf die Frage einstellen konnte. Mein Vorschlag: Beim Ausfüllen des Antrages: Alle Fragen auf eine Seite!\nWeiterhin wusste ich nachdem ich dann den Antrag abgesendet hatte wie es weitergeht. Was passiert jetzt? Eine Weile stand dort ein Button zur Passbeglaubigung, nach vielleicht einer Stunde ging er weg und es kamen die Buttons zum Einzahlen des Geldes. Das führte bei mir sehr zur Verwirrung. Außerdem sind sie das teuerste Unternehmen, welches Sperrkonten anbietet. Ich hab es nur genommen, weil sie eine deutsche Firma sind mit einer deutschen Bank.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Very slow process!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "1. Unable to change password. I have to log in every single time using 'forgot my password'. I followed the instructions from Fintibabot and customer support, but it's not working. They said, there is an option to change the password under the Profile section. THERE IS NO OPTION UNDER THE PROFILE SECTION TO CHANGE PASSWORD!!!!\n2. I made a request to transfer money to the Fintiba Blocked account using Transfermate. However, after some concerns related to hidden fees, I decided to transfer internationally directly to the bank account. In the meantime, Fintiba or transfermate keeps sending me emails to remind me to transfer money with Transfermate. I wanted to cancel this request. However, AGAIN, there is nowhere to be found an option to cancel this request. The instructions from Fintibabot (the only one available to support you) are inconsistent, and not helpful. The problems are unsolved. \nI wonder if Fintiba even tested this bot and the UX design of the app and website prior to launching. Because this is frustrating!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I tried 5 times for two days and all was failed due to technical issue. It was so long to get connected back. It needed patience and encourage to complete the process. I also hope the staff could be more friendly and patience. Importantly, all is done now.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I waited for the whole meeting time for on boarding but no one let me in", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Undoubtedly the worst customer service known to man. \nYou can only reach out via email that replies within 3 days. And none of them seem to care to focus on your specific case at hand.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Incomplete transfer information", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "verification process too slow", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I should be giving Fintiba one star for holding my money and not wiring it to my account. But i give it two stars since the first year I had Fintiba it was alright. This time however I cannot set up my payouts and Fintiba promised they’ll look into it. On 1st of August they said I will receive my first payout next week (so this week). It is now 9th of August and no news of my payout. This is money that students use to pay their rent and I dont think Fintiba understands the stress it puts students through.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "My problem hasn’t been resolved. I have said that “ May I ask if you can send me another 'Visa Documents'“which Including updated content”\nPause I think no one take a look on my problem.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Everything was good except very rude video app verification staff.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I tried to solve my problem of opening the account, but I didn’t get an answer from the mail, even no one picked up the call. At last, I saw my account was locked.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The customer service is not professional they can’t solve my issues in addition to saying to me directly by email (we don’t have a solution for you)", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I didn’t get a simple answer for my questions (", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am sending my son to Germany for his University studies. When I set up the blocked account I do not know if I need to put my information or my son information. I have not transferred the money yet, because my son is the person who is going to access the money in Germany, not me. Very confuse the initial process, where does it say that the beneficiary will be my son?", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "In ihrem Empfehlungsprogramm erhält man 10 Euro als Prämie, wenn man einen Freund einlädt.\nIch habe bereits viele Freunde eingeladen, aber leider keine Prämie erhalten. Die Prämien wurden in Form von Mastercard-Karten verschickt, die eine sehr komplizierte Aktivierung und einen schlechten Kundenservice durch ein Zwischenunternehmen beinhalteten. All das für 10 Euro 😂.\nLeider wird dir monatlich ein Betrag von deinem Bankkonto abgebucht. Wenn du die Karte zu lange wartest, verlierst du diesen Betrag von deinem Konto.\nEs ist traurig, dass die Abbuchung von deinem Konto einfach ist, aber die Auszahlung von Empfehlungsboni kompliziert und nicht unterstützend ist.\nEs ist ein Monat vergangen, seit ich eine Beschwerde bei ihnen eingereicht habe, aber leider ohne Ergebnis.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Good day,\n\nCould you please explain why the prices for services in your promotion differ from those I see when filling out the registration form? This is misleading.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The document upload doesn't clarify if the document is uploaded successfully.\n\nOn payment there is only option to freeze the rate but there is no option make the payment on go.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "After uploading my passport, I noticed that my first name on the website was \"Mohamed Amr Farouk\" and the last name was \"Ebrahim.\" I sent an email to Fintiba support to ensure that the name was correctly extracted from the passport automatically and to inquire about the discount code I used.\n\nHowever, a customer service employee edited my first name in the documents to \"-\" (hyphen), resulting in all emails and documents showing my first name as \"-\" and my last name as my full name. This does not seem correct. When I noticed this issue, I sent an email, and the same person responded:\n\n\"Hello Mohamed,\n\nThank you for your email.\n\nAs stated in the previous email, we enter all the passport information exactly as it is in the passport.\n\nWe only rectified the error. These changes will not affect your visa application process as we use the same format with all our customers.\"\n\nI would like this issue to be resolved as soon as possible and for my name to be corrected to \n\"first name/s: Mohamed Amr Farouk\" \nand \"sure name: Ebrahim\", \nas it was before the manual edit by the employee in the documents.\n\nThank you for your prompt attention to this matter.\n\nBest regards,  \nMohamed Amr Farouk Ebrahim (without hyphen)", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ich habe eine Absage von der Botschaft bekommen und sie haben das Geld nach anderthalb Monaten zurückerstattet, glaube ich, und es fehlten 1.900 Euro, und bis jetzt wollen sie den Rest des Geldes überweisen.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "No where they mentioned about the students insurance fees while I'm applying they mentioned only you will get free travel insurance worth 90 eours but never mentioned you need to pay every month 25 eours", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Unfortunately when it comes to take money from you it's very easy for Fintiba, they easily cut what they want from your account.\nBut when they want to pay you your referral reward, they give you useless mastercards and they never work.\nAfter making a complaint i haven't found any result.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "My nephew opened a blocked account with Fintiba to apply for a student visa for Germany. After his visa application was denied, we wanted to close the account and get the money back. However, Fintiba refused to close the account without an entirely unnecessary confirmation of the visa rejection from the German embassy. Even the embassy couldn’t understand why Fintiba demanded this document!\n\nAfter months of effort and immense stress, we finally obtained this confirmation and submitted it to Fintiba. Only then did they close the account and return the money. To our shock, Fintiba deducted a fee of €4.90 for each month the account existed – despite the fact that the account was not used and the money was blocked!\n\nIt’s clear that Fintiba deliberately delayed the closure to collect as many monthly fees as possible. They used my nephew’s blocked money for their own purposes and unnecessarily prolonged the process. These practices are absolutely outrageous and unacceptable.\n\nFintiba is the worst company we have ever dealt with. Their service is not only extremely inefficient but also fraudulent. I strongly advise everyone against using their services. Absolutely disappointing and frustrating. Stay away from Fintiba!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Your fintibot is giving deceiving information\nYour phone app is not properly constructed like the website\nThe problem is every time such tripping happens we get sick for weeks until somebody knows the problem to solve it", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Renovamos la cuenta bloqueda con Fintiba a partir de junio 24, sin embargo el dinero de mayo que corresponde al período anterior no ha sido girado, hoy cumplimos una semana de llamar y enviar correos con la promesa de liberar el dinero que corresponde y no se ha hecho efectivo. Ocasionan un grave perjuicio hay compromisos financieros que cumplir y de subsistencia. Muy mal Fintiba.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I had like the rapid method or the process of opening a closed account\nbut I dislike the 100€ buffer deposit that i should paid it.And It’s an extra to the 89€ at the beginning of opening the account", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I appreciate the quick reply but I asked for many points and you answered one or tow and I have to send another email with the same question. \nThanks", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Erstmal Google Bewertung löschen lassen für einen besseren Eindruck- STARK! Hier gibts nochmal einen Stern : \nIst okay für eine Eröffnung, aber nur weil alle anderen Banken in Deutschland keine Ahnung von Sperrkonten haben, es sei denn man wohnt in einer Studentenhochburg. Sehr unflexibel auf Änderungswünsche, manche Daten sollten schon individuell und je nach Bedarf anders erfasst werden können. In der App kann man nur pauschale Antworten auswählen, alles andere ist gesperrt. Es gibt z.B Länder aus denen man Visumfrei einreisen kann, dafür benötigt man kein Sperrkonto. Dies wird dann aber später für die Verlängerung einer Aufenthaltsgenehmigung benötigt. Diese Eingabe ist nicht möglich. Des Weiteren gibt es den Grund „Sprachkurs“ nicht. Berechtigt aber für einen Aufenthaltstitel. Es muss zwingend eine Universität ausgewählt werden, warum? Das Referenzkonto für spätere Auszahlungen muss auf den Namen des Studenten laufen - warum können keine Konten vom Lebenspartner oder von Freunden hinterlegt werden? Nicht jeder Student braucht zwingend ein Deutsches Konto. Die Einzahlung des Sperrbetrages ist als einmaliger Komplettbetrag „gewünscht“ - maximal jedoch in 3 Raten möglich. Das sagt einem vorher auch keiner. Wenn man seinen Aufenthalt in Deutschland plant, z.B 1 Jahr wäre es schon schön die Blocksumme von über 11.000€ über einen längeren Zeitraum anzusparen und zu überweisen……Die angebotene Incomming Versicherung ist für Studenten uninteressant, da nicht erlaubt wenn sich der Wohnsitz später in Deutschland befindet. Zur Beantragung einer Aufenthaltsgenehmigung wird mindestens eine freiwillige Versicherung in einer gesetzlichen Krankenkasse benötigt die dem deutschen Standard entspricht.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "team, to be honest, my consulate recommended fintiba but I did not think it is easier and simple like you said.\n\nUser and UX interface is not clear and easy to understand, many steps to be taken, money took 4 days to arrive etc. I wait to be happy with fintiba when I arrive in Germany and have a better experiencie with your app and profile site", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am grateful to your support team and I am glad that I contacted you, I can say that it was very helpful for me, But Your work processes should be more transparent for customers.\nThe process of verifying my account to receiving the money was long, which caused a little trouble for me.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The feedback and updates are not good.\nFINTIBA is very bad in answering client`s questions.\n(They have a rigid routine and they only follow it, therefore, other situations are left unanswered)\nThey do not guide for solving problems, they just say: Underprogress ... which is not infact.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I went to the insurance office and showed my appointment with a gastroenterologist on doctolib. I asked if my insurance cover this hospital i will make an appointment. They said yes it will cover. I made an appointment and waited for it for days. And when i go to hospital in my appointment day, the hospital said that they are not working with Mawista, it is not in out list, so your insurance will not cover this. I had to cancel my appointment! Because i am a student! Dont know what to do now. I wrote an email to the office and asked to give me the hospital names list that can cover my insurance. And they said that they dont have any list. So how will it work? Should i randomla pick a hospital and wait for days and cancel again? This is not a headache! I have a serious problem obviously but nobody cares!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "You offer a flawless transfer money using transfer mate but in ma case it took more than 2 weeks. In some time, nobody was able to tell me where my money was. I need to make contact with the local partner to find out more details about the transaction. It is unacceptable.\nIn my previous experience I did it using global66 and it was more efficient", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "On the 1921 bus in Grenoble (France) to Bucharest that was traveling at 06:30 in the morning; the two drivers forced us to pay him €10 in cash because they considered that we had excess baggage.\n\nIn the first instance they did not let us get on the bus, after talking with them we said that it's okay, that we paid for the excess luggage in the flix bus application. However, they told us no. That we had to pay the cash to them.\n\nWe are two people, each one traveled with a large suitcase and a hand backpack. Our suitcases have the standard measures that allow ALL airports and buses.\n\nIt is not the first time that we have traveled with these same suitcases and used the Flix bus.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Das ist so nervig, dass ich immer noch mein Geld nicht erhalten habe. Ich habe schon am 2. April das Geld für mein Sperrkonto mit TransferMate überwiesen. Obwohl es auf der Website von Fintiba TransferMate geschrieben ist, dass es 3 bis 5 Tage dauert, das Geld auf meinem Sperrkonto zu sehen. Jemand hat mir auf E_Mail 7-10 Tage gesagt. Trotzdem sind mehr als 10 Tage vorbei und ich habe mein Geld immer noch nicht bekommen. Ich empfehle Fintiba wirklich nicht mehr. Als Studentin so lange darauf warten ist schwer. Ich habe keine Ahnung warum Fintiba immer noch mein Geld behalt, statt mir zu schicken. Letztes Jahr hatte ich auch bei Fintiba ein Sperrkonto und damals hatte ich kein Problem damit.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Your company sucks,please don’t choose this company for insurance guys it’s a messup and the insurance partner is a joke, had if my education consultancy refered me to expatrio earlier I would’ve never chose fintiba cause expatrio is 10x better than this.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "No accountability,\nThere Indian bank connection took my money and said they can’t open the blocked account and held my money for over a month", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Useless application", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Not having anyone to answer questions. Lots of system bugs and errors. lots of ads on different services which may someone like me don't need at all.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Customer service is not so good. I called twice and the person was not able to give me a proper answer in German. He just gave me a vague explanation and politeness was something he didn’t know at all. “We’re a company and we need to make some money somehow”. That’s what he said in broken German.\nThe monthly payment for keeping the account is also a joke. It would be better to pay a whole fee at the beginning (which I already did to open the account).\nSummarizing, I’m not sure, if I could recommend Fintiba to another person. There are other options that are more convenient (I’m talking about fees).", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Der Status Sendung dauert an, ich bekomme keine Rückmeldung.\nDer Support ist unübersichtlich, nicht klar erreichbar.\nDas hochladen von Dokumenten wird zu wenig rückgemeldet oder überprüft.\nIch finde seit drei Monaten mein Dozentin auflösen können, jedoch funktioniert das nicht.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "They r sooo slow to reply that the haven't reply to my mail back which I have send them two month ego about my block account", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The process of opening an account was easy, but it took a long time to verify the documents and authentication.Also, if the service fee is reduced, your service will definitely be more competitive. In general, I can say that I was satisfied, but I expect more :)", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I can't transfer money into the account", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am waiting for my funds back to me", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Money takes a long time to enter the account and the money transfer process takes several days.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I would never recommend Fintiba Plus to anyone as I thought it would provide help but absolutely not. \nCustomer service is quick but not good, I kept making inquiries regarding my health insurance and the answers were misleading. Due to the unclarity, I was about to pay 170 euros to Mawista and my only option was making a new contract with DAK which was worse and the old one was cancelled for no such reason. No allignment between DAK and Fintiba.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Mi estado es:pendiente luego de 5 días de haber aplicado mi cuenta bloqueada y seguro", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Unclear customer service, weird payment issues, transfer got rejected and they have the audacity to ask about the source of the funds.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ich bekomme auf meine Fragen in deutsch keine Antwort. Livan ist schon seit 03.02.2024 in Deutschland.\nEure Seite ist wirklich nicht gut programmiert.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Where do I begin? The first two days of creating an account and transferring the funds were smooth and fast. Then everything changed. Their system is lacklustre; documents could not be uploaded for verification, and I had to do it several times. And eventually, I called and sent an email before it was rectified. And that was the process; I always had to call for something to be fixed. The system also repeats processes that have already been verified and then turns around, surprised when things don't work. They continuously pushed products, banks, insurance, and sim cards, even when I had answered all questions, proving I had my own set of products. This was extremely frustrating and made worse by their partnership with WEB ID, which is another can of worms. Customer service agents are a mixed bag. By day four, I was at my limit.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Bad experience overall from back office and customer service teams. No explanation whatsoever, just generic answers from people who do not care whatsoever that for you, it is an extremely important process. I opened an account for my brother who lives in Tanzania, I live in France (so a European country) and submitted all required documents. Honestly process was fast. But then comes proving source of funds. And that's where issues started (reminder I live in France) : I submitted a translated bank slip where you could view that my money come from my salary in october 2021, money transferred to my bank savings account, then in november 2023 transfer of the money to my brother's opened Fintiba account. I paid 270 euros to a certified translation company to have all bank documents  translated to English but they have been refused by Fintiba. When I tried to get information from customer service I was told to write an email to the back office. My brother did so by sending once again all the documents and explaining relevant lines of the bank statements (incoming salary, outgoing savings account, outgoing Fintiba opened account) 4 times I got THE SAME GENERIC ANSWER. The back office does not read the emails sent to them, nor do they take the time to explain what is missing from the submitted document. I tried calling, writing, asking for help, but they do not care and when they write back to you it is the exact same answer. Impossible to get a hold of someone who looks at your documents and tells you exactly why the bank account data is not accepted. And when you call and try to explain to customer service they answer you as if you are a dumb person. Do they even understand the importance of such processes for people who are opening these accounts ? I do not think so. It is very frustrating I do not recommend them.\nOh they closed the account and sent back the money to my bank account minus 90 euros. There is no little profit if I may say so.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "It's good for blocked account. But don't ever buy any other service from them. They will charge you for your whole life. Even if you request them multiple times, they are not going to terminate your contracts. The dates they mentioned said it will be automatically terminated after 1 year. But trust me they never do it, they keep on charging you & also if you don't pay they send threatening emails.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "merry Christmas", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I've used fintiba for my first block account in Germany, it works but I have experienced some major issues with them.\n- I've had ~20 euro extra buffer for my transfer in case of intermediary charges however once last payout was made, they simply did not transfer me the remaining 20 euros as it was below the 934 euro transfer rate and just deducted it as charges.\n- the customer service is Unaware, to release your funds, you can use any SEPA enabled account however the customer service insists that we should use DE accounts for some reason.\n- their fees are much higher than the market, just use Oracle, Studely or Expatrio and if you are already in Germany just use Sparkasse.\n-deleting account is not possible according to GDPR, it's mandatory to provide full data deletion if asked by the customer", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I applied a student insurance through your company addressed to OTH Amberg -wieden University and my enrollment deadline is tomorrow. Two days ago I received a message from you saying you have electronically send my insurance confirmation to the University but the University is saying they did not receive it.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Would ve good hace spanish instrucctions anf it takes almost 12 hours to confirm my passport to give me an iban and there is an special way to do they transfer I need all that could be more easy and not take SO long", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "it took so long to get my confirmation document. I did all on time and it took a week long for the money to be on my blocked account.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Monthly payments not divided equal after first payout [ ** Update bellow] \n\nIt should be 742, but it's 715, and when I asked where the extra money goes, the answer was it will be sent with last payout.\n\nWhat if I need this 27euo every month, why don't you just fix it, why should I wait till the last payment!!!\n______________________________\n**Update:\nSupport team contacted me and explained it, \n\"The monhtly administration fee is €4,90. And we start charging it from the moment the money is on your blocked account. \n \nIn your case, the money was in your account since 03.09.2019\"\n\nThat's how I missed the 240€, I hope the support team explain everything from the beginning next time.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Schlecht, wir haben alle verlangte Unterlagen zugefügt nach dem das Geld zu den Sperrkonto Uberwiesen  hat. Zweimal wurde die Unterlagen meiner Tochter an der Botschaft abgelehnt.  Laut Aussage, es erscheint noch keine Bestätigung über Sperrkonto zu denen nicht geschickt...Sehr Ärgerlich und ich bin sehr sauer... Ihr seid keine Hilfe..", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The helpdesk icon doesn t open, and i need to ask some questions before doing my tansfer", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I tried to take a picture of passport, but it failed many times. A message would always pop up and say “can not proceed further as your location is currently not supported”", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Virement effectué depuis la France , alors depuis une banque française , les relevés de comptes sont en français!!! La banque ne fourni pas des documents en Anglais!!! Mais les chiffres sont en tout cas en latin!!! Et c’est une banque sur le sol de l’ UE !!???? Bizarre de ne pas avoir la capacité de traiter des documents d’autres banque européenne??!!!!! et j’ai écrit une attestation en anglais pour expliquer tout ça !!! Mais ils refusent les documents !!! Et ils veulent retourner l’argent!!!!! Je les ai appelé et une dame s’appelle Nicole m’a dit d’envoyer alors les documents par mail , et encore ils ont refusé les documents!!!! Et toujours la même raison » une langue qu’on ne comprend pas »\n!!!!!!!! \nSupport code : 566-079-092", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Doesn’t make any sense. The app is not useful.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I don't know what else Fintiba and Sutor Bank wants me to submit, my father sold his land, he is a trader, and it is from the money that he sent to my sister, who kept it safe and later transfer to me when I was ready to make my payment, after other extended family members had transferred their donations to my account directly that summed up for the funds paid for my blocked account, it was a communal funding. There's no room to explain this, and Fintiba and Sutor Bank are threatening to send back my money with deadline at October 19th, sincerely it is frustrating, I don't know what to do and my interview date at the embassy is December 7th, my school has started classes already since October 2nd. I am already behind schedule now this extra stress.   My documents sent, were notarized. Everyone is tired including my father that sold his piece of land for this course, if there's a specific document Sutor Banks need, they should specifically mention it, I am tired, I'm academic pursuit is on the line.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "UPDATE- and REF number so they can’t have this review taken down is 663435\nIt is now December and nearly 2024, and Fintiba have still not resolved this issue despite replying they will.\n\nNUMEROUS attempts to speak to their “back of house” or to get a call back have gone ignored. We are now being told Sutor bank sent the money in October yet the money has not arrived.\n\nOn 22/12, I called four times to speak with a manager and have been told no manager can be contacted as the front operators don’t have authority to transfer a call. How ATROCIOUS.\n\nEven this review they replied to, we got a generic email saying they’re looking into it and waiting for Sutor bank to respond. Lies lies lies \nDO NOT USE FINTIBA. \nIf it is not resolved by January 2024 we are pursuing heavy legal action and I’ll be taking it to the EU high court to review all their cases which going by this trust pilot thread their are many. \n \n\n\nThis is the worst system I have ever had the displeasure of coming across.\nWe transferred money to fintiba who transferred to Suttor bank Germany to study there.\n\nWe no longer wanted to study in Germany. We have spent over a year trying to reverse the funds.\nWe’ve been told when doing the reversal that the IBAC number is wrong, the euro correspondent bank is wrong, the swift number is wrong. \nWe have spoken to our bank countless times and they have verified the information is correct. Fintiba have absolutely been no help, acting as the “middle man” with no expertise in reversals. \nOnce you submit your updated reversal transfer details on the app, it automatically submits the form, which you then need to download and sign and upload, but it 1- does not give you this notification, 2- \nThe form won’t upload in jpeg or pdf (which their system requires for every other form) so you have to email and 3- the information you fill out on the app doesn’t completely fill out the form completely that you’ve filled out on the app that you’re supposed to download, so they keep sending it to the bank, and it keeps getting rejected. \nDon’t get me started on Suttor Bank, who when we contacted them to ask for assistance were EXTREMELY rude and hung up on us countless times. When we contacted Fintiba, they advised they can’t help with the form, and they will receive notification from Suttor bank if the form is right or wrong.\nThis has been a year long process. I do not recommend using this company unless they will use a euro correspondent bank, which Suttor bank is not. Their process is so archaic and it is to confuse people so they lose money. We had fifteen people who were going to travel and study in Germany who we’ve now referred to a different country to avoid fintiba.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "i satisfy with your service but I ask a question and I did not receive my answer till now.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Unclear requirements caused me spending 200€ fine for delayed payment and 300+€ for notarising. \nIrresponsible and unprofessional.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "My accoauntant still not open thats why ı couldn’t transfer money to my bank accaountant.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I can’t believe this company is from Germany, a country with strictest rule. My friend (Rohan Shrestha)  had transferred the money to his blocked account more than 2 weeks ago. Sent Fintiba even the proof of the transaction from the sender bank. Yet, the support team whenever called doesn’t bother to take the issue seriously and simply answer with “they haven’t got the money”. Takes their sweet little time to reply to the urgent emails. I wonder if this is even a legit company or just a fraudulent one to torture international students. WE LITERALLY SUBMITTED THE PROOF (the official documents)  OF THE MONEY BEING CREDITED TO THE IBAN ACCOUNT. And they cannot even provide conclusive proof that they haven’t received the money. How can they not receive it if the sender bank has literally provided the Swift document for the transaction?\nGonna share this horrible experience from this company to every international student.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I didn't get to choose my health insurance", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "You advertised that health insurance is free but you withdraw money 25 Euro/per Month.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "There's no facility to directly write to a human agent. Contacting Fintiba is mainly handles by the chatbot.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "the internet connection is way to slow in China", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have extended my account for the next ten months. It said that my money would be transferred by the end of August, which is 31st August 2023. But until now 5th September I haven't received my payment yet. I have to pay for everything in September, like apartment, insurance, food, etc. Would fintiba be responsible ? I also have already made several calls, but their words were very unreliable, they said the money would come in either the 4th in the afternoon or the 5th in the morning. But until now I haven't received it at all. One customer servant said that the money had been transferred, but the other one said not yet. Their word is very unreliable. Email response from them is also very slow, I sent it on Thursday, but until now there has been no reply. This is a big disappointment. I will never use fintiba again in the future.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Every process takes too much time and the webpage doesnt report the changes on time, the emails say things that the webpage is not having them", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Es ist schon über einen Monat her, dass ich die Schließung meines Kontos beantragt habe, und es wird immer noch nicht bearbeitet.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Poor service. Too much bureaucracy. For an international student a horrible situation to go through! Take a look at other agencies and learn from them.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "On the 1st of august I send the money for my extend account but I did a mistake, I send the money before ı extend my account. They said it's okay we can send your money back within 3-4 working week, And you can extend your account. It's been a month I still didn't receive my money even though I already told them 5–6 times that I have an urgency. They accepted the money in a day, but they can't send it back in a month. The help center didn't help at all they always said we're gonna figure it out. But they didn't. I talked at least 5 different agents but always the responses were the same. I want to be solved this problem as soon as possible. You only lose your customers' trust in this way.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Die Webseite ist zu langsam！！！！", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "So problematisch und dauert zu viel", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "After completing the Face ID verification still getting the red bar at the top of the menu informing press CONTINUE to    Face ID !!!\nThat hold situation for last two weeks", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "No point in giving a proper feedback to the dumb questions asked. Proof of fund was the money I got from my family and they asked for statement of my family what can I say now?", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "From my experience of using blocked account in Fintiba, I can say the following:\n1. If you are a student, you are opening a blocked account for the first time, you don't have any specific situations (late arrival, non-standard blocked account term, reunion with a partner), you can be calm - everything worked like clockwork for me and some of my friends. Fast transfer and receipt of funds, quite convenient website and automation of the procedure (checking documents, determining the amount of payments, etc.)\n\n2. If your situation is specific, you should be:\na) Attentive. When renewing your account, keep an eye on the amounts charged. It could be that payments come in earlier than the last month of the period and the next renewal year starts a month earlier. The automation of the system makes it inflexible (it is difficult for specialists to make changes to standard procedures), and correcting past mistakes (additional funds, correcting deadlines) can take valuable time\n\nb) Be prepared for lengthy communication if the issue is not resolved. Response times to support requests (email) can be delayed many times, and it is often necessary to use the phone additionally, to communicate with various specialists, and to find out what exactly the problem is.\n\nI can hardly judge the reasons for the difficulties in solving some issues when subscribing to Fintiba, personally I and several of my friends have encountered difficulties in non-standard situations.\nOtherwise, I can still recommend Fintiba as a pretty convenient service if you need a blocked account.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I did not plan to apply for Governmental Insurance. However, Fintiba offered me no other solution. I was literally forced to buy it. That's why I am going to terminate my account.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I don't have more idei.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Utterly disappointed with the abysmal level of service provided. As a concerned parent who made a transfer, it is deeply frustrating to see that even after 20 days, the money has not been credited. The customer service team's only response seems to be a rehearsed script, promising a resolution in 2-3 working days, yet the issue remains unresolved. Every time I call, I am forced to wait for several minutes just to hear the same empty reassurances. This experience has been nothing short of a nightmare, and I urge others to steer clear of this incompetent service.I will keep posted here the prgress for others to know how many days will take to resolve the issue which Fintiba team already know has to be solved from their end. Unfortunately seems Fitiba team is relaxed and enjoying leving all the stress to their customer. I don't think anyone will accept such experience from anyhwere", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "very frustrating and not helpful with payment process", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Confirmation of documents takes too long the fact that confirmation doesn't take place on weekends is very frustrating.\nThe steps to complete the process is very confusing.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The way they make our life pathetic I have never experienced it before.\nThey have money with them in my wife bloedck account and for last 8 days they arw lying they don't have the money when I sent them the account statement they said we will transfer the money in new account ASAP and my wife missed her flight 4 times bcz of them", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have been trying to communicate with someone for months because I need the health insurance and blocked account documents for my visa application and the documents provided from the Fintiba app are useless, the people from BLS international told me that those documents aren´t the ones the German embassy needed and the \"support\" e-mails don´t work at all", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "WebID app is harrowingly terrible. Only the version for desktop browser allows to complete the process. \nAlso, despite I completed video legitimation, I still see a red strip with \"next step complete video legitimation\" after I logged in fintiba profile upon video legitimation has been completed.\nStill have no payment details for account replenishment.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "globalement lors de l'ouverture du compte tout est clair mais lorsqu'on a voulu fermer le compte et récupérer mes argents j'eu beaucoup de perte du temps et pas encore arriver a les récupérer(plus de 3 mois)", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ja, ich bin wieder zurück und mit einem Update über die verspätete Rückerstattung meines Geldes auf mein ursprüngliches Konto.\n\nEndlich wurde mein Geld zurückerstattet!! Aber ich kann nicht glauben, dass ich drei Monate damit verbringen musste, nach dem Verbleib meines Geldes zu fragen, und der Fintiba-Support teilte mir mit, dass das Geld bereits überwiesen worden sei, wobei ich mein Geld nicht zurückbekommen hatte. Ganz zu schweigen davon, dass die Transaktion drei bis vier Wochen dauern würde. \n\nDennoch hatte ich Geduld und vertraute auf die Serviceworte des Fintiba-Supports, auch wenn es zu einer Verzögerung von bis zu drei Monaten kam. Dies führte dazu, dass ich einen Anwalt beauftragen musste und erst zwei Wochen nachdem der Anwalt Fintiba kontaktiert hatte, wurde mein Geld zurückerstattet. \n\nEine solche Situation kann man doch nicht als Zufall bezeichnen, oder?!!! Wird Fintiba also zu einem Betrug oder was?!! \n\nIm Ernst freue ich mich über die Rückerstattung meines Geldes, aber ich kann Fintiba auf keinen Fall mehr empfehlen!!. Diese Situation hat gezeigt, wie unglaubwürdig und unseriös Fintiba ist. Und damit bin ich für immer mit Fintiba fertig und Sie, insbesondere Studenten, sollten sehr vorsichtig sein, denn wenn Sie Ihren Fall nicht richtig bearbeiten, verlieren Sie dann Ihr Geld für immer!!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Transfer process is too slow.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I appreciate your work…keep it up", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "So far easy to follow application, but with the registration of over age people should be looked at again.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Delayed transfer for nothing because of their advertisement for TransferMate. I could just easily transfer money in seconds from German account but their unnecessary partner does it in a week, although they say it takes 10 minutes. Don't believe their lies", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "no option of changing health insurance", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "the website lists Taiwan and Hongkong as a country", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I attached the required documents, and the response was not accepted, and I sent an e-mail for help, but the response was not useful, and I contacted Germany by phone, and the employee could not help me because she did not know", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Fintiba ist nicht zu empfehlen. Meine Cousine hat ihr Konto seit Februar verlängert und bekomme bis heute kein Geld. Wir haben 100 mal angerufen und müssten jedes Mal das Problem erneut erklären. Die Probleme von Kunden werden von den Mitarbeitern nicht ernst genommen. Ich muss für meine Cousine alles bezahlen, obwohl sie Geld bei Fintiba verfügt. Die Beratung ist sehr schlecht. Jedes Mal wird das Gleiche gesagt, aber passiert nichts. Sehr schade!!!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "i could not get any help to solve my problem!!! \ni have already ordered my free sim card in 27.4 , and requested to be delivered in egypt \nbut till now i received nothing \nand fintiba told me to send email but no response from Support ICS or fintiba", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Actually, everything went well and quickly. However, after I opened my account, I decided to delete it shortly afterwards because I came across comments from people who didn't receive their visas and money from your service for three months. This made me fearful.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Arbeiten seeeeehr langsam. Anscheinend ist an Brückentagen niemand anwesend, um Arbeitsschritte in der Kontoeröffnung zu bearbeiten. Sehr problematisch - daran hängt ein Visa-Antragstermin!! Echt nervig.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am writing to report my extremely unsatisfactory experience with Fintiba Transfermate. Despite your website stating that the transfer will be made to my Fintiba account the same day it is received, but after I paid on May 8, I was not able to get a blocking document, which causing me to miss my visa delivery appointment and potentially jeopardizing me to properly attend university. (I still don't get my account today on 15.5.2023)\n\nWhat's more, the fee for using Fintiba Transfermate was approximately 3000 RMB (450 EUR) more expensive than a bank transfer. This inconsistency between the information on your official website and the real consequences I faced is completely unacceptable.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Enttäuschend und ärgerlich!\nKeine Ernsthaftigkeit, keine Ehrlichkeit!! Sehr Langsam!\nMeine Schwester hat ein Sperrkonto bei FINTIBA eröffnet. Sie musste das Konto schließen, weil sie keinen Visumstermin bekam. Das Konto wurde erfolgreich geschlossen, aber auch nach mehr als zwei Monate wurde das gesperrte Geld noch nicht zurückerstattet. \nUnd der FINTIBA-Dienst zeigt keinerlei Ernsthaftigkeit bei der Lösung dieser Angelegenheit.\nIm Ernst, diese Angelegenheit wird vor Gericht gebracht. versprochen!! \nSeien Sie vorsichtig, Leute!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Be very careful with this company, the payout is not refunded. I will definitely not recommend it. After several request always the same answer, I have contracted a lawyer to solve the problem.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Hallo, tatsächlich bin ich auch sehr enttäuscht, FINTIBA diese Bewertung zu geben, denn ich habe von ihnen Ehrlichkeit, schnelle Arbeit und Seriosität erwartet, wie ich gesehen habe, bevor ich mich für FINTIBA entschieden habe.\n\nBei mir ist das leider nicht der Fall. Meine Erfahrung ist wie folgt: Ich habe 2021 ein Studenten-Sperrkonto bei FINTIBA eröffnet, musste dieses jedoch schließen, da ich nach längerer Zeit keinen Visumstermin mehr erhalten konnte. Dann habe ich kürzlich mein Sperrkonto im März 2023 erfolgreich geschlossen, aber was mein Geld betrifft, wurde es mir seit 2 Monaten nicht mehr zurückerstattet und normalerweise gibt FINTIBA auf ihrer Website an, dass die Rückerstattung des Geldes in 3-4 Wochen erfolgt. Aber wo ist denn mein Geld?! \n\nEs ist nicht nur enttäuschend, sondern auch ärgerlich, denn obwohl ich den FINTIBA-Supportdienst und die FINTIBA-Verwaltung zu diesem Thema kontaktiert habe, konnten sie immer noch keine Lösung finden und mir keine konkrete Antwort geben. Seit fast einem Monat antwortet der FINTIBA-Support nur noch auf meine Anfragen und sagt: „Sie warten auf die Rückmeldung der Bank, die mein Geld verwahrt.“\n\nHoffentlich wird mein Problem innerhalb einer Woche gelöst. Wenn nicht, werde ich die Angelegenheit sofort vor Gericht bringen!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "For my student visa to Germany, I opened a blocked account through the company FINTIBA on the 10/07/2021.\n\nDue to not been able to receive an appointment for the student visa, I requested to close my blocked account on the 28/02/2023, which was then successfully closed on the 3/03/2023 with the confirmation, that my documents were submitted to their partner bank Sutor Bank for further processing of the closing transaction and to execute the restitution payment to the original account where the deposit came from.\n\nThe company FINTIBA indicated as well that the processing can take 3-4 weeks until the money is back in the original account. But until presently 09/05/2023, more than 2 months later, the money hasn’t been returned back to my original account.\n\nAlthough I made several inquiries to the FINTIBA customer service regarding the delay of the money restitution, there hasn’t been any improvement apart from the fact, that nearly for a month now, they keep saying they are waiting for the response from their partner bank Sutor bank concerning the delay.\n\nIf you are also in the same situation, please contact me at marievirginienembotDotgmail.com. We want to collect all similar cases and forward them to my lawyer and the German authorities.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Very Very Poor Management. They claim to release the blocked amount in 4 weeks but they dont. they do not even care about your money. it has been more than a month that I uploaded my blocked amount release letter and they have not returned my money. dont know what is their deal... However stay away from them everybody....", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Я расторг контракт по мед. страховке и уведомил Финтиба об этом факте, но служба поддержки никак не отреагировала на мое письмо, при этом с моего счета списывают средства на оплату страховки, договор по которой расторгнут.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "There everything quiet good. But there email service is worst ever. I emailed them but they just auto -reply and give hope where 'Coracle' is much faster than it. Really, never suggested to anyone.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "i complete my payment but not update my document\nit make me miss the visa application", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am sorry to say that, but it is very frustrating that a month ago I transferred the amount, and until now, the amount has not entered the account.\n\nTrasfermate email was sent to me asked me to transfer the amount in US dollars, and it also asked me to transfer the amount from my bank account.  Indeed, I transferred the required amount on March 5th, and it took until the 28th, when I received an email that the amount had deposited in Trasfermate account, but there was a shortage that had to be covered, and this is surprising and unprofessional, but in any way, to save time, as the my German embassy interview is very close, I deposited this difference  to the trasfermate account through my friend's account in the same bank of trasfermate (Wells Fargo Bank), after discussing the matter with customer service employee, and that was on March 29\n\nUntil now, I have not received the updates, and now I am very disappointed and  I do not know what I can do, so please take attention for my case.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "health insurance company , no guidance for new international students where to go in case of sickness.....", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The personnel in general is kind and efficient. In the publicity said one time payment fee of 89.90 which is double as competence. When I tried to extend the account, again need to paid as a first customer. I definetly going with the competence. In general is only a rip off. I join this company because I did a mistake and I couldnt join the other options. I wont recommend to come here, is just taking advantage of the migrant money, that even is already facing so many other big expenses.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have been in Germany for three months now. And I just learned with a just arriving email that my insurance was finalized. What would have happened if I had an emergency which required my insurance that is supposed to cover my whole time here starting from when I arrived in January.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The company can not send me a link for password reset for 10 days. Starting from elongated transfer of my problem to the IT department despite Fintiba having information from me that the problem lies in their IT services, to no result from the IT department. It shows their incompetence in such a simple technical task as sending an email with a recovery link.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "It's always problems with account extension. I never can manage to do it in the APP, and it take eternity to fix this issue from writing an email or calling, and I have to pay each time the initial fee of 90 euro. As a matter of fact, I have an appointment tomorrow with Auslanderbehorde and still have no blocked amount, thanks Fintiba:) can't wait for our it to be over, real nightmare", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Fintiba is a terrible company. \nTheir response time is terribly long. \nIf you have a complain or problem, they sometimes don’t respond to emails and they don’t give clear instructions. \nJust a crappy experience for me.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Its been 3 months now, still Fintiba has not returned the money, they dont even respond properly to query over call. How much patience is required, the person is going under depression. I believe its time to take a legal action against this fake company", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The account opening fee is expensive. It is not possible to reach customer service quickly, you always get a very late reply. Sometimes you don't even get an answer. I was not satisfied and closed my account within 14 days, but still my data (email, ID, phone number etc.) is stored. That's why it's not reliable, I never recommend it.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "It was good, not great.\n\nIt was an overall good experience, even though I didn't feel supported throughout the whole process. I made an inquiry to make sure I was making the right choice and I still haven't got an answer. The way the money is handled could be a bit more transparent. I would recommend it, but with some observations.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I'm not able to login into my account from your application and also from web browser\nI need to download my documents for my VISA interview\nPlease fix this issue", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Worst company I have ever dealt with. They dont reply to chats, phone calls, emails. Everyone please blacklist this company.\nI have been asking for a refund since November 23rd and I still have not go my money back. I feel like im a hostage with this company.\nPlease dont make the same mistake. They have stolen 10,000 euros from me with NO INTENTION of paying it back. Greedy pigs", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "First of all, I had done everything right.\nI transferred everything and submitted all documents necessary but due to the laziness of the employees and their partner « Sutor Bank» which is a small bank, never release my blocking confirmation and made me skip my student visa appointments multiple times!! \nI have been calling their customer service multiple times everyday, still their only response is: «  you have been calling multiple times, you have to wait » no sympathy and no clarity from their customer service. \nI decided to put this review not to shame this company but to warn anybody who considers them for their blocking process. It is a delicate one for the visa as well so make sure you choose better than this company.\nThank you", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I arrived to Germany on 11th October 2022.I already uploaded the documents that needed to unblock my block account. I informed the finitiba bank that I haven’t payout option in the app due to that I can’t give my IBAN of the current account. Its been five months up to now. I informed them that I have to pay my insurance for five months and also rent. They haven’t sloved my problem yet.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I send the money 11 days ago. Still they didn’t reach account of my wife. The appointment in Ausländerbehörde was 3 days ago. I call and write to Fintiba every day since 1 February. Me and my family are not the first time clients of Fintiba and were satisfied. I hope you can solve problem today and the Behörde could take the missing documents.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Once they get your money, they will do everything in their means to make your life difficult. For example send you to 3 places in Berlin in order to verify your identity and ask you to write an email but then ignore you for a week.\nWould be better to open a Sperrkonto at a local bank", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "They charge an administrative fee from the time you open an account, which is very bad, especially for people from countries with VISA issues. They charged me all through the corona period when almost all countries/embassies were on lockdown. I called FINTIBA, who were also aware of the situation and know there was no way I could have gotten VISA or travel during the period, but they still insisted on charging their full administrative fee for that period. Don't understand how they expected me to get a VISA during those periods.\n\nIt is very bad that when other companies were making the corona period a relief period for their customer, FINTIBA was making it more difficult!\n\nAside from their normal charges for the 12 months of payout, I was charged for the additional 4 months (time taken for VISA processing) and 10 months (Lockdown in my home country + Travel restriction to Germany due to Corona), totalling up to 26 months of administrative fees. \n\nTheir service is an expensive option to take, in comparison with other providers, especially for people coming from countries with delay in issuing VISA. Once your money is with FINTIBA, they care less irrespective of the situation.\n\nDate of Experience between Nov 2020 - Dec 2022", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "You did nothing on time and I almost lost my acceptance due to your lack of professionalism.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I came here to Germany as a student, I completed all the document upload thing back in India itself. My amount is not yet unblocked due to some technical issue ( verification Issue ). I am chasing back and forth for my first payout but the customer support team has only one answer, \"Sir, It will be done by tomorrow. We have asked Sutor bank to prioritize your case.\". I need to pay my rent this week and I have not recieved any payout till now.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "très déçu par le service je deconseille à tous. \non fait confiance, pas de personnes physique jusque là on fait le virement mais le projet ne marche pas et nou ssommes conditionnés pour recupérer l'argent pourtant ils doivent garder les frais. plus jamais. si c'était studely je ne serai jamais dans cette situation", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Extremely bad customer service. Have literally zero sense in helping out, expecially at this time when Oct 2022 Winter Semester intake are in transition phase of blocked amount increase from 10332 to 11208. \n\nExpensive when compared to Expatrio or Coracle and yet services are so pathetic. Not to forget the UX is so bad and bugged that you can't even surf their website properly. Just waiting eagerly for my last monthly payout, after which I would close my account with Fintiba permanently.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Opening an account does NOT take a few minutes since it can take a couple of days for them to verify your documents. Also, you have to provide them with detailed documentation of where you got the money from if your country is at high risk for money laundering, which makes the process of opening the account longer. All in all it’s just annoying that a blocked account should be made to get a visa in the first place.\nupdate: to make things worse, when you block your money, you won't have access to it until you get your visa which means from 1-2 months. So you just have to somehow get by without what is possibly your life savings for a couple of months.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Slow  very much", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am not able to use my payouts as there is no option to legitimate the blocked account.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Absolutely not functional service, zero client orientation, from first to last days of work with Fintiba. \n1) proof of identity: I managed to verify my ID through about ten calls via mobile and laptop. There were multiple reasons including passport looking too shiny, too blurry - no way to show the halograms if your video quality is poor, internet quality is not right, etc etc.\n2) despite (finally) confirmation via phone that ID was verified, the mobile app kept showing \"video verification is required\" for many weeks after\n3) visa upload - with dual citizenship, we did not require a visa for the short-term stay in Germany. Thus wanted to access the funds to pay rent from the blocked account while waiting for the long term visa. THis was impossible - i.e. for four months I was funding additionally the stay of my son in teh country\n4) we finally found an alternative solution and I wanted to close the blocked account. The process took two months of mail exchanges between Fintiba, consulate and myself to succeed and get the money.\n\nNET: experience with Sutor Bank and Fintiba is horrible. ABout six thousand EURO spend from family budget unplanned. Lots of nerves and waiting for a response.\nBe ready, if you still choose to go for it, that Fintiba has short working hours; response time for each your request is about one week; robot on the site (chat bot) is totally useless; callcenter is also only partially helpful - they will recmmend to send an email eventually.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I recall a frustrating lack of returned communication on questions unanswered by the FAQs provided online. The customer service is generally not personal enough.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Its too slow and charge 4.99 euros every month for nothing", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The ux from the app is not only quite buggy, but also very complicated and word heavy. It is inconsistent in various interactions and it lacks timely mobile notifications that inform the user about their transactions. I think the company should invest in a proper team of product ux designers and researchers as well as in implementing best practices for service desgin that place users at the center of every touchpoint.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I’m only a student and I don’t think that fintiba are trying to help the students. No gifts, no reductions, no offers. They told me I got a free health insurance fir 2 months and then the 3rd month they cut me 3 months.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "You have done nothing. The money isn't transferred back to my Commerzbank account. And I still can't transfer money to my Commerzbank account. How do I reach my money? How can I get help? 3 Weeks passed since I reported the problem. Still problem is not solved. You are the worst Banking system that I have met. online service does not work, customer service does not work. They just pass the issue one to another. No one wants to take responsibility. As soon as I reach my money, I will close my Fintiba account. And never use it again.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I found it quite straightforward and good guide for the process. \nWhat area can they perhaps improve on? Offering an introductory virtual seminar could in future be used to explain the process, so that users can know what to expect in the different stages.\n\nUpdate to my review 2months later… I am taking down one star as I have seen that you are charged for the account for periods where you do not yet have your visa issued, which in my opinion is a bit unfair because this is not in your control. That in my case took over 3months. Just thought I should warn others out there.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I don’t like the service no solution", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Sehr sehr schlecht, ich habe das Geld seit November für mein Neffe überwiesen , habe auch zigmal angerufen. Jedes Mal wird gesagt, warten Sie 1-2 Tage. Es ist über zwei Monaten vergangen, tut sich nichts!!! Heute hat mein Neffe die Absage von der Botschaft bekommen, weil er den Termin bei der Botschaft nicht eingehalten könnte!! Ich bin sehr sauer 😡 er muss jetzt auf den nächsten Termin ein halbes Jahr warten.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Customer support is not capable of giving me a proper and thorough answer. So I have to ask my question here.\n\nI am studying at Studienkolleg (preparatory course) right now. I have Fintiba Plus. I do not intend to use my blocked account until December 2023. In September 2023, I will start my studies at a German university.\n\nWhat will happen to the insurance (Mawista travel and Mawista private student health insurance) which I have right now as Fintiba Plus? Will I be charged for these insurances in this case? And will I get the full amount when I activate the account in December 2023?", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "С сентября по сей день а это 13 декабря не могу забрать деньги. Вот и думайте стоит ли связываться с Fintibo", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The hotline services from Fintiba are very unprofesional. They have opened for me a new account, and within a month they took me 180 Euro. In the Emails, I wrote that I didn’t need a newer account. ( they took me 89 euro for a month for the new account). \n\nMawista has stolen me 170 Euro…(\nI was ordered to pay 170, although I didn’t get health insurance)!!!! They say.. they will fix the problem, but since June the problem isn’t fixed yet!\n\nWhen they transfer my money, I don’t know what happened with my 45 euros ( I have payed 15 euro for the transfer) ….\n\nSo, I am very disappointed( they took me 170+89+45) without reasons. Fortunately I have all Emails as facts! \nI want my money back, or this is considered as Abuse of Position!!!!! Misuse of others Money!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Hell fintiba, Actually i have alredy registerd on this but i am facing some issue while doing the payment and i am not getting any help from the website. when i am making payment there is option for putting the reference id of payment but when i am doing RTGS there is no option to fill the reference of the payment. Please suggest is it mandatory to use the reference id in RTGS form or i can directly pay the fees in bank transfer details. Please do the needful so that i can make the payment.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Pure incompetence or intentional criminal.\nThere has been a problem with setting up the recipient account of a blocked account for 5 weeks.\nThe customer service promises that the problem will be solved by IT in 1-2 days, instead nothing happens.\n\nAfter the problem was escalated to the management after 5 weeks, the money is suddenly completely gone.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "For complicating the system by holding the hard earned money in the name of security is condemnable. I am already torn in germany with unpleasant experiences with employer, internet provider, courts and immigration for past 6 years. Now even my right on my money is not with me. I have to depend on other to use my money. I loathe this. And this is how Germany has been working, a sad truth in the dream country of many.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Hallo Zusammen,\n\nBei Fintiba kann ich keine empfehlen, da die Service langsam und keine Mühe geben wollen. \n\nmein Geld habe ich von einer Woche überwiesen. rufe ich sie an, sie sagten zu mir, dass es zwei bis drei Wochen dauert. \nauf dem Email habe ich kein Bestätigung, dass Sie mein Geld innerhalb von zwei Wochen überwiesen. \nAlso nur von Mound hören. \n\nDeshalb warte ich maximal zwei Wochen, wenn keine Reaktion kommt, Sofort durch Anwalt.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Terrible, terrible banking service. \n\nAfter requesting an extension for my account, they asked for a source of funds which I provided. I was given information that my account was valid and good to go, and they were only asking me to upload my residence permit or the appointment for it.\n\nA month later, they terminate my account, without any notification. They leave me without any money in Germany, unable to pay my rent or insurance, and the excuse was \"WE ARE SORRY FOR PROVIDING YOU WITH MISLEADING INFORMATION\".\n\nThey also mention they only take 25Euros as a \"fee\" to transfer the money back, but they took 60Euros, and sent the money in two patches making it a total of 120Euro \"fee\".\n\nI would not recommend this bank, their customer support is terrible, and they think they can fix it by saying sorry for providing misleading information.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have been constantly mailing for a data change in my account , My date of birth needs to be changed , please do respond to mails and help out . The communication is too slow.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I try to transfer money to my blocked account but I cant do that because there is something wrong. under the Change IBAN button it says missing. Thats why I cant start to money transfer progress.I dont want to change my Iban i want to keep it same. But in IBAN CHANGE part writes missing", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Sehr Schlecht. Ich habe meinen Konto gschlossen. Dir Schließung wurde bestätigt, und in der Bestätigung wurde so geschrieben; innerhalb 2 Wochen wird meinen Geld überwiesen. Bis jetzt habe ich nichts bekommen, und wenn ich mit Kundenservice spreche, sie sagen immer dass es 4 Wochen dauert, obwohl ich wohne jetzt in Frankfurt, also die Überweisung muss nicht 4 Wochen dauern.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Very slow process regarding the health insurance. Also, the sim card didn't arrive at all.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Process was not according to my expectations", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have been waiting for about a month now to get back my funds from fintiba after closing the blocked account and submitting a Sperrfreigabe from the German consulate. It took them three days to block the funds but it’s taking them forever to make a refund to the originating German account!!!\nI have sent countless emails stating how urgently I need my money refunded, all I get is very slow automated response!\nVery very disappointing!\nI would advise people not to use this BANK! They would disappoint you!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "DON'T USE THIS SERVICE, HERE'S WHY: It's easy to open an account, but getting the money back is IMPOSSIBLE. I wanted to close my account and sent the request in August 2022. Now it's almost October 2022 and I still haven't got the money. They did not want to accept my new residence permit for which LEGALLY I DO NOT NEED their services anymore. They want the authority itself to confirm to them that I no longer need their services, AND THE NEW RESIDENCE PERMIT (for which one does not need the blocked account) FROM THE SAME AUTHORITY IS NOT ENOUGH??? The Berlin Immigration Office has not answered my emails or calls since July. And at my appointment for the new residence permit, they didn't want to give me an official confirmation, they said they weren't responsible for that. On the other hand, there is an email address on the Fintiba website where you can contact them if you have problems with the authorities. BUT THEY DON'T HELP YOU. I have sent them emails and called them several times and they have NOT helped me. THEY DON'T CARE BECAUSE THEY TAKE MONEY FROM YOU EVERY MONTH. PLEASE DO NOT USE THIS SERVICE. WORST EXPERIENCE IN MY LIFE. THEY DO NOT WANT TO GIVE YOU BACK 10,000.00 EUR.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ich bin sehr zufrieden mit Fintiba. Fintiba ist sehr zuverlässig.Ich hatte ein Konto bei Fintiba eröfnet, um ein Visum zu Studienzwecke zu beantragen.Ich hatte schon das Geld überwiesen und drei Monate später wollte ich die Reise nach Deutschland verschieben und habe Fintiba geschrieben, dass ich mein Konto abschliessen möchte.Jetzt ist mein Konto geschlossen und ich habe mein Geld erhalten. Es lebe Fintiba ! Sow B.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "You informed me about transfermate portal is cheaper and faster than İnternet transfer. But that is not true exactly. Tranfermate method both more expensive and slower than internettransfer.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Horrible customer service, they seem friendly but they honestly take forever to even answer.\nFor an international student like me i had a very unpleasant experience with them explaining over and over how I cant get them what they need right now to close my account and refund my money.\nI sent requests for close account and ask them about to refund my money 3month ago,after 2 month they send an emil,I should go to AHK and sent my legitimation letter,I sent them my legitimation documents 1 month ago to the fintiba from the AHK with an email and also by post.\n3weeks ago I called them but they didnt answer and i wrote an email to them , they answer me we didn't received yet,I called to the AHK and they said it was received to Fintiba.\nAnd I sent an email to fintiba again about you must received my letter but now its around 16days i didn't any respond from the fintiba and it was terrible for me.\nPlease some one helps to solve an issue, this is my ticket:475358 and 487235 and 492457", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "their customer service is very bad my mony is stuck in fintiba in past 15 days and i could not get a single peny i transferf my money in fintiba plus account then i mail them to convert my plus to basic account but after conversation my account iban was changed and my money stuck in my closed they said the call sutor bank wait for one or two you,ll get response in which they said we will transferred money in three working days but until i could not get my amount back in my amount my tikcet no is 490271", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I don't like the fact the the app crashes whenever there are updates. I couldn't even login through the internet.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have had quite a smooth experience with Fintiba so far. Getting my blocking confirmation was much faster than I expected. But recently, I experienced a little disappointment. When I sent an email to support@fintiba about a problem that needed to be resolved quickly, I was informed that I would have to wait for 3 to 5 working days to hear back. \n\nThis duration concerns me because it is quite lengthy. I believe that I have the right to ask for quicker responses since I deposited more than 11,000 EUR into an account in which Fintiba is my only point of contact.\n\nI also work for a SaaS in the financial industry where customer success is everything. It is critical to be easily accessible in order to establish a trustworthy relationship with your customers. Response times should, in my opinion, not exceed two working days. I hope this feedback will help you in improving your service.\n\nP.S. It is also quite disappointing to get a million times repeated copy-paste reply in response to a serious concern.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I had duly informed Fintiba in July itself that I would like to close the account when I was in Berlin what is the use of the just a namesake portal when an account cannot be closed and even after submitting the de-blocking letter the bank has charged me administration fee even when my visa was cancelled and I was not in Germany. Very slow service just to get own money transferrred back to the account.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Custom service is bad, I want to why if I want to open an account woth 11.208Eu should I transfer 11.397Eu", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Nachdem das Sperrkonto geöffnet wurde, ist eine Überweisung nicht angekommen!! Ich habe mit dem Kundenservice telefoniert und was haben sie getan?! nichts.. Sie haben mich einfach an meine andere Bank verwiesen wo mein Girokonto war ohne ein bisschen Mühe zu geben und selbst nachzufragen was beim Geldtransfer schief gelaufen worden ist!!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "客服回复太慢，申请账户繁琐", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Very bad experience and very slow service", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "No one answers your phone. I needed to ask how can i get my insurance number fast as i need it for my enrolment", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Three years ago, fintiba had great service. But now unfortunately it got worse. Especially customer service. There are some racist people there who refuse to serve the customers. It is awful. Guys take other alternatives and don't make the same mistake as me. Rude and disrespectful.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Very bad experience. They don't accept payments from Serbia and I think that should be stated somewhere on the internet or immediately when you download the app / open an account. I found that out only when I started the whole transfer process. Waste of my time and nerves. It's the same for Bosnia and Herzegovina and Montenegro.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "It's awful .............", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I don't know what happened but Fintiba automatically subscribed me an insurance and I have to pay for it.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "too slow when auditing my passport", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "It is a pretty good and fast service, but unfortunately, there is not any step by step guidance in the website so that for each step I needed to ask someone who has worked with Fintiba before.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Your phone consultant is awful! we spoke in German and she started to say Du to me and said that If I could not find mail from them it was my problem. Rude! \nof course, I wouldn't have called them every day regarding my support ticket, if I would have a detailed answer to every question in my mail and in time! 8-10 days waiting for an answer and then getting a short copy-paste like 'No worry and ask your Auslaenderbehoerde' is not acceptable for a financial service!!!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "They seem to provide the service they claim. But, Reaching their customer support is tiresome, you first have to go through a bot, and also they reply to emails late, 3-5 business days for emails is too long.\n\nFor example my birthplace was wrong in \nmy contract which I wanted to correct but was unable to reach some who could do it for me, and now my blocked account confirmation has same wrong birthplace, I can only hope it doesn't affect my visa approval and fund withdrawal.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I traveled to Germany to language school at level A1. I tried to open an account in German banks but I was rejected many times. I didn't need this payments also as I used cache and my debit card. Finally I could get a bank account. It was 4th month so I also needed to extend my visa.\nIt's possible to extend account only after you set up payments. \nAfter I set payments and I tried to extend account I got following message:\n\n \"Are you really sure you need to extend your account already? We're surprised because you've only just started receiving payments. Usually, you will need to extend your account later, for example, if you are applying for your residence permit or need to renew your visa. If you nonetheless need an account extension, simply email us at support fintiba.com and we will arrange it for you. Thank you very much!\"\n\nI messaged support immediately and one week later I have no response. \n\nIt's awkward! They could check that it left only 2 months of my 6 months account and of course I need to extend visa. But they decided to be \"surprised\" and pretend they know better!\n\nI am very dissapointed", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The App dose not work fluent in China Mainland. It always breaks down and can't connect to Internet or log in.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "It took over 24 hours for my blocked account to be opened. I read on your website that it takes 10 minutes for the account to be opened instead. I think you should work on this and ensure the time for opening the blocked account should not go beyond 12 hours. Thank you.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "L'application est tres propre et efficace, j'apprécie.mon seul souci a été le temps de traitement ,je l'ai trouvé un peu long, sinon c'est très efficace", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ich habe für meine Stieftochter ein Sperrkonto einrichten müssen. Die ersten telefonischen Auskünfte waren schlichtweg falsch. Ich habe trotzdem das Konto eröffnet, da mir zugesichert wurde, bei Ablehnung des Visums, das Geld nach. 1Woche wieder zurück zuerhalten. Das war wieder eine falsche Auskunft. Als ich nach einem Vorgesetzten der Dame am Telefon verlangte, wurde sie frech und schrie mich an und legte danach auf. Was ist das für ein Service?  Nur die Eröffnung geht einigermaßen problemlos und das nicht gerade wenige Geld auf das Sutor Konto zu bringen, geht schnell. Alles andere lässt sehr zu wünschen übrig.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Verification of passport and university admission letter took lot of time. Portal is quite unresponsive and lagging.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The service by itself is okay, easy to use, and very simple, but their option to make the transfer of the found (Tranfermate) is awful, how 5 business days to process a payment is fast? Hopefully, they will improve this service.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Hello : I have tried to open a blocked account with your Company for my daugther who is going to study in Germany..She is 16years old and I have to show the deposit at the embassy But I cant do it on line..I dont know what to do…Can you help me? Can I call to somebody of your Company to explain the situation? I live in Colombia south America..Thank you", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "123123123123", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "they sent my money in my blocked account about 850 euro less.  I sent e-mails dozens of times, but each time they said that they sent missing money due to the transfer cut of 25 euros.  they reply without examining my e-mails and the account statements I sent.  A bank that I will never use or recommend unless they solve my problem.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Achtung! Achtung! Achtung!\n\nFintiba ist nur ein Vermittler und keine Bank. Hat keine BaFin-Zulassung und ist eine ganz normal klein eingetragenes Gewerbe.\n\nUnser Geld ist bis jetzt nicht zurück und wohl futsch! Anwalt und Polizei sind verständigt.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "everything is ok but the amount of fee is too exepnsive", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "J'ai honneur de venir au près votre haute personnalité pour que vous acquérir mon demander d'un bourse de étude en Allemagne, finir mes études venir travailler dans mon pays s'il vous plaît.. Merci de votre compréhension", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have trouble connecting my smartphone!!!!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Das Sperrkonto zu schließen ist ohne Visaablehnung kaum möglich. Wirklich unfreundlicher Telefonservice. \nSchade!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "For some reasons i could not complete my application in the first place so I had to log out. after that i tried to login several times but i could not. the system was logging me in and in the next instance it was logging me out automatically. then i had to refer back to the email link that was sent during registration to complete my application on Fintiba. this technical issues need to be fixed for smoother experience. thanks.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "30€ Mawista student insurance packet is not supported.\nAlso i can not delete my account and informations from Fintiba", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "website sucks also why is it asking me for a review 10 seconds after I make an account", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "强制捆绑保险套餐，取消不了保险，而且提供的保险都是最贵的保险，咨询也不回复！\nTang Xue态度极差！威胁客户不让取消。\n还在群里求好评，拉倒吧！\n\nForced to bundle insurance packages, can not cancel the insurance, and the insurance provided are the most expensive insurance, consulting also does not respond!\nTang Xue has a very bad attitude! Threatened customers not to cancel.\nStill in the group begging for good reviews, stop it!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have to many problems contacting a human for explanation on the process. Also fintiba transfer is not so useful for my country and there is no warning about this.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Good Tank you", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The company should provide proper details or steps to help students \n1. There is no detail on what is covered and what is not covered\n2. How to get social security number\n3. How do i upgrade my existing insurance to something better.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "How to find details of following\n1. upgrade insurance\n2. what is covered and what is not?", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "You've been cancelling and changing my insurance without prior notice. Every time i try to contact you the problem doesn't get solved. Your fintiba bot doesn't work and reaching you by email is hard as no one replies directly. When i called, the phone operator told me to call the insurance company and get a contract myself, although i have fintiba plus package. That's really a bad service.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "In general Fintiba's webpage and the process to open the blocked bank account is pretty good. However I think you should inform clearly (before somebody buys your pack) all the payments that are required, such as the 100€ for buffer deposit. And maybe the page should be fixed. When I was checking the information to actually open my account I pushed the bottom “enter” because I finished writing A BLANK, but not the whole section, so the webpage automatically sent my info and I couldn’t go back to actually end the process properly. And I think you should be more clear with the health insurance aspect. I just want the governmental insurance and not the private one, and I still doubt wether you are going to respect that or not", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Fintiba best service provider. Helped me from my home country into Germany without me having any worries of how my insurance, monthly payout always on time and most important a SIM card with free service for a whole month.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I ordered the sim a month back and till today I have NOT got any so far. Sorry to say but an extremely poor service.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Keine Möglichkeit in Kontakt zu treten\nKeine Telefonnummer Email nur ein extrem schlecht programmierter Bot", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Anything works\nThey take days to answer and help you\nThey take a week to pay your money\nApp doesn't not work good", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am suppose to get this msg the moment I arrive in Germany, not after 22days!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "There has been many problems during the process of receiving the insurance, as well as that there has been a system mistake that forced me to buy another travel insurance (which wasn't cheap) until my actual travel and health insurance was issued. And I was told that I would get a refund for that, but it wasn't accepted.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am very disappointed with your service . My friend had block account with expatrio and she had a very good experience with them within two days she access her block account to her new account . I am also trying to access my money but the app doesn't submit my application don't know why its the last process and I am stuck in it .", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I have been searching for the next step on my account for the whole day and still couldn't find where to enter my Iban , I still didn't recieve the request to do legitimation altrought I already sended my Visa Scan.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "This is the most expensive block account without any superiority or special function. I've just waste my money", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "It was pathetic experience.\nI lost my VFS new delhi appointment due to 10 days it took to transfer money and no customer care number works on friday.\n\nIn a time when you can transfer money in click of mouse.\nDue to fintiba i lost my money and valuable time of 37 days.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "You didnt give to me my account open money back", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I thought that after transferring the money into my blocked account, I can receive the monthly payout, and I was not informed about the necessity for providing an approved visa extension as a requirement for paying out. Now, I have put all my money into the blocked account, and I don't have any money for the next two months until the new visa is issued.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I used Fintiba around one year ago for my visa process. I bought the Fintiba plus package that involves the health insurance.\nMy insurance sent me a reward for participating in one of their programs and I found it that they sent it to Fintiba without my agreement. I contacted Fintiba for a refund and they agreed to send me the money but sadly till this day after 2 months i still didn’t get my money back from them. They just keep answering me that there were problems in the transfer and they will try again. Highly doubt a problem can persist for that long. They just don’t want to pay me back.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Hello,\nI don't have access to my money for a very long time, so I wouldn't recommend Fintiba to anyone.\nI’ve entered my German cell phone number many times to receive my MTAN code but I haven’t received any code. I called Fintiba several times to solve this problem.\nUnfortunately, it didn’t work. They never return to emails or calls. I'm trying to explain it is really urgent but they are not helping at all. I have to reach my money as soon as possible because I have to pay my rent.\n#398850\nDoga Kilinc", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "2nd Update: Finally getting to the finish line with the refund process. I've done the whole photo selfie thing to change the ghost number, another back and forth with support and thankfully this ordeal is about to come to an end. The original review stays the same so you can read about my initial qualms but I've updated the title and added 2 more stars as I come to terms with the end of this process.\n\nUpdate: Support and I are going back and forth over account closure. Most of their replies are useless and irrelevant. I sent the account closure email on 10.11.2021 and two weeks later nothing. Good luck to all those posting 5-star reviews, we'll see how many stars you'll give once it's time to close your beloved account.\n\nThe story: I opted for Fintiba because they seemed to have the best overall package but this is a decision I am regretting.\n\nFaulty mobile app: Their mobile app is buggy and slow, and erroneous when it comes to uploading documents. For transfers, you need to submit multiple documents as evidence of the source of funds but their system(web and mobile) only allow one document at a time. The whole blocking confirmation process took longer than expected because I got stuck in the 'rejected, please provide more information loop'.\n\nSlow response time: Fintiba's fast when it comes to set up and account opening, but very slow on others. It's almost like they don't have a way of triaging priority issues. If you have an emergency, you'll die alone cursing and swearing. I received my Sperrfreigabe on November 10th and started the account closure process immediately. Once again the app refused to upload the files and I had to contact support. Support got back to me today but with irrelevant instructions on a photo selfie but no response to my actual query which is account closure. So I am back in the sample place I was a week ago.\n\nQuick to charge: Did I mention during the whole time they were silent about the account closure process they went ahead and deduced the setup fee for an account that was supposed to be closed? This they did, despite me, emailing them the documents in the support request and clearly labelling the issue as \"Closure of Account\" someone decided they need to make a quick Euro out of this ignorant sod who knows nothing about banking and finance. I want that money back Fintiba, your excuses won't hold.\n\nData persistence issues: My mobile phone number was mysteriously updated. How this happened, I have no idea. Even hilarious is the fact that you can't use the Fintiba mobile app without receiving an MTAN confirmation from a proper working number. The same number that received an MTAN for opening the account, is the same number that is being rejected by their system(probably was edited and replaced by another) so now I can't get the MTAN for closing the account. Oh, and updating the number requires a photo selfie, which makes me wonder how my number was updated without me sending a photo selfie with proof of the number change? God surely works in mysterious ways.\n\nConclusion: I'm waiting to see what other drama comes with the funds' reversal process and if there are other hidden charges they might spring upon me. I'll be satisfied once my money is back in my bank account where it belongs. To say that I am very disappointed is an understatement.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "HIDDEN FEE\n\ni am a fintiba plus package holder and because of the pandemic in my home country i have just received my pasaport and visa yesterday. \n\nI have received an e mail from fintiba where it says that i have to pay 170 EUR for traveling insurance, which were advertised free for 183 Days for the plus package holders!!\n\nI have sent an e mail to the customer service and still waiting a response. But guys, if there will be some hidden such fees, how can you even trust a service at all? Especially when there is cheaper options for the same service i have trusted to the fintiba and paid extra, because i thought they wouldn't do such thing. \n\nIt is a total disappointment and regret.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am trying to contact with Fintiba for downgrade my account to Fintiba Basic, because I want to cancel my private insurance. We had a lot of phone calls, I sent three different mails but they insist to keep my account as Fintiba Plus. It was a very bad service, if they continue to insist about not downgrade my account one more time, I will close my account and open another one in Expatrio.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I used Fintiba 2 years but now I'm planning to leave it. I wanted to extent my account, but because of their wrongly structured system I cannot do it, and their support desk does not answer my e-mail since one week. Because of their fault I'm on the edge of missing my visa appointment and no one care about that in the support desk. I'm even not sure is there someone in the support desk. They control your thousand of euroes but they do not put someone to support desk to solve your problems. Be clever and do not trust them. There are better alternatives who answer your e-mails in same day.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I transferred my money on 28th June and my visa appointment date was on 29th June but I cannot obtain my blocked account pdf yet I attached my account confirmation as well as money transfer pdf instead of my blocked account. Is it OK or not?", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "very bad refund process after visa rejection . It really takes time and you cant reach customer service any time you want.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am completely frustrated with the refund process with Finitba. I wired around USD $12900 for my brothers living expense into the blocked account with Finitba. However, my brother was not able to get the German Visa so we asked Finitba to refund the money back to the original account the wire came from. Now, they are asking to fill a reversal form and the reversal form states that they cannot send it back to the account in US. It asks for a correspondent bank in Europe (except UK). My bank states that this is a weird request and so long as they have the swift code and account number of the original account they should be able to send it back. It has been more than a month going back and forth about this while my money is stuck in their blocked account. It is very frustrating, time consuming and becoming expensive making those international phone calls. I don't know when this will be resolved and get my money. It's consuming too much of my time and maybe I might have to hire a lawyer to deal with this. Im completely lost at this point.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I wrote email since 1 week but nobody answered my email. I have a big problem right now.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The website is well designed and setting up the account is fast and easy. The only negative feedback i can mention is that setting up the payouts takes a long time. If you need to access the money quickly, you will have problems and there are a few bugs in their app so i just use the computer.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "On the 30th of November 2020, I have transferred my blocking money through my bank.  I heard fintiba provides blocking confirmation very quickly, but in my case, 4 days have going to end, no updates yet. The German embassy in my country has given me only 7 days deadline for submitting the document where 5 days already gone. I am very disappointed with the service", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "To provide more clear information about the right amount to be delivered(for example, blocked account fee+monthly fee+minimum amount=total sum) would be better. As I have sent money twice(and charged twice for transfer fee), but besides everything was very fast.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The App is good, that is what sets Fintiba apart. In addition they have some prominency among students. According to my friends Fintiba was good choice, but I am not able to access my money for weeks now. Plus I had to go to a DAK office to verify my documents which I wouldn't call digital. Also other friends who went with Expatrio and Coracle the process of them was faster and also cheaper, so no reason to go with Fintiba and I wouldn't recommend.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "On 21 of August I have received my Visa Rejection from German embassy. Right after, I have closed my account and attached official paper from the embassy, why my visa has been rejected. Since then, I have no updates from Fintiba. It’s been two months Fintiba has not transferred my money. Two weeks ago I called the call center and I was told that in two weeks they will transfer the money. But still, my account closure is in process. How long should I wait more?", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "EVEN THE GERMAN EMBASSY DOES NOT RECOMMEND FINTIBA ANYMORE!!!\nNIGHTMARE already for SIX WEEKS, making me BROKE. I NEED MY MONEY BACK!!! \nI have opened my account with Fintlba because fellow students said they are the largest and best provider. Maybe they are big, but certainly BAD. I have sent my money and they directly started CHARGING ME, well then I can expect some service as well, BUT THERE IS NO SERVICE, EMAILS GET REPLIED IN 5-7 WORKING DAYS, that is almost TWO FULL WEEKS. Then I tried to get my money back and for SEVERAL WEEKS ALREADY, they block it away telling me that I CANNOT ACCESS it even though I have sent my SPERRFREIGABE already SIX WEEKS ago on their own template. Also the GERMAN EMBASSY FINDS IT UNACCEPTABLE. SO DISAPPOINTING and actually causing me a LOOOOT of trouble.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Awful bank. Fintiba made mistakes with my bank account already second time and I am the person who has to solve it and pay for their mistakes!!! \nPlus to deal with their customer support it is actually a challenge, first it is really hard to explain to them what you want, second they are extremely rude.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Please do not take Fintiba plus. Period. The lame reason they give is that there is heavy traffic in emails. Does that justify 6 weekdays only to respond to a simple query? There is no doubt that Fintiba offers fastest processing of Blocked Account opening and other documents. However, when it comes to customer support, it is the worst. For a simple date change, they have taken more than 6 business days just to respond. God knows when the request is going to be attended. If i really need help during emergency, how will i be able to trust Fintiba with this customer support infrastructure?", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I can only say that I am disappointed by the service. Reply is way slow. Now with COVID I cannot get my money back and when asking, the service reply seems heavy overloaded and furthermore they seem to not knowing what to answer with inconsistency.\n\nUpdate: I got a fast reply and my case is now solved or at least promised I will receive return soon. I conclude to first complain to get issues solved.\n\nUpdate: fintiba is constantly contacting me now to change my review. But I am not satisfied. I will not change my opinion. Now they try to delete my review by reporting it to Trustpilot. I hope that will not work, otherwise a review does not make any sense, if you can only give positive review!!!!", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ein wirklich schlechter Service aber zusätzlich teurer als andere. Wenigstens ist die Seite teilweise auf Deutsch, daher 2 Stern.", "p": "trustpilot"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "absolutely terrible and stressful experience, never recommend fintiba for opening blocking accounts \n\nafter transferring my founds 23.08 - weeks without response, no support, months for “confirming sources of founds” with no time limits and clear requirements what else documents you need to send\n\nas a prospective student you put so much effort to get into the university and you get this attitude.. \n\nif you don’t want to risk your visa, stay away from fintiba", "p": "trustindex"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Stay far away from this service! Reaching their so-called \"customer support\" is nearly impossible and incredibly frustrating. Their AI bot is completely useless, unable to provide real help, and they offer no way to contact a human agent. The listed phone number doesn’t work, and email responses are nonexistent—I’ve been waiting a month without any reply to my urgent inquiries. My account, holding nearly all my savings, is blocked, and despite multiple requests for closure and a refund, I’ve gotten no resolution. This lack of support has put me in a dire financial situation. Avoid this service if you value your time and money.", "p": "trustindex"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Unacceptable service. Do not trust Fintiba to help you with your visa --  they will make every mistake possible and take forever to fix it. WE ARE MISSING OUR VISA APPOINTMENT BECAUSE OF THEM.\n\n1. They made two basic mistakes when opening the account: the name and place of birth were wrong. This information should have been verified against the passport, but clearly it wasn’t. Their support team did not care at all. It took more than a week to fix, and we had to chase them everywhere --  Instagram, Facebook, multiple emails, and calls -- to get any attention at all. \n\n2. Then, after we transferred the money, they displayed the WRONG amount on the visa document!! This document is incorrect now -- we cannot use it at the embassy, so we are missing our visa appointment..\n\nA financial service that is supposed to help with visas shouldn't work like this. Do not trust them!!", "p": "trustindex"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "It’s been a month since I created an account, and the email address associated with it is incorrect. I’ve repeatedly requested them to update it, along with the passport picture, but nothing has been resolved. This delay is incredibly frustrating and has caused unnecessary complications. The lack of responsiveness is disappointing, and I expected much better service.", "p": "trustindex"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ich bin äußerst enttäuscht vom Service und der gesamten Abwicklung.\n\nSeit über zwei Monaten ist mein Konto trotz vollständig, korrekt und nachweislich eingereichter Unterlagen nicht aktiviert worden.\n\nTrotz zahlreicher Kontaktversuche erfolgt keinerlei sachliche Bearbeitung meines Anliegens, sondern ausschließlich automatisierte Standardantworten ohne erkennbare Fortschritte oder Lösungen.\n\nDieses Vorgehen ist für einen Finanzdienst in Deutschland nicht akzeptabel und erfüllt in keiner Weise die Erwartungen an Zuverlässigkeit, Transparenz und Professionalität. Die anhaltende Verzögerung führt bei mir zu erheblichen Nachteilen.\n\nDer Kundenservice ist faktisch nicht erreichbar und zeigt weder eine angemessene Reaktionsfähigkeit noch eine lösungsorientierte Kommunikation.\n\nIch fordere daher umgehend eine vollständige Klärung sowie die sofortige Aktivierung meines Kontos ohne weitere Verzögerung.\n\nSollte dies nicht kurzfristig erfolgen, werde ich weitere offizielle Schritte prüfen.\n\nUnter diesen Umständen ist dieser Dienst für mich nicht empfehlenswert.", "p": "trustindex"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Worst customer service. Worst problem solving skills. After creating a blocked account and visa application was denied, my sister has been in contact with Fintiba since March 6th 2026. The fintiba App doesn't allow her to close the account. She has sent screenshots and videos recording of the problem but still no clearly guidance is given. She has appointed his brother who lives in Germany as power of attorney to follow up. After several calls and emails we don't know how to proceed with this case.", "p": "trustindex"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "It seems fine at first, but when you want to close the account, problems begin. There is no customer service. I recommend other applications.", "p": "trustindex"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "للأسف خدمة تحميل صورة جواز السفر غير عملية منذ أشهر أحاول ولم تنجح. تسببت في تعطيل لي", "p": "trustindex"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Die schlimmste Erfahrung meines Lebens mit der Eröffnung eines Bankkontos. Alle Schritte sind schwierig und kompliziert. Kundenservice braucht Service. Die Bank hat nirgendwo anders als in Frankfurt eine Filiale. Ist Ihnen das zu teuer? Seit 40 Tagen stecke ich in der Kontobestätigungsphase fest und mein Geld steht immer noch aus. Ich rate jedem, sich von dieser Bank fernzuhalten, wenn es eine andere Option gibt", "p": "trustindex"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Mein Neffe hat ein Sperrkonto bei Fintiba eröffnet, um ein Studentenvisum für Deutschland zu beantragen. Nachdem sein Visumantrag abgelehnt wurde, wollten wir das Konto schließen und das Geld zurücküberwiesen bekommen. Doch Fintiba weigerte sich, das Konto zu schließen, ohne eine völlig unnötige Bestätigung der Visumsablehnung von der deutschen Botschaft. Selbst die Botschaft konnte nicht nachvollziehen, warum Fintiba diese Bescheinigung forderte!\n\nNach monatelangem Aufwand und immensem Stress haben wir endlich diese Bestätigung erhalten und an Fintiba weitergeleitet. Erst dann wurde das Konto geschlossen und das Geld zurücküberwiesen. Zu unserer schockierenden Überraschung hat Fintiba für jeden Monat, den das Konto bestand, eine Gebühr von 4,90€ abgezogen – und das, obwohl das Konto nicht genutzt wurde und das Geld gesperrt war!\n\nEs ist offensichtlich, dass Fintiba die Schließung absichtlich hinausgezögert hat, um möglichst viele monatliche Gebühren abzuzocken. Sie haben das gesperrte Geld meines Neffen für ihre eigenen Zwecke genutzt und uns unnötig hingehalten. Diese Praktiken sind absolut unverschämt und inakzeptabel.\n\nFintiba ist das schlechteste Unternehmen, mit dem wir je zu tun hatten. Ihr Service ist nicht nur extrem ineffizient, sondern auch betrügerisch. Ich kann jedem nur dringend davon abraten, ihre Dienste in Anspruch zu nehmen. Absolut enttäuschend und frustrierend. Finger weg von Fintiba!\n\n———————————————————————-\nMy nephew opened a blocked account with Fintiba to apply for a student visa for Germany. After his visa application was denied, we wanted to close the account and get the money back. However, Fintiba refused to close the account without an entirely unnecessary confirmation of the visa rejection from the German embassy. Even the embassy couldn’t understand why Fintiba demanded this document!\n\nAfter months of effort and immense stress, we finally obtained this confirmation and submitted it to Fintiba. Only then did they close the account and return the money. To our shock, Fintiba deducted a fee of €4.90 for each month the account existed – despite the fact that the account was not used and the money was blocked!\n\nIt’s clear that Fintiba deliberately delayed the closure to collect as many monthly fees as possible. They used my nephew’s blocked money for their own purposes and unnecessarily prolonged the process. These practices are absolutely outrageous and unacceptable.\n\nFintiba is the worst company we have ever dealt with. Their service is not only extremely inefficient but also fraudulent. I strongly advise everyone against using their services. Absolutely disappointing and frustrating. Stay away from Fintiba", "p": "trustindex"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Worst option for blocking account, it just makes the procedure hard and waste waste your time.", "p": "trustindex"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I had a terrible experience with Fintiba. Their partner “Sutor bank” is unhelpful. I would not recommend it to anyone.\nExpatrio provides better service. Go for it.", "p": "trustindex"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Very bad bank please do not open account true fintiba, asking lot of documents after received documents finally saying rejected 😂", "p": "trustindex"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Respektlos Kundenservice", "p": "trustindex"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Customer service agents aren't kept up to date with what's going on. The services are all talk and no action! I ordered my simcard about 8 weeks ago and it still never arrived. But says active in my Fintiba App. Fintiba sent my name incorrectly to the legitimatization company to unblock my account and I waited more than a week extra to recieve my money! None of the agents knew how to solve the problem and I was given 2 different sets of info counteracting each other! Now my partner is facing similar issues after the legitimatization company won't work and Fintiba sent instructions... We followed the instructions and waited days.... Called fintiba today only for them to take half an hour to tell me this method doesn't work..... But it's the method they sent us! It's a fight to get your own money out and the advice list is missing so much crucial information... Its misleading as to how simple the process is.", "p": "trustindex"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "worst sperrkonto experience they won't help you", "p": "trustindex"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Extremely incompetent. Helpdesk is the worst. The more you call, the more confusing you are at end. Because there isn't any logic between what is being said and what is done on your account. And they always reject the fault on Sutor Bank, but they are still cooperating with this bank. Since almost two months still waiting for the blocking confirmation. Fintiba is the worst, rea nightmare.", "p": "trustindex"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Dont even think twice! Go to Coracle, much better service, faster and way cheaper ( no monthly charge). Having used both compaines. I  opened an extension account with them for 6 months! They took a monthly surcharge 2 months prior to first deposit and two month after the last payment was made to me means i paid 10 months charges for 6 months account. .", "p": "trustindex"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "From my experience of using blocked account in Fintiba, I can say the following:\n1. If you are a student, you are opening a blocked account for the first time, you don't have any specific situations (late arrival, non-standard blocked account term, reunion with a partner), you can be calm - everything worked like clockwork for me and some of my friends. Fast transfer and receipt of funds, quite convenient website and automation of the procedure (checking documents, determining the amount of payments, etc.)\n\n2. If your situation is specific, you should be:\na) Attentive. When renewing your account, keep an eye on the amounts charged. It could be that payments come in earlier than the last month of the period and the next renewal year starts a month earlier. The automation of the system makes it inflexible (it is difficult for specialists to make changes to standard procedures), correcting past mistakes (additional funds, correcting deadlines) can take valuable time\n\nb) Be prepared for lengthy communication if the issue is not resolved. Response times to support requests (email) can be delayed many times, and it is often necessary to use the phone additionally, to communicate with various specialists, and to find out what exactly the problem is.\n\nI can hardly judge the reasons for the difficulties in solving some issues when subscribing to Fintiba, personally I and several of my friends have encountered difficulties in non-standard situations.\nOtherwise, I can still recommend Fintiba as a pretty convenient service if you need a blocked account.", "p": "trustindex"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Worst customer service I have encountered in my life. They simply don’t care and won’t help no matter what the issue is and how bad it is impacting your life. Pretty sure it’s just a robot even for emails because the answer make no sense and aren’t related to the issue.\nA lot of companies offers this type of service and I am certain any of the other one is 200% better than fintiba.", "p": "trustindex"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I am compelled to share my extremely disappointing experience with Fintiba. First, their helpdesk is incapable of providing any meaningful assistance. It is astounding how helpless they are in resolving even the simplest of issues. When requesting to speak with a supervisor or manager, they conveniently find excuses to avoid forwarding the call, leaving customers feeling stranded and unheard and would keep suggest sending an email to their support email ID.\n\nThey insist on having customers describe their issues via email for every single request or problem encountered. While some matters are resolved effortlessly, others require countless back-and-forth email exchanges, causing unnecessary delays and frustration. On top of that, there have been instances where they reopen closed issues, sending emails requesting updates or providing new information, leading to significant confusion and lack of clarity.\n\nOne of the most frustrating incidents I encountered was when Fintiba unilaterally changed my insurance policy without seeking my consent. Initially, they canceled my Student Classic insurance policy and instructed me to directly contact MAWISTA to purchase a new insurance plan. However, a few months later, without any prior notification or consent, they changed my policy back to Student Classic and provided an incorrect effective date to MAWISTA, resulting in additional charges for my insurance premium. This resulted in a complete waste of my time, as I had to engage in lengthy and frustrating conversations with both MAWISTA and Fintiba.\n\nFurthermore, despite numerous attempts to seek closure on my request for a change in the insurance policy date, I am yet to receive a satisfactory resolution from Fintiba. The entire experience with Fintiba has been incredibly frustrating, leaving me deeply dissatisfied with their services.", "p": "trustindex"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Not very happy with their service. Automated answers only. Even when you write them an email\n\nAdding more context. Rather than addressing my issue, Fintiba has sent a “legal complaint” to google to get my review removed and said I don’t use their service. Guess what? I am a fintiba user and they still have most of my money in their blocked account service. I can prove it with bank statements and what not. The better way for them would be to just get in touch with me and address my concern (which is genuine).\n\nAnd I have sent all proof to google so my review is here to stay.", "p": "trustindex"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Even after payment done from fintiba partner transfermate, sutor bank and fintiba tells they have not received the finds. Last time they received my money 8 days after my payment. Because of which I lost my visa appointment and this time even after processing the payment within germany, I haven't received my funds. And best part is that fintiba replies you after 3 days for any query. Please fintiba atleast for your name sake look into this matter. My payment reference no is 507470371-fintiba-transfer. I have a visa appointment on 14 November. (Issue got resolved but this rating is for damage that is caused to me because of delay in payment).", "p": "trustindex"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Very bad service.", "p": "trustindex"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ich würde Fintiba gar nicht empfehlen, weil man nicht sicher sein kann, dass man nächsten Monat sein Geld bekommt. Bei mir ist es so, dass ich schon 2 Monate (Februar und April) keine Auszahlungen erhalte", "p": "trustindex"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "My couple has been waiting for 2 months to receive back her money for a blocked account. All she received from Fintiba were automatized answers and no solutions. I WOULD NEVER RECOMMEND this kind of service that doesn't take seriously resolving their customers issues with efficiency.", "p": "trustindex"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "DON'T EVER PUT YOUR MONEY HERE!\nThat's extortionate!\nEven if you do whatever they tell you, they will keep sending you messages that the bank isn't accepting the documents, and you can't get contact with the bank to understand what documents are missing.\nThey tell you you can close your account and we return your money without charging, then you do so and you see they took almost 100 euros for wasting your time.\nThere are much better companies out there, just Google blocked account..\nSeriously, I thought first I'll not listen to the bad comments, but you should!!!!", "p": "trustindex"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Fintiba Team should  Answer the Clients via Emails more quickly.", "p": "trustindex"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Ich verstehe nicht, warum die Dienste von Fintiba in 4,7/5 sind. Könnte gefälschte Konten sein, um ihre sehr schlechte Qualität zu verbergen. Ich vertraute darauf, das Sperrkonto bei Fintiba zu eröffnen. Abgesehen davon, dass sie unzumutbare Dokumente verlangen, überweisen sie nicht einmal Geld auf Ihr Konto, sondern nur, wenn Sie ihnen eine E-Mail schreiben oder sie anrufen. Das ist wirklich ärgerlich. Ich war auch ihr Opfer. Sie haben mich angelogen, dass sie das Geld am 30.12.2022 überwiesen haben und bis jetzt, 6.01.2023, habe ich den monatlichen Betrag nicht erhalten. Wenn ich am Telefon bin, schieben sich die Mitarbeiter nur gegenseitig die Verantwortung zu. Ich bin wirklich enttäuscht von der Qualität der Dienstleistungen von Fintiba. Ich weiß nicht, ob ich in Zukunft das Konto von Fintiba schließen kann, weil ich gesehen habe, dass es vielen Leuten hier so schlecht geht wie mir.\nSie sollten Fintiba nicht nutzen. Sie werden Geld und Zeit verlieren. Lassen Sie uns eine andere Bank wählen. Dies ist mein ehrlichster Rat. Die Deutsche Bank sollte nicht mit Fintiba zusammenarbeiten. #534076\n\nI don't understand why Fintiba's services are in 4,7/5. Could be fake accounts to conceal their very bad quality. I trusted to open the block account at Fintiba. Aside from asking for unreasonable documents, they don't even transfer money to your account, and only transfer money when you have to write E-mail or call them. That is really annoying. I was their victim, too. I have requested a transfer since December so that by the beginning of January I have money to pay for my personal expenses. They lied to me that they transferred money from 30.12.2022 and until now 6.01.2023 I have not received monthly amount. When I'm on the phone, the staff only pushes each other's responsibility. I'm really disappointed in the quality of Fintiba's services. I don't know if the future I can close Fintiba's account because I've seen a lot of people here in a bad case like me.\nYou shouldn't be using Fintiba service. You'll lose your money and a lot of time. Let's choose another bank. This is my most honest advice. Deutsche Bank shouldn't be working with Fintiba. #534076", "p": "trustindex"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The worst decision I ever did was signing up with Fintiba. If you’re a foreign student please go to ANY other company than Fintiba. They are taking more than 2 months to close my account and to give me back my money. The customer service is terrible and internal communication is nonexistent, WORST EVER. Give yourself a favor and save your money and time by NOT signing with Fintiba.", "p": "trustindex"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I sent my source of funds documents since 3 weeks and they said it’s unreadable after 2 weeks of waiting and till now i dont know what is the unreadable about my documents or which one of my documents is unreadable because everything is printed and digitalized and if not in english i translated it from a verified translator.\nI called fintiba and spent a-lot of money and in the end they told me to contact sutor bank the issue isn’t from them, then\nI called sutor bank to try to know whats the problem to solve it before my visa appointment because the blocking confirmation is required for the visa application at the German embassy but again they told me don’t contact us contact fintiba!!!!!\nLike what im supposed to do know for real!!\nMy visa appointment on 8th of December and if i don’t have the blocking confirmation by that time i will lose my opportunity to study in germany because the next available german embassy appointment is in march.\nI uploaded the documents again after making another scanned copies and now im waiting.\nPlease make the process quicker\nI can provide you with all the information needed\nPlease help me\n(Solved)\nI changed the rating from 1star to 3\nBecause it got solved i wont make it higher due to the slow pace of solution", "p": "trustindex"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I really had a terrible experience with Fintiba. It's always hard to reach them by phone. I did all the steps to unlock my account but still waiting for my money. They told me last time that it will be transferred on the 26th and nothing happened till the moment. The chatbot is useless. For now, I have 10cents to live with until they transfer my money.\nReally disappointed 😔", "p": "trustindex"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "It's worth five stars if you reply to emails faster than Google Maps comments.", "p": "trustindex"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "One pf the worst banks for your blocked account, im so tired of them. You will definetely have problems with them and the customer service is trash here. Please do your self a favor and open your blocked account somewhere else. Im so tired of waiting fpr my money.", "p": "trustindex"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Admittedly, Fintiba is a service that allows users to create accounts and confirm identities the fastest I've ever used. But the support and chat bots are terrible. I have a problem filling in the information and want to correct it but can't get in touch with the support staff. The hotline number I called for 3 days in a row but no one picked (both German and English). Writing emails also has no response and chat bots can't help because the information the bot gives me can be found on the internet. Hope you improve!", "p": "trustindex"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I dont know how to say this. But i feel so sad, because need more 3-4 weeks to get my mone back to my account. I get receipts when the money has transfered they said need 3-4 days to get my money. But it's been more then 4 days and i send email and asking about the money. They said unncorrect data bank, im ussing original account to get my money back and came from. They said to checj my statement account to confrim and check it that. I send the statement account with another document and i try to call the number and i dont get any answer about the money.\nPlease give me the right answer fot the case\n\nThankyou", "p": "trustindex"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Horrible customer service, they seem friendly but they honestly take forever to even answer.\n\nFor an international student like me i had a very unpleasant experience with them explaining over and over how I cant get them what they need right now to open my blocked bank account.\n\nIt was an extremely frustrating situation to not be able to access my account. And alot of time you need to explaining to customer service from the beginning everything again. I couldn’t verbally explain how difficult that was.\n\nI really dont recommend this and good luck to all of the international students out there and wishing you a better experience than mine, accessing your bank account easily.", "p": "trustindex"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "So far so good,  but there is a huge room for improvement, for example, the call center could listen to concerns before proffering  their well rehearsed solutions. Also they need to work on the video identification or better still place it in the trash can it's rightful place.", "p": "trustindex"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Very slow to solving problems", "p": "trustindex"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "the service is very slow, and they dont mention that its possible that it  would take a lot of time from when you open the account until you can start getting the money. the phone customer service is not friendly.. I would not recommend them", "p": "trustindex"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "It was good with the phone later....May be some technical issue was there.", "p": "trustindex"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "I faced issues opening the account, and closing it.\nI requested to close my account more than a month ago, I applied the requested papers one month ago, and was promised to receive my money \"soon\", and in 3 to 4 days.\nYou need to start adjusting your \"days\" to earth calendar, because I tried to understand it, maybe your company meant moon days... who knows?", "p": "trustindex"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "The only problem is that the video chat for switching the account free is not possible from China. The server is blocked in China.", "p": "trustindex"}, {"c": "Fintiba", "t": "Rude service when I contacted in phone in/with German", "p": "trustindex"}];